var htmlFileInfoList = ["404.html@@@null@@@...","OLVM/adding_olvm_vm.html@@@Adding an OLVM virtual machine@@@Add an Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machine to enable automated snapshot creation and data protection through SLA Domains...","OLVM/assigning_sla_domains_olvm.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to OLVM@@@Assign an SLA Domain to Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machines to automate data protection, retention, and archival...","OLVM/configuring_olvm_backup_network.html@@@Configuring the OLVM backup network@@@Configure subnet CIDRs to route OLVM backup traffic over a dedicated network, separate from OLVM management traffic...","OLVM/configuring_pre_post_scripts_olvm.html@@@Configuring pre- and post-backup scripts for OLVM virtual machines@@@Configure pre- and post-backup scripts on an Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machine to ensure application-consistent snapshots...","OLVM/editing_olvm_data_source.html@@@Editing an OLVM data source@@@Modify the connection details for an existing Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager data source in RSC...","OLVM/excluding_disks_from_olvm_snapshots.html@@@Excluding disks from OLVM virtual machine snapshots@@@Exclude specific virtual disks from OLVM virtual machine snapshots to reduce backup time and storage consumption...","OLVM/manage_olvm_vm_data_sources.html@@@Manage OLVM virtual machines and data sources@@@RSC provides centralized management for Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machines, enabling automated discovery, protection, and granular recovery of virtual machines...","OLVM/manage_protection_olvm_vms.html@@@Manage protection for OLVM virtual machines@@@RSC uses SLA Domains to automate the protection, retention, and replication of Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machines...","OLVM/olvm_minimum_privileges.html@@@Minimum oVirt privileges for OLVM@@@To add an OLVM Engine to Rubrik and enable protection, live mount, and export operations, you must create a custom oVirt role with specific permits granted on the appropriate object types...","OLVM/olvm_vms.html@@@Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machines@@@RSC provides Zero Trust Data Security for Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager environments, offering automated data protection and cyber resilience for virtual machines...","OLVM/placing_olvm_snapshot_legal_hold.html@@@Placing an OLVM snapshot on legal hold@@@Place a legal hold on an Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machine snapshot to retain it indefinitely...","OLVM/recover_olvm_vms.html@@@Recover OLVM virtual machines@@@RSC provides multiple recovery options for Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machines, ranging from granular file-level recovery to near-instant full virtual machine access...","OLVM/recover_olvm_vms_using_export.html@@@Recovering OLVM virtual machines using export@@@Recover an Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machine by exporting a snapshot to a specified destination cluster...","OLVM/recover_olvm_vms_using_files_folders.html@@@Recovering OLVM virtual machine files and folders@@@Recover files or folders from an Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machine snapshot to restore granular data...","OLVM/recover_olvm_vms_using_live_mount.html@@@Recovering OLVM virtual machines using live mount@@@Recover an Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machine by creating a Live Mount from a snapshot to provide immediate access to data...","OLVM/recover_olvm_vms_using_mount_virtual_disks.html@@@Recovering OLVM virtual machines using mount virtual disks@@@Mount virtual disks from an Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machine snapshot to an existing virtual machine to access data without performing a full recovery...","OLVM/refreshing_olvm_vms.html@@@Refreshing OLVM virtual machines@@@Manually refresh the Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager data source to ensure RSC has the latest inventory of virtual machines...","OLVM/removing_olvm_data_source.html@@@Removing an OLVM data source@@@Remove the Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager data source from RSC to remove its discovered virtual machines from the inventory...","OLVM/taking_on-demand_snapshot_olvm.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot for OLVM@@@You can initiate an on-demand snapshot of an Oracle Linux Virtualization Manager virtual machine to capture its state at a specific point in time...","adds/active_directory_domain_dc.html@@@Active Directory domains and domain controllers@@@You can protect and recover Active Directory domains and domain controllers by using the protection services offered by Rubrik Security Cloud...","adds/active_directory_forest.html@@@Active Directory forest@@@Rubrik Security Cloud offers protection services for the Active Directory forest hierarchy. You can protect and recover the entire forest hierarchy in the event of a disaster or ransomware attack...","adds/active_directory_inventory_management.html@@@Active Directory inventory management@@@The Active Directory inventory provides a summary of the actions involved in protecting the AD domain controllers in RSC. You can manage your domains and domain controllers using the information available in the AD inventory...","adds/active_directory_snapshots.html@@@Active Directory snapshots@@@RSC protects and manages data by taking snapshots of the domain controller. You can take an on-demand snapshot, or you can configure an SLA Domain to take scheduled snapshots...","adds/ad_acknowledging_forest_health_checks.html@@@Acknowledging failed Active Directory forest health checks@@@After an Active Directory forest recovery completes with failed health checks, you can acknowledge specific failures that are expected or acceptable to update the forest restore status...","adds/ad_ahr_prereq.html@@@AD alternate host recovery prerequisites@@@Information about Microsoft-recommended prerequisites that you must fulfill to successfully recover domain controllers or domains in an Active Directory forest...","adds/ad_ahr_prereq_2.html@@@AD alternate host recovery prerequisites@@@Information about Microsoft-recommended prerequisites that you must fulfill to successfully recover domain controllers or domains in an Active Directory forest...","adds/ad_alternate_host_compatibility_checks.html@@@AD alternate host recovery compatibility checks@@@Information about the compatibility checks that RSC performs on the target host before recovering a domain controller to an alternate host...","adds/ad_dc_recovery_options.html@@@AD domain controller recovery options@@@With RSC, you can recover Active Directory domain controller snapshots using either granular recovery or domain controller recovery options...","adds/ad_domain_controller_protection.html@@@Active Directory domain controller protection@@@To protect the information on your AD domain controllers by applying RSC data protection policies, you can assign SLA Domains to the domain controllers...","adds/ad_domain_controllers_info.html@@@AD domain controllers information@@@Information about the Active Directory domain controllers registered with Rubrik clusters. You can view information about registered domain controllers and start protecting a domain controller by assigning an SLA Domain...","adds/ad_domain_controllers_info_2.html@@@AD domain controllers information@@@Information about the Active Directory domain controllers registered with Rubrik clusters. You can view information about registered domain controllers and start protecting a domain controller by assigning an SLA Domain...","adds/ad_failed_health_checks.html@@@Failed AD forest health checks@@@After an Active Directory forest recovery completes, health checks validate the state of the recovered environment. In some cases, one or more health checks may fail, causing the recovery to finish with a Incomplete due to warnings status...","adds/ad_forest_discovery.html@@@AD forest discovery@@@When you add an Active Directory domain controller to a Rubrik cluster as a Windows host, RSC discovers the Active Directory forest and all the domains in the forest hierarchy...","adds/ad_forest_inventory_management.html@@@AD forest inventory management@@@The Active Directory inventory provides a summary of the actions involved in protecting and recovering the Active Directory domains in forest hierarchy using RSC. You can manage the domain controllers in a forest using the information available in the Active Directory inventory...","adds/ad_forest_protection.html@@@AD forest protection@@@To protect and recover the information from the Active Directory domain controllers in a forest hierarchy, you can assign an SLA Domain at the forest level. You can apply the data protection policies and recover the entire forest hierarchy using the automated forest recovery that RSC provides...","adds/ad_forest_protection_recovery_benefits.html@@@AD forest protection and recovery benefits@@@With RSC, you can effectively recover the entire Active Directory forest in the event of data threats. RSC provides many benefits through an automated recovery wizard to seamlessly recover the domains...","adds/ad_forest_protection_recovery_hierarchy.html@@@AD forest protection and recovery hierarchy@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based protection for Active Directory resources. You can protect a root domain to start protecting all the domains and domain controllers in the forest hierarchy...","adds/ad_forest_recovery_advanced_settings_options_.html@@@AD forest recovery advanced settings options@@@While initiating Active Directory forest recovery process, RSC provides an option to configure the advanced settings for Windows time service, global catalog servers, and reset KRBTGT password...","adds/ad_forest_recovery_health_checks.html@@@AD forest recovery health checks@@@RSC runs several integrity checks during an Active Directory forest recovery to verify the health of the restored forest and its successful restoration...","adds/ad_forest_recovery_using_replicated_snapshots.html@@@AD forest recovery using replicated snapshots@@@RSC provides the flexibility and robustness to recover Active Directory forest using replicated snapshots in the event of a disaster or ransomware attack...","adds/ad_forests_domains_info.html@@@AD forests and domains information@@@Information about the Active Directory forest and domains discovered by RSC. You can view the information about Active Directory forests and domains and manage protection for the domains by assigning an SLA Domain...","adds/ad_granular_recovery_supported_objects.html@@@Supported AD objects for granular recovery@@@With RSC, granular recovery supports Active Directory objects in the Domain, Configuration, and Application partitions. Support for each object type depends on the Rubrik CDM version of the protecting cluster...","adds/ad_host_promotion_prereqs.html@@@AD host promotion prerequisites@@@Information about the requirements for promoting a vanilla Windows host to an Active Directory domain controller using replication or Install from Media...","adds/ad_identity_first_recovery.html@@@Identity-first recovery for AD forest@@@Rubrik recommends the identity-first recovery method to recover an Active Directory forest. RSC extracts only the identity data from a domain controller snapshot and reintroduces it into a fresh Windows target, decoupling the recovery from the source operating system...","adds/ad_identity_first_recovery_prereq.html@@@Identity-first recovery prerequisites@@@Information about the prerequisites for recovering an Active Directory forest using Identity-first recovery...","adds/ad_object_comparison.html@@@AD object comparison@@@With RSC, you can select and recover specific attributes of the selected Active Directory object. You can compare the attributes with the live Active Directory to view the changes in attribute values for the selected Active Directory object...","adds/ad_object_conflict_during_recovery.html@@@AD object conflict during recovery@@@Information about object conflict scenarios during the Active Directory granular recovery process...","adds/ad_objects_search.html@@@AD objects search@@@With RSC, you can recover specific objects during granular recovery by searching the objects using object prefix name. You can search these objects within a snapshot or across snapshots in an Active Directory domain...","adds/ad_protection.html@@@Active Directory protection@@@Rubrik Security Cloud offers capabilities for protecting Active Directory, including features for backing up and recovering individual domain controllers and entire Active Directory forests, designed to enhance the identity resilience of an organization...","adds/ad_qauth.html@@@Quorum authorization for Active Directory@@@Quorum Authorization protects Active Directory operations by requiring multi-user approval before an administrator can run an action, preventing a single administrator from unilaterally performing destructive or high-impact tasks...","adds/ad_recovery_methods_comparison.html@@@Comparison of AD recovery methods@@@Compare the three recovery methods available for Active Directory recovery to choose the option that best matches your recovery scenario...","adds/ad_retrying_forest_health_checks.html@@@Retrying failed Active Directory forest health checks@@@After an Active Directory forest restore completes with failed health checks, you can retry only the failed checks without re-running the entire forest restore operation...","adds/ad_snapshot_filters.html@@@AD snapshot filters@@@RSC provides filters for snasphots based on various criteria. You can select specific snapshots based on your requirement...","adds/adding_ad_domain_controller.html@@@Adding an AD domain controller@@@Add an Active Directory domain controller as a Windows host to a Rubrik cluster to start protecting the domain controller...","adds/adding_ad_domain_controller_2.html@@@Adding an AD domain controller@@@Add an Active Directory domain controller as a Windows host to a Rubrik cluster to start protecting the domain controller...","adds/adfr_bmr_prereq.html@@@Prerequisites for AD forest bare-metal recovery@@@Information about the specific requirements for recovering domains in an Active Directory forest using the bare-metal recovery method...","adds/changing_dc_snapshot_retention.html@@@Changing domain controller snapshot retention@@@As an RSC user with required privileges, change the retention period if required for specified snapshots of a domain controller...","adds/configuring_rbrk_clstr_primry_win_host.html@@@Configuring a Rubrik cluster as primary for a Windows host@@@Configure Windows host settings to set a Rubrik cluster as the primary cluster for an AD domain controller host...","adds/deleting_ad_domain_controller.html@@@Deleting an AD domain controller@@@As an RSC user with the required privileges, delete a Active Directory domain controller from a Rubrik cluster if the domain controller fails and you want to stop protecting it...","adds/deleting_ad_domain_controller_2.html@@@Deleting an AD domain controller@@@As an RSC user with the required privileges, delete a Active Directory domain controller from a Rubrik cluster if the domain controller fails and you want to stop protecting it...","adds/deleting_dc_snapshot.html@@@Deleting domain controller snapshots@@@As a user with required privileges, delete domain controller snapshots that have Forever retention policies from RSC, as required...","adds/discovery_ad_domains_dc.html@@@Discovery of AD domains and domain controllers@@@When you add an AD domain controller to a Rubrik cluster as a Windows host, RSC discovers the AD domain of the domain controller and the associated domain controllers of that AD domain. This enables you to start protecting the domain controller you added...","adds/dns_debug_log_path_not_restored.html@@@DNS debug log file path not restored@@@During system state recovery of a domain controller with DNS debug logging enabled, the custom log file path may not be valid on the recovery target, causing DNS debug logging to revert to the default path or the DNS Service to fail if the path is inaccessible...","adds/dynamic_disk_foreign_state_dc.html@@@Dynamic disk foreign state after domain controller recovery@@@During a system state recovery of a domain controller to a new virtual machine, the status of dynamic disks appear as Foreign on the new virtual machine...","adds/info_ad_domains.html@@@Information about AD domains@@@Information about the AD domains discovered by RSC. You can view the information of an AD domain and manage protection for the AD domain by assigning an SLA Domain...","adds/managing_protection_ad_forest.html@@@Managing protection for AD forest@@@As an RSC user with the required privileges, manage protection for all the domains and domain controllers in an Active Directory forest by assigning an SLA Domain at the Active Directory forest level...","adds/managing_protection_ad_objects.html@@@Managing protection for AD objects@@@As an RSC user with the required privileges, manage protection for an Active Directory object by assigning an SLA Domain to an Active Directory domain or a domain controller...","adds/protection_hierarchy_ad.html@@@Protection hierarchy for AD@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based protection for AD resources. You can protect a parent AD object to start protecting all the objects in the hierarchy...","adds/recovering_ad_forest.html@@@Recovering an AD forest@@@When a ransomware attack or disaster occurs, recover the entire Active Directory forest to restore all of its domains. RSC provides a master wizard that combines all the steps to recover the domains...","adds/recovering_ad_forest_2.html@@@Recovering an AD forest@@@When a ransomware attack or disaster occurs, recover the entire Active Directory forest to restore all of its domains. RSC provides a master wizard that combines all the steps to recover the domains...","adds/recovering_dc_snapshot.html@@@Recovering domain controller snapshots@@@As an RSC user with the required privileges, recover on-demand and scheduled snapshots of a domain controller...","adds/reestablishing_ad_forest_protection.html@@@Re-establishing AD forest protection after recovery@@@After completing an Active Directory Forest Recovery and deciding to promote the recovered forest to your production environment, re-establish protection by removing old metadata, cleaning up registry entries, and reinstalling RBS. For test recoveries, no action is required as RSC continues to protect your original production forest...","adds/registering_unregistered_ad_dc.html@@@Registering an unregistered AD domain controller@@@To protect an unregistered AD domain controller, install Rubrik Backup Service (RBS) on the domain controller and add it to a Rubrik cluster as a Windows host. After registration, RSC moves the domain controller from the Unregistered DCs sub-tab to the Registered DCs sub-tab and you can assign an SLA Domain...","adds/resolving_dns_debug_log_path.html@@@Resolving the DNS debug log file path@@@Resolve DNS debug log file path issues on a recovered domain controller by verifying and correcting the LogFilePath registry value...","adds/resolving_dynamic_disk_foreign_state.html@@@Resolving the dynamic disk foreign state@@@Resolve the dynamic disk foreign state by importing any foreign dynamic disks while in Directory Services Restore Mode to make their volumes accessible before booting into normal mode...","adds/restoring_ad_objects_using_granular_recovery.html@@@Restoring AD objects using granular recovery@@@As an RSC user with required privileges, restore the Active Directory objects using granular recovery. With granular recovery, you can recover selected objects in Active Directory without disrupting to the Active Directory domain...","adds/restoring_dc_alternate_host.html@@@Restoring to alternative hosts@@@As an RSC user with the required privileges, restore your domain controller data to an alternative host in the event of a ransomware attack or if the domain controller is corrupted and does not start...","adds/restoring_new_host_using_bmr.html@@@Restoring to a new host using bare-metal recovery@@@As an RSC user with required privileges, restore a failed server or domain controller to a new host or virtual machine using the bare-metal recovery type...","adds/restoring_objects_using_search_recovery.html@@@Restoring AD objects using search recovery@@@As an RSC user with the required privileges, restore the Active Directory objects using search recovery. With search recovery, you can search for specific objects by object name across a range of snapshots in a domain controller...","adds/restoring_original_domain_controller.html@@@Restoring to an original domain controller@@@As an RSC user with the required privileges, restore domain controller data to the same domain controller if the data is corrupted and you want to restore it to a last known good state. You can also use this recovery type if you want to recover the deleted objects...","adds/taking_ods_ad_domain_controller.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of AD domain controllers@@@As an RSC user with required privileges, manually initiate an on-demand snapshot of an AD domain controller. You can take on-demand snapshots in addition to the scheduled snapshots, using the take on-demand snapshot option...","adds/tracking_ad_forest_recovery.html@@@Tracking AD forest recovery@@@After initiating Active Directory forest recovery, RSC provides a tracker that details each step, the status, and any errors or warnings. It also outlines the next course of action required to complete the recovery process...","adds/unregistered_ad_domain_controllers.html@@@Unregistered AD domain controllers@@@During AD forest discovery, RSC identifies all the domain controllers in each discovered domain, including domain controllers that are not registered with a Rubrik cluster. RSC classifies the discovered domain controllers as registered or unregistered and displays them in separate sub-tabs on the Domain Controllers page...","adds/unregistered_ad_domain_controllers_info.html@@@Unregistered AD domain controllers information@@@Information about the Active Directory domain controllers that RSC discovered through AD forest topology but that are not registered with a Rubrik cluster...","adds/viewing_ad_domain_controllers.html@@@Viewing AD domain controllers@@@As an RSC user with the required privileges, you can view the registered AD domain controllers. You can also view the domain controllers associated with a specific AD domain and manage protection by assigning SLA Domains...","agent_cloud/adding_policy_packs_account.html@@@Adding policy packs to an account@@@Add a policy pack to an RSC account to include its system policies in the list of policies that appear on the My Policies page...","agent_cloud/administer_agent_cloud.html@@@Administer Agent Cloud@@@Control who can view and manage Agent Cloud, review platform and user activity, and follow best practices for rollout and for building agents that are easier to govern...","agent_cloud/agent_cloud_RSC.html@@@Agent Cloud with RSC@@@Agent Cloud with RSC provides a comprehensive solution for discovering AI agents in your environment, understanding which tools they have access to, detecting risky actions they perform on your data and configurations, and rewinding unauthorized changes without downtime...","agent_cloud/agent_cloud_best_practices.html@@@Best practices for AI agents managed by Agent Cloud@@@Follow these practices to roll out Agent Cloud safely and to get the most accurate inventory, monitoring, and enforcement for your agents...","agent_cloud/agent_cloud_data_plane_provisioning.html@@@Deploy your data plane@@@The Agent Cloud data plane runs as a SaaS deployment that Rubrik operates, or in your own AWS VPC or Azure VNet. Decide where it runs before you connect your AI providers and agents...","agent_cloud/agent_cloud_overview.html@@@Agent Cloud overview@@@Agent Cloud with RSC gives you visibility into AI agents and their tools, controls over their actions, and the ability to rewind their mistakes. It enforces policies in real time, detects risky actions on your data and configurations, and reverts unauthorized changes without affecting other work...","agent_cloud/agent_cloud_prerequisites.html@@@Agent Cloud prerequisites@@@Before you set up Agent Cloud, make sure that your account, network, and protected workloads meet specific requirements...","agent_cloud/agent_cloud_system_policies.html@@@Agent Cloud system policies@@@Agent Cloud includes multiple system policies. These policies are not enabled by default. You can enable them from the Policies page...","agent_cloud/ai_inventory_agent_cloud.html@@@AI inventory@@@The inventory lists everything that Agent Cloud has discovered across your connections: agents, tools, identities, models, and MCP servers...","agent_cloud/ai_inventory_agent_cloud_all.html@@@AI inventory@@@The inventory lists everything that Agent Cloud has discovered across your connections: agents, tools, identities, models, and MCP servers...","agent_cloud/alerts_violations_agent_cloud.html@@@Alerts and violations@@@Alerts and violations are the findings that your policies produce. An alert is a specific action or message that broke a policy. A violation is a standing configuration that breaks one...","agent_cloud/alerts_violations_agent_cloud_all.html@@@Alerts and violations@@@Alerts and violations are the findings that your policies produce. An alert is a specific action or message that broke a policy. A violation is a standing configuration that breaks one...","agent_cloud/api_key_management.html@@@Manage gateway API keys@@@Agent Cloud uses API keys to authenticate AI agents and a dual-key architecture, upstream keys and model gateway keys, to secure agent traffic...","agent_cloud/api_key_management_all.html@@@Manage gateway API keys@@@Agent Cloud uses API keys to authenticate AI agents and a dual-key architecture, upstream keys and model gateway keys, to secure agent traffic...","agent_cloud/available_policy_packs.html@@@Available policy packs@@@Information on the policy packs available on Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/aws_azure_region_support.html@@@Region support for Agent Cloud@@@Agent Cloud supports regions across SaaS, AWS, and Azure deployments...","agent_cloud/aws_bedrock_agent_operations.html@@@AWS Bedrock Agents deployed in Agent Cloud@@@Agent Cloud reads Amazon Bedrock model invocation logs from Amazon CloudWatch Logs or an Amazon S3 bucket, through an IAM role in your AWS account that Agent Cloud assumes...","agent_cloud/aws_bedrock_agentcore_agent_cloud.html@@@Amazon Bedrock AgentCore deployed in Agent Cloud@@@Agent Cloud reads the OpenTelemetry runtime logs that Amazon Bedrock AgentCore writes to Amazon CloudWatch, through an IAM role in your AWS account that Agent Cloud assumes...","agent_cloud/aws_bedrock_agentcore_requirements.html@@@Amazon Bedrock AgentCore requirements for Agent Cloud@@@Deploying Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to Agent Cloud requires an AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) policy and a RSC account with an Agent Cloud entitlement...","agent_cloud/aws_bedrock_requirements_agent_operations.html@@@AWS Bedrock requirements for Agent Cloud@@@Deploying AWS Bedrock Agents on Agent Cloud requires specific AWS Identity and Access Management settings, model invocation logging, and a RSC account with an Agent Cloud entitlement...","agent_cloud/chatgpt_ent_prereqs_coverage_agent_cloud.html@@@ChatGPT Enterprise coverage and requirements for Agent Cloud@@@Deploying ChatGPT Enterprise on Agent Cloud requires a ChatGPT Enterprise workspace with Compliance API access, as well as administrative roles in both OpenAI and Agent Cloud. Administrators must also review the coverage and limitations of integration before deploying ChatGPT Enterprise on Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/chatgpt_enterprise_deployed_agent_cloud.html@@@ChatGPT Enterprise deployed in Agent Cloud@@@Agent Cloud polls Compliance API of OpenAI every 10 minutes to discover custom GPTs and ingest conversations and tool calls from a ChatGPT Enterprise workspace...","agent_cloud/choose_how_to_connect_agents.html@@@Choose how to connect your agents@@@The connection that you use for an agent depends on where the agent runs, and it determines whether Agent Cloud can block the actions of the agent in real time...","agent_cloud/claude_ai_enterprise_requirements.html@@@Claude Enterprise requirements for Agent Cloud@@@Information about the Claude Compliance API key, scopes, and administrator permissions, and blocking method required to connect Agent Cloud to Claude Enterprise...","agent_cloud/claude_anthropic_agent_cloud.html@@@Claude Enterprise deployed in Agent Cloud@@@Agent Cloud reads Claude Enterprise activity after the fact through Anthropic&apos;s Compliance API, using a read-only Compliance API key...","agent_cloud/claude_code_endpoint_detection.html@@@Claude Code@@@Agent Cloud captures Claude Code sessions from the device and enforces policies on Claude Code prompts, tool calls, and tool results in real time, through hooks in Claude Code&apos;s managed settings...","agent_cloud/claude_connections_overview.html@@@Claude connections overview@@@You can connect Claude Code, Claude Cowork, and Claude chat to Agent Cloud for session visibility and real-time enforcement...","agent_cloud/common_agent_operations_terms.html@@@Common Agent Cloud terms@@@Definitions of the terms used throughout the Agent Cloud documentation...","agent_cloud/configure_ai_connections.html@@@Connect your agents@@@A connection links Agent Cloud to a source of agent activity, such as an enterprise AI platform, a gateway that your custom agents use, or the endpoint detection binary on employee devices...","agent_cloud/configuring_anthropic_sdk_opentelemetry.html@@@Configuring an Anthropic SDK agent with OpenTelemetry@@@Configure an Anthropic SDK agent to export OpenTelemetry traces to Agent Cloud using the OpenLLMetry Anthropic instrumentation library...","agent_cloud/configuring_aws_privatelink.html@@@Configuring AWS PrivateLink@@@Configure AWS PrivateLink to create a private endpoint in your workload VPC using the AWS Management Console...","agent_cloud/configuring_aws_privatelink_using_aws_cli.html@@@Configuring AWS PrivateLink using the AWS CLI@@@Configure AWS PrivateLink to create a private endpoint in your VPC using the AWS CLI...","agent_cloud/configuring_azure_private_link.html@@@Configuring Azure Private Link@@@Configure Azure Private Link to create a private endpoint in your VNet...","agent_cloud/configuring_content_capture.html@@@Configuring content capture for Claude Desktop@@@Set content capture on managed devices so that Claude Cowork sessions that Claude Desktop sends to Agent Cloud include prompts and tool content...","agent_cloud/configuring_google_adk_opentelemetry.html@@@Configuring a Google ADK agent with OpenTelemetry@@@Configure a Google Agent Development Kit agent to export OpenTelemetry traces to Agent Cloud using environment variables...","agent_cloud/configuring_langchain_opentelemetry.html@@@Configuring a LangChain or LangGraph agent with OpenTelemetry@@@Configure a LangChain or LangGraph agent to export OpenTelemetry traces to Agent Cloud using the OpenLLMetry LangChain instrumentation library...","agent_cloud/configuring_llamaindex_opentelemetry.html@@@Configuring a LlamaIndex agent with OpenTelemetry@@@Configure a LlamaIndex agent to export OpenTelemetry traces to Agent Cloud by instrumenting the underlying OpenAI SDK...","agent_cloud/configuring_ms_agent_framework_opentelemetry.html@@@Configuring a Microsoft Agent Framework agent with OpenTelemetry@@@Configure a Microsoft Agent Framework agent to export OpenTelemetry traces to Agent Cloud using the built-in instrumentation of the framework...","agent_cloud/configuring_openai_sdk_opentelemetry.html@@@Configuring an OpenAI SDK agent with OpenTelemetry@@@Configure an OpenAI SDK agent to export OpenTelemetry traces to Agent Cloud using the OpenLLMetry instrumentation library...","agent_cloud/configuring_pydantic_ai_opentelemetry.html@@@Configuring a Pydantic AI agent with OpenTelemetry@@@Configure a Pydantic AI agent to export OpenTelemetry traces to Agent Cloud using the built-in instrumentation support of Pydantic AI...","agent_cloud/connect_multiple_projects_own_app_registration.html@@@Multiple project connection with your own app registration@@@You can connect many Microsoft Foundry projects to Agent Cloud in a single connection. This method uses an app registration that you create and manage in your Microsoft Entra tenant...","agent_cloud/connect_single_project_rubrik_managed_app.html@@@Single project connection with a Rubrik-managed app@@@You can connect a single Microsoft Foundry project to Agent Cloud using the Rubrik-managed app method. Rubrik creates and manages an app in your Microsoft Entra tenant...","agent_cloud/connecting_mdm_agent_cloud.html@@@Connecting Mobile Device Management@@@Connect Mobile Device Management to Agent Cloud to monitor and manage AI agent actions on managed endpoints...","agent_cloud/connecting_multiple_projects_own_app_registration.html@@@Connecting multiple projects with your own app registration@@@Connect many Microsoft Foundry projects to Agent Cloud in a single connection by using an app registration that you create and manage...","agent_cloud/connecting_opentelemetry_agent_cloud.html@@@Creating an OpenTelemetry connection@@@Create an OpenTelemetry connection to obtain the OTLP endpoint URL and bearer token that your instrumented AI agents use to export traces to Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/connectors_page.html@@@Connections@@@The Connections page displays all the connections configured on Agent Cloud. These include SaaS platform integrations, such as Microsoft Copilot Studio or AWS Bedrock, MDM connections for endpoint detection, and AI gateways (Rubrik-managed or plug-ins to third-party gateways such as LiteLLM)...","agent_cloud/connectors_page_all.html@@@Connections@@@The Connections page displays all the connections configured on Agent Cloud. These include SaaS platform integrations, such as Microsoft Copilot Studio or AWS Bedrock, MDM connections for endpoint detection, and AI gateways (Rubrik-managed or plug-ins to third-party gateways such as LiteLLM)...","agent_cloud/creating_custom_policies.html@@@Creating custom policies using an AI judge@@@Create a custom policy using an AI judge in Agent Cloud to control which tools, models, and actions AI agents in your environment can use...","agent_cloud/creating_tool_exception.html@@@Creating tool policy exceptions@@@Edit the configuration of a tool to create exceptions for policies...","agent_cloud/custom_agents_built_in_model_gateway.html@@@Rubrik AI gateway@@@The Rubrik AI gateway is a Rubrik-hosted proxy between your custom agents and model providers. It records every prompt, response, and tool call, and blocks the ones that break a block policy before they reach the model or the agent...","agent_cloud/custom_agents_deployed_agent_cloud.html@@@AI gateways@@@Custom agents that you build connect to Agent Cloud through the Rubrik AI gateway or through your existing LiteLLM proxy. Agents that export OpenTelemetry traces connect under Observability...","agent_cloud/custom_agents_existing_model_gateways.html@@@LiteLLM@@@If your custom agents already route their model traffic through a LiteLLM proxy, the Rubrik plugin sends that traffic to Agent Cloud for recording and real-time policy enforcement. Review the capabilities, requirements, limitations, and responsibilities before you connect the proxy...","agent_cloud/custom_policies.html@@@Custom policies@@@A custom policy is a rule that you write in plain English. The Semantic AI Governance Engine turns it into a policy that it judges against agent activity by intent, not by matching keywords...","agent_cloud/dashboard_explorer_agent_cloud.html@@@Dashboard and Explorer@@@The Dashboard summarizes your agent environment and its open issues. The Explorer maps which agents can access which tools and applications...","agent_cloud/dashboard_explorer_agent_cloud_all.html@@@Dashboard and Explorer@@@The Dashboard summarizes your agent environment and its open issues. The Explorer maps which agents can access which tools and applications...","agent_cloud/deleting_api_key.html@@@Deleting an API key@@@Delete an API key you no longer need...","agent_cloud/deleting_connected_model_gateways.html@@@Deleting the connected model gateways@@@Delete an AI model gateway connected to Agent Cloud and clean up associated resources, including API keys, webhooks, and log processors...","agent_cloud/deploy_azure_vpc_ao.html@@@Azure VNet deployment@@@Deploy the Agent Cloud data plane in your own Azure subscription, and review what the deployment creates, the architecture, data privacy mechanisms, best practices, your responsibilities, and the costs before you deploy...","agent_cloud/deploying_aws_bedrock_agent_operations.html@@@Deploying AWS Bedrock Agents on Agent Cloud@@@Deploy AWS Bedrock Agents to Agent Cloud to ingest model invocation logs and gain visibility into AI agent activity for monitoring and policy enforcement...","agent_cloud/deploying_aws_bedrock_agentcore.html@@@Deploying Amazon Bedrock AgentCore in Agent Cloud@@@Deploy Amazon Bedrock AgentCore in Agent Cloud to ingest OpenTelemetry runtime telemetry and gain visibility into AI agent activity for monitoring and policy enforcement...","agent_cloud/deploying_aws_vpc_rsc.html@@@Deploying AWS VPC on Agent Cloud@@@Deploy AWS VPC infrastructure in your AWS account to enable Agent Cloud. Rubrik Support completes the final configuration steps...","agent_cloud/deploying_azure_vpc_agent_operations.html@@@Deploying Azure VNet on Agent Cloud@@@Deploy Azure VNet on Agent Cloud by provisioning the Azure infrastructure in your Azure subscription. Rubrik Support completes the deployment by performing the final deployment steps...","agent_cloud/deploying_chatgpt_enterprise_agent_cloud.html@@@Deploying ChatGPT Enterprise in Agent Cloud@@@Deploy ChatGPT Enterprise in Agent Cloud to enable agent discovery, conversation ingestion, and tool-call monitoring for a ChatGPT Enterprise workspace...","agent_cloud/deploying_claude_ai_enterprise.html@@@Deploying Claude Enterprise in Agent Cloud@@@Deploy Claude Enterprise to Agent Cloud to ingest compliance activity from your Claude Enterprise tenant for monitoring and policy enforcement...","agent_cloud/deploying_endpoint_detection_windows_intune.html@@@Deploying endpoint detection on Windows using Microsoft Intune@@@Use Microsoft Intune to deploy the Rubrik endpoint detection binary to the Windows devices in your fleet, so that Agent Cloud can discover agents, capture sessions, and enforce policies in real time...","agent_cloud/deploying_endpoint_macos_intune.html@@@Deploying endpoint detection on macOS using Microsoft Intune@@@Use Microsoft Intune to deploy the Rubrik endpoint detection binary to your fleet of macOS devices so Agent Cloud can monitor Claude Code activity...","agent_cloud/deploying_endpoint_macos_jamf.html@@@Deploying endpoint detection on macOS using Jamf Pro@@@Use Jamf Pro to deploy the Rubrik endpoint detection binary to a fleet of macOS devices so Agent Cloud can discover agents, capture sessions, and enforce policies...","agent_cloud/deploying_gemini.html@@@Connecting Google Cloud Gemini Enterprise to Agent Cloud@@@Connect your Google Cloud Gemini Enterprise environment to Agent Cloud to discover, monitor, and enforce policies on your AI agents...","agent_cloud/deploying_litellm_model_gateway_agent_cloud.html@@@Connecting a LiteLLM proxy@@@Connect an existing LiteLLM proxy to Agent Cloud to enable real-time monitoring and governance of custom AI agents...","agent_cloud/deploying_ms_copilot_365_agent_ops.html@@@Deploying Microsoft Copilot 365 on Agent Cloud@@@Deploy Microsoft Copilot 365 to Agent Cloud to enable agent discovery and activity logging...","agent_cloud/deploying_ms_foundry_agent_operations.html@@@Deploying Microsoft Foundry (new) with a Rubrik-managed app@@@Deploy Microsoft Foundry (new) to Agent Cloud by establishing a secure service principal connection to your Azure tenant and mapping project resources...","agent_cloud/deploying_ms_foundry_classic_agent_operations.html@@@Deploying Microsoft Foundry (classic) with a Rubrik-managed app@@@Deploy Microsoft Foundry (classic) to Agent Cloud by establishing a secure service principal connection to your Microsoft Entra tenant and mapping project resources...","agent_cloud/deploying_mscs_custom_app_registration.html@@@Deploying Microsoft Copilot Studio for custom app registration@@@Connect up to 500 Microsoft Copilot Studio environments to Agent Cloud in a single connection using an app registration that you create and manage...","agent_cloud/deploying_mscs_rubrik_managed_apps.html@@@Deploying Microsoft Copilot Studio for Rubrik-managed applications@@@Connect a single Microsoft Copilot Studio environment to Agent Cloud by using an application that Rubrik creates and manages in your Microsoft Entra tenant, to enable agent discovery, activity logging, and real-time tool blocking...","agent_cloud/determine_domain_sharing_policy.html@@@Determining Domain Restricted Sharing policy enforcement@@@Determine whether your organization enforces a Domain Restricted Sharing policy, and add an exception for the Rubrik service account or the Rubrik organization domain before connecting Google Cloud Gemini Enterprise to Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/discover_observe_agent_cloud.html@@@Discover and observe@@@Agent Cloud builds an inventory of the agents, tools, identities, models, and MCP servers in your environment, and records what each agent does, session by session...","agent_cloud/editing_custom_policy_llm_judge.html@@@Editing a custom policy using an AI judge@@@Modify the configuration, conditions, or enforcement settings of an existing Agent Cloud custom policy to align with updated organizational security requirements...","agent_cloud/editing_roles_session_viewing_access.html@@@Editing roles for session viewing access@@@Edit a custom role to add the View Session Timelines and Summaries permission, granting users access to view session data in Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/enabling_disabling_ai_operations_policies.html@@@Enabling or disabling Agent Cloud policies@@@Enable or disable policies to control which agent actions Agent Cloud monitors and enforces...","agent_cloud/enabling_tool_blocking_custom_app_registration.html@@@Enabling tool blocking on custom app registration@@@Enable tool blocking so that Microsoft Copilot Studio intercepts and blocks unauthorized tool usage and policy violations in real-time using Agent Cloud for a connection that uses a custom app registration...","agent_cloud/enabling_tool_blocking_existing_copilot_connections.html@@@Enabling tool blocking on existing Rubrik-managed connections@@@Enable tool blocking on an existing connection that uses the Rubrik-managed application so that Microsoft Copilot Studio intercepts and blocks unauthorized tool usage and policy violations in real time using Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/enabling_tool_blocking_rubrik_managed_applications.html@@@Enabling tool blocking on Rubrik-managed applications@@@Enable tool blocking so that Microsoft Copilot Studio intercepts and blocks unauthorized tool usage and policy violations in real-time using Agent Cloud for a connection that uses a Rubrik-managed application...","agent_cloud/endpoint_detection_agent_cloud.html@@@Endpoint detection@@@The Rubrik endpoint detection binary runs on employee devices to discover the AI agents installed there and the identities that use them, and, for supported agents, to capture their sessions and enforce policies in real time...","agent_cloud/endpoint_detection_requirements_agent_cloud.html@@@Endpoint detection requirements@@@Requirements for running the Rubrik endpoint detection binary on employee devices: the requirements that apply to every deployment, and the additional requirements for MDM deployments and for manual installation...","agent_cloud/enforcement_modes_agent_cloud_all.html@@@Enforcement modes@@@The enforcement mode of a policy determines what happens when agent activity breaks it: Monitor records an alert, Block stops the action before it runs, and Ask hands the action to the approval prompt of the agent...","agent_cloud/events_page_agent_cloud.html@@@Event log and audit log@@@The event log records platform activity in Agent Cloud, such as policy updates and connection changes. The audit log records who did what. Open both from the Events menu...","agent_cloud/exporting_custom_otlp_opentelemetry.html@@@Exporting custom or generic OTLP traces@@@Configure a custom agent or an OpenTelemetry Collector to export OTLP traces to Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/foundry_classic_rqmnts_agent_cloud.html@@@Microsoft Foundry (classic) requirements for Agent Cloud@@@Microsoft Foundry (classic) deployed on Agent Cloud requires client-side tracing instrumentation, specific Microsoft Entra ID (formerly Azure AD) administrative roles, resource identifiers, and service principal permissions to enable agent discovery and log ingestion...","agent_cloud/foundry_deployed_agent_cloud.html@@@Microsoft Foundry deployed in Agent Cloud@@@Agent Cloud monitors AI agents in Microsoft Foundry by ingesting activity logs from Azure Application Insights through an app registration connection...","agent_cloud/gemini_agent_operations.html@@@Google Cloud Gemini Enterprise in Agent Cloud@@@Agent Cloud uses a Google Cloud service account that you create to discover agents and read their conversation sessions in a Google Cloud project, covering both Gemini Enterprise and Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform (Vertex AI Agent Engine)...","agent_cloud/gemini_requirements.html@@@Google Cloud Gemini Enterprise requirements for Agent Cloud@@@Connecting Google Cloud Gemini Enterprise to Agent Cloud requires specific Google Cloud and RSC administrative accounts, along with Google Cloud Identity and Access Management (IAM) settings...","agent_cloud/generating_api_key.html@@@Generating an API key@@@Generate an API key to use for authentication on Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/get_started_agent_cloud.html@@@Get started with Agent Cloud@@@To start using Agent Cloud, confirm the prerequisites, deploy a data plane, connect your agents, verify the setup, and then add policies...","agent_cloud/github_copilot_agent_cloud.html@@@GitHub Copilot@@@Agent Cloud captures GitHub Copilot sessions from the device and, on macOS and Linux, blocks Copilot tool calls in real time through hooks that the endpoint detection binary installs...","agent_cloud/granting_session_viewing_access.html@@@Granting session viewing access@@@Grant users the permission to view session data in Agent Cloud by creating a custom role with the View Session Timelines and Summaries permission...","agent_cloud/high_level_implementation_workflow.html@@@Agent Cloud implementation workflow@@@Set up Agent Cloud in this order: plan, deploy a data plane, connect your agents, add policies, and then discover and rewind agent activity...","agent_cloud/how_agent_cloud_works.html@@@How Agent Cloud works@@@Agent Cloud splits its work between a control plane in RSC and a data plane that processes agent traffic, and it connects to your agents in one of four ways...","agent_cloud/how_policies_work_agent_cloud.html@@@How policies work@@@A policy is a named rule with a severity that Agent Cloud evaluates against your agents, tools, and sessions. When agent activity breaks a policy, Agent Cloud records a violation or an alert and, depending on the policy&apos;s enforcement mode, can stop the action...","agent_cloud/how_policies_work_agent_cloud_all.html@@@How policies work@@@A policy is a named rule with a severity that Agent Cloud evaluates against your agents, tools, and sessions. When agent activity breaks a policy, Agent Cloud records a violation or an alert and, depending on the policy&apos;s enforcement mode, can stop the action...","agent_cloud/https_endpoint_access_aws.html@@@HTTPS endpoint access for AWS@@@When you have established network connectivity, Rubrik configures an HTTPS endpoint for your dataplane...","agent_cloud/https_endpoint_access_azure.html@@@HTTPS endpoint access for Azure@@@When you have established network connectivity, Rubrik configures an HTTPS endpoint for your dataplane...","agent_cloud/installing_endpoint_binary_linux.html@@@Installing the endpoint detection binary on Linux@@@Install the Rubrik endpoint detection binary on a Linux device and schedule it to run every five minutes so Agent Cloud can monitor Claude Code activity and enforce policies...","agent_cloud/installing_endpoint_binary_macos.html@@@Installing the endpoint detection binary on macOS@@@Install the Rubrik endpoint detection binary on a macOS device and schedule it to run every five minutes so Agent Cloud can monitor Claude Code activity and enforce policies...","agent_cloud/installing_endpoint_binary_windows.html@@@Installing the endpoint detection binary on Windows@@@Install the Rubrik endpoint detection binary on a Windows device and register a scheduled task that runs it every five minutes so Agent Cloud can monitor Claude Code activity and enforce policies...","agent_cloud/key_concepts_agent_operations.html@@@Key concepts for Agent Cloud@@@Information about the core components of Agent Cloud and how these components work together to provide observability, security, and remediation for your AI infrastructure...","agent_cloud/limitations_connecting_single_project_rubrik_managed_app.html@@@Limitations of a single project connection with a Rubrik-managed app@@@A Rubrik-managed app connection covers one project and works only with commercial Azure tenants. You cannot change the project after you create the connection...","agent_cloud/manage_agent_operations_policies.html@@@Govern and control@@@Agent Cloud policies are the governance rules that define the acceptable behavior for your AI agents. Use them to detect risky activity and, on connections that support it, stop it...","agent_cloud/marking_alerts_violations_safe.html@@@Marking alerts and violations as safe@@@Mark an alert or a violation as safe when the activity it flagged is legitimate and will recur. Marking as safe creates a policy exception that suppresses future alerts, violations, and blocks for a specific tool or agent...","agent_cloud/mdm_deployed_agent_cloud.html@@@Deploy with MDM@@@Mobile Device Management integrates endpoint management data into Agent Cloud for visibility into AI agent identities and the devices they run on, and it deploys the endpoint detection binary to employee devices through Jamf Pro or Microsoft Intune...","agent_cloud/microsoft_copilot_365_deployed_agent_operations.html@@@Microsoft 365 Copilot deployed in Agent Cloud@@@Agent Cloud reads Microsoft 365 Copilot interactions through the Microsoft Graph API to discover the users and agents that use Copilot and to record their sessions...","agent_cloud/ms_copilot_365_requirements_agent_operations.html@@@Microsoft Copilot 365 requirements for Agent Cloud@@@Successfully deploying Agent Cloud with Microsoft Copilot 365 requires technical components to be configured in the Microsoft Entra ID and Agent Cloud environments...","agent_cloud/ms_copilot_studio_agent_operations.html@@@Microsoft Copilot Studio deployed in Agent Cloud@@@Agent Cloud reads Microsoft Copilot Studio agents and conversation transcripts through the Dataverse API and, when you enable tool blocking, intercepts tool calls in real time through the external threat detection integration of Copilot Studio...","agent_cloud/ms_copilot_studio_requirements_limitations_agent_cloud.html@@@Microsoft Copilot Studio requirements and limitations for Agent Cloud@@@Deploying Agent Cloud with Microsoft Copilot Studio requires specific components, administrator roles, API access, and table permissions. The requirements differ for a custom app registration, which Rubrik recommends, and the Rubrik-managed application. A Copilot Studio limitation causes Agent Cloud to display conversations only after 30 minutes of inactivity...","agent_cloud/ms_foundry_requirements_agent_operations.html@@@Microsoft Foundry (new) requirements for Agent Cloud@@@Microsoft Foundry (new) integration requires specific Azure administrative roles, resource identifiers, and service principal permissions to enable agent discovery and log ingestion...","agent_cloud/onboarding_agent_rewind.html@@@Creating a Rubrik AI gateway@@@Create a Rubrik AI gateway so that your custom agents send their model traffic through Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/opentelemetry_agent_cloud.html@@@OpenTelemetry@@@An OpenTelemetry connection monitors AI agent activity from your existing agent frameworks and displays it as sessions in Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/opentelemetry_agent_cloud_all.html@@@OpenTelemetry@@@An OpenTelemetry connection monitors AI agent activity from your existing agent frameworks and displays it as sessions in Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/opentelemetry_requirements_agent_cloud.html@@@OpenTelemetry requirements@@@Information about the permissions, endpoint configuration, and span attributes required to connect Agent Cloud to an agent instrumented with OpenTelemetry...","agent_cloud/plan_policy_rollout_agent_cloud.html@@@Plan your policy rollout@@@Introduce policies in Monitor mode, review the alerts they produce, and move a policy to Block only after it behaves as you expect and only on connections that support blocking...","agent_cloud/policy_enforcement_types_agent_cloud.html@@@Enforcement modes@@@The enforcement mode of a policy determines what happens when agent activity breaks it: Monitor records an alert, Block stops the action before it runs, and Ask hands the action to the approval prompt of the agent...","agent_cloud/policy_packs_agent_cloud.html@@@Agent Cloud policy packs@@@Agent Cloud policy packs are curated collections of system policies you can add to your Agent Cloud account to enable a focused set of controls for a specific risk area, compliance framework, or industry...","agent_cloud/policy_packs_agent_cloud_all.html@@@Agent Cloud policy packs@@@Agent Cloud policy packs are curated collections of system policies you can add to your Agent Cloud account to enable a focused set of controls for a specific risk area, compliance framework, or industry...","agent_cloud/prerequisites_custom_agents_agent_cloud.html@@@Prerequisites for custom agents@@@Before you connect custom agents, ensure that your environment meets the required account, network, and configuration prerequisites...","agent_cloud/prerequisites_limitations_connecting_multiple_foundry_projects.html@@@Prerequisites and limitations for connecting multiple Foundry projects with your own app registration@@@Connecting multiple Foundry projects with your own app registration requires specific Azure roles, resources, and permissions, and has limits on project counts, Foundry versions, and Azure environments...","agent_cloud/provisioning_aws_vpc_agent_operations.html@@@AWS VPC deployment@@@Deploy the Agent Cloud data plane in your own AWS account, and review the architecture, data privacy mechanisms, best practices, your responsibilities, and the costs before you deploy...","agent_cloud/provisioning_saas_infrastructure_agent_clouds.html@@@Provision SaaS infrastructure@@@The SaaS deployment of Agent Cloud uses a Rubrik-managed data plane that RSC provisions automatically when you onboard your AI provider connections. Traffic between your SaaS-based AI agents and Agent Cloud is managed through this dedicated Rubrik-managed infrastructure...","agent_cloud/quick_links.html@@@Quick links for Agent Cloud@@@Navigate directly to the most-used tasks and information for setup, daily operations, and rewind...","agent_cloud/rac_rbac_overview.html@@@Access control for Agent Cloud@@@Agent Cloud separates seeing what it found from reading what agents said. Session content is the most sensitive data that Agent Cloud holds, so viewing it requires its own privilege, which no built-in role includes...","agent_cloud/rac_rbac_overview_all.html@@@Access control for Agent Cloud@@@Agent Cloud separates seeing what it found from reading what agents said. Session content is the most sensitive data that Agent Cloud holds, so viewing it requires its own privilege, which no built-in role includes...","agent_cloud/regenerating_api_key_model_gateway.html@@@Regenerating an API key for a model gateway@@@Regenerate an API key use to authenticate a model gateway connection to Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/removing_policy_packs.html@@@Removing policy packs from an account@@@Remove a policy pack from a RSC account. After removed, the policies the pack provides stop generating new alerts...","agent_cloud/rewind_agent_action.html@@@Rewinding an agent action@@@Undo the changes that an AI agent action made, by restoring the affected objects to their state before the action...","agent_cloud/rewind_agent_violations.html@@@Rewind agent actions@@@Agent Rewind undoes the changes that an agent action made to your data by restoring the affected objects from Rubrik backups, without rolling back the entire workload. You can start a rewind from the Sessions page, or from any page that displays the action or alert detail tray. Rewind requires a complete Rubrik snapshot taken within seven days before the action...","agent_cloud/rewinding_actions_sessions_page.html@@@Rewinding sessions from the Sessions page@@@From the Sessions page, select one or more sessions and rewind the actions they include to the state before the agent changed the affected items...","agent_cloud/sessions_actions_agent_cloud.html@@@Sessions and actions@@@Agent Cloud records what your agents do as sessions, each with a timeline of prompts, responses, and tool calls, and as actions, the individual tool calls within them...","agent_cloud/sessions_actions_agent_cloud_all.html@@@Sessions and actions@@@Agent Cloud records what your agents do as sessions, each with a timeline of prompts, responses, and tool calls, and as actions, the individual tool calls within them...","agent_cloud/supported_frameworks_opentelemetry.html@@@Supported OpenTelemetry frameworks@@@Agent Cloud supports the OpenTelemetry frameworks and instrumentation libraries...","agent_cloud/supported_workloads_for_agent_rewind.html@@@Supported workloads for Agent Rewind@@@Information about the workloads that Agent Rewind supports, including their restore scope, restore destination, and notes for each workload type...","agent_cloud/testing_custom_policy_manual_input.html@@@Testing a custom policy using manual input@@@Submit sample content to test that a custom policy correctly identifies violations before you rely on it in production...","agent_cloud/testing_custom_policy_using_backtest.html@@@Testing a custom policy using a backtest@@@Run a backtest against recent session history to test that a custom policy correctly identifies violations before you rely on it in production...","agent_cloud/tool_blocking_support.html@@@Blocking support by connection@@@Which items Agent Cloud can block, and whether Ask is supported, depends on the connection. Check this table before you set a policy to Block...","agent_cloud/troubleshooting_connecting_multiple_projects_own_app.html@@@Troubleshooting connections for multiple projects with your own app registration@@@Information about errors that can occur when connecting multiple projects with your own app registration, and how to resolve them...","agent_cloud/troubleshooting_discovery_errors.html@@@Troubleshooting discovery errors@@@Information about resolving errors that Agent Cloud displays when it discovers or connects Microsoft Copilot Studio environments with a custom app registration...","agent_cloud/understand_how_model_gateways_work.html@@@How model gateways work@@@Model gateways are the fundamental infrastructure components that enable Agent Cloud to govern, monitor, and secure your AI agent interactions...","agent_cloud/uninstalling_endpoint_binary.html@@@Uninstalling the endpoint detection binary@@@Remove the Claude Code managed settings and the recurring schedule installed by the Rubrik endpoint detection binary so Agent Cloud no longer monitors or enforces policies in Claude Code on the device...","agent_cloud/verifying_claude_code_monitoring.html@@@Verifying endpoint monitoring and enforcement@@@Confirm that Agent Cloud captures the agent activity of an endpoint from a device, and that real-time blocking takes effect when you enable a block policy...","agent_cloud/verifying_endpoint_ingestion.html@@@Verifying endpoint session ingestion@@@Run the Rubrik endpoint detection binary once on a single device and confirm that Agent Cloud ingests the agent sessions...","agent_cloud/viewing_actions.html@@@Viewing the Actions@@@View the actions recorded by Agent Cloud across all monitored AI agents...","agent_cloud/viewing_agent_cloud_policies.html@@@Viewing the Agent Cloud policies@@@View the list of policies that govern Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/viewing_ai_agent_inventory.html@@@Viewing the AI agent inventory@@@View the list of AI agents monitored by Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/viewing_alert_details.html@@@Viewing Alert Details@@@View comprehensive information about real-time activity alerts, including a summary, application name, agent name, and date and time of the alert...","agent_cloud/viewing_api_keys.html@@@Viewing the API keys@@@View the API keys listed on Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/viewing_connected_models_gateways.html@@@Viewing the connected model gateways@@@View the model gateways connected to Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/viewing_explorer.html@@@Viewing the Explorer@@@View a map of agent-to-tool relationships in Agent Cloud, showing which agents have access to which tools and to which applications they belong...","agent_cloud/viewing_gateway_model_inventory.html@@@Viewing the model inventory@@@View information about models discovered by Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/viewing_insights.html@@@Viewing insights@@@View the Insights page to review security recommendations and posture improvements identified by Agent Cloud...","agent_cloud/viewing_mcp_server_details.html@@@Viewing MCP server details@@@View specific information about an MCP server, including its configuration, the identities that use it, and the endpoints where it is installed...","agent_cloud/viewing_policies_policy_pack.html@@@Viewing the policy packs and their policies@@@View the policy packs catalog to see which packs are available and which are added to the account, and view the policies that a pack contains, including the name, category, and current status of each policy in the account...","agent_cloud/viewing_session_details.html@@@Viewing session details@@@View session metadata, the event timeline, alerts, and actions to review what an AI agent did during a session...","agent_cloud/viewing_tool_details.html@@@Viewing tool details@@@View specific information about a tool, including its description, functional capabilities, and authorized agents...","agent_cloud/viewing_violation_details.html@@@Viewing violation details@@@View details regarding policy violations, including the affected application, the tool used, and the underlying LLM model...","ai/annapurna-chat-controls.html@@@Annapurna chat controls@@@Annapurna provides several UI elements that help you work with your chats...","ai/annapurna.html@@@Annapurna@@@Rubrik Security Cloud includes the Annapurna application which you can use to obtain answers from your data, using generative AI...","ai/annapurna_benefits.html@@@Benefits of Annapurna@@@Annapurna enables enterprises to securely leverage retrieval-augmented generation and generative AI for enhanced data understanding, solving complex business use cases by correlating data from multiple sources without disrupting backup and recovery operations...","ai/annapurna_framework.html@@@Annapurna framework@@@Annapurna uses an embedding model to change source data and chatbot questions into vector embeddings. These embeddings are stored in a vector database. The vector embeddings from the data source that match the query vector embeddings are then combined to create the prompt sent to the LLM...","ai/creating_annapurna_chatbot.html@@@Creating a chatbot@@@Create an Annapurna chatbot that uses retrieval-augmented generation to answer your data-related questions...","ai/deleting_annapurna_chatbot.html@@@Deleting a chatbot@@@Delete a chatbot to prevent users from accessing the chatbot...","ai/editing_annapurna_chatbot.html@@@Editing a chatbot@@@Edit an Annapurna chatbot to modify the settings...","ai/using_annapurna_chatbot.html@@@Using a chatbot@@@Use an Annapurna chatbot to start a natural language conversation about your data...","amazon_S3/accessing_aws_s3_page.html@@@Accessing the AWS S3 page@@@Access the AWS S3 inventory page from the Data Protection dashboard to view, manage, and protect the Amazon S3 buckets. You can also take on-demand snapshots of the S3 buckets from the AWS S3 inventory page and recover the S3 buckets and their objects using the Export and In-place recovery options from the corresponding S3 bucket snapshot page...","amazon_S3/amazon_s3.html@@@Manage Amazon S3@@@With RSC, you can protect and recover your Amazon S3 buckets and objects...","amazon_S3/amazon_s3_inventory_management.html@@@Amazon S3 inventory management@@@You can use Amazon S3 inventory management to view AWS S3 buckets across accounts and manage protection policies to protect your data...","amazon_S3/amazon_s3_protection_mechanism.html@@@Amazon S3 protection mechanism@@@RSC protects your Amazon S3 buckets and objects by taking backups according to the assigned SLA Domain and providing options for recovery of your buckets and objects...","amazon_S3/anomaly_detection_amazon_s3_buckets.html@@@Anomaly Detection for Amazon S3 buckets@@@Anomaly Detection for your Amazon S3 buckets identifies and analyzes anomaly events that can indicate a ransomware attack and provides data recovery services on protected resources...","amazon_S3/assigning_protection_amazon_S3_bucket.html@@@Assigning protection for an Amazon S3 bucket@@@Assign a data protection policy to an Amazon S3 bucket...","amazon_S3/aws_managing_glacier_ir_backup.html@@@Managing Glacier Instant Retrieval backup@@@Enable or disable backup support for Amazon S3 objects in the Glacier Instant Retrieval storage class...","amazon_S3/aws_s3_backup_location.html@@@Backup location for Amazon S3@@@The Amazon S3 backup location is an S3 bucket used to store scheduled backups of your source bucket. It supports various storage classes to optimize costs and ensures data immutability with Object Lock and Versioning features...","amazon_S3/aws_s3_recovery.html@@@Amazon S3 recovery@@@You can recover Amazon S3 buckets using the various recovery options that RSC provides...","amazon_S3/creating_tag_rule_for_amazon_s3_buckets.html@@@Creating tag rules for Amazon S3 buckets@@@Create and assign a tag rule to group Amazon S3 buckets and assign SLA Domains to protect S3 buckets and their objects...","amazon_S3/deleting_tag_rule_for_amazon_s3_buckets.html@@@Deleting tag rules for Amazon S3 buckets@@@Delete a tag rule assigned to a group of Amazon S3 buckets associated with your AWS account...","amazon_S3/downloading_report_for_partially_recovered_snapshots.html@@@Downloading a report for partially recovered snapshots@@@Download a report with the list of objects associated with the Amazon S3 bucket that were partially recovered or that could not be recovered because of technical issues. You can download the report and use it for troubleshooting...","amazon_S3/exporting_amazon_s3_bucket_objects.html@@@Exporting an Amazon S3 bucket or its objects@@@Export the S3 bucket to recover a snapshot associated with an entire Amazon S3 bucket or individual objects to an existing S3 bucket...","amazon_S3/ip_planning_eks_cluster_s3.html@@@IP address planning for Exocompute on Amazon S3@@@Based on the number of Amazon S3 buckets you want to protect, the Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service cluster requires additional IP address planning. The number of IP addresses required and the corresponding subnet size are calculated based on your specific environment and workload...","amazon_S3/recovery_amazon_s3_snapshots.html@@@Recover Amazon S3 buckets@@@You can recover your data from a snapshot of an Amazon S3 bucket by using an on-demand or policy-based snapshots. You can take an on-demand snapshot when needed and a policy-based snapshot depending on the policies associated with the SLA Domain assigned to the S3 bucket...","amazon_S3/recovery_report_for_amazon_s3_buckets.html@@@Recovery report for Amazon S3 buckets@@@If the Amazon S3 bucket backup process fails because of technical issues, you can download a report with a list of objects that could not be completely recovered and use the report for troubleshooting...","amazon_S3/required_perm_protect_amazon_s3_resources.html@@@Required permissions for protecting Amazon S3 resources@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires at Read and Write access levels to protect Amazon S3 resources in terms of various use cases...","amazon_S3/restoring_amazon_s3_bucket_object.html@@@Restoring an Amazon S3 bucket or its objects@@@Restore the S3 bucket or the individual objects by using the in-place recovery option when you want to recover an entire Amazon S3 bucket or individual objects to their source location...","amazon_S3/s3_recovery_options.html@@@Recovery options for Amazon S3@@@A comparative overview of the various recovery options for Amazon S3 buckets or its objects...","amazon_S3/s3_retrieving_fqdn_url_maclinx.html@@@Retrieving FQDN with Amazon S3 URL on macOS or Linux@@@Retrieve the necessary IP address to add to the allowlist, using the URL in the Metadata Store DNS column associated with an Amazon S3 account on macOS or Linux...","amazon_S3/s3_retrieving_fqdn_url_windows.html@@@Retrieving FQDN with Amazon S3 URL on Windows OS@@@Retrieve the necessary IP address to add to the allowlist, using the URL in the Metadata Store DNS column associated with an Amazon S3 account on Windows OS...","amazon_S3/searching_file_across_backups_of_s3_bucket.html@@@Searching for a file across the backups of an S3 bucket@@@When you want to search for a specific file for recovery, search across all the backups or within a backup of an Amazon S3 bucket...","amazon_S3/tag_rule_edits_for_amazon_s3_bucket.html@@@Tag rule edits for Amazon S3 buckets@@@After creating a tag rule, if you want to update the protection details related to an Amazon S3 bucket, you can edit the name of the tag rule, associated AWS account, and the SLA Domain...","amazon_S3/taking_ods_amazon_s3_buckets.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Amazon S3 buckets@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, take an on-demand snapshot of Amazon S3 buckets to protect the information that resides in the buckets...","archival/add_amzn_s3_arch_loc_dc_workloads.html@@@Creating Amazon S3 archival locations for data center workloads@@@Add an Amazon S3 archival location for data center workloads in RSC and configure its storage, encryption, and advanced settings...","archival/add_aws_cld_accnt_iam_rbac_dc_arch_loc.html@@@Creating AWS cloud accounts with IAM roles to access data center archival locations@@@Add an AWS cloud account with IAM roles to authenticate access to Amazon S3 archival locations...","archival/adding_aws_cloud_account_ak_dc_arch_loc.html@@@Creating AWS cloud accounts with access keys for data center archival locations@@@To use Amazon S3 for archiving snapshots of data center workloads, add an AWS cloud account for authentication with access keys...","archival/adding_azr_arch_loc_dc_workloads.html@@@Creating Azure archival locations for data center workloads@@@Add an Azure archival location for data center workloads in RSC and configure the settings to enable integration between Azure storage accounts and RSC...","archival/adding_dell_ecs_arch_loc.html@@@Creating a Dell ECS archival location@@@Add the Dell ECS archival location by configuring the settings in RSC. By adding the Dell ECS archival location, you can enable integration between Dell ECS and RSC...","archival/adding_ibm_cos_archival_locations.html@@@Creating IBM COS archival locations@@@Configure IBM Cloud Object Storage (COS) as an archival location in RSC...","archival/adding_netapp_sg_arch_loc.html@@@Creating a NetApp StorageGRID archival location@@@Add the NetApp StorageGRID archival location by configuring the settings and parameters in RSC. By adding the NetApp StorageGRID archival location, you can integrate NetApp StorageGRID and RSC...","archival/adding_ps_flashblade_arch_loc.html@@@Adding a Pure Storage FlashBlade archival location with object-level immutability@@@Add a Pure Storage FlashBlade archival location with object-level immutability for data center workloads to enable integration between Pure Storage FlashBlade and RSC...","archival/adding_qstar_archival_locations.html@@@Creating QStar archival locations@@@Add QStar archival locations on RSC to establish and configure the settings and parameters for integration between the QStar archival location and RSC...","archival/adding_s3_comp_arch_loc_bli.html@@@Creating S3-compatible archival locations with bucket-level immutability@@@Add an Amazon S3-compatible archival location with bucket-level immutability to enable integration between the object storage and RSC...","archival/adding_s3_comp_arch_loc_oli.html@@@Creating S3-compatible archival locations with object-level immutability@@@Add an Amazon S3-compatible archival location with object-level immutability to enable integration between the object storage and RSC...","archival/amazon_s3_arch_loc_immu_storage.html@@@Amazon S3 archival locations with immutable storage@@@Amazon S3 archival locations with immutable storage prevent modification or deletion of archived data. Rubrik CDM 9.3.1 and later use object-level immutability by default. Bucket-level immutability is available only for clusters running earlier CDM versions...","archival/amazon_s3_bucket_level_immu_lck_periods.html@@@Amazon S3 bucket-level immutability lock periods@@@Immutability lock periods for Amazon S3 archival locations with bucket-level immutability...","archival/amazon_s3_comp_arch_loc_bli.html@@@S3-compatible archival locations with bucket-level immutability@@@S3-compatible archival locations on Rubrik clusters running Rubrik CDM versions earlier than 9.4.0-p1 can use bucket-level immutability...","archival/amazon_s3_comp_arch_loc_oli.html@@@S3-compatible archives with object-level immutability@@@RSC provides object-level immutability for S3-compatible archival locations, offering a highly flexible and cost-effective method for securing backups...","archival/amazon_s3_comp_archival_loc.html@@@S3-compatible archival locations@@@RSC supports archival locations compatible with standard S3 APIs, with options for object-level or bucket-level immutability depending on your Rubrik cluster version...","archival/amazon_s3_comp_archival_loc_settings.html@@@S3-compatible archival location settings@@@Information about the settings required for creating an Amazon S3 compatible object store as an archival location without immutability...","archival/arch_adding_gcp_arch_loc.html@@@Creating a GCP archival location for data center workloads@@@Add a Google Cloud Platform (GCP) archival location in RSC to archive data center workloads to a Google Cloud Storage bucket...","archival/arch_adding_nfs_arch_loc.html@@@Creating an NFS archival location for data center workloads@@@Add an NFS archival location in RSC to archive data center workloads to an NFS share...","archival/arch_adding_s3_compatible_arch_loc.html@@@Creating S3-compatible archival locations for data center workloads@@@Add an S3-compatible object store as an archival location in RSC to archive data center workloads to IBM COS, Dell ECS, NetApp StorageGRID, or another S3-compatible provider...","archival/arch_amazon_s3.html@@@Amazon S3 archival locations@@@Rubrik CDM supports Amazon S3 as an archival location. You can use RSC to create an Amazon S3 archival location...","archival/arch_archival_data_encryption.html@@@Archival data encryption@@@The Rubrik cluster supports client-side data encryption for archival storage types, including key-based and password-based mechanisms...","archival/arch_archival_locations_page.html@@@Archival locations@@@The Archival locations page provides summary information about existing archival locations...","archival/arch_archival_reader_repl_coexistence.html@@@Archival reader and replication pair coexistence@@@A Rubrik cluster can serve as both an archival reader (also known as Archival DR) and a replication target for the same workloads, without requiring separate clusters for each function...","archival/arch_archiving_overview.html@@@Archiving overview@@@Archiving copies aged backup data from a Rubrik cluster to cost-efficient, long-term storage, freeing primary cluster capacity while keeping data recoverable for compliance and long-term retention...","archival/arch_azure_access_types.html@@@Access types for Azure archival locations@@@You can configure Azure archival locations with owner access or reader access, depending on whether the connected Rubrik cluster writes archives or only reads them...","archival/arch_azure_cloud_compute_settings.html@@@Azure cloud compute settings@@@Information about the cloud compute settings required for Archival Consolidation during Azure archival location configuration...","archival/arch_azure_encryption_options.html@@@Encryption options for Azure archival locations@@@RSC supports RSA key and Azure Key Vault encryption to protect Azure archival data at rest. Data in transit is always protected by TLS, regardless of the encryption configuration...","archival/arch_azure_immutability_settings.html@@@Azure archival immutability settings for CDM versions earlier than 9.1@@@When you create an Azure archival location for Rubrik clusters running Rubrik CDM versions earlier than 9.1, you can enable the immutability setting for the archival location to protect the archived data from changes for a specified time period...","archival/arch_choosing_archival_location_type.html@@@Choose an archival location type@@@Compare archival location types by their key characteristics to select the option that best fits your workload, compliance requirements, and existing cloud agreements...","archival/arch_cluster_owner_role.html@@@Rubrik cluster owner role@@@Owner Rubrik clusters can pause, disable, and delete archival locations. The actions available on a location vary depending on its current state...","archival/arch_common_archiving_terms.html@@@Common archiving terms@@@A glossary of key terms used in data center archiving documentation for Rubrik Security Cloud...","archival/arch_compare_archival_location_options.html@@@Compare archival location options@@@Use these comparison tables to evaluate archival location options across authentication, immutability, and encryption before you commit to a provider...","archival/arch_compute_proxy_settings.html@@@Compute proxy settings@@@The archival location configuration includes an option for setting proxy server properties to route the API calls for instantiating virtual machines on the archival location through the proxy server...","archival/arch_configure_locations.html@@@Configure archival locations@@@Configure a data center archival location for your chosen storage provider. Each provider has specific preparation steps and configuration requirements...","archival/arch_configuring_nw_throttling.html@@@Configuring archival network throttling and scheduling overrides@@@To free up bandwidth for backup and restore operations on your Rubrik cluster by limiting the bandwidth used by the archiving jobs on the cluster, configure archival network throttling for the Rubrik cluster. You can also configure the system to override archival network throttling threshold during scheduled periods...","archival/arch_connecting_reader_arch_loc.html@@@Connecting a reader to an archival location manually@@@Connect a Rubrik cluster to an archival location as a reader Rubrik cluster for disaster recovery...","archival/arch_connecting_reader_owner_loc.html@@@Connecting reader cluster to archival location using owner cluster@@@Connect a Rubrik cluster to an archival location when the owner cluster is available...","archival/arch_connectivity_troubleshooting.html@@@Connectivity troubleshooting for cloud archival locations@@@You can diagnose and resolve connectivity failures between the Rubrik cluster and cloud archival locations...","archival/arch_cost_considerations_archiving.html@@@Cost considerations for archiving@@@Understand the storage, retrieval, and data egress cost implications of each archival location type before making a provider selection...","archival/arch_create_azure_arch_loc.html@@@Create an Azure archival location@@@After you complete the Azure prerequisites, you can add an Azure archival location in RSC and configure its settings...","archival/arch_create_gcp_arch_loc.html@@@Create a GCP archival location@@@After you complete the GCP prerequisites, you can add a GCP archival location in RSC and configure its settings...","archival/arch_create_nfs_arch_loc.html@@@Create an NFS archival location@@@After you prepare the NFS share, add an NFS archival location in RSC and configure its settings...","archival/arch_create_s3_arch_loc.html@@@Create an Amazon S3 archival location@@@After you complete the Amazon S3 prerequisites, add an Amazon S3 archival location in RSC and configure its settings...","archival/arch_create_s3_compatible_arch_loc.html@@@Create an S3-compatible archival location@@@After you complete the S3-compatible prerequisites, add an S3-compatible archival location in RSC and configure provider-specific settings...","archival/arch_create_tape_arch_loc.html@@@Create a tape archival location@@@You can add a tape archival location in RSC after you prepare the QStar environment by using the QStar Integral Volume path...","archival/arch_dc_arch_loc_details.html@@@Data center archival location details@@@The Data Center Archival Locations page provides information about each archival location associated with the account in the Locations tab. Additionally, you can monitor the archival throughput for all the archival locations from the Performance tab...","archival/arch_dc_archival_location_filters.html@@@Data center archival location filters@@@You can filter archival locations based on various criteria in RSC...","archival/arch_dc_archival_locations.html@@@Data center archival locations@@@RSC supports archiving backed-up data from data center workloads to external storage destinations, including cloud storage providers, NFS shares, S3-compatible object stores, and tape...","archival/arch_dc_creating_an_archival_location.html@@@Creating a data center archival location@@@Create a data center archival location and associate it with a Rubrik cluster for archiving data...","archival/arch_dc_managing_archival_locations.html@@@Manage data center archival locations@@@RSC provides management options to update, pause, disable, delete, or change the ownership of a data center archival location after it has been created...","archival/arch_deleting_archival_location.html@@@Deleting an archival location@@@Delete an archival location to permanently remove it from RSC. The delete operation is irreversible...","archival/arch_disabling_enabling_arch_loc.html@@@Disabling and enabling an archival location@@@Disable an archival location to prevent all archive and background operations, including data lifecycle management tasks...","archival/arch_disaster_recovery_using_arch_loc.html@@@Data recovery using another Rubrik cluster@@@Rubrik CDM supports connecting a different Rubrik cluster to an existing archival location as a reader, enabling data recovery from archived snapshots when the primary cluster is unavailable...","archival/arch_displaying_smart_tiering_azr.html@@@Viewing smart tiering details for Azure workloads@@@Viewing SLA Domains in Storage Tiering in RSC is only possible when they have already been configured in CDM with smart tiering enabled for Azure archival locations. RSC does not support configuring new smart tiering policies for SLA Domains...","archival/arch_editing_archival_location.html@@@Editing an archival location@@@Edit an existing data center archival location to update its configuration settings...","archival/arch_editing_gcp_arch_loc.html@@@Editing GCP archival locations for data center workloads@@@Edit an existing GCP archival location in RSC to update the service account credentials or encryption key...","archival/arch_editing_nfs_arch_loc.html@@@Editing NFS archival locations for data center workloads@@@Edit an existing NFS archival location in RSC to update the NFS server address or destination folder settings...","archival/arch_editing_smart_tiering_azr.html@@@Editing smart tiering for Azure workloads@@@You can modify the minimum retention period for snapshots of SLA Domains configured with smart tiering for Azure workloads. Additionally, you can switch from smart tiering to other storage tiering options...","archival/arch_error_codes.html@@@Common archival error codes and solutions@@@A reference list of common error codes returned by archival jobs in RSC, along with probable causes and recommended solutions...","archival/arch_gcp.html@@@Google Cloud Platform archival locations@@@Rubrik CDM supports Google Cloud Platform as an archival location with four storage classes, regional and multiregional deployments, and enforced immutability...","archival/arch_gcp_advanced_settings.html@@@GCP archival location advanced settings@@@Information about the advanced settings available for GCP archival locations, including proxy, cloud compute, and network throttle configuration...","archival/arch_gcp_archival_location_settings.html@@@GCP archival location settings@@@Information about specific settings required for creating a GCP archival location for a Rubrik cluster...","archival/arch_immutability_compliance_issues.html@@@Immutability and compliance issue resolution@@@You can identify and resolve common immutability configuration issues on archival locations, including lock period conflicts and compliance mode restrictions...","archival/arch_implementation_workflow.html@@@High-level workflow for archiving@@@The archiving workflow consists of six high-level phases, starting from planning to recovery...","archival/arch_instant_tiering_snapshots.html@@@Instant tiering of snapshots@@@The instant tiering feature archives data immediately to the specified cold storage tier in the cloud. This approach is ideal for optimizing storage costs when data restoration is a rare requirement...","archival/arch_intro_to_archiving.html@@@Introduction to archiving@@@Archiving enables you to copy backup data from a Rubrik cluster to a cost-efficient, long-term storage location, freeing up primary cluster capacity while retaining recovery capability...","archival/arch_loc_agent_reqs.html@@@Rubrik data mover and AWS DataSync agent requirements@@@Information about the compute, network, and firewall requirements for deploying the Rubrik data mover and the AWS DataSync agent in your environment...","archival/arch_loc_migration.html@@@Archival location migration@@@You can migrate archived data between storage locations by using a supported data mover. You can manage the migration with support from Rubrik Professional Services...","archival/arch_loc_migration_planning.html@@@Archival location migration planning@@@Planning the migration scope, SLA Domain configurations, tool selection, and sequencing before migrating archival data minimizes disruption and ensures a smooth transition. Effective planning reduces the risk of errors, lowers storage costs from running parallel systems, and ensures that the migration preserves data integrity and meets retention requirements...","archival/arch_loc_migration_prereq.html@@@Prerequisites for archival location migration@@@Before migrating an archival location, ensure that your source location, Rubrik cluster, and SLA Domain configurations meet all the requirements for the selected migration type...","archival/arch_loc_update_sla_archive_tier_migration.html@@@Updating SLA Domains after migrating to RCV Archive tier@@@After migrating an S3-compatible archival location to an RCV Archive tier location, you must update the associated SLA Domains to enable instant tiering to Glacier Deep Archive before re-enabling the location...","archival/arch_manage_azure_arch_loc.html@@@Manage Azure archival locations@@@Manage existing Azure archival locations by connecting reader clusters, promoting readers to owners, and switching access types...","archival/arch_manage_gcp_arch_loc.html@@@Manage GCP archival locations@@@Manage existing GCP archival locations by editing location settings and service account credentials...","archival/arch_manage_nfs_arch_loc.html@@@Manage NFS archival locations@@@Manage existing NFS archival locations by editing location settings...","archival/arch_manage_s3_arch_loc.html@@@Manage Amazon S3 archival locations@@@Manage existing Amazon S3 archival locations by editing location settings and cloud account credentials...","archival/arch_manage_s3_compatible_arch_loc.html@@@Manage S3-compatible archival locations@@@Manage existing S3-compatible archival locations by editing location settings and access credentials...","archival/arch_manage_tape_arch_loc.html@@@Manage tape archival locations@@@Manage existing tape archival locations by editing settings or removing locations that are no longer needed...","archival/arch_migrating_cloud_providers.html@@@Migration between cloud providers@@@When changing cloud providers for archiving, create an archival location with the target provider and update your SLA Domain archival policies to redirect new archives while retaining access to existing archived data...","archival/arch_migration_mobility.html@@@Migrate data center archival locations@@@Manage archival data mobility scenarios including cloud provider migrations, cluster retirements, and moving archives between Rubrik clusters...","archival/arch_migration_overview.html@@@Overview of archival migration scenarios@@@Rubrik supports several archival migration scenarios, with key considerations for migrating archival data between providers or clusters...","archival/arch_monitor_locations.html@@@Monitor data center archival locations@@@RSC provides visibility into the status, storage consumption, throughput, and job activity of your data center archival locations...","archival/arch_monitoring_archival_jobs.html@@@Monitoring archival jobs@@@Monitor archival job status in RSC to verify that workloads are being archived as configured and to identify failures that require attention...","archival/arch_moving_archives_between_clusters.html@@@Moving archives between Rubrik clusters@@@Transfer archival location ownership between Rubrik clusters using the Promote to Owner operation, without moving or copying any archived data...","archival/arch_ms_azure_loc.html@@@Microsoft Azure archival locations@@@Configure Microsoft Azure archival locations for data center workloads. Setting up an Azure archival location involves preparing Azure resources and RSC, creating the archival location, and managing it after creation...","archival/arch_network_connectivity_requirements.html@@@Network and connectivity requirements for archiving@@@You can configure network connectivity settings, throttling, and proxy options to control how archival transfers use your available bandwidth...","archival/arch_nfs.html@@@NFS archival locations@@@An NFS archival location is storage on an NFS server where you can archive snapshots from your Rubrik cluster. You must identify a specific location on the NFS server to serve as the archival location...","archival/arch_nfs_advanced_settings.html@@@NFS archival location advanced settings@@@Information about the advanced settings available for NFS archival locations, including network throttling configuration...","archival/arch_nfs_archival_location_settings.html@@@NFS archival location settings@@@Information about the settings required to create an NFS archival location for a Rubrik cluster...","archival/arch_nfs_encryption.html@@@Encryption for NFS archival locations@@@RSC supports client-side encryption for NFS archival locations to protect archived data at rest on the NFS server...","archival/arch_nw_throttling.html@@@Archival network throttling@@@Archival network throttling limits the bandwidth that a Rubrik cluster uses to archive data, leaving more bandwidth available for backup and recovery operations. You can set a global threshold and configure time-based overrides to increase or decrease the limit for specific periods...","archival/arch_older_cdm_functionality.html@@@Older CDM functionality@@@This section covers archival features available in Rubrik CDM versions earlier than 9.4.0-p1, including bucket-level and container-level immutability for S3 and Azure archival locations...","archival/arch_pausing_resuming_arch_loc.html@@@Pausing and resuming an archival location@@@Pause an archival location to temporarily stop new archive operations while preserving access to existing archived data...","archival/arch_performance_troubleshooting.html@@@Archival performance troubleshooting@@@Information about diagnosing slow archival job performance, including low throughput, high latency, and archival jobs that do not complete within expected windows...","archival/arch_plan_for_disaster_recovery.html@@@Plan recovery from another Rubrik cluster@@@Decide whether to configure reader cluster access to your archival locations to enable recovery when the primary Rubrik cluster is unavailable. Understanding the model, the cluster roles, and the allowed actions before you create archival locations helps you avoid costly redesign later...","archival/arch_planning_prerequisites.html@@@Plan your archiving setup@@@Before creating an archival location, evaluate your storage provider options, cost model, security requirements, and network capacity to ensure a successful deployment...","archival/arch_prepare_azure_arch_loc.html@@@Prepare to archive to Azure@@@Complete the planning decisions and prerequisites required before you create an Azure archival location. This includes choosing immutability and tiering options and preparing the Azure storage account...","archival/arch_prepare_gcp_arch_loc.html@@@Prepare to archive to GCP@@@Complete the planning decisions and prerequisites required before you create a GCP archival location. This includes understanding the automatic object-level immutability behavior, choosing archive tiering options, and configuring the GCP service account and permissions...","archival/arch_prepare_nfs_arch_loc.html@@@Prepare to archive to NFS@@@Complete the planning decisions and prerequisites required before you create an NFS archival location. This includes choosing encryption options and preparing the NFS share and export settings...","archival/arch_prepare_s3_arch_loc.html@@@Prepare to archive to Amazon S3@@@Complete the planning decisions and prerequisites required before you create an Amazon S3 archival location. This includes choosing immutability and tiering options, understanding storage classes and multipart uploads, and creating the AWS cloud account in RSC...","archival/arch_prepare_s3_compatible_arch_loc.html@@@Prepare to archive to S3-compatible storage@@@Complete the planning decisions and prerequisites required before you create an S3-compatible archival location. This includes choosing the immutability model and gathering the required access credentials...","archival/arch_prepare_tape_arch_loc.html@@@Prepare to archive to QStar tape@@@Before you create a QStar tape archival location, set up the QStar Archive Manager, configure QStar Integral Volumes, and ensure the Rubrik cluster can access the Windows server over SMB...","archival/arch_protect_data_archival_locations.html@@@Protect data in archival locations@@@Use SLA Domain archival policies to configure how data center workloads are archived to your archival locations, and monitor archival jobs to ensure data is protected as expected...","archival/arch_proxy_settings.html@@@Archival proxy settings@@@The archival location configuration includes an option for setting proxy server properties to route archival data and requests through the proxy server...","archival/arch_recover_data_archival_locations.html@@@Recover data from archival locations@@@You can recover data from an archival location when the primary Rubrik cluster is unavailable or when archived snapshots are needed for restore operations...","archival/arch_recover_from_cloud_arch_loc.html@@@Recovering data from cloud archival locations@@@Restore workloads from snapshots stored in Azure, Amazon S3, or GCP archival locations using the owner cluster or a connected reader cluster...","archival/arch_recover_from_nfs_arch_loc.html@@@Recovering data from NFS archival locations@@@Restore workloads from snapshots stored in an NFS archival location using the owner Rubrik cluster...","archival/arch_recovery_options.html@@@Recovery options from archival locations@@@Several recovery methods are available for data in archival locations, ranging from single-file restore to full disaster recovery using a reader cluster...","archival/arch_retiring_cluster_with_archived_data.html@@@Cluster retirement with archived data@@@When you decommission a Rubrik cluster that owns archival locations, you must transfer ownership of those locations to a replacement cluster to preserve access to archived data...","archival/arch_s3_archival_location_settings.html@@@Amazon S3 archival location settings@@@Review the settings required to create an Amazon S3 archival location and determine which values can be edited after creation...","archival/arch_s3_cloud_compute_settings.html@@@Amazon S3 cloud compute settings@@@Information about the Amazon S3 cloud compute advanced settings required to launch a transient instance in an AWS Virtual Private Cloud...","archival/arch_s3_compatible_required_permissions.html@@@Required permissions for S3-compatible archival locations@@@The access credentials used by RSC to connect to an S3-compatible object store require specific permissions on the target bucket...","archival/arch_s3_immutability_setting.html@@@Amazon S3 immutability settings@@@The advanced settings configuration of an Amazon S3 archival location includes an option to enable bucket-level immutability. Amazon S3 archival locations created for Rubrik clusters running Rubrik CDM version 9.3.1 and later support object-level immutability, which is always enabled...","archival/arch_s3_obj_level_immutability.html@@@Object-level immutability for Amazon S3@@@Object-level immutability uses Amazon S3 Object Lock in Governance mode to apply Write Once, Read Many (WORM) protection to individual archived objects...","archival/arch_security_compliance_requirements.html@@@Security and compliance requirements for archiving@@@Review encryption and immutability requirements before creating an archival location to ensure your deployment meets organizational and legal standards...","archival/arch_storage_optimization.html@@@Storage optimization@@@You can reduce the storage footprint and cost of your archives by using archival consolidation, archive tiering, and the appropriate storage class for each workload...","archival/arch_tier_existing_snapshots.html@@@Tier existing snapshots@@@You can tier existing snapshots to different AWS and Azure storage tiers to help manage storage costs...","archival/arch_troubleshooting.html@@@Troubleshooting data center archiving issues@@@You can diagnose and resolve common archival issues, including error codes, connectivity failures, performance problems, and immutability compliance issues...","archival/arch_types_of_archival_locations.html@@@Types of archival locations@@@Rubrik Security Cloud supports multiple types of archival locations to accommodate different workloads, access patterns, cost requirements, and security policies...","archival/arch_viewing_arch_loc_page.html@@@Viewing the Archival Locations page@@@View the Archival Locations page to create and manage archival locations. You can also view the details and manage settings for each location...","archival/archive_preparation_in_azure.html@@@Archive preparation in Azure@@@Before archiving data from a Rubrik cluster to Azure, prepare your Azure storage account, storage container, permissions, and Service Principal identities...","archival/archiving_qstar_tape_archive.html@@@QStar tape archive@@@QStar tape archive enables a Rubrik cluster to store data on tape for long-term retention and regulatory compliance using QStar Archive Manager on a Windows server...","archival/aws_archive_tiering.html@@@AWS archive tiering@@@You can use AWS archive tiering to tier data to the Glacier Flexible Retrieval or Glacier Deep Archive storage classes based on an SLA Domain policy...","archival/aws_cold_tier_archival_loc_support.html@@@AWS cold tier support for archival location@@@You can archive backups of supported AWS workloads to Amazon S3 cold storage tiers to significantly reduce long-term storage costs and meet compliance and regulatory retention requirements...","archival/aws_s3_bucket_level_immutability.html@@@Bucket-level immutability for Amazon S3@@@Amazon S3 archival locations on Rubrik clusters running Rubrik CDM versions earlier than 9.3.1 can use bucket-level immutability of Amazon S3 storage...","archival/azr_blob_immutability.html@@@Blob-level immutability for Azure archival locations@@@Azure archival locations created for Rubrik clusters running CDM version 9.1 or later support blob-level immutability by default...","archival/azr_cli.html@@@Container-level immutability for Azure@@@Container-level immutability applies only to archival locations created on Rubrik clusters running Rubrik CDM versions earlier than 9.1...","archival/azr_container_immutability.html@@@Container-level immutability for Azure archival locations@@@Azure archival locations created for Rubrik clusters running Rubrik CDM versions earlier than 9.1 use the container-level immutability feature of Azure storage containers and require manual configuration of immutability settings when creating the archival location in RSC...","archival/azr_immutability_lock_periods.html@@@Immutability lock period for container-level immutability@@@The immutable archival locations on Rubrik clusters running Rubrik CDM versions earlier than 9.1 rely on the container-level immutability feature of Azure for data immutability. In this case, an immutability lock period is required for the archival location, and the period is limited by the retention period of the associated SLA Domain...","archival/azr_immutable_archival_locations.html@@@Azure archival locations with immutable storage@@@Azure archival locations with immutable storage protect data from being modified or deleted from archives. Rubrik CDM 9.1 and later use blob-level immutability by default. Container-level immutability is available only for clusters running CDM versions earlier than 9.1...","archival/azr_lifecycle_management_tiering.html@@@Azure lifecycle management for tiering@@@Information about lifecycle management policy configuration to be completed on the Azure portal when you want to transfer archived data from the Hot or Cool tier to the Cold tier...","archival/azure_archival_location_settings.html@@@Azure archival location settings@@@Information about the settings required for creating an Azure archival location for a Rubrik cluster...","archival/azure_archive_tiering.html@@@Azure Archive tiering options@@@You can configure archive tiering for Azure archival locations to move older data to the Archive tier based on an SLA Domain policy...","archival/azure_cold_tier_support_archival_location.html@@@Azure Cold tier support for archival location@@@When you want to store data for a longer duration and access the data infrequently, you can transfer the archived data from the Hot or Cool access tier to the Cold access tier by using the Azure storage lifecycle management policy. Cold tier movement is not managed by Rubrik. You must configure an Azure lifecycle management policy directly in the Azure portal...","archival/azure_permissions_archival.html@@@Azure permissions for archiving@@@Azure archival locations require two Service Principals with distinct permissions: one for snapshot archival operations and one for cloud compute operations during archival consolidation...","archival/azure_storage_account_access_key.html@@@Azure storage account access keys@@@Accessing archived data in an Azure storage account requires an access key...","archival/azure_storage_account_settings.html@@@Azure storage account settings@@@Configure an Azure storage account with specific settings in the Azure portal before creating an Azure archival location in Rubrik...","archival/create_addnl_aws_iam_roles_dc_arch_loc.html@@@Creating additional AWS IAM roles for data center archival locations@@@For an AWS cloud account in RSC, create different IAM roles corresponding to each data center to isolate access to your Amazon S3 archival locations...","archival/creating_azr_acc_ak_dc_arch_loc.html@@@Creating an access key based Azure cloud account for data center archival locations@@@Create an Azure cloud account in RSC to provide RSC with access-key-based permissions to manage a data center archival location in an Azure storage account...","archival/creating_azr_cloud_accnt_with_oauth_dc_arch_loc.html@@@Creating an Azure cloud account with OAuth for data center archival locations@@@Create an Azure cloud account in RSC using OAuth configuration to provide RSC with Service Principal-based access and permissions to manage a data center archival location in an Azure storage account...","archival/creating_azr_cloud_accnt_without_oauth_dc_arch_loc.html@@@Creating an Azure cloud account without OAuth for data center archival locations@@@Create an Azure cloud account in RSC without an OAuth configuration to provide Rubrik with Service Principal-based access and permissions to manage a data center archival location in an Azure storage account...","archival/delete_aws_cloud_accnt_dc_arch_loc.html@@@Deleting AWS cloud accounts@@@Delete an AWS cloud account when you do not need the cloud account anymore...","archival/delete_aws_iam_role_dc_arch_loc.html@@@Deleting an AWS IAM role for data center archival locations@@@Delete an IAM role in RSC for data center archival locations in Amazon S3 when you do not need the IAM role anymore...","archival/deleting_service_principal_based_azr_cloud_account.html@@@Deleting a service principal-based Azure cloud account@@@You can delete an Azure cloud account configured with the service principal-based authentication method for snapshot archival operations if you do not want RSC to access the Azure subscription specified in the cloud account...","archival/dell_ecs_arch_loc.html@@@Dell ECS archival location@@@RSC supports Dell ECS Object Store as an archival location with bucket-level immutability for archiving encrypted data...","archival/dell_ecs_arch_loc_immutable_storage.html@@@Dell ECS archival location with immutable storage@@@Dell ECS Object Store archival location provides immutable storage for enhanced data protection and compliance...","archival/dell_ecs_arch_loc_settings.html@@@Dell ECS archival location settings@@@Information about the settings available when creating a Dell ECS archival location, and whether each setting can be edited after the location is created...","archival/dell_ecs_immutability_settings.html@@@Dell ECS immutability settings@@@You can enable immutable archive settings for Dell ECS Object Store archival locations...","archival/edit_aws_iam_roles_dc_arch_loc.html@@@Editing AWS IAM roles for data center archival locations@@@Edit the details associated with an IAM role in RSC for data center archival locations in Amazon S3...","archival/edit_azr_svc_principal_cloud_acct.html@@@Editing a service principal-based Azure cloud account@@@You can edit an Azure cloud account without OAuth, configured with the service principal-based authentication method to update the client secret key for snapshot archival operations...","archival/editing_amzn_s3_arch_loc_dc_workloads.html@@@Edit Amazon S3 archival locations for data center workloads@@@Edit the Amazon S3 archival locations for a data center workload to modify archival location information, including archival location name, cloud account, storage class, and other advanced settings...","archival/editing_aws_cloud_account_dc_archl_loc.html@@@Editing AWS accounts for data center archival locations@@@Edit an AWS cloud account in RSC for a data center archival location to modify the account name or access key credentials...","archival/gcp_arch_loc_immu_storage.html@@@GCP archival locations with immutable storage@@@RSC automatically applies object-level immutability to all data archived to GCP buckets on Rubrik clusters running CDM version 9.6.0 or later. No user configuration is required...","archival/iam_permissions_required_for_archiving.html@@@IAM permissions required for archiving@@@The IAM permissions required for archiving depend on the encryption method, archival consolidation status, and CDM version...","archival/ibm_cos_archival_location_settings.html@@@IBM COS archival location settings@@@Information about specific settings required for creating an IBM COS archival location for a Rubrik cluster...","archival/ibm_cos_archival_locations.html@@@IBM COS archival locations@@@RSC supports IBM Cloud Object Storage as an archival location for which you can configure immutability...","archival/ibm_cos_archival_locations_with_immutable_storage.html@@@IBM COS archival locations with immutable storage@@@IBM Cloud Object Storage archival locations provide immutable storage for enhanced data protection and compliance...","archival/ibm_cos_immutability_settings.html@@@IBM COS immutability settings@@@The advanced settings configuration of the IBM Cloud Object Storage archival location that provides an option to enable Immutable Archive...","archival/netapp_sg_arch_loc.html@@@NetApp StorageGRID archival locations@@@RSC supports using NetApp StorageGRID as archival locations for encrypted data. For data stored in NetApp StorageGRID archival locations, Rubrik provides bucket-level immutability...","archival/netapp_sg_arch_loc_immutable_storage.html@@@NetApp StorageGRID archival locations with immutable storage@@@NetApp StorageGRID archival locations provide immutable storage for enhanced data protection and compliance...","archival/netapp_sg_arch_loc_settings.html@@@NetApp StorageGRID archival location settings@@@Information about the settings required for creating and specifying a NetApp StorageGRID archival location where archived data can be stored...","archival/nfs_export_settings.html@@@NFS export settings@@@For an NFS share to be used as a Rubrik archival location, the export point must have specific NFS export settings...","archival/preparing_nfs_share_as_arch_loc.html@@@Preparing to use an NFS share as an archival location@@@You can use an NFS share as an archival location for a Rubrik cluster, but you must first prepare the NFS share settings...","archival/prereq_azr_cld_acnt_without_oauth.html@@@Prerequisites for an Azure cloud account without OAuth@@@Information about the prerequisites before creating an Azure cloud account without OAuth configuration in RSC...","archival/rcv_data_mover_rbac_setup.html@@@Creating a service account for Rubrik data mover credential issuance@@@Create an RSC service account with the Generate data mover credentials permission so that the Rubrik data mover can obtain short-lived AWS credentials during the migration...","archival/rcv_reader_location_info.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault reader location information@@@Information about the Rubrik Cloud Vault archival location settings to create a location on the reader Rubrik cluster...","archival/reader_cluster_arch_location_connections.html@@@Reader cluster and archival location connections@@@Connecting a reader Rubrik cluster to an archival location lets you recover snapshot data from the archival location...","archival/reader_cluster_workload_refresh.html@@@Reader cluster workload refresh@@@Refreshing workloads on the reader Rubrik cluster synchronizes the recovery view of the reader cluster with the contents of the archival location...","archival/reader_cluster_workload_refresh_2.html@@@Reader cluster workload refresh@@@Refreshing workloads on the reader Rubrik cluster synchronizes the recovery view of the reader cluster with the contents of the archival location...","archival/reader_writer_arch_model.html@@@Reader-writer archiving model@@@The reader-writer archival model permits mapping a single owner Rubrik cluster to one or more reader Rubrik clusters. This model increases the availability of archived data for disaster recovery...","archival/resolving_lifecycle_policy_alerts.html@@@Resolving harmful lifecycle policy alerts@@@If RSC detects lifecycle policies configured outside Rubrik on a data center archival location, an alert banner appears on the Data Center Archival Locations page. These policies can cause recovery failures or data loss. Delete the detected policies from your cloud provider account to restore archival operations...","archival/rsc_refreshing_reader_cluster_content.html@@@Refreshing reader clusters@@@Refresh the contents of a reader Rubrik cluster to synchronize its recovery view with the latest data from the archival location...","archival/s3_adding_non_immu_comp_arch_loc.html@@@Adding non-immutable S3-compatible archival locations@@@Add a non-immutable archival location compatible with Amazon S3 in RSC to enable integration between the object storage and RSC...","archival/s3_archive_prep.html@@@Archive preparation in Amazon S3@@@Before creating an Amazon S3 archival location in RSC, prepare your S3 bucket with the correct settings and ensure the AWS IAM user has the required permissions...","archival/s3_compatible_api_operations.html@@@S3 API operations for archiving to S3-compatible object stores@@@Information about the S3 API operations that Rubrik uses when archiving to S3-compatible object storage. The object store account must have permissions to perform these operations...","archival/storage_class.html@@@Storage classes@@@You can choose the storage class depending on the data access, resiliency, and cost requirements of your workload. You can edit the storage class after adding the archival location. The Rubrik cluster applies the new storage class to data archived after the storage class change...","archival/switching_access_types_azr_arch_loc_settings.html@@@Switching access types in Azure archival location settings@@@You can switch the access type to either Service Principal Based or Access Key Based by editing the Azure archival location settings. The specified access type authenticates the Rubrik Security Cloud account for accessing the Azure storage account when creating an archival location...","archival/switching_arch_loc.html@@@Switching archival locations managed by a Rubrik cluster@@@Switch archival locations managed by a Rubrik cluster to RSC for centralized management and improved control of archived data...","archival/update_perm_aws_iam_roles_dc_arch_loc.html@@@Updating permissions of AWS IAM roles for data center archival locations@@@Update IAM roles for a data center archival location in AWS when a missing permission status appears for IAM roles in the RSC AWS cloud account page...","archival/updating_aws_account_permissions_lifecycle_policy.html@@@Updating AWS cloud account permissions for lifecycle policy detection@@@If an AWS cloud account does not have the permissions required for lifecycle policy detection, update the account to grant RSC access to scan the account for harmful lifecycle policies...","archival/updating_azure_account_permissions_lifecycle_policy.html@@@Updating Azure cloud account permissions for lifecycle policy detection@@@If an Azure cloud account does not have the permissions required for lifecycle policy detection, update the account to grant RSC access to scan the account for harmful lifecycle policies...","archival/upload_downloaded_snapshots.html@@@Upload of downloaded snapshots to archival locations@@@Rubrik can upload a snapshot that was previously downloaded from an archival location or a replication target to a different archival location. Normally, Rubrik does not re-archive a downloaded snapshot. With this capability, you can upload it on demand by using a separate SLA Domain that you specify...","archival/verifying_cloud_compute_connectivity.html@@@Verifying cloud compute connectivity@@@Use the cloud compute connectivity check in RSC to verify connectivity between cloud compute instances, a Rubrik cluster, and AWS or Azure cloud storage services for deployments using Archival Consolidation, or Smart Tiering for applicable deployments...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_access_reports.html@@@Manage reports for AWS cloud applications@@@You can create and manage reports in RSC to review protection compliance, recovery readiness, and operational status for your AWS cloud applications...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_add_cloud_app.html@@@Add AWS cloud application to RSC@@@Add your AWS cloud account to RSC, configure a recovery account, and create a cloud application by specifying tags or by manually selecting your AWS resources...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_add_indv_aws_acc_using_cft_protect.html@@@Adding an AWS account using CFT for protection@@@To protect the AWS resources within an individual AWS account, add the account to RSC by specifying the account name and account ID and using the AWS CloudFormation template...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_adding_aws_account_manually_for_protection.html@@@Adding an AWS account manually for protection@@@To protect the AWS resources within an AWS account, add your account in RSC manually by creating the required roles in the AWS Management Console and providing the role ARNs in RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_adding_cloud_apps.html@@@Adding a cloud application for Autonomous Business Recovery@@@Add a cloud application in RSC by specifying application details, defining the application objects by tag, by manual selection, or both, and reviewing the discovered resources...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_assigning_config_sla.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to AWS cloud application@@@Assign a cloud application SLA Domain to an AWS cloud application to protect configuration resource metadata and workloads in RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_aws_adding_acc_using_org_protection.html@@@Adding AWS accounts using AWS Organization for protection@@@Add multiple AWS accounts using an AWS Organization for protection...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_aws_cloud_account_addition.html@@@AWS cloud account addition for Autonomous Business Recovery@@@You can add your source AWS cloud account to RSC with the Cloud Applications feature enabled...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_aws_cloud_applications.html@@@Autonomous Business Recovery for Cloud Applications@@@RSC provides Autonomous Business Recovery for Cloud Applications (ABR) to protect and recover complete AWS cloud applications, including workloads such as EC2 instances, RDS databases, and S3 buckets, along with the configuration resources that define your application infrastructure...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_aws_creating_inst_prof_iam_role_console.html@@@Creating instance profiles for IAM roles using AWS console@@@Create an instance profile for an Exocompute EKS worker node role using AWS Management Console...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_aws_creating_inst_prof_iam_roles_cli.html@@@Creating instance profiles for IAM roles using CLI@@@Create an instance profile for an Exocompute EKS worker node role using the CLI...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_aws_role_customization_fields.html@@@AWS role customization fields@@@Information about the role names and paths you must specify to use the AWS role customization option...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_best_practices_sla_assign.html@@@Best practices for SLA assignment in AWS cloud applications@@@Follow these best practices when assigning SLA Domains to AWS cloud applications and their workloads in RSC to ensure that the application reaches and maintains Fully Protected status...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_cloud_accounts_application.html@@@Configure AWS cloud accounts and application@@@Configure the source and recovery AWS cloud accounts and create a cloud application in RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_cloud_app_details.html@@@AWS cloud application details@@@Information available on the AWS cloud application details page in RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_cloud_apps_overview.html@@@Autonomous Business Recovery for Cloud Applications overview@@@Autonomous Business Recovery for Cloud Applications protects an AWS cloud application as a single unit by capturing both its configuration resources and its workloads, so that you can recover the entire application stack together...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_common_protection_terms.html@@@Common terms for Autonomous Business Recovery@@@It is important to understand some common terms associated with Autonomous Business Recovery when protecting AWS cloud applications with RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_configure_protection.html@@@Configure protection for AWS cloud applications@@@Create and assign SLA Domains for the configuration resources and workloads in your AWS cloud application using RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_configure_recovery_account.html@@@Adding a recovery account for Autonomous Business Recovery@@@Add a separate AWS account as the recovery account for cyber recovery of your cloud applications in RSC using Autonomous Business Recovery...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_configuring_vpc_networking.html@@@VPC networking configuration for AWS cloud application recovery@@@Information about the VPC networking options available in the recovery account when recovering an AWS cloud application in RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_creating_custom_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for AWS cloud application@@@Create a custom role with Role-based Access Control privileges for managing your AWS cloud applications. These privileges provide finer granularity for determining which permissions an RSC user has for performing specific actions on specific objects...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_creating_reports.html@@@Creating a report for AWS cloud applications@@@Create a custom report for AWS cloud applications in RSC to review protection and recovery metrics...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_creating_sla_domain.html@@@Creating an SLA Domain for AWS cloud applications@@@Create an SLA Domain for AWS cloud applications using the Manage Protection wizard in Cloud Applications...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_deleting_feature.html@@@Deleting an AWS cloud application@@@Delete Cloud Applications from an AWS account...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_downloading_snapshot_data.html@@@Downloading snapshot data for an AWS cloud application@@@Download configuration resource metadata from an AWS cloud application snapshot in RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_edit_cloud_app.html@@@Editing an AWS cloud application@@@Edit the configuration of an existing AWS cloud application in RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_event_log_details.html@@@Event log details for AWS cloud applications@@@The Event Logs page displays the events occurring for AWS cloud applications across all AWS cloud accounts, shown in the local time zone...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_high_level_arch.html@@@High-level architecture for Autonomous Business Recovery@@@A high-level architectural overview about how RSC protects and recovers AWS cloud applications, including configuration resources and workloads...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_key_features.html@@@Key features for Autonomous Business Recovery for Cloud Applications@@@RSC provides application-level protection, automated resource discovery, comprehensive cyber recovery, and centralized management to protect your AWS cloud applications...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_limitations.html@@@Autonomous Business Recovery limitations@@@Information about the known limitations that apply to Autonomous Business Recovery for Cloud Applications, that is, protection and recovery of AWS cloud application with RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_manage_cloud_apps.html@@@Manage AWS cloud application data@@@Monitor and manage your AWS cloud applications in RSC, including viewing inventory, refreshing applications, reviewing snapshots, and monitoring events...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_managing_recovery_errors.html@@@Manage recovery errors for AWS cloud applications@@@Understand details regarding handling errors that occur during AWS cloud application recovery in RSC, including selecting the right error handling mode, responding to non-critical and critical errors, finalizing the recovery, and downloading the recovery report...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_on_demand_snapshot.html@@@Taking an on-demand AWS configuration snapshot of a cloud application@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of the AWS configuration resources of a cloud application in RSC and assign the SLA Domain that governs its retention...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_permission_categories.html@@@Permission categories for Autonomous Business Recovery@@@RSC uses two AWS IAM permission categories, Basic and Recovery, to control access to AWS cloud application discovery, protection, and recovery operations...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_plan_protection.html@@@Plan for Autonomous Business Recovery for Cloud Applications@@@Before deploying Autonomous Business Recovery for Cloud Applications in RSC, plan the user and access management for RSC users who will manage cloud applications. Planning also involves reviewing the permissions, supported resource types, and limitations of Autonomous Business Recovery...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_pre_post_recovery_actions.html@@@Pre-recovery and post-recovery actions for AWS cloud applications@@@You can configure automated actions that RSC runs before, during, and after an AWS cloud application recovery to customize the recovery workflow, validate the recovered environment, and update dependent systems...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_quick_start_aws_cloud_apps.html@@@Quick start with Autonomous Business Recovery for Cloud Applications@@@You can follow this quick start to complete an end-to-end workflow for protecting and recovering a single AWS cloud application with Autonomous Business Recovery for Cloud Applications...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_recommendations_add_cloud_app.html@@@Recommendations for adding AWS cloud applications@@@Rubrik recommends specific actions and best practices when adding AWS cloud applications to RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_recover.html@@@Recover an AWS cloud application@@@Recover your AWS cloud application to a separate recovery AWS cloud account by using RSC to restore the workloads and configuration resources from a selected recovery point...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_recovering_cloud_app.html@@@Recovering an AWS cloud application to a recovery account@@@Recover an AWS cloud application to a recovery AWS account by using the recovery wizard in RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_recovery_point_selection.html@@@Recovery point selection for AWS cloud application@@@Information about the recovery point selection options available when recovering an AWS cloud application in RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_refreshing_cloud_app.html@@@Refreshing an AWS cloud application@@@Refresh an AWS cloud application in RSC to discover new or changed resources in your AWS environment...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_req_rsc_perms.html@@@RSC user permissions for AWS cloud application@@@Information about the Role-based Access Control permissions that an RSC user requires to view, manage, protect, and recover AWS cloud applications...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_rsc_communication.html@@@Communication between RSC and AWS for cloud application protection@@@An overview of how RSC communicates with your AWS environment to discover, protect, and recover cloud application resources...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_set_up_protection.html@@@Set up protection for AWS cloud applications@@@Configure SLA Domains to protect the configuration resources and workloads in your AWS cloud application using RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_sla_assignment_hierarchy.html@@@SLA Domain assignment hierarchy for AWS cloud applications@@@RSC uses a two-layer SLA Domain assignment model for AWS cloud applications, with separate SLA Domains for the cloud application and for each workload in the application...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_supported_resource_types_aws_cloud_app.html@@@Supported resource types for AWS cloud applications@@@Information about the AWS resource types that RSC supports for cloud application protection and recovery...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_tag_based_discovery.html@@@Tag-based resource discovery for cloud applications@@@RSC uses tags on EC2 instances, RDS databases, and load balancers to identify the resources belonging to a cloud application, and then runs auto-discovery to map all connected configuration resources into the complete application topology...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_understanding_protection_status.html@@@Protection status details for AWS cloud applications@@@Information about the protection status indicators for AWS cloud applications in RSC. You can use these indicators to set the target before assigning SLA Domains, verify that the assignments produce full protection, and monitor cloud applications on an ongoing basis to identify and remediate gaps in coverage...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_user_management_aws_cloud_app.html@@@User management for AWS cloud application@@@You must set up user roles and access permissions for Autonomous Business Recovery in RSC to manage the protection and recovery of AWS cloud applications...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_viewing_events.html@@@Viewing events for an AWS cloud application@@@View the event logs and activity history for your AWS cloud application in RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_viewing_inventory.html@@@Viewing AWS cloud application inventory@@@View all cloud applications and their protection status in RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_viewing_recovery_status.html@@@Viewing recovery status and history for AWS cloud applications@@@Monitor the progress and status of an AWS cloud application recovery operation and review historical recoveries in RSC...","autonomous_business_recovery/abr_viewing_snapshots.html@@@Viewing snapshots of an AWS cloud application@@@View the available snapshots for your AWS cloud application in RSC, organized by workload type...","autonomous_business_recovery/aws_car_recovery_prerequisites.html@@@AWS cloud applications recovery prerequisites@@@You must fulfill specific prerequisites in RSC and in the AWS Management Console before recovering a cloud application, so that the recovery operation does not fail because of a missing permission, key, certificate, or external resource in the recovery account...","autonomous_business_recovery/cloud_app_aws_iam_permissions.html@@@Required RSC permissions for AWS cloud application@@@Information about the specific AWS permissions that RSC requires for discovery, backup, and recovery of AWS cloud applications...","aws/aws_glue_tables.html@@@Manage AWS Glue Iceberg Tables@@@RSC protects Iceberg tables registered in your AWS Glue catalog with automated snapshots configured in SLA Domain policies. You can view inventory details, manage protection assignments, and recover Iceberg tables from the AWS Glue Iceberg Tables inventory page...","aws/aws_glue_tables_acc_management.html@@@AWS Glue Iceberg Tables management@@@Using RSC, you can monitor and manage the details of your AWS Glue Iceberg Tables. You can view Glue catalog details, database and table inventory, and snapshot information for your protected Iceberg tables...","aws/aws_glue_tables_assigning_protection.html@@@Assigning protection to AWS Glue Iceberg Tables@@@Assign a data protection policy to specific AWS Glue Iceberg Tables, databases, or AWS accounts to protect your Iceberg data...","aws/aws_glue_tables_details.html@@@AWS Glue Iceberg Tables details@@@The AWS Glue Iceberg Tables details page provides information about the protection status, attributes, snapshot calendar, and events log for a selected Iceberg table...","aws/aws_glue_tables_protection_mechanism.html@@@Cloud-native protection for AWS Glue Iceberg Tables@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects AWS Glue Iceberg Tables in an AWS account...","aws/aws_glue_tables_recovery.html@@@AWS Glue Iceberg Tables recovery@@@You can recover AWS Glue Iceberg Tables using the various recovery options provided by RSC...","aws/aws_glue_tables_recovery_options.html@@@Recovery options for AWS Glue Iceberg Tables@@@RSC provides recovery options for AWS Glue Iceberg Tables. You can use in-place recovery to a named branch and export recovery to a new or existing Iceberg table...","aws/aws_glue_tables_req_permissions.html@@@Required permissions for AWS Glue Iceberg Tables@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to discover, protect, and recover AWS Glue Iceberg Tables in your AWS account...","aws/aws_glue_tables_snapshot_info_list.html@@@AWS Glue Iceberg Tables snapshot information list@@@The Snapshots tab displays information about the snapshots for a selected AWS Glue Iceberg Table...","aws/aws_glue_tables_taking_ods.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of an AWS Glue Table@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, take an on-demand snapshot of an AWS Glue Table to capture the current state of your Iceberg data...","aws/aws_glue_tables_viewing_accounts_page.html@@@Viewing the AWS Glue Iceberg Tables inventory page@@@Access the AWS Glue Iceberg Tables inventory page to view the Glue catalogs, databases, and Iceberg tables discovered in your AWS accounts...","aws/aws_glue_tables_viewing_inv_page.html@@@Viewing AWS Glue Iceberg Table details@@@View the details page for a specific Iceberg table to check its protection status, snapshot history, and associated attributes...","aws/aws_iceberg_creating_sla_domain.html@@@Creating an SLA Domain for Iceberg tables@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to define snapshot frequency, retention, and backup policies for your AWS Glue Tables and AWS S3 Tables Iceberg workloads...","aws/aws_rds_archival_resource_lifecycle.html@@@Amazon RDS archival cost and resource lifecycle@@@RSC creates temporary AWS resources each time RSC archives an Amazon RDS database. Understanding what is created, when it is removed, and what drives cost helps plan and monitor archival spend...","aws/aws_rds_archiving_prereq_exo.html@@@Prerequisites for archiving Amazon RDS using Exocompute@@@When archiving Amazon RDS databases using a central Exocompute configuration, certain resources must exist in the Exocompute account before archiving can succeed...","aws/aws_rds_protection_removal.html@@@Amazon RDS protection removal@@@When you remove an SLA Domain from an Amazon RDS database or a cloud account from RSC, certain AWS resources and configurations persist. Review this behavior before removing protection...","aws/aws_rds_reporting_fields.html@@@Amazon RDS reporting fields@@@RSC derives capacity and identity fields for Amazon RDS databases from AWS API data. Some field values differ from what the AWS Management console displays. You must review these definitions to interpret reporting data correctly...","aws/aws_s3_tables.html@@@Manage AWS S3 Tables@@@RSC protects Iceberg tables stored in your AWS S3 table buckets with automated snapshots configured in your SLA Domain policies. You can view inventory details, manage protection assignments, and recover Iceberg tables from the AWS S3 Tables inventory page...","aws/aws_s3_tables_acc_management.html@@@AWS S3 Tables management@@@You can monitor and manage the details of your AWS S3 Tables in RSC.You can view S3 table bucket details, namespace, and snapshot information for your Iceberg tables...","aws/aws_s3_tables_assigning_protection.html@@@Assigning protection to AWS S3 Tables@@@Assign a data protection policy to specific AWS S3 Tables, namespaces, or AWS accounts to protect your Iceberg data...","aws/aws_s3_tables_details.html@@@AWS S3 Tables details@@@The AWS S3 Tables details page provides information about the protection status, attributes, snapshot calendar, and events log for a selected Iceberg table...","aws/aws_s3_tables_protection_mechanism.html@@@Cloud-native protection for AWS S3 Tables@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects AWS S3 Tables in an AWS account...","aws/aws_s3_tables_recovery.html@@@AWS S3 Tables recovery@@@You can recover AWS S3 Tables using the various recovery options provided by RSC...","aws/aws_s3_tables_recovery_options.html@@@Recovery options for AWS S3 Tables@@@RSC provides different recovery options for AWS S3 Tables. You can perform an in-place recovery to a named branch, or an export recovery to a new or existing Iceberg table...","aws/aws_s3_tables_req_permissions.html@@@Required permissions for AWS S3 Tables@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to discover, protect, and recover AWS S3 Tables in your AWS account...","aws/aws_s3_tables_snapshot_info_list.html@@@AWS S3 Tables snapshot information list@@@The Snapshots tab displays information about the snapshots for a selected AWS S3 Table...","aws/aws_s3_tables_taking_ods.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of an AWS S3 Table@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, take an on-demand snapshot of an AWS S3 Table to capture the current state of your Iceberg data...","aws/aws_s3_tables_viewing_details_page.html@@@Viewing AWS S3 Table details@@@View the details page for a specific Iceberg table to check its protection status, snapshot history, and associated attributes...","aws/aws_s3_tables_viewing_inventory.html@@@Viewing the AWS S3 Tables inventory page@@@Access the AWS S3 Tables inventory page to view the S3 table buckets, namespaces, and Iceberg tables discovered in your AWS accounts...","aws/exporting_aws_glue_table.html@@@Exporting an AWS Glue Iceberg Table to a different location@@@Export a recovered AWS Glue Iceberg Table to a new or existing Iceberg table in the same or a different AWS account, region, or catalog type...","aws/exporting_aws_s3_table.html@@@Exporting an AWS S3 Table to a different location@@@Export a recovered AWS S3 Table to a new or existing Iceberg table in the same or a different AWS account, region, or catalog type...","aws/recovering_aws_s3_table.html@@@Recovering an AWS S3 Table in-place@@@Recover an AWS S3 Table to its original location by restoring data to a named Iceberg branch...","aws/recovering_glue_table_inplace.html@@@Recovering an AWS Glue Iceberg Table in-place@@@Recover an AWS Glue Iceberg Table to its original location by restoring data to a named Iceberg branch...","azure_blob/accessing_azr_blob_inventory_page.html@@@Accessing the Azure Blob Storage inventory page@@@Access the Azure Blob Storage inventory page to manage Azure Blob Storage accounts, create tag-based rules, view resource groups, and manage subscriptions. Also, you can take on-demand snapshot of Azure Blob Storage from the inventory page and recover the Azure Blob Storage accounts...","azure_blob/anomaly_detection_azure_blob_storage.html@@@Anomaly Detection for Azure Blob Storage@@@Anomaly Detection for the Azure Blob Storage accounts identifies and analyzes anomaly events that can indicate a ransomware attack and provides data recovery services for the protected resources...","azure_blob/assigning_protection_azr_blob_storage.html@@@Assigning protection to Azure Blob Storage@@@Assign a data protection policy to an Azure Blob Storage account...","azure_blob/azr_blb_strg_retrieving_fqdn_url_maclinx.html@@@Retrieving FQDN with Azure Blob storage URL on macOS or Linux@@@Retrieve the necessary IP address to add to the allowlist, using the URL in the Metadata Store DNS column associated with an Azure Blob storage account on macOS or Linux...","azure_blob/azr_blb_strg_retrieving_fqdn_url_maclinx_2.html@@@Retrieving FQDN with Azure Blob storage URL on macOS or Linux@@@Retrieve the necessary IP address to add to the allowlist, using the URL in the Metadata Store DNS column associated with an Azure Blob storage account on macOS or Linux...","azure_blob/azr_blb_strg_retrieving_fqdn_url_windows.html@@@Retrieving FQDN with Azure Blob storage URL on Windows OS@@@Retrieve the necessary IP address to add to the allowlist, using the URL in the Metadata Store DNS column associated with an Azure Blob storage account on Windows OS...","azure_blob/azr_blb_strg_retrieving_fqdn_url_windows_2.html@@@Retrieving FQDN with Azure Blob storage URL on Windows OS@@@Retrieve the necessary IP address to add to the allowlist, using the URL in the Metadata Store DNS column associated with an Azure Blob storage account on Windows OS...","azure_blob/azr_blob_excluding_protection_container.html@@@Excluding protection for specific Azure containers@@@Exclude specific Azure containers while protecting other containers in an Azure Blob Storage account. This is useful for managing storage resources efficiently when certain containers do not require backup...","azure_blob/azr_blob_inventory_management.html@@@Azure Blob Storage inventory management@@@For Azure Blob Storage accounts, you can perform the inventory management tasks, such as managing protection policies, taking on-demand snapshots, creating tag-based rules, and performing recovery operations...","azure_blob/azr_blob_outbound_rules_nsg.html@@@Outbound rules for network security group of Azure Blob Storage@@@Information about the minimal set of outbound rules required to configure on the network security group associated with the subnet used for the Azure Kubernetes Service cluster associated with the Azure Blob Storage...","azure_blob/azr_blob_prioritized_recovery_storage.html@@@Prioritized recovery for Azure Blob storage@@@You can prioritize the recovery of specific Azure Blobs using glob patterns to recover your most critical data first. You can also use glob patterns to selectively recover specific blobs from your Azure Blob storage account...","azure_blob/azr_blob_recovery_report.html@@@Recovery report for Azure Blob Storage@@@If the backup process for an Azure Blob Storage account fails because of technical issues, you can download a report with a list of objects that could not be completely recovered and use the report for troubleshooting...","azure_blob/azr_blob_storage_recovery.html@@@Azure Blob Storage recovery@@@You can recover Azure Blob Storage using the various recovery options that RSC provides...","azure_blob/azr_blob_subscription_info.html@@@Azure Blob Storage subscription information@@@Information about Azure Blob Storage subscriptions. RSC periodically refreshes Azure subscription information...","azure_blob/azr_manage_blob_storage.html@@@Manage Azure Blob Storage@@@By using the protection services offered by RSC, you can protect and recover your objects in Azure Blob Storage...","azure_blob/configuring_azr_pe_blob.html@@@Configuring an Azure private endpoint for Azure Blob Storage@@@To ensure secure access to your Azure Blob Storage account, before assigning an SLA Domain or initiating on-demand snapshots, configure an Azure private endpoint. This setup restricts access to your storage account to a specific virtual network, providing enhanced security and network isolation...","azure_blob/configuring_azr_se_blob.html@@@Configuring an Azure service endpoint for Azure Blob Storage@@@Configure an Azure service endpoint for an Azure Blob Storage account to ensure secure connectivity through selected VNets and subnets. With this configuration, Exocompute instances can access the storage account while maintaining network security and isolation...","azure_blob/creating_tag_rule_azr_blob.html@@@Creating a tag rule for Azure Blob storage@@@Create a tag rule to group the Azure Blob Storage accounts and assign an SLA Domain to protect the accounts and their objects...","azure_blob/deleting_azr_blob_snapshot.html@@@Deleting a snapshot from Azure Blob Storage@@@Delete a snapshot from an Azure Blob Storage account that has a retention policy of Forever...","azure_blob/downloading_report_partial_recovered_snapshot.html@@@Downloading a report for partially recovered snapshots@@@Download a report with the list of objects associated with the Azure blob snapshot that were partially recovered or that could not be recovered because of technical issues. You can download the report and use it for troubleshooting...","azure_blob/enabling_ad_azure_blob_storage_accnts.html@@@Enabling Anomaly Detection for Azure Blob Storage accounts@@@Enable Anomaly Detection for an Azure Blob storage account to perform behavioral and content analysis on the Azure Blob Storage account and show details about potentially anomalous incidents. Enabling Anomaly Detection for an Azure Blob Storage account helps protect the data in the account from ransomware attacks...","azure_blob/feature_support_azr_blob.html@@@Feature support in Azure Blob Storage@@@Information about the features that are supported and not supported in Azure Blob Storage...","azure_blob/prereq_immutable_azr_blob_backup.html@@@Prerequisites for immutable Azure Blob Storage backups@@@Information about specific prerequisites that you must meet to create and manage immutable backups of Azure Blob Storage in RSC. These prerequisites are based on the network access configuration of your Azure Blob Storage account...","azure_blob/recover_azr_blob_storage.html@@@Recover Azure Blob Storage@@@After RSC takes snapshots, you can recover the Azure Blob Storage account or individual blobs in the account...","azure_blob/recovery_options_azr_blob_storage.html@@@Recovery options for Azure Blob Storage@@@A comparative overview of the various recovery options for Azure Blob Storage...","azure_blob/refreshing_azr_blob_subscription.html@@@Refreshing an Azure Blob Storage subscription@@@Refresh an Azure Blob Storage subscription as an on-demand task...","azure_blob/req_permissions_azr_blob_protection.html@@@Required permissions for protecting Azure Blob Storage@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to protect your Azure Blob Storage...","azure_blob/restoring_entire_azr_blob.html@@@Restoring an entire Azure Blob Storage@@@Restore an entire Azure Blob Storage account in disaster situations to ensure data integrity...","azure_blob/restoring_indvidual_azr_blob_snapshot.html@@@Restoring an individual Azure blob from a snapshot@@@When you want to recover an Azure blob to an alternative storage location or overwrite an Azure blob with a blob selected from a snapshot, restore an individual Azure blob from a snapshot...","azure_blob/searching_azr_blob_account.html@@@Searching for an Azure Blob Storage account@@@If you know the name of an Azure Blob Storage account, instead of scrolling through a list of accounts to select a specific one, search for an Azure Blob Storage account by its name...","azure_blob/searching_file_azr_blob_backup.html@@@Searching for a file across the backups of Azure Blob Storage@@@When you want to search for a specific file, search across all the backups or within a backup of an Azure Blob Storage account...","azure_blob/tag_rule_edits_azr_blob.html@@@Tag rule edits for Azure Blob storage@@@After creating a tag rule, if you want to update the protection details related to an Azure Blob Storage account, you can edit the name of the tag rule, the associated Azure account, and the SLA Domain...","azure_blob/taking_ods_azr_blob.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Azure Blob Storage@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of the Azure Blob Storage account...","azure_devops/azr_devops.html@@@Azure DevOps@@@RSC protects the data and resources of Azure DevOps projects, repositories, and Developer Collaboration tools within the Azure DevOps organization...","azure_devops/azr_devops_access_reports.html@@@Access Azure DevOps reports@@@With RSC, you can create and download reports based on templates to monitor the protection status of your Azure DevOps organizations, projects, and repositories...","azure_devops/azr_devops_add_orgs.html@@@Add Azure DevOps organizations to RSC@@@Adding Azure DevOps organizations to RSC involves completing prerequisite planning tasks and choosing an onboarding method that fits the authentication model and infrastructure requirements of your organization...","azure_devops/azr_devops_assigning_protection.html@@@Assigning protection to Azure DevOps@@@Assign a data protection policy to specific Azure DevOps organization, projects, or repositories...","azure_devops/azr_devops_best_practices_sla_assign.html@@@Best practices for Azure DevOps SLA Domain assignment@@@Information about the best practices for assigning SLA Domains to Azure DevOps organizations, ensuring effective data protection and compliance...","azure_devops/azr_devops_common_protection_terms.html@@@Common protection terms for Azure DevOps@@@It is important to understand some common terms when protecting an Azure DevOps organization with RSC...","azure_devops/azr_devops_configure_backup_loc.html@@@Configure Azure DevOps backup location@@@You must create a backup location for storing the snapshots of Azure DevOps organizations, projects, and repositories. Additionally, you can configure a private or service endpoint to back up snapshots to the backup location...","azure_devops/azr_devops_configure_protection.html@@@Configure Azure DevOps protection@@@After you have decided on the protection policies you want to configure, you can begin the protection setup by creating an SLA Domain and assigning protection to Azure DevOps organizations, projects, and repositories...","azure_devops/azr_devops_configuring_azr_pvt_endpoint.html@@@Configuring an Azure private endpoint for Azure DevOps@@@To back up snapshots to an archival location with a region-specific setting, configure an Azure private endpoint...","azure_devops/azr_devops_creating_archival_locations.html@@@Creating archival locations for Azure DevOps@@@Create an archival location for the Azure storage account created for storing the snapshots of Azure DevOps organizations, projects, and repositories...","azure_devops/azr_devops_creating_custom_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for Azure DevOps@@@Create a custom role with Role-based Access Control privileges for managing your Azure DevOps organization. These privileges provide finer granularity for determining which permissions an RSC user has for performing specific actions on specific objects...","azure_devops/azr_devops_creating_custom_sla_domain.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain for Azure DevOps@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to streamline and customize the Azure DevOps organization protection and management policies...","azure_devops/azr_devops_creating_reports.html@@@Creating reports for Azure DevOps@@@Create reports for the Azure DevOps organization to view information such as compliance status and protection status using the available templates. You can use the information generated in the reports to perform audits and data management planning...","azure_devops/azr_devops_dev_collab_recovery_details.html@@@Developer Collaboration recovery details@@@Information about the Developer Collaboration resources that RSC recovers when you recover an Azure DevOps project...","azure_devops/azr_devops_evaluate_backup_options.html@@@Evaluate backup options for Azure DevOps@@@It is important to evaluate the backup options for Azure DevOps to align with the performance and data retrieval needs. Key considerations include backup location, access tiers, endpoint usage, and encryption standards...","azure_devops/azr_devops_evaluate_protection_options.html@@@Evaluate Azure DevOps protection options@@@Understanding the various protection options is important when creating an SLA Domain for your Azure DevOps organization. This ensures alignment with organizational needs. Thoroughly evaluating these options enables making informed decisions and providing effective protection for the workloads...","azure_devops/azr_devops_evaluate_recovery_options.html@@@Evaluate Azure DevOps recovery options@@@RSC provides two options for recovering Azure DevOps repositories: individual repository recovery and project-level bulk recovery. Compare these options to choose the approach that best fits the scope and requirements of your recovery scenario...","azure_devops/azr_devops_evaluate_setup_options.html@@@Evaluate Azure DevOps setup options@@@RSC provides three methods for adding Azure DevOps organizations: Configure with OAuth, Configure without OAuth, and Rubrik-hosted Exocompute. Compare these methods to choose the approach that best fits the authentication requirements of your organization, infrastructure model, and onboarding scale...","azure_devops/azr_devops_event_log_details.html@@@Event log details for Azure DevOps@@@The Events page displays the events occurring in all Azure DevOps organizations, shown in the local time zone...","azure_devops/azr_devops_granting_basic_access.html@@@Granting Basic access level in Azure DevOps@@@Grant Basic access level to a user in an Azure DevOps organization to enable onboarding and protection operations with RSC...","azure_devops/azr_devops_high_level_arch_protection.html@@@High-level architecture for Azure DevOps protection@@@A high-level architectural overview about how RSC protects the Azure DevOps projects and repositories within your Azure DevOps organization...","azure_devops/azr_devops_high_level_implement_workflow.html@@@High-level implementation workflow for Azure DevOps@@@The Azure DevOps protection implementation workflow involves a structured approach to secure data management, starting with planning and preparation, followed by Azure DevOps organization setup, Azure DevOps protection, continuous management and optimization, and repository recovery...","azure_devops/azr_devops_indv_vs_prj_recv.html@@@Azure DevOps individual versus project-level bulk recovery@@@A comparative overview of individual repository recovery and project-level bulk recovery for Azure DevOps...","azure_devops/azr_devops_limitations.html@@@Limitations for Azure DevOps protection@@@Review the known limitations for Azure DevOps backup and recovery before configuring protection for your organization...","azure_devops/azr_devops_manage_organizations.html@@@Manage Azure DevOps organizations@@@After completing the protection setup for Azure DevOps organizations, projects, and repos, RSC takes automated snapshots of those repos based on the configured policies in SLA Domains. You can also take on-demand snapshots and refresh Azure DevOps organizations for better resource management...","azure_devops/azr_devops_managing_granular_permissions.html@@@Managing granular permissions for Azure DevOps organization@@@Update granular permissions for an Azure DevOps organization to enable or modify backup and recovery for repositories and Developer Collaboration tools...","azure_devops/azr_devops_permission_categories.html@@@Permission categories for Azure DevOps@@@For the backup and recovery tasks associated with Azure DevOps organizations, projects, and repositories, RSC requires specific permissions. RSC groups these permissions into categories for granular management so that you can include or exclude these categories as required...","azure_devops/azr_devops_permission_model.html@@@Permission model for Azure DevOps@@@RSC provides a least permission model for Azure DevOps organization, granting minimal necessary permissions, starting with read-only access. You can add the Basic permission category initially and elevate permissions for recovery operations when required...","azure_devops/azr_devops_plan_protection.html@@@Plan your Azure DevOps protection@@@Before setting up an Azure DevOps organization in RSC, you are required to plan the user and access management for designated RSC users. This planning also involves reviewing the permissions that RSC requires in your Azure environment to protect your Azure DevOps organizations...","azure_devops/azr_devops_primary_snapshot_retention.html@@@Primary snapshot retention for Azure DevOps@@@Primary snapshot retention for Azure DevOps organizations ensures data protection and recoverability by enabling you to set various retention policies, such as retaining hourly, daily, monthly, and yearly snapshots, to meet compliance, business continuity, and disaster recovery requirements...","azure_devops/azr_devops_private_service_endpoints_usage.html@@@Private and service endpoints usage for Azure DevOps@@@You can back up Azure DevOps snapshots to an Azure storage account by using Azure private or service endpoints...","azure_devops/azr_devops_privilege_elevation.html@@@Privilege elevation for Azure DevOps recovery@@@RSC enhances the security of your Azure DevOps environment by employing a least privilege model that limits the access granted to the minimal necessary roles and resources for both repository and Developer Collaboration recovery...","azure_devops/azr_devops_project_details.html@@@Project details page@@@The project details page provides an overview of the protection status of an Azure DevOps project, Developer Collaboration tool counts, and change activity, and gives you access to protection and recovery actions for the project...","azure_devops/azr_devops_protection_key_features.html@@@Key features for protecting Azure DevOps@@@RSC provides unified data management, automated global data protection, various recovery options, and additional security features to protect your Azure DevOps organization...","azure_devops/azr_devops_protection_retention_lock.html@@@Retention lock for Azure DevOps protection@@@A retention lock on an RSC is a security feature that prevents premature deletion of Azure DevOps snapshots...","azure_devops/azr_devops_quick_links.html@@@Quick links for Azure DevOps@@@Immediate access to important tasks and information, enabling quick setup, daily operations, and critical recovery...","azure_devops/azr_devops_rbk_communication.html@@@Communication between RSC and Azure DevOps organization@@@A high-level architecture overview of how RSC communicates with your Azure DevOps organization while onboarding. It explains the use of Service Principals, custom roles, and the trust relationship established between Microsoft Entra ID and RSC for secure operations...","azure_devops/azr_devops_recover.html@@@Recover Azure DevOps@@@After RSC takes snapshots of your Azure DevOps repositories and Developer Collaboration tools, you can recover them using individual repository recovery or one-stop project recovery...","azure_devops/azr_devops_recovering_dev_collab.html@@@Recovering a project@@@Recover an Azure DevOps project by restoring Developer Collaboration tools and repositories into a new project within the same organization...","azure_devops/azr_devops_recovering_proj_repos.html@@@Recovering individual Azure DevOps repositories@@@Recover a single Azure DevOps repository from a protected snapshot...","azure_devops/azr_devops_recovering_project.html@@@Recovering all repositories in an Azure DevOps project@@@Recover some or all repositories within an Azure DevOps project to a new target project in a single bulk restore operation...","azure_devops/azr_devops_refreshing_organization.html@@@Refreshing an Azure DevOps Organization@@@Refresh an Azure DevOps organization as an on-demand task to retrieve the latest metadata of all projects and repositories from Azure DevOps...","azure_devops/azr_devops_removing_organization.html@@@Removing Azure DevOps organization@@@Remove an Azure DevOps organization when you do not want to protect the organization with Rubrik...","azure_devops/azr_devops_req_rsc_perms.html@@@Required RSC permissions for Azure DevOps@@@RSC requires certain permissions to protect Azure DevOps organization, configure an Exocompute instance, store data, and manage encryption of the stored data...","azure_devops/azr_devops_set_up_backup_loc.html@@@Set up backup location for Azure DevOps@@@RSC protects your Azure DevOps organizations, projects, and repositories. You can set up a backup location in Azure for storing the snapshots of Azure DevOps organizations, projects, and repositories...","azure_devops/azr_devops_set_up_exocompute.html@@@Set up Exocompute for Azure DevOps@@@With the Exocompute on Azure feature, RSC launches an Azure Kubernetes Service cluster to perform backup and recovery operations to protect Azure DevOps organizations. RSC uses the Azure Kubernetes Service cluster to serve as a compute resource in your Azure DevOps organization...","azure_devops/azr_devops_set_up_protection.html@@@Set up protection for Azure DevOps@@@You can set up SLA Domains to apply data protection policies, ensuring automatic and hierarchical protection of Azure DevOps organizations, projects, repositories, and Developer Collaboration tools with granular control overriding higher-level assignments...","azure_devops/azr_devops_settings_backup_recovery.html@@@Azure DevOps repository settings backup and recovery@@@In addition to repository contents, RSC backs up a set of Azure DevOps repository-level settings and the branch policies of the repository as part of every repository snapshot. During recovery, RSC re-applies the settings and recreates the branch policies on the destination repository...","azure_devops/azr_devops_sla_assignment_hierarchy.html@@@SLA Domain assignment hierarchy for Azure DevOps@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based, automatic protection for Azure DevOps organizations, simplifying the assignment of SLA domains across organizations, projects, and repositories...","azure_devops/azr_devops_supported_encryption_types.html@@@Supported encryption types for Azure DevOps snapshots@@@RSC supports snapshot encryption stored in the Azure storage account through platform-managed keys or customer-managed keys...","azure_devops/azr_devops_taking_ods.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Azure DevOps repository@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of the Azure DevOps repository...","azure_devops/azr_devops_taking_ods_dev_collab.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot for Developer Collaboration tools@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of Developer Collaboration tools in an Azure DevOps project independently of repository snapshots...","azure_devops/azr_devops_update_client_secret.html@@@Updating the client secret for Azure DevOps organization@@@Update the Service Principal client secret in RSC after rotating it in Azure AD to prevent backup and recovery job failures...","azure_devops/azr_devops_user_management.html@@@RSC user management for Azure DevOps@@@Designating specific users with appropriate privileges and roles in RSC enhances security for managing Azure DevOps organization...","azure_devops/azr_devops_user_perms_backup_loc.html@@@User permissions for Azure DevOps backup location@@@To set up Azure DevOps backup location in RSC, the RSC user must be assigned a role with specific permissions...","azure_devops/azr_devops_viewing_events.html@@@Viewing events for Azure DevOps@@@View the Events page from the Data Protection dashboard to see the events for the Azure DevOps organization...","azure_devops/azr_devops_viewing_inventory.html@@@Viewing Azure DevOps inventory@@@View the Azure DevOps inventory page to manage organizations, projects, repos, and Developer Collaboration tools...","azure_devops/azure_devops_adding_orgs_oauth.html@@@Adding Azure DevOps organizations with OAuth@@@Add one or more Azure DevOps organizations to RSC using the Configure with OAuth method to protect repositories and enable backup and recovery...","azure_devops/azure_devops_adding_orgs_rubrik_hosted.html@@@Adding Azure DevOps organization using Rubrik-hosted Exocompute@@@Add an Azure DevOps organization using rubrik-hosted Exocompute with RSC to back up and recover repositories, manage organizations, and minimize downtime...","azure_devops/azure_devops_adding_orgs_without_oauth.html@@@Adding Azure DevOps organization without OAuth@@@Add an Azure DevOps organization to RSC using the Configure without OAuth method to retain full control over your Service Principal lifecycle and permission setup...","azure_devops/azure_devops_details.html@@@Azure DevOps details@@@RSC monitors, analyses, and restores Azure DevOps repositories associated with the Azure DevOps projects and organizations. RSC also shows the important details such as organization status, protected projects, and protected repos, and summary of backup jobs...","azure_devops/azure_devops_edit_org.html@@@Edit an Azure DevOps organization@@@You can edit an existing Azure DevOps organization in RSC to change the data protection preferences...","cdm/certificate_management_page.html@@@Certificate management page@@@The Certificate Management page in RSC provides options for generating, editing, and deleting certificates and certificate chains...","cdm/oracle/clone_mount_params_or.html@@@Advanced Oracle database clone and mount parameters@@@A parameters file provides the ability to specify advanced recovery options for live mount and cloning tasks...","cdm/oracle/cloning_oracle_db_snapshot_or.html@@@Cloning an Oracle database snapshot@@@Use Clone to create an Oracle database snapshot that you can use for database recovery or for recovering data files from the clone...","cdm/oracle/creating_empty_etc_oratab_file_or.html@@@Creating an empty oratab file@@@If the Oracle host has no databases running, create an empty /etc/oratab file before installing RBS software...","cdm/oracle/db_clone_prereqs_or.html@@@Database clone prerequisites@@@Before cloning, an Oracle database must meet all preliminary requirements...","cdm/oracle/directories_created_before_recovery_operation_or.html@@@Directories created before a recovery operation@@@The Rubrik cluster automatically attempts to create the most common directories before the recovery operation...","cdm/oracle/failed_clones_or.html@@@Managing failed clones@@@Any instance created by a failed clone task is automatically shut down when the clone task fails...","cdm/oracle/lm_clone_for_pdbs_or.html@@@Live Mount and clone operations on PBDs@@@Rubrik includes behaviors you should be aware of when you perform a Live Mount or clone operation on pluggable databases...","cdm/oracle/lm_oracle_db_backup_or.html@@@Live Mounting an Oracle database backup@@@Use Live Mount to create a database from a point-in-time copy of an Oracle database...","cdm/oracle/lm_oracle_rac_db_backup_or.html@@@Live Mounting an Oracle RAC database backup@@@Use Live Mount to create a database from a point-in-time copy of an Oracle RAC database...","cdm/oracle/lm_prerequisites_or.html@@@Live Mount prerequisites@@@Before performing a Live Mount using an Oracle database snapshot, ensure that the target host meets the preliminary requirements...","cdm/oracle/optional_advanced_parameters_using_clone_or.html@@@Optional Advanced Settings parameters using Clone@@@The Advanced Settings section of a Clone operation includes a number of optional parameters...","cdm/oracle/optional_advanced_params_lm_or.html@@@Optional Advanced Settings parameters for Live Mount@@@The Advanced Settings section of a Live Mount includes a number of optional parameters...","cdm/oracle/oracle_config_or.html@@@Oracle configuration@@@Initial configuration of the Rubrik cluster for Oracle requires at least one open or mounted Oracle database and a user account with SYSDBA privileges...","cdm/oracle/oracle_data_guard_live_mount_or.html@@@Oracle Data Guard Live Mount@@@Live Mount instantiates a database from a copy stored on the Rubrik cluster...","cdm/oracle/oracle_live_mount_or.html@@@Live Mount for Oracle@@@A Live Mount creates a new database from a point-in-time copy of the source database to expedite the total recovery time...","cdm/oracle/oracle_rbs_or.html@@@Rubrik Backup Service@@@Rubrik Backup Service is required in order to perform automated discovery of Oracle hosts, Oracle RAC systems, and Oracle databases...","cdm/oracle/point_in_time_recovery_or.html@@@Point-in-time recovery@@@Point-in-time recovery restores database and log snapshots to the defined point in time...","cdm/oracle/spfile_requirements_or.html@@@SPFILE requirements@@@The Rubrik cluster uses the original SPFILE of the source database for recovery during clone and Live Mount operations unless an alternate custom PFILE is specified...","cdm/vcd/minimum_vmware_cloud_director_privileges.html@@@Minimum privileges granted by VMware Cloud Director@@@To perform the required operations on the objects hosted by a software-defined data center, Rubrik cluster requires a few minimum privileges. These minimum required privileges are granted to the Rubrik cluster by the user role assigned to the VMware Cloud Director account used by the Rubrik cluster...","cdm/vcd/vcd_minimum_access_control_privileges.html@@@Minimum Access Control privileges@@@Information about the minimum Access Control privileges required by the Rubrik cluster to perform operations on objects hosted by a software-defined data center...","cdm/vcd/vcd_minimum_additional_privileges.html@@@Minimum additional privileges granted by VMware Cloud Director@@@Information about the minimum additional privileges required by the Rubrik cluster to perform the required operations on the objects hosted by a software-defined data center. The user role assigned to the VMware Cloud Director account used by the Rubrik cluster grants the minimum additional privileges to the Rubrik cluster...","cdm/vcd/vcd_minimum_administration_privileges.html@@@Minimum Administration privileges@@@Information about the minimum Administration privileges required by the Rubrik cluster to perform operations on objects hosted by a software-defined data center. The user role assigned to the VMware Cloud Director account used by the Rubrik cluster grants the minimum Administration privileges to the Rubrik cluster...","cdm/vcd/vcd_minimum_compute_privileges.html@@@Minimum Compute privileges@@@Information about the minimum Compute privileges required by the Rubrik cluster to perform operations on objects hosted by a software-defined data center. The user role assigned to the VMware Cloud Director account used by the Rubrik cluster grants the minimum Compute privileges to the Rubrik cluster...","cdm/vcd/vcd_minimum_extensions_privileges.html@@@Minimum Extensions privileges@@@Information about the minimum Extensions privileges required by the Rubrik cluster to perform operations on objects hosted by a software-defined data center. The user role assigned to the VMware Cloud Director account used by the Rubrik cluster grants the minimum Extensions privileges to the Rubrik cluster...","cdm/vcd/vcd_minimum_infrastructure_privileges.html@@@Minimum Infrastructure privileges@@@Information about the minimum Infrastructure privileges required by the Rubrik cluster to perform operations on objects hosted by a software-defined data center. The user role assigned to the VMware Cloud Director account used by the Rubrik cluster grants the minimum Infrastructure privileges to the Rubrik cluster...","cdm/vcd/vcd_minimum_libraries_privileges.html@@@Minimum Libraries privileges@@@Information about the minimum Libraries privileges required by the Rubrik cluster to perform operations on objects hosted by a software-defined data center. The user role assigned to the VMware Cloud Director account used by the Rubrik cluster grants the minimum Libraries privileges to the Rubrik cluster...","cdm/vcd/vcd_minimum_networking_privileges.html@@@Minimum Networking privileges@@@Information about the minimum Networking privileges required by the Rubrik cluster to perform operations on objects hosted by a software-defined data center. The user role assigned to the VMware Cloud Director account used by the Rubrik cluster grants the minimum Networking privileges to the Rubrik cluster...","cdm/vmc/min_privs_req_sched_tasks_vmc.html@@@Minimum privileges required for scheduled tasks in VMware Cloud@@@To perform required operations on hosted objects, the VMware Cloud account user role used by a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum privileges for scheduled tasks on the software-defined data center...","cdm/vmc/minimum_vmc_datastore_privileges.html@@@Minimum VMware Cloud Datastore privileges@@@The VMware Cloud account user role used by a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum privileges on the software-defined data center...","cdm/vmc/minimum_vmc_privileges.html@@@Minimum VMware Cloud privileges@@@The role assigned to the VMware Cloud account of the Rubrik cluster must grant specific privileges on the software-defined data center...","cdm/vmc/minimum_vmware_cloud_global_privileges.html@@@Minimum VMware Cloud Global privileges@@@The VMware Cloud account user role of a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum privileges on the software-defined data center...","cdm/vmc/minimum_vmware_cloud_network_privileges.html@@@Minimum VMware Cloud Network privileges@@@The VMware Cloud account user role of a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum privileges on the software-defined data center...","cdm/vmc/minimum_vmware_cloud_resource_privileges.html@@@Minimum VMware Cloud Resource privileges@@@The VMware Cloud account user role of a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum privileges on the software-defined data center...","cdm/vmc/minimum_vmware_cloud_sessions_privileges.html@@@Minimum VMware Cloud Sessions privileges@@@The VMware Cloud account user role of a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum privileges on the software-defined data center...","cdm/vmc/minimum_vmware_cloud_vapp_privileges.html@@@Minimum VMware Cloud vApp privileges@@@The VMware Cloud role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum vApp privileges on the software-defined data center...","cdm/vmc/minimum_vmware_cloud_virtual_machine_privileges.html@@@Minimum VMware Cloud Virtual Machine privileges@@@The VMware Cloud account user role of a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum privileges on the software-defined data center...","cdm/vmc/minimum_vmware_profile-driven_privileges.html@@@Minimum VMware Cloud Profile-driven privileges@@@The VMware Cloud account user role of a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum privileges on the software-defined data center...","cdm/vmc/minimum_vmware_tagging_privileges.html@@@Minimum VMware Cloud tagging privileges@@@The VMware Cloud account user role of a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum privileges on the software-defined data center...","cdm/vmc_hotadd_proxy_reqs.html@@@Virtual machine HotAdd proxy requirements@@@Each cloud-based datastore that hosts virtual machines protected by a Rubrik cluster requires a number of HotAdd proxies...","cdm/vmc_hotadd_proxy_reqs_2.html@@@Virtual machine HotAdd proxy requirements@@@Each cloud-based datastore that hosts virtual machines protected by a Rubrik cluster requires a number of HotAdd proxies...","cdm/vmc_hotadd_proxy_reqs_3.html@@@Virtual machine HotAdd proxy requirements@@@Each cloud-based datastore that hosts virtual machines protected by a Rubrik cluster requires a number of HotAdd proxies...","cdm/vmware_cloud_on_aws.html@@@VMware Cloud on AWS@@@A Rubrik Cloud Cluster can protect virtual machines deployed on VMware Cloud on AWS...","cdm/vmware_cloud_on_aws_2.html@@@VMware Cloud on AWS@@@A Rubrik Cloud Cluster can protect virtual machines deployed on VMware Cloud on AWS...","cdm/vmware_cloud_on_azure.html@@@Microsoft Azure VMware Solution@@@A Rubrik cluster can protect virtual machines deployed on the Microsoft Azure VMware Solution...","cdm/vmware_cloud_on_azure_2.html@@@Microsoft Azure VMware Solution@@@A Rubrik cluster can protect virtual machines deployed on the Microsoft Azure VMware Solution...","cdm/vsphere/min_content_library_privileges.html@@@Minimum Content Library privileges@@@The vSphere role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum Content Library privileges on the vCenter Server...","cdm/vsphere/min_cryptographic_ops_privileges.html@@@Minimum cryptographic\u00A0operations privileges@@@The vCenter Server role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must have the minimum cryptographic operations privileges on the vCenter Server...","cdm/vsphere/min_datastore_privileges.html@@@Minimum datastore privileges@@@The vSphere role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum datastore privileges on the vCenter Server or ESXi host...","cdm/vsphere/min_global_privileges.html@@@Minimum global privileges@@@The vSphere role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum global privileges on the vCenter Server or ESXi host...","cdm/vsphere/min_host_privileges.html@@@Minimum host privileges@@@The vSphere role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum host privileges on the vCenter Server or ESXi host...","cdm/vsphere/min_network_privileges.html@@@Minimum network privileges@@@The vSphere role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum network privileges on the vCenter Server or ESXi host...","cdm/vsphere/min_resource_privileges.html@@@Minimum resource privileges@@@The vSphere role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum resource privileges on the vCenter Server or ESXi host...","cdm/vsphere/min_sessions_privileges.html@@@Minimum session privileges@@@The vSphere role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must include the Validate session privilege on the vCenter Server or ESXi host...","cdm/vsphere/min_system_privileges_esxi.html@@@Minimum system privileges for ESXi@@@The ESXi role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum system privileges on the ESXi host...","cdm/vsphere/min_virtual_machine_privileges.html@@@Minimum virtual machine privileges@@@The vSphere role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum virtual machine privileges on the vCenter Server or ESXi host...","cdm/vsphere/min_virtual_machine_storage_policy_privs.html@@@Minimum virtual machine storage policy privileges@@@The vCenter Server role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum virtual machine storage policy privileges on the vCenter Server...","cdm/vsphere/min_vsphere_tagging_privileges.html@@@Minimum vSphere tagging privileges@@@The vCenter Server role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum vSphere tagging privileges on the vCenter Server...","cdm/vsphere/min_vsphere_vapp_privileges.html@@@Minimum vSphere vApp privileges@@@The vCenter Server role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum vSphere vApp privileges on the vCenter Server...","cdm/vsphere/vsphere_privs.html@@@Minimum vSphere privileges@@@The vSphere role assigned to a Rubrik cluster must provide minimum privileges on the vCenter Server or ESXi host...","cdm_old/about_vm_templates.html@@@About VM templates@@@Rubrik CDM supports vSphere VM templates for selected backup and recovery operations...","cdm_old/activity_log.html@@@Activity Log@@@The Activity Log contains log messages about standard tasks and notifications that are considered time sensitive...","cdm_old/activity_log_filters.html@@@Activity Log filters@@@The Activity Log provides filters on four filter menus...","cdm_old/adding_all_groups_claim_rule.html@@@Adding a group claim rule for all groups@@@Add a custom group claim rule that includes all group claims in the SAML assertion response sent to Rubrik CDM...","cdm_old/adding_an_email_claim_rule.html@@@Adding an email claim rule@@@Add a claim rule to tell ADFS how to format the email claims sent to Rubrik CDM...","cdm_old/adding_azure_arch_loc.html@@@Adding Microsoft Azure as an archival location@@@Configure a Rubrik cluster to use Microsoft Azure as the archival location...","cdm_old/adding_group_filter_claim_rule.html@@@Adding a group filter claim rule@@@Add claim rules that allow only group claims that start with certain characters to be sent to Rubrik CDM...","cdm_old/adding_nameid_claim_rule.html@@@Adding a nameId claim rule@@@Add a claim rule to tell ADFS how to format the nameId claims sent to Rubrik CDM...","cdm_old/adding_rubrik_as_a_relying_party_trust.html@@@Adding Rubrik as a Relying Party Trust@@@To establish a trust relationship between Rubrik CDM and ADFS, add Rubrik as a Relying Party Trust in the ADFS management console...","cdm_old/adding_s3_arch_loc.html@@@Adding an Amazon S3 archival location@@@Configure a Rubrik cluster to use an Amazon S3 archival location...","cdm_old/adding_subnet_to_existing_virtual_network.html@@@Adding subnet to existing virtual network@@@Add a subnet to an existing virtual network...","cdm_old/adding_subnet_to_new_virtual_network.html@@@Adding subnet to new virtual network@@@The Rubrik cluster must have private connectivity to instances within the subnet. Configure the subnet to have a VPN access to the Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/ahv_config_for_nutanix_backup_over_vlan.html@@@Configuration required for Nutanix backup over VLAN@@@Backing up Nutanix AHV virtual machines over VLAN requires configuring VLANs and routes on Nutanix and Rubrik clusters...","cdm_old/ahv_creating_a_live_mount_with_optional_migration.html@@@Creating a Live Mount with optional migration@@@Creating a Live Mount of an AHV virtual machine with optional migration involves immediate or delayed migration of the data source...","cdm_old/ahv_creating_a_live_mount_without_migration.html@@@Creating a Live Mount without migration@@@Live Mount an AHV virtual machine on a Nutanix cluster from a snapshot on the Rubrik cluster without migrating the data source to the Nutanix cluster...","cdm_old/ahv_exporting_vm_snapshot.html@@@Exporting an AHV VM snapshot@@@An Export creates a new virtual machine from a point-in-time copy of the source virtual machine. The datastore of the selected AHV host is the datastore for the recovered virtual machine. Rubrik can export the resulting VHD as either Thick Provisioned or Thin Provisioned...","cdm_old/ahv_live_mounts_page_for_vms.html@@@Live Mounts page for AHV virtual machines@@@The Live Mounts page for AHV virtual machines displays the details of the mounted virtual machines and provides options to unmount, change the power status, and migrate the data source...","cdm_old/ahv_migrating_a_live_mounted_virtual_machine.html@@@Migrating a live mounted virtual machine@@@Migrate the data source of a live mounted AHV virtual machine from the Rubrik cluster to a Nutanix storage container...","cdm_old/ahv_network_segmentation_on_nutanix_clusters.html@@@Network segmentation on Nutanix clusters@@@Rubrik supports AHV virtual machine backup from Nutanix clusters that have network segmentation enabled...","cdm_old/ahv_selecting_a_snapshot.html@@@Selecting a snapshot or archival snapshot@@@Use the Rubrik CDM web UI to select a snapshot before applying a recovery action...","cdm_old/ahv_unmounting_a_virtual_machine.html@@@Unmounting a virtual machine@@@Unmount the live mounted AHV virtual machine from the Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/ahv_virtual_machine_scripts.html@@@AHV virtual machine scripts@@@You can configure the Rubrik cluster to run scripts on a guest OS before creating a snapshot, after creating a snapshot, and after the Rubrik cluster completes the backup process...","cdm_old/ahv_vm_live_mount_operations.html@@@AHV virtual machine Live Mount operations@@@The operations available for a Live Mounted AHV virtual machine on the Live Mounts page vary depending on the type of the Live Mount...","cdm_old/ahv_vm_recovery_using_live_mount.html@@@AHV virtual machine recovery using Live Mount@@@Rubrik supports the Live Mount operation for AHV virtual machine snapshots from Rubrik clusters on to Nutanix clusters...","cdm_old/amazon_s3_advanced_settings.html@@@Amazon S3 advanced settings@@@Information on advanced settings for Amazon S3 archival location...","cdm_old/api_rtb_endpoints.html@@@API endpoints for replication throttling bypass@@@The Rubrik REST API provides endpoints for managing the network throttle bypass settings of replication targets...","cdm_old/api_rtb_http_response_model.html@@@HTTP response model for replication throttling bypass@@@Description of the elements contained in the responses from the replication throttling bypass endpoints...","cdm_old/api_rtb_modifying_replication_throttling_bypass_status.html@@@Modifying replication throttling bypass status@@@Modify the replication throttling bypass status for a specific target cluster...","cdm_old/api_rtb_replication_throttling_bypass.html@@@Replication throttling bypass@@@The Rubrik REST API can be used to bypass the network throttle to provide more bandwidth for replication...","cdm_old/api_rtb_retrieving_replication_throttling_bypass_status.html@@@Retrieving replication throttling bypass status@@@Retrieve the replication throttling bypass status for all replication target clusters...","cdm_old/api_rtb_retrieving_replication_throttling_bypass_status_for_target.html@@@Retrieving replication throttling bypass status for a target@@@Retrieve the replication throttling bypass status for a specified replication target cluster...","cdm_old/api_tokens.html@@@API tokens@@@API tokens can be used in scripts to provide secure authentication, rather than hard-coding credentials directly in the script and exposing them as clear text. Tokens are generated directly from the...","cdm_old/application_consistency.html@@@Application consistency@@@The Rubrik cluster supports application-consistent snapshots for a variety of guest OS types and application types...","cdm_old/arch_consolidation.html@@@Archival Consolidation@@@Archival Consolidation frees archival storage by deleting expired snapshots...","cdm_old/arch_consolidation_cloud.html@@@Archival consolidation for Amazon S3 and Azure@@@For Amazon S3 and Azure, archival consolidation permits the automatic removal of expired and unnecessary snapshot data from the cloud archival location, reducing storage requirements...","cdm_old/arch_loc_config.html@@@Archival location configuration@@@Configure the Rubrik cluster to support a specific archival location by providing the requested archive-specific information...","cdm_old/arch_policy.html@@@Archival policy@@@An archival policy specifies how to handle archiving for the protected workloads assigned to an SLA Domain...","cdm_old/archival_location_actions.html@@@Hyper-V archival location actions@@@Snapshots stored at an archival location support downloading snapshots and and browsing files...","cdm_old/archival_location_prep_S3.html@@@Archival location preparation for Amazon S3@@@Preparing Amazon S3 storage for archiving involves creating a bucket with required permissions...","cdm_old/archival_policy_settings.html@@@Archival policy settings@@@Archival policies include settings for the archival location targets, tiering policies, snapshot frequencies, archival threshold, and local retention...","cdm_old/archiving_amazon_s3.html@@@Amazon S3 archival locations@@@Rubrik CDM supports Amazon S3 as an archival location and provides data encryption with an RSA key...","cdm_old/archiving_microsoft_azure.html@@@Microsoft Azure@@@Rubrik CDM supports Microsoft Azure as an archival location...","cdm_old/archiving_nfs_share.html@@@NFS share@@@The Rubrik cluster supports using an NFS share as an archival location...","cdm_old/archiving_object_storage_system.html@@@Object storage system@@@Information about the supported object storage systems as archival locations for archiving your data...","cdm_old/assigning_protection_resources_tenant_org.html@@@Assigning protection resources to a tenant organization@@@Finalize the creation of a tenant organization by assigning resources that can be used to permit data management and protection...","cdm_old/assigning_roles_to_sso_groups.html@@@Assigning roles to SSO groups@@@Add SSO groups and assign roles to those groups...","cdm_old/assigning_roles_to_sso_users.html@@@Assigning roles to SSO users@@@Assign a role to an SSO user account to specify the permissions for the account...","cdm_old/assigning_sla_domain_setting_hv_cluster_server.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain setting to a Hyper-V cluster or server@@@Specify an SLA Domain setting for Hyper-V host to have the setting applied to the objects and virtual machines contained by the clusters and host...","cdm_old/assigning_sla_domain_setting_nutanix_cluster.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain setting to a Nutanix cluster@@@Specify an SLA Domain setting for Nutanix clusters to have the setting applied to the objects and virtual machines contained by the clusters and server...","cdm_old/assigning_tenant_storage_quota.html@@@Assigning tenant organization storage quota@@@Assign storage-based quota to a tenant organization to restrict resource utilization and protect resource availability...","cdm_old/authorizing_a_rubrik_rest_api_session.html@@@Authorizing a Rubrik REST API session@@@Obtain an authorization token and create an authorized session in the Rubrik REST API playground...","cdm_old/auto_protect_rules_ahv.html@@@Automatic protection rules@@@To provide consistency when applying automatic protection the Rubrik cluster adheres to a specific set of rules...","cdm_old/automatic_protection.html@@@Automatic protection@@@A Rubrik cluster provides automatic protection of virtual machines through inheritance of the SLA Domain assigned to a parent object...","cdm_old/aws_arch_consolidation_cft.html@@@Archival consolidation CloudFormation template@@@Rubrik uses the AWS CloudFormation service to create the archival consolidation CloudFormation template that provisions the resources required for the AWS archival consolidation application...","cdm_old/aws_cft_outputs.html@@@CloudFormation template output@@@After creating a stack by using the archival consolidation CloudFormation template, helpful information appears in the AWS console...","cdm_old/azure_advanced_settings.html@@@Azure advanced settings@@@Setting Field Description Cloud Compute Settings After you configure Cloud Compute Settings, the Rubrik cluster launches a compute instance in the cloud to perform archival consolidation. Import JSON...","cdm_old/azure_arch_consolidation_config_setup.html@@@Azure Archival Consolidation configuration and setup@@@Successful implementation of Azure Archival Consolidation requires the completion of the configuration and setup tasks in a specified order...","cdm_old/azure_downloading_rubrik_cloud_compute.html@@@Downloading the Rubrik Cloud Compute for Azure zip file@@@Download and expand the Rubrik Cloud Compute for Azure zip file...","cdm_old/azure_setting_up_powershell.html@@@Setting up and configuring the PowerShell in Cloud Shell@@@Use the PowerShell in the Azure Cloud Shell to manage Azure resources...","cdm_old/base_frequency_changes.html@@@Base Frequency changes@@@Editing the SLA rules can change the frequency with which snapshots are created. When changes to the frequency impact the Base Frequency of the SLA Domain, all future snapshots are created using the new Base Frequency...","cdm_old/base_frequency_decreased.html@@@Base Frequency decreased@@@Decreasing the snapshot creation frequency causes new policy driven snapshots associated with the SLA Domain to be created based on the lower frequency...","cdm_old/base_frequency_increased.html@@@Base Frequency increased@@@Increasing the Base Frequency causes the SLA Domain to create new snapshots based on the higher frequency. When the retention periods are unchanged, there are no changes to existing snapshots...","cdm_old/cdm_configuration.html@@@Configuration@@@Configure a Rubrik cluster and perform other system tasks...","cdm_old/cdm_vs_recovery_vm.html@@@Recovery of virtual machines and VM templates@@@To recover a virtual machine or a VM template, a Rubrik cluster mounts a point-in-time copy of that virtual machine...","cdm_old/cdm_vs_vm_protection.html@@@vSphere virtual machine protection@@@Use SLA Domains to apply the data protection policies to an individual virtual machine, a VM template, or a selected set of virtual machines or VM templates...","cdm_old/cdp_filter_status.html@@@CDP filter status@@@Information about Continuous Data Protection filter status that RSC displays at the compute cluster and host level. You can take an appropriate action based on the CDP filter status of a compute cluster or host...","cdm_old/cli_access_through_ssh.html@@@CLI access through SSH@@@SSH protocol is the standard way for Rubrik CDM users to access the Rubrik CLI. To use the SSH protocol, users require both administrator and CLI administrator roles...","cdm_old/cli_administrator_role.html@@@CLI administrator role@@@As a CLI administrator, a Rubrik cluster user can connect to nodes in Rubrik clusters through the CLI Secure Shell (SSH) protocol...","cdm_old/comparing_rubrik_envoy_web_certs.html@@@Comparing Rubrik Envoy web certificates@@@Optionally check the validity of the certificate displayed during Rubrik Envoy registration...","cdm_old/config_auth_rubrik_cli_ssh.html@@@Configuring Rubrik CLI SSH Key authentication@@@You can assign an SSH key to a user account. With this key, users can authenticate as a Rubrik cluster administrator without needing to transmit an account password...","cdm_old/config_email_settings_notif.html@@@Configuring event email settings@@@Specify the types of events and the recipients for event notifications that are sent through email...","cdm_old/configuring_aws_arch_consolidation_with_cft.html@@@Configuring Amazon S3 archival consolidation using the CloudFormation template@@@Use the archival consolidation CloudFormation template to configure archival consolidation for Amazon S3...","cdm_old/configuring_azure_objects.html@@@Configuring Azure Objects@@@The first time the Cloud Shell is launched, the Cloud Shell prompts for the one-time creation of a resource group, storage account, and Azure Files share...","cdm_old/configuring_azure_tiering.html@@@Configuring Azure tiering@@@Configure the archival policy for an SLA Domain when creating a custom SLA Domain or when editing an SLA Domain to enable Azure smart tiering...","cdm_old/configuring_envoy.html@@@Configuring Envoy@@@Configure the Rubrik Envoy virtual appliance...","cdm_old/configuring_first_full_time.html@@@Configuring a first full backup window@@@Configure a first full backup window for an SLA Domain when creating a custom SLA Domain or when editing an SLA Domain...","cdm_old/configuring_replication_policy_for_an_sla_domain.html@@@Configuring replication policy for an SLA Domain@@@Configure the replication policy for an SLA Domain when creating a custom SLA Domain or when editing any SLA Domain...","cdm_old/configuring_snapshot_window.html@@@Configuring a snapshot window@@@Configure a snapshot window for an SLA Domain when creating a custom SLA Domain or when editing an SLA Domain...","cdm_old/connect_glacier_arch_loc_disaster_recover.html@@@Connecting to an Amazon S3 Glacier archival location for disaster recovery@@@To connect another Rubrik cluster to an Amazon S3 Glacier archival location for disaster recovery, provide the recovery Rubrik cluster with the connection details that were used by the owner Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/connecting_reader_arch_loc.html@@@Connecting to a reader archival location@@@Use the Rubrik CDM web UI to connect to a reader archival location and perform metadata recovery from the archival target...","cdm_old/creating_a_static_route_for_a_live_mount.html@@@Creating a static route from a Rubrik node@@@The Rubrik CLI provides several utilities to configure static routing between nodes of a Rubrik cluster and the backup sources...","cdm_old/creating_custom_sla_domain.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain@@@Create a custom SLA Domain with policies that meet specific SLA requirements...","cdm_old/custom_sla_domains.html@@@Custom SLA Domains@@@Custom SLA Domains provide the ability to create sets of data protection policies that meet the requirements of various groups of data sources in an enterprise...","cdm_old/data_measurements.html@@@Data measurements@@@The Rubrik CDM web UI depicts data values using the decimal definition for the prefixes used with bits and bytes...","cdm_old/deleting_all_snapshots_for_datasource.html@@@Deleting all snapshots for a data source@@@Delete all snapshots that have a Retain Forever policy for a data source...","cdm_old/deleting_managed_volume.html@@@Deleting a Managed Volume@@@Use the Rubrik CDM web UI to delete a Managed Volume...","cdm_old/deleting_vcloud_director_instance.html@@@Deleting a vCloud Director instance@@@Remove vApp protection by deleting a vCloud Director instance from the Rubrik cluster. The Rubrik cluster marks the vApps from that vCloud Director instance as relics...","cdm_old/deploying_envoy.html@@@Deploying Envoy@@@Deploy a Rubrik Envoy virtual appliance using the VMware hypervisor...","cdm_old/deregistering_envoy_from_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Deregistering Rubrik Envoy from a Rubrik cluster@@@Remove the association between a Rubrik Envoy virtual machine and a Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/direct_archive.html@@@Direct Archive@@@The Direct Archive feature permits direct transfer of snapshots to archival storage, rather than first storing the snapshots on the drives of the Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/direct_nfs.html@@@Direct NFS@@@Available in Oracle 11g and newer, Direct NFS runs in the database kernel and provides an optimized NFS client...","cdm_old/disabling_ssh_passwords.html@@@Disabling SSH password authentication@@@Disable password authentication for Secure Shell sessions to authenticate using SSH key pairs...","cdm_old/edit_an_amazon_s3_archival_location.html@@@Editing an Amazon S3 archival location@@@Edit configuration for an existing Amazon S3 archival location...","cdm_old/editing_an_sla_domain.html@@@Editing an SLA Domain@@@Edit an existing local SLA Domain to change the specified data protection...","cdm_old/editing_the_assigned_tenant_storage_quota.html@@@Editing the assigned tenant organization storage quota@@@Edit the assigned tenant organization storage quota to increase or decrease the storage limits for an organization...","cdm_old/enabling_and_configuring_replication_throttling.html@@@Enabling and configuring replication throttling@@@Specify the maximum bandwidth for replication by configuring replication throttling. Replication throttling can only be set by a global administrator...","cdm_old/enabling_cyber_event_lockdown.html@@@Enabling Cyber Event Lockdown@@@Enable Cyber Event Lockdown to protect all data stored on a Rubrik cluster from an event that could affect data integrity, such as a security breach or accidental deletion...","cdm_old/enabling_jumbo_frames.html@@@Enabling jumbo frames@@@Use the Rubrik CLI to enable jumbo frames by changing the maximum transmission unit settings on the Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/envoy_configuring_nat_addresses.html@@@Configuring Envoy to connect to a cluster using NAT@@@Configure Rubrik Envoy to set NAT addresses instead of bond0 IP addresses when using provider-side NAT...","cdm_old/envoy_dual_nic.html@@@Envoy dual-NIC support@@@Rubrik Envoy supports up to two virtual NICs...","cdm_old/envoy_network_interfaces.html@@@Envoy network interfaces@@@Rubrik Envoy can connect with a single Ethernet interface or with an optional, second Ethernet interface...","cdm_old/envoy_network_requirements.html@@@Envoy network requirements@@@Rubrik Envoy registration has specific network configuration requirements...","cdm_old/envoy_security.html@@@Envoy security@@@Rubrik Envoy provides secure multitenancy...","cdm_old/envoy_topology.html@@@Envoy topology@@@Rubrik Envoy allows tenant organizations to connect to Rubrik services on a shared Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/file_and_folder_restore_vs.html@@@File and folder restore@@@The Rubrik cluster provides file level restore of files and folders from any local snapshot, replica, or archival snapshot that was successfully indexed...","cdm_old/file_systems_filesets.html@@@Filesets@@@Rubrik CDM protects folders and files on host computers and NAS shares through filesets...","cdm_old/filtering_messages.html@@@Filtering messages@@@Filter the messages that appear on the Activity Log by status, data source type, message type, and date...","cdm_old/finding_protection_objects_vs.html@@@Finding protection objects@@@The Rubrik CDM web UI provides several tools for finding protection objects...","cdm_old/generating_an_api_token.html@@@Generating an API token@@@Generate an API token for use in REST API calls to the Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/google_cloud_platform_advanced_settings.html@@@Google Cloud Platform advanced settings@@@Information on advanced settings for Google Cloud Platform archival location...","cdm_old/guest_os_credentials.html@@@Guest OS credentials@@@Guest OS credentials are the username and password that a Rubrik cluster uses to provide access to the guest operating system and files of a vSphere virtual machine. When Rubrik Backup Service is not installed or disconnected, you can use guest OS credentials to recover virtual machine files...","cdm_old/guest_os_settings.html@@@Guest OS settings@@@Enable the administration of guest OS credentials for virtual machines. When Rubrik Backup Service is not installed or not connected to your cluster, you can recover vSphere virtual machine files through guest OS credentials...","cdm_old/host_specific_fields.html@@@Host-specific fields@@@Some fileset fields support particular host types...","cdm_old/hyper-v_back_up_processes.html@@@Backup processes@@@A Rubrik cluster backs up a virtual machine by using VSS to create a snapshot of the virtual machine...","cdm_old/hyper-v_backup_consistency_levels.html@@@Backup consistency levels@@@By default, the Rubrik cluster provides the highest level of backup consistency that is available for a virtual machine...","cdm_old/hyperv_day_view_actions_snapshots.html@@@Actions available on the day view for Hyper-V snapshots@@@The day view provides the ability to initiate various actions with Hyper-V virtual machine snapshots. Access the actions by clicking the ellipsis menu...","cdm_old/hyperv_instant_recovery.html@@@Hyper-V Instant Recovery@@@Using Instant Recovery, you can quickly bring a full Hyper-V virtual machine online while also deprecating and replacing the original virtual machine...","cdm_old/hyperv_recovery_folders_and_files.html@@@Folders and files recovery@@@The Rubrik cluster provides file level restore of files and folders from any local snapshot, replica, or archival snapshot that was successfully indexed...","cdm_old/hyperv_restoring_download_notification_msg.html@@@Restoring from notification link@@@Search or browse for a file or folder and restore that file or folder by download from a link in the notification message...","cdm_old/hyperv_vm_snapshots.html@@@Hyper-V virtual machine snapshots@@@The Rubrik cluster provides protection for virtual machines by combining native snapshot technology with the fast and scalable cloud data management platform of the Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/impact_of_sla_domain_changes_on_snapshots.html@@@Impact of SLA Domain changes on snapshots@@@Examples showing the impact of changing the retention policy of the SLA Domain assigned to an object. Examines the impact of retroactive and non-retroactive retention changes on local, archived, and replicated snapshots...","cdm_old/impact_retention_changes_arch_rep_policies.html@@@Impact of retention changes on archival and replication policies@@@When the retention period associated with any SLA rule is changed, it can potentially trigger an automatic change of existing archival and replication policies in an SLA Domain...","cdm_old/information_provided_by_activity_log_messages.html@@@Information provided by Activity Log messages@@@The Rubrik cluster provides detailed task information in the Activity Log messages...","cdm_old/installing_the_cdp_filter.html@@@Installing the CDP Filter@@@Before CDP is enabled, install the CDP Filter on vCenter 6.7 (or newer version)...","cdm_old/interception_proxy.html@@@Trusted SSL-TLS interception@@@Trusted SSL-TLS interception provides a trusted point of visibility and inspection into SSL-TLS encrypted network traffic...","cdm_old/ip_address_changes_envoy.html@@@IP address changes in Rubrik Envoy@@@The effect of changes to the IP address of a Rubrik Envoy virtual appliance...","cdm_old/jumbo_frame_support.html@@@Jumbo frame support@@@For Rubrik CDM versions 9.4 and later, you can set the value for the maximum transmission unit to a maximum value of 10000, instead of the default value of 1500. This larger unit size is called jumbo frames...","cdm_old/latest_snapshot_expiration_behavior.html@@@Latest snapshot expiration behavior@@@If additional snapshots are taken at a given location, then the latest snapshot at that location will not expire. The following scenarios determine the behavior of the latest snapshot...","cdm_old/local_host_page_vs.html@@@Local host page@@@The local host page provides detailed information about the protection of a virtual machine and tasks related to the virtual machine. The local host page provides the following sections: An...","cdm_old/local_retention_period.html@@@Local retention period@@@The Rubrik cluster retains a snapshot or backup locally based on the local retention period specified by the SLA Domain...","cdm_old/manage_protection_options.html@@@Manage Protection options@@@Select the virtualization hierarchy entities and click Manage Protection to view the Manage Protection dialog box for the selected entities. The Manage Protection dialog box provides several options for the selected entities...","cdm_old/manage_vcenters_vs.html@@@Manage vCenters@@@The Rubrik cluster accesses virtual machine data through a connection with the VMware vCenter Server that manages the hypervisor that is running the virtual machine. To successfully connect with a vCenter Server, the Rubrik cluster requires connection information for that vCenter Server...","cdm_old/managed_volumes.html@@@Managed Volumes@@@The Managed Volume feature in Rubrik CDM protects and manages data...","cdm_old/managing_consolidation_for_azure.html@@@Managing consolidation for Azure@@@Enable or disable snapshot consolidation for an Azure archival location...","cdm_old/managing_consolidation_for_s3.html@@@Managing consolidation for Amazon S3@@@Enable or disable snapshot consolidation for an Amazon S3 archival location...","cdm_old/mounting_vm_from_latest_pit.html@@@Mounting a virtual machine from latest PIT on a Rubrik cluster@@@A virtual machine can be mounted from the latest PIT on a local or replicated Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/mounting_vm_from_pit.html@@@Mounting a virtual machine from specific PIT on a Rubrik cluster@@@A virtual machine can be mounted from a specific PIT on the local Rubrik cluster or a replication target Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/mt_envoy_org_networks.html@@@Envoy and Organization Networks@@@With Rubrik Envoy, you can enable secure data movement between Rubrik clusters and a tenant organization network...","cdm_old/mtu_settings_verification.html@@@MTU settings verification@@@You can use a few methods to verify the maximum transmission unit settings after you reconfigure them...","cdm_old/naming_org_adding_users_ad_groups.html@@@Naming the organization and adding users or AD groups@@@The first steps in defining a tenant organization are assigning a name, creating administrator roles, and adding users or AD groups...","cdm_old/network_throttling.html@@@Network Throttling@@@Rubrik provides settings for replication and archiving to specify the maximum bandwidth allowed for outbound traffic...","cdm_old/optional_archival_fields_for_sla_domains.html@@@Optional archival fields for SLA Domains@@@Archival fields are optional when creating or editing an SLA Domain...","cdm_old/optional_frequency_and_retention_fields_for_sla_domains.html@@@Optional frequency and retention fields for SLA Domains@@@Some frequency and retention fields are optional when creating or editing an SLA Domain...","cdm_old/optional_replication_fields_for_sla_domains.html@@@Optional replication fields for SLA Domains@@@Replication settings are an optional part of creating or editing an SLA Domain...","cdm_old/optional_summary_fields_for_sla_domains.html@@@Optional summary fields for SLA Domains@@@Optional fields on the Summary page become available when editing an SLA Domain...","cdm_old/overview_card.html@@@Overview card@@@The Overview card provides a summary of the Managed Volumes...","cdm_old/protecting_objects_in_an_organization.html@@@Protecting objects in an organization@@@Specify the organization objects to protect...","cdm_old/protection_exceptions.html@@@Protection exceptions for Hyper-V virtual machine snapshots@@@The Rubrik cluster cannot protect data if protection exceptions exist...","cdm_old/protection_policies.html@@@Protection policies@@@The SLA Domain feature has default protection policies and user configured protection policies...","cdm_old/protection_policies_sla_domain_changes.html@@@SLA Domain changes@@@Edit Local SLA Domain policies when changes are needed...","cdm_old/protection_vs.html@@@Virtual machine and VM template protection@@@A Rubrik cluster provides protection for virtual machines and VM templates through either individual assignment to an SLA Domain or through automatic protection...","cdm_old/recovery_points_card.html@@@Recovery Points card@@@The Recovery Points card provides access to the available snapshots and log backups of the database...","cdm_old/refreshing_reader_location_objects.html@@@Refreshing reader location objects@@@Use the Rubrik CDM web UI to update a reader cluster with the latest snapshot metadata...","cdm_old/register_envoy_with_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Registering Rubrik Envoy with a Rubrik cluster@@@Register the Rubrik Envoy virtual machine with the Rubrik cluster using the Rubrik Envoy CLI...","cdm_old/removing_a_host.html@@@Removing a host@@@Delete a Linux, Unix, or Windows host from the Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/replication_policy.html@@@Replication policy@@@Enable a replication policy for an SLA Domain to replicate the snapshot and backup data of the source objects that are protected by the SLA Domain...","cdm_old/replication_target_changes.html@@@Replication target changes@@@Editing the replication targets in an SLA Domain does not impact existing snapshots...","cdm_old/replication_target_changes_2.html@@@Replication target changes@@@Editing the replication targets in an SLA Domain does not impact existing snapshots...","cdm_old/retention_changes.html@@@Retention changes@@@Editing the SLA rules can have an effect on existing snapshots and future snapshots of associated data sources...","cdm_old/retention_changes_removing_sla_domain.html@@@Existing snapshots retention@@@After removing the SLA Domain setting, you can select the retention policy for existing snapshots...","cdm_old/rubrik_mib_file.html@@@Rubrik MIB file@@@The MIB file on the Rubrik cluster contains the management data of the devices on the IP network. You can download the MIB file from the Rubrik cluster to view the measurements and notification messages (traps) specified in the file...","cdm_old/running_cloud_compute_connectivity_check.html@@@Running cloud compute connectivity check@@@Verify the connectivity between the Rubrik cluster and the cloud compute instances by running the cloud compute connectivity check. The connectivity is required for consolidation and smart tiering...","cdm_old/selecting_replica.html@@@Selecting a replica@@@Use the Rubrik CDM web UI of the replication target Rubrik cluster to select a replica before applying a recovery action...","cdm_old/service_level_agreement.html@@@Service Level Agreement@@@The Service Level Agreement section defines snapshot frequency and retention...","cdm_old/setting_up_perms_azure.html@@@Setting up permissions on Azure@@@The Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) authenticates to the Rubrik cluster by registering the Rubrik cluster in Azure AD...","cdm_old/sla_domain_name.html@@@SLA Domain name@@@SLA Domain names must be unique and follow character usage requirements...","cdm_old/sla_domains_with_cdp_enabled.html@@@SLA Domains with CDP enabled@@@SLA Domains with Continuous Data Protection enabled are used for near-term recovery...","cdm_old/sla_update_log_backups.html@@@SLA update log backups@@@The Rubrik cluster allows administrators to configure log backups as part of an SLA Domain...","cdm_old/snapshot_retention_period_decreased.html@@@Snapshot retention period decreased@@@Decreasing the retention period causes the Rubrik cluster to retain new snapshots for the shorter retention period...","cdm_old/snapshot_retention_period_increased.html@@@Snapshot retention period increased@@@Increasing the retention period causes the Rubrik cluster to retain all new snapshots for the new longer retention period...","cdm_old/snapshot_window.html@@@Snapshot window@@@You can configure an SLA Domain to include a snapshot window...","cdm_old/snapshot_window_2.html@@@Snapshot window@@@You can configure an SLA Domain to include a snapshot window...","cdm_old/snapshot_window_changes.html@@@Snapshot window changes@@@Changing the snapshot window causes the Rubrik cluster to use the new snapshot window when creating new snapshots...","cdm_old/snapshots_recovery_points_card.html@@@Snapshots card or Recovery Points card@@@For a selected remote data source, the Snapshots card or Recovery Points card provides the ability to browse and work with the replicas that reside on the local Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/snapshots_vs.html@@@Snapshots@@@The Rubrik cluster provides protection for virtual machines by combining native snapshot technology with the fast and scalable cloud data management platform of the Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/snmp_polling.html@@@SNMP polling@@@SNMP managers can poll the SNMP agent on the Rubrik cluster and request information using the SNMPv2c or SNMPv3 protocol...","cdm_old/specifying_custom_date_range.html@@@Specifying a custom date range@@@The Rubrik CDM web UI provides a custom date range filter in several views. Use this filter to show the information that was generated during a specified date range...","cdm_old/supported_envoy_network_assgnmnts.html@@@Supported Envoy network assignments@@@Rubrik Envoy supports both static IP and DHCP network assignments...","cdm_old/syslog_export_rule_settings.html@@@Syslog export rule settings@@@With Rubrik clusters, you can create syslog export rules based on various settings...","cdm_old/syslog_messages_as_snmp_objects.html@@@Syslog messages as SNMP objects@@@The Management Information Base module inside the Rubrik cluster represents syslog messages as SNMP objects...","cdm_old/syslog_settings.html@@@Syslog protocol@@@The Rubrik cluster supports transmission of system activities to an external syslog server using standard syslog protocol...","cdm_old/take_first_full_changes.html@@@Take first full backup changes@@@Changing the time specified by the Take first full field causes the Rubrik cluster to wait until the specified time before creating the first full snapshot or backup of newly added data sources. When a snapshot window is specified, the Rubrik cluster creates the first full during the next available snapshot window after the specified Take first full time...","cdm_old/tenant_storage_quota.html@@@Tenant organization storage quota@@@Storage-based quotas can be assigned to tenant organizations in multitenant environments to restrict resource utilization and protect resource availability...","cdm_old/testing_the_connection.html@@@Testing the SSO connection@@@Test the connection to verify that users can access the Rubrik cluster using single sign-on...","cdm_old/tpr_admin_role_details.html@@@TPR Admin role details@@@A user account with the TPR Admin role has specific permissions in the two-person rule context...","cdm_old/tpr_approver_role_details.html@@@TPR Approver role details@@@A user account with the TPR Approver role is responsible for approving or denying TPR requests...","cdm_old/tpr_disabling_tpr.html@@@Disabling TPR@@@Process of disabling the two-person rule on a Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/tpr_enabling.html@@@Enabling TPR@@@Process of enabling the two-person rule on a Rubrik cluster and creating a user account with the TPR administrator role...","cdm_old/tpr_global_administrator_role_details.html@@@Global administrator role details@@@A user account with the global administrator role has specific permissions in the two-person rule context...","cdm_old/tpr_initial_configuration.html@@@Initial TPR configuration@@@Configuring the two-person rule for the first time involves creating the first user account with the TPR Admin role and enabling a policy that enforces the two-person rule on selected actions...","cdm_old/tpr_managing_protected_actions.html@@@Managing actions protected by TPR@@@Process of enabling or disabling the two-person rule for selected actions on a Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/tpr_protected_actions.html@@@Actions protected by TPR@@@A global administrator can enable or disable the two-person rule protection for a predefined set of actions on a Rubrik cluster. Disabling TPR protection for an action is subject to approval from a TPR administrator...","cdm_old/tpr_roles.html@@@TPR roles@@@Enforcing the two-person rule on a Rubrik cluster requires assigning multiple roles that have specific permissions...","cdm_old/tpr_two_person_rule.html@@@The two-person rule@@@The two-person rule provides additional data security on Rubrik CDM by ensuring that no individual user can perform key operations on data without the approval of a secondary user...","cdm_old/unmounting_live_mount_database.html@@@Unmounting a Live Mount database@@@Use the Live Mounts page to unmount a Live Mount database...","cdm_old/unprotected_vm_vs.html@@@Unprotected virtual machines and VM templates@@@Information about the labels and protection policies applied to virtual machines and VM templates that are not protected by an SLA Domain...","cdm_old/verifying_adfs_service_provider_settings.html@@@Verifying ADFS Service Provider settings@@@After downloading the Rubrik metadata file and setting up custom claim rules, verify that all ADFS Service Provider settings have the correct values...","cdm_old/viewing_activity_log_messages.html@@@Viewing Activity Log messages@@@View recent messages of the Activity Log to see the 15 most recent activity messages...","cdm_old/viewing_current_mtu_settings.html@@@Viewing the current MTU settings@@@Use the Rubrik CLI to view the current maximum transmission unit settings...","cdm_old/viewing_local_host_page.html@@@Viewing a local host page@@@Access a local host page to view information about a local virtual machine...","cdm_old/viewing_the_assigned_tenant_quota_for_the_organization.html@@@Viewing the tenant organization storage quota@@@View the assigned and used storage-based quota for a tenant organization...","cdm_old/virtual_machine_linking.html@@@Virtual machine and VM template linking@@@You can use automatic linking to link and present duplicate virtual machine or VM templates as a single instance...","cdm_old/vmc_hotadd_proxy_req.html@@@Virtual machine HotAdd proxy requirements@@@Each cloud-based datastore that hosts virtual machines protected by a Rubrik cluster requires a number of HotAdd proxies, which is determined by the number of nodes in the Rubrik cluster and the number of ESXi hosts...","cdm_old/vmware_cloud_on_gcve.html@@@Google Cloud VMware Engine@@@A Rubrik cluster can protect virtual machines deployed on the Google Cloud VMware Engine...","cdm_old/vmware_cloud_on_gcve_2.html@@@Google Cloud VMware Engine@@@A Rubrik cluster can protect virtual machines deployed on the Google Cloud VMware Engine...","cdm_old/vs_assigning_sla_domain_setting_to_vm.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain setting to a virtual machine or VM template@@@Specify an SLA Domain for a virtual machine or VM template, set the virtual machine or VM template to inherit from a parent, or specify Do Not Protect for the virtual machine or VM template...","cdm_old/vs_auto_protect_rules.html@@@Automatic protection rules@@@To provide consistency when applying automatic protection, the Rubrik cluster adheres to a specific set of rules...","cdm_old/vs_automatic_protection.html@@@Automatic protection@@@A Rubrik cluster provides automatic protection of virtual machines and VM templates through inheritance of the SLA Domain assigned to a parent object...","cdm_old/vs_backup_consistency_levels.html@@@Backup consistency levels@@@The Rubrik cluster provides the highest possible level of backup consistency for a vSphere virtual machine. The highest possible level is determined by several factors...","cdm_old/vs_large_file_recovery_vmware_tools.html@@@Large file recovery with VMware tools and disk mount@@@Large file recovery uses VMware tools and disk mount to restore large files efficiently, enhancing the speed for faster data recovery operations...","cdm_old/vs_recovering_file_folder_vm.html@@@Recovering a file or folder on a virtual machine@@@Recover files or folders on a virtual machine using the Rubrik CDM web UI to ensure quick and efficient critical data restoration. Recovering files and folders on a virtual machine leverages snapshots, replicas, or archival snapshots to provide multiple recovery options, enabling seamless data retrieval and minimizing downtime...","cdm_old/vs_restore_guest_file_system.html@@@Restore files and folders directly to a guest file system@@@For supported Windows and Unix/Linux guest operating systems, the Rubrik cluster can restore files and folders directly to the source file system...","cdm_old/vs_restoring_files_folders_guest.html@@@Restoring directly to a guest file system@@@Restore a file or folder to the source file system of a supported Windows or Linux guest operating system...","cdm_old/vs_vm_continuous_data_protection.html@@@Continuous Data Protection@@@Continuous Data Protection uses VMware vSphere APIs for I/O Filtering to continuously capture changes to data on a vSphere virtual machine and sends them to a Rubrik cluster...","cdm_old/vsphere_virtual_machines.html@@@vSphere virtual machines and VM templates@@@A Rubrik cluster provides data management and protection for virtual machines and VM templates deployed in a VMware vSphere environment...","cdm_old/warning_messages_vs.html@@@Warning messages@@@As part of the task of assigning SLA Domains, the Rubrik cluster may display warning messages...","cloud/about_rubrik_cloud_clusters.html@@@About Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage runs Rubrik CDM software in a virtual Rubrik cluster hosted on an AWS, Azure, GCP, or OCI virtual private cloud...","cloud/aws_adding_nodes.html@@@Adding AWS nodes@@@Use the Rubrik CLI to add nodes to Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage. Adding nodes provides additional capacity and improved performance...","cloud/aws_instantiating_nodes_cc_es.html@@@Instantiating the nodes for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services@@@To start creating a new Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services deployment, instantiate either a single node or three or more nodes using the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage AMI available through the AWS Marketplace...","cloud/aws_node_instantiation_settings.html@@@AWS node instantiation settings@@@Instantiating a node requires the correct configuration of AWS settings...","cloud/aws_setting_up_cc_es.html@@@Setting up Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services@@@Use an SSH session to set up Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services...","cloud/aws_workflow_for_cc_es.html@@@Workflow for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services@@@Setting up Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services consists of several tasks...","cloud/azure_adding_disks.html@@@Adding data disks for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Azure@@@Add required data disks to each node in the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure deployment...","cloud/azure_adding_nodes.html@@@Adding Azure nodes@@@Use the Rubrik CLI to add nodes to Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage. Adding nodes provides additional capacity and improved performance...","cloud/azure_cc_es_workflow.html@@@Workflow for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Setting up Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure consists of a sequence of tasks performed in the correct order...","cloud/azure_creating_cc_es.html@@@Creating Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Create a Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure deployment by adding virtual machine nodes and attaching disks and your Managed Identity to the nodes...","cloud/azure_setting_up_cc_es.html@@@Setting up Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Use an SSH session to set up Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure...","cloud/gcp_adding_nodes.html@@@Adding GCP nodes@@@Use the Rubrik CLI to add nodes to Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage. Adding nodes provides additional capacity and improved performance...","cloud/gcp_cces_creating_role_service_acct.html@@@Creating roles and service accounts for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on GCP@@@Create a custom role with specific permissions required for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Google Cloud Platform and assign it to a service account...","cloud/gcp_cloud_cluster_es.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster ES on GCP@@@A Rubrik Cloud Cluster protects applications and data by running Rubrik CDM software on Google Cloud Platform instances within a virtual private cloud...","cloud/gcp_creating_key.html@@@Creating a key to authenticate the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on GCP service account@@@Create a key to authenticate the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Google Cloud Platform service account...","cloud/gcp_customer_details_file.html@@@GCP customer details file for Rubrik Cloud Cluster ES for GCP@@@The GCP customer details file provides information for Rubrik Cloud Cluster ES configuration and platform settings...","cloud/gcp_deploying_cluster.html@@@Deploying a Rubrik Cloud Cluster on GCP@@@Edit the customer details file and use that file to deploy a Rubrik Cloud Cluster ES on Google Cloud Platform...","cloud/gcp_performing_offline_entitlement.html@@@Performing offline entitlement for GCP@@@Perform entitlement on nodes that are not connected to the internet...","cloud/gcp_performing_online_entitlement.html@@@Performing online entitlement for GCP@@@When you have internet access, perform online node entitlement so that the nodes can join Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage...","cloud/gcp_setting_up_rubrik_ccl.html@@@Setting up the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Google Cloud Platform@@@Set up Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Google Cloud Platform by opening an SSH connection to one of the virtual nodes and performing the system setup task...","cloud/installing_the_rubrik_backup_service.html@@@Installing the Rubrik Backup Service on each host@@@Obtain the Rubrik Backup Service installation file from Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage and install it on protected hosts...","cloud/logging_in_rubrik_cdm_web_ui.html@@@Logging in to the Rubrik CDM web UI@@@Log in to the Rubrik CDM web UI of the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage for the first time using the admin account...","cloud/node_entitlement_gcp.html@@@Node entitlement@@@Node entitlement gives you permission to use Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage software...","cloud/oci_adding_nodes.html@@@Adding OCI nodes@@@Use the Rubrik CLI to add nodes to Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage. Adding nodes provides additional capacity and improved performance...","cloud/oci_deploying_rubrik_cc.html@@@Deploying Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI@@@To deploy Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure, you create and configure a new compute instance and then deploy it, repeating the process for additional nodes as needed...","cloud/oci_downloading_access_token.html@@@Downloading an access token@@@Generate a secret key and access token to authenticate the Rubrik Cloud Cluster on the Oracle Cloud Infrastructure...","cloud/oci_rubrik_cc.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI protects applications and data by running Rubrik CDM software on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure instances, supporting single or multi-node configurations and storing data in an Oracle Cloud Infrastructure bucket...","cloud/oci_rubrik_cc_block_vol_values.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI block volume values@@@Each Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI deployment contains three block volumes that require specific configuration values...","cloud/oci_setting_up_rubrik_cc.html@@@Setting up Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI@@@Set up Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI by opening an SSH connection to a virtual node and performing the system setup task...","cloud/rubrik_cloud_cluster_aws.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services protects applications and data by running Rubrik CDM software on Amazon EC2 instances within a virtual private cloud...","cloud/rubrik_cloud_cluster_azure.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure provides the ability to run a Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage to protect applications and data within a Microsoft Azure virtual network...","cloud/security_group_rules.html@@@Security group rules for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services@@@The Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage security group requires specific inbound and outbound rules to enable CLI access, web UI sessions, node-to-node communication, and Rubrik service connectivity...","cloud/workflow_rubrik_cloud_cluster_oci.html@@@Workflow for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI@@@Setting up Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure involves downloading an access token, preparing and deploying the custom image, and configuring the cluster...","common/accepted_values_fileset_descs.html@@@Accepted values for fileset descriptions@@@Rubrik clusters accept a specific set of values in fileset descriptions...","common/automatic_detection_and_display.html@@@Automatic detection and display@@@The Rubrik Backup Service provides automatic detection of WSFC...","common/aws_access_policies.html@@@AWS access policies@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage deployments use AWS policies to define permissions for cluster nodes and Amazon S3 storage...","common/aws_cloud_cluster_prerequisites.html@@@Prerequisites for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on AWS@@@Information about the prerequisites for configuring Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services...","common/aws_creating_cse.html@@@Creating an encryption key for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on AWS@@@Create an encryption key in the AWS Key Management Service that Rubrik can use to protect the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage recovery package before the cluster stores data from the package in cloud storage...","common/azr_cc_es_prereq.html@@@Prerequisites for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Information about the prerequisites for provisioning Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure...","common/azure_creating_cse.html@@@Creating an encryption key for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Azure@@@Create an encryption key in the Azure Key Vault that Rubrik can use to protect the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage recovery package before the cluster stores data from the package in cloud storage...","common/azure_permissions_created_rsc.html@@@Permissions that RSC uses for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Information about the permissions that RSC creates when you provision Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure...","common/azure_permissions_required.html@@@Permissions required by Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Information about the permissions and actions required to provision Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure...","common/azure_preparing_deploy.html@@@Preparing to deploy Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Prepare the Azure environment before deploying Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage...","common/azure_storage_settings.html@@@Storage settings required by Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Information about the storage account settings required for provisioning Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure...","common/cces_accepting_azure_terms_using_cli.html@@@Accepting Azure Marketplace terms with the Azure CLI@@@Use the Azure CLI to accept the Azure Marketplace agreement and licensing terms for the software plan...","common/cces_encryption_keys.html@@@Encryption keys for the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage recovery package@@@Encrypting the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage recovery package protects the package in your cloud account before the cluster writes the data in the package to cloud storage...","common/cces_immutable_storage.html@@@Immutable storage in Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage@@@Immutability enforces retention policies and prevents alteration or deletion of snapshots for the specified period, safeguarding data integrity...","common/cloud_cluster_security_model.html@@@Security model for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage@@@You can protect data managed on Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage by using a simple security model...","common/endpoint_types_cces_azure.html@@@Endpoint types for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage requires Azure endpoints so that traffic between Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage and Azure Blob Storage stays on the Azure network...","common/failover_events.html@@@Failover events@@@A Rubrik cluster handles WSFC failover events automatically...","common/fileset_description_rules.html@@@Fileset description rules@@@Fileset descriptions must meet specific requirements...","common/fileset_fields_rules_value_types.html@@@Fileset fields, rules, and value types@@@The Rubrik cluster interprets a fileset based on the values provided in the Include, Exclude, and Do Not Exclude fields. The Rubrik cluster applies a set of rules to the values provided in these fields and permits several types of values to be added to the fields...","common/fileset_regular_expression_conversions.html@@@Fileset regular expression conversions@@@The Rubrik cluster converts regular expressions used during the specification of a fileset rule...","common/fileset_regular_expression_handling.html@@@Regular expression handling@@@Fileset rules convert to regular expressions that follow the Boost regular expression syntax guidelines...","common/gcp_cces_cloud_api_access.html@@@GCP cloud API access points@@@Information about the cloud API access points for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Google Cloud Platform...","common/gcp_cloud_cluster_prereqs.html@@@Prerequisites for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on GCP@@@Information about the prerequisites for configuring Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Google Cloud Platform...","common/gcp_creating_cse.html@@@Creating a key to encrypt the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on GCP recovery package@@@Create an encryption key in the Google Cloud Key Management Service that Rubrik can use to protect the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage recovery package before the cluster stores data from the package in cloud storage...","common/gcp_preparing_deploy.html@@@Preparing to deploy Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on GCP@@@Complete the prerequisite tasks to prepare the Google Cloud Platform environment for the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage deployment...","common/gcp_private_google_access.html@@@Private Google Access@@@You can configure Private Google Access on the subnet used by the network interface of the virtual machine, enabling virtual machines with only internal IP addresses to access Google APIs and services...","common/generating_an_rsa_key.html@@@Generating an RSA key@@@Generate an RSA key pair before creating an archival location that uses RSA key (Bring Your Own Key) encryption...","common/generating_an_rsa_key_2.html@@@Generating an RSA key@@@Generate an RSA key pair before creating an archival location that uses RSA key (Bring Your Own Key) encryption...","common/host_specific_fileset_desc_rules.html@@@Host-specific fileset description rules@@@Rules for fileset descriptions differ for host types, ensuring accurate file path configurations, preventing backup errors, and optimizing backup processes for different systems...","common/intelligent_data_lock.html@@@Intelligent Data Lock@@@Intelligent Data Lock is a feature that protects your account from malicious activity by delaying the deletion of the snapshots of the data sources backed up by Rubrik clusters...","common/mssql_server_backup_permissions.html@@@Microsoft SQL Server backup and restore permissions@@@Permissions and roles required for Rubrik CDM backup and restore operations on Microsoft SQL Server...","common/node_req_cces_aws.html@@@Node requirements for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services@@@Lists the required node configurations for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services, based on workload density...","common/node_req_cces_azure.html@@@Node requirements for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Lists the required node configurations for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure, based on workload density...","common/node_req_cces_gcp.html@@@Node requirements for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on GCP@@@Lists the required node configurations for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Google Cloud Platform, based on workload density...","common/node_req_cces_oci.html@@@Node requirements for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI@@@Lists the required node configurations for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure, based on workload density...","common/oci_cloud_cluster_prereqs.html@@@Prerequisites for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI@@@Information about the prerequisites for provisioning Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure...","common/oci_create_image_capability_schema.html@@@Create an image capability schema@@@An image capability schema enables a Rubrik custom image to boot Gen 2 virtual machines on OCI...","common/oci_network_security_group_rules.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI network security group rules@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure requires specific network security group rules, including inbound and outbound access for SSH, HTTPS, and communication between cluster nodes and the Rubrik Backup Service...","common/oci_policy_reqs_rubrik_cc.html@@@Policy requirements for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI@@@A Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage deployment on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure requires a custom policy, which you configure through Oracle Cloud Infrastructure...","common/oci_preparing_custom_image.html@@@Preparing the Rubrik OCI custom image@@@To prepare the Rubrik Oracle Cloud Infrastructure custom image, log in to the Oracle Cloud Console and import the Rubrik VMDK image from an Oracle Storage bucket that you select...","common/oci_uploading_custom_image.html@@@Uploading the Rubrik OCI custom image@@@To deploy Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure, upload the Rubrik VMDK image to an Oracle Cloud Infrastructure object storage bucket by logging into the Oracle Cloud Console, selecting the appropriate bucket, and completing the upload process...","common/oci_uploading_image_oci_cloud_shell.html@@@Uploading the custom image from OCI Cloud Shell@@@Download the Rubrik OCI VMDK file from Rubrik support, then use Oracle Cloud Shell commands to upload the file and import it as a custom image...","common/required_ports_cc_gcp.html@@@Required ports for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on GCP@@@Information about the inbound, outbound, and HotAdd proxy ports required for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Google Cloud Platform...","common/required_settings_private_endpoints.html@@@Required settings for private endpoints@@@The following settings are required when you create a private endpoint. All other settings accept default values or values appropriate for your environment...","common/saas_audit_logs.html@@@SaaS application audit logs table@@@Use the audit logs for SaaS applications to view and filter details about user-initiated events, such as displaying the events with a specific severity or status...","common/saas_audit_logs_2.html@@@SaaS application audit logs table@@@Use the audit logs for SaaS applications to view and filter details about user-initiated events, such as displaying the events with a specific severity or status...","common/saas_creating_reports_instances.html@@@Creating reports for SaaS applications@@@Create reports for SaaS applications to view information in your application, such as compliance status and protection status, using the available templates, which you can customize for each report type. You can use the data gathered in the reports to perform audits and data management planning...","common/saas_creating_reports_instances_2.html@@@Creating reports for SaaS applications@@@Create reports for SaaS applications to view information in your application, such as compliance status and protection status, using the available templates, which you can customize for each report type. You can use the data gathered in the reports to perform audits and data management planning...","common/saas_creating_sla_domains.html@@@Creating an SLA Domain for SaaS applications@@@Create an SLA Domain with custom backup frequency and retention policies to retain snapshot data beyond a year...","common/saas_creating_sla_domains_2.html@@@Creating an SLA Domain for SaaS applications@@@Create an SLA Domain with custom backup frequency and retention policies to retain snapshot data beyond a year...","common/saas_creating_sla_domains_3.html@@@Creating an SLA Domain for SaaS applications@@@Create an SLA Domain with custom backup frequency and retention policies to retain snapshot data beyond a year...","common/saas_deleting_sla_domain.html@@@Deleting an SLA Domain for SaaS applications@@@Delete an SLA Domain you created for SaaS applications from RSC when it is no longer needed...","common/saas_deleting_sla_domain_2.html@@@Deleting an SLA Domain for SaaS applications@@@Delete an SLA Domain you created for SaaS applications from RSC when it is no longer needed...","common/saas_deleting_sla_domain_3.html@@@Deleting an SLA Domain for SaaS applications@@@Delete an SLA Domain you created for SaaS applications from RSC when it is no longer needed...","common/saas_downloading_file_prep_center.html@@@Downloading reports from the SaaS Preparation Center@@@Download reports from the File Preparation Center, for example, a compliance report that you created...","common/saas_downloading_file_prep_center_2.html@@@Downloading reports from the SaaS Preparation Center@@@Download reports from the File Preparation Center, for example, a compliance report that you created...","common/saas_events.html@@@SaaS application events@@@RSC tracks, monitors, and displays all SaaS application events in a unified view for all connected instances. For example, you can view backup and recovery events and statuses, such as succeeded or failed...","common/saas_events_2.html@@@SaaS application events@@@RSC tracks, monitors, and displays all SaaS application events in a unified view for all connected instances. For example, you can view backup and recovery events and statuses, such as succeeded or failed...","common/saas_events_filter.html@@@SaaS application events filters table@@@SaaS application events can alert you when backup is unsuccessful...","common/saas_events_filter_2.html@@@SaaS application events filters table@@@SaaS application events can alert you when backup is unsuccessful...","common/saas_file_preparation_center.html@@@SaaS File Preparation Center@@@The File Preparation Center tab on the Events page provides information about reports downloaded or sent to email recipients...","common/saas_file_preparation_center_2.html@@@SaaS File Preparation Center@@@The File Preparation Center tab on the Events page provides information about reports downloaded or sent to email recipients...","common/saas_managing_protection.html@@@Managing protection for SaaS applications@@@Protect SaaS applications, such as Atlassian Jira and Salesforce, by assigning them to an SLA Domain. This protects the instance by applying backup frequency and retention policies...","common/saas_managing_protection_2.html@@@Managing protection for SaaS applications@@@Protect SaaS applications, such as Atlassian Jira and Salesforce, by assigning them to an SLA Domain. This protects the instance by applying backup frequency and retention policies...","common/saas_report_templates.html@@@SaaS application report templates table@@@RSCprovides a template for each report category. You can use default reports as basic templates and modify them to create new reports. The following table describes the available report template types...","common/saas_report_templates_2.html@@@SaaS application report templates table@@@RSCprovides a template for each report category. You can use default reports as basic templates and modify them to create new reports. The following table describes the available report template types...","common/saas_viewing_audit_logs.html@@@Viewing SaaS application audit logs@@@The Audit logs display user-initiated events listed by user name for SaaS application events. You can also download audit log messages...","common/saas_viewing_audit_logs_2.html@@@Viewing SaaS application audit logs@@@The Audit logs display user-initiated events listed by user name for SaaS application events. You can also download audit log messages...","common/saas_viewing_events.html@@@Viewing SaaS application events@@@View SaaS application events for important details, such as successful data restores...","common/saas_viewing_events_2.html@@@Viewing SaaS application events@@@View SaaS application events for important details, such as successful data restores...","common/sass_reporting.html@@@SaaS application reporting@@@You can create reports about SaaS application data protection to view status information about an instance. You can use the provided report type templates and customize the default templates as needed...","common/sass_reporting_2.html@@@SaaS application reporting@@@You can create reports about SaaS application data protection to view status information about an instance. You can use the provided report type templates and customize the default templates as needed...","common/setting_boot_firmware_oci_cloud_shell.html@@@Setting the boot firmware from OCI Cloud Shell@@@Set the boot firmware from the OCI Cloud Shell to change the image capability...","common/setting_boot_firmware_oci_console_ui.html@@@Setting the boot firmware from OCI Console UI@@@Use the OCI Console to set the boot firmware and change the image capability...","common/sql_always_on_availability_groups.html@@@Always On Availability Groups@@@The Rubrik cluster supports data protection for availability databases in an Always On availability group...","common/sql_change_block_tracking.html@@@SQL Change Block Tracking@@@Change Block Tracking uses a filter driver to track SQL database file changes as they happen...","common/sql_live_mount.html@@@Live Mount@@@A Live Mount creates a new database from a point-in-time copy of the source database. The Rubrik cluster provides a Samba share of the new database directly from the Rubrik cluster storage layer...","common/sql_point_in_time_recovery.html@@@Point-in-time recovery@@@For a database that uses the full recovery model or the bulk-logged recovery model, the Rubrik cluster uses a combination of a snapshot of the database and the database transaction log backups to recover a database...","common/sql_protect_mssql_databases.html@@@Protect Microsoft SQL Server databases@@@RSC provides automated and on-demand methods for protecting your Microsoft SQL Server databases...","common/sql_requirements.html@@@Microsoft SQL Server requirements@@@Requirements for adding Microsoft SQL Server hosts to RSC for data protection...","common/sql_server_databases.html@@@Microsoft SQL Server databases@@@A Rubrik cluster provides data management and protection for Microsoft SQL Server databases...","common/sql_server_log_shipping.html@@@Microsoft SQL Server log shipping@@@Automatically send transaction log backups from a primary database running on a primary server instance to one or more secondary databases running on separate secondary server instances by using the Microsoft SQL Server log shipping feature...","common/sql_windows_server_hosts.html@@@Windows Server hosts@@@Manage and protect Microsoft SQL Server databases through the Rubrik Backup Service running on a Windows Server host...","common/vcenter_metro_storage_clusters.html@@@vCenter Metro Storage Clusters@@@A Metro Storage Cluster is a type of vCenter Server that is geographically distributed...","common/vs_in_place_recovery.html@@@In-place recovery of virtual machines@@@VMware In-Place Recovery is a faster and more efficient alternative for virtual machine recovery, compared with other VMware recovery options...","common/vs_ipr_prechecks_and_failure.html@@@In-place recovery pre-check and failure conditions@@@To avoid any potential loss of data and network misconfiguration, the In-Place Recovery process performs certain checks before proceeding with the recovery...","compat_matrix/rac_support_matrix.html@@@Agent Cloud support matrix@@@Agent Cloud supports multiple platform integrations, each with varying capabilities for AI agent discovery, session activity monitoring, policy enforcement, configuration violations, monitoring alerts, blocking, and ask enforcement...","confluence/confluence.html@@@Atlassian Confluence protection@@@RSC backs up your Atlassian Confluence Cloud data so that you can restore pages when content is deleted, corrupted, or compromised...","confluence/confluence_adding_site.html@@@Adding an Atlassian Confluence site@@@Add an Atlassian Confluence site to RSC to back up your Confluence spaces and restore pages and attachments...","confluence/confluence_backups.html@@@Atlassian Confluence backups@@@RSC backs up Atlassian Confluence data by taking snapshots of the spaces in your Atlassian site, automatically according to an SLA Domain or on demand...","confluence/confluence_common_terms.html@@@Common terms for Atlassian Confluence protection@@@Information about common terms that appear in the tasks for protecting and restoring Atlassian Confluence data with RSC...","confluence/confluence_configuring_roles.html@@@Creating a custom role for Atlassian Confluence@@@Create a custom role so that users can view, protect, and restore Atlassian Confluence data without full administrator access...","confluence/confluence_deleting_site.html@@@Removing an Atlassian site@@@Remove an Atlassian site from RSC to stop protecting it and delete its snapshots and configuration...","confluence/confluence_key_features.html@@@Key features for Atlassian Confluence protection@@@RSC provides automated backups, granular recovery, and centralized monitoring for your Atlassian Confluence Cloud data...","confluence/confluence_permissions.html@@@OAuth authentication for Atlassian Confluence site connection@@@RSC uses OAuth to connect to the Atlassian site that you want to protect. You must use the global administrator credentials of the site to authorize the connection...","confluence/confluence_protection_sla_domain.html@@@Protecting Atlassian Confluence with SLA Domains@@@You can protect Atlassian Confluence data by assigning an SLA Domain to the Atlassian site. The SLA Domain defines how often RSC takes snapshots and how long it retains them...","confluence/confluence_rbac.html@@@Required RBAC permissions for Atlassian Confluence@@@Managing Atlassian Confluence protection in RSC requires a role with the appropriate RBAC permissions...","confluence/confluence_recovering_pages.html@@@Restoring Atlassian Confluence pages@@@Restore Confluence pages and their child pages from a snapshot to their original location or to a new folder in the same space...","confluence/confluence_recovery.html@@@Atlassian Confluence recovery@@@You can restore Atlassian Confluence pages from any snapshot that RSC retains...","confluence/confluence_requirements.html@@@Atlassian Confluence protection requirements@@@Your Atlassian site and accounts must meet specific requirements before you add an Atlassian Confluence site to RSC...","confluence/confluence_supported_data_types.html@@@Supported Atlassian Confluence data types@@@RSC backs up Atlassian Confluence spaces and restores pages, blog posts, attachments, and related metadata, with some limitations...","confluence/confluence_taking_on_demand_snapshots.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Atlassian Confluence spaces@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of one or more Confluence spaces to back up data outside the SLA Domain schedule, such as before a large content change...","confluence/confluence_workflow.html@@@Atlassian Confluence protection implementation workflow@@@Protecting Atlassian Confluence data with RSC follows a workflow from planning and onboarding through recovery and monitoring...","cshelp.html@@@Context Sensitive Help@@@...","db2/access_db2_reports.html@@@Access Db2 reports@@@You can use reports in RSC to track the protection status, SLA compliance, and backup activity of Db2 instances and databases for audits, compliance reviews, and data management planning...","db2/adding_db2_db_instance.html@@@Adding a Db2 database instance@@@Add a Db2 database instance to a Rubrik cluster to establish a connection for database protection...","db2/adding_db2_host_high_avail_clstrng.html@@@Adding a Db2 host for high availability clustering@@@Add a Db2 host to protect a single Db2 instance or individual host data for different workloads along with the Db2 instance for Rubrik CDM version 9.1.1 and later for high availability cluster configurations...","db2/archiving_db2_snapshots.html@@@Archiving for Db2 snapshots@@@You can include an archival policy in an SLA Domain to archive Db2 snapshots to an archival location for long-term retention...","db2/assigning_protection_db2_objects.html@@@Assigning protection to Db2 objects@@@To protect Db2 databases, manage protection by selecting an SLA Domain with defined data protection policies...","db2/changing_retention_db2_snapshot.html@@@Changing retention policy of a Db2 snapshot@@@You can change the retention policy of a Db2 snapshot to optimize storage and data accessibility of Db2 databases. The SLA Domain policy retains snapshots for the maximum SLA Domain period, while the Forever retention policy retains snapshots until you delete them manually...","db2/common_db2_protection_terms.html@@@Common Db2 protection terms@@@Common terms used when protecting Db2 workloads with RSC...","db2/configuration_parameters_db2_databases.html@@@Configuration parameters for Db2 databases@@@Database configuration parameters that RSC validates and sets for Db2 protection...","db2/configure_db2_protection.html@@@Configure Db2 protection@@@Configure protection for your Db2 workloads by assigning SLA Domains, managing protection settings, and taking on-demand snapshots...","db2/configure_high_availability_db2.html@@@Configure high availability for Db2@@@Db2 high availability with RSC supports Db2 high availability clustering and High Availability Disaster Recovery (HADR)...","db2/configuring_compression_db2.html@@@Configuring compression for Db2 databases@@@To reduce the storage footprint of Db2 backups, configure compression at the source for individual Db2 databases...","db2/configuring_multiple_concurrent_sessions_db2.html@@@Configuring multiple concurrent sessions in Db2@@@To optimize Db2 backup performance, configure multiple concurrent sessions for simultaneous tasks. This reduces downtime and maximizes resource utilization...","db2/configuring_parallelism_db2.html@@@Configuring parallelism in Db2@@@To optimize Db2 backup performance, configure parallel reading across multiple table spaces. This enables simultaneous backup streams, minimizing database downtime and maximizing resource utilization...","db2/creating_custom_sla_db2.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain for Db2@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to define the backup frequency, retention, and archival policies for your Db2 workloads...","db2/creating_reports_db2.html@@@Creating reports for Db2@@@Create a report in RSC to summarize the protection, compliance, capacity, or task details for your Db2 objects...","db2/creating_template_scripts_dpf_cdm_v9.x.html@@@Creating template scripts for DPF environment@@@Create a template script to restore the Db2 database for Database Partitioning Feature environment in CDM version 9.x...","db2/creating_template_scripts_standalone_cdm_v9.x.html@@@Creating template scripts for standalone environment@@@To support the restoration process, enhance operational efficiency, and ensure data integrity, create a template script to restore the Db2 database for a standalone environment in CDM version 9.x...","db2/db2_adding_host.html@@@Adding a Db2 host@@@To establish a connection between the Db2 server and RSC, add a host to enable backup and recovery operations...","db2/db2_compressed_backups.html@@@Db2 backup compression@@@Db2 backup compression reduces the storage footprint of Db2 backups by compressing backup data at the source using Db2 default compression...","db2/db2_cross_host_recovery.html@@@Db2 cross-host recovery@@@You can restore a database to a host other than the original database host using Db2 cross-host recovery...","db2/db2_data_retrieval.html@@@Db2 data retrieval@@@Data retrieval methods such as db2_fetch_tool or db2_fetch_log_main ensure data integrity and continuity by downloading the data and log backup images if a Db2 system fails...","db2/db2_database_restore_cdm_v9.x.html@@@Db2 database restore in CDM@@@Db2 database restore in CDM supports restoring databases in standalone, DPF, and HADR environments, covering both same-instance and cross-instance restore scenarios across CDM versions 9.x...","db2/db2_db_cross_restore_dpf_cdm_v9.x.html@@@Db2 database cross restore for DPF environment@@@The Db2 database cross restore process to different instances in a Database Partitioning Feature environment involves creating and editing a template script. The modified script then migrates data while maintaining data integrity in CDM versions 9.x...","db2/db2_db_cross_restore_standalone_cdm_v9.x.html@@@Db2 database cross restore for standalone environment@@@The Db2 database cross restore process to different instances in a standalone environment involves creating and editing a template script. The modified script then migrates data while maintaining data integrity in CDM versions 9.x...","db2/db2_db_details.html@@@Db2 database details@@@Information about the selected Db2 database, including the Overview, Events, and Snapshots tabs, and the available actions...","db2/db2_db_overview.html@@@Db2 database overview@@@Information about the Db2 database Overview tab for viewing protection status, object details, capacity, and tracking snapshot history through a calendar view that provides a summary of key metrics and details for the selected Db2 database...","db2/db2_db_recovery_using_rsc.html@@@Db2 database recovery using RSC@@@RSC provides two Db2 recovery options, point-in-time and end-of-backup, and supports recovering databases to the original, a different, or a new database instance...","db2/db2_db_snapshots.html@@@Db2 database snapshots@@@Information about the Db2 database Snapshots tab for managing and monitoring the snapshots that provide insights into details such as the date and time of the snapshot, snapshot type, and other relevant information for the selected Db2 database. You can filter the snapshots by time range, snapshot type, customizations, and legal hold...","db2/db2_external_backup_trigger.html@@@Db2 external backup trigger@@@RSC enables you to initiate Db2 database backups using external tools such as the Db2 CLI. This method provides control and flexibility over backup scheduling because it does not rely on Rubrik-managed SLA Domain policies to trigger backups...","db2/db2_high_avail_clstrng_config.html@@@Db2 high availability cluster configurations@@@High availability cluster configurations are host-side configurations for Db2 environments on AIX and Linux operating systems. These configurations manage the failover of applications and resources to ensure application availability during hardware or software failures...","db2/db2_instance_configuration.html@@@Configure Db2 instance@@@You can add Db2 hosts and Db2 database instances to RSC so that RSC can discover and protect the databases that belong to each instance...","db2/db2_purescale.html@@@Db2 pureScale@@@Db2 pureScale is a clustered system that facilitates collaborative and scalable processing of database requests. With Db2 pureScale, you can achieve enhanced performance and shared data management by adding members to the pureScale cluster...","db2/db2_recovery_prerequisites.html@@@Db2 RSC-based recovery prerequisites@@@To ensure a successful recovery using RSC, the Db2 environment must meet specific requirements...","db2/db2_restore_purescale_cluster.html@@@Db2 database restore within a pureScale cluster@@@When maintaining continuity of operations and ensuring data integrity are crucial, you can initiate database restoration within a pureScale cluster, thereby achieving seamless data recovery and enhancing overall reliability...","db2/db2_snapshots_replication.html@@@Db2 snapshots replication@@@You can use the SLA Domain replication policy to replicate Db2 snapshots from one Rubrik cluster to another for disaster recovery...","db2/deleting_db2_db_instance.html@@@Deleting a Db2 database instance@@@To manage and organize the Rubrik cluster by removing databases that are not contributing to a Db2 workload, delete the Db2 database instance...","db2/deleting_hadr_entity.html@@@Deleting HADR entities@@@To remove an obsolete HADR configuration, delete the HADR entity associated with the outdated configuration from the Db2 database...","db2/disabling_cross_host_recovr_db2_databases.html@@@Disabling cross-host recovery for Db2 databases@@@Disable cross-host recovery for a Db2 database to prevent its files from being restored to a host other than its original host...","db2/discovery_db2_purescale.html@@@Discovery of Db2 pureScale@@@Db2 pureScale discovery involves identifying components within a pureScale cluster, such as member hosts and pureScale instances. You can discover and protect your pureScale instances and their associated databases within Db2 using RSC for improved management and protection...","db2/downloading_archived_db2_snapshot.html@@@Downloading an archived Db2 snapshot@@@Download an archived snapshot of a Db2 database to a Rubrik cluster to restore the snapshot...","db2/downloading_db2_data_backup_img_linux.html@@@Downloading a Db2 data backup image@@@From a set of data backup images, download the data backup image for a database using the standalone, Database Partitioning Feature, or High Availability Disaster Recovery configurations. Then, use the downloaded backup image to verify the Db2 data retrieval process on CDM versions 9.0.1 or later...","db2/downloading_db2_log_backup_images_9.0.0_9.0.1.html@@@Downloading Db2 log backup images for CDM@@@Download the log backup images for a database to retrieve transaction logs that are required for verifying the Db2 data retrieval process for Rubrik CDM versions 9.0.0 and 9.0.1...","db2/downloading_db2_log_backup_img_linux.html@@@Downloading a Db2 log backup image@@@From a set of data backup images, download the log backup image for a database using the standalone, Database Partitioning Feature, or High Availability Disaster Recovery configuration. Then, use the downloaded backup image to retrieve transaction logs required for verifying the Db2 data retrieval process on Rubrik CDM versions 9.0.1 or later...","db2/downloading_replicated_db2_snapshot.html@@@Downloading a replicated Db2 snapshot@@@Download a replicated data snapshot of a Db2 database to the source Rubrik cluster for recovery...","db2/editing_cross_host_recovr_db2_databases.html@@@Editing cross-host recovery for Db2 databases@@@Edit cross-host recovery settings for Db2 databases to add or remove hosts where the database can be restored...","db2/editing_db2_db_instance.html@@@Editing a Db2 database instance@@@To modify a Db2 database instance protected by a Rubrik cluster, edit the Db2 database instance settings...","db2/editing_template_scripts_dpf_cdm_v9.x.html@@@Editing template scripts for DPF environment@@@After creating a template script, edit the script to customize and ensure accuracy of the recovery procedure for the target Db2 database in CDM version 9.x...","db2/editing_template_scripts_standalone_cdm_v9.x.html@@@Editing template scripts for standalone environment@@@After creating a template script, edit the script to customize and ensure accuracy of the recovery procedure for the target Db2 database in CDM version 9.x...","db2/enabling_cross_host_recovr_db2_databases.html@@@Enabling cross-host recovery for Db2 databases@@@Enable cross-host recovery for Db2 databases to authorize restoring Db2 files to a host other than its original host. This feature is available for Rubrik CDM versions 9.3.1 and later...","db2/evaluate_db2_protection_options.html@@@Evaluate Db2 protection options@@@Before you configure protection, evaluate the retention, archival, and replication options available for your Db2 workloads...","db2/event_log_details_db2.html@@@Event log details for Db2@@@Information about Db2 event logs that provide insights into details such as event types, statuses, and timestamps for Db2 databases. You can filter events by time range, severity, status, and event type...","db2/hadr_setup_management.html@@@HADR setup management@@@With HADR setup management, you can gain control of your High Availability Disaster Recovery environment, ensuring disaster recovery and minimizing downtime and data loss. This includes the flexibility to delete HADR entities in any state, simplifying management tasks, and enhancing data protection...","db2/high_availability_disaster_recovery.html@@@High Availability Disaster Recovery@@@High Availability Disaster Recovery in Db2 for Linux, Unix, and Windows ensures uninterrupted system operation and data protection against hardware failures, software errors, natural disasters, power outages, and network issues...","db2/high_level_architecture_db2_protection.html@@@High-level architecture for Db2 protection@@@RSC uses an agent-based architecture to communicate with Db2 hosts through Rubrik Backup Service (RBS) and its Vendorlib client, and applies a protection hierarchy to assign SLA Domains to Db2 instances and databases...","db2/high_level_impl_workflow_db2.html@@@High-level implementation workflow for Db2@@@The Db2 protection implementation workflow involves a structured approach to secure data management, starting with planning and preparation, followed by Db2 workload setup, protection configuration, ongoing management, high availability configuration where required, and workload recovery...","db2/ibm_db2.html@@@IBM Db2@@@RSC protects IBM Db2 databases running on Linux, Windows, and AIX hosts across on-premises and supported public cloud deployments, with automated discovery, application-consistent backups, and point-in-time recovery...","db2/ibm_db2_protection_overview.html@@@IBM Db2 protection overview@@@RSC protects IBM Db2 databases running on Linux, Windows, and AIX hosts across on-premises and supported public cloud deployments, with automated discovery, application-consistent backups, and point-in-time recovery...","db2/key_features_db2_protection.html@@@Key features for Db2 protection@@@RSC provides automated discovery, declarative policy-based protection, point-in-time recovery, and unified management for Db2 workloads running on-premises and in the public cloud...","db2/legal_hold_db2_snapshots.html@@@Legal hold for Db2 snapshots@@@Legal hold ensures that snapshots required for litigation are protected for the duration of the legal hold, providing a compliant and efficient way to manage data subject to legal obligations...","db2/limitations_db2_protection.html@@@Limitations for Db2 protection@@@Known limitations for Db2 protection with RSC across backup, restore, deployment, and configuration...","db2/manage_db2_objects.html@@@Manage Db2 objects@@@Managing Db2 instances and databases in RSC includes viewing, editing, refreshing, and deleting Db2 database instances, accessing database details and snapshots, and viewing events...","db2/multiple_archival_locations_db2.html@@@Multiple archival locations for Db2@@@RSC supports multiple archival locations for Db2 objects, providing granular control over data archiving with up to two distinct archiving policies...","db2/parallelism_sessions_database_level.html@@@Parallelism and sessions at the database level@@@Parallelism is the ability to simultaneously read and back up different sections within the database during backup operations. Sessions represent the maximum number of concurrent connections allowed between Db2 and the Rubrik cluster. With support for parallelism and sessions at the database level, you can optimize your backup process for improved efficiency and speed...","db2/permissions_db2_protection.html@@@Permissions for Db2 protection@@@Role-based Access Control (RBAC) permissions in RSC required to protect, manage, and recover Db2 workloads, together with the Db2 host operating system privileges required by Rubrik Backup Service (RBS)...","db2/placing_legal_hold_db2_db_snapshot.html@@@Placing a legal hold on the Db2 database snapshot@@@To prevent the automatic expiration and removal of the Db2 database snapshot by the Rubrik cluster, place a legal hold on the snapshot for compliance and data retention...","db2/plan_db2_protection.html@@@Plan Db2 protection@@@Before adding Db2 hosts and instances to RSC, you can plan your deployment by reviewing the workload requirements, configuration parameters, role-based access control permissions, and known limitations...","db2/post_rbs_upgrade_mgmt_db2_win.html@@@Post RBS upgrade management for Db2 on Windows@@@After the Rubrik Backup Service upgrade, Db2 may encounter errors due to outdated processes. Restarting the database manager fixes the issue by updating necessary processes, ensuring that Db2 archives logs without errors...","db2/primary_snapshot_retention_db2.html@@@Primary snapshot retention for Db2@@@Primary snapshot retention for Db2 databases provides data protection and recoverability by making it possible to set various retention policies. These policies include hourly, daily, monthly, and yearly retention of snapshots to meet compliance, business continuity, and disaster recovery requirements...","db2/protecting_hadr_entity.html@@@Protecting an HADR entity@@@To ensure high availability and disaster recovery capabilities for your Db2 database, protect an HADR entity for an SLA Domain...","db2/quick_links_db2.html@@@Quick links for Db2@@@Immediate access to the most-used Db2 setup, day-to-day operations, and recovery tasks...","db2/recover_db2.html@@@Recover Db2@@@When incidents that result in data failure or corruption occur, the Db2 restore and rollforward processes recover data from backups to ensure that all data is available, accurate, and complete...","db2/recoverable_range_db2.html@@@Recoverable range for Db2 database@@@The recoverable range for a Db2 database is a visual representation of the duration within which you can recover a database to a specific point in time...","db2/recovering_db2_db_different_db.html@@@Restoring a Db2 database to a different database@@@Recover a Db2 database to an existing database that is different from the source database...","db2/recovering_db2_db_new_db.html@@@Restoring a Db2 database to a new database@@@Recover a Db2 database by creating a new database on a target instance...","db2/refreshing_db2_db_instance.html@@@Refreshing a Db2 database instance@@@To ensure that the information on a Rubrik cluster is up to date and accurate, refresh the Db2 database instance. When you refresh a Db2 database instance, all databases local to the selected instance are discovered and the relevant metadata is updated...","db2/refreshing_hadr_entity.html@@@Refreshing HADR entities@@@When configuration changes or inconsistencies occur, refresh the HADR entity to maintain consistent information between primary and standby instances of the Db2 database...","db2/removing_hadr_protection.html@@@Removing the HADR protection@@@To adjust protection strategies or reallocate resources, remove the HADR protection from SLA Domain assignments, excluding the HADR protection from upcoming backup and recovery workflows...","db2/removing_legal_hold_db2_snapshot.html@@@Removing a legal hold from the Db2 database snapshot@@@To return to regular retention management and optimize storage, remove the legal hold from the Db2 database snapshot, allowing it to follow the SLA Domain policies and be managed or deleted automatically as needed...","db2/requirements_db2_protection.html@@@Requirements for Db2 protection@@@Requirements for adding Db2 hosts and Db2 database instances to RSC for data protection...","db2/restoring_db2_db_hadr_cdm_v9.x.html@@@Restoring Db2 databases for HADR environment@@@In CDM version 9.x, when the source and target instances are the same, restore a database with the same instance for High Availability Disaster Recovery environment...","db2/restoring_db2_db_original_database.html@@@Restoring a Db2 database to the original database@@@Perform an in-place restoration of a Db2 database to its original instance and location...","db2/restoring_db2_db_standalone_cdm_v9.x.html@@@Restoring Db2 databases for standalone environment using CLI@@@In CDM version 9.x, when the source and target instances are the same, restore a database with the same instance for a standalone environment...","db2/retention_lock_db2_protection.html@@@Retention lock for Db2 protection@@@A retention lock on an RSC SLA Domain is a security feature that prevents premature deletion of Db2 snapshots...","db2/retrieving_db2_backup_id_type_snapshot.html@@@Retrieving the Db2 backup ID and backup type of a snapshot@@@To restore the Db2 backup and recovery process, retrieve the backup ID and backup type associated with a snapshot. These attributes serve as distinctive identifiers and define the category of a backup...","db2/setup_db2_workload.html@@@Set up Db2 workload@@@You can set up your Db2 workload by adding Db2 hosts and database instances to RSC, and by configuring Db2 pureScale clusters where applicable...","db2/setup_protection_db2.html@@@Set up Db2 protection@@@Setting up protection for Db2 instances and databases involves evaluating SLA Domain options, assigning protection, and configuring archival, on-demand snapshots, retention, legal holds, parallelism, and sessions...","db2/sla_domains_db2_protection.html@@@SLA Domains for Db2 protection@@@An SLA Domain defines the data protection policies that RSC applies to Db2 workloads, covering backup types, frequency, retention, archival, replication, and log archival settings...","db2/supported_db2_instance_types.html@@@Supported Db2 instance types@@@RSC protects three Db2 instance types. The instance type is determined automatically during discovery from the contents of the db2nodes.cfg file...","db2/taking_on_demand_snapshot_db2_db.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of a Db2 database@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of a Db2 database to protect critical data and ensure backups are available for recovery before high-risk tasks, peak activity, or maintenance windows...","db2/topology_changes_purescale_cluster.html@@@Topology changes within a pureScale cluster@@@Topology changes within a pureScale cluster, such as adding or dropping members, optimize performance and resource utilization across the database system...","db2/troubleshooting_db2.html@@@Troubleshooting Db2@@@You can diagnose and resolve common issues that affect Db2 host discovery, log archival, backups, and rollforward operations in RSC...","db2/using_template_scripts_dpf_cdm_v9.x.html@@@Using template scripts for DPF environment@@@After creating a template script and editing it, use the modified script to restore a Db2 database for a Database Partitioning Feature environment in CDM version 9.x...","db2/using_template_scripts_standalone_cdm_v9.x.html@@@Using template scripts for standalone environment@@@After creating a template script and editing it, use the modified script to restore a Db2 database for a standalone environment in CDM version 9.x...","db2/viewing_db2_instances.html@@@Viewing Db2 instances@@@View a list of all added Db2 instances on RSC, including their status and connectivity details...","db2/viewing_events_db2.html@@@Viewing events for Db2@@@View events for Db2 workloads to monitor backups, log archival, configuration updates, and recovery operations on Db2 databases...","db2/viewing_workload_id.html@@@Viewing workload IDs@@@View and obtain the workload ID of a Db2 database to facilitate the database restoration process...","dlc/dlc_configuring_monthly_granular_ss.html@@@Configuring monthly granular snapshot scheduling@@@Configure granular scheduling when creating or editing an SLA Domain in RSC. The options appear within the monthly frequency sections of the snapshot schedule...","dlc/dlc_configuring_weekly_granular_ss.html@@@Configuring weekly granular snapshot scheduling@@@Configure granular scheduling when creating or editing an SLA Domain in RSC. The options appear within the weekly frequency sections of the snapshot schedule...","dlc/dlc_configuring_yearly_granular_ss.html@@@Configuring yearly granular snapshot scheduling@@@Configure yearly granular snapshot scheduling when creating or editing an SLA Domain in RSC. The options appear within the yearly frequency section of the snapshot schedule...","dlc/dlc_granular_snapshot_scheduling.html@@@Granular snapshot scheduling@@@Granular snapshot scheduling gives you precise control over when Rubrik Security Cloud captures and retains snapshots, enabling flexible multi-day selections for weekly, monthly, and yearly snapshot frequencies...","dscc/data_security_command_center.html@@@Data Security Command Center@@@The Data Security Command Center provides you with an assessment of the data security readiness for your organization, providing scores for different categories and overall. The Data Security Command Center also offers recommendations to improve low data security scores...","dscc/dscc_dashboard.html@@@Data Security Command Center dashboard@@@The Data Security Command Center dashboard displays data security health scores and recommendations to improve the data security readiness of your organization...","dscc/dscc_metrics.html@@@Data Security Command Center metrics@@@The Data Security Command Center extracts metrics from supported workloads and provides scores for each category...","dscc/dscc_viewing_category_details_page.html@@@Viewing category details@@@View the category details page for the current data risk profile for a specific category and the detailed trend for the selected time period...","dscc/sharing_dscc_report.html@@@Sharing a Data Security Command Center report@@@A Data Security Command Center report lets you check how ready your organization is for data security. You can also see suggestions to improve low data security scores, helping you to make the right decisions to boost data security...","dscc/viewing_the_dscc_dashboard.html@@@Viewing Data Security Command Center dashboard@@@Access the Data Security Command Center dashboard to view the Data Security Score for the supported workloads...","dspm/actions_available_for_dsp.html@@@Actions available for data security policies@@@Actions available on the Data Security Policies page...","dspm/assigning_resources_classification.html@@@Assigning resources for classification@@@You can assign data categories to resources such as objects or clusters located in data centers, Microsoft 365 workloads, and optionally to Azure virtual machines...","dspm/category_activation_behavior.html@@@Category activation behaviors@@@The activation status of data categories and document types determines classification results and system behavior...","dspm/changing_violation_status.html@@@Changing violation status@@@Change a violation status manually to track violations more effectively...","dspm/classification_rms_encrypt_files.html@@@Classification of Azure RMS encrypted files@@@Rubrik Security Cloud decrypts and classifies Microsoft 365 files encrypted by Azure Rights Management Services to identify sensitive data within protected documents...","dspm/configuring_discovery_prefs.html@@@Configuring Data Discovery Preview and Image Classification@@@Configure Data Discovery Preview, which generates previews of identified data, and Image Classification, which detects passports and national IDs in image files, for each Rubrik cluster...","dspm/creating_data_category.html@@@Creating a data category@@@Create a data category to look for specific classification information in Data Security Posture...","dspm/creating_data_type.html@@@Creating a data type@@@You can create customized data types to reflect your business and security policies and processes...","dspm/creating_jira_ticket_insights.html@@@Creating a Jira ticket from Insights@@@Create a Jira ticket to address sensitive data access issues identified by Insights in Data Security Posture...","dspm/creating_policies_in_dsp.html@@@Creating policies in Data Security Posture@@@Create a policy with specific conditions to identify violations in Data Security Posture...","dspm/creating_sn_ticket_insights.html@@@Creating a ServiceNow ticket from Insights@@@Create a ServiceNow ticket to address sensitive data access issues identified by Insights in Data Security Posture...","dspm/data_categories.html@@@Data categories@@@Data Categories are logical groupings of data types that define the scope of Data Discovery and Classification across your protected environment...","dspm/data_classification_mgmt.html@@@Data classification management@@@Data Security Posture provides a centralized framework for managing data categories, data types, and document types...","dspm/data_classification_scope.html@@@Data classification scope@@@The data categories that you enable define the scope of Data Discovery and Classification across an organization...","dspm/data_masking.html@@@Data masking@@@Data masking replaces sensitive values in sampled data with obfuscated substitutes. This feature protects privacy while preserving the ability to understand data classified by Data Discovery and Classification...","dspm/data_security_posture.html@@@Data Security Posture@@@Data Security Posture provides agile data security across multi-cloud environments for posture management and access governance. It also includes threat monitoring and response to protect your data...","dspm/data_types.html@@@Data types@@@Data Types are the detection rules that Data Discovery and Classification uses to identify specific patterns of sensitive information across your workloads...","dspm/document_type_classification.html@@@Document type classification@@@The document type classification provided by Data Security Posture helps you to set better data protection policies, reduce risks, and ensure regulatory compliance...","dspm/document_types.html@@@Document types@@@Document types control which file formats are included in Data Discovery and Classification scans...","dspm/downloading_remediation_logs.html@@@Downloading remediation logs in Data Security Posture@@@Generate and download a remediation log for a specific violation in Data Security Posture...","dspm/downloading_violating_files_log.html@@@Downloading the violating files log in Data Security Posture@@@Generate and download a log of violating files in Data Security Posture...","dspm/dsp_aws_identities_information.html@@@AWS identities information@@@The AWS Identities page provides data access assessment and monitoring capabilities for data found in assets across your cloud landscape...","dspm/dsp_aws_req_perms.html@@@Required permissions for Data Security Posture@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to generate Data Security Posture insights for AWS objects...","dspm/dsp_azr_req_perms.html@@@Required permissions for Data Security Posture@@@Information about permissions RSC requires to scan and provide Data Security Posture information in Azure subscriptions...","dspm/dsp_azr_req_perms_outpost_accnt.html@@@Required permissions for the Azure outpost account@@@Information about the permissions that the outpost account requires to access the Azure account...","dspm/dsp_enterprise_edition_dashboard.html@@@Data Security Posture Enterprise Edition dashboard@@@The Data Security Posture dashboard for the Rubrik Enterprise Edition provides a high-level view of your sensitive data, across protected workloads configured for Data Security Posture...","dspm/dsp_epe_dashboard.html@@@Data Security Posture management dashboard@@@The Data Security Posture management dashboard provides a unified view of where sensitive data resides across cloud, datacenter, and SaaS environments. Interactive charts and detailed breakdowns allow you to quickly identify, investigate, and address data most at risk to strengthen overall data security...","dspm/dsp_policies.html@@@Data Security Posture policies@@@Data Security Posture policies deliver specific data security frameworks for protecting data and simplifying the management of data breaches in complex cloud infrastructures...","dspm/dsp_req_perms_aws_outpost_accnt.html@@@Required permissions for the AWS outpost account@@@Information about the permissions that the outpost account requires to access the AWS account...","dspm/dsp_single_violation_details.html@@@Single violation details@@@You can view the details of a single violation for an object, the data at risk, and the object...","dspm/dsp_threats.html@@@Threats feature in Data Security Posture@@@You can use the Threats feature in Data Security Posture to detect external and internal data breaches in your environment...","dspm/dsp_violations.html@@@Violations in Data Security Posture@@@Policy violations in Data Security Posture provide detailed information and analysis of why a data security or compliance violation is indicated...","dspm/dsp_violations_info.html@@@Data Security Posture violations information@@@The Data Security violations page in Data Security Posture provides information on the active, created, and resolved violations on objects that Data Security Posture protects...","dspm/dspm_identity_inventory.html@@@Identity Inventory@@@The Identity Inventory provides visibility into data that identities in your environment can access...","dspm/identity_document_classification.html@@@Identity document classification@@@Data Security Posture uses machine learning to detect passports and national IDs in image files that text-based classification cannot identify...","dspm/managing_allowed_hits.html@@@Managing allowed hits@@@Manage allowed hits in Data Security Posture for current and future files...","dspm/managing_data_category_class.html@@@Managing data category classification@@@Manage data category status to control which data types are included in classification across workloads...","dspm/managing_data_types.html@@@Managing data types@@@Manage data type status to control which detection rules are active during Data Discovery and Classification scans...","dspm/managing_doc_types.html@@@Managing document types@@@Manage document type status to restrict or expand the types of files included in data classification scans...","dspm/object_inventory.html@@@Object Inventory@@@The Object Inventory provides visibility into cloud objects, including sensitive data hits, impacted data categories, and active violations...","dspm/object_sensitive_data_info.html@@@Sensitive data information@@@The object details page in Data Security Posture provides information about the sensitive data in an object...","dspm/overview_dsp.html@@@Data Security Posture overview@@@Using Data Security Posture, you can leverage extensive information about data living in your cloud, SaaS, and on-premises environments to easily prevent data breaches. Additionally, you can create effective data security guardrails, and meet compliance and regulatory needs...","dspm/predefined_data_categories.html@@@Predefined data types@@@Predefined data types are used in predefined data categories. They are available in RSC for creating custom data categories to detect sensitive data...","dspm/previewing_data_samples.html@@@Previewing data samples@@@Preview data samples to verify Data Discovery and Classification accuracy...","dspm/rbac_dsp.html@@@RBAC for Data Security Posture@@@Information about the privileges required for Data Security Posture access. These privileges help in configuring Role-Based Access Control for users...","dspm/remediating_viols_jira_ticket.html@@@Remediating violations by creating Jira tickets@@@Remediate data security violations by creating Jira tickets to assign tasks to stakeholders in an external ticketing system...","dspm/remediating_viols_sn_ticket.html@@@Remediating violations by creating ServiceNow tickets@@@Remediate data security violations by creating ServiceNow tickets to assign tasks to stakeholders in an external ticketing system...","dspm/scanning_error_statuses.html@@@Scanning status types@@@The Object Inventory page displays the scanning status for each object. The scanning status indicates the outcome of each scan and provides details to help resolve scan failures...","dspm/single_identity_details.html@@@Single identity details@@@You can view detailed information about a single identity, the assigned groups, and assigned radius in Data Security Posture...","dspm/supported_file_types.html@@@Supported file types@@@Information about the file types that Data Security Posture analyzes and performs deep inspection for classifying discovered data...","dspm/supported_workloads_data_classification.html@@@Supported workloads for data classification@@@Information about the supported workloads for data classification across on-premises environments, Rubrik clusters, and auto scanning configurations...","dspm/threat_alert_information.html@@@Threat information in Data Security Posture@@@The Threats feature in Data Security Posture identifies anomalies and malicious indicators that impact sensitive data and alerts you about data exfiltration, suspicious third-party access, insider threats, accidental data leaks, data misuse, and other threats...","dspm/user_insights.html@@@User Insights in Data Security Posture@@@You can view changes in user access to sensitive data in the Insights widget in the Data Security Posture dashboard. You can use these insights to monitor and manage potential data security risks more effectively by setting appropriate access limits...","dspm/viewing_data_security_policies.html@@@Viewing data security policies@@@View the details of the data security policies for your organization...","dspm/viewing_object_inventory.html@@@Viewing the Object Inventory@@@View the Object Inventory in Data Security Posture to understand the sensitive hits, data categories impacted, and active violations for the object...","dspm/violation_remediation.html@@@Violation remediation@@@Remediate a violation from the single violation details window...","dspm/violation_tracking_management.html@@@Violation tracking and management@@@Manage and track violations from the violations details page...","envoy/creating_organization_network.html@@@Creating an organization network@@@Create an organization network to provide a secure tunnel for communications between the tenant organization and the Rubrik cluster...","envoy/deleting_envoy_org_network.html@@@Deleting Envoy from the organization network@@@Delete a connected Rubrik Envoy from the organization network...","envoy/deleting_org_network.html@@@Deleting the organization network@@@Delete an organization network when it is no longer required...","envoy/envoy_features.html@@@Envoy features@@@The Rubrik Envoy virtual appliance connects tenant networks to the Rubrik cluster...","envoy/organization_networks.html@@@Organization networks@@@An organization network provides a secure tunnel for point-to-point communication with organization resources. An organization network also provides secure connectivity when NAT is used between a network segment and a shared Rubrik cluster that is not directly routable...","envoy/registering_envoy_on_rsc.html@@@Registering Envoy on RSC@@@Register the Rubrik Envoy virtual appliance with RSC...","envoy/reqs_configuring_specific_workloads_envoy.html@@@Requirements for configuring specific workloads to use Envoy@@@vSphere virtual machines, filesets, SQL Server databases, and Oracle databases have additional requirements for using Rubrik Envoy and connecting to the organization network...","envoy/setting_live_mount_ips_org_network.html@@@Setting Live Mount IP addresses in the organization network@@@Configure Live Mount IP addresses for use by specific workloads on RSC...","envoy/viewing_envoy_status.html@@@Viewing Envoy status@@@View the version, IP address, and connectivity status of Rubrik Envoy virtual appliances connected to an organization network...","envoy/workload_configuration_envoy_rsc.html@@@Workload configuration prerequisites when using Envoy with RSC@@@The hosts of the workloads must be assigned to the corresponding organization network to provide a secure connection to the Rubrik cluster...","forecast/amazon_s3_storage_classes.html@@@Amazon S3 storage classes@@@Amazon S3 offers several storage classes to meet different storage requirements...","forecast/arch_consol_existing_snaps.html@@@Archival Consolidation with existing snapshots@@@When enabled for an archival location with previously archived snapshots, Archival Consolidation performs consolidation tasks for new and existing snapshots only in the latest chain for each workload...","forecast/arch_consol_triggers.html@@@Consolidation trigger conditions@@@Archival Consolidation starts a compute instance to perform consolidation tasks when any of the trigger conditions exists...","forecast/azure_access_tiers.html@@@Azure access tiers@@@Azure storage offers four access tiers to meet different storage requirements...","forecast/azure_access_tiers_2.html@@@Azure access tiers@@@Azure storage offers four access tiers to meet different storage requirements...","forecast/azure_access_tiers_3.html@@@Azure access tiers@@@Azure storage offers four access tiers to meet different storage requirements...","forecast/cci_overview.html@@@Cloud cost insights overview@@@You can reduce the cost of archiving data by enabling the Archival Consolidation, Smart Tiering, and Instant Tiering settings...","forecast/instant_tiering_storage.html@@@Instant Tiering storage@@@A Rubrik cluster uses Instant Tiering based on specific SLA Domain settings...","forecast/restore_from_cold_storage.html@@@Restore from cold storage@@@To restore data from a snapshot in cold storage, the Rubrik cluster must first move the data to default storage...","forecast/smart_tiering_logic.html@@@Smart Tiering logic@@@Smart Tiering completes three decision phases when determining whether a snapshot should be moved to the archive access tier...","forecast/storage_cost_reduction_using_archival_consolidation.html@@@Storage cost reduction using archival consolidation@@@You can enable Archival Consolidation to remove expired and unnecessary snapshot data automatically from an archival location in the cloud, reducing storage requirements and costs...","forecast/storage_cost_reduction_using_instant_tiering.html@@@Storage cost reduction using Instant Tiering@@@Instant Tiering instructs the Rubrik cluster to send snapshots to cold storage immediately on archiving...","forecast/storage_cost_reduction_using_smart_tiering.html@@@Storage cost reduction using Smart Tiering@@@Smart Tiering automatically moves snapshots from higher availability access tiers to lower availability access tiers. This can save on storage costs...","gcp/adding_gcp_project_protection_oauth.html@@@Adding GCP projects for protection using OAuth@@@Add a GCP project using the OAuth method to RSC to protect the GCE instances and persistent disks, Cloud SQL instances, and BigQuery datasets in the project...","gcp/adding_gcp_projects_key_management.html@@@Adding GCP projects for key management@@@Add a GCP project to RSC to manage Google Cloud KMS keys for client-side encrypted cloud-native archival locations. RSC uses the service account of the project to access your Google Cloud KMS key...","gcp/adding_gcp_projects_storage.html@@@Adding GCP projects for cloud-native storage@@@Add a GCP project to RSC to create a cloud-native archival location used for GCP storage tiering. RSC archives snapshots of objects from other GCP projects to this project...","gcp/anomaly_detection_gce_pd.html@@@Anomaly Detection for GCE instances and persistent disks@@@Anomaly Detection for the GCE instances and persistent disks within a GCP project identifies and analyzes anomaly events that can indicate a ransomware attack and provides data recovery services for the protected resources...","gcp/archiving_gcp.html@@@Archiving for GCP workloads@@@Archiving in RSC tiers GCE instance or persistent disk snapshots to lower-cost GCS storage classes, ensuring cost savings, compliance, and security...","gcp/assigning_perm_cat_gcp_recovery.html@@@Assigning a permission category for GCP recovery@@@When you are performing recovery operations such as exporting, restoring, and file-level recovery and the target GCP project does not have the required permission category, assign the permission category to ensure recovery...","gcp/assigning_protection_gce_pd.html@@@Assigning protection to GCE instances or persistent disks@@@Assign a data protection policy to specific GCE instances or persistent disks...","gcp/assigning_protection_gcp_project.html@@@Assigning protection to GCP projects@@@Assign a data protection policy at the GCP project level...","gcp/assigning_sla_bigquery.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to BigQuery@@@You can assign an SLA Domain to Google BigQuery datasets to start protecting them with Rubrik backups...","gcp/assigning_sla_cloud_sql.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to Cloud SQL@@@You can assign an SLA Domain to Google Cloud SQL instances to start protecting them with Rubrik backups...","gcp/best_practices_gcp_sla_assignment.html@@@Best practices for GCP SLA Domain assignment@@@Information about the best practices for assigning SLA Domains to GCP workloads, ensuring effective data protection and compliance...","gcp/cnp_bigquery_gcp.html@@@Cloud-native protection for BigQuery@@@RSC protects Google BigQuery datasets in your Google Cloud Platform projects by backing up each dataset and its contents to a backup location...","gcp/cnp_gcp.html@@@Cloud-native protection for GCP@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects GCP workloads within your GCP project...","gcp/comm_rbk_gcp_project.html@@@Communication between RSC and GCP project@@@A high-level architecture overview of how RSC uses GCP IAM roles and GCP service account credentials to manage GCP workloads securely...","gcp/common_gcp_protection_terms.html@@@Common GCP protection terms@@@It is important to understand some common terms when protecting GCP workloads with RSC...","gcp/config_exocompute_gcp.html@@@Configuration of Exocompute on GCP@@@You can configure Exocompute on GCP to launch Exocompute resources to perform tasks such as restoring files and leveraging storage tiering...","gcp/config_gcp_project.html@@@Configuration of GCP project@@@Start the configuration of your GCP projects by adding them to RSC and performing other maintenance operations, such as upgrading accounts...","gcp/config_gcp_protection.html@@@Configuration of GCP protection@@@After you have decided on the SLA Domain options you want to configure, you can begin configuration by creating a custom SLA Domain and assigning protection to GCP workloads and GCP projects...","gcp/config_gcp_storage_tiering.html@@@Configuration of GCP storage tiering@@@To configure GCP storage tiering, you must create an archival location for archiving snapshots and storing backups...","gcp/creating_arch_loc_gcp_project.html@@@Creating archival locations for a GCP project@@@Create an archival location in the GCP project that you have added for the cloud-native storage use case. RSC uses this location to store GCE instance and persistent disk snapshots according to the archival policy specified in the SLA Domain...","gcp/creating_label_rules_bigquery.html@@@Creating label rules for BigQuery@@@You can create and assign a label rule to protect BigQuery datasets associated with your Google Cloud Platform projects...","gcp/creating_label_rules_cloud_sql.html@@@Creating label rules for Google Cloud SQL@@@You can create and assign a label rule to protect Cloud SQL instances associated with your GCP projects...","gcp/custom_strg_encryption_gcp.html@@@Custom storage encryption for GCP@@@When creating a GCP archival location in RSC, you can use custom storage encryption to encrypt the archived data using Customer-managed encryption keys...","gcp/deleting_gcp_projects.html@@@Deleting GCP projects@@@You can delete a GCP project from RSC when it is no longer in use...","gcp/disk_encrypt_options_export_gce_snap.html@@@Disk encryption options for exporting GCE snapshots@@@A comparative overview of the various disk encryption options available when you are exporting the snapshots of GCE instances and persistent disks...","gcp/enabling_ad_gce_pd.html@@@Enabling Anomaly Detection for GCE instances and persistent disks@@@Enable Anomaly Detection for a GCP project to analyze behavior and content of the GCE instances and persistent disks within the GCP project. This will show details about incidents that might be unusual. Enabling Anomaly Detection for a GCP project helps protect the data in the GCE instances and persistent disks from ransomware attacks...","gcp/enabling_file_index_specific_gcp_snap.html@@@Enabling file indexing for a specific GCP snapshot@@@Enable file indexing of a snapshot of a GCE instance or persistent disk for enabling file recovery...","gcp/evaluate_options_gcp_project_setup.html@@@Evaluation of options for GCP project setup@@@When adding a GCP project to RSC, it is important to evaluate the available options for adding the project...","gcp/evaluate_options_gcp_storage_tiering.html@@@Evaluation of options for GCP storage tiering@@@Before setting up Google Cloud Platform (GCP) storage tiering, it is important to evaluate the tiering options to align with archiving needs, balancing cost, performance, and data retrieval...","gcp/evaluate_sla_options_gcp.html@@@Evaluation of GCP SLA Domain options@@@Understanding the various protection options is important when creating an SLA Domain for your GCP workloads. This ensures alignment with organizational needs. By thoroughly evaluating these options, you can take informed decisions and provide effective protection for the workloads...","gcp/evaluation_options_gcp_recovery.html@@@Evaluation of options for GCP recovery@@@Understanding the recovery options for GCP is essential to ensure alignment with business needs for data consistency and availability. Thorough evaluation of these options, including disk encryption strategies, enables informed decision-making and effective data protection during recovery...","gcp/exo_gcp_setup_automation.html@@@Exocompute on GCP setup and automation@@@RSC sets up and automates Exocompute infrastructure on Google Cloud Platform by creating and configuring necessary resources...","gcp/exo_gcp_workflow_example.html@@@Exocompute on GCP workflow example@@@A workflow example to demonstrate the Exocompute lifecycle on GCP when indexing a snapshot of a GCE instance...","gcp/exocompute_gcp.html@@@Exocompute on GCP@@@With the Exocompute on GCP feature, RSC launches a Google Kubernetes Engine cluster to perform various operations to protect GCP workloads. RSC uses the Google Kubernetes Engine cluster to serve as a compute resource in your GCP project...","gcp/exporting_gce_instance_snapshot.html@@@Exporting a GCE instance snapshot@@@Export a snapshot of a GCE instance to create a point-in-time copy of that instance...","gcp/exporting_persistent_disk_snapshot.html@@@Exporting a persistent disk snapshot@@@Export a snapshot of a persistent disk to create a point-in-time copy of that disk...","gcp/file_indexing_gce_pd.html@@@File Indexing for GCE instances and disks@@@RSC uses Exocompute on GCP to extract file system index metadata from the persistent disk snapshots created when protecting GCE instances and persistent disks...","gcp/gce_disk_snapshot_management.html@@@GCE instance and persistent disk snapshots management@@@You can manage snapshots of GCE instances and persistent disks. This includes taking on-demand snapshots, changing retention policies, and deleting snapshots...","gcp/gce_instances_persistent_disks.html@@@GCE instances and persistent disks@@@After you set up protection for GCE instances and persistent disks, RSC takes automated snapshots of those instances and disks based on the policies configured in SLA Domains. You can also take on-demand snapshots and refresh GCP projects...","gcp/gce_pd_details.html@@@GCE instances and persistent disks details@@@Viewing and analyzing detailed information about GCE instances and persistent disks helps in making informed decisions. Key aspects include protection status, detailed attributes, snapshots calendar, and events log for audit and compliance...","gcp/gcp.html@@@Google Cloud Platform workloads@@@RSC protects the following types of Google Cloud Platform workloads: Google Compute Engine instances and persistent disks, Cloud SQL instances, and BigQuery datasets...","gcp/gcp_adding_projects_manually_protection.html@@@Adding GCP projects manually for protection@@@Manually onboard your Google Cloud Platform project to RSC by providing the service account key and running a Terraform template that grants the required permissions...","gcp/gcp_archive_prep.html@@@Archive preparation in GCP@@@Preparing a GCP bucket for archiving requires creating a service account and enabling object versioning and object lock on the bucket for clusters running CDM version 9.6 or later...","gcp/gcp_archive_tiering.html@@@GCP archive tiering@@@Rubrik CDM supports tiering to the GCP Archive storage class by configuring lifecycle rules in the GCP console. The Archive storage class cannot be selected directly when creating a GCP archival location in RSC...","gcp/gcp_bigquery.html@@@Google BigQuery@@@RSC supports backup and recovery of Google BigQuery datasets...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_changing_ret_pol_snapshots.html@@@Changing retention for BigQuery policy-based snapshots@@@You can change the retention policy of existing policy-based snapshots of BigQuery datasets with no SLA Domain...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_changing_retention_ods.html@@@Changing retention policy for BigQuery on-demand snapshots@@@You can change the retention policy of on-demand snapshots of a BigQuery dataset...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_changing_retention_relic.html@@@Changing retention policy for BigQuery relic snapshots@@@You can change the retention policy of snapshots of BigQuery relic datasets...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_dataset_details.html@@@BigQuery dataset details@@@Information available on the Google BigQuery dataset details page in RSC...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_deleting_label_rules.html@@@Deleting label rules for BigQuery@@@You can delete label rules assigned to BigQuery datasets...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_deleting_snapshots.html@@@Deleting BigQuery snapshots@@@You can delete snapshots of BigQuery datasets that have a Forever retention policy...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_limitations.html@@@BigQuery backup and recovery limitations@@@Backup and recovery of Google BigQuery datasets in RSC have specific backup and recovery limitations...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_pitr.html@@@BigQuery point-in-time recovery@@@RSC supports point-in-time recovery for Google BigQuery datasets, so you can recover data to a specific point in time within the BigQuery time travel window...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_recovery_options.html@@@BigQuery recovery options@@@When you recover a Google BigQuery dataset, you select a recovery source and a recovery operation...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_reservation_project.html@@@BigQuery reservation project@@@RSC uses a dedicated reservation project to run the compute for BigQuery backup and recovery operations...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_snapshot_types.html@@@Snapshot types for BigQuery@@@You can manage snapshots of Google BigQuery datasets by taking on-demand and policy-based snapshots, changing retention policies, and deleting snapshots...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_taking_ods.html@@@Taking on-demand BigQuery snapshots@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, you can take on-demand snapshots of Google BigQuery datasets...","gcp/gcp_bigquery_viewing_details.html@@@Viewing BigQuery dataset details@@@You can access the Google BigQuery inventory page to view the details of your BigQuery datasets...","gcp/gcp_changing_retention_policy_relic_snapshots.html@@@Changing the retention policy for relic snapshots of a GCP instance@@@Change the retention policy of the snapshots of GCP relic objects...","gcp/gcp_changing_the_retention_policy_for_a_policy_based_snapshot.html@@@Changing the retention policy for GCP workloads@@@Change the retention policy of existing policy-based snapshots of GCP objects with no SLA Domain...","gcp/gcp_changing_the_retention_policy_for_an_on_demand_snapshot.html@@@Changing the on-demand snapshot retention policy@@@Change the retention policy of on-demand snapshots of the chosen GCP object...","gcp/gcp_cloud_sql.html@@@Google Cloud SQL@@@RSC supports backup and recovery of Google Cloud SQL instances...","gcp/gcp_cloud_sql_changing_ret_pol_snapshots.html@@@Changing retention for Cloud SQL policy-based snapshots@@@You can change the retention policy of existing policy-based snapshots of Cloud SQL instances with no SLA Domain...","gcp/gcp_cloud_sql_changing_retention_ods.html@@@Changing retention policy for Cloud SQL on-demand snapshots@@@You can change the retention policy of on-demand snapshots of a Cloud SQL instance...","gcp/gcp_cloud_sql_changing_retention_relic.html@@@Changing retention policy for Cloud SQL relic snapshots@@@You can change the retention policy of snapshots of Cloud SQL relic instances...","gcp/gcp_cloud_sql_deleting_label_rules.html@@@Deleting label rules for Google Cloud SQL@@@You can delete label rules assigned to Cloud SQL instances...","gcp/gcp_cloud_sql_deleting_snapshots.html@@@Deleting Cloud SQL snapshots@@@You can delete snapshots of Cloud SQL instances that have a Forever retention policy...","gcp/gcp_cloud_sql_instance_details.html@@@Google Cloud SQL instance details@@@Information available on the Google Cloud SQL instance details page in RSC...","gcp/gcp_cloud_sql_limitations.html@@@Google Cloud SQL Rubrik backup limitations@@@Rubrik backups of Google Cloud SQL instances have certain limitations...","gcp/gcp_cloud_sql_snapshot_types.html@@@Snapshot types for Google Cloud SQL@@@You can manage snapshots of Google Cloud SQL instances by taking on-demand snapshots, changing retention policies, and deleting snapshots...","gcp/gcp_cloud_sql_taking_ods.html@@@Taking on-demand Cloud SQL instance snapshots@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, you can take on-demand snapshots of Google Cloud SQL instances...","gcp/gcp_cloud_sql_viewing_details.html@@@Viewing Google Cloud SQL instance details@@@You can access the Google Cloud SQL inventory page to view the details of your Cloud SQL instances...","gcp/gcp_cnp_archival_encryption_options.html@@@Encryption options for GCP cloud-native archival@@@RSC supports three encryption options for GCP cloud-native archival locations: client-side encryption using your Google Cloud KMS key, server-side encryption using a customer-managed key, and server-side encryption using a platform-managed key...","gcp/gcp_cnp_client_side_encryption.html@@@Client-side encryption for GCP cloud-native archival@@@Client-side encryption encrypts archived Google Compute Engine instance and persistent disk data using your Google Cloud Key Management Service key before the data leaves the Exocompute environment...","gcp/gcp_configuring_pcr.html@@@Configuring a Private Container Registry@@@Configure a Private Container Registry so that Exocompute pulls container images from a Google Artifact Registry repository that you host...","gcp/gcp_creating_custom_sla_domain.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain for Google workloads@@@You can create a custom SLA Domain for Google Compute Engine instances and persistent disks, Google Cloud SQL instances, and BigQuery datasets to customize workload protection and management policies...","gcp/gcp_creating_label_rules.html@@@Creating label rules for GCP workloads@@@Create and assign a label rule to protect GCE instances and persistent disks associated with your GCP projects...","gcp/gcp_deleting_an_ondemand_snapshot.html@@@Deleting GCE instance and persistent disk snapshots@@@Delete snapshots that have a Forever retention policy...","gcp/gcp_deleting_label_rules.html@@@Deleting label rules for GCP workloads@@@Delete label rules assigned to GCE instances or persistent disks...","gcp/gcp_deleting_relic_snapshot.html@@@Deleting snapshots of relic GCP instances@@@Delete a snapshot of GCP relic objects...","gcp/gcp_excluding_disks_gce.html@@@Excluding disks from a GCE instance@@@Exclude specific disks while protecting other disks attached to a GCE instance. This is useful for managing storage resources efficiently when certain disks do not require backup...","gcp/gcp_exo_cost_best_practices.html@@@Best practices for reducing Exocompute on GCP costs@@@You can configure your GCP network, storage class selection, and snapshot retention settings to reduce ongoing costs when using Exocompute on GCP for archiving and data protection operations...","gcp/gcp_exo_cust_managed_network_prereq.html@@@Exocompute on GCP customer-managed networking prerequisites@@@Information about the required settings for the VPC network, subnets, and firewalls that will host the Exocompute GKE cluster when you select the customer-managed networking mode while onboarding a GCP project for the Exocompute use case...","gcp/gcp_exo_service_account_prereq.html@@@Exocompute service account prerequisites@@@Information about required GCP IAM role bindings for the service account used to manually add a GCP project for the Exocompute use case...","gcp/gcp_exocompute_health_check.html@@@Exocompute health check for GCP@@@The Exocompute health check for GCP feature in RSC runs a health check for a GKE cluster and displays the cluster&apos;s current status. With this health check feature, you can confirm if the GKE cluster is functioning correctly...","gcp/gcp_exocompute_networking_modes.html@@@Exocompute on GCP networking modes@@@It is important that you evaluate the available options for Exocompute on GCP networking modes when adding a GCP project...","gcp/gcp_exporting_bigquery_dataset.html@@@Exporting a BigQuery dataset@@@You can export a Google BigQuery dataset to a new dataset, or selected tables to a new or existing dataset, in the same or a different Google Cloud Platform project or region...","gcp/gcp_exporting_cloud_sql.html@@@Exporting a Cloud SQL instance@@@You can export a Cloud SQL instance snapshot to create a Cloud SQL instance, including export to a different GCP project...","gcp/gcp_gce_instance_details_page.html@@@GCE instance details@@@The details page for GCE instances displays protection status, calendar view of the snapshots, and events. You can view the details for each snapshot by expanding the entry in the Day view...","gcp/gcp_health_check_status_exocompute.html@@@Health check statuses for GCP Exocompute@@@You can find information about the various health check statuses for Exocompute on GCP...","gcp/gcp_instant_tiering.html@@@GCP instant tiering@@@In RSC, you can instantly tier GCE instance or persistent disk snapshots to the specified archival location, enhancing cost efficiency...","gcp/gcp_label_based_protection.html@@@Label-based protection for GCP workloads@@@You can protect GCE instances and persistent disks, Cloud SQL instances, and BigQuery datasets by grouping them using labels and assigning SLA Domains using the label...","gcp/gcp_manual_onboarding_projects.html@@@Manual onboarding for GCP projects@@@Manual onboarding offers a non-OAuth method for connecting GCP projects to RSC, granting you full control over all necessary IAM resource creation...","gcp/gcp_manual_vs_oauth_methods_projects.html@@@Manual versus OAuth methods for GCP projects@@@A comparative overview of the Add manually and Add using OAuth methods for adding a GCP project to RSC...","gcp/gcp_multiple_key_value_pair_labels.html@@@Multiple key-value pair labels@@@Label-based assignment automates GCP protection by replacing manual selection with dynamic, multi-layered logic. By using multiple key-value pair labels, you can either apply the AND or the IN condition to precisely target high-risk data while reducing rule complexity...","gcp/gcp_obtaining_service_account_key.html@@@Obtaining the service account key@@@Generate and securely download the JSON private key file for the newly provisioned service account in GCC...","gcp/gcp_permission_validation.html@@@GCP permission validation@@@You can perform on-demand checks on all GCP projects added to RSC and identify any missing permissions required for protecting GCP workloads...","gcp/gcp_perms_cmek_workloads.html@@@Permissions for CMEK-encrypted GCP workloads@@@You can grant the roles/cloudkms.cryptoKeyEncrypterDecrypter role to the relevant Google Cloud Platform Service Agent at the key, key ring, or project level for GCP workloads encrypted with Customer-managed Encryption Keys...","gcp/gcp_persistent_disk_details_page.html@@@Persistent disks details@@@The details page for persistent disks displays protection status, calendar view of the snapshots, and events...","gcp/gcp_private_bucket_network_access.html@@@Private bucket network access for GCP storage tiering@@@When creating a Google Cloud Platform archival location, you can restrict bucket access to Exocompute Virtual Private Cloud networks only, preventing RSC deployment IP addresses from accessing the Google Cloud Storage bucket directly...","gcp/gcp_private_container_registry.html@@@Private Container Registry for GCP@@@For the Google Cloud Platform Exocompute project that you add manually, you can configure a Private Container Registry so that Exocompute pulls container images from a Google Artifact Registry repository that you host, instead of a registry that Rubrik hosts...","gcp/gcp_private_exocompute.html@@@Private Exocompute on GCP@@@Private Exocompute on GCP isolates the Exocompute GKE cluster from the public internet by keeping the Kubernetes API server endpoint within your VPC network...","gcp/gcp_proj_vs_folder_onboarding.html@@@Project versus folder onboarding for GCP@@@When you add GCP projects to RSC using the OAuth method, you can select individual projects or entire folders...","gcp/gcp_project_addition_terraform.html@@@GCP project addition using Terraform@@@You can add multiple GCP projects to RSC at once using the RSC provider for Terraform...","gcp/gcp_project_management.html@@@GCP project management@@@Using RSC, you can monitor and manage the details of your GCP projects. You can also refresh a GCP project on-demand to obtain the up-to-date metadata based on your specific requirements...","gcp/gcp_project_setup.html@@@GCP project setup@@@You can set up a GCP project by adding the project to RSC and start protecting your GCP workloads...","gcp/gcp_project_status.html@@@GCP project status@@@The status column on the GCP page provides information about the status of a GCP project in RSC...","gcp/gcp_recovery_bigquery_datasets.html@@@Recovery of BigQuery datasets@@@You can recover protected Google BigQuery datasets from the backups that RSC stores in your backup locations...","gcp/gcp_recovery_cloud_sql_instances.html@@@Recovery of Cloud SQL instances@@@You can recover your Cloud SQL instances using options, such as exporting and restoring the instances...","gcp/gcp_refreshing_a_project.html@@@Refreshing a GCP project@@@RSC refreshes the GCP project data both as an on-demand task or as a periodic background job that runs every three hours...","gcp/gcp_removing_pcr_configuration.html@@@Removing a Private Container Registry@@@Remove your Private Container Registry configuration when no longer in use so that Exocompute pulls container images from the Google Artifact Registry repository that Rubrik hosts...","gcp/gcp_restoring_bigquery_dataset.html@@@Restoring a BigQuery dataset@@@You can restore selected tables from a snapshot in place to the source Google BigQuery dataset...","gcp/gcp_restoring_cloud_sql.html@@@Restoring a Cloud SQL instance@@@You can restore a Cloud SQL instance to a point-in-time copy from a snapshot...","gcp/gcp_rubrik_hosted_gar_pcr.html@@@Rubrik-hosted GAR versus PCR@@@Information about the Rubrik-hosted Google Artifact Registry and a Private Container Registry for Exocompute on Google Cloud Platform...","gcp/gcp_running_on_demand_exo_health_check.html@@@Running an on-demand Exocompute health check for GCP@@@You can run an on-demand health check for an existing Exocompute configuration in your GCP environment to verify connectivity and cluster status...","gcp/gcp_snapshots_information_list.html@@@GCP snapshots information list@@@Information about the snapshots for a GCE instance or persistent disk...","gcp/gcp_storage_tiering_setup.html@@@GCP storage tiering setup@@@You can use GCP storage tiering to archive GCE instance or persistent disk snapshots that are older than a specified threshold to GCS storage classes. By archiving snapshots to these storage classes, you can optimize costs...","gcp/gcp_taking_ods.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of GCP objects@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, you can take snapshots of GCP protectable objects by using the on-demand snapshot process...","gcp/gcp_troubleshooting_pcr.html@@@Troubleshooting PCR failures@@@Information about the errors that you can see when you register a Private Container Registry or when Exocompute pulls container images from your Google Artifact Registry repository, and how to resolve them...","gcp/gcp_viewing_gce_instances.html@@@Viewing the GCE instance details page@@@Access the instance details page to view information about a GCE instance...","gcp/gcp_viewing_persistent_disks.html@@@Viewing persistent disks@@@Access the instance details page to view information about a persistent disk...","gcp/gcp_workload_identity_binding_exo.html@@@Workload Identity binding for Exocompute@@@Information about the Workload Identity binding required to connect the GCP IAM service account with the Exocompute service account before initiating Exocompute operations on a manually onboarded GCP project...","gcp/gcp_workload_protection_setup.html@@@GCP workloads protection setup@@@You can set up SLA Domains to apply data protection policies, ensuring automatic and hierarchical protection of GCP projects and individual GCP workloads, with granular control overriding higher-level assignments...","gcp/gcp_workload_recovery.html@@@GCP workloads recovery@@@After RSC takes snapshots of your GCP workloads, you can recover the required workloads using these snapshots...","gcp/gcs_storage_classes.html@@@GCS storage classes@@@RSC supports four GCS storage classes when creating an archival location to meet different storage requirements...","gcp/gcs_storage_classes_2.html@@@GCS storage classes@@@RSC supports four GCS storage classes when creating an archival location to meet different storage requirements...","gcp/high_level_arch_gcp_protection.html@@@High-level architecture for GCP protection@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects GCP workloads and RSC and GCP IAM roles provisioning process...","gcp/key_features_gcp_protection.html@@@Key features for protecting GCP workloads@@@RSC provides unified data management, automated global data protection, and various recovery options to protect your GCP workloads...","gcp/maint_exo_gcp.html@@@Maintenance of Exocompute on GCP@@@Maintaining Exocompute on GCP involves regularly reviewing and updating permissions to ensure optimal performance and resource management...","gcp/managing_file_index_gcp_wrkld.html@@@Managing file indexing of a GCP workload@@@Manage file indexing for GCE instances or persistent disks by turning on or turning off file indexing. Turning on file indexing facilitates quick file recovery by allowing you to search across indexed snapshots and initiate recovery. When it is no longer needed, you can turn off file indexing...","gcp/managing_granular_perms_gcp_proj.html@@@Managing granular permissions for GCP projects@@@Manage the permission categories for a GCP project that you have already added to RSC by including or excluding permission categories, as required...","gcp/multiple_arch_loc_gcp.html@@@Multiple archival locations for GCP@@@RSC supports multiple archival locations for GCE instances or persistent disks, allowing granular control over data archiving with up to two distinct archiving policies...","gcp/perm_categories_gcp.html@@@Permission categories for GCP workloads@@@For tasks that operate on GCP workloads, such as export and restore and file-level recovery, RSC requires specific permissions. RSC groups these permissions into categories for granular management...","gcp/perm_model_privilege_elevation_gcp.html@@@Permission model and privilege elevation for GCP@@@RSC provides a least permission model for GCP projects, granting minimal necessary permissions, starting with read-only access. You can add the Basic permission category initially and elevate permissions for recovery operations when required...","gcp/perms_add_gcp_project.html@@@Permissions to add GCP projects@@@The GCP IAM user account requires specific permissions to add GCP projects to RSC...","gcp/planning_gcp_protection.html@@@Planning for GCP protection@@@Before setting up a GCP project in RSC, you need to plan user and access management for designated RSC users. This planning also involves reviewing the permissions that RSC requires in your GCP environment to protect your GCP workloads...","gcp/privilege_elevation_gcp_recovery.html@@@Privilege elevation for GCP recovery@@@RSC provides you an option to secure GCP projects by using a least permission model, granting only necessary read permissions. For recovery operations, you can temporarily elevate permissions by authorizing a service account role...","gcp/recommend_add_gcp_proj.html@@@Recommendations for adding GCP projects@@@Rubrik recommends specific actions and best practices for adding GCP projects to RSC...","gcp/recover_gce_pd.html@@@Recovery of GCE instances and persistent disks@@@You can recover your GCE instances and persistent disks using options such as recovering files or folders, exporting, and restoring...","gcp/recovering_files_folders_gcp_snap.html@@@Recovering files or folders from a GCP snapshot@@@Recover files or folders from GCE instances or persistent disks to a GCS bucket if the files that you want to access are deleted or corrupted...","gcp/recovery_options_gce_pd.html@@@Recovery options for GCE instances and persistent disks@@@A comparative overview of the various recovery options for GCE instances and persistent disks...","gcp/req_perms_gcp_bigquery.html@@@Required permissions for BigQuery datasets@@@RSC requires specific permissions in your Google Cloud Platform projects to protect and recover Google BigQuery datasets...","gcp/req_perms_gcp_cloud_sql.html@@@Required permissions for Google Cloud SQL instances@@@RSC requires specific permissions in your GCP project to protect and recover Google Cloud SQL instances...","gcp/req_perms_gcp_networking_setup.html@@@Required permissions for GCP networking setup@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to set up the GCP network for Exocompute purposes...","gcp/req_perms_gcp_pcr.html@@@Required permissions for Private Container Registry@@@Information about the permissions that the Artifact Registry Reader role includes to pull container images from your Google Artifact Registry repository for a Private Container Registry...","gcp/req_perms_gcp_strg_tiering_recovery.html@@@Required permissions for GCP storage tiering and recovery@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires for the GCP storage tiering and recovery operations...","gcp/req_perms_gcp_telemetry_setup.html@@@Required permissions for GCP telemetry setup@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires for the GCP telemetry setup...","gcp/req_perms_gke_setup.html@@@Required permissions for GKE setup@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires for the Google Kubernetes Engine setup...","gcp/req_perms_native_gcp_protection.html@@@Required permissions for native GCP protection@@@RSC requires certain permissions to protect GCP resources...","gcp/req_rbk_perms_gcp_env.html@@@Required RSC permissions for GCP environment@@@RSC requires specific permissions in your GCP environment to protect the GCP workloads...","gcp/restoring_gce_instance.html@@@Restoring a GCE instance@@@Use a GCE instance snapshot to replace the original GCE instance with a fully functional point-in-time copy...","gcp/retention_lock_gcp.html@@@Retention lock for GCP workloads@@@A retention lock on an SLA Domain is a security feature that prevents premature deletion of snapshots of GCP workloads...","gcp/sharing_encrypt_key_diff_gcp_prj.html@@@Sharing encryption key with a different GCP project@@@To export a GCE instance snapshot to a different target GCP project, share the disk encryption key from the original project with the target project...","gcp/sla_assignment_hierarchy_gcp.html@@@SLA Domain assignment hierarchy for GCP@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based, automatic protection of GCP workloads, simplifying the assignment of protection across various levels, such as GCP projects and individual workloads...","gcp/source_snapshot_retention_gcp.html@@@Source snapshot retention for GCP workloads@@@Source snapshot retention for GCP workloads ensures data protection and recoverability by allowing you to set various retention policies. These policies include retaining hourly, daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, and yearly snapshots to meet compliance, business continuity, and disaster recovery requirements...","gcp/upgrading_gcp_projects.html@@@Upgrading GCP projects@@@Upgrade the GCP project in RSC to update the permissions required to protect GCP resources...","gcp/user_mgmt_gcp_protection.html@@@RSC user management for GCP protection@@@Designating specific users with appropriate privileges and roles in RSC enhances security for managing GCP projects...","gcp/validating_perms_gcp_projects.html@@@Validating permissions for GCP projects@@@You can run the on-demand validation check for GCP projects to identify missing permissions necessary for cloud-native protection of GCP workloads...","github/github.html@@@GitHub@@@RSC provides data protection for GitHub organizations and repositories...","github/github_access_reports.html@@@Access GitHub reports@@@With RSC, you can create and download reports based on templates to monitor the protection status of your GitHub organizations and repositories...","github/github_adding_organization.html@@@Adding GitHub organization@@@Add a GitHub organization to RSC to back up and recover repositories, manage organizations, and minimize downtime...","github/github_adding_rubrik_hosted_organizaton.html@@@Adding GitHub organization using Rubrik-hosted Exocompute@@@Add a GitHub organization using Rubrik-hosted Exocompute to RSC to back up and recover repositories, manage organizations, and minimize downtime...","github/github_assigning_apps_manager_role.html@@@Assigning the GitHub Apps manager role@@@Assign the GitHub Apps manager role to an organization member so they can register and request installation of GitHub apps without the organization owner role...","github/github_assigning_protection.html@@@Assigning protection to GitHub@@@Assign a data protection policy to specific GitHub organizations or repositories...","github/github_best_practices_sla_assign.html@@@Best practices for GitHub SLA Domain assignment@@@Information about the best practices for assigning SLA Domains to GitHub organizations and repositories, ensuring effective data protection and compliance...","github/github_common_protection_terms.html@@@Common protection terms for GitHub@@@It is important to understand some common terms when protecting a GitHub organization with RSC...","github/github_configure_backup_loc.html@@@Configure GitHub backup location@@@You must create a backup location for storing snapshots of GitHub repositories. Additionally, you can configure a private or service endpoint to back up snapshots to the backup location...","github/github_configure_protection.html@@@Configure GitHub protection@@@After you have decided on the protection policies you want to configure, you can begin the protection setup by creating an SLA Domain and assigning protection to GitHub organizations and repositories...","github/github_configuring_azr_pvt_endpoint.html@@@Configuring an Azure private endpoint for GitHub@@@To backup snapshots to an archival location with a region-specific setting, configure an Azure private endpoint...","github/github_creating_aws_archival_locations.html@@@Creating AWS archival locations for GitHub@@@Create an archival location for the AWS storage account created for storing the snapshots of GitHub repositories...","github/github_creating_azr_archival_locations.html@@@Creating Azure archival locations for GitHub@@@Create an archival location for the Azure storage account created for storing the snapshots of GitHub repositories...","github/github_creating_custom_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for GitHub@@@Create a custom role with Role-based Access Control privileges for managing your GitHub organization. These privileges provide finer granularity for determining which permissions a RSC user has for performing specific actions on specific objects...","github/github_creating_custom_sla_domain.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain for GitHub@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to streamline and customize the GitHub organization protection and management policies...","github/github_creating_reports.html@@@Creating reports for GitHub@@@Create reports for the GitHub organization and repositories to view information such as compliance status and protection status using the available templates. You can use the information generated in the reports to perform audits and data management planning...","github/github_details.html@@@GitHub details@@@RSC monitors, analyzes, and restores GitHub repositories associated with GitHub organizations. RSC also shows important details such as organization status and protected repositories, and a summary of backup jobs...","github/github_edit_organization.html@@@Edit a GitHub organization@@@You can edit an existing GitHub organization in RSC to update its data protection preferences...","github/github_evaluate_backup_options.html@@@Evaluate backup options for GitHub@@@It is important to evaluate the backup options for GitHub to align with the performance and data retrieval needs. Key considerations include the choice of cloud provider, storage locations, access tiers, and network security configurations...","github/github_evaluate_protection_options.html@@@Evaluate GitHub protection options@@@Understanding the various protection options is important when creating an SLA Domain for your GitHub organization. This ensures alignment with organizational needs. Thoroughly evaluating these options enables making informed decisions and providing effective protection for the workloads...","github/github_event_log_details.html@@@Event log details for GitHub@@@The Event Logs page displays the events occurring in all GitHub organizations, shown in the local time zone...","github/github_high_level_arch_protection.html@@@High-level architecture for GitHub protection@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects GitHub organizations and repositories within your Azure or AWS environment...","github/github_high_level_implement_workflow.html@@@High-level implementation workflow for GitHub@@@The GitHub protection implementation workflow involves a structured approach to secure data management, starting with planning and preparation, followed by GitHub organization setup, GitHub protection, continuous management and optimization, and repository recovery...","github/github_manage_orgs_repos.html@@@Manage GitHub organizations and repositories@@@After completing the protection setup for GitHub organizations and repositories, RSC takes automated snapshots of those repositories based on the configured policies in SLA Domains. You can also take on-demand snapshots and refresh GitHub organizations for better resource management...","github/github_managing_granular_permissions.html@@@Managing granular permissions for GitHub organization@@@Update granular permissions for a GitHub organization when needed...","github/github_permission_model.html@@@Permission model for GitHub@@@RSC provides a least permission model for GitHub organizations, granting minimal necessary permissions starting with read-only access. You can add the GitHub Backup app while onboarding to establish data protection and install the GitHub Restore app to elevate permissions for recovery operations when required...","github/github_permissoon_categories.html@@@Permission categories for GitHub@@@For the backup and recovery tasks associated with GitHub repositories, RSC requires specific permissions. RSC groups these permissions into categories for granular management so that you can include or exclude these categories as required...","github/github_plan_protection.html@@@Plan your GitHub protection@@@Before setting up a GitHub organization in RSC, you need to plan user and access management for designated RSC users. This involves reviewing the permissions that RSC requires for GitHub, as well as in your Azure or AWS cloud provider, to install Exocompute and create storage accounts for protecting GitHub organizations...","github/github_primary_snapshot_retention.html@@@Primary snapshot retention for GitHub@@@Primary snapshot retention for GitHub organizations ensures data protection and recoverability by enabling you to set various retention policies, such as retaining hourly, daily, monthly, and yearly snapshots, to meet compliance, business continuity, and disaster recovery requirements...","github/github_private_service_endpoints_usage.html@@@Private and service endpoints usage for GitHub@@@You can back up GitHub repositories to Azure Blob Storage or an AWS S3 bucket by using private or service endpoints...","github/github_privilege_elevation.html@@@Privilege elevation for GitHub recovery@@@RSC enhances the security of your GitHub organization by employing a least permission model that limits the access granted to the minimal necessary roles and resources...","github/github_protection_key_feature.html@@@Key features for protecting GitHub@@@RSC provides unified data management, automated global data protection, and cyber resilience features to protect your GitHub organization...","github/github_protection_limitations.html@@@GitHub protection limitations@@@Information about the current limitations and unsupported features for protecting GitHub organizations with RSC...","github/github_protection_retention_lock.html@@@Retention lock for GitHub protection@@@A retention lock on RSC is a security feature that prevents premature deletion of GitHub snapshots...","github/github_quick_links.html@@@Quick links for GitHub@@@Immediate access to important tasks and information, enabling quick setup, daily operations, and critical recovery...","github/github_recover.html@@@Recover GitHub@@@After RSC takes snapshots of your GitHub repositories, you can recover the necessary details...","github/github_recovering_issues_prs.html@@@Recovering GitHub repository with pull requests and issues@@@Recover a GitHub repository together with its pull requests and issues into a new repository in the same organization...","github/github_recovering_repos.html@@@Recovering GitHub repositories@@@Recover GitHub repositories from a protected snapshot...","github/github_refreshing_organization.html@@@Refreshing GitHub organizations@@@Refresh GitHub organizations as an on-demand task to retrieve the latest metadata of all repositories from GitHub...","github/github_removing_organization.html@@@Removing GitHub organization@@@Remove a GitHub organization when you do not want to protect the organization with Rubrik...","github/github_req_rsc_perms.html@@@Required RSC permissions for GitHub@@@RSC requires specific permissions to protect GitHub organizations, store data, and manage the encryption of stored data...","github/github_rsc_communication.html@@@Communication between RSC and GitHub organization@@@A high-level architecture overview of how RSC communicates with your GitHub organization while onboarding. It explains the use of the GitHub app, secure credential exchange, and the trust relationship established for secure operations...","github/github_set_up_backup_loc.html@@@Set up backup location for GitHub@@@RSC provides data protection for GitHub organizations and repositories. You can set up a backup location in Azure or AWS to store snapshots associated with GitHub organizations and repositories...","github/github_set_up_exocompute_aws.html@@@Set up Exocompute for GitHub on AWS@@@With the Exocompute for GitHub on AWS feature, RSC launches an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service cluster to serve as a dedicated compute resource within your AWS account. This cluster executes the core logic for data protection operations while ensuring data remains within your security boundaries...","github/github_set_up_exocompute_azure.html@@@Set up Exocompute for GitHub on Azure@@@With the Exocompute for GitHub on Azure feature, RSC launches an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) cluster to perform data protection operations for your GitHub repositories. RSC uses this AKS cluster as a dedicated compute resource within your Azure subscription to ensure data sovereignty and efficient processing...","github/github_set_up_protection.html@@@Set up protection for GitHub@@@You can set up SLA Domains to apply data protection policies, ensuring automatic and hierarchical protection of GitHub organizations and repositories, with granular control overriding higher-level assignments...","github/github_settings_backup_recovery.html@@@GitHub repository backup and recovery settings@@@In addition to repository contents, RSC backs up a curated set of GitHub repository-level settings as part of every repository snapshot and reapplies them to the destination repository during recovery...","github/github_setup_organization.html@@@Set up GitHub organization@@@You can add a GitHub organization in RSC to start protecting GitHub resources...","github/github_sla_assignment_hierarchy.html@@@SLA Domain assignment hierarchy for GitHub@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based, automatic protection for GitHub organizations, simplifying the assignment of protection across organizations and repositories...","github/github_supported_encryption_types.html@@@Supported encryption types for GitHub snapshots@@@RSC supports snapshot encryption for GitHub repositories stored in either Azure or AWS cloud environments, using either platform-managed keys or customer-managed keys...","github/github_taking_ods.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of a GitHub repository@@@Manually take an on-demand snapshot of the GitHub repository to protect the data residing in it...","github/github_user_management.html@@@RSC user management for GitHub@@@Designating specific users with appropriate privileges and roles in RSC secures the management of GitHub organizations...","github/github_user_perms_backup_loc.html@@@User permissions for GitHub backup location@@@Configuring a GitHub backup location in RSC requires a role with specific permissions to manage cloud accounts and archival settings. These permissions enable you to connect the Azure or AWS cloud accounts used for storage and compute, and to configure the archival locations where GitHub repository data will be stored...","github/github_viewing_events.html@@@Viewing events for GitHub@@@View the Event Logs page from the Data Protection dashboard to see the events for the GitHub organization...","github/github_viewing_inventory.html@@@Viewing GitHub inventory@@@View the GitHub inventory page to manage GitHub organizations and repositories...","gql/accessing_api_playground.html@@@Accessing API Playground@@@Access API Playground in your RSC domain by authenticating to RSC using your account credentials. With access to API Playground, you can explore the Rubrik GraphQL schema and perform data security operations using GraphQL queries and mutations...","gql/api_playground.html@@@API Playground@@@API Playground is an integrated development environment (IDE) in Rubrik Security Cloud that you can use to run GraphQL API operations on the data managed in real time by RSC...","gql/api_playground_ui.html@@@API Playground user interface@@@The API Playground user interface in RSC uses the GraphiQL integrated development environment (IDE) to run Rubrik GraphQL operations...","gql/k8s_manifest_config_values.html@@@Accepted values for generateK8sManifest distribution and transport fields@@@The distribution and transport fields on the generateK8sManifest GraphQL mutation accept the values in the following tables...","gql/sa_session_non_persistence_api_playground.html@@@Non-persistence of service account sessions in API Playground@@@When you use a service account to run GraphQL API operations in API Playground, for security reasons, API Playground does not persist the service account credentials and renders the service account access token invalid when the service account session ends or becomes inactive...","gql/using_sa_to_run_gql.html@@@Using a service account to run GraphQL APIs@@@In API Playground, run GraphQL queries and mutations with a service account to test and validate the service account&apos;s use in automation scripts...","gws/configure_protection_gws.html@@@Configure protection for Google Workspace@@@You can create a custom SLA Domain and assign it to your Google Workspace workloads to begin the protection setup...","gws/gcalendar_changing_snapshot.html@@@Changing a snapshot for Google Calendar@@@Change to a different point-in-time snapshot to view and restore Google Calendar data...","gws/gcalendar_recover_data.html@@@Recover Google Calendar data@@@RSC enables you to recover entire Google Calendars or individual events from a protected Gmail workload...","gws/gcalendar_recovery_scopes.html@@@Google Calendar recovery scopes@@@Recovery scopes determine the calendar data that can be restored, such as specific calendars and events, or all calendars of a user...","gws/gcalendar_restoring_events.html@@@Restoring specific events from Google Calendar@@@Use a snapshot to find and restore individual events to the Google Calendar of a user. You can browse or search calendars and events and use advanced filters to locate specific events...","gws/gcalendar_restoring_full_calendar.html@@@Restoring a full Google Calendar@@@Restore all events in a Google Calendar from a point-in-time snapshot to the original or a different user account...","gws/gcontacts_changing_snapshot.html@@@Changing a snapshot for Google Contacts@@@Change to a different point-in-time snapshot to view and restore Google Contacts data...","gws/gcontacts_recover_data.html@@@Recover Google Contacts data@@@RSC enables you to recover specific contacts, contact groups, or other contacts from a protected Gmail workload...","gws/gcontacts_recovery_scopes.html@@@Google Contacts recovery scopes@@@Recovery scopes determine the contact data that can be restored, such as specific contacts, contact groups, or other contacts...","gws/gcontacts_restoring_contacts.html@@@Restoring contacts from Google Contacts@@@Use a snapshot to find and restore contacts, contact groups, or other contacts to the Google Contacts of a user. RSC provides contact browsing and search to enable you to locate specific items...","gws/gdrive_changing_snap_shared_drive.html@@@Changing a snapshot for a shared drive@@@Select a specific point-in-time snapshot to view and restore data from a shared drive...","gws/gdrive_exporting_data.html@@@Exporting Google Drive data@@@Export specific files and folders, an entire user drive or shared drive from a Google Drive snapshot as a downloadable ZIP file...","gws/gdrive_performing_prioritized_recovery.html@@@Restoring Google Drive data using prioritized recovery@@@Perform a prioritized recovery for Google Drive to restore the most recently modified files first before recovering the remaining data...","gws/gdrive_recover_data.html@@@Recover Google Drive data@@@After RSC protects your Google Drive workloads, you can recover entire drives, or specific files and folders...","gws/gdrive_recovery_scopes.html@@@Recovery scopes for Google Drive@@@Recovery scopes determine the data included when restoring Google Drive data...","gws/gdrive_restoring_data_ou_entire_app.html@@@Restoring Google Drive data for organizational units or entire application@@@Restore Google Drive data for users in selected organizational units or for the entire Google Drive application from a point-in-time snapshot using mass recovery...","gws/gdrive_restoring_entire_shared_drive.html@@@Restoring an entire shared drive@@@Use RSC to restore the full contents of a Shared Drive from a point-in-time snapshot to the original location or a different Shared Drive...","gws/gdrive_restoring_files_folders.html@@@Restoring files or folders from Google Drive@@@Use a snapshot to find and restore individual files or folders from a User Drive or a Shared Drive...","gws/gdrive_restoring_groups.html@@@Restoring Google Drive data of groups@@@Restore Google Drive data for all members of selected Google groups from a point-in-time snapshot using mass recovery...","gws/gdrive_restoring_multiple_shared_drives.html@@@Restoring multiple shared drives@@@Restore multiple shared drives simultaneously to their original locations from a point-in-time snapshot using mass recovery...","gws/gdrive_restoring_multiple_users.html@@@Restoring Google Drive data for multiple users@@@Restore the entire My Drive of multiple users simultaneously from a point-in-time snapshot using mass recovery...","gws/gdrive_restoring_user_drive.html@@@Restoring a user drive@@@Use RSC to restore the full contents of a user My Drive from a point-in-time snapshot to the original location or a different user drive...","gws/gdrive_self_service_recovery.html@@@Restoring Google Drive data for self-service users@@@As a self-service user, you can search for and restore your Google Drive files and folders...","gws/gmail_changing_snapshot.html@@@Changing a snapshot for Gmail@@@Select a specific point-in-time snapshot to view and restore Gmail data...","gws/gmail_exporting_data.html@@@Exporting Gmail, Calendar, and Contacts data@@@Export Gmail messages, Calendar events, and Contacts from a point-in-time snapshot as a downloadable ZIP file...","gws/gmail_performing_prioritized_recovery.html@@@Restoring Gmail data using prioritized recovery@@@Perform a prioritized recovery of Gmail, Calendar, and Contacts data to first restore the most recent emails, calendar events, and contacts data before recovering the remaining data...","gws/gmail_recover_data.html@@@Recover Gmail data@@@RSC enables you to recover emails, calendar events, and contacts from a point-in-time snapshot of a protected Google account...","gws/gmail_recovery_scopes.html@@@Recovery scopes for Gmail@@@Recovery scopes determine the data included when restoring Gmail messages and mailboxes...","gws/gmail_restoring_data_ou_entire_app.html@@@Restoring Gmail data for organizational units or entire application@@@Restore Gmail inboxes along with Calendar and Contacts data for users in selected organizational units or for the entire Gmail application from a point-in-time snapshot using mass recovery...","gws/gmail_restoring_emails_threads.html@@@Restoring specific emails or threads from Gmail@@@Use a snapshot to find and restore individual emails or entire conversation threads to a user mailbox. RSC uses an indexed search to enable you to locate messages by subject prefix or labels...","gws/gmail_restoring_full_mailbox.html@@@Restoring a full Gmail mailbox@@@Restore the entire contents of a Gmail mailbox from a point-in-time snapshot to the original or a different user account...","gws/gmail_restoring_groups.html@@@Restoring Gmail, Calendar, and Contacts data of groups@@@Restore Gmail, Calendar, and Contacts data for all members of selected Google groups from a point-in-time snapshot using mass recovery...","gws/gmail_restoring_multiple_users.html@@@Restoring Gmail data for multiple users@@@Restore Gmail, Calendar, and Contacts data for multiple users simultaneously from a point-in-time snapshot using mass recovery...","gws/gmail_self_service_recovery.html@@@Restoring Gmail data for self-service users@@@As a self-service user, you can search for and restore your emails, calendar events, and contacts...","gws/google_workspace.html@@@Google Workspace@@@Rubrik Security Cloud protects your Google Workspace workloads, such as Google Drive and Gmail data, for your organization...","gws/gws_adding_group.html@@@Adding a Google group@@@Add a Google group to RSC to apply data protection policies to all users in the group...","gws/gws_assigning_sla_group.html@@@Assigning group-based SLA Domains@@@Assign or modify the SLA Domain of a Google group in group-based protection to manage data protection for the Google Drive and Gmail data of its members...","gws/gws_assigning_sla_ou.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to Organizational Units@@@Assign an SLA Domain to all users and Shared Drives within a specific OU...","gws/gws_assigning_sla_shared_drives.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to Shared Drives@@@Assign an SLA Domain directly to one or more Shared Drives...","gws/gws_assigning_sla_users.html@@@Assigning SLA Domain to User mailboxes or Drive@@@Assign an SLA Domain directly to the My Drive of one or more individual users...","gws/gws_changing_sla_domain_google_groups.html@@@Changing the SLA Domain of Google groups@@@Change the SLA Domain of the Google groups workload to update the snapshot frequency and retention of all groups...","gws/gws_creating_custom_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for Google Workspace@@@Create a custom role with specific permissions for managing and protecting Google Workspace workloads...","gws/gws_creating_custom_sla.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain for Google Workspace@@@Create a custom SLA Domain for Google Workspace to streamline and customize workload protection and management policies...","gws/gws_creating_self_service_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for self-service recovery@@@Create a custom role that grants only the Google Workspace Self-Service Recovery permission, so that SSO users are redirected to the self-service recovery pages...","gws/gws_data_export.html@@@Google Workspace data export@@@You can export Google Workspace data from a point-in-time snapshot as a downloadable ZIP file...","gws/gws_enabling_groups_protection.html@@@Enabling Google groups protection@@@Authorize RSC to access the Google groups of an onboarded Google Workspace organization, and assign an SLA Domain to start backing them up...","gws/gws_google_groups_protection.html@@@Google groups protection@@@Google groups protection backs up the Google groups of your Google Workspace organization, including the settings, aliases, and members of each group, so that you can restore a group that was deleted or changed...","gws/gws_group_based_protection.html@@@Group-based protection@@@Group-based protection applies an SLA Domain to the Google Drive and Gmail data of the members of the groups that you add...","gws/gws_groups_conflict_resolution.html@@@Conflict resolution for Google groups@@@When Google Workspace users are members of multiple Google groups, RSC automatically applies rules to resolve conflicts in SLA Domain assignments...","gws/gws_groups_recovery.html@@@Google groups recovery@@@You can restore Google groups from a snapshot to recover a group that was deleted, or to roll back changes to the settings, members, and roles of a group...","gws/gws_groups_recovery_scopes.html@@@Recovery scopes for Google groups@@@Recovery scopes determine whether RSC restores the entire group, only the membership list, or only the settings of a Google group...","gws/gws_implementation_workflow.html@@@Google Workspace protection implementation workflow@@@An overview of the end-to-end workflow for planning, implementing, and managing Google Workspace data protection with RSC...","gws/gws_mass_recovery.html@@@Google Workspace mass recovery@@@Mass recovery restores Google Drive data along with Gmail, Calendar, and Contacts data from a point-in-time snapshot. Depending on the workload, mass recovery restores data for multiple users, multiple shared drives, specific organizational units, Google groups, or the entire Google Workspace application...","gws/gws_onboarding_org.html@@@Onboarding a Google Workspace organization@@@Add your Google Workspace organization to RSC to start protecting your Google Drive, Gmail, and Google groups data...","gws/gws_prioritized_recovery.html@@@Google Workspace prioritized recovery@@@Prioritized recovery enables you to first restore high-priority data during a recovery at the Organizational Unit (OU), Google groups, or application level, before recovering the remaining data...","gws/gws_protection_architecture.html@@@High-level architecture for Google Workspace protection@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects Google Workspace workloads...","gws/gws_protection_common_terms.html@@@Common Google Workspace protection terms@@@Understanding common terms helps you manage Google Workspace workloads with RSC...","gws/gws_protection_key_features.html@@@Key features for Google Workspace protection@@@RSC provides unified data management, automated global data protection, and various recovery options to protect your Google Workspace workloads...","gws/gws_protection_plan.html@@@Plan your Google Workspace protection@@@Before setting up a Google Workspace organization in RSC, you must plan the user and access management for designated RSC users. This planning also involves reviewing the permissions that RSC requires in your Google Workspace environment to protect your workloads...","gws/gws_protection_requirements.html@@@Requirements for protecting Google Workspace@@@A Google Workspace user must meet specific requirements to configure Google Workspace protection with RSC...","gws/gws_quick_links.html@@@Quick links for Google Workspace workloads@@@Immediate access to important tasks and information, enabling quick setup, daily operations, and critical recovery...","gws/gws_rbac_protection.html@@@RBAC for Google Workspace protection@@@Designating specific users with appropriate privileges and roles in RSC enhances security for managing your Google Workspace organization...","gws/gws_removing_groups.html@@@Removing Google groups@@@Remove Google groups from RSC when you no longer want to manage the SLA Domains at the group level...","gws/gws_removing_org.html@@@Removing a Google Workspace organization from RSC@@@Remove a Google Workspace organization from RSC if you no longer need to protect its Gmail, Google Drive, or Google groups workloads...","gws/gws_required_permissions.html@@@Required RSC permissions for Google Workspace@@@RSC requires specific API permissions within your Google Workspace environment to protect Google Drive, Gmail, Calendar, Contacts, and Google groups...","gws/gws_restoring_google_groups.html@@@Restoring Google groups@@@Restore Google groups, or only their members or settings, from a snapshot to recover a deleted or incorrectly changed group...","gws/gws_self_service_recovery.html@@@Google Workspace self-service recovery@@@Self-service recovery enables Google Workspace users to search for and recover their own data without assistance from an administrator...","gws/gws_skipped_items_backup.html@@@Skipped items during Google Workspace backup@@@RSC occasionally skips backing up some Google Workspace items due to Google API errors or, in rare cases, internal errors...","gws/gws_view_details.html@@@View Google Workspace details@@@You can view the protection status, SLA Domain compliance, and backup health of Google Workspace workloads, such as Google Drive, Gmail, and Google groups, using the Google Workspace dashboard...","gws/gws_view_reports.html@@@View reports for Google Workspace@@@RSC provides reports that enable you to manage and monitor data protection for your Google Workspace workloads...","gws/gws_viewing_drive_dashboard.html@@@Viewing the Google Workspace dashboard@@@View the Google Workspace dashboard to get an overview of your data protection status...","gws/gws_viewing_reports.html@@@Viewing reports@@@Generate and view reports to monitor the protection and recovery of your Google Workspace workloads...","gws/onboard_google_workspace.html@@@Onboard a Google Workspace@@@Onboard a Google Workspace to connect your Google Workspace organization to RSC to enable data protection for your Google Workspace workloads, including Gmail and Google Drive...","gws/recover_gws_data.html@@@Recover Google Workspace data@@@After RSC takes snapshots of your Google Workspace workloads, you can recover the required data from Google Drive, Gmail, Calendar, Contacts, and Google groups...","gws/setup_protection_gws.html@@@Set up protection for Google Workspace@@@After onboarding your Google Workspace organization, you can set up data protection policies to begin protecting Google Drive, Gmail, and Google groups workloads...","gws/sla_assignment_hierarchy_gws.html@@@SLA Domain assignment hierarchy for Google Workspace@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based, automatic protection for Google Drive and Gmail workloads to simplify protection across organizations, Organizational Units (OUs), and individual items...","gws/sla_options_gws.html@@@SLA Domain options for Google Workspace@@@Understanding the various protection options is important when creating an SLA Domain for your Google Workspace workloads. This ensures alignment with organizational needs...","hadr/creating_ha_policies.html@@@Creating HA Policies@@@Create HA Policies to define the primary and secondary Rubrik cluster pair, hosts, and the archival locations that participate in a failover...","hadr/creating_ha_sla_domains.html@@@Creating HA SLA Domains@@@Create an HA SLA Domain with bidirectional replication to protect workloads with an HA Policy...","hadr/deleting_ha_policies.html@@@Deleting HA Policies@@@Delete HA Policies that are no longer needed...","hadr/ha_policy_management.html@@@HA Policy management@@@You can add or remove members from an HA Policy, edit HA SLA Domains, and delete HA Policies that are no longer needed...","hadr/hadr_key_concepts.html@@@High Availability key concepts@@@High Availability Policies use the following key concepts to manage failovers and failbacks...","hadr/hadr_overview.html@@@High Availability for Rubrik clusters@@@High Availability keeps backup and archival operations running even when a Rubrik cluster becomes unavailable. By pairing clusters into primary and secondary roles, you can fail over to the secondary cluster and continue your scheduled backups and uploads with minimal disruption...","hadr/hadr_prerequisites.html@@@High Availability prerequisites@@@Information about the requirements, supported configurations, and limitations for High Availability...","hadr/how_failover_works.html@@@How failover works@@@High Availability Policies follow a defined sequence of actions to manage data protection during a failover...","hadr/performing_failback.html@@@Performing a failback@@@Start a failback to restore backup and recovery operations from the secondary Rubrik cluster to the original primary Rubrik cluster after a failover...","hadr/performing_failover.html@@@Performing a failover@@@Start a manual failover to transfer backup and recovery operations from the primary Rubrik cluster to the secondary Rubrik cluster in a High Availability Policy...","hadr/preparing_create_ha_policy.html@@@Preparing to create an HA Policy@@@Prepare the clusters and hosts that you want to manage with the HA Policy...","hadr/protecting_workloads_ha_policy.html@@@Protecting workloads with an HA Policy@@@Assign a High Availability SLA Domain to the protected workloads that you want to manage with an HA Policy...","identity_recovery/identity_recovery.html@@@Identity Recovery@@@Identity Recovery orchestrates the recovery of identity infrastructure, including Active Directory forests and Microsoft Entra ID tenants, from accidental deletion, misconfiguration, account compromise, or catastrophic failure...","identity_recovery/irec_accidental_changes.html@@@Recovery from accidental deletion or misconfiguration@@@Rubrik Security Cloud provides tools to identify and revert changes to directory objects, such as Active Directory Organizational Units or Microsoft Entra ID Security Groups...","identity_recovery/irec_ad_ransomware_recovery.html@@@Ransomware isolated to Active Directory@@@When a ransomware attack is confined to on-premises Active Directory and Microsoft Entra ID remains operational, RSC performs a targeted recovery that restores only AD-synced identities...","identity_recovery/irec_compromised_accounts.html@@@Remediation of compromised accounts in Microsoft Entra ID@@@Remediation of compromised high-privilege accounts and unauthorized configuration changes restores identity attributes to a known-good state...","identity_recovery/irec_entra_id_selective_recovery.html@@@Selective recovery of Microsoft Entra ID changes@@@RSC restores specific attribute changes in Microsoft Entra ID objects to a previous state...","identity_recovery/irec_full_disaster_recovery.html@@@Full disaster or tenant compromise@@@When both on-premises Active Directory and Microsoft Entra ID are compromised or unavailable, RSC orchestrates a complete recovery across the full hybrid identity infrastructure...","identity_recovery/irec_hybrid_environments.html@@@Recovery of hybrid identity environments@@@Rubrik Security Cloud provides orchestrated recovery workflows to restore hybrid identity environments that include on-premises Active Directory and cloud-based Microsoft Entra ID...","identity_recovery/irec_hybrid_post_recovery_tasks.html@@@Post recovery tasks for hybrid identity environments@@@Post-recovery tasks performed outside of RSC finalize the restoration of a hybrid identity environment...","identity_recovery/irec_identifier_persistence.html@@@Identifier persistence during identity recovery@@@The identity recovery method determines whether the original identifier is preserved or a new identifier is generated, impacting object permissions and relationships...","identity_recovery/irec_rto_factors.html@@@Factors influencing identity recovery time objectives@@@Environmental and technical factors influence the time required to recover identities from Active Directory and Microsoft Entra ID snapshots...","identity_recovery/irec_scenarios.html@@@Identity Recovery scenarios@@@RSC supports recovery of Active Directory and Microsoft Entra ID across a range of scenarios, from targeted rollback of accidental changes to full forest and tenant recovery after a cyberattack or disaster...","identity_recovery/irec_strategy.html@@@Identity Recovery strategy@@@An Identity Recovery strategy provides a framework for restoring Identity Provider services from isolated, immutable backups after a cyberattack or accidental deletion...","identity_recovery/irec_use_cases_triggers.html@@@Identity Recovery use cases and triggers@@@Identity Recovery in Rubrik Security Cloud addresses common causes of identity failure through specific recovery use cases, technical triggers, and recommended restoration methods...","identity_resilience/creating_alert_rule.html@@@Creating an alert rule@@@Create a custom alert rule to generate alerts for specific activities detected in an Identity Provider...","identity_resilience/deleting_alert_rule.html@@@Deleting an alert rule@@@Delete a custom alert rule to stop triggering alerts and remove the alert rule from RSC permanently when you no longer need it...","identity_resilience/disabling_alert_rule.html@@@Disabling an alert rule@@@Disable an alert rule to stop triggering alerts from a specific alert rule...","identity_resilience/duplicating_alert_rule.html@@@Duplicating an alert rule@@@Duplicate a custom alert rule to apply the same alert rule or add conditions to the existing alert rule to generate alerts that are uniquely specific to your requirements...","identity_resilience/editing_alert_rule.html@@@Editing an alert rule@@@Edit a custom alert rule to modify the alert rule details and add conditions to generate alerts that are uniquely specific to your requirements...","identity_resilience/enabling_alert_rule.html@@@Enabling an alert rule@@@Enable a disabled alert rule to resume triggering alerts from a specific alert rule...","identity_resilience/identity_resilience.html@@@Identity Resilience@@@Rubrik Identity Resilience secures, monitors, and recovers the Identity Providers...","identity_resilience/ir_activity_auditor.html@@@Activity auditor in Identity Resilience@@@The Activity auditor provides a centralized, immutable record of identity management events and authentication attempts across supported identity providers...","identity_resilience/ir_activity_log_filters.html@@@Activity log filters@@@RSC provides filters for activity logs across your hybrid identity environments...","identity_resilience/ir_activity_logs.html@@@Activity logs@@@Rubrik Identity Resilience provides a comprehensive, immutable, and actionable audit log of all changes within identity providers, such as Active Directory, Entra ID, and Okta...","identity_resilience/ir_activity_revert.html@@@Activity revert@@@Activity revert restores Microsoft Entra ID, Active Directory, and Okta objects to a known good state by reverting discrete change events captured in the Activity Log...","identity_resilience/ir_ad_authentication_log.html@@@AD authentication logs@@@RSC monitors and logs various authentication actions for the Active Directory identity provider...","identity_resilience/ir_ad_domain_config.html@@@AD domain configuration@@@You can configure an Active Directory (AD) domain so that RSC can track identity activities in the domain...","identity_resilience/ir_ad_privileged_groups.html@@@Privileged groups in Active Directory@@@Privileged groups are built-in administrative groups in Active Directory that carry elevated access across the domain...","identity_resilience/ir_ad_privileged_groups_2.html@@@Privileged groups in Active Directory@@@Privileged groups are built-in administrative groups in Active Directory that carry elevated access across the domain...","identity_resilience/ir_adding_idp.html@@@Adding an Identity Provider@@@Add your first Identity Provider to RSC to start protecting the identities in your hybrid identity environment...","identity_resilience/ir_agent_activity.html@@@Identity Resilience integration with Rubrik Agent Cloud@@@Identity Resilience integrates with Rubrik Agent Cloud to add the Agent Activity tab. The tab shows the AI agent sessions, actions, active alerts, and accessed agents of an identity, so that you can assess what the identity did through AI agents after a suspected compromise...","identity_resilience/ir_agent_activity_filters.html@@@Agent Activity filters and table columns@@@Information about the filters and table columns on the Agent Activity tab...","identity_resilience/ir_agent_activity_prereq.html@@@Prerequisites for Identity Resilience with Agent Cloud@@@Information about the requirements for using agent activity in Identity Resilience...","identity_resilience/ir_alert_rules.html@@@Alert rules in Identity Resilience@@@Alert rules trigger alerts when specific activities are detected within an Identity Provider by monitoring changes captured through activity logging...","identity_resilience/ir_alerts.html@@@Alerts in Identity Resilience@@@The Alerts feature within Rubrik Identity Resilience provides real-time, live tracking of critical events and suspicious activities detected within your Active Directory and Entra ID environments...","identity_resilience/ir_app_access.html@@@Application access for Entra ID identities@@@RSC maps how Entra ID users gain access to enterprise applications and tracks the downstream impact of identity changes on application access...","identity_resilience/ir_auto_rollback_alert_rules.html@@@Automatic rollback for alert rules@@@You can configure custom alert rules to automatically roll back in-scope Active Directory and Entra ID changes when an alert is triggered, without manual intervention...","identity_resilience/ir_benefits.html@@@Identity Resilience benefits@@@Rubrik Identity Resilience offers faster recovery from identity-based attacks, reduces risk by identifying security gaps, supports scalable recovery across environments, and integrates identity and data protection for comprehensive security. This aids in global compliance and ransomware resilience...","identity_resilience/ir_change_classifications.html@@@Change classifications in clean recovery@@@RSC assigns each change detected during clean recovery one of three classifications based on signals from connected integrations and user-uploaded files...","identity_resilience/ir_changing_policy_violation_status.html@@@Changing policy violation status@@@Change the status of a policy to manage the violation investigation and response...","identity_resilience/ir_changing_status_alerts.html@@@Changing status for alerts@@@Change the status of alerts generated for privilege group membership changes or Group Policy Object modifications...","identity_resilience/ir_classif_src_file_req.html@@@Classification source file requirements@@@IP address range files and IOC files used as classification sources must meet specific format requirements before upload...","identity_resilience/ir_classifying_changes_entra_id.html@@@Classifying changes for targeted rollback recovery@@@Classify changes in a Microsoft Entra ID tenant to identify suspicious and legitimate activity before rolling back only the suspicious changes...","identity_resilience/ir_clean_rec_entra_id.html@@@Clean recovery for Microsoft Entra ID@@@Clean recovery returns a compromised Microsoft Entra ID tenant to a known clean state using one of two recovery types: roll forward or targeted rollback...","identity_resilience/ir_clean_rec_recovery_summ.html@@@Recovery summary for clean recovery@@@The recovery summary for clean recovery includes updated object counts, a new deletion details file, and result statuses that reflect the outcome of excess object deletion...","identity_resilience/ir_clean_recovery.html@@@Clean recovery@@@Clean recovery returns a compromised identity environment to a clean and current state by selectively recovering legitimate business changes alongside the identity infrastructure...","identity_resilience/ir_clean_recovery_ad.html@@@Clean recovery for Active Directory@@@Clean recovery for Active Directory combines Active Directory Forest Recovery with roll forward recovery to return the AD forest to a clean and current state after a security breach...","identity_resilience/ir_comparing_gpo_versions.html@@@Comparing GPO versions@@@Compare a Group Policy Object against a historical snapshot to identify configuration changes and optionally roll back to a previous state...","identity_resilience/ir_computer_memberships.html@@@Memberships@@@The Memberships tab on the computer summary page displays the identities, such as Active Directory groups, that the computer account is a member of...","identity_resilience/ir_computer_summary.html@@@Computer summary@@@RSC provides a summary of a single Active Directory computer account with insights into its attributes and security posture...","identity_resilience/ir_computers.html@@@Computers in Identity Resilience@@@The Computers page in Identity Resilience provides a centralized view of Active Directory computer accounts discovered in your environment...","identity_resilience/ir_computers_filters.html@@@Computers filters@@@RSC provides filters for Active Directory computer accounts discovered from your environment...","identity_resilience/ir_configuring_ad_domain_gpo.html@@@Configuring GPO settings for an AD domain@@@Create a dedicated Group Policy Object that enables the audit policies RSC requires to track changes in an Active Directory domain...","identity_resilience/ir_configuring_ad_domain_manual.html@@@Configuring an AD domain manually@@@Configure your Active Directory domain so that RSC can track identity activities in the domain...","identity_resilience/ir_configuring_event_log_readers.html@@@Configuring Event Log Readers permissions@@@Grant the account that RBS uses read access to the Security event log on the domain controllers, so that RSC can identify which user made each change...","identity_resilience/ir_creating_custom_policy.html@@@Creating a custom policy@@@Create a custom policy to continuously monitor identity security requirements that the Rubrik predefined policies do not cover...","identity_resilience/ir_creating_report.html@@@Creating a report@@@Create Identity Resilience reports for supported operations and auditing use cases...","identity_resilience/ir_creating_report_schedule.html@@@Creating a report schedule@@@Create a schedule for Identity Resilience reports to send the report to the selected email addresses at specific intervals...","identity_resilience/ir_creating_servicenow_ticket_alerts.html@@@Creating a ServiceNow ticket for alerts@@@Create a ServiceNow ticket to track and respond to alerts generated for privilege group membership changes and Group Policy Object modifications...","identity_resilience/ir_creating_servicenow_ticket_violations.html@@@Creating a ServiceNow ticket for violations@@@Create a ServiceNow ticket to track and remediate the policy violations for an identity...","identity_resilience/ir_custom_policies.html@@@Custom policies in Identity Resilience@@@In addition to the Rubrik predefined policies, you can create custom policies to detect identity security risks that are specific to your organization&apos;s compliance requirements and risk tolerance...","identity_resilience/ir_dashboard.html@@@Identity Resilience dashboard@@@The Identity Resilience dashboard provides a unified overview of identity-related policy violations, activity alerts, and the protection status of hybrid identity environments...","identity_resilience/ir_deleting_custom_policy.html@@@Deleting a custom policy@@@Delete a custom policy to stop evaluating it. Deleting a policy closes the violations associated with the policy...","identity_resilience/ir_disabling_policy.html@@@Disabling a policy in Identity Resilience@@@Disable a policy to stop evaluating the policy and prevent the generation of new violations. Disabling a policy closes the violations associated with the policy...","identity_resilience/ir_downloading_violations_csv.html@@@Downloading policy violations as a CSV file@@@Download the Identity Resilience policy violations in your environment as a CSV file for offline analysis and reporting...","identity_resilience/ir_duplicating_policy.html@@@Duplicating a predefined policy@@@Duplicate a Rubrik predefined policy to create a custom policy with modified conditions, such as a different threshold value...","identity_resilience/ir_edit_classif_sources.html@@@Editing classification sources@@@Adjust the integrations and custom files used to classify changes in a Clean Recovery session to refine results without rerunning the full analysis...","identity_resilience/ir_editing_custom_policy.html@@@Editing a custom policy@@@Edit a custom policy to update its conditions or other details as your security requirements change...","identity_resilience/ir_enabling_dns_logs.html@@@Enabling DNS Logs@@@Enable DNS Logs to monitor the creation and deletion of DNS zones and DNS records in Active Directory...","identity_resilience/ir_enabling_policy.html@@@Enabling a disabled policy in Identity Resilience@@@Enable a disabled policy to identify violations associated with that policy...","identity_resilience/ir_events.html@@@Events in Identity Resilience@@@The Identity Resilience Events page provides a detailed operational log and audit trail for managing and protecting your hybrid identity environments, distinct from security alerts...","identity_resilience/ir_excess_obj_del_clean_rec.html@@@Excess object deletion in clean recovery@@@During clean recovery, RSC deletes objects present in the live tenant but absent from the snapshot, returning the tenant to the state captured at the recovery point...","identity_resilience/ir_excess_obj_del_obj_types.html@@@Supported object types for deletion@@@Clean recovery deletes a defined set of Microsoft Entra ID object types present in the live tenant but absent from the snapshot. RSC restores object types not in the supported set without deleting excess objects of that type...","identity_resilience/ir_gpo_inventory.html@@@GPO inventory@@@RSC provides a Group Policy Objects inventory that gives Active Directory administrators a centralized view of all Group Policy Objects, their metadata, and their full change history...","identity_resilience/ir_gpo_inventory_reference.html@@@GPO inventory details@@@Information available on the GPO inventory page and GPO details page in RSC...","identity_resilience/ir_identities.html@@@Identities in Identity Resilience@@@The Identities page in Identity Resilience provides a centralized view of all human and non-human identities discovered in your environment...","identity_resilience/ir_identities_filters.html@@@Identities filters@@@RSC provides filters for identities discovered from your hybrid identity environments based on various criteria...","identity_resilience/ir_identity_api_perms.html@@@API permissions@@@The API Permissions tab lists the Microsoft Graph API permissions that a Microsoft Entra ID service principal has, including privilege status and unique identifiers...","identity_resilience/ir_identity_memberships.html@@@Memberships@@@The Memberships tab displays the privileged memberships and roles associated with an identity...","identity_resilience/ir_identity_summary.html@@@Identity summary@@@RSC provides a summary of a single identity with insights into identity components...","identity_resilience/ir_idp_protection_planning.html@@@IdP protection planning@@@Effective planning for Identity Provider protection involves defining the scope, assessing criticality, strategizing onboarding and integration, managing permissions and credentials, establishing SLA Domains, and preparing for recovery scenarios to ensure robust defense and rapid recovery of identity environments...","identity_resilience/ir_info_computers.html@@@Information about computers@@@Information about the Active Directory computer accounts discovered by RSC...","identity_resilience/ir_info_identities.html@@@Information about identities@@@Information about the identities discovered by RSC...","identity_resilience/ir_investigating_agent_activity_alert.html@@@Investigating agent activity from an alert@@@Review the AI agent activity of the actor in an alert to determine what the actor did after a suspected compromise...","identity_resilience/ir_investigating_agent_activity_identity.html@@@Investigating agent activity for an identity@@@Review the AI agent activity of an identity to assess what a compromised or suspicious identity did...","identity_resilience/ir_investigating_violations.html@@@Investigating a violation@@@Investigate a violation to review the specific attribute values that triggered a policy violation and inspect the full policy logic...","identity_resilience/ir_key_features.html@@@Key features of Identity Resilience@@@RSC provides unified identity management, identity protection, and identity security for human and non-human identities in hybrid identity environments...","identity_resilience/ir_managed_id_agent_id.html@@@Managed identities and agent identities@@@Managed identities and agent identities are types of service accounts used in Microsoft Entra ID to interact securely with RSC and cloud environments...","identity_resilience/ir_managing_notifications_alerts.html@@@Managing notifications for alerts@@@Manage notification channels for alerts generated for privileged group membership changes and Group Policy Object modifications...","identity_resilience/ir_managing_notifications_violations.html@@@Managing notifications for violations@@@Manage notification channels for violations detected in your environment...","identity_resilience/ir_nhi_secrets.html@@@Secrets for service principals@@@The Overview tab for a Microsoft Entra ID service principal displays a Secrets node in the identity graph that shows the client secrets associated with the service principal...","identity_resilience/ir_perform_roll_fwd_entra_id.html@@@Performing roll forward recovery for Microsoft Entra ID@@@Restore a compromised Microsoft Entra ID tenant to a clean state and roll forward legitimate changes from the compromise window...","identity_resilience/ir_perform_roll_fwd_rec_ad.html@@@Performing roll forward recovery for Active Directory@@@Monitor a Clean Recovery session, review classified changes, and execute the roll forward to return the restored Active Directory forest to an operational state...","identity_resilience/ir_perform_tgt_rollback_entra_id.html@@@Performing targeted rollback recovery for Microsoft Entra ID@@@Review classified changes in a Microsoft Entra ID tenant and roll back only the suspicious changes while keeping legitimate changes intact...","identity_resilience/ir_policies_violations.html@@@Policies and violations in Identity Resilience@@@Identity Resilience policies are predefined by Rubrik to identify gaps in your identity security posture and simplify the process to mitigate identity-based cyber risks...","identity_resilience/ir_prereq.html@@@Identity Resilience prerequisites@@@Information about specific requirements for Identity Resilience...","identity_resilience/ir_prereq_clean_rec.html@@@Prerequisites for Active Directory clean recovery@@@Before performing clean recovery for Active Directory, ensure the required license, software version, snapshots, and activity logging configuration are in place...","identity_resilience/ir_protection_identities.html@@@Protection for identities@@@RSC provides the core features of data protection and recovery for identities in Identity Resilience. You can configure, manage, and monitor the protection status of your identity infrastructure...","identity_resilience/ir_rbac.html@@@RBAC for Identity Resilience@@@Information about the privileges required for Identity Resilience access. These privileges help in configuring role-based access control for users...","identity_resilience/ir_recover_ad_forest.html@@@Recovering an Active Directory forest@@@Restore an Active Directory forest to a verified recovery point as the first step of the clean recovery process...","identity_resilience/ir_recovery_paths.html@@@Recovery paths@@@Comparison between roll forward and targeted rollback. Roll forward is recommended when a clean rebuild is required, and targeted rollback is recommended when the attack is contained and minimal disruption to the live environment is a priority...","identity_resilience/ir_remediating_violations.html@@@Remediating violations@@@Remediate policy violations by investigating the impacted identities or domains, understanding the violations, and initiating remediation through direct action or ticket creation...","identity_resilience/ir_remediation_actions.html@@@Remediation actions@@@Information about remediation steps and guidance Rubrik recommends to resolve identified security violations and mitigate risks within your identity environment...","identity_resilience/ir_remediation_preview.html@@@Remediation Summary@@@The Remediation Summary shows the exact changes a remediation action applies to your Active Directory environment before you confirm...","identity_resilience/ir_reports.html@@@Identity Resilience reports@@@The Identity Resilience Reports page offers comprehensive analytics and actionable insights into your identity security posture. It provides various report templates for protection status, identity violations, audit trails, and operational activities across Identity Providers...","identity_resilience/ir_revert_events_audits.html@@@Revert events and audits@@@Information about the events and audit logs that RSC generates during Microsoft Entra ID and Active Directory revert actions...","identity_resilience/ir_reverting_activities.html@@@Reverting detected actions in the Activity Log@@@Restore Microsoft Entra ID, Active Directory, and Okta objects to their state prior to a specific event by reverting changes captured in the Activity Log...","identity_resilience/ir_reverting_alerts.html@@@Reverting alerts@@@Identify and revert accidental errors or unintended changes that could compromise business operations. You can revert and remediate malicious changes by compromised identities to revert the identity system to previous state without performing a full system rollback...","identity_resilience/ir_roll_forward.html@@@Roll forward@@@Roll forward restores a compromised identity environment to a clean baseline snapshot, then replays only legitimate changes from the compromise window into the restored environment...","identity_resilience/ir_roll_forward_entra_id.html@@@Roll forward recovery for Microsoft Entra ID@@@Roll forward recovery restores a compromised Microsoft Entra ID tenant to a snapshot baseline, then classifies and reapplies legitimate changes from the compromise window...","identity_resilience/ir_rolling_back_gpo_changes.html@@@Rolling back GPO changes@@@Roll back Group Policy Object changes to mitigate risks and protect your identity systems. RSC raises an alert if there are modifications to Group Policy Objects...","identity_resilience/ir_setting_up_sacl.html@@@Setting up SACLs for the domain partition@@@Set up the System Access Control List on the domain partition to identify the actor responsible for detected actions in Active Directory...","identity_resilience/ir_setting_up_sacl_configuration.html@@@Setting up SACLs for configuration partition@@@Set up the System Access Control List on the configuration partition to enable actor identification for Active Directory site topology changes...","identity_resilience/ir_sla_domains.html@@@Identity Resilience SLA Domains@@@The SLA Domains page in Identity Resilience manages policy-driven automation for protecting your hybrid identity infrastructure. It defines how identity data is backed up, retained, replicated, and archived, ensuring consistent and compliant protection for your Identity Providers...","identity_resilience/ir_snapshot_comparison.html@@@Snapshot comparison@@@Snapshot comparison identifies every object that changed between the clean baseline snapshot and the latest available snapshot, and attributes each change to the actor who made it using the activity log...","identity_resilience/ir_snapshot_threat_enrichment.html@@@Snapshot threat enrichment@@@Snapshot threat enrichment marks snapshots that fall within a confirmed compromise window, helping you select a safe recovery point and avoid restoring from a compromised state. For Active Directory, enrichment uses both Rubrik&apos;s internal Threat Monitoring scan and identity threat integration alerts. For Microsoft Entra ID, enrichment uses identity threat integration alerts...","identity_resilience/ir_supported_func_idp.html@@@Supported functionalities and identities for IdP@@@Information about the functionalities and identities supported for specific Identity Provider in Identity Resilience...","identity_resilience/ir_supported_revert_actions.html@@@Supported revert actions@@@Lists of actions that RSC performs when reverting a Microsoft Entra ID or Active Directory activity...","identity_resilience/ir_targeted_rollback.html@@@Targeted rollback@@@Targeted rollback stays in the current live environment and reverts only the changes you select, preserving all other changes from the same window...","identity_resilience/ir_targeted_rollback_entra_id.html@@@Targeted rollback recovery for Microsoft Entra ID@@@Targeted rollback reverts suspicious changes in a Microsoft Entra ID tenant while keeping legitimate ones intact...","identity_resilience/ir_verifying_ad_domain_gpo.html@@@Verifying GPO settings for an AD domain@@@Verify that the GPO settings are configured correctly on the Active Directory domain controllers...","identity_resilience/ir_viewing_activity_log.html@@@Viewing activity logs@@@View the activity logs of your identity provider (IdP) to investigate activities that might be non-compliant or that could compromise security...","identity_resilience/ir_viewing_app_access.html@@@Viewing application access for an Entra ID user@@@View the current application access graph and investigate historical access changes for an Entra ID user identity...","identity_resilience/ir_viewing_computer_summary.html@@@Viewing the computer summary@@@View the computer summary page to investigate Active Directory computer accounts suspected of compromise or non-compliance...","identity_resilience/ir_viewing_gpo_inventory.html@@@Viewing the GPO inventory@@@View and filter the Group Policy Object inventory to inspect GPO metadata and navigate to individual GPO details...","identity_resilience/ir_viewing_identity_summary.html@@@Viewing the identity summary@@@View the identity summary page to investigate identities suspected of compromise or non-compliance...","identity_resilience/ir_viewing_violation_history.html@@@Viewing the history of a policy violation@@@View the history of an Identity Resilience policy violation to track its status changes and remediation activity over time...","identity_resilience/ir_violation_history.html@@@Violation history@@@The violation history provides a timeline of a single policy violation&apos;s lifecycle, from detection through status changes and remediation...","identity_resilience/signin_log_details.html@@@Sign-in log details@@@Sign-in log details include authentication information, identity context, and security metadata for sign-in events...","identity_resilience/signin_logs.html@@@Sign-in logs@@@Sign-in logs capture and surface authentication events from Microsoft Entra ID and Okta to provide visibility into access attempts and identity risks...","identity_resilience/viewing_signin_logs.html@@@Viewing sign-in logs@@@Viewing and filtering authentication events for identity providers helps investigate failed sign-ins and suspicious authentication patterns...","informix/adding_informix_instances.html@@@Adding Informix instances@@@Add an IBM Informix instance to RSC to enable data protection...","informix/considerations_manual_data_recovery.html@@@Considerations for manual data recovery@@@Manual data recovery considerations for IBM Informix instances...","informix/deleting_informix_instances.html@@@Deleting Informix instances@@@Delete an IBM Informix instance when data protection for the instance is no longer necessary...","informix/editing_informix_instances.html@@@Editing Informix instances@@@Edit the configuration details of an existing Informix instance on RSC, such as updating credentials or changing the IBM Informix user name...","informix/high_availability_support.html@@@High availability support@@@High availability in Informix helps ensure uninterrupted data protection for Informix hosts in the event of hardware failures, software errors, natural disasters, power outages, and network issues...","informix/ibm_informix.html@@@IBM Informix@@@RSC provides native data protection and recovery for IBM Informix instances...","informix/informix_requirements_limitations.html@@@Informix requirements and limitations@@@Protecting IBM Informix databases with RSC requires meeting specific requirements and prerequisites...","informix/key_features_informix_protection.html@@@Key features for Informix protection@@@RSC provides unified data protection, flexible recovery options, and advanced security for IBM Informix instances...","informix/manage_informix_protection.html@@@Manage Informix protection@@@After adding an Informix instance, you can manage protection of the instance from the RSC IBM Informix instances page...","informix/manually_adding_linux_unix_hosts.html@@@Manually adding Linux or Unix hosts@@@Add a Linux or Unix host to register the host with RSC and manually install the RBS software...","informix/manually_performing_informix_recovery.html@@@Manually performing an Informix recovery@@@Manually recover an IBM Informix instance to a specific snapshot or point in time...","informix/pausing_resuming_protection_informix.html@@@Pausing and resuming protection for Informix instances@@@Pause scheduled backup, archival, and replication actions for a specific database workload without affecting the protection of other objects managed by the SLA Domain...","informix/plan_informix_protection.html@@@Plan your Informix protection@@@Informix protection planning covers user access management, system requirements, prerequisites, and current protection limitations...","informix/protect_informix_instances.html@@@Protect Informix instances@@@RSC provides automated and on-demand methods for protecting your IBM Informix instances...","informix/recover_informix_instances.html@@@Recover Informix instances@@@RSC protects IBM Informix instances so that you can recover critical data...","informix/recovering_informix_instances.html@@@Recovering Informix instances@@@Recover an IBM Informix instance to the state of a specific snapshot or to a specific point in time...","informix/recovery_point_options.html@@@Recovery point options@@@You can recover Informix instance data to a scheduled or on-demand backup snapshot or to its state at a specific point in time...","informix/refreshing_informix_instances.html@@@Refreshing Informix instances@@@Manually refresh an IBM Informix instance on RSC to update its inventory and current status...","informix/remotely_adding_linux_unix_hosts.html@@@Remotely adding Linux or Unix hosts@@@Add a Linux or Unix host to register the host with RSC and automatically install the RBS software on the host...","informix/rsc_user_management_informix.html@@@RSC user management for Informix protection@@@You can manage access to Informix protection tasks in RSC by assigning roles and privileges to user accounts...","informix/scheduling_automated_backups.html@@@Scheduling automated backups@@@Schedule automated backups for IBM Informix instances by assigning an SLA Domain...","informix/setup_informix.html@@@Set up Informix@@@To begin protecting IBM Informix, add the Linux or Unix system that hosts your Informix instance to the RSC inventory...","informix/sla_domain_assignments_informix_objects.html@@@SLA Domain assignments for Informix objects@@@Assigning an SLA Domain activates automated protection for your Informix instances and enables policy-driven backup management...","informix/supporting_high_availability_protection.html@@@Supporting high availability protection@@@Configure RSC to back up Informix instances that participate in a high availability configuration in Informix...","informix/taking_on_demand_snapshots_informix.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Informix instances@@@Initiate an immediate, on-demand snapshot on RSC for one or more protected IBM Informix instances...","informix/unmounting_informix_live_mount.html@@@Unmounting an Informix Live Mount@@@Unmount an Informix Live Mount after completing a manual recovery or when it is no longer required...","informix/viewing_informix_sla_domains.html@@@Viewing Informix SLA Domain details@@@Review the protection policy of an IBM Informix instance by viewing its assigned SLA Domain details...","install/adding_certificate_during_cluster_registration.html@@@Adding a custom certificate during cluster registration@@@If your environment uses packet inspection that requires a custom certificate for outbound connectivity, add the certificate during cluster registration before completing the online registration process...","install/configuring_node_use_lacp.html@@@Configuring a node to use LACP@@@Configures a node to use LACP from the command line for an existing cluster...","install/download_install_cdm_on_appliance_nodes.html@@@Downloading and installing Rubrik CDM@@@Before you set up your Rubrik cluster, you can install a version of Rubrik CDM that is different from the one already installed on the Rubrik appliance nodes. This involves downloading the software, transferring it to one of the nodes, and running the installation...","install/guidelines_strong_password.html@@@Guidelines for choosing a strong password@@@When choosing a password, you are required to follow the guidelines recommended by Rubrik to set a strong password that is difficult to guess or extract through a password cracker application, but is something that is easy to remember...","install/lacp_configuration.html@@@LACP configuration@@@Link Aggregation Control Protocol combines multiple network connections in parallel to increase throughput and fault tolerance for Rubrik clusters...","install/node_ipmi_port.html@@@Node IPMI port@@@Rubrik nodes use the IPMI interface and protocol to gather hardware information. The IPMI socket enables console access when required. An IPMI connection is optional during normal operation, but the installation of Rubrik CDM on third-party servers requires this connection...","install/registering_clusters_offline.html@@@Registering Rubrik clusters using the offline method@@@Use the offline registration method when the Rubrik cluster cannot establish a connection with Rubrik Security Cloud...","install/registering_clusters_online.html@@@Registering Rubrik clusters using the online method@@@Register your Rubrik cluster using the online method to connect it to Rubrik Security Cloud for centralized management and entitlement activation...","install/rsc_cluster_config_considerations.html@@@Cluster configuration considerations@@@You determine network related settings and capabilities of a Rubrik cluster through the set up task...","install/rsc_cluster_deployment.html@@@Rubrik cluster deployment@@@Deploying a Rubrik cluster running on Rubrik appliance nodes involves installing the CDM software on the nodes and setting up that software for your environment...","install/rsc_cluster_registration.html@@@Cluster registration@@@Rubrik offers two methods for registering clusters with Rubrik Security Cloud, online and offline...","install/rsc_disabling_mfa.html@@@Disabling MFA@@@Disable multi-factor authentication for newly registered clusters...","install/rsc_enabling_mfa.html@@@Enabling MFA@@@Enable multi-factor authentication for newly registered clusters...","install/rsc_resolving_cluster_regn_issues.html@@@Resolving cluster registration issues@@@Provide the Rubrik Support team with secure, time-limited access to the cluster for help resolving issues encountered during Rubrik cluster registration with Rubrik Security Cloud...","install/rsc_service_types.html@@@Rubrik Security Cloud service types@@@Rubrik Security Cloud offers two distinct service types, SaaS mode and software mode, which provide different sets of functionality...","install/rsc_unified_cluster_regn.html@@@Unified Rubrik cluster registration@@@The unified cluster registration process applies to all types of Rubrik cluster deployments...","install/setting_up_rubrik_cluster_VLAN_using_cli.html@@@Setting up a Rubrik cluster with VLAN using the CLI@@@Set up a Rubrik cluster using the Rubrik CLI and provide VLAN support. VLAN support allows you to set up logical segmentation and management of network traffic...","install/setting_up_rubrik_cluster_using_cli.html@@@Setting up a Rubrik cluster using the CLI@@@Use the Rubrik CLI to set up a new Rubrik cluster...","install/setting_up_rubrik_cluster_using_ui.html@@@Setting up a Rubrik cluster using the UI@@@Set up a Rubrik cluster using the system setup UI provided on a node...","install/shutting_down_a_node.html@@@Shutting down a node@@@The node shutdown process powers down a specific node in a Rubrik cluster...","install/shutting_down_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Shutting down the Rubrik cluster@@@To power down all the nodes in a Rubrik cluster, shut down the cluster using CLI...","install/switch_configuration_examples.html@@@Switch configuration examples@@@Various network switch models require specific configurations for Rubrik CDM connectivity...","install/system_shutdown.html@@@System shutdown@@@A system shutdown can be done from the Rubrik CLI...","install/troubleshooting_lost_port_conn.html@@@Troubleshooting lost port connections@@@Updating the bond configuration based on the switch Link Aggregation Control Protocol support resolves lost port connections...","install/vlan_tagging_cluster_mgmt_networks.html@@@VLAN tagging Rubrik cluster management and data networks@@@You can add VLAN tagging to a Rubrik cluster to help manage network traffic...","integrations/connecting_jira_instance.html@@@Connecting a Jira instance@@@Connect a Jira instance to RSC to enable Jira ticket creation for Data Security Posture...","integrations/jira_integration.html@@@Jira integration@@@Integrate Jira with RSC to create tickets and start security investigations directly from RSC...","integrations/jira_prerequisites.html@@@Prerequisites for Jira integration@@@The Jira integration requires specific environment and account configurations in RSC...","integrations/jira_ticket_creation_dsp.html@@@Jira ticket creation in Data Security Posture@@@Jira ticket creation in RSC enables remediation of data access issues in Data Security Posture through automated workflows and contextual data sharing...","integrations/viewing_status_tickets.html@@@Viewing ticket status in Data Security Posture@@@Monitor the progress and status of tickets created for Data Security Posture issues...","jira/jira.html@@@Atlassian Jira@@@To protect your Atlassian Jira data, you can back up and restore data, such as projects, settings, workflows, and issues, in your Jira site...","jira/jira_adding_instance.html@@@Adding an Atlassian Jira instance@@@Add an Atlassian Jira instance of the Jira site that you want to back up and restore. For example, you can back up and restore data types such as projects, workflows, and issues. You can add more Jira instances if your have multiple sites that you want to protect...","jira/jira_analyzing_data.html@@@Analyzing Atlassian Jira data@@@RSC provides graphs about snapshot activity for an Atlassian Jira instance that helps you analyze the point in time to use to restore data when an anomaly is detected in deleted, changed, or added issues or settings. Analyzing data helps you understand if and when data was lost and what data was lost...","jira/jira_backups.html@@@Atlassian Jira backups@@@You can securely back up your Atlassian Jira data types with snapshots and restore your data from those snapshots. You can back up data such as tasks and subtasks and restore that information if the data is compromised...","jira/jira_data_event_backup_failure.html@@@Data event backup failure for Atlassian Jira@@@RSC sends an event when Atlassian Jira data backup fails because access to Jira projects was denied to an authenticated user...","jira/jira_deleting_instance.html@@@Removing Jira instances@@@Remove a Jira instance to remove all snapshots and configurations from RSC...","jira/jira_instance_details.html@@@Atlassian Jira instance details@@@The Atlassian Jira details page helps you monitor and analyze your data to view important details, such the number of backups during a specified time period. You can also access features from the details page, such as managing protection and restoring data...","jira/jira_protection_sla_domain.html@@@Atlassian Jira protection using SLA Domains@@@You can manage protection for Atlassian Jira sites by using SLA Domains. SLA Domains provide protection policies for your sites so that you can securely back up and restore data...","jira/jira_rbac_required_permissions.html@@@Required RBAC permissions for Atlassian Jira@@@Accessing Atlassian Jira protection features within RSC requires the appropriate RBAC permissions. You can use the default Jira Admin role or a custom role...","jira/jira_reauthenticate.html@@@Reauthenticating your Atlassian Jira account@@@Reauthenticate your Atlassian Jira account when Jira revokes authentication after a period of time or when the account used to authenticate is no longer active in the Jira site...","jira/jira_recovery.html@@@Atlassian Jira recovery@@@You can restore data for your Atlassian Jira issues and Jira settings to their original location from any point-in-time snapshot...","jira/jira_regions.html@@@Supported regions for Atlassian Jira@@@RSC provides support for Atlassian Jira protection in several regions. You select the region when you set up the Jira instance in RSC...","jira/jira_relationships.html@@@Atlassian Jira data relationships and cascading impact@@@Atlassian Jira data types are based on data type relationships. RSC allows you to maintain these relationships when restoring information...","jira/jira_restore_issue_keys.html@@@Restore Atlassian Jira issue keys@@@When the Atlassian Jira issue you are restoring has been deleted in your Atlassian Jira site, Jira creates a new issue key that identifies your work in Jira. RSC provides a mapping of the new key value to the old key value for your reference...","jira/jira_restoring_issue.html@@@Restoring Altassian Jira issues@@@Restore issue types, such as epics, stories, bugs, tasks, and subtasks, to their original location from any point-in-time snapshot if data is lost or compromised...","jira/jira_restoring_settings.html@@@Restoring Altassian Jira settings@@@Restore Atlassian Jira settings, including workflows, filters, dashboards, and screens, to their original location. Use any point-in-time snapshot to restore data if your data is lost...","jira/jira_site_connection_oauth.html@@@OAuth authentication for Jira site connection@@@RSC uses OAuth to connect to the Atlassian Jira sites that you want to back up. You must use a Jira user with the site admin permissions to authorize connection to the Jira site with OAuth...","jira/jira_supported_data_types.html@@@Supported Atlassian Jira data types@@@RSC can back up and restore a variety of Atlassian Jira data types, such as project issues and workflows...","jira/jira_taking_on_demand_snapshots.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Atlassian Jira instances@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, you can back up your data at any time by taking an on-demand snapshot of Atlassian Jira projects or settings for a Jira instance...","jira/jira_viewing_details.html@@@Viewing details about an Atlassian Jira instance@@@View details about an Atlassian Jira instance to monitor and analyze data and to access features, such as managing protection...","kubernetes/K8s_crd_rsc.html@@@RSC Custom resource definitions@@@You can use the RSC custom resource definitions to create custom resources for backup and recovery workflows using APIs native to Kubernetes...","kubernetes/anomaly_detection_k8.html@@@Anomaly Detection for Kubernetes@@@You can enable Anomaly Detection for Kubernetes virtual machines and protection sets to identify and analyze anomalous events that can indicate a ransomware attack...","kubernetes/assigning_sla_domains_kubernetes_labels.html@@@Assigning SLA Domains to Kubernetes labels@@@Assign SLA Domains to Kubernetes labels to protect the Kubernetes virtual machines...","kubernetes/custom_resource_definition_examples.html@@@Custom resource definition examples@@@The examples in this section use the RSC custom resource definitions to create custom resources for backup and recovery, for assigning SLA Domains, performing on-demand shots, and for many other operations typically done using the RSC UI...","kubernetes/definitions_additional_recovery_operations.html@@@Additional recovery operation definitions@@@You can perform additional recovery operations using various definitions, including filtering and PVC-only recovery...","kubernetes/example_recover_ps_other_namespace.html@@@Exporting a protection set to another namespace@@@You can use CRDs to export a protection set to a different namespace for a specific point in time...","kubernetes/example_restoring_snapshot_using_crds.html@@@Restoring a protection set to the same namespace@@@You can use CRDs to restore a protection set to the same namespace for a specific point in time...","kubernetes/example_taking_ods_using_crds.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots using CRDs@@@You can take an on-demand snapshot of a Kubernetes cluster using CRDs...","kubernetes/example_using_crds_to_assing_an_sla_domain.html@@@Using CRDs to add an SLA Domain@@@You can use CRDs to add an SLA Domain UUID to a protection set to protect Kubernetes workloads...","kubernetes/examples_creating_protection_sets_exclude.html@@@Protection set examples using exclude parameters@@@You can use CRDs to create protection sets to determine which filtered objects to exclude...","kubernetes/examples_creating_protection_sets_using_crds.html@@@Protection set examples using include parameters@@@You can use CRDs to create protection sets with include parameters, to determine which filtered objects to include...","kubernetes/exporting_snapshots_created_k8s_labels.html@@@Exporting snapshots created using Kubernetes labels@@@Export a snapshot of a Kubernetes virtual machine that includes labels to recover data to a new namespace...","kubernetes/k8s_adding_amazon_eks_cluster.html@@@Adding an Amazon EKS cluster to RSC@@@To protect the applications and data in an Amazon EKS cluster, add the EKS cluster to RSC by configuring an AWS cloud account and an ARN for the EKS cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_adding_k8s_cluster.html@@@Adding a Kubernetes cluster to RSC@@@To protect the applications and data in your Kubernetes cluster, add it to RSC by uploading a kubeconfig, applying a generated manifest, or installing with Helm...","kubernetes/k8s_application_protection_set.html@@@Application protection sets@@@An application protection set protects enterprise workloads spanning multiple Kubernetes namespaces as a single unit...","kubernetes/k8s_application_protectionset_crd.html@@@ApplicationProtectionSet Custom Resource Definition@@@The ApplicationProtectionSet custom resource definition enables you to create and manage an application protection set using Kubernetes-native tools such as kubectl...","kubernetes/k8s_application_ps_namespace_patterns.html@@@Namespace patterns and dependency traversal@@@Application protection sets use namespace patterns to define scope and filters to identify entry-point workloads. Rubrik automatically captures dependency resources linked to matched workloads...","kubernetes/k8s_applying_image_patch.html@@@Applying a Kubernetes protection image patch@@@Apply an image-only patch to the Kubernetes protection images on your cluster, based on the method you used to onboard the cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_browse_kubernetes_snapshots.html@@@Browse Kubernetes snapshots@@@You can use RSC to browse the resources in a Kubernetes snapshot for protection sets and virtual machines...","kubernetes/k8s_browsing_kubernetes_snapshots.html@@@Browsing Kubernetes snapshots@@@Browse the contents of a Kubernetes snapshot to view the resources...","kubernetes/k8s_changing_retention_for_ods_snapshots.html@@@Changing retention for on-demand Kubernetes snapshots@@@Change the retention for on-demand snapshots of a Kubernetes protection set...","kubernetes/k8s_cluster.html@@@K8SCluster CRD@@@The K8SCluster custom resource definition creates a read-only custom resource that provides information about your Kubernetes clusters...","kubernetes/k8s_cluster_example.html@@@K8SCluster CRD example@@@Example of the information provided in a K8SCluster custom resource for a Kubernetes cluster protected by a Rubrik cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_cluster_onboard_discover_rsc.html@@@Kubernetes cluster onboarding@@@To onboard your Kubernetes cluster, add it to your RSC domain and provide RSC with access to the cluster and sufficient permissions...","kubernetes/k8s_cluster_protection_set.html@@@Protection sets for Kubernetes cluster workloads@@@A Kubernetes cluster protection set define the resources to protect on a Kubernetes cluster. A cluster protection set can include an entire Kubernetes namespace or a subset of resources within a namespace...","kubernetes/k8s_cluster_spec_and_status_fields.html@@@K8SCluster CRD spec and status fields@@@The K8SCluster custom resource definition spec and status fields provide information about Kubernetes clusters that are protected by Rubrik clusters...","kubernetes/k8s_clusterroles.html@@@Kubernetes ClusterRoles@@@RSC includes the kupr-admin and kupr-user ClusterRoles...","kubernetes/k8s_configuring_namespace_protection.html@@@Configuring namespace protection@@@Create the kubeconfig file, the ClusterRole, and the ClusterRoleBinding for the kubeconfig user to assign the permissions required to protect all namespaces...","kubernetes/k8s_configuring_perms_kubeconfig.html@@@Configuring permissions to protect all resources@@@Create the kubeconfig file, and then set up the ClusterRole and ClusterRoleBinding to grant the kubeconfig user the necessary permissions to protect all namespaces and cluster-wide resources...","kubernetes/k8s_configuring_perms_specific_resources.html@@@Configuring permissions to protect specific resources@@@Create the kubeconfig file, the ClusterRole, and the ClusterRoleBinding for the kubeconfig user to use to assign the required permissions to protect specific resources within a namespace...","kubernetes/k8s_crd_prerqs.html@@@Kubernetes Protection CRD requirements@@@To use Kubernetes Protection custom resource definitions you must have certain resources available...","kubernetes/k8s_create_bindings_k8s_crd.html@@@Creating role bindings for working with CRDs@@@Create kupr-user and kupr-namespace-user role bindings for users that work with Kubernetes custom resource definitions...","kubernetes/k8s_creating_application_protection_set.html@@@Creating an application protection set@@@Create an application protection set to protect workloads that span multiple Kubernetes namespaces as a single unit...","kubernetes/k8s_creating_custom_protection_set.html@@@Creating a custom protection set for a namespace@@@To protect the applications and data of Kubernetes cluster namespaces or resources using RSC, create a custom protection set that includes specific types of resources...","kubernetes/k8s_creating_dflt_protec_set_namespace.html@@@Creating a default protection set for a namespace@@@To protect the applications and data of an entire Kubernetes namespace using RSC, create a protection set that includes the entire namespace without filtering for specific types of resources...","kubernetes/k8s_creating_live_mount.html@@@Creating a Live Mount for OpenShift virtual machines@@@Create a Live Mount for an OpenShift virtual machine on a Kubernetes cluster from a snapshot on the Rubrik cluster. The live mounted virtual machine uses the Rubrik cluster as its underlying storage...","kubernetes/k8s_csi_driver_prereq.html@@@CSI driver prerequisite@@@RSC provides Persistent Volume protection only for the volumes provisioned using a Container Storage Interface that supports VolumeSnapshot...","kubernetes/k8s_custom_resources_k8s_protection.html@@@Kubernetes protection CRDs@@@You can perform backup and recovery workflows using native APIs for Kubernetes by using the Rubrik custom resource definitions...","kubernetes/k8s_default_protection_sets.html@@@Default protection sets@@@RSC includes default protection sets that are automatically created for Kubernetes clusters. These protection sets include all namespaces, and relieve you of having to create protection sets manually...","kubernetes/k8s_deleting_k8s_cluster.html@@@Deleting a Kubernetes cluster@@@Delete a Kubernetes cluster from RSC to stop protecting the data and applications associated with the protection sets of the cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_deleting_protection_set_rsc.html@@@Deleting a Kubernetes protection set from RSC@@@Delete a Kubernetes protection set from RSC to stop protecting the data and applications associated with the protection set...","kubernetes/k8s_deleting_snapshot.html@@@Deleting a Kubernetes snapshot@@@Delete a Kubernetes snapshot that has the Forever retention policy assigned...","kubernetes/k8s_deployment_architecture.html@@@Deployment architecture for Kubernetes protection@@@RSC serves as the control plane for Kubernetes protection. A connected Rubrik cluster stores the Persistent Volume backups...","kubernetes/k8s_disabling_default_protection_set.html@@@Disabling a default protection set@@@Disable a default protection set you no longer need...","kubernetes/k8s_editing_kubernetes_cluster.html@@@Editing the Kubernetes cluster@@@Edit a Kubernetes cluster to update its configuration or refresh its connection to RSC...","kubernetes/k8s_editing_protection_set.html@@@Editing a protection set@@@Edit the protection set to change the kind and label filters...","kubernetes/k8s_exporting_openshift_snapshots.html@@@Exporting OpenShift virtual machine snapshots@@@Export an OpenShift cluster virtual machine snapshot to recover data to a new namespace...","kubernetes/k8s_hook_crd.html@@@Hook CRD@@@The Hook custom resource definition can be used to run commands before and after running a backup of a protection set...","kubernetes/k8s_hook_example.html@@@Hook CRD example@@@Example of adding commands to the pre and post fields of the spec field for a Hook custom resource definition. These commands run before or after the backup of a resource set...","kubernetes/k8s_hook_spec_and_status_fields.html@@@Hook CRD spec@@@The spec fields of the Hook custom resource definition describe commands to run before and after a backup...","kubernetes/k8s_image_tags.html@@@Kubernetes protection image tags@@@Rubrik publishes the Kubernetes protection images to Docker Hub with version tags that match the Rubrik CDM version...","kubernetes/k8s_label_recommendations_limitations.html@@@Kubernetes label recommendations and limitations@@@Using Kubernetes labels with RSC includes certain recommendations and limitations...","kubernetes/k8s_limitations_openshift_clusters.html@@@Limitations for OpenShift virtual machine support@@@Protecting OpenShift clusters on RSC has some limitations. You can work around most limitations...","kubernetes/k8s_managing_workload_protection.html@@@Managing Kubernetes workload protection@@@Manage protection for Kubernetes workloads by assigning SLA Domains to schedule policy-based snapshots, change retention for policy-based snapshots, or exclude the workloads from protection...","kubernetes/k8s_manifest_based_onboarding_resources.html@@@Manifest-based onboarding resources@@@When you onboard a Kubernetes cluster using the manifest-based method, RSC deploys some resources in the Kubernetes cluster. After the connection is established, RSC deploys additional resources during the first refresh job...","kubernetes/k8s_map_pset_storage_recovery.html@@@Mapping StorageClasses during Kubernetes protection set recovery@@@Map source StorageClasses to target StorageClasses when recovering resources from a Kubernetes protection set...","kubernetes/k8s_map_vm_storage_recovery.html@@@Mapping StorageClasses during Kubernetes virtual machine recovery@@@Map source StorageClasses to target StorageClasses when recovering a Kubernetes virtual machine...","kubernetes/k8s_mounting_virtual_disks.html@@@Mounting OpenShift virtual machine disks@@@Mount specific virtual disks from an OpenShift virtual machine snapshot to an existing virtual machine. The mounted virtual disks use the Rubrik cluster as their datastore...","kubernetes/k8s_multi_networking.html@@@Kubernetes multi-networking for backup traffic@@@You can configure a dedicated network for Rubrik backup and restore traffic on on-premises Kubernetes clusters to improve performance and isolate backup traffic from application traffic. This feature requires Rubrik CDM versions 9.4.2 and later...","kubernetes/k8s_nfs_ip_configuration.html@@@NFS client IP configuration@@@Rubrik uses specific IP addresses from Kubernetes nodes to expose NFS shares during a Live Mount operation...","kubernetes/k8s_node_proxy_transport.html@@@Node Proxy transport for Kubernetes backups@@@The Node Proxy transport routes backup and restore traffic for Rubrik Backup Agent pods, including backups of OpenShift virtual machines, over a dedicated backup network without assigning a routable IP address to each pod...","kubernetes/k8s_openshift_clusters.html@@@OpenShift Virtual Machine workload@@@You can use RSC to protect containers and virtual machines managed on Kubernetes OpenShift clusters...","kubernetes/k8s_openshift_recovering_files.html@@@Recovering files from an OpenShift virtual machine snapshot@@@Download files or folders from an OpenShift virtual machine snapshot. You can then manually recover the downloaded files and folders to the source virtual machine or another location...","kubernetes/k8s_performing_ods_openshift_clusters.html@@@Creating an on-demand snapshot of an OpenShift virtual machine@@@Create an on-demand snapshot of a virtual machine that is hosted on an OpenShift cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_prereqs.html@@@Kubernetes protection prerequisites@@@There are common and specific prerequisites for Kubernetes protection...","kubernetes/k8s_prereqs_aws_eks.html@@@K8S prerequisites for AWS EKS deployments@@@Protecting the EKS Kubernetes clusters deployed in the AWS public cloud RSC requires specific configurations on the Kubernetes clusters...","kubernetes/k8s_prereqs_azure_aks.html@@@K8S prerequisites for Azure AKS deployments@@@Protecting the AKS Kubernetes clusters deployed in the Azure public cloud RSC requires specific configurations on the Kubernetes clusters...","kubernetes/k8s_prereqs_openshift_vm_live_mount.html@@@Prerequisites for OpenShift virtual machine Live Mount@@@Before creating a Live Mount, you must ensure the Kubernetes cluster environment is configured to support network file system, specific version requirements, and the required volume types...","kubernetes/k8s_prereqs_rosa.html@@@Prerequisites for ROSA cluster deployments on K8s@@@To protect your Red Hat Openshift Service hosted on an AWS cluster, RSC requires specific configurations on the Kubernetes clusters...","kubernetes/k8s_protect_prereqs.html@@@Kubernetes workload protection requirements@@@Protecting Kubernetes workloads with RSC requires that the Kubernetes clusters and the Rubrik clusters meet specific prerequisites...","kubernetes/k8s_protection.html@@@Kubernetes protection requirements@@@You can use Rubrik Security Cloud to secure your on-premise or public cloud Kubernetes clusters by protecting either entire Kubernetes namespaces or specific subsets within a namespace using the protection set filtering feature...","kubernetes/k8s_protection_hierarchy.html@@@Kubernetes protection hierarchy@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based automatic protection for Kubernetes objects...","kubernetes/k8s_protection_images.html@@@Kubernetes protection images@@@RSC deploys container images on your Kubernetes cluster as part of Kubernetes protection...","kubernetes/k8s_protection_prereqs_onprem.html@@@K8S prerequisites and configurations for on-premises deployments@@@Protecting on-premises Kubernetes clusters with RSC requires specific prerequisites and configurations on the Kubernetes clusters...","kubernetes/k8s_protection_set_updates_rsc.html@@@Kubernetes protection set updates on RSC@@@After creating the Kubernetes protection set in RSC, these are the properties you can update...","kubernetes/k8s_protectionset.html@@@ProtectionSet CRD@@@The ProtectionSet custom resource definition provides information about an application in the Kubernetes cluster. Rubrik Kubernetes data protection can use a ProtectionSet custom resource to protect that application...","kubernetes/k8s_protectionset_example.html@@@ProtectionSet CRD examples@@@Examples of ProtectionSet custom resource definitions for an application in the Kubernetes cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_protectionset_spec_fields.html@@@ProtectionSet CRD spec and status fields@@@The ProtectionSet custom resource definition spec field defines an application on the Kubernetes cluster to protect, and the status field reports the status of that protection. You can also use the spec field to assign an SLA Domain that protects the application...","kubernetes/k8s_rba_affinity.html@@@Affinity for Rubrik Backup Agent pod placement@@@You can use affinity to pin Rubrik Backup Agent pods to the availability zone of the Persistent Volume you are backing up. This ensures that backup workloads run on nodes that can access the volumes they need...","kubernetes/k8s_rba_affinity_prerequisites.html@@@Prerequisites and limitations for RBA affinity@@@Prerequisites and limitations apply when enabling affinity for a Kubernetes cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_recoveryjob.html@@@RecoveryJob CRD@@@The RecoveryJob CRD defines a namespace-level recovery job in the Rubrik cluster, allowing application owners to use kubectl for snapshot recovery, with jobs retained as long as tracked in the cluster metadata...","kubernetes/k8s_recoveryjob_example.html@@@RecoveryJob example@@@Examples of the RecoveryJob custom resource definition for recovery jobs running in the Rubrik cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_recoveryjob_spec_and_status_fields.html@@@RecoveryJob CRD spec and status fields@@@The RecoveryJob custom resource definition spec and status fields provide information about a recovery job running on the Rubrik cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_refreshing_k8s_cluster.html@@@Refreshing a Kubernetes cluster@@@Start a refresh of a Kubernetes cluster to update the information for the protected namespaces on that cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_resource_requirements.html@@@Resource requirements for Kubernetes protection components@@@RSC deploys three components in the rubrik-kupr namespace on your Kubernetes cluster. Each component has default CPU, memory, and ephemeral storage requests and limits...","kubernetes/k8s_resource_transforms.html@@@Resource transforms for Kubernetes recovery@@@You can apply a resource transformation to modify a Kubernetes resource manifest during recovery without changing the original snapshot or source cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_restore_pvc_snapshots_k8s_protect.html@@@Restoring PersistentVolumeClaims snapshots using Kubernetes protection@@@Restore a PersistentVolumeClaims snapshot by recovering it to the same Kubernetes cluster or exporting it to another Kubernetes cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_restore_snpsht_resources_k8s_protect.html@@@Restoring snapshot resources using Kubernetes protection@@@Restore a snapshot that includes specific resources by recovering it to the same Kubernetes cluster or exporting it to another Kubernetes cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_restoring_protection_set_snapshots.html@@@Restoring Kubernetes resources from protection set snapshots@@@Restore Kubernetes resources from a protection set snapshot by recovering to the same Kubernetes cluster or exporting to another Kubernetes cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_rubrikcluster.html@@@RubrikCluster CRD@@@The RubrikCluster custom resource definition can be used to view information about the Rubrik clusters associated with a Kubernetes cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_rubrikcluster_example.html@@@RubrikCluster CRD example@@@Example of a RubrikCluster custom resource created from the RubrikCluster custom resource definition...","kubernetes/k8s_rubrikcluster_spec_and_status_fields.html@@@RubrikCluster CRD spec and status fields@@@The spec and status fields of the RubrikCluster custom resource definition provide information about the state of a Rubrik cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_sladomain.html@@@SLADomain CRD@@@The SLADomain custom resource definition provides information about the SLA Domains in a Rubrik cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_sladomain_example.html@@@SLADomain CRD example@@@Example of an SLADomain custom resource created from the SLADomain custom resource definition...","kubernetes/k8s_sladomain_spec_and_status_fields.html@@@SLADomain CRD spec and status fields@@@The spec and status fields of the SLADomain custom resource definition provide information about an SLA Domain...","kubernetes/k8s_snapshot.html@@@Snapshot CRD@@@The Snapshot custom resource definition provides details about protection set snapshots...","kubernetes/k8s_snapshot_example.html@@@Snapshot CRD example@@@Example of the custom resource created from the Snapshot custom resource definition for a snapshot...","kubernetes/k8s_snapshot_retention.html@@@Kubernetes snapshot retention@@@RSC allows changing the retention period of Kubernetes snapshots with the help of SLA Domains. Kubernetes snapshot retention works only with Rubrik clusters running Rubrik CDM version 7.0.2-p2 and later...","kubernetes/k8s_snapshot_spec_and_status_fields.html@@@Snapshot CRD spec and status fields@@@The spec and status fields of the Snapshot CRD provides details about protection set snapshots...","kubernetes/k8s_snapshotjob.html@@@SnapshotJob CRD@@@The SnapshotJob custom resource definition allows you to create and manage on-demand and policy-driven snapshot jobs...","kubernetes/k8s_snapshotjob_example.html@@@SnapshotJob CRD examples@@@Examples that demonstrate working with a Snapshot job custom resource...","kubernetes/k8s_snapshotjob_spec_and_status_fields.html@@@SnapshotJob CRD spec and status fields@@@The spec and status fields of the SnapshotJob custom resource definition allow you to create and manage on-demand and policy-driven snapshot jobs...","kubernetes/k8s_storage_class_mapping.html@@@StorageClass mapping for Kubernetes@@@StorageClass mapping provides the ability to select or define new storage tiers when restoring Kubernetes workloads to a different cluster or environment...","kubernetes/k8s_storage_class_prereq.html@@@StorageClass prerequisite@@@The storage class setup on the Kubernetes cluster must be able to take snapshots of the Persistent Volumes compliant with Container Storage Interface...","kubernetes/k8s_supported_distributions.html@@@Supported Kubernetes distributions@@@RSC provides data protection for containerized applications and business-critical data deployed on conforming Kubernetes distributions...","kubernetes/k8s_taking_a_volume_snapshot.html@@@Taking a volume snapshot@@@Verify that a VolumeSnapshot can be taken by manually creating a PersistentVolumeClaim and taking a snapshot...","kubernetes/k8s_taking_protection_set_ods.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of a Kubernetes protection set@@@Manually initiate an on-demand snapshot of a Kubernetes protection set...","kubernetes/k8s_transform_pset_recovery.html@@@Applying transforms in protection set recovery@@@Apply transforms to modify Kubernetes resource manifests when recovering a protection set, by configuring image substitutions, name remapping, or JSON patch operations in the recovery wizard...","kubernetes/k8s_transform_vm_recovery.html@@@Applying transforms in Kubernetes VM recovery@@@Apply transforms to modify Kubernetes resource manifests when recovering a Kubernetes virtual machine by configuring image substitutions, name remapping, or JSON patch operations...","kubernetes/k8s_unmount_behavior_openshift_vms.html@@@Unmount behavior for OpenShift virtual machines@@@Unmount a Live Mount to end the recovery session and clean up Rubrik-hosted resources. The final state of the virtual machine depends on its storage status and whether a storage migration occurred during the session...","kubernetes/k8s_unmounting_virtual_disks.html@@@Unmounting virtual disks from an OpenShift virtual machine@@@Unmount virtual disks that were mounted to an OpenShift virtual machine from RSC...","kubernetes/k8s_unmounting_vm.html@@@Unmounting an OpenShift virtual machine@@@Unmount a recovered OpenShift virtual machine from RSC...","kubernetes/k8s_updating_backup_network_config.html@@@Updating the dedicated backup network configuration@@@Turn on, change, or turn off the dedicated backup network to control how RSC routes backup traffic for an existing Kubernetes cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_validate_k8s_cluster_resources.html@@@Verifying the Kubernetes cluster resources@@@Verify that the resources available on a Kubernetes cluster are adequate for the RSC custom resources...","kubernetes/k8s_velero_exclude_label.html@@@Kubernetes resource exclusion with Velero labels@@@Exclude specific Kubernetes resources from RSC backup by applying a Velero label to those resources when protection set exclusion filters are not a viable option...","kubernetes/k8s_verifying_helm_chart.html@@@Verifying the Helm chart signature@@@Verify the signature of the Kubernetes protection Helm chart using the Cosign CLI to confirm the chart is authentic...","kubernetes/k8s_verifying_protection_images.html@@@Verifying Kubernetes protection image signatures@@@Verify the signatures of the Kubernetes protection container images using the Cosign CLI to confirm that the images are authentic...","kubernetes/k8s_viewing_agent_configuration.html@@@Viewing the Data Protection Agent configuration@@@View the Data Protection Agent configuration for a Kubernetes cluster by adding the configuration columns to the Kubernetes Protection page...","kubernetes/k8s_viewing_helm_values.html@@@Viewing Helm values@@@View the Helm values file for a Kubernetes cluster to verify the deployed configuration or regenerate the file before running helm upgrade...","kubernetes/k8s_viewing_manifest_file.html@@@Viewing the manifest file@@@For Kubernetes clusters that were added to RSC using an manifest file, you can view that file to determine whether it is producing the appropriate state for Kubernetes objects within the cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_vm_recovery_live_mount.html@@@OpenShift virtual machine recovery using Live Mount@@@RSC supports the Live Mount operation for OpenShift virtual machine snapshots from a Rubrik cluster onto a Kubernetes cluster...","kubernetes/k8s_volume_snapshot_class_prereq.html@@@VolumeSnapshotClass prerequisite@@@The driver associated with the VolumeSnapshotClass should match the CSI driver intended for use...","kubernetes/k8s_volume_snapshot_prereq.html@@@Volume snapshot prerequisite@@@Information about the prerequisites related to volume snapshot APIs and common controllers...","kubernetes/k8s_workload_protection.html@@@Kubernetes protection@@@RSC protects your on-premises or cloud-native Kubernetes clusters by backing up resources you add to protection sets...","kubernetes/k8s_workload_protection_policies.html@@@Kubernetes workload protection policies@@@In RSC, you can take both policy-based and on-demand snapshots of Kubernetes protection sets...","kubernetes/kubernetes_diagnostics.html@@@Kubernetes diagnostics@@@RSC Kubernetes diagnostics confirm connectivity and access permissions for a Kubernetes cluster connected to a Rubrik cluster. You can use Kubernetes diagnostics to verify and troubleshoot connectivity, backup, and recovery of a Kubernetes object or component...","kubernetes/kubernetes_labels.html@@@Kubernetes labels@@@RSC integrates with Kubernetes native labels to manage data protection, enabling you to use Kubernetes labels to identify and group resources, and then associate those labels with SLA Domains...","kubernetes/least_privilege_configuration_K8S.html@@@Least privilege configuration for Kubernetes@@@You can set up your Kubernetes kubeconfig with the least privileges so that only minimal RBAC permissions are assigned to users and service accounts...","kubernetes/placing_k8s_snapshots_legal_hold.html@@@Placing Kubernetes snapshots on Legal Hold@@@You can place a Legal Hold on a Kubernetes snapshot to prevent the Rubrik cluster from expiring and removing the snapshot at the end of the assigned retention period...","kubernetes/post_onboarding_perms_updates.html@@@Post-onboarding permissions updates@@@Rubrik recommends maintaining the most current privileges in your Kubernetes cluster. The method for updating privileges depends on which onboarding method you used...","kubernetes/post_onboarding_perms_updates_2.html@@@Post-onboarding permissions updates@@@Rubrik recommends maintaining the most current privileges in your Kubernetes cluster. The method for updating privileges depends on which onboarding method you used...","kubernetes/recovering_files_using_kubernetes_labels.html@@@Recovering files using Kubernetes labels@@@Download files or folders from a snapshot of a Kubernetes virtual machine or namespace that includes labels. You can then manually recover the downloaded files and folders to the source virtual machine, namespace, or another location...","kubernetes/regenerating_manifest_file.html@@@Regenerating the manifest file@@@Regenerate the manifest file to update the Kubernetes cluster configuration...","kubernetes/rubrik_cluster_access_to_kubernetes_data.html@@@Rubrik cluster access to Kubernetes data@@@Rubrik clusters access Kubernetes data through a connection with the Kubernetes API...","kubernetes/supported_mirrored_registry_methods.html@@@Supported mirrored registry methods@@@RSC supports three mirrored registry methods...","kubernetes/using_hook_crd_run_commands.html@@@Definitions for using the Hook CRD to run commands@@@The Hook CRD can define a single or multiple commands to run in a pod before and after a volume backup...","kubernetes/using_kubernetes_diagnostics_validation.html@@@Using Kubernetes diagnostics for validation@@@For a Kubernetes account assigned to a Rubrik cluster, use Kubernetes diagnostics to validate connectivity and to verify access permissions...","kubernetes/viewing_k8s_labels_rsc.html@@@Viewing Kubernetes labels on RSC@@@View the Kubernetes labels on RSC...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_adding_sharepoint_groups.html@@@Adding SharePoint groups for Microsoft 365 Backup Storage@@@Add a SharePoint group for Microsoft 365 Backup Storage to RSC...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_adding_subscriptions.html@@@Adding Microsoft 365 Backup Storage subscriptions@@@Add a Microsoft 365 subscription to back up and restore data associated with Microsoft 365 applications such as SharePoint sites, OneDrive user accounts, and Exchange mailboxes using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_creating_rbac_role.html@@@Creating an RBAC role for Microsoft 365 Backup Storage@@@Create a role with Role-based Access Control privileges for protecting objects using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage. These privileges provide finer granularity for determining what permissions the administrator has for performing actions and on which objects...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_dashboard.html@@@Microsoft 365 Backup Storage dashboard@@@The Microsoft 365 Backup Storage dashboard provides details about the status, protection policy, and number of protected objects...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_dashboard_details.html@@@Microsoft 365 Backup Storage dashboard details@@@Information about the tabs available on the dashboards specific to Microsoft 365 applications protected using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_data_recovery.html@@@Data Recovery using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage@@@Using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage, you can recover data associated with Microsoft 365 applications, such as SharePoint sites, OneDrive user accounts, and Exchange mailboxes...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_deployment_reqs.html@@@Microsoft 365 Backup Storage deployment requirements@@@Information about requirements for the Rubrik-hosted deployment mode for Microsoft 365 Backup Storage...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_editing_group_details.html@@@Editing Microsoft 365 Backup Storage group details@@@Edit an Entra ID or SharePoint group details to update the protection hierarchy of RSC...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_get_start_protecting_apps.html@@@Get started with protecting M365 applications@@@You can manage protection and recover data associated with Microsoft 365 applications protected using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage by completing a series of tasks...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_groups.html@@@Microsoft 365 Backup Storage groups@@@You can use groups in RSC to assign data protection policies uniformly to Microsoft 365 Backup Storage objects, such as user Exchange mailboxes, OneDrive accounts, and SharePoint sites...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_managing_obj_protection.html@@@Managing protection for M365 objects@@@Manage protection for the objects associated with Microsoft 365 applications such as SharePoint sites, OneDrive user accounts, and Exchange mailboxes using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage. You can protect the objects associated with Microsoft 365 applications by assigning a data protection policy predefined by Microsoft and specified in the SLA Domain...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_managing_protection_apps.html@@@Managing protection for M365 applications@@@Manage protection for Microsoft 365 applications such as SharePoint sites, OneDrive user accounts, and Exchange mailboxes using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage. You can protect Microsoft 365 applications by assigning a data protection policy predefined by Microsoft and specified in the SLA Domain...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_managing_protection_grps.html@@@Managing protection for Microsoft 365 Backup Storage groups@@@Manage the protection of Microsoft 365 Backup Storage workloads by assigning a data protection policy to an Entra ID or SharePoint group...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_permissions.html@@@Microsoft 365 Backup Storage permissions@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to protect your Microsoft 365 applications using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_protection.html@@@Microsoft 365 Backup Storage protection@@@You can use the SLA Domain predefined by Microsoft to apply the data protection and management policies to protect Microsoft 365 applications such as SharePoint sites, OneDrive user accounts, and Exchange mailboxes using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_protection_hierarchy.html@@@Protection hierarchy for M365 applications and objects@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based automatic protection to Microsoft 365 applications and its objects using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_rbac.html@@@RBAC for Microsoft 365 Backup Storage in RSC@@@Role-Based Access Control and implicit permissions in RSC streamline the management and security of Microsoft 365 Backup Storage, enhancing efficient navigation and access control for essential data...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_removing_groups.html@@@Removing groups from Microsoft 365 Backup Storage protection@@@Remove an Entra ID or a SharePoint group associated with Microsoft 365 Backup Storage from the protection hierarchy from RSC...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_removing_subscriptions.html@@@Removing Microsoft 365 Backup Storage subscriptions@@@Remove a Microsoft 365 subscription associated with Microsoft 365 applications using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage when no longer needed...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_restoring_exchange.html@@@Restoring M365 Exchange using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage@@@Restore a Microsoft 365 Exchange mailbox user account to mitigate data loss events such as accidental deletion, ransomware attacks, or other unforeseen incidents using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_restoring_onedrive.html@@@Restoring M365 OneDrive user accounts using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage@@@Restore Microsoft 365 OneDrive user accounts to mitigate data loss events, such as accidental deletion, ransomware attacks, or other unforeseen incidents using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage. You can also restore data using express restore points that are either the most recent or closest to a specific date or time...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_restoring_sharepoint.html@@@Restoring M365 SharePoint sites using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage@@@Restore a Microsoft 365 SharePoint site to mitigate data loss events such as accidental deletion, ransomware attacks, or other unforeseen incidents using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage. You can also restore data using express restore points that are either the most recent or closest to a specific date or time...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_searching_obj.html@@@Searching objects across specific M365 applications dashboard@@@When you want to quickly search for a specific Microsoft 365 application such as SharePoint sites, OneDrive user accounts, or Exchange mailboxes, search across the list...","m365_backup_storage/m365_b_s_viewing_apps_dashboard.html@@@Viewing the Microsoft 365 applications dashboard@@@View the dashboards for Microsoft 365 applications (SharePoint sites, OneDrive user accounts, and Exchange mailboxes) protected using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage for information about the connection status, protection policy, total objects, and protected objects...","m365_backup_storage/m365_backup_storage.html@@@Microsoft 365 Backup Storage@@@With the Microsoft 365 Backup Storage feature, you can back up Microsoft 365 applications such as SharePoint sites, OneDrive user accounts, and Exchange mailboxes. You can also restore large volumes of data during ransomware attacks, accidental deletion, or malicious data deletion and overwrite events...","m365_backup_storage/m365_bs_adding_entra_id_groups.html@@@Adding Entra ID groups for Microsoft 365 Backup Storage@@@Add an Entra ID group for Microsoft 365 Backup Storage to RSC...","m365_backup_storage/m365_bs_configuration_groups.html@@@Configuration of Microsoft 365 Backup Storage groups@@@To configure Microsoft 365 Backup Storage groups, you must add the Entra ID and SharePoint groups for Microsoft 365 Backup Storage to RSC. After adding the groups, you need to assign the SLA Domains to the groups to apply the data protection policies...","m365_backup_storage/m365_bs_groups_maintenance.html@@@Maintenance of Microsoft 365 Backup Storage groups@@@Maintaining Entra ID and SharePoint groups for Microsoft 365 Backup Storage involves regularly reviewing and updating the group details, and removing obsolete group configurations to ensure optimal performance and resource management...","m365_backup_storage/mass_recovery_m365_b_s.html@@@Microsoft 365 Backup Storage mass recovery events@@@Information about the progress and results of mass recovery operations for your Microsoft 365 Backup Storage data. You can view these details on the mass recovery events page...","m365_backup_storage/mr_m365_b_s_groups.html@@@Mass recovery of Microsoft 365 Backup Storage groups@@@Using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage, you can recover one or more groups associated with Microsoft 365 applications such as SharePoint sites, OneDrive user accounts, or Exchange mailboxes...","m365_backup_storage/performing_mr_m365_b_s_exchange_data.html@@@Performing mass recovery of Microsoft 365 Backup Storage Exchange data@@@Performing mass recovery of the Microsoft 365 Backup Storage Exchange data for one or more Entra ID groups to mitigate data loss events such as accidental deletion, ransomware attacks, or other unforeseen incidents using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage...","m365_backup_storage/performing_mr_m365_b_s_onedrive_data.html@@@Performing mass recovery of Microsoft 365 Backup Storage OneDrive data@@@Perform mass recovery of Microsoft 365 OneDrive data for one or more Entra ID groups to mitigate data loss events such as accidental deletion, ransomware attacks, or other unforeseen incidents using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage...","m365_backup_storage/performing_mr_m365_b_s_sharepoint_data.html@@@Performing mass recovery of Microsoft 365 Backup Storage SharePoint data@@@Perform mass recovery of sites for one or more Microsoft 365 Backup Storage SharePoint groups to mitigate data loss events such as accidental deletion, ransomware attacks, or other unforeseen incidents using Microsoft 365 Backup Storage. You can also restore data using express restore points that are either the most recent or closest to a specific date or time...","managedvolumes/mv_assigning_sla_domain.html@@@Assigning SLA Domains to Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes@@@Assign an SLA Domain to the Managed Volume or SLA Managed Volume snapshots to provide policy-based management...","managedvolumes/mv_backup_script_settings.html@@@Backup script settings for SLA Managed Volumes@@@Information about backup script settings for SLA Managed Volumes creation, including details on host script execution and pre-backup and post-backup commands...","managedvolumes/mv_changing_retention_snapshot.html@@@Changing Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes snapshot retention policy@@@Change the retention policy for specified snapshots of a Managed Volume or SLA Managed Volume workload type...","managedvolumes/mv_channel_guidelines.html@@@Guidelines for Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes channel creation@@@Guidelines for creating Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes channels...","managedvolumes/mv_common_terms.html@@@Common Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes protection terms@@@Definitions of common terms used when protecting data with Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes in RSC...","managedvolumes/mv_configure.html@@@Configure Managed Volumes@@@Information about the configuration settings used when creating a Managed Volume...","managedvolumes/mv_configure_sla_mv.html@@@Configure SLA Managed Volumes@@@Information about the configuration settings used when creating an SLA Managed Volume...","managedvolumes/mv_creating_livemount_mv_snapshot.html@@@Creating a Live Mount of a Managed Volume snapshot@@@A Live Mount of a Managed Volume snapshot enables access to the data in the snapshot...","managedvolumes/mv_creating_livemount_slamv_snapshot.html@@@Creating a Live Mount of an SLA Managed Volume snapshot@@@A Live Mount of an SLA Managed Volume snapshot enables access to the data in the snapshot...","managedvolumes/mv_creating_mv.html@@@Creating a Managed Volume@@@Create a Managed Volume for each application that Rubrik protects...","managedvolumes/mv_creating_sla_mv.html@@@Creating an SLA Managed Volume@@@Create an SLA Managed Volume on a Rubrik cluster to schedule and initiate backups using an SLA Domain...","managedvolumes/mv_custom_sla_domains_sla_managed_volumes.html@@@Custom SLA Domains for SLA Managed Volumes@@@SLA Domains for SLA Managed Volumes are customized based on backup requirements...","managedvolumes/mv_deleting_managed_volume_sla_managed_volume.html@@@Deleting Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volume@@@You can delete a Managed Volume or an SLA Managed Volume from RSC...","managedvolumes/mv_deleting_managed_volumes_snapshots.html@@@Deleting a Managed Volume and SLA Managed Volume snapshot@@@Delete snapshots for a Managed Volume or an SLA Managed Volume...","managedvolumes/mv_editing_mv_rsc.html@@@Editing a Managed Volume@@@You can modify the volume name, client name, and provisioned size of a Managed Volume...","managedvolumes/mv_editing_sla_mv.html@@@Editing an SLA Managed Volume@@@To modify the volume name, provisioned size, and client name of an SLA Managed Volume, edit the associated values on the SLA Managed Volumes page...","managedvolumes/mv_floating_ip_addresses.html@@@Floating IP addresses for Managed Volumes@@@You must set up floating IP addresses before creating any Managed Volume...","managedvolumes/mv_high_level_architecture.html@@@Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes protection architecture@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects host data through Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes...","managedvolumes/mv_high_level_implementation.html@@@Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes protection implementation workflow@@@A high-level workflow that outlines the phases for implementing Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes protection in RSC...","managedvolumes/mv_limitations.html@@@Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes protection limitations@@@The following limitations apply to Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes protection with RSC...","managedvolumes/mv_live_mount_mv_snapshots.html@@@Live Mount for Managed Volumes or SLA Managed Volumes@@@A Live Mount exposes a snapshot of a Managed Volume or an SLA Managed Volume as a new NFS or SMB mount point on the Rubrik cluster, which hosts can mount in read-only or read-write mode...","managedvolumes/mv_manage_snapshots.html@@@Manage Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes snapshots@@@You can monitor Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes, take on-demand snapshots, place legal holds, change retention policies, and delete snapshots when they are no longer needed...","managedvolumes/mv_managed_volume_object_details.html@@@Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes object details@@@The Managed Volumes object details page provides an Overview page, a Snapshots page, and an Events page for each Managed Volume and SLA Managed Volume...","managedvolumes/mv_managed_volume_snapshot_management.html@@@Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes snapshot management@@@The SLA Domain assigned to a Managed Volume or SLA Managed Volume controls snapshot frequency, retention, archiving, and replication...","managedvolumes/mv_managed_volumes_sla_managed_volumes.html@@@Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes@@@RSC protects host application data using Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes, providing network-attached backup targets on a Rubrik cluster with SLA Domain-driven snapshot management...","managedvolumes/mv_monitoring_events.html@@@Monitoring Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes events@@@You can monitor Managed Volumes or SLA Managed Volumes for in-progress, failed, canceled, completed, and scheduled tasks from the Events page...","managedvolumes/mv_obj_level_pause_resume.html@@@Object-level pause and resume for Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes@@@You can temporarily pause and resume protection for individual Managed Volumes or SLA Managed Volumes without affecting the protection of other objects managed by the same SLA Domain...","managedvolumes/mv_overview_details_actions.html@@@Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes overview details and actions@@@The Overview page presents details for each Managed Volume or SLA Managed Volume and lists the available actions for managing protection and snapshots...","managedvolumes/mv_placing_snapshot_legalhold.html@@@Placing a legal hold on a Managed Volume or an SLA Managed Volume snapshot@@@Place a legal hold on a Managed Volume or SLA Managed Volumes snapshot to prevent the Rubrik cluster from expiring and removing the snapshot at the end of the assigned retention period...","managedvolumes/mv_plan_protection.html@@@Plan your Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes protection@@@Before setting up Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes in RSC, review the host setup requirements, channel creation guidelines, network configuration, and protection limitations...","managedvolumes/mv_prohibited_mount_points_script_dirs_sla_mv.html@@@Prohibited mount points and script directories for SLA Managed Volumes@@@For SLA Managed Volumes, RSC prevents the use of some paths as mount points and host-side script locations...","managedvolumes/mv_protection_key_features.html@@@Key features for Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes protection@@@RSC provides unified data management, automated global data protection, backup and recovery options, and advanced security features to protect critical data for Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes...","managedvolumes/mv_quick_links.html@@@Quick links for Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes@@@Immediate access to important tasks and information, enabling quick setup, daily operations, and critical recovery...","managedvolumes/mv_recover.html@@@Recover Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes@@@You can recover files and folders from a Managed Volume and an SLA Managed Volume snapshot, or you can create a Live Mount of a Managed Volume or SLA Managed Volume snapshot for in-place recovery...","managedvolumes/mv_recovering_files_folders.html@@@Recovering files and folders from a snapshot@@@Use snapshots to search for and recover specific files from Managed Volumes or SLA Managed Volumes...","managedvolumes/mv_reset_reasons.html@@@Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes reset reasons@@@When a Managed Volume or SLA Managed Volume encounters a condition that requires intervention, RSC displays the reset reason on the Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes pages so you can identify the cause and take the appropriate action...","managedvolumes/mv_resizing_managed_volume_sla_managed_volume.html@@@Resizing Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes@@@Resize a Managed Volume or an SLA Managed Volume to increase its size...","managedvolumes/mv_scripted_backups_snapshots_assigned_sla_domain.html@@@Scripted backups for snapshots with assigned SLA Domains@@@Client-side scripted backups interact with the assigned SLA Domain to control how frequently the Rubrik cluster creates and retains snapshots for a Managed Volume...","managedvolumes/mv_set_up_managed_volumes.html@@@Set up your Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes@@@You can set up floating IP addresses on the Rubrik cluster and configure Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes for hosts to write backup data into the volumes...","managedvolumes/mv_set_up_protection.html@@@Set up your Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes protection@@@You can configure backup script settings for SLA Managed Volumes, define custom SLA Domains, and assign SLA Domains to Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes to protect the backup data that hosts write into them...","managedvolumes/mv_setting_up_floating_ip_addresses.html@@@Setting up floating IP addresses for Managed Volumes@@@Set up floating IP addresses to ensure that all Managed Volumes are available if a Rubrik node fails...","managedvolumes/mv_setup_requirements_slamv.html@@@Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes setup requirements@@@Establishing a Managed Volume or an SLA Managed Volume protected by an SLA Domain requires a specific setup. After an administrator establishes the connection, the Managed Volume or SLA Managed Volume is treated as any other protected data source...","managedvolumes/mv_slamv_application_tags.html@@@Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes application tags@@@Application tags specify the type of application data that is stored on a Managed Volume or an SLA Managed Volume...","managedvolumes/mv_snapshots_details_actions.html@@@Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes snapshots details and actions@@@The Snapshots page presents details for each Managed Volume and SLA Managed Volume snapshot and lists actions to filter, manage, and recover from snapshots...","managedvolumes/mv_taking_managed_volume_snapshot.html@@@Taking a Managed Volume snapshot@@@Take a snapshot of a Managed Volume for a copy of data at a particular point in time...","managedvolumes/mv_taking_ondemand_slamv_snapshot.html@@@Taking an on-demand SLA Managed Volume snapshot@@@Manually initiate an on-demand snapshot of an SLA Managed Volume...","managedvolumes/mv_unmounting_mv_live_mount.html@@@Unmounting a Managed Volume or an SLA Managed Volume Live Mount@@@After creating a Live Mount, unmount the Live Mount of a Managed Volume or an SLA Managed Volume to remove the metadata associated with the selected Managed Volume or SLA Managed Volume...","managedvolumes/mv_versus_sla_managed_volumes.html@@@Managed Volumes versus SLA Managed Volumes@@@You must review the differences between Managed Volumes and SLA Managed Volumes to determine which option best suits your requirement...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_adding_subs_protection.html@@@Adding a Dynamics 365 subscription for protection@@@Add a Microsoft Dynamics 365 subscription to back up the data in your environment...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_admin_permissions.html@@@Dynamics 365 administrator permissions@@@Information about Role-based Access Control permissions required for administrators to perform actions on Microsoft Dynamics 365 workload...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_analyzing_data_changes.html@@@Analyzing Dynamics 365 data changes@@@Analyze changes in Microsoft Dynamics 365 data over a period and make informed decisions about restoring the data...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_assigning_protection_subs.html@@@Assigning protection to Dynamics 365 subscriptions@@@Protect the tables and global metadata in the Microsoft Dynamics 365 subscription by assigning a data protection policy to the subscription...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_backup_recovery.html@@@Dynamics 365 backup and recovery@@@After RSC takes snapshots of your Microsoft Dynamics 365 workloads, you can recover the required rows or metadata whenever required...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_cloning_sla_domain.html@@@Cloning a Dynamics 365 SLA Domain@@@You can clone an existing, properly configured SLA Domain to save time. This approach lets you avoid creating and configuring an SLA Domain from the start, allowing you to make any necessary adjustments to the cloned domain instead...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_comm_rsc_dynamics_subs.html@@@Communication between RSC and Dynamics 365 subscription@@@A high-level architecture overview of how RSC uses Microsoft Entra ID and OAuth 2.0 authorization flows to manage Microsoft Dynamics 365 workloads securely...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_common_terms_protection.html@@@Common terms for Dynamics 365 protection@@@It is important to understand some common terms when protecting Microsoft Dynamics 365 workloads with RSC...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_creating_custom_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for Dynamics 365@@@Create a role with Role-based Access Control privileges for protecting rows and metadata associated with Microsoft Dynamics 365. These privileges provide finer granularity for determining the permissions the administrator has for performing actions and on which objects...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_creating_report_subs.html@@@Creating a report for Dynamics 365 subscription@@@Create reports for Dynamics 365 subscription to view information such as compliance status and protection status, using the available templates. You can use the information generated in the reports to perform audits and data management planning...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_dashboard_details.html@@@Dynamics 365 dashboard details@@@RSC monitors, analyses, and restores Dynamics 365 data and shows the important details, such as backup jobs, status, changed rows, and backup summary...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_downloading_report_subs.html@@@Downloading a report for Dynamics 365 subscription@@@Download reports for Dynamics 365 subscription from RSC for monitoring or auditing...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_event_log_details.html@@@Event log details@@@The Events page displays the events occurring in all Dynamics 365 subscriptions, shown in the local time zone...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_key_features_protection.html@@@Key features for Dynamics 365 protection@@@RSC provides unified data management, automated global data protection, various recovery options for Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Relationship Management workloads, and advanced security features to protect your workloads...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_microsoft_dataverse.html@@@Dynamics 365 and Microsoft Dataverse@@@Microsoft Dataverse is a data storage platform that stores the data associated with the Microsoft Dynamics 365 application...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_monitoring_subs_dashboard.html@@@Monitoring Dynamics 365 subscription dashboard@@@View details about a Dynamics 365 subscription to monitor data changes in backup jobs, status, backup summary, and changed rows...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_planning_protection.html@@@Planning for Dynamics 365 protection@@@Before setting up a Microsoft Dynamics 365 subscription in RSC, you need to plan user and access management for designated RSC users. This planning also involves reviewing the permissions that RSC requires in your Microsoft Dynamics 365 environment to protect your Microsoft Dynamics 365 workloads...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_protection_config.html@@@Configuration of Dynamics 365 protection@@@To ensure the resilience and availability of your Microsoft Dynamics 365 subscription, it is important to implement a data protection strategy using SLA Domains. Key actions include creating and assigning SLA Domains to Microsoft Dynamics 365 subscriptions, deleting unused SLA Domains, and cloning properly configured SLA Domains for efficiency...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_protection_setup.html@@@Dynamics 365 workload protection setup@@@You can set up SLA Domains to apply data protection policies, ensuring automatic protection of Microsoft Dynamics 365 workloads...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_recommendations_add_subs.html@@@Recommendations for adding Dynamics 365 subscription@@@Rubrik recommends specific actions and best practices for adding a Microsoft Dynamics 365 subscription to RSC...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_recovery_options.html@@@Dynamics 365 recovery options@@@Information about recovery options for Microsoft Dynamics 365 workloads...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_regions.html@@@Supported regions for Dynamics 365 data protection@@@RSC supports Microsoft Dynamics 365 protection in several regions. You choose the region when you set up the Microsoft Dynamics 365 subscription in RSC...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_reporting.html@@@Dynamics 365 reporting@@@You can create and download reports for Dynamics 365 data protection to view status information about a subscription...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_req_perms_protection.html@@@Required permissions for Dynamics 365 protection@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to protect Microsoft Dynamics 365 workloads...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_reqs_protection.html@@@Requirements for Dynamics 365 protection@@@It is important to meet specific requirements to configure Microsoft Dynamics 365 protection by RSC...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_restoring_data.html@@@Restoring Dynamics 365 data@@@Restore Dynamics 365 data from a snapshot to a Microsoft Dynamics 365 source environment...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_restoring_global_metadata.html@@@Restoring Dynamics 365 global metadata@@@Restore Microsoft Dynamics 365 global metadata from a snapshot to a Microsoft Dynamics 365 source environment...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_restoring_rows.html@@@Restoring Dynamics 365 rows@@@Restore Microsoft Dynamics 365 rows from a snapshot to a source Microsoft Dynamics 365 environment...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_restoring_table_metadata.html@@@Restoring Dynamics 365 table metadata@@@Restore Microsoft Dynamics 365 table metadata from a snapshot to a Microsoft Dynamics 365 source environment...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_retention_lock.html@@@Retention Lock for Dynamics 365@@@A retention lock on an RSC SLA Domain is a security feature that prevents premature deletion of Microsoft Dynamics 365 snapshots...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_rsc_user_management.html@@@RSC user management for Dynamics 365@@@Designating specific users with appropriate privileges and roles in RSC enhances security for managing Microsoft Dynamics 365 subscriptions...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_setup.html@@@Dynamics 365 setup@@@You can set up a Microsoft Dynamics 365 subscription in RSC and start protecting your Microsoft Dynamics 365 environments...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_table_analysis.html@@@Dynamics 365 table analysis@@@RSC generates comprehensive insights about the changes in Microsoft Dynamics 365 data, making it easier to analyze and restore data securely...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_taking_ods.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Dynamics 365 data@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of Microsoft Dynamics 365 data or metadata...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_viewing_events.html@@@Viewing events for Dynamics 365@@@View the Events page from the Dashboard to see the events for Dynamics 365 subscription...","microsoft_dynamics_365/d365_workload_recovery.html@@@Dynamics 365 workload recovery@@@You can recover the rows or metadata of Microsoft Dynamics 365 workloads using the various recovery options that RSC provides...","microsoft_dynamics_365/microsoft_dynamics_365.html@@@Microsoft Dynamics 365@@@RSC protects the tables and metadata in your Microsoft Dynamics 365 subscription...","mongodb/adding_mdb_host_pbr_ops_mgr.html@@@Adding a MongoDB host for physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager@@@Add a MongoDB host for physical backup and recovery of MongoDB sources using Ops Manager by specifying the required configuration details to establish a connection to the port and enable data storage and retrieval on the MongoDB server...","mongodb/adding_mdb_src_pbr_ops_mgr.html@@@Adding a MongoDB source for physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager@@@Add a MongoDB source cluster for physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager by providing the configuration details and credentials to establish a connection with the Rubrik cluster...","mongodb/adding_mongodb_host.html@@@Adding a MongoDB host for logical backup and recovery@@@To establish a connection to the port and enable data storage and retrieval on the MongoDB server, add a host for MongoDB by specifying the required configuration details...","mongodb/adding_mongodb_source_cluster.html@@@Adding a MongoDB source cluster for logical backup and recovery@@@To establish a connection with the Rubrik cluster, add a MongoDB source cluster by providing the configuration details and credentials...","mongodb/app_config_ops_manager.html@@@Application configuration for Ops Manager@@@Application configuration for physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager provides guidelines for configuring Ops Manager to support third-party backups. To ensure secure and efficient backup management within Ops Manager, you must configure it with TLS encryption, a Backup Admin API key, and specific key-value pairs...","mongodb/assigning_sla_mongodb_admin_db.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to the MongoDB Admin DB object@@@Assign an SLA Domain to the Admin DB object of a MongoDB source to protect the role and user configuration of the source...","mongodb/changing_retention_policy_mdb_snapshots.html@@@Changing the retention policy of MongoDB snapshots@@@Change the retention period of MongoDB snapshots to optimize their storage and data accessibility...","mongodb/creating_api_key_protect_mdb_src_ops_mgr.html@@@Creating API key to protect MongoDB sources using Ops Manager@@@Create an API key using Ops Manager to help you add your MongoDB sources to RSC...","mongodb/deleting_mongodb_snapshots.html@@@Deleting MongoDB snapshots@@@Delete MongoDB snapshots that are no longer required for data protection. RSC supports the deletion of MongoDB snapshots from Rubrik CDM version 9.5.0 and later...","mongodb/editable_settings_mdb_src_ops_mgr.html@@@Editable settings for MongoDB sources managed by Ops Manager@@@Information about the settings that you can edit for MongoDB source clusters with physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager integration method...","mongodb/editing_mdb_src_pbr_ops_mgr.html@@@Editing a MongoDB source for physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager@@@Edit the Ops Manager details such as the CA certificate and API keys for a MongoDB source cluster...","mongodb/importing_ca_cert_ops_mgr.html@@@Importing CA certificates for Ops Manager@@@Import a CA certificate for Ops Manager to support physical backup and recovery of MongoDB sources using Ops Manager...","mongodb/limitations_mdb_ops_mgr.html@@@Limitations of MongoDB sources managed by Ops Manager@@@RSC mandates specific limitations on MongoDB source clusters with physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager integration method...","mongodb/logical_backup_recv_mdb_protection.html@@@Key features for protecting MongoDB logical backup and recovery@@@RSC provides unified data management, automated global data protection, backup and recovery options, and advanced security features to protect your MongoDB logical backup and recovery sources...","mongodb/managing_protection_mdb_src_ops_mgr.html@@@Assigning protection for MongoDB@@@Assign an SLA Domain to your MongoDB objects to optimize data management and enhance data protection...","mongodb/mdb_SLA_assignment_hierarchy.html@@@SLA Domain assignment hierarchy for MongoDB@@@Information about the protection hierarchy for MongoDB workloads, including the structured framework of RSC. This framework covers sources, databases, and collections to ensure optimal data security and organization...","mongodb/mdb_access_reports.html@@@Access MongoDB reports@@@Use RSC reports to monitor the protection, compliance, capacity, and task activity of your MongoDB workloads...","mongodb/mdb_archiving_snapshots.html@@@Archiving for MongoDB snapshots@@@You can include an archival policy in an SLA Domain to archive MongoDB snapshots to an archival location for long-term retention...","mongodb/mdb_best_practices_sla_assign.html@@@Best practices for MongoDB SLA Domain assignment@@@Rubrik recommends the following best practices when you assign SLA Domains to your MongoDB sources, databases, and collections...","mongodb/mdb_common_protection_terms.html@@@Common protection terms for MongoDB@@@It is important to understand some common terms when protecting MongoDB workloads with RSC...","mongodb/mdb_communication_rsc.html@@@Communication between RSC and MongoDB workload@@@An overview of how RSC communicates with your MongoDB workload during backup and recovery operations...","mongodb/mdb_configure_protection.html@@@Configure MongoDB protection@@@Configure protection for your MongoDB workloads by creating SLA Domains, assigning protection, and managing snapshots...","mongodb/mdb_creating_custom_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for MongoDB@@@Create a role with RBAC privileges for managing MongoDB workloads. These privileges provide granularity for determining which permissions an RSC user has for performing specific actions on specific objects...","mongodb/mdb_creating_custom_role_2.html@@@Creating a custom role for MongoDB@@@Create a role with RBAC privileges for managing MongoDB workloads. These privileges provide granularity for determining which permissions an RSC user has for performing specific actions on specific objects...","mongodb/mdb_creating_custom_sla.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain for MongoDB@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to define the backup frequency, retention, and archival policies for your MongoDB workloads...","mongodb/mdb_creating_reports.html@@@Creating reports for MongoDB@@@Create a report in RSC to summarize the protection, compliance, capacity, or task details for your MongoDB objects...","mongodb/mdb_cross_version_compatibility.html@@@MongoDB cross-version compatibility@@@Recovery behavior between MongoDB versions varies based on whether the version difference is at the patch, minor, or major level...","mongodb/mdb_database_details.html@@@MongoDB database details@@@The MongoDB database details page provides an overview of the selected MongoDB database and available object information...","mongodb/mdb_downloading_archived_snapshots.html@@@Downloading archived MongoDB snapshots@@@Download a MongoDB snapshot from an archival location to a Rubrik cluster when the snapshot is not available in local storage...","mongodb/mdb_downloading_replicated_snapshots.html@@@Downloading replicated MongoDB snapshots@@@Download replicated snapshots of a MongoDB object to local storage on the source cluster for recovery...","mongodb/mdb_evaluate_protection_options.html@@@Evaluate MongoDB protection options@@@Before you configure protection, evaluate the retention and archival options available for your MongoDB workloads...","mongodb/mdb_event_log_details.html@@@Event log details for MongoDB@@@The Event Logs page displays the events that occur for all MongoDB objects in your local time zone...","mongodb/mdb_high_level_architecture_protection.html@@@High-level architecture for MongoDB protection@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects your MongoDB workloads using the logical backup and recovery method and the physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager method...","mongodb/mdb_high_level_implementation_workflow.html@@@High-level implementation workflow for MongoDB@@@The MongoDB protection implementation workflow involves a structured approach to secure data management, starting with planning and preparation, followed by source setup, protection configuration, ongoing management, recovery, and reporting...","mongodb/mdb_large_scale_sharded_support.html@@@Large-scale sharded MongoDB deployment support@@@RSC supports data protection for large-scale MongoDB deployments with sharded clusters of up to 30 shards in Rubrik CDM 9.6.0 and later...","mongodb/mdb_logic_br_editing_source.html@@@Editing a MongoDB source for logical backup and recovery@@@Edit a MongoDB source cluster to update its settings, such as the ignore nodes, SSL authentication, and driver authentication...","mongodb/mdb_logic_br_plan_protection.html@@@Plan your MongoDB logical backup and recovery protection@@@Before you set up MongoDB logical backup and recovery, plan user and access management for your RSC users, and review the permissions, deployment scale thresholds, and limitations that apply to your MongoDB environment...","mongodb/mdb_logic_br_req_rsc_perms.html@@@Required RSC permissions for MongoDB logical backup and recovery@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires in your MongoDB environment to protect your logical backup and recovery sources...","mongodb/mdb_logic_br_set_up_source.html@@@Set up MongoDB source for logical backup and recovery@@@Set up a MongoDB source for logical backup and recovery by meeting the prerequisites, adding the MongoDB hosts, and adding the MongoDB source to RSC...","mongodb/mdb_logic_br_user_management.html@@@RSC user management for MongoDB logical backup and recovery@@@Designating specific users with appropriate privileges and roles in RSC enhances security for protecting your MongoDB logical backup and recovery sources...","mongodb/mdb_manage_objects.html@@@Manage MongoDB objects@@@After you complete the protection setup for your MongoDB sources, RSC takes automated snapshots of your MongoDB objects based on the configured policies in SLA Domains. You can also manage your sources, databases, and collections for better resource management...","mongodb/mdb_multiple_archival_locations.html@@@Multiple archival locations for MongoDB@@@RSC supports multiple archival locations for MongoDB objects, providing granular control over data archiving with up to two distinct archiving policies...","mongodb/mdb_physic_br_plan_protection.html@@@Plan your MongoDB physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager protection@@@Before you set up MongoDB physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager, plan user and access management for the designated RSC users, and review the permissions and limitations that apply to your MongoDB environment...","mongodb/mdb_physic_br_req_rsc_perms.html@@@Required RSC permissions for MongoDB physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to protect your MongoDB sources through the Ops Manager integration...","mongodb/mdb_physic_br_set_up_source.html@@@Set up MongoDB source for physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager@@@Set up a MongoDB source for physical backup and recovery by meeting the prerequisites, configuring Ops Manager access, and adding the MongoDB hosts and source to RSC...","mongodb/mdb_physic_br_user_management.html@@@RSC user management for MongoDB physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager@@@Designating specific users with appropriate privileges and roles in RSC enhances security for protecting your MongoDB sources managed by Ops Manager...","mongodb/mdb_primary_snapshot_retention.html@@@Primary snapshot retention for MongoDB@@@Primary snapshot retention for MongoDB objects provides data protection and recoverability by making it possible to set various retention policies. These policies include hourly, daily, monthly, and yearly retention of snapshots to meet compliance, business continuity, and disaster recovery requirements...","mongodb/mdb_protection_overview.html@@@MongoDB protection overview@@@Rubrik Security Cloud protects your MongoDB sources, databases, and collections, ensuring optimal storage efficiency and smooth database operations with its advanced security features and strong data protection...","mongodb/mdb_protection_retention_lock.html@@@Retention lock for MongoDB protection@@@A retention lock on an RSC SLA Domain is a security feature that prevents premature deletion of MongoDB snapshots...","mongodb/mdb_quick_links.html@@@Quick links for MongoDB@@@Immediate access to important tasks and information, enabling quick setup, daily operations, and critical recovery...","mongodb/mdb_rbac_backup_restore_overview.html@@@MongoDB Admin DB object for RBAC backup and recovery@@@The Admin DB object protects the RBAC configuration of a MongoDB source, including custom roles and users. Recovery applies at the source level, so it affects the users and roles for every database in the source...","mongodb/mdb_rbac_backup_restore_requirements.html@@@Requirements for MongoDB RBAC backup and recovery@@@Information about the version, privilege, and environment requirements for protecting and recovering the Admin DB object of a MongoDB source...","mongodb/mdb_recover.html@@@Recover MongoDB@@@Recover MongoDB objects to a specific point in time...","mongodb/mdb_replication_snapshots.html@@@Replication for MongoDB snapshots@@@You can use the SLA Domain replication policy to replicate MongoDB snapshots from one Rubrik cluster to another for disaster recovery...","mongodb/mdb_set_up_protection.html@@@Set up MongoDB protection@@@Protect your MongoDB workloads by assigning SLA Domains and configuring the protection options that meet your data protection requirements...","mongodb/mdb_viewing_events.html@@@Viewing events for MongoDB@@@View the Event Logs page from the Data Protection dashboard to see the events for your MongoDB objects...","mongodb/mdb_viewing_inventory.html@@@Viewing MongoDB inventory@@@View your MongoDB sources, databases, and collections to monitor their inventory and protection status...","mongodb/mongodb_auth_mechanisms.html@@@Evaluate authentication mechanisms for MongoDB sources@@@Rubrik supports Salted Challenge Response Authentication Mechanism and Lightweight Directory Access Protocol authentication mechanisms that MongoDB provides for database access, and SSL/TLS for securing database connections...","mongodb/mongodb_collection_details_page.html@@@MongoDB collection details page@@@The collection details page provides an overview of the selected MongoDB collection...","mongodb/mongodb_db_limitations.html@@@Limitations for MongoDB objects with logical backup and recovery@@@RSC has specific limitations for MongoDB objects with logical backup and recovery...","mongodb/mongodb_db_protection.html@@@MongoDB database protection@@@With the MongoDB protection feature, you can use SLA Domains to apply data protection and management policies to MongoDB databses to ensure optimal protection...","mongodb/mongodb_legal_hold_snapshots.html@@@Legal hold for MongoDB snapshots@@@Legal hold ensures that snapshots required for litigation are protected for the duration of the legal hold, providing a compliant and efficient way to manage data subject to legal obligations...","mongodb/mongodb_placing_snapshots_legal_hold.html@@@Placing a MongoDB snapshot on legal hold@@@Placing a legal hold on a MongoDB snapshot indefinitely retains that snapshot regardless of the assigned SLA Domain retention policy. RSC supports legal hold for MongoDB snapshots from Rubrik CDM version 9.6 and later...","mongodb/mongodb_point_in_time_recovery.html@@@MongoDB point-in-time recovery@@@You can use point-in-time recovery for MongoDB to restore your data to a specific point in time, ensuring data consistency and accuracy...","mongodb/mongodb_removing_legal_hold_snapshots.html@@@Removing legal hold from MongoDB snapshots@@@Remove legal hold from a MongoDB snapshot to return the snapshot to normal retention management. RSC supports legal hold for MongoDB snapshots from Rubrik CDM version 9.6 and later...","mongodb/mongodb_source_cluster_edit_settings.html@@@Editable settings for MongoDB sources for logical backup and recovery@@@Information about the settings available for editing a MongoDB source cluster for logical backup and recovery...","mongodb/mongodb_workloads.html@@@MongoDB workloads@@@RSC protects MongoDB sources, databases, and collections using the logical backup and recovery and physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager integration methods...","mongodb/ops_manager_details_retrieval.html@@@Retrieve Ops Manager details@@@To add a MongoDB source with physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager integration method, you need details such as the Group/Project ID and Cluster/Deployment ID from Ops Manager, which you can retrieve...","mongodb/physical_backup_recv_mdb_ops_mgr.html@@@Key features for protecting MongoDB physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager@@@RSC provides unified data management, automated global data protection, backup and recovery options, and advanced security features to protect your MongoDB sources through the Ops Manager integration...","mongodb/prereq_mdb_source_ops_manager.html@@@Prerequisites for MongoDB physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager@@@RSC has specific prerequisites for protecting MongoDB source clusters managed by the physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager integration method...","mongodb/prereq_mongodb_workload_protection.html@@@Prerequisites for MongoDB logical backup and recovery@@@RSC has some prerequisites and general requirements for protecting MongoDB logical backup and recovery workloads...","mongodb/protection_mdb_src_ops_mgr.html@@@Protection for MongoDB sources managed by Ops Manager@@@With MongoDB protection using physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager integration, you can use SLA Domains to apply data protection and management policies to MongoDB sources for optimal protection...","mongodb/recoverable_range_mdb_source.html@@@Recoverable range for MongoDB sources@@@The recoverable range of a MongoDB source with physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager integration is a visual representation of the period of time during which you can recover a source to a specific point in time...","mongodb/recoverable_range_mongodb_db_collection.html@@@Recoverable range for MongoDB databases and collections@@@The recoverable range is a visual representation of the period during which you can recover a database or a collection to a specific point in time...","mongodb/recovering_batch_mongodb_collections.html@@@Recovering a batch of MongoDB collections@@@Recover a batch of MongoDB collections by retrieving specific data from a backup source if you are overwriting an original collection or duplicating it in the same or another MongoDB source. You might use this in cases of a data loss or system corruption...","mongodb/recovering_batch_mongodb_db.html@@@Recovering a batch of MongoDB databases@@@Recover a batch of MongoDB databases by retrieving specific data from a backup source if you are overwriting an original collection or duplicating it in the same or another MongoDB source. This might be used in cases such as data loss or system corruption...","mongodb/recovering_mdb_src_ops_mgr.html@@@Recovering MongoDB sources managed by Ops Manager@@@Recover a MongoDB source managed through the physical backup and recovery using Ops Manager integration by retrieving specific data from a backup source, whether you are overwriting the original source or restoring it to another MongoDB source...","mongodb/recovering_mongodb_admin_db.html@@@Recovering the MongoDB Admin DB object@@@Recover the Admin DB object of a MongoDB source to return the custom roles and users of the source to the state in a selected snapshot...","mongodb/recovering_mongodb_collection.html@@@Recovering a MongoDB collection@@@Recover a MongoDB collection by retrieving specific data from a backup source if you are overwriting an original collection or duplicating it in the same or another MongoDB source. This might be used in cases such as data loss or system corruption...","mongodb/refreshing_mongodb_source_cluster.html@@@Refreshing a MongoDB source cluster@@@To refresh a MongoDB source cluster, update it to reflect the latest changes...","mongodb/removing_mongodb_source_cluster.html@@@Removing a MongoDB source cluster@@@Removing a MongoDB source cluster deletes the entire database along with its associated data...","mongodb/scripts_create_roles_backup_restore_mgdb.html@@@Scripts for MongoDB backup and restore role creation@@@You can use specific scripts to create roles and users with backup and restore permissions in MongoDB by defining specific privileges and assigning roles to control data access...","mongodb/taking_ods_physical_mdb_src_ops_mgr.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of MongoDB@@@In addition to the policy-based snapshots, use the on-demand snapshot process to take snapshots of your MongoDB objects...","mysql/mysql.html@@@MySQL@@@RSC protects the MySQL databases from accidental deletions, ransomware attacks, and other potential threats...","mysql/mysql_adding_ha_instance_group.html@@@Adding a MySQL HA instance group@@@Add a primary MySQL instance and its standby instances to RSC as a single High Availability instance group...","mysql/mysql_adding_hosts.html@@@Adding MySQL hosts@@@To establish a connection between MySQL and RSC, add a host for performing backup and recovery operations...","mysql/mysql_adding_instances.html@@@Adding MySQL instances@@@Add a MySQL instance to protect the instance and its databases through backup and recovery...","mysql/mysql_archiving_snapshots.html@@@Archiving for MySQL snapshots@@@Archiving in RSC tiers MySQL instance snapshots to lower-cost storage for cost savings, compliance, and security...","mysql/mysql_assigning_sla_ha_instance_group.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to a MySQL HA instance group@@@Assign an SLA Domain to a MySQL High Availability instance group, and select the backup source and instance priority for the group...","mysql/mysql_best_practices_db_recovery.html@@@Best practices for database-level recovery@@@Information on best practices to follow before performing database-level recovery in MySQL...","mysql/mysql_changing_retention_policy.html@@@Changing the retention policy of MySQL snapshots@@@Change the retention period of individual MySQL snapshots to optimize storage and data accessibility of MySQL snapshots...","mysql/mysql_cloning_sla_domain.html@@@Cloning MySQL SLA Domains@@@Clone an existing SLA Domain to save time by avoiding having to create and configure a new SLA Domain from scratch. Instead, you can make any necessary adjustments to the cloned SLA Domain...","mysql/mysql_common_protection_terms.html@@@Common MySQL protection terms@@@It is important to understand some common terms when protecting MySQL instances with RSC...","mysql/mysql_creating_custom_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for MySQL@@@Create a role with role-based access control privileges for managing MySQL databases. These privileges provide finer granularity for determining which permissions an RSC user has for performing specific actions on specific objects...","mysql/mysql_creating_custom_sla_domain.html@@@Creating custom SLA Domains for MySQL@@@Create a custom SLA Domain for MySQL to streamline and customize protection and recovery plans for MySQL instances...","mysql/mysql_creating_restore_mp_db_snap.html@@@Creating a restore mount point for MySQL database snapshots@@@Create a mount point for restoring your MySQL database snapshots by mounting a snapshot of backup data to the mount point using NFS...","mysql/mysql_creating_restore_mp_instance_snap.html@@@Creating a restore mount point for MySQL instance snapshots@@@Create a mount point to restore your MySQL instance snapshots by mounting a snapshot of backup data to the mount point using NFS...","mysql/mysql_deleting_ha_instance_group.html@@@Deleting a MySQL HA instance group@@@Delete a MySQL High Availability instance group to remove the group and all associated metadata from RSC...","mysql/mysql_deleting_instances.html@@@Deleting MySQL instances@@@To manage and organize the Rubrik cluster by removing databases that are not contributing to a MySQL workload, you can delete the MySQL instance...","mysql/mysql_deleting_sla_domain.html@@@Deleting MySQL SLA Domains@@@Delete an SLA Domain created for MySQL when it is no longer needed...","mysql/mysql_deleting_snapshots.html@@@Deleting MySQL snapshots@@@Delete MySQL snapshots that are no longer required for data protection...","mysql/mysql_downloading_archived_snapshots.html@@@Downloading archived MySQL snapshots@@@Download a MySQL snapshot from an archival location to a Rubrik cluster when the snapshot is not available in local storage...","mysql/mysql_downloading_replicated_snapshots.html@@@Downloading replicated MySQL snapshots@@@Download replicated MySQL snapshots to local storage on the source Rubrik cluster for data recovery...","mysql/mysql_editing_ha_instance_group.html@@@Editing a MySQL HA instance group@@@Update the name of a MySQL High Availability (HA) instance group or modify the details of individual instances in the group...","mysql/mysql_editing_instances.html@@@Editing MySQL instances@@@To modify a MySQL instance protected by a Rubrik cluster, you can edit the MySQL instance settings...","mysql/mysql_editing_sla_domain.html@@@Editing MySQL SLA Domains@@@Edit an SLA Domain to change the backup and recovery objectives of the associated MySQL instances...","mysql/mysql_eval_auth_options.html@@@Evaluate MySQL authentication options@@@When adding a MySQL instance to RSC, it is important to evaluate the available authentication options. Socket-based and TCP-based are two core authentication methods for a MySQL client to verify its identity with the server...","mysql/mysql_evaluate_sla_domain_options.html@@@Evaluate MySQL protection options@@@Before creating an SLA Domain for a MySQL workload, you can evaluate various protection options that RSC provides for MySQL instances...","mysql/mysql_ha_considerations.html@@@Considerations for MySQL HA instance groups@@@Specific considerations apply before you configure a MySQL HA instance group in RSC...","mysql/mysql_ha_instance_group.html@@@MySQL High Availability instance groups@@@High Availability for MySQL instances protects a group of primary and standby instances and maintains backup continuity when a failover promotes a standby instance to the primary role...","mysql/mysql_ha_instance_taking_ods.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of a MySQL HA instance group@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of a MySQL High Availability instance group outside the schedule of the assigned SLA Domain...","mysql/mysql_ha_mount_instance_snapshot.html@@@Mounting a MySQL HA snapshot for manual recovery@@@Mount a snapshot from a MySQL High Availability (HA) instance group to a host as a read-only point-in-time image for manual data extraction...","mysql/mysql_ha_recovering_databases.html@@@Database recovery from a MySQL HA instance group@@@RSC provides options for recovering selected databases from a MySQL High Availability (HA) instance group snapshot...","mysql/mysql_ha_recovering_databases_mount.html@@@Mounting a MySQL HA database snapshot for manual recovery@@@Mount selected databases from a MySQL High Availability (HA) instance group snapshot to a target host as a read-only image for manual data extraction...","mysql/mysql_ha_recovering_databases_new.html@@@Creating databases from a MySQL HA instance group snapshot@@@Create databases on a target instance using data from a MySQL High Availability (HA) instance group snapshot...","mysql/mysql_ha_recovering_databases_original.html@@@Restoring original databases from a MySQL HA instance group@@@Restore selected databases to their original location across all instances in a MySQL High Availability (HA) instance group using a selected recovery point...","mysql/mysql_ha_recovering_databases_target.html@@@Restoring databases to a target instance from a MySQL HA instance group snapshot@@@Restore selected databases to existing databases on a target instance that have the same table structure and schema as the source...","mysql/mysql_ha_recovering_instance_standalone.html@@@Recovering a MySQL HA snapshot to a standalone instance@@@Restore a recovery point from a MySQL High Availability (HA) instance group to a standalone instance...","mysql/mysql_ha_recovering_instance_target_ha.html@@@Recovering a MySQL HA group to a target HA group@@@Restore a MySQL High Availability (HA) instance group to an alternate target HA instance group using a selected recovery point...","mysql/mysql_ha_recovery.html@@@Recovery options for MySQL HA instance groups@@@RSC provides recovery options for a MySQL High Availability (HA) instance group based on the scope of recovery and the target location...","mysql/mysql_ha_split_brain.html@@@Split-brain in a MySQL HA instance group@@@A split-brain scenario occurs when RSC detects more than one primary instance in a MySQL High Availability (HA) instance group...","mysql/mysql_high_level_architecture.html@@@MySQL protection architecture@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects your MySQL databases...","mysql/mysql_instance_assigning_protection.html@@@Assigning protection to MySQL instances@@@You can assign a data protection policy to a MySQL instance to protect data against accidental deletion, corruption, and cyber threats...","mysql/mysql_instance_configuration.html@@@Configure MySQL instance@@@To configure MySQL instances with RSC, integrate the MySQL environment by registering Linux servers with a Rubrik cluster and installing the Rubrik Backup Service agent. Using this setup, RSC discovers MySQL instances, requiring configuration details and credentials for effective backup and restore management...","mysql/mysql_instance_taking_ods.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of MySQL instances@@@You can take a full snapshot of MySQL instances by using the on-demand snapshot method...","mysql/mysql_legal_hold_snapshots.html@@@Legal hold for MySQL snapshots@@@Legal hold ensures that snapshots required for litigation are protected for the duration of the legal hold, providing a compliant and efficient way to manage data subject to legal obligations...","mysql/mysql_multiple_archival_locations.html@@@Multiple archival locations for MySQL@@@You can configure multiple archival policies within a single SLA Domain to automate the delivery of snapshots to distinct cloud storage targets...","mysql/mysql_obj_level_pause_protection.html@@@Object-level pause and resume for MySQL protection@@@You can temporarily pause and resume protection for individual MySQL instances without affecting the protection of other objects managed by the same SLA Domain...","mysql/mysql_pausing_protection.html@@@Pausing protection for MySQL instances@@@You can pause protection for individual MySQL instances to temporarily suspend scheduled backup operations during maintenance windows or troubleshooting without affecting other instances in the environment...","mysql/mysql_placing_snapshots_legal_hold.html@@@Placing a MySQL snapshot on legal hold@@@Placing a legal hold on a MySQL snapshot indefinitely retains that snapshot regardless of the assigned SLA Domain retention policy...","mysql/mysql_planning_protection.html@@@Plan your MySQL protection@@@Before setting up a MySQL instance in RSC, it is necessary to plan user and access management for designated RSC users. This planning also involves reviewing the permissions that RSC requires in your MySQL environment to protect your MySQL instance...","mysql/mysql_primary_snapshot_retention.html@@@Primary snapshot retention for MySQL@@@Primary snapshot retention for MySQL instances provides data protection and recoverability by making it possible to set various retention policies. These policies include hourly, daily, monthly, and yearly retention of snapshots to meet compliance, business continuity, and disaster recovery requirements...","mysql/mysql_protection_config.html@@@Configure MySQL protection@@@Implementing a data protection strategy using SLA Domains ensures the resilience and availability of MySQL instances...","mysql/mysql_protection_key_features.html@@@Key features for MySQL protection@@@RSC provides unified data management, automated global data protection, various recovery options for MySQL databases, and advanced security features to protect your critical data...","mysql/mysql_protection_limitations.html@@@Limitations for MySQL protection@@@Information about RSC limitations for MySQL protection...","mysql/mysql_protection_setup.html@@@Protect MySQL databases@@@Protect MySQL instances using automated, policy-driven backups, ensuring data resilience and compliance with organizational standards...","mysql/mysql_recovering_databases_auto.html@@@Recovering MySQL databases automatically@@@Use the automated recovery workflow to restore specific MySQL databases within an instance. This process automates the manual mount-and-script steps required for database-level recovery...","mysql/mysql_recovering_ha_grp_org_loc.html@@@Recovering a MySQL HA group to the original location@@@Restore all instances in a MySQL High Availability (HA) instance group to their original location using a selected recovery point...","mysql/mysql_recovering_instances_auto.html@@@Recovering MySQL instances automatically@@@Use the automated recovery workflow to restore a MySQL instance as a standalone setup. This process simplifies recovery by automating manual steps required for instance-level recovery...","mysql/mysql_recovery.html@@@Recover MySQL data@@@After RSC takes snapshots of your MySQL workloads, you can recover the required workloads using different recovery options...","mysql/mysql_recovery_options.html@@@MySQL recovery options@@@RSC provides flexible and versatile options for MySQL recovery. You can recover either the entire MySQL instance or specific databases, ensuring rapid and granular data restoration from secure, immutable backups...","mysql/mysql_refreshing_ha_instance_group.html@@@Refreshing a MySQL HA instance group@@@Refresh a MySQL High Availability instance group so that RSC re-verifies the primary and standby roles of the instances in the group...","mysql/mysql_refreshing_instances.html@@@Refreshing MySQL instances@@@To ensure that the information on a Rubrik cluster is up to date and accurate, refresh the MySQL instance. When you refresh a MySQL database instance, all databases local to the selected instance are discovered and the relevant metadata is updated...","mysql/mysql_removing_legal_hold_snapshots.html@@@Removing legal hold from MySQL snapshots@@@Remove legal hold from a MySQL snapshot to return the snapshot to normal retention management...","mysql/mysql_required_perms.html@@@Required permissions for MySQL protection@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to protect your MySQL instances...","mysql/mysql_restoring_snap_new_db.html@@@Restoring MySQL snapshots to a new database@@@Restore the MySQL snapshots to a new MySQL database...","mysql/mysql_restoring_snap_new_instance.html@@@Restoring MySQL snapshots to a new instance@@@Restore the MySQL instance snapshots to a newly created MySQL instance...","mysql/mysql_restoring_snap_original_db.html@@@Restoring MySQL snapshots to the original database@@@Restore the MySQL snapshots to the original MySQL database from which the backup was taken...","mysql/mysql_restoring_snap_original_instance.html@@@Restoring MySQL snapshots to the original instance@@@Restore MySQL snapshots to the original MySQL instance from which the backup was taken...","mysql/mysql_resuming_protection.html@@@Resuming protection for MySQL instances@@@You can resume protection for MySQL instances that were previously paused to restore scheduled backup operations according to the assigned SLA Domain policy...","mysql/mysql_retention_lock_sla_domain.html@@@Retention lock for MySQL SLA Domains@@@A retention lock on an RSC SLA Domain is a security feature that prevents premature deletion of MySQL snapshots...","mysql/mysql_rsc_user_management.html@@@RSC user management for MySQL protection@@@Designating specific users with appropriate privileges and roles in RSC enhances security for protecting your MySQL databases...","mysql/mysql_setup.html@@@Set up your MySQL system@@@You can protect MySQL database using RSC by configuring MySQL hosts and instances with it. This setup automates backups and enables rapid recovery from threats such as ransomware, providing unified data security and resilience for your MySQL databases...","mysql/mysql_setup_prerequisites.html@@@Prerequisites for MySQL protection@@@Information about prerequisites that you must complete before adding MySQL hosts and instances to RSC...","mysql/mysql_snapshot_replication.html@@@Replication for MySQL snapshots@@@Overview of the MySQL replication process and its benefits...","mysql/mysql_syncing_sla_domain_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Synchronizing SLA Domains with a Rubrik cluster@@@Synchronize an SLA Domain with a Rubrik cluster to take on-demand snapshots and to maintain data protection during ransomware recovery...","mysql/mysql_unmounting_restore_mp.html@@@Unmounting the restore mount point after MySQL snapshot recovery@@@After recovering MySQL snapshots, unmount the restore mount point to remove the metadata associated with the selected MySQL cluster...","mysql/mysql_user_notes.html@@@User notes for MySQL@@@You can add user notes to explain the reason behind performing a specific task, ensuring comprehensive audit tracking for your MySQL environment...","nas/adding_nas_system.html@@@Adding a NAS system@@@To enhance data management and protection, add a NAS system to a Rubrik cluster...","nas/nas_adding_dell_nas_system.html@@@Adding Dell EMC Isilon as a NAS system@@@To manage and protect backup and recovery data efficiently on a NAS share hosted on a Dell EMC Isilon, add Dell EMC Isilon as a NAS system to a Rubrik cluster...","nas/nas_adding_generic_nas_system.html@@@Adding Generic NAS as a NAS system@@@To manage and protect data on a NAS share hosted on Generic NAS, add Generic NAS as a NAS system to a Rubrik cluster for efficient backup, recovery, and data management...","nas/nas_adding_netapp_cluster_nas_system.html@@@Adding NetApp Cluster as a NAS system@@@To manage and protect data efficiently on a NAS share hosted on a NetApp Cluster, add NetApp Cluster as a NAS system to a Rubrik cluster...","nas/nas_adding_nx_fs_nas_system.html@@@Adding Nutanix File Server as a NAS system@@@To manage and protect data on a NAS share hosted on Nutanix File Server, add Nutanix File Server as a NAS system to a Rubrik cluster for efficient backup, recovery, and data management...","nas/nas_adding_pure_nas_system.html@@@Adding Pure System as a NAS system@@@To manage and protect data on a NAS share hosted on Pure System, add Pure System as a NAS system to a Rubrik cluster for efficient backup, recovery, and data management...","nas/nas_configuring_smb_auth_namespace.html@@@Configuring SMB authentication for namespaces@@@For NetApp, Isilon, and Pure FlashBlade namespaces, configure SMB credentials at the namespace level to enable SMB authentication for NAS shares...","nas/nas_configuring_smb_auth_shares.html@@@Configuring SMB authentication for SMB shares@@@For NetApp and Isilon systems, configure SMB credentials manually at the SMB share level to enable SMB authentication and protection for all namespaces and shares on the system...","nas/nas_configuring_smb_auth_system.html@@@Configuring SMB authentication for NAS systems@@@For NetApp and Isilon systems, configure SMB credentials manually at the system level to enable SMB authentication for all namespaces and NAS shares on the system, or to meet your site requirements for SMB authentication...","nas/nas_manage_protection.html@@@Manage protection for NAS systems@@@You can manage protection for NAS shares and directories by assigning them an SLA Domain...","nas/nas_manage_protection_netapp_snapmirror.html@@@Manage protection for NetApp SnapMirror NAS volumes@@@RSC backs up the latest snapshot of read-only NetApp SnapMirror volumes, allowing the flexibility to specify a particular snapshot...","nas/nas_management.html@@@NAS management@@@You can register, refresh, and delete NAS shares from the NAS systems page in Rubrik Security Cloud...","nas/nas_managing_protection_nas_directory.html@@@Managing protection for a NAS directory@@@Assign a data protection policy to protect the selected NAS directory...","nas/nas_managing_protection_share.html@@@Managing protection for a NAS share@@@Assign a data protection policy to protect a selected NAS share...","nas/nas_managing_protection_snapmirror_vol.html@@@Managing protection for a NetApp SnapMirror volume@@@Protect and manage data for a NetApp SnapMirror volume. NetApp SnapMirror volumes are read-only...","nas/nas_ods.html@@@On-demand snapshots of NAS shares and directories@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, you can use the on-demand snapshot process to take snapshots of protected NAS shares and directories...","nas/nas_recovering_files_folder_share.html@@@Recovering files or folders from a NAS share@@@Recover files or folders from a NAS share by downloading the share, overwriting original files, or recovering the share to a separate folder...","nas/nas_recovery_of_nas_shares.html@@@NAS shares recovery options@@@Rubrik Security Cloud supports recovery from backups of NAS shares...","nas/nas_removing_protection_for_a_nas_directory.html@@@Removing protection for a NAS directory@@@Remove protection for a NAS directory when it is not required...","nas/nas_share_recovery_export.html@@@Exporting NAS shares@@@You can recover selected NAS shares by exporting them...","nas/nas_shares_details_page.html@@@NAS share details@@@The NAS share details page displays object details, protection status, a calendar view of snapshots, and event and snapshot details...","nas/nas_smb_local_user_mgmt.html@@@SMB local user management of NAS components@@@SMB local user management of NAS components is crucial for mounting, protecting, and managing SMB backup effectively, and for restore operations...","nas/nas_snapdiff_netapp.html@@@NetApp SnapDiff API integration@@@The NetApp SnapDiff API integration enables Rubrik CDM cluster to identify the files that changed between two snapshots, which speeds up incremental backups on large NetApp shares...","nas/nas_systems.html@@@NAS systems@@@RSC manages and protects NFS and SMB shares on NAS systems for efficient data storage and retrieval...","nas/nas_systems_actions.html@@@Actions available for NAS systems@@@Information about the actions available for NAS systems in RSC, including various operations for protecting your data, managing NAS systems, and options to hide and reveal the selected NAS shares. You can access these actions on the NAS Systems page in RSC...","nas/nas_taking_an_on_demand_snapshot_of_a_nas_directory.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of a NAS directory@@@You can take an on-demand snapshot of a NAS directory...","nas/nas_taking_on_demand_snapshots_of_a_nas_share.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of a NAS share@@@You can take snapshots of NAS shares by using the on-demand snapshot process...","nas/required_isilon_privileges.html@@@Required Isilon privileges@@@When you add an Isilon NAS system, RSC creates a service account and a role with specific privileges...","nas/required_netapp_privileges.html@@@Required NetApp privileges@@@When you add a NetApp NAS system, RSC creates a service account and role with specific privileges...","nas/rsc_nas_service_account.html@@@RSC service account for NAS systems@@@RSC creates a Rubrik service account and an associated role with the necessary privileges on the NAS system and uses the service account for backup, restore, and auto-discovery of NAS systems...","nascd/rncd_adding_credentials_targets.html@@@Adding credentials for targets from NAS CD@@@Add credentials to access a supported target that NAS CD can use to back up and archive data...","nascd/rncd_adding_targets.html@@@Adding targets from NAS CD@@@Add supported NAS CD targets to back up or archive data...","nascd/rncd_creating_archive_policy.html@@@Creating archive policies@@@Create an archival policy to archive your data to a target location with specific retention requirements...","nascd/rncd_creating_backup_policy.html@@@Creating a NAS CD backup policy@@@Create a NAS CD backup policy to back up your data to a target with specific retention requirements...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_accessing_local_vm_page.html@@@Accessing the local page of an AHV virtual machine@@@Access the local page of an AHV virtual machine to view information about the virtual machine...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_adding_nx_cluster.html@@@Adding a Nutanix cluster@@@To protect the AHV virtual machines deployed on a Nutanix cluster or a Nutanix Cloud Clusters (NC2), add the Nutanix cluster or the NC2 to a Rubrik cluster by providing the required details...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_adding_nx_prism_central_rbk_clstr.html@@@Adding Nutanix Prism Central to Rubrik clusters@@@To protect AHV virtual machines managed by Nutanix Prism Central, add Nutanix Prism Central to one or more Rubrik clusters by providing the required details, such as the IP address, login credentials, and root certificate...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_addition_nx_cluster_rsc.html@@@Addition of Nutanix clusters to RSC@@@By adding Nutanix clusters, Nutanix Cloud Clusters, or Nutanix Prism Central to RSC, you can protect the AHV virtual machines deployed on Nutanix clusters or Nutanix Cloud Clusters...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_batch_recovery_of_vm.html@@@Recovery of a batch of AHV virtual machines@@@You can recover a batch of AHV virtual machines in a single operation from the Nutanix Virtual Machines inventory page...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_changing_retention_policy.html@@@Changing the retention policy for an AHV virtual machine snapshot@@@Assign a retention policy to existing snapshots of a specific AHV virtual machine...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_creating_custom_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for Nutanix workloads@@@Create a custom role with Role-based Access Control privileges for managing your Nutanix workloads. These privileges give you finer control over the actions that each RSC user can perform on specific objects...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_creating_live_mount.html@@@Creating a live mount for AHV@@@Live mount an AHV virtual machine on a Nutanix cluster from a snapshot on the Rubrik cluster. The live mounted virtual machine uses the Rubrik cluster as its datastore...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_deleting_nx_cluster.html@@@Deleting the Nutanix cluster information@@@Delete the connection information of the Nutanix cluster that is stored by a Rubrik cluster to remove protection of the virtual machines of that Nutanix cluster...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_deleting_vm_snapshots.html@@@Deleting snapshots for an AHV virtual machine@@@Delete eligible snapshots of an AHV virtual machine...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_downloading_vdisk_local.html@@@Downloading an AHV virtual disk to a local machine@@@After you have downloaded the AHV virtual disks to your CDM cluster, download the virtual disks to a local machine for offline analysis...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_downloading_vdisks_cdm_cluster.html@@@Downloading an AHV virtual disk to a CDM cluster@@@Download a specific virtual disk from an AHV virtual machine snapshot to a CDM cluster...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_dr_support_prism_central.html@@@Disaster Recovery support for Nutanix Prism Central@@@Disaster Recovery for Nutanix Prism Central ensures uninterrupted protection of AHV virtual machines during a planned failover...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_editing_nx_cluster.html@@@Editing the Nutanix cluster information@@@Edit some properties of the Nutanix cluster as required...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_editing_nx_prism_central.html@@@Editing a Nutanix Prism Central configuration@@@Edit a Nutanix Prism Central configuration to update credentials, map newly discovered Nutanix clusters to Rubrik clusters, or associate unmapped Nutanix clusters with new Rubrik clusters...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_edits_nx_pc.html@@@Edits for a Nutanix Prism Central@@@After adding a Nutanix Prism Central and mapping its Nutanix clusters to specific Rubrik clusters, you can edit the username, password, and root certificate. You can also map a newly discovered Nutanix cluster that you added to the Nutanix Prism Central to any available Rubrik cluster...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_enabling_vm_scripts.html@@@Enabling scripts for AHV virtual machines@@@Configure RSC to run scripts when backing up a virtual machine...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_excluding_vm_disks.html@@@Excluding AHV virtual disk files@@@Exclude specific managed disks while protecting other managed disks attached to a virtual machine instance...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_exporting_vm_snapshot.html@@@Exporting an AHV virtual machine snapshot@@@Perform an export operation to create a virtual machine from a point-in-time copy of the source virtual machine...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_local_host_page.html@@@Local host page for AHV virtual machine@@@The local host page provides detailed information about the virtual machine, protection of the virtual machine, available snapshots, and tasks related to the virtual machine and snapshots...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_migrating_live_mounted_vdisk.html@@@Migrating a live mounted AHV virtual disk@@@Migrate the data source of a live mounted AHV virtual disk from the Rubrik cluster to a Nutanix storage container...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_migrating_live_mounted_vm.html@@@Migrating a live mounted AHV virtual machine@@@Migrate the data source of a live mounted AHV virtual machine from a Rubrik cluster to a Nutanix storage container...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_nc2_aws_and_azure.html@@@Nutanix Cloud Clusters on AWS, Azure, and GCP@@@Nutanix NC2 provides a platform for running applications in public clouds and for extending your on-premises Nutanix infrastructure to AWS, Azure, and GCP. With RSC, you can protect Nutanix NC2 workloads on AWS, Azure, and GCP...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_nx_live_mount_page.html@@@Live Mounts page for Nutanix virtual machines@@@The Live Mounts page for Nutanix virtual machines displays details about the mounted virtual machines and virtual disks and provides options to unmount virtual machines and virtual disks, change the power status, and migrate the data source...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_nx_pc_deplymnt_multiple_rbk_clstr.html@@@Nutanix Prism Central deployment on multiple Rubrik clusters@@@You can protect AHV virtual machines with RSC by deploying a Nutanix Prism Central instance on one or more Rubrik clusters. You can add the details of the instance in RSC and map the Nutanix clusters within the Prism Central instance to specific Rubrik clusters...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_ods.html@@@On-demand snapshots of AHV virtual machines@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, you can create AHV virtual machine snapshots by using the on-demand snapshot process...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_overview_snapshot_card.html@@@AHV Snapshots card@@@For a selected local virtual machine, the Snapshots card in the Overview tab provides the ability to browse snapshots that reside on the local Rubrik cluster and on the replication location...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_overview_tab.html@@@AHV Overview tab@@@Information available on the Overview card...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_overview_tab_actions.html@@@Actions available on the AHV Overview tab@@@Actions available for a selected virtual machine on the AHV Overview tab...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_powering_off_vm.html@@@Powering off an AHV virtual machine after live mount@@@Power off a mounted AHV virtual machine from the Live Mounts page...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_prerequisites.html@@@Prerequisites for onboarding Nutanix workloads@@@For RSC to protect your Nutanix workloads, you must fulfill specific prerequisites before you start onboarding Nutanix clusters or Nutanix Cloud Clusters in RSC...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_protecting_nx_cluster.html@@@Protecting Nutanix clusters@@@Specify an SLA Domain setting for Nutanix clusters to have the setting applied to the objects and virtual machines contained by the clusters and server...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_protecting_vm.html@@@Protecting AHV virtual machines@@@Assign an SLA Domain to protect an AHV virtual machine...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_rbac_protection.html@@@RBAC for Nutanix workload protection@@@Instead of using the Administrator role, you can create a custom role with minimum privileges to onboard and manage Nutanix workloads in RSC...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_rbs_installation.html@@@Rubrik Backup Service installation for AHV@@@The Rubrik Backup Service is a software installed on a host that coordinates activity between the Rubrik cluster and the host...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_recovering_batch_of_vm_using_export.html@@@Recovering a batch of AHV virtual machines using exports@@@Perform exports for recovering a batch of AHV virtual machines in a single operation on the Nutanix Virtual Machines inventory page...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_recovering_batch_of_vm_using_live_mount.html@@@Recovering a batch of AHV virtual machines using Live Mounts@@@Create live mounts for recovering a batch of AHV virtual machines in a single operation on the Nutanix Virtual Machines inventory page...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_recovering_files.html@@@Recovering AHV files or folders@@@Restore files or folders from successfully indexed snapshots...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_recovering_v_disk_mounting.html@@@Recovering AHV virtual disks by mounting@@@Recover specific virtual disks by mounting the disks from a snapshot on to a target AHV virtual machine...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_refreshing_cluster_metadata.html@@@Refreshing metadata provided by Nutanix cluster@@@Manually refresh the metadata provided by a Nutanix cluster...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_registering_vm_running_rbs.html@@@Registering a virtual machine running the Rubrik Backup Service@@@After installing Rubrik Backup Service on a virtual machine, register the virtual machine with RSC...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_required_permissions.html@@@Required RSC privileges for Nutanix workloads@@@The minimum RSC privileges required to onboard, protect, and recover Nutanix workloads...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_sla_assignment_options.html@@@SLA Domain assignment options for AHV virtual machines@@@Protect a set of virtual machines by assigning the selected set to an SLA Domain. Assigning virtual machines to an SLA Domain protects the virtual machines by applying the data protection policies of the SLA Domain...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_snapshot_consistency.html@@@AHV snapshot consistency@@@With the AHV snapshot consistency feature, you can select the type of snapshot you want RSC to take. Depending on your specific requirements, RSC can take either application-consistent snapshots or crash-consistent snapshots...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_snapshots_information.html@@@Information available on the AHV Snapshots tab@@@Information about the snapshots for a selected virtual machine...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_snapshots_tab.html@@@AHV Snapshots tab@@@The Snapshots tab contains information for all snapshots for the chosen virtual machine...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_taking_ods.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of an AHV virtual machine@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of a specific AHV virtual machine and assign an SLA Domain to that snapshot. The retention, replication, and archiving settings of the SLA Domain are applied to the snapshot to protect the virtual machine effectively...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_unmounting_vdisk.html@@@Unmounting an AHV virtual disk@@@Unmount a live mounted AHV virtual disk from a Rubrik cluster...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_unmounting_vm.html@@@Unmounting an AHV virtual machine@@@Unmount the live mounted AHV virtual machine from the Rubrik cluster...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_v_disk_recovery_mounting.html@@@AHV virtual disk recovery by mounting@@@You can use RSC to recover specific virtual disks in an AHV virtual machine by mounting the disks from a snapshot on to a target AHV virtual machine...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_viewing_details_nx_pc.html@@@Viewing the details of Nutanix Prism Central@@@View all the relevant details related to Nutanix Prism Central and its associated Nutanix clusters or Nutanix Cloud Clusters to manage your Nutanix environment effectively...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_virtual_machine_in_place_recovery.html@@@AHV virtual machine in-place recovery@@@Nutanix AHV virtual machine in-place recovery provides a faster and easier option for recovering an AHV virtual machine from snapshots, compared to other recovery options...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_virtual_machine_protection.html@@@AHV virtual machine protection@@@SLA Domains can be used to apply the data protection policies to an individual virtual machine or a selected set of virtual machines...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_virtual_machines.html@@@AHV virtual machines@@@RSC provides data management and protection for virtual machines deployed in a Nutanix Acropolis environment...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_vm_automatic_protection.html@@@AHV virtual machine automatic protection@@@Rubrik cluster adheres to set rules to provide consistency when applying automatic protection...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_vm_instant_recovery.html@@@AHV virtual machine instant recovery@@@You can use the instant recovery option to quickly replace the source virtual machine with a new virtual machine created from a snapshot...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_vm_protection.html@@@AHV virtual machine protection@@@RSC provides protection for AHV virtual machines either by individually assigning the virtual machine to an SLA Domain or through automatic protection...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_vm_protection_state.html@@@States of AHV virtual machine protection@@@Information about several states of AHV virtual machine protection...","nutanix_ahv/ahv_vm_recovery.html@@@Recovery of AHV virtual machines@@@You can recover an AHV virtual machine or specific disks within a virtual machine from snapshots that are locally available on a Rubrik cluster...","nutanix_ahv/configuring_ahv_snapshot_consistency_ahv_vm.html@@@Configuring AHV snapshot consistency for an AHV VM@@@Depending on your specific requirements, you can configure RSC to take application-consistent or crash-consistent snapshots for your AHV virtual machine at the AHV virtual machine level...","nutanix_ahv/configuring_ahv_snp_consistncy_nx_clster.html@@@Configuring AHV snapshot consistency for Nutanix cluster@@@Depending on your specific requirements, you can configure RSC to take application-consistent or crash-consistent snapshots for your AHV virtual machines at the Nutanix cluster level...","nutanix_ahv/criteria_inherit_protection_setting.html@@@Criteria for inheriting a protection setting@@@Information about how an AHV virtual machine that is associated with multiple Nutanix categories inherits a protection setting based on specific criteria...","nutanix_ahv/inplace_rcvry_prchk_fail_condtns_ahv_vm.html@@@Prechecks and failure conditions for in-place recovery of AHV VMs@@@To mitigate the risk of data loss and execute a smooth recovery process, RSC performs prechecks to ensure that the initiated in-place recovery meets the required conditions...","nutanix_ahv/performing_ahv_vm_instant_recovery.html@@@Performing AHV virtual machine instant recovery@@@Perform an instant recovery of an AHV virtual machine to replace the source virtual machine with a fully functional point-in-time copy of the source virtual machine...","nutanix_ahv/performing_inplace_recovery_ahv_vm.html@@@Performing in-place recovery for AHV VMs@@@Perform an in-place recovery of an AHV virtual machine for faster recovery of its data using a Rubrik snapshot...","nutanix_ahv/permissions_adding_pc_rubrik_clusters.html@@@Permissions for adding Prism Central to Rubrik clusters@@@To add Prism Central to a Rubrik cluster and protect your data, you must provide credentials for a user role or account with specific permissions. These permissions ensure Rubrik can access the Nutanix cluster, discover assets, and perform backup operations...","nutanix_ahv/port_requirements_nutanix.html@@@Port requirements for Nutanix@@@Information about the ports you must open so that RSC can protect your Nutanix workloads...","nutanix_ahv/protecting_ahv_vm_nx_category.html@@@Protecting the AHV VMs in a Nutanix category@@@To protect the AHV virtual machines grouped under a Nutanix category, assign a protection setting to a Nutanix category or a category value...","nutanix_ahv/req_perm_inplace_recoveries.html@@@Required permissions for in-place recoveries@@@Information about the user permissions required to perform an in-place recovery for AHV virtual machines...","nutanix_ahv/sla_domain_assignment_nx_categories.html@@@SLA Domain assignment to Nutanix categories@@@A Nutanix category groups AHV virtual machines. By assigning an SLA Domain to a Nutanix category, you can protect the AHV virtual machines in that category...","oci/adding_oci_compartment.html@@@Adding an OCI compartment@@@Add an OCI account and OCI compartment to provision an OCI account on RSC...","oci/deleting_oci_compartment.html@@@Deleting an OCI compartment@@@Delete an OCI compartment from RSC...","oci/editing_oci_compartment.html@@@Editing an OCI compartment@@@Edit OCI permissions and service account information for an OCI compartment and service account already added to RSC...","oci/oci_compartment_permissions.html@@@OCI compartment permissions@@@Information about the permissions required for adding an OCI compartment to RSC...","oci/oci_compartment_prereq.html@@@OCI compartment prerequisites@@@Information about the prerequisites for adding an OCI compartment to RSC...","oci/oci_compartment_setup.html@@@OCI compartment setup@@@You can set up an OCI compartment by adding the compartment to RSC and start protecting your OCI workloads...","oci/oci_workload_protection.html@@@Oracle Cloud Infrastructure workloads@@@Rubrik provides protection for Oracle Cloud Infrastructure workloads...","oci/recommendations_adding_oci_compartments.html@@@Recommendations for adding OCI compartments@@@Rubrik recommends specific actions and best practices for adding OCI compartments to RSC...","oci/updating_oci_policy_perms.html@@@Updating policy permissions on an OCI compartment@@@Update the policy permissions on an OCI cloud account added to RSC...","offrec/oracle/cloning_dg_groups_or.html@@@Cloning Data Guard groups@@@Replace an Oracle Data Guard group or restore datafiles with a fully functional point-in-time copy...","okta/adding_okta_tenant.html@@@Adding Okta tenant@@@Add an Okta tenant to configure Okta IdP in RSC to protect the identity data of the users...","okta/adding_rsc_app_oin.html@@@Adding RSC application in Okta@@@Add the RSC application in your Okta Admin Console and generate secure credentials required for the Okta integration with RSC...","okta/assigning_protection_okta_tenants.html@@@Assigning protection to Okta tenants@@@Assign an SLA Domain to an Okta tenant to apply automated snapshot management policies, ensuring data protection aligns with organizational requirements...","okta/auth_server_recovery_considerations.html@@@Considerations for recovering authorization servers@@@Information about the limitations and post-recovery steps to consider when you recover an Okta authorization server, because Okta cannot back up or regenerate certain configurations...","okta/configure_okta_idp.html@@@Configure Okta IdP@@@Configure your Okta Identity Provider by adding Okta tenants to RSC and perform other maintenance operations, such as editing and removing the Okta tenants...","okta/configuring_workflows_svc_account.html@@@Configuring Okta Workflows service account@@@Create and configure a dedicated service account in the Okta Admin Console to allow RSC to access and back up your Okta Workflows...","okta/creating_sla_domain_okta.html@@@Creating SLA Domain for Okta tenants@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to define and apply customized data protection and management policies for your Okta tenants...","okta/deleting_okta_snapshots.html@@@Deleting Okta snapshots@@@Manually delete an Okta snapshot from RSC if that snapshot is no longer required...","okta/editing_okta_tenants.html@@@Editing Okta tenant@@@Edit an Okta tenant to update the domain URL, client ID, and client secret. You cannot change the backup location...","okta/evaluate_okta_configuration_options.html@@@Evaluate Okta configuration options@@@You can add Okta tenants to RSC using the Identity Resilience inventory, Data Protection inventory, or Settings menu...","okta/manage_okta_tenants.html@@@Manage Okta tenants@@@Viewing and analyzing detailed information about your protected Okta IdP from the Inventory page enables you to make informed decisions. Key aspects include viewing tenants, checking protection status, reviewing detailed object attributes, browsing the snapshot calendar, viewing events log for audit and compliance, and performing maintenance such as deleting snapshots...","okta/manage_protection_okta_idp.html@@@Manage protection for Okta IdP@@@You can use SLA Domains to apply data protection and management policies to Okta tenants for optimal protection...","okta/multivalued_data_recovery_rules.html@@@Multi-valued data recovery rules@@@Information about how to handle conflicts for multi-valued data, both attributes and relationships, during recovery. RSC provides two options, overwrite or merge values, enabling you to select the option that best meets your organizational requirements for data consistency...","okta/okta_app_recovery_post_req.html@@@Okta application recovery requirements@@@Recovering an Okta application may require manual action to restore credentials, certificates, and provisioning configuration that RSC cannot automatically recover...","okta/okta_authentication_settings_recovery.html@@@Authentication settings recovery for Okta objects@@@When you recover Okta Identity Providers or Applications, RSC restores the client secrets and public trust configuration that Okta exposes, so recovered objects can authenticate without manual reconfiguration...","okta/okta_authenticator_recovery_considerations.html@@@Considerations for recovering Okta authenticators@@@Information about prerequisites for capturing authenticators in backups, limitations for authenticators that hold secrets, and authenticator-specific behavior during recovery...","okta/okta_authenticator_recovery_post_req.html@@@Okta authenticator post-recovery requirements@@@Information about failure scenarios, remediation steps, and post-recovery validation checks for Okta authenticator recovery...","okta/okta_cross_tenant_recovery.html@@@Okta cross-tenant recovery@@@RSC cross-tenant recovery for Okta restores directory objects from a source tenant snapshot to a different onboarded target tenant...","okta/okta_cross_tenant_recovery_config.html@@@Okta cross-tenant recovery configuration@@@Cross-tenant recovery for Okta requires onboarded source and target tenants, specific RSC privileges, a compatible Okta license tier, active target tenant credentials, and post-recovery domain adjustments...","okta/okta_cross_tenant_recovery_limitations.html@@@Okta cross-tenant recovery limitations@@@Cross-tenant recovery has specific limitations related to object identity matching, Universal Directory schema dependencies, and supported use cases...","okta/okta_group_rules_recovery.html@@@Okta group rules recovery@@@To recover a group rule, it is important to understand that an Okta group rule cannot exist without its target groups. RSC applies dependency-aware behavior when recovering group rules...","okta/okta_hooks_recovery_considerations.html@@@Considerations for recovering Okta hooks@@@Information about backup and recovery behavior for Okta event hooks and inline hooks, including limitations that require manual steps after recovery...","okta/okta_hooks_recovery_post_req.html@@@Post-recovery steps for Okta hooks@@@Manual steps required after recovering Okta event hooks or inline hooks to restore full functionality...","okta/okta_idp.html@@@Okta IdP@@@Rubrik Security Cloud provides protection and recovery for Okta Identity Provider objects. By integrating your Okta tenant with Rubrik, you can leverage a comprehensive set of data protection features designed for security, simplicity, and reliability...","okta/okta_idp_recovery_post_req.html@@@Okta identity provider recovery requirements@@@Recovering an Okta identity provider can require manual steps, such as re-entering a credential or updating a certificate that RSC cannot complete automatically...","okta/okta_key_features_protection.html@@@Key features for protecting Okta IdP@@@RSC provides unified identity management, identity protection, and recovery for critical Okta IdP objects...","okta/okta_permissions.html@@@Okta permissions@@@Information about the Okta permissions that RSC requires when you add the RSC application within your Okta Admin Console...","okta/okta_supported_objects.html@@@Supported Okta objects@@@Information about the critical Okta objects supported by Rubrik for backup and granular recovery, including those related to user access, security, and application functionality...","okta/plan_okta_idp_protection.html@@@Plan your Okta IdP protection@@@Before integrating Okta IdP with RSC, you must meet certain requirements to start protecting your critical Okta objects...","okta/recover_okta_objects.html@@@Recover Okta objects@@@RSC recovers individual Okta objects, along with their related objects and relationships, from automated or on-demand snapshots. You can recover objects to the same tenant or to a different onboarded tenant...","okta/recovering_okta_objects.html@@@Recovering Okta objects@@@Recover required Okta objects using automated or on-demand snapshots of your Okta tenant when a critical object is accidentally deleted or changed...","okta/recovering_okta_objects_cross_tenant.html@@@Recovering Okta directory objects to a different tenant@@@Recover Okta directory objects from a source tenant snapshot to a different onboarded target tenant...","okta/recovering_okta_workflows.html@@@Recovering Okta workflows@@@Recover specific Okta workflow automations from a snapshot when workflows are accidentally deleted, misconfigured, or corrupted...","okta/recreate_objects_restore_relationships.html@@@Recreate objects and restore relationships@@@RSC enhances granular recovery of critical Okta objects by discovering, displaying, and simplifying the complex, interlinked object structure and dependencies in Okta. This enables you to precisely select and manage the recovery of critical Okta objects and their associated dependencies...","okta/relationship_restore_scope.html@@@Relationship restore scope@@@Granular recovery for Okta objects enables you to restore selected objects along with their dependencies. RSC provides options to recover selected objects, interconnected objects, and their relationships. This feature enables you to re-establish broken links and corrupted relationships, such as those between users and groups...","okta/removing_okta_tenant.html@@@Removing Okta tenant@@@Remove an Okta tenant from RSC when that tenant is no longer needed for protection...","okta/setting_up_okta_workflows_protection.html@@@Setting up Okta Workflows protection@@@To protect your Okta Workflows automation, connect a dedicated service account for backup access...","okta/taking_ods_okta_tenants.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Okta tenants@@@As an RSC user with the required privileges, you can manually initiate an immediate, on-demand snapshot of an Okta tenant. You can take on-demand snapshots in addition to your regularly scheduled backups...","okta/user_status_recovery_rules.html@@@User status recovery rules@@@Information about how RSC recovers users that were in a Staged or Locked Out status when the snapshot was taken. Okta does not support reverting user statuses, so RSC provides settings to control how it restores user statuses...","okta/viewing_okta_snapshots.html@@@Viewing Okta snapshots@@@Access the calendar view to review the backup history and list all successful snapshots taken for a specific Okta tenant...","okta/viewing_okta_tenant_details.html@@@Viewing Okta tenant details@@@View the comprehensive details of a specific Okta tenant to check its protection status, review snapshot information, and track recovery and snapshot events in the Events tab...","okta/viewing_okta_tenants.html@@@Viewing Okta tenants@@@View all Okta tenants that you have successfully added to RSC using the Inventory page...","openstack/add_openstack_virtual_machine.html@@@Add an OpenStack environment@@@Add OpenStack environments in RSC to take snapshots and protect your data...","openstack/adding_openstack_environment.html@@@Adding an OpenStack environment@@@Add an OpenStack environment to RSC to ensure data protection...","openstack/adding_openstack_environment_2.html@@@Adding an OpenStack environment@@@Add an OpenStack environment to RSC to ensure data protection...","openstack/assigning_sla_domains_openstack.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to OpenStack assets@@@Assign SLA Domains to OpenStack assets to protect your OpenStack virtual machines or regions...","openstack/configuring_ceph_openstack.html@@@Configuring Native Ceph Backup for an OpenStack volume type@@@Configure Ceph cluster settings for an OpenStack volume type so that virtual machines that use Ceph-backed Cinder storage can use incremental backups...","openstack/editing_openstack_environments.html@@@Editing OpenStack environments@@@Edit the Keystone authentication settings for an OpenStack environment that RSC manages...","openstack/editing_openstack_proxy_vm_environments.html@@@Editing an OpenStack proxy virtual machine environment@@@Edit the network, flavor, and security group settings for an OpenStack proxy virtual machine...","openstack/exporting_openstack_vm_snapshots.html@@@Exporting OpenStack virtual machine snapshots@@@Export an OpenStack virtual machine snapshot to create a point-in-time copy for backup or migration...","openstack/monitoring_openstack_proxy_vms.html@@@Monitoring OpenStack proxy virtual machines@@@Monitor the OpenStack proxy virtual machines to determine their status...","openstack/openstack_ceph_native_backup.html@@@Native Ceph Backup for OpenStack virtual machines@@@Native Ceph Backup enables incremental backups for OpenStack virtual machines that use Ceph-backed Cinder storage, improving backup performance by transferring only changed data blocks...","openstack/openstack_glance_image_details.html@@@OpenStack Glance image details@@@The OpenStack Glance image details page displays the protection status, configuration, and snapshot history for a specific Glance image...","openstack/openstack_glance_image_protection.html@@@OpenStack Glance image protection@@@RSC protects the Glance images that OpenStack virtual machines use as boot disks to reliably recover virtual machines even when the original image is no longer available in Glance...","openstack/openstack_minimum_rbac_permissions.html@@@Configuring minimum RBAC permissions for OpenStack@@@Configure the Rubrik integration to use a non-admin OpenStack service account by creating a custom role that grants only the permissions that Rubrik requires...","openstack/openstack_virtual_machines.html@@@OpenStack virtual machines@@@RSC provides data management, SLA Domain protection, and recovery for OpenStack virtual machines and Glance images...","openstack/openstack_vm_management.html@@@OpenStack virtual machine management@@@You can use RSC to onboard, refresh, edit, monitor, and remove OpenStack virtual machines...","openstack/openstack_vm_onboarding_prerequisites.html@@@OpenStack virtual machine onboarding prerequisites@@@Before protecting OpenStack virtual machines with RSC, ensure your environment meets the following requirements...","openstack/protecting_openstack_glance_images.html@@@Protecting OpenStack Glance images@@@Assign an SLA Domain to one or more OpenStack Glance images so that RSC automates snapshots and retention of the boot images used by your virtual machines...","openstack/recover_openstack_vm_glance_image.html@@@Recovering a Glance-backed OpenStack virtual machine@@@Recover an OpenStack virtual machine launched from a Glance image, choosing whether to reuse the original boot image or substitute a different protected Glance image...","openstack/recover_openstack_vms.html@@@OpenStack virtual machine recovery@@@You can recover files, folders, and virtual machines from point-in-time snapshots of OpenStack virtual machines...","openstack/recovering_files_folders.html@@@Recovering files and folders from OpenStack virtual machines@@@Recover files or folders from an OpenStack virtual machine or region snapshot...","openstack/refreshing_openstack_environments.html@@@Refreshing OpenStack environments@@@Refresh OpenStack environments to display the current settings...","openstack/removing_openstack_environments.html@@@Removing OpenStack environments@@@Remove an OpenStack environment from RSC when you no longer need it...","openstack/setup_protection_openstack_vms.html@@@Set up protection for OpenStack virtual machines@@@RSC provides SLA Domain and on-demand snapshot protection for OpenStack virtual machines and regions...","openstack/taking_ods_openstack.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot for OpenStack@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of an OpenStack virtual machine or region to create an immediate recovery point...","openstack/taking_ods_openstack_glance_image.html@@@Taking a snapshot of an OpenStack Glance image@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of an OpenStack Glance image to capture an immediate recovery point for the boot image, independent of the SLA Domain schedule...","openstack/viewing_openstack_glance_images.html@@@Viewing OpenStack Glance images@@@View the Glance images available in your onboarded OpenStack environments to assess their protection status and locate images for snapshot or recovery operations...","oracle/about_db_clones.html@@@Database clones for Oracle@@@You can clone an Oracle database to a target location by selecting a recovery point...","oracle/adding_oracle_db.html@@@Adding an Oracle database@@@Add an Oracle host to the Rubrik cluster to permit discovery of the databases on that host...","oracle/adding_oracle_host_cdm_93.html@@@Adding an Oracle host for CDM version 9.3@@@Add an Oracle host to a Rubrik cluster using CDM version 9.3 to permit database discovery and protection on that Oracle host...","oracle/adding_oracle_host_cloud_cluster.html@@@Adding an Oracle host to a Rubrik cluster@@@Add an Oracle host to a Rubrik cluster to enable discovery of the databases on that host...","oracle/adv_settings_oracle_clone_recovery.html@@@Advanced settings for Oracle clone recovery@@@Information about advanced settings for an Oracle clone recovery where you can customize the clone operation...","oracle/adv_settings_oracle_live_mount_recovery.html@@@Advanced settings for Oracle Live Mount recovery@@@Information about advanced settings for an Oracle Live Mount recovery where you can customize the Live Mount operation...","oracle/advanced_setting_options.html@@@Advanced setting options@@@Backing up Oracle Data Guard groups includes a number of options for the Advanced Settings...","oracle/applying_oracle_patch_32931941.html@@@Applying Oracle patch 32931941@@@Apply patch 32931941 to Oracle servers to avoid corrupting your Oracle database backups...","oracle/archived_log_deletion_retry.html@@@Retry attempts to delete archived logs@@@The Rubrik cluster automatically retries an archived log deletion that fails...","oracle/archived_log_restore.html@@@Archived log restore@@@Archived log restore reinstates archived logs from a specified time range or SCN range...","oracle/assigning_protection_oracle_workloads.html@@@Assigning protection to Oracle workloads@@@Protect Oracle databases and logs by assigning SLA Domains to Oracle hosts and Oracle RAC systems. The assigned SLA Domain schedules regular backups of the protected databases and their associated logs...","oracle/assigning_sla_domain.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to a host or database@@@Manage and protect discovered Oracle databases with assigned SLA Domains...","oracle/backing_up_databases.html@@@Backing up databases@@@To protect your data, back up the Oracle databases on a Rubrik cluster by using an incremental RMAN merge...","oracle/backups_archived_logs.html@@@Backups and archived logs@@@RSC protects Oracle databases using database snapshots and archived log backups, which run as separate jobs at different frequencies...","oracle/bigfile_tablespace_restore_for_orcl_dbs.html@@@Bigfile tablespace restore for Oracle databases@@@The Rubrik cluster supports restoring Oracle databases that are configured for bigfile tablespaces, which create very large data or temporary files...","oracle/clone_lm_recovery_customization.html@@@Clone and Live Mount recovery customization@@@You can customize clone or live mount recoveries by specifying your own initialization parameter values...","oracle/clone_mount_file_loc_params.html@@@Clone and mount file location parameters@@@You can use file location parameters to account for differences in storage structures between the source and target hosts or Oracle RAC...","oracle/clone_mount_memory_params.html@@@Memory parameters@@@You can use memory parameters to account for differences in resource limitations between the source and target hosts or Oracle RAC...","oracle/cloning_databases.html@@@Cloning databases@@@Restore an Oracle database or recover datafiles by cloning a database snapshot...","oracle/cloning_oracle_rac_database_snapshot.html@@@Cloning an Oracle RAC database snapshot@@@Clone an Oracle RAC database snapshot to create a database snapshot that you can use for database recovery or for recovering Oracle datafiles...","oracle/config_arch_log_delet_policy_delay.html@@@Archived log deletion policy delays@@@You can configure how long archived redo logs are retained on the Oracle host after the Rubrik cluster completes its backup by setting a specific retention period or skipping deletion entirely...","oracle/configure_oracle_workloads.html@@@Configure Oracle workloads@@@After setting up Oracle workloads, you can optionally configure data transfer, access control, and security settings to meet the specific requirements of your environment...","oracle/configuring_auth_multinode_rac.html@@@Configuring authentication for multi-node backup@@@Set up Oracle SEPS wallet credentials to enable passwordless authentication among the participating Oracle RAC nodes during a multi-node backup...","oracle/configuring_multinode_rac_backup.html@@@Configuring multi-node backup for an Oracle RAC database@@@Increase the speed of database backups by distributing the processing across multiple nodes in the Oracle RAC...","oracle/configuring_oracle_seps_wallet.html@@@Configuring the Oracle SEPS wallet@@@Configure an Oracle SEPS wallet to discover and back up standalone, Data Guard, and RAC databases, and to manage connections during a switchover or failover event...","oracle/configuring_sens_data_auth_host.html@@@Configuring sensitive data authentication for Oracle hosts@@@Configure an Oracle host to authenticate to an Oracle database with an authenticated RBS user account to perform Data Discovery and Classification...","oracle/create_on_demand_snapshot.html@@@Creating an on-demand snapshot@@@In addition to the policy-based snapshots of a database, you can initiate database snapshots manually and assign an SLA Domain to manage that snapshot...","oracle/create_the_initial_pfile.html@@@Creating the initial pfile@@@Recovering an Oracle database requires creating an initial pfile...","oracle/creating_empty_etc_oratab_file.html@@@Creating an empty oratab file@@@If the Oracle host has no databases running, create an empty /etc/oratab file before installing RBS software so that RBS can discover the host...","oracle/creating_query_user_cdb_databases.html@@@Creating a discovery user account on CDB databases@@@Create an Oracle discovery user account with privileges to query an Oracle container database (CDB) instead of the SYSDBA user...","oracle/creating_query_user_non_cdb_databases.html@@@Creating a discovery user account on non-CDB databases@@@Create an Oracle discovery user account with privileges to query an Oracle non-CDB database instead of the SYSDBA user...","oracle/customizing_database_backups.html@@@Customizing database backups@@@Define default configuration settings to use during backups of a specific Oracle database or Oracle RAC...","oracle/data_transfer_mechanisms_oracle.html@@@Data transfer mechanisms for Oracle databases@@@The Rubrik cluster uses NFS as the default data transfer mechanism for Oracle databases. You can enable secure thrift for encrypted, authenticated data transfer...","oracle/database_backup_customization.html@@@Database backup customization@@@You can customize the Oracle database backup process to suit your datafile sizes and rates of change by controlling the number of RMAN channels, multi-section backup settings, and channel throughput rates...","oracle/db_clone_prereqs.html@@@Database clone prerequisites@@@Information about prerequisites for cloning an Oracle database...","oracle/determine_the_rman_channels.html@@@Determine the RMAN channels@@@The number of RMAN Channels is set, by default, to 4 or the number of nodes in the Rubrik cluster, whichever is smaller...","oracle/determining_current_db_checkpoint.html@@@Determining the current database checkpoint@@@Use Rubrik REST APIs to determine the current checkpoint of the database from which you export the logs to a USB device attached to a Rubrik cluster node...","oracle/displaying_details_db_log_export_job.html@@@Displaying details of the database log export job@@@Use Rubrik REST APIs to view the details of a job to export the database log...","oracle/dnfs_support.html@@@Direct NFS support@@@Rubrik CDM supports dNFS-enabled Oracle systems. Using dNFS-enabled Oracle databases requires granting the discovery user specific privileges and applying the required Oracle patches for your database version...","oracle/downloading_archived_oracle_db_snapshot.html@@@Downloading an archived Oracle database snapshot@@@Recover an Oracle database snapshot that is no longer stored on the local cluster but remains available in an archival location...","oracle/dropping_rac_db.html@@@Dropping a database@@@Before performing an instant recovery, drop the Oracle RAC or standalone Oracle database...","oracle/dropping_tablespace.html@@@Dropping a tablespace@@@Before performing a recovery of a tablespace, drop the existing tablespace from the database...","oracle/enabling_secure_thrift_using_gql.html@@@Enabling secure thrift using Rubrik GraphQL APIs@@@To securely transfer data between the Rubrik cluster and the Oracle host, enable the secure thrift data transfer mechanism for Oracle databases using Rubrik GraphQL APIs...","oracle/enabling_secure_thrift_using_rest_apis.html@@@Enabling secure thrift using REST APIs@@@To securely transfer data between the Rubrik cluster and the Oracle host, enable the secure thrift data transfer mechanism for Oracle databases using Rubrik REST APIs...","oracle/example_initialization_parameters.html@@@Example of initialization parameters for customization@@@This example text file shows initialization parameters that you can specify to customize the clone or live mount recovery of an Oracle database...","oracle/export_database_logs_usb.html@@@Export Oracle database logs to a USB device@@@You can use Rubrik REST APIs to export logs from multiple Oracle databases to USB devices...","oracle/exporting_oracle_database_logs_usb.html@@@Exporting Oracle database logs to a USB device@@@Use Rubrik REST APIs to export Oracle database logs to a USB device attached to a Rubrik cluster node...","oracle/failed_clones.html@@@Failed clones management@@@Instances created by a failed Oracle Clone task automatically shut down. To ensure data integrity, you must remove any files, directories, control files, and database entries placed during the failed task...","oracle/files_required_for_file_only_lm_recovery.html@@@Files required for a files-only live mount recovery@@@Files required for a files-only live mount recovery include the virtual machine configuration file, virtual disk files, and any associated snapshot files...","oracle/ibm_gpfs_support.html@@@IBM GPFS support@@@RSC supports Oracle databases running on IBM GPFS, but these databases have specific limitations and recovery parameter requirements to review before configuring protection...","oracle/installing_rbs_oracle_hosts.html@@@Installing RBS on Oracle hosts@@@Download and install RBS on Oracle hosts...","oracle/live_mount_and_clone_for_pluggable_databases.html@@@Live Mount and clone operations on PDBs@@@Live Mount and clone operations on a subset of pluggable databases behave differently in terms of performance and failure conditions. Review these behaviors before choosing which operation to perform...","oracle/live_mount_prerequisites.html@@@Live Mount prerequisites@@@Information about the requirements you must meet before you can Live Mount an Oracle database...","oracle/live_mount_snapshot_chain_consol.html@@@Oracle Live Mount and snapshot chain consolidation@@@Live-mounted databases can delay snapshot chain consolidation and space reclamation as you cannot remove expired snapshots until the database is unmounted...","oracle/lm_oracle_db_using_oracle_scn.html@@@Live Mounting an Oracle database using an Oracle SCN@@@Recover Oracle snapshots using the system change number instead of the date and time the snapshot occurs, providing a more accurate point of recovery...","oracle/manage_oracle_databases.html@@@Manage Oracle databases@@@You can refresh Oracle hosts or RACs to discover new databases, or remove hosts and RACs from RSC...","oracle/manage_oracledbs.html@@@Oracle database management@@@Manage discovered Oracle hosts and Oracle RAC systems from the Rubrik CDM Oracle DBs page...","oracle/migrating_managed_volumes.html@@@Migrating from Managed Volumes to native Rubrik protection@@@Migrate Oracle databases from Managed Volume-based protection to RSC for automated protection...","oracle/mounting_db_backup_using_livemount.html@@@Mounting a database backup using Oracle Live Mount@@@Use Oracle Live Mount to create a database from a point-in-time copy of a source Oracle database...","oracle/mounting_oracle_database_backup.html@@@Mounting an Oracle database backup@@@Use Live Mount to mount an Oracle database snapshot directly to an Oracle host for immediate access without a full restore...","oracle/mounting_oracle_rac_database_backup.html@@@Mounting an Oracle RAC database backup@@@Use Live Mount to mount an Oracle RAC database snapshot directly to an Oracle host for immediate access without a full restore...","oracle/multinode_rac_backup.html@@@Multi-node backup for Oracle RAC databases@@@Multi-node backup distributes RMAN backup channels across multiple Oracle RAC nodes, increasing backup throughput by leveraging the combined network bandwidth and processing power of the selected nodes...","oracle/multinode_rac_backup_reqs.html@@@Multi-node RAC backup requirements and limitations@@@Supported configurations, prerequisites, and limitations for Oracle RAC multi-node backup...","oracle/number_of_channels_in_recovery.html@@@Number of channels in recovery@@@The number of RMAN channels RMAN uses during a recovery controls the number of concurrent streams that can process data...","oracle/optional_fields_for_oracle_databases.html@@@Optional fields for Oracle databases@@@Backing up an Oracle database and assigning an SLA Domain to a host or database includes a number of optional fields...","oracle/oracle_26ai_database_protection.html@@@Oracle 26ai database recovery@@@RSC supports protection of Oracle 26ai and Oracle 23ai databases running on Oracle Exadata on-premises. The following known issues might affect recovery operations...","oracle/oracle_acfs_support.html@@@Oracle ACFS support@@@RSC supports Oracle databases running on Oracle ACFS, but these databases have specific limitations and recovery parameter requirements that you must consider before configuring protection...","oracle/oracle_backup_immutability.html@@@Oracle backup immutability@@@When you archive Oracle backup data to an archival location with an immutability policy, RSC automatically protects Oracle database snapshot and log backup files with object-level locks that prevent deletion for the duration of the retention period...","oracle/oracle_data_guard_database_conversion.html@@@Oracle Data Guard database conversion@@@Converting a standard, non-Data Guard database to a Data Guard database, or vice versa, requires that you assign an SLA Domain to protect the converted database...","oracle/oracle_data_guard_group_backups.html@@@Oracle Data Guard group backups@@@During an Oracle Data Guard group backup, RMAN reads the previous snapshot and aggregates the changes to form a new snapshot backup. Archivelog deletion policies and standby log switch configuration affect how the Rubrik cluster manages logs during backup...","oracle/oracle_data_guard_live_mount.html@@@Oracle Data Guard Live Mount@@@Live Mount for Oracle Data Guard creates a primary database from a point-in-time copy stored on the Rubrik cluster, with only the datafiles migrated to the target host...","oracle/oracle_data_guard_rubrik_clusters.html@@@Oracle Data Guard on Rubrik clusters@@@Rubrik clusters support Oracle Data Guard configurations to back up primary and standby databases and to discover Data Guard groups...","oracle/oracle_data_guard_tablespace_recovery.html@@@Oracle Data Guard group tablespace point-in-time recovery@@@The primary database in the Data Guard group triggers tablespace point-in-time recovery operations...","oracle/oracle_databases_cdm.html@@@Oracle databases on the Rubrik cluster@@@You can use the Rubrik cluster to back up, archive, replicate, and recover Oracle databases...","oracle/oracle_databases_rsc.html@@@Oracle databases@@@RSC provides data management and protection for Oracle databases across on-premises and supported public cloud deployments...","oracle/oracle_exacs_database_protection.html@@@Oracle ExaCS database recovery@@@RSC supports protection of Oracle Exadata Cloud Service databases. The following known issues might affect recovery operations...","oracle/oracle_exadata_exascale_db_protection.html@@@Oracle Exadata Exascale database recovery@@@RSC supports recovery of Oracle Exadata Exascale databases. The following known issues might affect recovery operations...","oracle/oracle_initialization_parameters.html@@@Oracle initialization parameters@@@Information about required or recommended initialization parameters to specify when you customize an Oracle database instance that is created during a recovery...","oracle/oracle_instant_recovery.html@@@Instant Recovery for Oracle@@@Instant Recovery for Oracle replaces an existing database with a point-in-time copy, requiring specific configurations and directory setup...","oracle/oracle_live_mount.html@@@Oracle Live Mount@@@An Oracle Live Mount creates a database from a point-in-time copy of the source database to reduce the recovery time...","oracle/oracle_on_windows_feature_support.html@@@Oracle on Windows feature support@@@Information about feature support for Oracle on Windows...","oracle/oracle_pluggable_databases.html@@@Oracle pluggable databases@@@RSC supports granular pluggable database-level recovery for Oracle container databases, including restore, Live Mount, and clone operations...","oracle/oracle_query_user_account.html@@@Oracle discovery user account@@@An Oracle discovery user account has privileges to query Oracle databases, as an alternative to using a SYSDBA account...","oracle/oracle_recovery_using_scns.html@@@Oracle recovery using SCNs@@@You can recover Oracle snapshots and mount archive logs using the system change number instead of the date and time when the snapshot occurs, providing a more accurate point of recovery...","oracle/oracle_seps_wallet.html@@@Oracle SEPS wallet@@@The Oracle Secure External Password Store wallet stores database connection credentials in a client-side wallet, preventing credentials from being exposed on the command line during database discovery and backup operations...","oracle/oracle_tde_databases.html@@@Oracle TDE databases@@@Rubrik clusters support backups for Oracle databases that use Transparent Data Encryption to secure data at rest...","oracle/oracle_vers_11g_lm_lmtns.html@@@Oracle version 11g Live Mount limitations@@@Due to a limitation in Oracle version 11g, RSC issues an error when you perform a Live Mount with Rename...","oracle/pausing_resuming_protection_oracle.html@@@Pausing and resuming protection for Oracle databases@@@Pause scheduled backup, archival, and replication actions for a specific database workload without affecting the protection of other objects managed by the SLA Domain...","oracle/pdb_restore_restrictions.html@@@Pluggable database restore restrictions@@@The Rubrik cluster includes several restrictions for restoring an Oracle pluggable database...","oracle/perform_same_host_recovery.html@@@Performing a Same Host recovery@@@Recover a database from a snapshot back to the production host...","oracle/performing_ir_oracle_scn.html@@@Performing an Instant Recovery using an Oracle SCN@@@Use Instant Recovery to replace a database with a point-in-time copy using an Oracle SCN...","oracle/performing_same_host_recovery_oracle_scn.html@@@Performing a Same Host recovery using an Oracle SCN@@@Use a snapshot to recover a database to the production host using an Oracle SCN...","oracle/plan_oracle_workload_protection.html@@@Plan Oracle workload protection@@@Before setting up Oracle database protection, review the prerequisites and security considerations, and configure user access in RSC...","oracle/point-in-time_recovery.html@@@Point-in-time recovery@@@Point-in-time recovery uses database snapshots and their associated logs to restore a database to its state at a specific point in time...","oracle/policies_for_archived_log_deletion.html@@@Policies for archived log deletion@@@The Rubrik cluster can delete archived redo logs immediately, after a specified period, or retain them indefinitely, depending on the configured policy...","oracle/policy_managed_database_recovery.html@@@Policy-managed database recovery@@@RSC protects both policy-managed databases and admin-managed databases...","oracle/prerequisites_for_same_host_recovery.html@@@Prerequisites for Same Host recovery@@@Recovering a backup to the source host requires preliminary actions and settings...","oracle/protect_oracle_databases.html@@@Protect Oracle databases@@@RSC provides automated and on-demand methods for protecting Oracle databases...","oracle/rbk_adding_query_user_existing_hosts.html@@@Adding a discovery user to existing hosts@@@Update an existing Oracle host with information on the Oracle discovery user to use the Oracle discovery user instead of the user with SYSDBA privileges...","oracle/rbk_backing_up_data_guard_logs.html@@@Backing up Data Guard logs@@@Create a backup of an archived redo log for an Oracle Data Guard group...","oracle/rbk_backup_oracle_data_guard_groups.html@@@Backing up Oracle Data Guard groups@@@Protect the databases in a Data Guard group by assigning the group to an SLA Domain...","oracle/rbk_changing_retention_for_an_oracle_data_guard_snapshot.html@@@Changing retention for an Oracle Data Guard snapshot@@@Change the retention period for specified Data Guard group snapshots...","oracle/rbk_cloning_data_guard_groups.html@@@Cloning Data Guard groups@@@Clone an Oracle Data Guard group to create a fully functional point-in-time copy of the database on a target Oracle host...","oracle/rbk_cloning_oracle_database_snapshot.html@@@Cloning an Oracle database snapshot@@@Clone an Oracle database snapshot to create a database snapshot that you can use for database recovery or for recovering Oracle datafiles...","oracle/rbk_instantly_recovering_oracle_data_guard_groups.html@@@Instantly recovering Oracle Data Guard groups@@@Replace an Oracle Data Guard group with a fully functional point-in-time copy...","oracle/rbk_mounting_archived_logs.html@@@Mounting archived logs@@@Mount archived logs to restore them to a specific time range...","oracle/rbk_mounting_oracle_data_guard_group.html@@@Mounting an Oracle Data Guard group@@@Live Mount an Oracle Data Guard group to create a primary database from a point-in-time copy of a source Data Guard group...","oracle/rbk_performing_a_pdb_restore_on_rsc.html@@@Performing PDB restore on RSC@@@Restore multiple PDBs to the active source container database to recover it to a specific point in time...","oracle/rbk_performing_a_roll_forward_recovery.html@@@Performing a roll forward recovery@@@Complete a roll forward recovery of a database, applying archive logs present on the host...","oracle/rbk_performing_a_same_host_recovery.html@@@Performing a Same Host recovery@@@Use a snapshot to recover a database to the production host...","oracle/rbk_performing_an_instant_recovery.html@@@Performing an Instant Recovery for Oracle during RSC service disruption@@@Use Instant Recovery to replace a database with a point-in-time copy...","oracle/rbk_placing_oracle_data_guard_groups_on_legal_hold.html@@@Placing Oracle Data Guard groups on legal hold@@@Place a Legal Hold on a Data Guard group snapshot to prevent the Rubrik cluster from expiring and removing the snapshot at the end of the assigned retention period...","oracle/rbk_refreshing_oracle_hosts.html@@@Refreshing Oracle hosts or RACs@@@Refresh an Oracle host or RAC so that the Rubrik cluster can discover new Oracle databases and mark removed databases as archived...","oracle/rbk_removing_oracle_hosts_racs.html@@@Removing an Oracle host or RAC@@@Remove an Oracle host or RAC by removing each node in the Oracle system...","oracle/rbk_restoring_an_oracle_data_guard_group.html@@@Restoring an Oracle Data Guard group@@@Restore files from an Oracle Data Guard group using a fully functional point-in-time copy...","oracle/rbk_restoring_tablespaces.html@@@Restoring tablespaces@@@The Rubrik cluster restores tablespaces by exporting them in-place on the same database...","oracle/rbk_reviewing_oracle_data_guard_groups.html@@@Reviewing Oracle Data Guard groups@@@RSC provides details about the Oracle Data Guard groups assigned to Rubrik clusters...","oracle/rbk_taking_on_demand_backups_dg_group.html@@@Taking on-demand backups of Oracle Data Guard groups@@@Initiate an on-demand backup of the databases in an Oracle Data Guard group to provide a point-in-time backup, and assign an SLA Domain to manage the snapshot...","oracle/rbk_unmounting_oracle_live_mount.html@@@Unmounting an Oracle Live Mount on RSC@@@Unmount live mounted Oracle databases and mounted objects from RSC...","oracle/rbk_validating_oracle_data_guard_groups.html@@@Validating Oracle Data Guard groups@@@Validate the data in an Oracle Data Guard snapshot to ensure that the database can be recovered or restored without any corrupt files or missing blocks...","oracle/rbk_validating_oracle_database_snapshots.html@@@Validating Oracle database snapshots@@@Validate the data in an Oracle database snapshot to confirm that there are no corrupt files or missing blocks before you recover or restore the database...","oracle/rbk_viewing_pdbs_protected_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Viewing PDBs protected by Rubrik cluster@@@View a list of the PDBs and determine which are protected by the Rubrik cluster...","oracle/recover_db_after_files_only_live_mount.html@@@Recover databases after a files-only Live Mount@@@Files-only Live Mounts enable DBAs to mount backup images from the Rubrik cluster to an Oracle host or RAC, keeping datafiles on the Rubrik cluster...","oracle/recover_oracle_databases.html@@@Recover Oracle databases@@@Provides a summary of the methods available in RSC for recovering Oracle databases...","oracle/recovering_an_oracle_database.html@@@Recovering an Oracle database@@@Use the Oracle Recovery Manager utility to perform an Oracle database recovery...","oracle/recovering_oracle_database_replica.html@@@Recovering an Oracle database from a replica@@@Recover an Oracle database from a replicated snapshot of the database stored on another Rubrik cluster...","oracle/recovery_chains.html@@@Recovery chains@@@Converting a backed-up database to a different Oracle database format breaks the recovery chain after a host refresh...","oracle/recovery_rac_standalone_oracle_hosts.html@@@Recovery from RAC to standalone Oracle hosts@@@You can use the Live Mount or Clone recovery methods to recover a database snapshot that was originally hosted on an Oracle RAC to an Oracle standalone host...","oracle/recovery_secondary_oracle_host.html@@@Recovery to a secondary Oracle host@@@You can add a secondary Oracle host to a Rubrik cluster to provide more target options for snapshot recovery...","oracle/reqs_oracle_windows_support.html@@@Oracle support requirements on Windows@@@Requirements for protecting Oracle databases on Windows with RSC...","oracle/rest_apis_for_db_export_usb.html@@@REST APIs for database export to USB device@@@REST API parameters for exporting database logs to a USB device...","oracle/restoring_an_oracle_data_guard_group.html@@@Restoring an Oracle Data Guard group@@@Restore files from an Oracle Data Guard group using a fully functional point-in-time copy...","oracle/restoring_archived_logs_manually.html@@@Restoring archived logs manually@@@You can restore archived logs manually after a Log Mount completes...","oracle/reviewing_oracle_data_groups.html@@@Reviewing Oracle Data Guard groups@@@The Rubrik CDM web UI provides details about the Oracle Data Guard groups assigned to Rubrik clusters...","oracle/rsc_user_management_oracle.html@@@RSC user management for Oracle protection@@@You can manage access to Oracle protection tasks in RSC by assigning roles and privileges to user accounts...","oracle/samehost_recover.html@@@Same Host Recovery@@@Recover a database to the source Oracle host or Oracle RAC...","oracle/section_sizes_for_oracle_databases.html@@@Section sizes for Oracle databases@@@You can expedite Oracle database backups by specifying a section size for the database, which enables the Rubrik cluster to divide database datafiles into multiple sections and back them up simultaneously...","oracle/secure_thrift_backup_param.html@@@Secure thrift backup parameter recommendations@@@When you are using secure thrift, Rubrik recommends adding parameters to the SPFILE on your Oracle database to improve performance during backup operations...","oracle/security_considerations.html@@@Security considerations@@@Before setting up Oracle protection, review how RSC interacts with the security mechanisms configured on your Oracle hosts...","oracle/seps_wallet_db_permissions_support.html@@@SEPS wallet database permissions and support@@@Using a SEPS wallet for secure connections requires special permissions and support for Oracle databases...","oracle/setup_oracle.html@@@Set up Oracle workloads@@@You get started with Oracle database protection by installing RBS on each Oracle host and adding each host to the RSC inventory...","oracle/sla_domain_assignments_oracle_objects.html@@@SLA Domain assignments for Oracle objects@@@Assigning an SLA Domain activates automated protection for your Oracle databases. Direct or inherited SLA Domain assignment enables policy-driven management of database backups...","oracle/specification_table_oracle_db_unmounts.html@@@Specifications for Oracle database unmounts@@@Describes the behavior for database file locations when an Oracle database shuts down during an unmount operation...","oracle/sys_reqs_oracle_dbs.html@@@System requirements for Oracle databases@@@Information about the system requirements for protecting Oracle databases with the Rubrik cluster...","oracle/tablespace_recovery.html@@@Tablespace recovery@@@Restore a tablespace in place to the same database...","oracle/taking_on_demand_database_backups.html@@@Taking on-demand database backups@@@Manually initiate a database snapshot in addition to policy-based snapshots, and assign an SLA Domain to manage the on-demand snapshot...","oracle/taking_on_demand_log_backups.html@@@Taking on-demand log backups@@@Create an archived redo log backup of a database...","oracle/taking_on_demand_snapshot_oracle_data_guard_group.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of an Oracle Data Guard group@@@Manually initiate a snapshot of the databases in a Data Guard group. Assign an SLA Domain to manage that snapshot...","oracle/unmounting_oracle_live_mount.html@@@Unmounting an Oracle Live Mount@@@You can unmount live mounted Oracle databases and mounted objects from the Rubrik cluster after datafiles have been migrated back to the host...","oracle/validating_data_oracle_database_snapshot.html@@@Validating the data in an Oracle database snapshot@@@To ensure that an Oracle database can be recovered or restored, validate the data in the Oracle database snapshot so that there are no corrupt files or missing blocks...","oracle/validating_db_snapshot_using_oracle_scn.html@@@Validating a database snapshot using an Oracle SCN@@@To ensure that an Oracle database can be recovered or restored, you can validate the data in the Oracle database snapshot using an Oracle SCN to verify that there are no corrupt files or missing blocks...","oracle/verifying_cluster_okv_configuration.html@@@Verifying the cluster OKV configuration@@@After you have added OKV-managed databases to the Rubrik cluster, verify the OKV is correctly configured for the Rubrik cluster and the TDE databases...","oracle/verifying_oracle_user_account.html@@@Verifying the Oracle discovery user account@@@Check the permissions of the Oracle discovery user account to ensure that the Rubrik cluster can fully discover Oracle databases...","oracle/verifying_the_live_mount_post_recovery.html@@@Verifying the live mount using SQLPLUS@@@Use the SQLPLUS tool to verify a live mount after recovering an Oracle database...","ports/additional_network_requirement.html@@@Additional network requirements@@@To provide IPMI management information, Rubrik nodes must be able to receive packets sent from a local ping program...","ports/aws_ports.html@@@AWS ports@@@The Rubrik cluster requires the following ports to be configured for AWS virtual machines...","ports/hotadd_proxy_port_requirements.html@@@HotAdd proxy port requirements@@@A Rubrik Cloud Cluster requires access to several TCP ports in order to protect virtual machines in a cloud-based environment...","ports/hotadd_proxy_port_requirements_2.html@@@HotAdd proxy port requirements@@@A Rubrik Cloud Cluster requires access to several TCP ports in order to protect virtual machines in a cloud-based environment...","ports/hotadd_proxy_port_requirements_3.html@@@HotAdd proxy port requirements@@@A Rubrik Cloud Cluster requires access to several TCP ports in order to protect virtual machines in a cloud-based environment...","ports/hotadd_proxy_port_requirements_4.html@@@HotAdd proxy port requirements@@@A Rubrik Cloud Cluster requires access to several TCP ports in order to protect virtual machines in a cloud-based environment...","ports/ports_comm_btwn_cluster_nodes.html@@@Communication between nodes in a cluster@@@Rubrik clusters require specific ports for internode communication...","ports/rubrik_port_specifications.html@@@Rubrik port specifications@@@Rubrik clusters require specific ports and protocols for internode communication, external services, and workload integrations...","ports/uses_for_secure_port_443_tcp.html@@@Uses for secure port 443 TCP@@@Each Rubrik cluster requires that you open an outbound connection through TCP port 443 for secure transmission while accessing specific sites...","postgresql/adding_host_postgresql.html@@@Adding a host for PostgreSQL@@@To establish a connection between the PostgreSQL cluster and RSC, add a host for performing backup and recovery operations...","postgresql/adding_postgresql_cluster.html@@@Adding a PostgreSQL cluster@@@Add a PostgreSQL cluster to establish a connection with the Rubrik cluster with the required configuration details...","postgresql/adding_postgresql_ha_cluster_group.html@@@Adding an HA cluster group@@@Add a primary PostgreSQL cluster and its standby clusters to RSC as a single HA cluster group...","postgresql/assigning_sla_postgresql_ha_group.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to an HA group@@@Assign an SLA Domain to a PostgreSQL HA cluster group, and select the backup source for the HA cluster group...","postgresql/changing_retention_policy_postgresql.html@@@Changing the retention policy of PostgreSQL snapshots@@@To optimize data accessibility, change the retention policy of a PostgreSQL snapshot...","postgresql/creating_restore_mp_postgresql.html@@@Creating a restore mount point for a PostgreSQL cluster@@@To recover a PostgreSQL cluster, create a restore mount point by mounting a snapshot of backup data to the mount point using NFS and then performing the recovery instructions...","postgresql/deleting_postgresql_cluster.html@@@Deleting a PostgreSQL cluster@@@To remove a PostgreSQL cluster that is no longer required, delete the PostgreSQL cluster from the Rubrik cluster...","postgresql/deleting_postgresql_ha_cluster_group.html@@@Deleting an HA cluster group@@@Delete a PostgreSQL HA cluster group from RSC...","postgresql/editing_postgresql_cluster.html@@@Editing a PostgreSQL cluster@@@To modify a PostgreSQL cluster, edit the PostgreSQL cluster settings...","postgresql/editing_postgresql_ha_cluster_group.html@@@Editing an HA cluster group@@@Edit the details of a PostgreSQL HA cluster group, such as the HA group name, the primary cluster, or the standby clusters...","postgresql/ha_postgres_cluster.html@@@Configure High Availability for a PostgreSQL cluster@@@High Availability for PostgreSQL clusters protects a primary and standby cluster setup and maintains backup continuity when a failover promotes a standby cluster to the primary role...","postgresql/managing_protection_postgresql_cluster.html@@@Managing protection for a PostgreSQL cluster@@@To protect your PostgreSQL clusters, manage protection by assigning data protection policies...","postgresql/multiple_archival_locations_postgresql.html@@@Multiple archival locations for PostgreSQL@@@You can configure multiple archival policies within a single SLA Domain to automate the delivery of snapshots and log data to distinct cloud storage targets...","postgresql/postgres_downloading_archived_snapshots.html@@@Downloading archived PostgreSQL snapshots@@@Download a PostgreSQL snapshot from an archival location to a Rubrik cluster when the snapshot is not available in local storage...","postgresql/postgres_downloading_replicated_snapshot.html@@@Downloading replicated PostgreSQL snapshots@@@Download replicated snapshots of a PostgreSQL cluster to local storage on the source cluster for recovery...","postgresql/postgres_legal_hold_snapshots.html@@@Legal hold for PostgreSQL snapshots@@@Legal hold ensures that snapshots required for litigation are protected for the duration of the legal hold, providing a compliant and efficient way to manage data subject to legal obligations...","postgresql/postgresql.html@@@PostgreSQL@@@Rubrik Security Cloud protects your PostgreSQL cluster by simplifying complex backup and recovery processes, discovering the databases automatically, and protecting data using SLA Domains...","postgresql/postgresql_archiving_snapshots.html@@@Archiving for PostgreSQL snapshots@@@You can include an archival policy in an SLA Domain to archive PostgreSQL snapshots to an archival location for long-term retention...","postgresql/postgresql_automated_recovery.html@@@PostgreSQL automated recovery@@@PostgreSQL automated recovery enables you to recover PostgreSQL clusters on RSC from Rubrik CDM versions 9.4.1 and later without requiring manual steps...","postgresql/postgresql_cloning_sla_domain.html@@@Cloning PostgreSQL SLA Domains@@@Clone an existing SLA Domain to save time by avoiding having to create and configure a new SLA Domain. You can customize the cloned SLA Domain according to your requirement...","postgresql/postgresql_cluster_configuration.html@@@Configure PostgreSQL clusters@@@Configuring a PostgreSQL cluster involves registering the Linux servers with a Rubrik cluster, installing RBS, and then manually adding each PostgreSQL cluster to RSC with the required configuration details and credentials...","postgresql/postgresql_common_protection_terms.html@@@Common PostgreSQL protection terms@@@It is important to understand some common terms when protecting PostgreSQL clusters with RSC...","postgresql/postgresql_creating_custom_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for PostgreSQL@@@Create a role with RBAC privileges for managing PostgreSQL databases. These privileges provide granularity for determining which permissions an RSC user has for performing specific actions on specific objects...","postgresql/postgresql_creating_custom_sla_domain.html@@@Creating custom SLA Domains for PostgreSQL@@@Create a custom SLA Domain for PostgreSQL to streamline and customize protection and recovery plans for PostgreSQL clusters...","postgresql/postgresql_deleting_sla_domain.html@@@Deleting PostgreSQL SLA Domains@@@Delete an SLA Domain created for PostgreSQL when it is no longer needed...","postgresql/postgresql_deleting_snapshots.html@@@Deleting PostgreSQL snapshots@@@Delete PostgreSQL snapshots that are no longer required for data protection...","postgresql/postgresql_editing_sla_domain.html@@@Editing PostgreSQL SLA Domains@@@Edit an SLA Domain to change the backup and recovery objectives of the associated PostgreSQL clusters...","postgresql/postgresql_eval_auth_options.html@@@Evaluate PostgreSQL authentication options@@@When adding a PostgreSQL cluster to RSC, it is important to evaluate the available socket-based method for a PostgreSQL client to verify its identity with the server...","postgresql/postgresql_evaluate_sla_domain_options.html@@@Evaluate PostgreSQL SLA Domain options@@@Before creating an SLA Domain for a PostgreSQL workload, you can evaluate various protection options that RSC provides for PostgreSQL clusters...","postgresql/postgresql_ha_cluster_group_considerations.html@@@Considerations for HA cluster groups@@@Review the following considerations before configuring a PostgreSQL High Availability (HA) cluster group in RSC...","postgresql/postgresql_ha_split_brain.html@@@Split-brain in an HA cluster group@@@A split-brain scenario occurs when RSC detects more than one primary cluster in a PostgreSQL HA cluster group...","postgresql/postgresql_high_level_architecture.html@@@High-level architecture for PostgreSQL protection@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects your PostgreSQL databases...","postgresql/postgresql_log_snapshot_visibility.html@@@PostgreSQL log snapshot visibility@@@When you perform point-in-time recovery of a PostgreSQL cluster, you can view log snapshots that cover a recovery point on the snapshot calendar and in the recovery details...","postgresql/postgresql_manage_protection.html@@@Manage PostgreSQL protection@@@After you set up PostgreSQL protection in RSC, you can configure SLA Domains, assign protection to PostgreSQL clusters, and manage the lifecycle of PostgreSQL snapshots...","postgresql/postgresql_manage_snapshots.html@@@Manage PostgreSQL snapshots@@@You can manage the lifecycle of PostgreSQL snapshots by taking on-demand snapshots, changing retention policies, deleting snapshots, applying legal hold, and pausing or resuming protection for individual clusters...","postgresql/postgresql_obj_level_pause_resume.html@@@Object-level pause and resume for PostgreSQL@@@You can temporarily pause and resume protection for individual PostgreSQL clusters without affecting the protection of other clusters managed by the same SLA Domain...","postgresql/postgresql_placing_snapshots_legal_hold.html@@@Placing PostgreSQL snapshots on legal hold@@@Placing a legal hold on a PostgreSQL snapshot indefinitely retains that snapshot regardless of the assigned SLA Domain retention policy...","postgresql/postgresql_planning_protection.html@@@Plan your PostgreSQL protection@@@Before setting up a PostgreSQL cluster in RSC, it is necessary to plan user and access management for designated RSC users...","postgresql/postgresql_primary_snapshot_retention.html@@@Primary snapshot retention for PostgreSQL@@@Primary snapshot retention for PostgreSQL clusters provides data protection and recovery by setting snapshot retention policies for various periods, including hourly, daily, monthly, and yearly retention to meet compliance, business continuity, and disaster recovery requirements...","postgresql/postgresql_protection_config.html@@@Configure PostgreSQL protection@@@Implementing a data protection strategy using SLA Domains ensures the resilience and availability of PostgreSQL clusters...","postgresql/postgresql_protection_key_features.html@@@Key features for PostgreSQL protection@@@RSC provides unified data management, automated global data protection, backup and recovery options for PostgreSQL clusters, and advanced security features to protect critical data...","postgresql/postgresql_protection_limitations.html@@@PostgreSQL protection limitations@@@PostgreSQL clusters are subject to certain protection limitations...","postgresql/postgresql_protection_prereq.html@@@PostgreSQL protection prerequisites@@@Information about the specific prerequisites that RSC requires for protecting PostgreSQL clusters...","postgresql/postgresql_protection_setup.html@@@Set up PostgreSQL protection@@@You can protect PostgreSQL clusters using automated, policy-driven backups, ensuring data resilience and compliance with organizational standards...","postgresql/postgresql_protection_workflow.html@@@PostgreSQL protection implementation workflow@@@Describes the workflow for implementing PostgreSQL protection with RSC, from planning through recovery...","postgresql/postgresql_quick_links.html@@@Quick links for PostgreSQL@@@Immediate access to important tasks and information, enabling quick setup, daily operations, and critical recovery...","postgresql/postgresql_rbk_cloud_cluster_elastic_storage.html@@@Rubrik cloud cluster elastic storage for PostgreSQL@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage is a cloud-native Rubrik deployment model that protects PostgreSQL workloads running on virtual instances within a Virtual Private Cloud in public cloud environments...","postgresql/postgresql_recovery.html@@@Recover PostgreSQL@@@After RSC takes snapshots of your PostgreSQL workloads, you can recover the required workloads using different recovery options...","postgresql/postgresql_recovery_options.html@@@PostgreSQL recovery options@@@RSC provides flexible options for PostgreSQL cluster recovery from secure, immutable backups...","postgresql/postgresql_removing_legal_hold_snapshots.html@@@Removing legal hold from PostgreSQL snapshots@@@Remove legal hold from a PostgreSQL snapshot to return the snapshot to normal retention management...","postgresql/postgresql_replication.html@@@Replication for PostgreSQL snapshots@@@You can use the SLA Domain replication policy to replicate PostgreSQL snapshots from one Rubrik cluster to another for disaster recovery...","postgresql/postgresql_required_perms.html@@@Required permissions for PostgreSQL protection@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to protect your PostgreSQL clusters...","postgresql/postgresql_retention_lock_sla_domain.html@@@Retention lock for PostgreSQL SLA Domains@@@A retention lock on an RSC SLA Domain is a security feature that prevents premature deletion of PostgreSQL snapshots...","postgresql/postgresql_rsc_user_management.html@@@RSC user management for PostgreSQL protection@@@Designating specific users with appropriate privileges and roles in RSC enhances security for protecting your PostgreSQL databases...","postgresql/postgresql_setup.html@@@Set up PostgreSQL clusters@@@You can protect PostgreSQL clusters using RSC by configuring PostgreSQL hosts that run them. This setup automates backups and enables rapid recovery from ransomware threats, providing unified data security and resilience for your PostgreSQL databases...","postgresql/postgresql_syncing_sla_domain_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Synchronizing SLA Domains with a Rubrik cluster@@@Synchronize an SLA Domain with a Rubrik cluster to take on-demand snapshots and to maintain data protection during ransomware recovery...","postgresql/postgresql_user_notes.html@@@User notes for PostgreSQL@@@You can add user notes to explain the reason behind performing a specific task, ensuring comprehensive audit tracking for your PostgreSQL environment...","postgresql/recover_postgresql_ha_clusters.html@@@Recover PostgreSQL HA clusters@@@RSC provides recovery options for a PostgreSQL HA cluster group based on the scope of recovery and the target location...","postgresql/recovering_postgresql_clstr_alt_loc.html@@@Recovering a PostgreSQL cluster to an alternate location@@@After you have created a recovery point for the PostgreSQL cluster, recover the cluster automatically to an alternate location...","postgresql/recovering_postgresql_clstr_orig_state.html@@@Recovering a PostgreSQL cluster to its original state@@@After you have created a recovery point for the PostgreSQL cluster, recover the cluster automatically to its original in-place state...","postgresql/recovering_postgresql_cluster.html@@@Recovering a PostgreSQL cluster@@@After you have created a mount point for the PostgreSQL cluster, recover the cluster manually by following the recovery instructions...","postgresql/recovering_postgresql_entire_cluster_ha_grp_org_loc.html@@@Recovering an entire HA cluster group to the original location@@@Recover all clusters in a PostgreSQL HA cluster group to the original location...","postgresql/recovering_postgresql_ha_cluster_org_loc.html@@@Recovering a PostgreSQL HA cluster to the original location@@@Recover a single cluster in a PostgreSQL HA cluster group to the original location, and set the cluster role to its current role or to read-only after recovery...","postgresql/recovering_postgresql_ha_target_cluster_alt_loc.html@@@Recovering a PostgreSQL HA target cluster to an alternate location@@@Recover a single cluster in a PostgreSQL HA cluster group to an alternate location outside the HA cluster group...","postgresql/refreshing_postgresql_cluster.html@@@Refreshing a PostgreSQL cluster@@@To ensure that the PostgreSQL cluster information is up to date, refresh the PostgreSQL cluster...","postgresql/refreshing_postgresql_ha_cluster_group.html@@@Refreshing an HA cluster group@@@Refresh a PostgreSQL HA cluster group so that RSC re-verifies the primary and standby cluster roles...","postgresql/taking_ods_postgresql_cluster.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of PostgreSQL clusters@@@To protect critical data for immediate recovery and enhance overall snapshot security, take an on-demand snapshot of a PostgreSQL cluster...","postgresql/taking_ods_postgresql_ha_group.html@@@Taking an on-demand HA group snapshot@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of a PostgreSQL HA cluster group outside the schedule of the assigned SLA Domain...","postgresql/unmounting_restore_mount_point_postgresql_cluster.html@@@Unmounting restore mount point after PostgreSQL cluster recovery@@@After recovering a PostgreSQL cluster, unmount it to remove the metadata associated with the selected PostgreSQL cluster...","postgresql/viewing_postgresql_recovery_details.html@@@Viewing PostgreSQL recovery details@@@View the data snapshots and any log snapshots that RSC requires to recover a PostgreSQL cluster to a selected recovery point...","postgresql/wal_file_retention_postgresql_host.html@@@WAL file retention on PostgreSQL host@@@Write-Ahead Log (WAL) file retention enables you to retain local WAL files on a PostgreSQL host for a specific duration after backup, providing faster access to local logs directly on the host for local recovery requirements...","proxmox/adding_proxmox_environment.html@@@Adding a Proxmox environment to RSC@@@Add a Proxmox Virtual Environment to RSC to enable protection of Proxmox virtual machines...","proxmox/adding_proxmox_hosts_manual_rbs_install.html@@@Adding Proxmox hosts with manual RBS installation@@@Add Proxmox hosts to your RSC inventory to protect your Proxmox environment using manual Rubrik Backup Service installation...","proxmox/adding_proxmox_hosts_remote_rbs_install.html@@@Adding Proxmox hosts with remote RBS installation@@@Add Proxmox hosts to your RSC inventory to protect your Proxmox environment using remote Rubrik Backup Service installation...","proxmox/assigning_sla_domain_proxmox_clusters.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to Proxmox clusters@@@Assign an SLA Domain to protect a Proxmox cluster and define its backup frequency and their retention policies...","proxmox/assigning_sla_domain_proxmox_nodes.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to Proxmox nodes@@@Assign an SLA Domain to protect Proxmox nodes and define their backup frequency and retention policies...","proxmox/assigning_sla_domain_proxmox_vms.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to Proxmox virtual machines@@@Assign an SLA Domain to protect Proxmox virtual machines and define their backup frequency and their retention policies...","proxmox/downloading_proxmox_vm_snapshot.html@@@Downloading folders or files from a Proxmox snapshot@@@Recover individual folders or files from a Proxmox virtual machine by downloading them from a point-in-time snapshot...","proxmox/editing_proxmox_environment.html@@@Editing a Proxmox environment@@@You can edit the connection and authentication details for a Proxmox Virtual Environment registered in RSC...","proxmox/exporting_proxmox_vm_snapshot.html@@@Exporting a Proxmox virtual machine snapshot@@@Recover a Proxmox virtual machine by exporting a snapshot from a point-in-time copy of the source workload...","proxmox/onboarding_proxmox_environment.html@@@Onboarding a Proxmox environment@@@Onboard a Proxmox Virtual Environment in RSC to protect Proxmox virtual machines...","proxmox/prerequisites_proxmox_ve_protection.html@@@Prerequisites for Proxmox VE protection@@@Proxmox VE protection on RSC requires specific platform configurations, software installations, and account permissions to enable successful backup and recovery operations through RSC...","proxmox/proxmox.html@@@Proxmox@@@Rubrik Security Cloud provides discovery, backup, and recovery of Proxmox VE virtual machines...","proxmox/proxmox_environment_management.html@@@Manage the Proxmox environment@@@RSC manages and protects Proxmox VE virtual machines through native platform operations...","proxmox/proxmox_protection_management.html@@@Manage Proxmox protection@@@RSC uses SLA Domains to manage Proxmox protection of workloads by ensuring consistent backups and data retention...","proxmox/proxmox_vm_recovery_options.html@@@Proxmox virtual machine recovery options@@@RSC provides multiple options for recovering data from a protected Proxmox virtual machine snapshot...","proxmox/recovering_proxmox_vm_snapshot.html@@@Recovering folders or files from a Proxmox snapshot@@@Recover folders or files from a Proxmox virtual machine snapshot by downloading them or restoring them to a virtual machine...","proxmox/refreshing_proxmox_environment_manually.html@@@Refreshing a Proxmox environment manually@@@You can manually refresh a Proxmox environment to ensure that RSC discovers the latest virtual machines and configuration changes...","proxmox/removing_proxmox_environment.html@@@Removing a Proxmox environment@@@You can remove a Proxmox environment from RSC to discontinue data protection...","proxmox/taking_on_demand_snapshot_proxmox_vm.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of a specific Proxmox virtual machine and assign an SLA Domain to that snapshot. The retention, replication, and archiving settings of the SLA Domain are applied to the snapshot to protect the virtual machine effectively...","qauth/approving_denying_qauth_requests.html@@@Approving or denying a quorum authorization request@@@If you are a user with the QAuth administrator or QAuth approver role, review the requests on the Quorum Authorization requests page and then approve or deny a request for quorum authorization...","qauth/assigning_qauth_custom_role_local_users.html@@@Assigning the QAuth approver custom role to local users@@@Assign the QAuth approver custom role to local users by selecting the local users and editing their role assignments. This ensures that the designated users have the necessary permissions to approve quorum authorization requests...","qauth/assigning_qauth_custom_role_local_users_2.html@@@Assigning the QAuth approver custom role to local users@@@Assign the QAuth approver custom role to local users by selecting the local users and editing their role assignments. This ensures that the designated users have the necessary permissions to approve quorum authorization requests...","qauth/assigning_rl_custom_role_local_users.html@@@Assigning the retention-lock custom role to local users@@@Assign the retention-lock custom role to local users by selecting the local users and editing their role assignments. This ensures that the designated users have the necessary permissions to approve quorum authorization requests for retention-locked SLA Domains...","qauth/canceling_qauth_action.html@@@Canceling an action after requesting quorum authorization@@@To withdraw a quorum authorization request, cancel the requested action while the request is in the Pending or Approved state...","qauth/config_qauth_policy_role.html@@@Configuration of quorum authorization policies and roles@@@Configuring quorum authorization policies and roles enforces comprehensive data governance, enabling RSC administrators to centrally control, customize, and secure data management and system configuration actions...","qauth/creating_custom_role_qauth_approver.html@@@Creating a dedicated custom role for QAuth approvers@@@Create a dedicated custom role for QAuth approvers by configuring system privileges and selecting specific policies for global cluster-level or workload-specific policy sets...","qauth/creating_custom_role_qauth_approver_2.html@@@Creating a dedicated custom role for QAuth approvers@@@Create a dedicated custom role for QAuth approvers by configuring system privileges and selecting specific policies for global cluster-level or workload-specific policy sets...","qauth/creating_data_mgmt_qauth_policy.html@@@Creating a quorum authorization policy for data management actions@@@To prevent specific data management actions from being performed by a single user, create a policy for quorum authorization of such actions. The policy includes the actions that you want to protect, the objects whose data you want to protect, and the service accounts that do not require quorum authorization for performing the selected actions on the selected objects...","qauth/creating_qauth_approver_role.html@@@Creating a quorum authorization approver role@@@When actions that require quorum authorization are triggered, quorum authorization requests are generated. To review and then approve or deny these requests, create a role with permissions to view requests, view policies, and approve and deny requests...","qauth/creating_qauth_cluster_policy.html@@@Creating a Clusters policy@@@Create a Clusters policy by selecting data management actions, specifying clusters, setting required approvals, and defining policy details...","qauth/creating_qauth_obj_policy_rl_sla.html@@@Creating an Objects policy for retention-locked SLA Domains@@@Create an Objects policy for retention-locked SLA Domains by specifying the actions you want to protect and the objects whose data you want to safeguard...","qauth/creating_qauth_objects_policy.html@@@Creating an Objects policy@@@Create an Objects policy by including the actions you want to protect and the objects whose data you want to protect...","qauth/creating_qauth_sla_policy.html@@@Creating an SLA Domains policy@@@Create an SLA Domains policy by including the actions you want to protect and the SLA Domains you want to protect...","qauth/creating_qauth_sla_policy_2.html@@@Creating an SLA Domains policy@@@Create an SLA Domains policy by including the actions you want to protect and the SLA Domains you want to protect...","qauth/creating_qauth_sla_policy_rl_sla.html@@@Creating an SLA Domains policy for retention-locked SLA Domains@@@Create an SLA Domains policy for retention-locked SLA Domains by including the actions and SLA Domains you want to protect...","qauth/creating_rl_custom_role_qauth_approver.html@@@Creating a retention-lock custom role for QAuth approver@@@Create a retention-lock custom role for QAuth approvers by configuring system privileges and selecting the Objects and SLA Domains policies you created for the retention-locked SLA Domains...","qauth/creating_sysconfig_qauth_policy.html@@@Creating a quorum authorization policy for system configuration actions@@@To prevent a single user from performing specific system configuration actions, create a policy for quorum authorization of such actions. The policy specifies the actions that you want to protect, the Rubrik clusters where you want to protect the actions, and the service accounts that do not require quorum authorization for performing the selected actions...","qauth/deleting_qauth_policy.html@@@Deleting a quorum authorization policy@@@Delete a quorum authorization policy if you no longer need additional approval for the actions protected by the policy. Deleting a quorum authorization policy requires approval from a user account with the QAuth Admin role...","qauth/disabling_qauth.html@@@Disabling quorum authorization@@@Disable quorum authorization for your RSC domain to relax the requirement of obtaining additional approvals before allowing critical, data-modifying actions. Disabling quorum authorization cancels pending quorum authorization requests, deletes the configured policies and the QAuth Admin role, and removes the permission to approve or deny requests from the QAuth reviewer role...","qauth/enabling_qauth.html@@@Enabling quorum authorization@@@Enable quorum authorization for your RSC domain to enforce the requirement of receiving approvals from a minimum number of users before allowing critical, data-modifying operations to proceed...","qauth/global_cluster_level_policy_set.html@@@Global cluster-level policy set@@@Global cluster-level policy sets in quorum authorization enable RSC administrators to enforce centralized data governance across Rubrik clusters...","qauth/gov_mode_qauth_policy_setup.html@@@Governance mode QAuth policy setup@@@Maintaining the integrity of retention-locked SLA Domains in Governance mode requires setting up quorum authorization with specific administrators and approvers. This involves configuring quorum authorization, creating policies, assigning custom roles, and ensuring proper approval processes for any actions on retention-locked SLA Domains...","qauth/qauth_actors_responsibilities.html@@@Key actors and responsibilities in quorum authorization@@@Understanding the roles and responsibilities of key actors in quorum authorization management helps you to establish and maintain a secure and effective system...","qauth/qauth_and_mt.html@@@Quorum authorization and multitenancy@@@In a multitenant environment, when quorum authorization is enabled, the quorum authorization policies also apply to the actions initiated in the tenant organizations...","qauth/qauth_bypass_automation_scripting.html@@@Quorum authorization bypass for automation and scripting@@@Quorum authorization can hinder API-driven automation by blocking actions covered by quorum authorization policies. To address this, RSC provides service accounts exempt from quorum authorization policy enforcement, designed specifically for automation purposes. However, these accounts must be managed securely to avoid security risks...","qauth/qauth_initial_setup.html@@@Initial setup of quorum authorization@@@Initial setup includes configuring the QAuth feature to manage secure user authentication and administrative requests...","qauth/qauth_management_actions.html@@@Quorum authorization management actions@@@Actions related to the management of quorum authorization policies and roles require additional approval, which RSC enforces through policies. Only a user with the QAuth administrator role can approve or deny requests to perform these actions...","qauth/qauth_policy.html@@@Quorum authorization policy@@@A quorum authorization policy is the means by which quorum authorization is enforced. To ensure that a single user does not run data-modifying actions, a quorum authorization policy specifies such actions that require additional approval...","qauth/qauth_policy_editing_rules.html@@@Considerations for editing quorum authorization policies@@@When the system configuration requirements or data security requirements in your RSC domain change, you can edit the corresponding quorum authorization policies...","qauth/qauth_policy_for_data_mgmt_actions.html@@@Data management quorum authorization policies@@@A quorum authorization policy for data management actions is a user-defined policy that prevents a user from running data management actions on specific objects without the required approvals...","qauth/qauth_process.html@@@Quorum authorization process@@@The Quorum Authorization (QAuth) process secures actions related to data management and system configuration. This involves enabling QAuth, creating and associating QAuth policies and roles, requesting and reviewing actions, and optionally excluding service accounts to ensure automation scripts are not blocked...","qauth/qauth_request_approval.html@@@Quorum authorization requests and approvals@@@When a requester attempts an action protected by a policy, RSC triggers a quorum authorization request. The requester cannot perform the action until the request is approved by a user with the QAuth approver role...","qauth/qauth_requests_page.html@@@Quorum Authorization requests page@@@The Quorum Authorization requests page provides details about the requests submitted for quorum authorization and the response options available for the requests. Although the reviewers and requesters can view the same request details, the options available to respond to the requests vary depending on the role of the user viewing the page...","qauth/qauth_requests_page_filters.html@@@Filters on the Quorum Authorization requests page@@@The Quorum Authorization requests page provides filters that you can use to customize your view of the requests. Filtering the list of requests helps categorize the requests and results in efficient request processing...","qauth/qauth_roles.html@@@Quorum authorization roles@@@Quorum authorization roles in RSC provide structured management of approvals and permissions, ensuring appropriate reviews for system changes. The QAuth administrator role oversees quorum authorization activities. The QAuth approver role, which can be added to custom roles, allows users to approve specific policy changes...","qauth/qauth_roles_actions_summary.html@@@Quorum authorization roles and actions summary@@@Information about the quorum authorization roles and the corresponding actions these roles authorize users to perform...","qauth/qauth_roles_permissions_summary.html@@@Quorum authorization roles and permissions summary@@@A summary of all the quorum authorization roles in RSC and their respective permissions...","qauth/quorum_authorization.html@@@Quorum authorization@@@Quorum authorization is a security feature that requires additional approvals before a requester can perform data-modifying actions in RSC...","qauth/rl_qauth.html@@@Retention lock and quorum authorization@@@The retention lock feature helps organizations meet legal and compliance standards by providing Compliance and Governance modes, both requiring quorum authorization approvals for specific actions...","qauth/role_based_response_options_qauth_requests.html@@@Role-based response options for quorum authorization requests@@@When you access the Quorum Authorization requests page, your options to approve or deny requests, cancel requests, or run the action that triggered the request depend on your role...","qauth/running_qauth_action.html@@@Running an action after obtaining quorum authorization@@@If you are a requester, run an action you requested after the request is approved using quorum authorization. For you to be able to run the action, the action status of the request must be Approved...","qauth/sysconfig_qauth_policies.html@@@System configuration quorum authorization policies@@@A quorum authorization policy for system configuration actions is a user-defined policy that prevents a user from running actions related to system configuration without the required approvals. The policy applies to actions related to system configuration for the connected Rubrik clusters and to global configuration actions for RSC...","qauth/updating_qauth_settings.html@@@Updating quorum authorization settings@@@You can optimize the management of quorum authorization requests using the quorum authorization settings. With the required privileges, update the quorum authorization settings, such as the time-to-live setting for requests with manually scheduled actions and the timeout setting to indicate the duration after which inactive requests expire...","qauth/viewing_qauth_requests_page.html@@@Viewing quorum authorization requests@@@If you are assigned a role with the permission to view quorum authorization requests, view a list of requests by navigating to the Quorum Authorization requests page. You can also view the summary and history of each request...","qauth/workload_specific_policy_set.html@@@Workload-specific policy set@@@A workload-specific policy set in quorum authorization enables RSC administrators to apply data management policies to specific workloads, ensuring tailored protection for different data types...","rbs/adding_hosts_another_cluster.html@@@Adding hosts to another cluster@@@Add hosts to a secondary Rubrik cluster through RSC to enable recovery operations from the secondary cluster without removing the host from the primary cluster...","rbs/clearing_rbs_ntwk_thrtl_win_lnx_host.html@@@Clearing RBS network throttle for Windows and Linux hosts@@@Clear the network bandwidth consumption of RBS on your Windows and Linux hosts. Clearing the network throttle allows RBS to use unlimited network bandwidth for the hosts...","rbs/configuring_rbs_ntwk_thrtl_win_lnx_host.html@@@Configuring RBS network throttle for Windows and Linux hosts@@@Configure the network bandwidth consumption of RBS on your Windows and Linux hosts...","rbs/determining_if_rbs_runs_windows_sys.html@@@Determine when RBS is running on a Windows system@@@View the status of RBS on a Windows system...","rbs/managing_rbs_connection.html@@@Managing the RBS connection@@@After registering a host running RBS, you can refresh the RBS connection, update the RBS certificate, or disconnect RBS...","rbs/oracle_install_rbs.html@@@Installing Rubrik Backup Service software on Oracle@@@Download and install the Rubrik Backup Service software on selected Oracle hosts/nodes...","rbs/oracle_rbs.html@@@Rubrik Backup Service for Oracle@@@Rubrik Backup Service is required in order to perform automated discovery of Oracle hosts, Oracle RAC systems, and Oracle databases...","rbs/prereq_limits_rbs_network_throttling.html@@@Prerequisites and limitations for RBS network throttling@@@The necessary prerequisites and the operational limitations for configuring network throttling for RBS in RSC...","rbs/rbs_about.html@@@Rubrik Backup Service@@@The Rubrik Backup Service provides enhanced integration with protected resources and host systems...","rbs/rbs_account_windows_host.html@@@RBS account on Windows@@@RBS must use an account with local administrators group privileges on the Windows Server host...","rbs/rbs_automatically_deploying.html@@@Automatically deploying RBS@@@A Rubrik cluster can install and register RBS on a supported Windows guest at the next scheduled or on-demand backup of that Windows guest...","rbs/rbs_download_for_scvmm.html@@@Downloading RBS for SCVMM hosts@@@Obtain the Rubrik Backup Service software for System Center Virtual Machine Manager hosts from the web UI of a Rubrik cluster...","rbs/rbs_downloading_cnp.html@@@Downloading RBS for cloud-native protection@@@Download the RBS for cloud-native protection to coordinate backup activity between the Exocompute instance and RSC...","rbs/rbs_downloading_cnp_2.html@@@Downloading RBS for cloud-native protection@@@Download the RBS for cloud-native protection to coordinate backup activity between the Exocompute instance and RSC...","rbs/rbs_downloading_rbs_software.html@@@Downloading the RBS software@@@Obtain the Rubrik Backup Service software from the web UI of a Rubrik cluster...","rbs/rbs_firewall_rules.html@@@RBS firewall rules@@@The firewall on the host must allow communication with the ports used by RBS...","rbs/rbs_guest_registering.html@@@Registering a guest OS install of RBS@@@After installing the Rubrik Backup Service software on a virtual machine guest OS, register the Rubrik Backup Service with a Rubrik cluster...","rbs/rbs_installation.html@@@RBS installation@@@When installed on host systems, RBS provides integration with protected resources and coordinates activities between the Rubrik cluster and the host...","rbs/rbs_installing_linux.html@@@Installing RBS on Linux hosts@@@Install RBS software on Linux hosts...","rbs/rbs_installing_on_scvmm_host.html@@@Installing RBS on an SCVMM host@@@You can download the RBS software and then install and use it on an SCVMM host to integrate the protected resources and host systems that use SCVMM...","rbs/rbs_installing_windows.html@@@Installing RBS on Windows hosts@@@Install RBS on a computer or virtual machine that is running the Windows Server operating system...","rbs/rbs_installing_windows_2.html@@@Installing RBS on Windows hosts@@@Install RBS on a computer or virtual machine that is running the Windows Server operating system...","rbs/rbs_log_locations.html@@@RBS log locations@@@You can use RBS logs to determine the root cause of issues. The location of files used by RBS varies by operating system...","rbs/rbs_management_commands.html@@@RBS management commands@@@List of commands to manage RBS on different operating systems...","rbs/rbs_min_privileges_windows.html@@@Minimum RBS privileges for Windows@@@RBS requires certain privileges and permissions on Windows for both installation and regular operations...","rbs/rbs_network_throttling.html@@@RBS network throttling@@@RBS manages data backups and may consume all network bandwidth, affecting other applications. Network throttling helps to limit the usage of RBS bandwidth and ensures that essential services remain unaffected...","rbs/rbs_obtaining_connector.html@@@Obtaining Rubrik Backup Service connector@@@Download the Rubrik Backup Service connector to enable the connected Rubrik clusters to restore folders and files over corrupted data in the file system on the host...","rbs/rbs_obtaining_connector_2.html@@@Obtaining Rubrik Backup Service connector@@@Download the Rubrik Backup Service connector to enable the connected Rubrik clusters to restore folders and files over corrupted data in the file system on the host...","rbs/rbs_obtaining_connector_3.html@@@Obtaining Rubrik Backup Service connector@@@Download the Rubrik Backup Service connector to enable the connected Rubrik clusters to restore folders and files over corrupted data in the file system on the host...","rbs/rbs_package_verification.html@@@RBS package verification for platforms based on Linux RPM@@@RBS package verification confirms the authenticity and integrity of the downloaded package for platforms based on Linux RPM...","rbs/rbs_remote_installing_multiple_hosts.html@@@Installing RBS remotely on multiple hosts@@@From RSC, you can install RBS remotely to manage and protect multiple Linux, Solaris, HP-UX, AIX, or Windows hosts...","rbs/rbs_removal.html@@@RBS removal@@@The removal of RBS from a protected host terminates the connection between the host system and the Rubrik cluster...","rbs/rbs_remove_rbs_unix_linux.html@@@Removing RBS from a Linux host@@@Remove RBS by using standard Linux package manager commands...","rbs/rbs_remove_sap_hana.html@@@Removing RBS from SAP HANA@@@Remove the Rubrik Backup Service from a SAP HANA database...","rbs/rbs_remove_solaris.html@@@Removing RBS from an Oracle Solaris host@@@Remove RBS from an Oracle Solaris host...","rbs/rbs_remove_windows.html@@@Removing RBS from a Windows host@@@Remove the Rubrik Backup Service from a Windows host...","rbs/rbs_sap_hana.html@@@Rubrik Backup Service for SAP HANA@@@Install and configure the Rubrik Backup Service on a SAP HANA host to allow backup and restore of SAP HANA databases...","rbs/rbs_software_url.html@@@Obtaining the RBS software by URL@@@Obtain the Rubrik Backup Service software directly by URL instead of through the web UI...","rbs/rbs_sql_server_role_perms_reqs.html@@@SQL Server roles and permissions for RBS@@@To provide SQL Server protection, assign specific roles and permissions to the account used for RBS. In some cases, you might need to assign the SQL Server sysadmin role to this account...","rbs/rbs_status_commands_non_windows_sys.html@@@Commands for obtaining RBS status on a non-Windows system@@@You can view the status of RBS on a non-Windows system. The method to view the status depends on the platform RBS is running on...","rbs/reconnecting_rbs_after_losing_connection.html@@@Reconnecting a host and retaining existing backups on reinstallation@@@Reconnect a Windows or Linux host after reinstallation, update the certificate, and link existing backups to the host...","rbs/reinstallation_rbs_host.html@@@RBS reinstallation on a host@@@Reinstalling RBS on a host may generate a new host certificate and agent UUID, and as a result, the Rubrik cluster will not identify the host...","rbs/rsc_deploying_rbs_automatically.html@@@Deploying RBS automatically@@@A Rubrik cluster can automatically install and register RBS on a supported Windows guest at the next scheduled or on-demand backup of that Windows virtual machine...","rbs/rsc_downloading_rbs_software.html@@@Downloading the RBS software@@@Obtain the Rubrik Backup Service software from the web UI of a Rubrik cluster...","rbs/rsc_rbs_firewall_rules.html@@@RBS firewall rules@@@The firewall on the host must allow communication with the ports used by RBS...","rbs/rsc_rbs_installing_aix.html@@@Installing RBS on AIX hosts@@@Install RBS software on AIX hosts...","rbs/rsc_rbs_installing_hpux.html@@@Installing RBS on HP-UX hosts@@@Install RBS software on HP-UX hosts...","rbs/rsc_rbs_installing_solaris.html@@@Installing RBS on Solaris hosts@@@Install RBS on Solaris hosts...","rbs/rsc_rbs_remove_hpux.html@@@Removing RBS from a HP-UX host@@@Remove RBS from a HP-UX host...","rbs/rsc_rbs_remove_rbs_aix_host.html@@@Removing RBS from an AIX host@@@Remove RBS from an AIX host...","rbs/rubrik_backup_service.html@@@Rubrik Backup Service@@@The Rubrik Backup Service provides integration with protected resources and host systems and coordinates activities between the Rubrik cluster and the host...","rbs/rubrik_backup_service_2.html@@@Rubrik Backup Service@@@The Rubrik Backup Service provides integration with protected resources and host systems and coordinates activities between the Rubrik cluster and the host...","rbs/rubrik_backup_service_3.html@@@Rubrik Backup Service@@@The Rubrik Backup Service provides integration with protected resources and host systems and coordinates activities between the Rubrik cluster and the host...","rbs/rubrik_backup_status.html@@@Rubrik Backup Service status@@@The RBS Status column provides information about the status of the Rubrik Backup Service...","rbs/trusting_rbs_package_api.html@@@Using the API to trust the RBS package@@@Use the API to retrieve the public key of the private-public key pair for the Rubrik cluster to trust the RBS package downloaded from the Rubrik cluster...","rbs/trusting_rbs_package_browser.html@@@Using a browser to trust the RBS package@@@Use a browser to retrieve the public key of the private-public key pair for the Rubrik cluster to trust the Rubrik Backup Service package downloaded from the Rubrik cluster...","rbs/wvg_recover_files_secondary_cluster.html@@@Recovering files to Windows from a secondary cluster@@@Recover files from a volume group snapshot on a secondary Rubrik cluster by downloading them or exporting them to a different host...","rbs/wvg_recovery_secondary_cluster.html@@@Recovery to Windows from a secondary cluster@@@A Windows host connected to multiple Rubrik clusters can use secondary clusters for specific recovery operations without changing its primary cluster designation...","rbs/wvg_recovery_seconday_cluster_prereqs.html@@@Prerequisites for recovery to a secondary Windows host@@@Recovery to a secondary Windows host requires RBS, compatible CDM versions, and version alignment across the host and both clusters...","replication/benefits_marking_isolated_rubrik_cluster_not_isolated.html@@@Benefits of marking an isolated Rubrik cluster as not isolated@@@Marking an isolated Rubrik cluster as not isolated enhances network connectivity, data redundancy through replication, and simplifies cluster management...","replication/configuring_cross_acct_replication_policy.html@@@Configuring a cross-account replication policy in an SLA Domain@@@In the replication source RSC account, configure a cross-account replication policy in an SLA Domain when creating a custom SLA Domain or when editing any SLA Domain...","replication/creating_cross_acct_connection.html@@@Creating a cross-account connection@@@To facilitate the synchronization of Rubrik cluster metadata, create a cross-account connection between two accounts. The metadata synchronization is required for cross-account replication between the RSC account of the service consumer and the tenant organization in the RSC account of the service provider...","replication/creating_cross_acct_replication_pair.html@@@Creating a cross-account replication pairing@@@Create a cross-account replication pairing between the source and target Rubrik clusters across different RSC accounts using Network Address Translation. Network Address Translation method enables the source and target Rubrik clusters across different RSC accounts to communicate through the internet...","replication/creating_rep_pairings_pvt_ntwrk.html@@@Creating replication pairings using private network@@@Create replication pairings between source and target Rubrik clusters using a private network to ensure secure and efficient replication between clusters...","replication/creating_replication_pairings_nat.html@@@Creating replication pairings using NAT@@@Create replication pairings between source and target Rubrik clusters using Network Address Translation to enable data replication and facilitate monitoring and auditing of replication activities...","replication/creating_tenant_org_for_cross_acct_replication.html@@@Creating a tenant organization for cross-account replication@@@In the RSC account of the service provider, create a tenant organization for cross-account replication by allocating Rubrik clusters to be used as replication targets and assigning the tenant organization administrator role to at least one user from the RSC account of the service consumer...","replication/cross_account_replication.html@@@Cross-account replication@@@Cross-account replication is a disaster-recovery feature that you can use to create a replication pairing between Rubrik clusters that are connected to different RSC accounts...","replication/cross_account_replication_workflow.html@@@Cross-account replication workflow@@@Setting up cross-account replication between two different RSC accounts involves configuration on both accounts...","replication/deleting_cross_acct_connection.html@@@Deleting a cross-account connection@@@To stop the exchange of Rubrik cluster metadata between the RSC accounts of the service provider and consumer, delete the cross-account replication connection between the two RSC accounts...","replication/deleting_replication_pairing.html@@@Deleting a replication pairing@@@Delete a source Rubrik cluster and a target Rubrik cluster pairing...","replication/download_replicated_snapshot_rubrik_web_ui.html@@@Downloading a replicated snapshot@@@Download a copy of the replicated snapshot to the source Rubrik cluster for the snapshot recovery...","replication/editing_rep_pairings_pvt_ntwrk.html@@@Editing replication pairings using private network@@@Edit the replication pairing to update the source and target Rubrik clusters and to switch the IP version to either IPv4 or IPv6...","replication/expired_snapshot_recovery.html@@@Expired snapshot recovery@@@RSC provides an option to download a copy of the replicated snapshot to the source Rubrik cluster for the snapshot recovery...","replication/global_repli_pause.html@@@Global replication pause@@@Global replication pause pauses inbound replication to a Rubrik cluster and reduces the load on system resources...","replication/isolated_rubrik_cluster_limitations.html@@@Isolated Rubrik cluster limitations@@@Isolated Rubrik clusters have some limitations due to their disconnected state, including constraints on managing and protecting workloads...","replication/isolated_rubrik_cluster_operations.html@@@Isolated Rubrik cluster operational capabilities@@@Information about the operations that you can and cannot perform on isolated Rubrik clusters when they are not connected to the RSC. The source clusters are required to be connected to RSC to perform all operations...","replication/isolated_rubrik_clusters.html@@@Isolated Rubrik clusters@@@Isolated Rubrik clusters are a network setup in which the clusters are separated from the larger network by a firewall, thereby minimizing the clusters&apos; exposure to the network. By using this setup, you can enhance the security of your data...","replication/marking_isolated_rubrik_cluster_not_isolated.html@@@Marking an isolated Rubrik cluster as not isolated@@@To remove the isolation status of a Rubrik cluster, mark it as not isolated. This allows inbound traffic and enables the cluster to be used for replication, without the data protection restrictions of an isolated environment...","replication/marking_rubrik_cluster_isolated.html@@@Marking a Rubrik cluster as isolated@@@To secure your data by keeping a cluster protected behind a firewall and disconnected from the network, mark a Rubrik cluster as isolated...","replication/mgmt_isolated_rubrik_clusters_rsc.html@@@Management of isolated Rubrik clusters using RSC@@@The management of isolated Rubrik clusters using Rubrik Security Cloud involves establishing a brief, initial connection to the Rubrik cluster for configuration, updates, and data synchronization, managing SLA Domains, and opening port 443...","replication/nat_replication_requirements.html@@@NAT replication requirements@@@Replication with Network Address Translation requires dedicated replication ports on the source and target gateways...","replication/reconnecting_with_tenant_org.html@@@Reconnecting with a tenant organization@@@To resume the synchronization of Rubrik cluster metadata between the RSC account of the service consumer and a disconnected tenant organization, reconnect the RSC account of the service consumer with the tenant organization...","replication/rep_config_ntwrk_interface_types.html@@@Replication configuration network interface types@@@Information about network interface types for replication configuration, which includes Data, Management, and VLAN. These network interface types handle data transfer, management tasks, or specific services...","replication/rep_determining_nw_throttling_bypass_status.html@@@Determining the network throttling bypass status@@@For a replication source Rubrik cluster, determine whether the associated replication target Rubrik clusters are configured to bypass network throttling. You can determine this by using a Rubrik GraphQL API query...","replication/rep_determining_nw_throttling_bypass_status_by_cluster.html@@@Determining the network throttling bypass status for a specific target cluster@@@For a replication source Rubrik cluster, determine whether a specific replication target Rubrik cluster is configured to bypass network throttling. You can determine this by using a Rubrik GraphQL API query...","replication/rep_editing_replication_throttling.html@@@Editing replication throttling@@@Edit the replication throttling configured for a source cluster and all its replication pairings...","replication/rep_key_features_isolated_clusters.html@@@Key features of isolated Rubrik clusters@@@Isolated Rubrik target clusters offer enhanced security by managing incoming traffic to the target Rubrik cluster and handling snapshot replication efficiently...","replication/rep_network_throttling_bypass.html@@@Network throttling bypass for replication@@@Network throttling bypass is a mechanism by which you can configure Rubrik clusters to bypass the network throttling setting so that they have more bandwidth for certain tasks. For replication tasks, you can configure some replication target Rubrik clusters to bypass the network throttling setting in favor of more bandwidth...","replication/rep_network_throttling_rsc.html@@@Network throttling for replication@@@Rubrik provides settings to limit the network bandwidth usage for replication by specifying the maximum bandwidth allowed for outbound replication traffic for a Rubrik cluster...","replication/rep_pausing_replication.html@@@Pausing replication@@@Pause replication jobs temporarily to reduce network bandwidth demand...","replication/rep_replication_monitoring_and_reporting.html@@@Replication monitoring and reporting@@@The target Rubrik cluster provides real-time monitoring and reporting of replication activity...","replication/rep_replication_pairings_details.html@@@Replication pairings details@@@The Replication Pairings page includes the details of each replication pairing, including the paired clusters, source to target connection and target to source connection, task activity, storage usage, and throttling settings...","replication/rep_replication_policy.html@@@Replication policy@@@A replication policy for an SLA Domain enables replication of the snapshot and backup data of the objects that are protected by the SLA Domain...","replication/rep_replication_policy_config.html@@@Replication policy configuration@@@Creating a replication policy involves pairing source and target clusters and selecting a replication configuration. You can either select a many-to-one or one-to-one replication configuration...","replication/rep_resuming_replication_after_pause.html@@@Resuming replication after a pause@@@Resume replication after a replication pause from the web UI...","replication/rep_setting_replication_throttling.html@@@Setting replication throttling@@@Set replication throttling for a source Rubrik cluster and all of its target clusters...","replication/rep_updating_nw_throttling_bypass_status.html@@@Updating the network throttling bypass status for a target cluster@@@For a replication source Rubrik cluster, update the network throttling bypass status for a specific replication target Rubrik cluster by using a Rubrik GraphQL API mutation...","replication/rep_viewing_replication_pairings_page.html@@@Viewing the Replication Pairings page@@@From the Replication Pairings page, view summary information about configured replication pairings, including source and target clusters. The list of target clusters can include isolated clusters...","replication/replication.html@@@Replication@@@The replication feature directs the Rubrik cluster to send replicas of source snapshots or backups to a target Rubrik cluster and defines the maximum time to keep the replica on each cluster...","replication/replication_over_vlan.html@@@Replication over VLAN@@@Replication over VLAN enhances security, performance, and data transfer efficiency by isolating replication traffic from other network traffic, ensuring optimized handling, and reducing the risk of interference...","replication/replication_policy_changes.html@@@Replication policy changes@@@Editing an SLA Domain results in a variety of changes that impact the replication policy...","replication/replication_policy_disabled.html@@@Replication policy disabled@@@When the replication policy is disabled, the Rubrik cluster does not create additional replicas on the target Rubrik cluster...","replication/replication_policy_re_enabled.html@@@Replication policy re-enabled@@@When a replication policy is disabled and then re-enabled, the Rubrik cluster does not create replicas for existing snapshots and backups...","replication/replication_private_network.html@@@Replication using a private network@@@To perform replication, a source Rubrik cluster can communicate with a target Rubrik cluster through a private network...","replication/replication_retention_period_decreased.html@@@Replication retention period decreased@@@Decreasing the replication period configured in the SLA Domain decreases the replication retention period for new snapshots...","replication/replication_retention_period_increased.html@@@Replication retention period increased@@@Increasing the replication period configured in the SLA Domain increases the replication retention period for new snapshots...","replication/replication_start.html@@@Replication start@@@For any data source, the start of replication depends on adding the replication target to the Rubrik cluster and adding the replication policy to the associated SLA Domain...","replication/replication_target_setup.html@@@Replication target setup@@@A Rubrik cluster can replicate data to other Rubrik clusters. To use a Rubrik cluster as a replication target, the source Rubrik cluster must be provided with information about the target...","replication/replication_using_nat.html@@@Replication using NAT@@@To perform replication, a source Rubrik cluster can communicate with a target Rubrik cluster by using NAT...","replication/rsc_network_utilization_graph_replication.html@@@Network utilization graph for replication@@@The network bandwidth utilized by the incoming and outgoing data traffic generated by the replication feature is shown in a graph. To ensure optimal utilization of network bandwidth, you can monitor and analyze this graph and set a throttle to limit the network bandwidth utilized by the replication feature...","replication/viewing_network_utilization_graph_replication.html@@@Viewing the network utilization graph for replication@@@With administrator or RSC owner privileges, by viewing a graph, you can monitor the incoming and outgoing data traffic on a Rubrik cluster and thereby assess the network bandwidth utilized by the replication feature...","reuse/comments_suggestions.html@@@Comments and suggestions@@@We welcome your comments and suggestions about our products and our product documentation...","reuse/notices.html@@@Legal Notices@@@Copyright Copyright \u00A9 2026 Rubrik, Inc. All rights reserved. This document may be used free of charge. Selling without prior written consent is prohibited. Obtain permission before redistributing. In...","reuse/support.html@@@Support@@@You can contact Rubrik Support through the following methods...","reuse/support_g.html@@@Support for Rubrik Security Cloud - Government@@@Use one of the following methods to contact Rubrik Support to ensure that your support case is directed to the correct portal and handled efficiently...","rncd/rncd_add_mng_systems_ncd.html@@@Add and manage NAS CD systems from NAS CD@@@You can add and manage NAS CD systems from the NAS CD...","rncd/rncd_add_systems.html@@@Add NAS CD systems@@@You can protect unstructured data in a data storage system by adding the system in NAS CD using the RSC user interface. When you add a system using RSC, you can manage protection of the NAS CD data sets by backing up, archiving or restoring the data sets using RSC...","rncd/rncd_adding_systems_ncd.html@@@Adding NAS CD systems from NAS CD@@@Add a NAS CD system using the NAS CD UI to configure the system as a data source...","rncd/rncd_amzn_s3_immutability_prereq.html@@@Amazon S3 immutability prerequisites for NAS CD data sets@@@Information about IAM policies with the required permissions for an AWS user account to set up Amazon S3 buckets with Object Lock and Versioning for immutable backups...","rncd/rncd_azr_ver_lvl_immutability_prereq.html@@@Azure version-level immutability prerequisites for NAS CD data sets@@@When you use Azure Blob Storage to store your NAS CD backups, you can leverage the Azure version-level immutability feature to keep your NAS CD objects immutable for any retention period you require...","rncd/rncd_config_mng_protn_dataset_ncd.html@@@Configure and manage protection from NAS CD@@@You can assign policies to your NAS CD data sets to protect them by backing up or archiving the data...","rncd/rncd_configure_targets.html@@@Configure NAS CD targets@@@You can use RSC to back up and archive your NAS data to the supported storage destinations, known as targets...","rncd/rncd_creating_targets_rsc.html@@@Creating NAS CD targets from RSC@@@Create a target to backup and archive your NAS data from a source system using RSC...","rncd/rncd_data_protection_mgmt_using_rsc_ncd.html@@@Data protection and Recovery using RSC and NAS CD@@@You can manage your NAS CD datasets depending on whether you import or set up the NAS systems in NAS CD or RSC...","rncd/rncd_eval_sla_domains_options_ncd.html@@@Evaluate SLA Domain options for NAS CD@@@You can use SLA Domains to unify data protection policies, providing a unified approach to manage data protection of NAS CD data sets...","rncd/rncd_nfs_immutability_prereq.html@@@NFS immutability prerequisites for NAS CD data sets@@@Information about NFS immutability and its configuration details for NAS CD data sets...","rncd/rncd_recover.html@@@Recover NAS CD data sets@@@You can recover shares from the snapshots on the Overview tab of a share on the NAS CD Inventory page...","rncd/rncd_recover_2.html@@@Recover NAS CD data sets@@@You can recover shares from the snapshots on the Overview tab of a share on the NAS CD Inventory page...","rncd/rncd_s3_storage_immutability_prereq.html@@@S3 storage immutability prerequisites for NAS CD data sets@@@Information about prerequisites for setting up immutable NAS CD targets on supported S3-compatible storage. You must configure IAM policies with specific permissions. These permissions enable the storage user account to set up S3 buckets with Object Lock and Versioning for immutable backups...","rncd/rncd_setup_datasets_ncd.html@@@Set up NAS CD datasets from NAS CD@@@You can set up and protect your NAS CD data sets from the NAS CD...","rncd/rncd_setup_ncd_datasets_rsc.html@@@Set up NAS CD data sets from RSC@@@You can set up and protect your NAS CD data sets from the RSC...","rsc_ports/complete_port_list.html@@@Complete port list@@@Lists all ports that the Rubrik cluster uses for internode communication, external services, and workload integrations...","rsc_ports/db_port_reqs.html@@@Database workload port requirements@@@Port requirements for IBM Db2, IBM Informix, Microsoft SQL Server, MongoDB, MySQL, Oracle, PostgreSQL, and SAP HANA...","rsc_ports/dc_port_reqs.html@@@Data center workload port requirements@@@Port requirements for Filesets, Hyper-V, Kubernetes, Managed Volumes, Nutanix AHV, OLVM, OpenStack virtual machines, Proxmox VE, and VMware vSphere protection...","rsc_ports/envoy_org_port_reqs.html@@@Envoy organization network port requirements@@@Port requirements for Rubrik Envoy virtual appliances used in RSC multitenancy deployments with organization networks...","rsc_ports/port_specs.html@@@Port specifications@@@Port requirements for RSC deployments. Includes workload-specific tables, Envoy organization network ports, Rubrik cluster administration ports, and a complete port list...","rsc_ports/rbk_cluster_admin_port_reqs.html@@@Rubrik cluster administration port requirements@@@Port requirements for Rubrik clusters onboarded to RSC, covering cluster administration access, infrastructure services, notifications, monitoring, authentication, physical appliance, internode communication, and RSC connectivity...","rsc_ports/storage_nw_port_reqs.html@@@Storage and network workload port requirements@@@Port requirements for Dell EMC Isilon/PowerScale, NetApp, Pure Storage FlashBlade, Nutanix Files, and cluster-to-cluster replication...","rscintegrations/configuring_workday_api_client.html@@@Configuring the Workday API client@@@Create an integration system user, security group, and API client in your Workday tenant to enable Workday integration in RSC...","rscintegrations/connecting_crowdstrike_context_enrichment.html@@@Connecting CrowdStrike Context Enrichment Card to RSC@@@Configure the Rubrik Security Cloud app in the CrowdStrike Marketplace to surface Rubrik data context in the Falcon console...","rscintegrations/connecting_crowdstrike_rbk.html@@@Connecting CrowdStrike Identity Protection to RSC@@@Connect CrowdStrike Identity Protection to RSC to get a deeper context of correlated actions for each alert, simplifying your investigation workflow and efficiently remediating identity alerts...","rscintegrations/connecting_msft_defender_rsc.html@@@Connecting Microsoft Defender to RSC@@@Connect Microsoft Defender to RSC and an Entra ID Domain to get a deeper context of correlated actions for each alert, simplifying your investigation workflow and efficiently remediating identity alerts...","rscintegrations/connecting_workday_rsc.html@@@Connecting Workday to RSC@@@Connect your Workday tenant to RSC to enable automatic classification of changes in Entra ID and in Active Directory connected to SailPoint during identity recovery...","rscintegrations/creating_crowdstrike_api_client.html@@@Creating CrowdStrike API client@@@Create the API client in your CrowdStrike platform and ensure to assign the required API scope permissions for alerts...","rscintegrations/crowdstrike_context_enrichment_integration.html@@@CrowdStrike Context Enrichment Card integration@@@The CrowdStrike Context Enrichment Card integration with RSC surfaces Rubrik backup, data security, and threat detection context directly in the CrowdStrike Falcon console...","rscintegrations/crowdstrike_integration.html@@@CrowdStrike Identity Protection integration@@@The CrowdStrike Identity Protection integration with RSC provides bidirectional identity threat response, from detection and contextual enrichment to clean recovery of the affected identity...","rscintegrations/crowdstrike_reverting_related_actions.html@@@Reverting related actions@@@Revert related actions the identified actor has performed for a specific CrowdStrike alert to mitigate the risk posed by specific actions...","rscintegrations/disconnecting_crowdstrike_rbk.html@@@Disconnecting CrowdStrike Identity Protection from RSC@@@Disconnect the integration between CrowdStrike and RSC to stop the ingestion of new alerts...","rscintegrations/disconnecting_msft_entra_id_domain_rbk.html@@@Disconnecting Microsoft Entra ID Domain from RSC@@@Disconnect the integration between a Microsoft Entra ID Domain and RSC to stop the ingestion of new alerts from Microsoft Defender...","rscintegrations/google_secops/connecting_google_secops_rsc.html@@@Connecting Google SecOps to RSC@@@Connect Google SecOps to RSC using the integration wizard to configure SIEM event streaming, SOAR automated response, or both...","rscintegrations/google_secops/deleting_google_secops_integration.html@@@Deleting the Google SecOps integration@@@Delete a Google SecOps integration from RSC to stop event streaming and disable API access for SOAR playbooks...","rscintegrations/google_secops/editing_google_secops_integration.html@@@Editing the Google SecOps integration@@@Edit your Google SecOps integration settings in RSC to update webhook credentials, modify event types, or change the service account...","rscintegrations/google_secops/google_secops_integration.html@@@Google SecOps integration@@@The Google SecOps integration with RSC enables you to stream RSC security events to Google Security Operations for threat detection and to automate incident response workflows using RSC data...","rscintegrations/google_secops/prerequisites_google_secops.html@@@Prerequisites for the Google SecOps integration@@@The Google SecOps integration with RSC has specific prerequisites that must be met before you begin setup...","rscintegrations/msft_defender_identity_integration.html@@@Microsoft Defender integration@@@The Microsoft Defender integration with RSC streamlines the response to identity threats, including detection, containment, and clean recovery of compromised identities...","rscintegrations/msft_defender_reverting_related_actions.html@@@Reverting related actions for Microsoft Defender@@@Revert related actions the identified actor has performed for a specific Microsoft Defender alert to mitigate the risk posed by specific actions...","rscintegrations/registering_msft_defender_app.html@@@Registering a Microsoft Entra app for Defender@@@Register an application in Microsoft Entra and assign the required API permissions to enable alert ingestion from Microsoft Defender...","rscintegrations/sailpoint/connecting_sailpoint_rsc.html@@@Connecting SailPoint IdentityNow to RSC@@@Connect SailPoint IdentityNow to RSC to enable RSC to classify identity provider changes as governed actions when they originate from a SailPoint access request...","rscintegrations/sailpoint/disconnecting_sailpoint_rsc.html@@@Disconnecting SailPoint IdentityNow from RSC@@@Disconnect SailPoint IdentityNow from RSC to stop classifying identity provider access requests and user provisioning against SailPoint access requests...","rscintegrations/sailpoint/generating_sailpoint_pat.html@@@Generating a Personal Access Token in SailPoint IdentityNow@@@Generate a Personal Access Token in SailPoint IdentityNow to enable RSC to authenticate with SailPoint and retrieve fulfilled access request data...","rscintegrations/sailpoint/sailpoint_integration.html@@@SailPoint integration@@@The SailPoint integration with RSC classifies identity provider access requests as governed actions when they originate from SailPoint...","rscintegrations/viewing_crowdstrike_alerts.html@@@Viewing CrowdStrike alerts in RSC@@@Monitor and investigate identity threats detected by CrowdStrike directly within the RubrikIdentity Resilience dashboard...","rscintegrations/viewing_msft_defender_alerts.html@@@Viewing Microsoft Defender alerts in RSC@@@Monitor and investigate identity threats detected by Microsoft Defender directly within the Rubrik Identity Resilience dashboard...","rscintegrations/workday_integration.html@@@Workday integration@@@The Workday integration connects RSC to your Workday HRIS tenant to automatically identify and classify legitimate changes in Entra ID and in Active Directory connected to SailPoint during identity recovery...","rscintegrations/xsoar/connecting_xsoar_rsc.html@@@Connecting Cortex XSOAR to RSC@@@Connect Cortex XSOAR to RSC to enable automated ingestion of data security findings into XSOAR for investigation and remediation using SOAR playbooks...","rscintegrations/xsoar/deleting_xsoar_integration.html@@@Deleting the Cortex XSOAR integration@@@Delete the Cortex XSOAR integration to remove the integration configuration from RSC...","rscintegrations/xsoar/editing_xsoar_integration.html@@@Editing the Cortex XSOAR integration@@@Edit the Cortex XSOAR integration to update the integration name or change the associated service account...","rscintegrations/xsoar/prerequisites_xsoar_integration.html@@@Prerequisites for the Cortex XSOAR integration@@@Information about RSC permissions, XSOAR environment requirements, and service account recommendations for the Cortex XSOAR integration...","rscintegrations/xsoar/xsoar_integration.html@@@Cortex XSOAR integration@@@The Cortex XSOAR integration enables security operations teams to automatically ingest RSC data security findings into XSOAR for investigation and remediation using SOAR playbooks...","rubrik/supported_workloads.html@@@Rubrik Security Cloud workloads@@@RSC securely manages and protects data from a wide variety of workload types...","saas-ai/enabling_rubrik_ai.html@@@Enabling Rubrik AI@@@Enable Rubrik AI to provide environment-aware insights, visual reporting, and guided remediation workflows in Rubrik Security Cloud...","saas-ai/rubrik_ai_best_practices_limitations.html@@@Best practices and limitations for Rubrik AI@@@Guidelines for optimizing your experience with Rubrik AI and an overview of technical boundaries...","saas-ai/rubrik_ai_data_privacy_security.html@@@Data privacy and security for Rubrik AI@@@Rubrik AI ensures data privacy and security by isolating tenant data, enforcing existing RBAC permissions, and maintaining a strict no-model-training policy for all user interactions...","saas-ai/rubrik_ai_key_capabilities_workflows.html@@@Key capabilities and workflows for Rubrik AI@@@You can use Rubrik AI to detect security anomalies, discover sensitive data, and automate recovery workflows...","saas-ai/rubrik_ai_overview.html@@@Rubrik AI@@@Rubrik AI is the AI agent built into Rubrik Security Cloud. It provides environment-aware insights and streamlines data security operations...","saas-ai/rubrik_ai_tasks.html@@@Rubrik AI capabilities@@@Use Rubrik AI to troubleshoot issues, get configuration guidance, and run diagnostic checks across your protected environment...","saas-ai/rubrik_mcp.html@@@Rubrik MCP@@@You can use MCP-compatible AI agents to query Rubrik Security Cloud for protection status, event investigation, and select operational actions without leaving your AI tool...","saas-ai/troubleshooting_rubrik_ai.html@@@Troubleshooting Rubrik AI@@@Resolve common Rubrik AI issues related to connectivity, access permissions, and session behavior...","saas/Configuring_ri_events_for_protected_objects.html@@@Configuring Anomaly Detection events for protected objects@@@Configure Anomaly Detection events for protected objects of connected Rubrik clusters for more fine-grained control of alerts...","saas/Performing_inplace_recovery_multiple_vms.html@@@Performing In-place recovery for multiple virtual machines@@@Perform in-place recovery of multiple vSphere virtual machines using the In-place recovery option available on the vSphere VMs page...","saas/RSC_customizable_dashboards.html@@@Customizable dashboards@@@You can customize the Data Protection dashboard and adjust it to display widgets from the Data Security Posture, Data Threat Analytics, and M365 dashboards...","saas/Recovering_multiple_VMs_exports.html@@@Recovering multiple vSphere virtual machines with Export@@@Use the Export option to perform bulk recovery of vSphere virtual machines by exporting snapshots to a vSphere datastore...","saas/Recovering_multiple_vms_using_live_mount.html@@@Recovering multiple virtual machines using Live Mounts@@@Create live mounts to recover multiple vSphere virtual machines using the Live Mount option available on the vSphere VMs page...","saas/accessing_identity_inventory.html@@@Accessing the Identity Inventory@@@When you enable the Identity Inventory, you can view details of user access, risk contributors, and risk changes over time on the Identity Inventory page...","saas/accessing_licenses_usage_details.html@@@Accessing license and usage details@@@Access license and usage details in RSC to track expiration dates and plan license renewals...","saas/accessing_sso_user_details.html@@@Accessing the SSO user details@@@Access SSO user details from the SSO Users and Groups page...","saas/actions_available_recovery.html@@@Actions available for a recovery@@@You can take specific actions for a selected recovery from the recovery details page...","saas/add_aws_acc_data_scanning.html@@@Adding an AWS account for data scanning@@@Add an AWS account in RSC for protection and to enable data scanning. Data scanning helps you manage cloud posture risks...","saas/add_indv_aws_acc_using_cft_protect.html@@@Adding a self-managed AWS account using a template for protection@@@To protect AWS resources within an individual AWS account, add the account to RSC using the AWS CloudFormation template. You add the AWS account using the self-managed deployment model where you provision and manage compute resources such as Exocompute in your own AWS account...","saas/adding_a_host.html@@@Adding an SAP HANA host@@@To begin managing and protecting SAP HANA databases on a Linux host, add the host to the Rubrik cluster...","saas/adding_a_sap_hana_system.html@@@Adding an SAP HANA system@@@Add an SAP HANA system to the RSC domain to start protecting SAP HANA workloads...","saas/adding_a_service_account.html@@@Adding a service account@@@Add a service account in RSC to generate client credentials and enable client-side applications to authenticate to RSC...","saas/adding_a_syslog_export_rule.html@@@Adding a syslog export rule@@@A syslog export rule is added to specify the details for sending syslog events to a remote syslog server...","saas/adding_additional_accounts.html@@@Adding additional accounts@@@The initial RSC user account, and every subsequently added user account, can add additional users...","saas/adding_akv.html@@@Adding Azure Key Vaults@@@Add an Azure Key Vault to manage encryption for Azure based archives or Rubrik Cloud Vault. You can configure the integration using secretless provisioning or secret-based provisioning...","saas/adding_aws_account_dsp.html@@@Adding AWS accounts for configuring Data Security Posture@@@Add a new AWS account to RSC and configure Data Security Posture. Data Security Posture generates insights that you can use to measure and manage your data security risk...","saas/adding_aws_account_manually_for_protection.html@@@Adding a self-managed AWS account manually for protection@@@To protect the AWS resources within an AWS account, add your account in RSC manually by creating the required roles in the AWS Management Console and providing the Amazon Resource Names (ARNs) of the required roles in RSC. You add the AWS account manually using the self-managed deployment model where you provision and manage compute resources such as Exocompute in your own AWS account...","saas/adding_aws_account_manually_storage.html@@@Adding a self-managed AWS account manually for storage@@@Add your AWS account in RSC manually for storage by creating an cross-account role on the AWS Management Console and providing the role ARN in RSC. You add the AWS account manually using the self-managed deployment model where you provision and manage compute resources such as Exocompute in your own AWS account...","saas/adding_aws_account_rsc_managed.html@@@Adding an RSC-managed AWS account for protection@@@Add an AWS account to RSC using the RSC-managed deployment model so that RSC provisions and manages all compute and storage resources on your behalf...","saas/adding_aws_cloud_account_kms_manager.html@@@Adding a cloud account-based AWS key manager@@@Add a cloud account-based key manager to give RSC access to your AWS KMS key for client-side encrypted cloud-native archival locations...","saas/adding_aws_cloud_account_using_cft_storage.html@@@Adding a self-managed AWS account using a template for storage@@@Add the AWS account in RSC using the AWS CloudFormation template for storage. You add the AWS account using the self-managed deployment model where you provision and manage compute resources such as Exocompute in your own AWS account...","saas/adding_aws_custom_tag.html@@@Adding an AWS custom tag in RSC@@@To implement specific policies for cost allocation, financial management, and resource creation, after you have created a custom tag on the AWS Management Console, add the details of that tag in RSC...","saas/adding_aws_kms_manager.html@@@Adding a secret-based AWS KMS key manager@@@Add a secret-based AWS key manager for RSC to access your AWS KMS key using IAM credentials for data center archival locations...","saas/adding_aws_role_chaining_acc.html@@@Adding an AWS role chaining account@@@Add a dedicated AWS role chaining account in RSC to centrally manage secure access across your AWS accounts and simplify emergency revocations...","saas/adding_aws_role_chaining_acc_manually.html@@@Adding an AWS role chaining account manually@@@Add a dedicated AWS role chaining account in RSC by manually creating the required IAM roles in the AWS Management Console and providing the role ARN in RSC...","saas/adding_aws_tag_exclusion.html@@@Adding an AWS tag exclusion pattern in RSC@@@To prevent specific tags on AWS source resources from being propagated to snapshots, add tag exclusion patterns in RSC...","saas/adding_azure_cloud_account_dsp.html@@@Adding Azure subscriptions for configuring Data Security Posture@@@Add a new Azure account to RSC and configure Data Security Posture. You can use the insights to measure and manage your data security risk...","saas/adding_azure_custom_tag.html@@@Adding an Azure custom tag in RSC@@@To implement specific policies for cost allocation, financial management, and resource creation, after you have created a custom tag on the Azure portal, add the details of that tag in RSC...","saas/adding_brand_logo_organization.html@@@Adding a brand logo to your organization&apos;s page@@@Add a brand logo to personalize RSC for the global organization and all the associated tenant organizations...","saas/adding_cdm_admin_ssh_keys.html@@@Adding SSH keys for the CDM admin user@@@Add SSH public keys to the admin account on a Rubrik CDM cluster from RSC to enable key-based CLI access...","saas/adding_cluster.html@@@Adding a Rubrik cluster@@@To enhance data protection capabilities, add a Rubrik cluster to a Rubrik Security Cloud account...","saas/adding_cluster_2.html@@@Adding a Rubrik cluster@@@To enhance data protection capabilities, add a Rubrik cluster to a Rubrik Security Cloud account...","saas/adding_comments_files_support_case.html@@@Adding comments and uploading files to a support case@@@Add comments and attach files to a support case from the Case Detail view to communicate with your Rubrik support engineer...","saas/adding_custom_feed.html@@@Adding a custom intel feed@@@Create a custom intel feed with specific indicators of compromise to monitor for threats...","saas/adding_domains_allowlist.html@@@Adding domains to the allowlist@@@Add the email domains that RSC permits when you create local users...","saas/adding_email_addresses_allowlist.html@@@Adding email addresses to the allowlist@@@Add the individual email addresses that RSC permits when you create local users...","saas/adding_email_claim_rule.html@@@Adding email claim rules@@@Add a claim rule to define how ADFS formats email claims sent to RSC...","saas/adding_email_notification_setting.html@@@Adding an email notification setting@@@Add an email notification setting to notify users about different RSC events based on event severity...","saas/adding_entra_id_with_oauth.html@@@Adding a Microsoft Entra ID directory with OAuth@@@Add a Microsoft Entra ID directory as a protected workload with OAuth authentication...","saas/adding_entra_id_without_oauth.html@@@Adding a Microsoft Entra ID directory without OAuth@@@Add a Microsoft Entra ID directory as a protected workload without OAuth, authenticated by your existing Microsoft Entra ID domain application registration...","saas/adding_gcp_cloud_account_kms_manager.html@@@Adding a cloud account-based Google Cloud KMS key manager@@@Add a cloud account-based key manager to give RSC access to your Google Cloud Key Management Service key for client-side encrypted cloud-native archival locations...","saas/adding_group_claim_rule_all_groups.html@@@Adding a group claim rule for all groups@@@Add a claim rule to include all the group claims in the outgoing token sent to RSC...","saas/adding_group_filter_claim_rules.html@@@Adding group filter claim rules@@@Add claim rules that allow only group claims that start with certain characters to be sent to RSC...","saas/adding_guest_os_credentials.html@@@Adding guest OS credentials@@@Add guest OS credentials for a virtual machine. Guest OS credentials provide service account details with the appropriate privileges...","saas/adding_ioc_to_custom_intel_feed.html@@@Adding an IOC to a custom intel feed@@@Add an indicator of compromise to a custom intel feel for additional monitoring...","saas/adding_kmip_server.html@@@Adding KMIP servers@@@To manage your Key Encryption Key and self-encrypting drive passwords on a Rubrik cluster using a KMIP-compliant external key manager, you must add the details of the KMIP server in RSC...","saas/adding_netapp_system.html@@@Adding a NetApp system@@@Add a NetApp system for the SnapMirror Cloud to protect...","saas/adding_node_cces.html@@@Adding a node to Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage@@@Add a node to a Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage deployment to increase capacity and improve performance...","saas/adding_node_predeployed_cces.html@@@Adding a pre-deployed node to Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage@@@Add a node that you have manually deployed to a Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage deployment in RSC to increase capacity and improve performance...","saas/adding_pam_configuration.html@@@Adding a PAM configuration@@@Add a Privileged Access Management configuration to create and manage its associated API credentials...","saas/adding_private_endpoint.html@@@Adding a private endpoint for RCV Cloud Native locations@@@Create a private endpoint connection from your environment to an RCV Cloud Native location to secure network traffic between your workloads and the RCV archival storage...","saas/adding_qauth_based_pam_config.html@@@Adding a QAuth-based PAM Configuration@@@Add a Privileged Access Management configuration that requires a QAuth approval...","saas/adding_relying_party_trust.html@@@Adding RSC as a Relying Party Trust@@@Add RSC as a Relying Party Trust in the ADFS management console to establish a trust relationship between RSC and ADFS...","saas/adding_rubrik_cluster_to_smb_domain.html@@@Adding a Rubrik cluster to an SMB Domain@@@To enforce user authentication through Active Directory, add a Rubrik cluster that hosts SMB shares to an SMB domain...","saas/adding_sso_idp.html@@@Adding an SSO IdP@@@You can add multiple SSO IdPs in RSC to support different security policies, compliance requirements, and isolated environments for testing and production...","saas/adding_standalone_esxi_host.html@@@Adding a standalone ESXi host@@@Add a standalone ESXi host to manage virtual machines for improved data backup and to export tasks in on-premise environments...","saas/adding_the_initial_account.html@@@Adding the initial account@@@Use the instructions in the email sent by Rubrik to set up the initial account...","saas/adding_trap_receivers_rsc.html@@@Adding trap receivers@@@Trap receivers are configured by specifying the IP address or FQDN along with the receiver port. Traps from the Rubrik MIB file are send to a trap receiver for further processing...","saas/adding_vcenter_metro_storage_cluster_connection_information.html@@@Adding vCenter Metro Storage Cluster connection information@@@Add connection information for a vCenter Metro Storage Cluster to a Rubrik cluster...","saas/adding_vcenter_server_aws_evs.html@@@Adding vCenter Server on AWS EVS@@@Protect the virtual machines of a vCenter Server hosted on AWS EVS by adding the vCenter Server to a Rubrik Cloud Cluster...","saas/adding_zscaler_integration.html@@@Adding a Zscaler integration in RSC@@@To secure sensitive data in your production environment by combining Rubrik Data Security Posture and Zscaler Data Loss Prevention services, add a Zscaler integration in RSC using the Integrations page...","saas/adfs_integrate_workflow.html@@@ADFS integration workflow@@@The workflow provides a high-level view of the tasks involved in configuring SSO with ADFS...","saas/allowing_idp_initiated_sso.html@@@Allowing IdP-initiated SSO for an identity provider@@@Turn on Allow IdP-Initiated SSO for an identity provider so that users can access RSC directly from the identity provider&apos;s portal...","saas/anomaly_compliance_report.html@@@Anomaly Detection Compliance Report@@@The Anomaly Detection Compliance Report provides visibility into Anomaly Detection coverage by showing which objects were scanned, which were not, and why...","saas/anomaly_compliance_report_charts.html@@@Compliance Report charts and table columns@@@The Anomaly Detection Compliance Report provides chart and table information about Anomaly Detection coverage for protected objects...","saas/anomaly_compliance_report_filter.html@@@Compliance Report filters and grouping controls@@@RSC provides several filters and grouping controls for use with the Anomaly Detection Compliance Report...","saas/anomaly_det_aws_ec2_ebs_vol.html@@@Anomaly Detection in Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes@@@Enabling Anomaly Detection for your AWS account can detect ransomware attack in Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes and protect data from the ransomware attack...","saas/anomaly_detection.html@@@Anomaly Detection@@@Anomaly Detection examines file system statistics to check for anomalies in usage patterns...","saas/anomaly_detection_behavioral_model.html@@@Anomaly Detection behavioral model@@@Anomaly Detection uses machine learning techniques and behavioral heuristics to build models that define normal baseline behavior and identify malicious data encryption patterns...","saas/anomaly_detection_details.html@@@Anomaly Detection details@@@The Anomaly Detection details page provides information about the protected workload, files changed within the snapshot, the sensitivity of impacted data, and the event timeline...","saas/anomaly_detection_filters.html@@@Anomaly Detection filters@@@The Anomaly Detection page provides information about objects that contain detected anomalies. You can use the filters to sort the data on the page...","saas/anomaly_detection_report_details.html@@@Anomaly Detection report details@@@The Anomaly Detection report provides information about scanned and unscannable objects. You can download a CSV or PDF file of the report or save a copy of the report...","saas/anomaly_event_details.html@@@Anomaly event details@@@Data Threat Analytics provides detailed information about the detected anomaly events, including the event timeline and an option to investigate the specific snapshot...","saas/anomaly_report_filters.html@@@Anomaly report filters@@@You can use the anomaly report filters in the Anomaly Detection Details Report to investigate anomalies. These filters help you perform a more granular analysis of events...","saas/api_access_with_service_accounts.html@@@API access with service accounts@@@Service accounts enable client applications and other services to invoke the RSC APIs securely...","saas/app_consistent_backups_azure.html@@@Application-consistent protection for Azure virtual machines@@@Application-consistent backups preserve the working state of applications running on a protected Azure virtual machine...","saas/app_consistent_snapshot_aws_ec2_instances.html@@@Application-consistent snapshot for AWS EC2 instances@@@Application-consistent snapshot is a feature that you can use to take snapshots that include data from pending I/O operations. You can use this feature with AWS to take snapshots that include data from pending I/O operations between the applications running on the AWS EC2 instance and the disk attached to the AWS EC2 instance...","saas/app_integration_okta.html@@@Application integration with Okta@@@You can integrate an application with Okta by configuring the SAML protocol information...","saas/applying_sla_changes_existing_snapshot.html@@@Applying SLA Domain changes to existing snapshots@@@Apply SLA Domain changes to existing snapshots, including on-demand and downloaded snapshots...","saas/arch_location_dashboard_info.html@@@Archival locations dashboard@@@The archival location dashboard provides insights into your data center archival locations. You can monitor storage growth over time, archival lag, and storage consumption by workloads at each location on this dashboard...","saas/arch_viewing_arch_loc_dashboard.html@@@Viewing the archival locations dashboard@@@View the archival locations dashboard for enhanced visibility into your data center archival locations. You can monitor information such as storage growth over time, archival lag, and detailed storage consumption breakdown by protected workloads at each location...","saas/archival_policy.html@@@Archival policy@@@An archival policy is a configurable set of rules in an SLA Domain that defines where, when, and how long a Rubrik cluster archives protected data...","saas/archive_log_snapshot_multiple_policies.html@@@Archive log snapshots with multiple archival policies@@@RSC archives the log snapshots for database workloads to the location with the higher archival frequency...","saas/archiving_settings_for_specific_workloads.html@@@Archiving settings for specific workloads@@@Optional archiving settings for specific workloads when creating or editing an SLA Domain...","saas/assiging_sla_domain_without_snapshot_schedules.html@@@Assigning SLA Domain without snapshot schedules@@@Assign an SLA Domain without snapshot schedules for Continuous Data Protection-only SLA Domains for the selected workloads...","saas/assigning_mip_labels.html@@@Assigning MIP labels@@@Assign Microsoft Information Protection (MIP) labels to documents in Microsoft 365 environments connected to the Microsoft Purview platform...","saas/assigning_permission_category_for_recovery.html@@@Assigning a permission category for recovery@@@When you are performing recovery operations such as exporting, restoring, mounting virtual disks, and downloading files or folders and the target Azure subscription does not have the required permission category, assign the permission category to ensure recovery...","saas/assigning_sap_hana_perm_strg_snapsht_recovery.html@@@Assigning the SAP HANA permission for storage snapshot recovery@@@When you are performing the recovery operation for an SAP HANA storage snapshot and the Azure subscription, containing the Azure virtual machines running the SAP HANA systems, does not have the SAP HANA Snapshot - Recovery permission assigned, assign the permission to ensure recovery...","saas/assigning_sla_domains_to_vsphere_tags.html@@@Assigning SLA Domains to vSphere tags@@@Assign an SLA Domain to the virtual machines with the assigned vSphere tags...","saas/audit_notes.html@@@Audit notes@@@There is a provision to add notes during certain tasks for audit-tracking purposes...","saas/auth_sso_user_accounts_saml.html@@@Authentication of SSO user accounts using SAML@@@RSC uses a third-party identity provider for authentication. The identity provider authenticates the SSO user accounts through the SAML 2.0 protocol...","saas/authorizing_adfs_sso_groups.html@@@Authorizing ADFS SSO groups@@@Authorize an SSO group in RSC so that its members can authenticate using ADFS credentials...","saas/authorizing_okta_sso_groups.html@@@Authorizing Okta SSO groups@@@Authorize an SSO group in RSC so that its members can authenticate using Okta credentials...","saas/authorizing_onelogin_sso_groups.html@@@Authorizing OneLogin SSO groups@@@Authorize an SSO group in RSC so that its members can authenticate using OneLogin credentials...","saas/authorizing_sso_group.html@@@Authorizing an SSO group@@@Authorize an SSO group in RSC and assign roles to users in the group...","saas/authorizing_sso_user.html@@@Authorizing an SSO user@@@Authorize an SSO user directly from RSC and assign the required roles so that they can perform their tasks effectively...","saas/aws_acc_management.html@@@AWS account management@@@Using RSC, you can monitor and manage the details of your AWS accounts. You can also refresh an AWS account on-demand to obtain the most up-to-date metadata based on your specific requirements...","saas/aws_account_status.html@@@AWS account status@@@The Status column of the AWS accounts page provides information about the status of the RSC cloud account for Amazon...","saas/aws_adding_acc_using_org_protection.html@@@Adding self-managed AWS accounts using AWS Organization for protection@@@Add multiple AWS accounts for protection using an AWS Organization. You add the AWS accounts using the self-managed deployment model where you provision and manage compute resources such as Exocompute in your own AWS accounts...","saas/aws_ami_allowlist_exocompute.html@@@AMI allowlisting for Exocompute on AWS@@@If the AWS Service Control Policies related to your organization blocks the launch of shared and AWS Marketplace AMIs, you must allowlist the Amazon EKS node AMIs used by Exocompute to prevent backup failures...","saas/aws_archiving.html@@@Archiving for AWS workloads@@@RSC supports archiving of Amazon EC2 instances or EBS volumes, Amazon RDS PostgreSQL, Aurora PostgreSQL, RDS SQL Server, RDS MySQL, and Aurora MySQL database snapshots to lower-cost storage, ensuring cost savings, compliance, and security...","saas/aws_assigning_protection_account.html@@@Assigning protection to AWS accounts@@@Assign a data protection policy at the AWS account level...","saas/aws_assigning_protection_ec2_ebs.html@@@Assigning protection to EC2 instances and EBS volumes@@@Assign a data protection policy to specific Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes...","saas/aws_best_practices_sla_assignment.html@@@Best practices for AWS SLA Domain assignment@@@Information about the best practices for assigning SLA Domains to AWS workloads, ensuring effective data protection and compliance...","saas/aws_cc_es_rsc.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services protects applications and data by running Rubrik CDM software on Amazon EC2 instances within a virtual private cloud...","saas/aws_cloud_acc_addition_terraform.html@@@AWS cloud account addition using Terraform@@@You can add multiple AWS cloud accounts to RSC at once using the RSC provider for Terraform...","saas/aws_cloud_acc_setup.html@@@Set up AWS cloud accounts@@@You can set up an AWS cloud account in RSC and start protecting your AWS workloads...","saas/aws_cloud_account_deletion.html@@@Delete AWS cloud accounts@@@You can delete an AWS cloud account from RSC when it is no longer in use...","saas/aws_cloud_discovery.html@@@AWS cloud discovery@@@The cloud discovery feature provides a read-only view of AWS resources in RSC. This feature separates workload discovery from workload protection, so you can view all the resources that exist before choosing what to protect...","saas/aws_cnp_archival_encryption_options.html@@@Encryption options for AWS cloud-native archival@@@RSC supports two encryption modes for archiving AWS EC2 instance, EBS volume, and Amazon S3 bucket snapshots: server-side encryption using a platform-managed or customer-managed key, and client-side encryption using your own AWS KMS key...","saas/aws_cnp_client_side_encryption.html@@@Client-side encryption for AWS workloads@@@Client-side encryption protects archived workload data using your AWS KMS key before the data is written to cloud storage...","saas/aws_cnp_dynamodb.html@@@Cloud-native protection for Amazon DynamoDB@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects Amazon DynamoDB in an AWS account...","saas/aws_cnp_ec2.html@@@Cloud-native protection for Amazon EC2 instances@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects Amazon EC2 instances in your AWS account...","saas/aws_cnp_permission_boundary.html@@@Permissions boundary for cloud-native workloads protection@@@An AWS IAM permissions boundary defines the maximum permissions available to an RSC role. Configuring the boundary with explicit Allow statements for all required RSC permissions prevents common allowlist misconfiguration that can break cloud-native workload protection...","saas/aws_cnp_rds.html@@@Cloud-native protection for Amazon RDS@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects Amazon RDS and Aurora databases in an AWS account...","saas/aws_comm_rbk_aws.html@@@Communication between RSC and AWS@@@A high-level architecture overview of how RSC uses AWS IAM roles and temporary credentials to manage AWS workloads securely...","saas/aws_comm_rbk_aws_role_chaining.html@@@Communication between RSC and AWS using role chaining@@@A high-level architecture overview of how RSC uses AWS IAM roles and role chaining with temporary credentials to manage AWS accounts securely...","saas/aws_common_protection_terms.html@@@Common AWS protection terms@@@It is important to understand some common terms when protecting AWS workloads with RSC...","saas/aws_config_storage_tiering.html@@@Configure AWS storage tiering@@@To configure AWS storage tiering, you must create an archival location for archiving snapshots and storing backups...","saas/aws_configuration_cloud_acc.html@@@Configure AWS cloud accounts@@@Start the configuration of your AWS cloud accounts by adding them to RSC. This topic lists the options for adding an account that uses the self-managed deployment model...","saas/aws_configuration_exocompute.html@@@Configure Exocompute on AWS@@@The configuration workflow sequence for localized and centralized Exocompute on AWS, AWS accounts onboarded using the self-managed deployment model, Rubrik-hosted Elastic Container Registry, and Rubrik-managed Elastic Kubernetes Service cluster...","saas/aws_configuring_gateway_kms_key.html@@@Configuring a gateway KMS key@@@Configure a customer-managed KMS key for each region to encrypt intermediate snapshots created during archival, indexing, and related operations in the centralized Exocompute model...","saas/aws_configuring_pcr.html@@@Configuring Private Container Registry for AWS@@@Configure a Private Container Registry for AWS to retrieve the Docker images from a registry you host...","saas/aws_create_stackset_settings.html@@@AWS StackSets settings specific to RSC@@@Information about the settings specific to RSC when creating a stack set to add multiple AWS cloud accounts at once...","saas/aws_creating_cust_key_exo_app_acc.html@@@Creating AWS custom KMS key in the application account@@@If your source snapshot is encrypted using a default KMS key in the application account, you need to create a custom KMS key and share it with the centralized Exocompute host account...","saas/aws_creating_custom_rbac_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for AWS@@@Create a custom role with Role-based Access Control privileges for managing your AWS workloads. These privileges provide finer granularity for determining which permissions an RSC user has for performing specific actions on specific objects...","saas/aws_creating_custom_sla.html@@@Creating a self-managed SLA Domain for AWS@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to streamline and customize workload protection and management policies for AWS accounts that use the self-managed deployment model...","saas/aws_creating_inst_prof_iam_role_console.html@@@Creating instance profiles for IAM roles using AWS console@@@Create an instance profile for an Exocompute EKS worker node role using AWS Management Console...","saas/aws_creating_inst_prof_iam_roles_cli.html@@@Creating instance profiles for IAM roles using CLI@@@Create an instance profile for an Exocompute EKS worker node role using the CLI...","saas/aws_creating_s3_gateway_endpoint.html@@@Creating an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint@@@Create an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint to enable private connectivity between your Amazon VPC and Amazon S3, enhancing security and reducing costs...","saas/aws_creating_subnets.html@@@Creating subnets for Amazon VPC@@@Create two primary subnets in different availability zones for the Amazon VPC you have created. Optionally, you can create two secondary subnets specifically for pods to prevent IP address exhaustion...","saas/aws_creating_vpc.html@@@Creating an Amazon VPC@@@Create an Amazon Virtual Private Cloud on the AWS Management Console to configure localized or centralized Exocompute with Rubrik-hosted ECR and Rubrik-managed EKS clusters...","saas/aws_creating_vpc_interface_endpoint.html@@@Creating an Amazon VPC interface endpoint@@@Create Amazon VPC interface endpoints to allow secure and private access to AWS services within the same region without requiring public IP addresses or internet connectivity...","saas/aws_cse_required_permissions.html@@@Required permissions for client-side encryption of archival locations@@@Information about the AWS KMS permissions that RSC requires to create, manage, and rekey client-side encrypted cloud-native archival locations...","saas/aws_cust_controlled_storage.html@@@Customer-controlled storage and keys@@@You can archive the backups of an RSC-managed AWS account to a customer-controlled archival location and encrypt them with your own AWS Key Management Service key...","saas/aws_custom_tag.html@@@AWS custom tags@@@You can specify AWS custom tags in RSC to implement specific policies for cost allocation, financial management, and resource creation...","saas/aws_customer_hosted_planning.html@@@Plan your self-managed AWS protection@@@Before you add an AWS account, confirm your license, permissions, account setup options, and, if you use them, Exocompute and storage tiering...","saas/aws_ddb_primary_backup_immutability.html@@@DynamoDB primary backup immutability in AWS@@@RSC supports S3 object-level immutability for Amazon DynamoDB backup data, preventing modification or deletion of backup objects for the duration defined by the SLA Domain...","saas/aws_deleting_cloud_account_resources.html@@@Deleting an AWS cloud account and its resources@@@Delete an AWS cloud account and its resources when no longer in use...","saas/aws_deploy_rsc_managed.html@@@Deploy RSC-managed AWS protection@@@Plan, connect, and verify an AWS account that uses the RSC-managed deployment model, where RSC provisions and operates the compute and storage resources for you...","saas/aws_deploy_self_managed.html@@@Deploy self-managed AWS protection@@@Plan, connect, and verify an AWS account that uses the self-managed deployment model, where you provision and manage compute and storage resources in your own AWS account...","saas/aws_deployment_checklist_rsc_managed.html@@@Deployment checklist for RSC-managed AWS protection@@@Use this pre-flight checklist to confirm that the licenses, access, AWS account, and protection plan are in place before you add an AWS account that uses the RSC-managed deployment model...","saas/aws_deployment_checklist_self_managed.html@@@Deployment checklist for self-managed AWS protection@@@Use this pre-flight checklist to confirm that the licenses, access, permissions, network, and storage are in place before you add an AWS account that uses the self-managed deployment model...","saas/aws_deployment_models_cloud_acc.html@@@Deployment models for AWS cloud accounts@@@When adding an AWS cloud account to RSC, you can choose between an RSC-managed model and a self-managed model...","saas/aws_disabling_cloud_discovery.html@@@Disabling and deleting AWS cloud discovery@@@Disable and delete cloud discovery when you want to remove an AWS account integration with RSC or stop metadata collection...","saas/aws_disabling_data_scanning.html@@@Disabling data scanning for AWS accounts@@@Disable data scanning for an AWS account to stop the collection of data sensitivity insights...","saas/aws_dynamodb.html@@@Manage Amazon DynamoDB@@@RSC secures Amazon DynamoDB tables with automated snapshots governed by SLA Domain policies. You can gain insights from detailed snapshot data and optimize resources using on-demand account refresh and AWS custom tags...","saas/aws_dynamodb_acc_management.html@@@Amazon DynamoDB table management@@@Using RSC, you can monitor and manage the details of your Amazon DynamoDB tables. You can also refresh a table on-demand to obtain the most up-to-date metadata based on your specific requirements...","saas/aws_dynamodb_assigning_protection.html@@@Assigning protection to Amazon DynamoDB@@@Assign a data protection policy to specific Amazon DynamoDB tables...","saas/aws_dynamodb_continuous_backup_pitr.html@@@Continuous backups PITR for Amazon DynamoDB@@@RSC configures and relies on native Point-in-Time Recovery associated with Amazon DynamoDB for continuous backup of source tables...","saas/aws_dynamodb_creating_tag_rules.html@@@Creating tag rules for Amazon DynamoDB tables@@@Create and assign a tag rule to group Amazon DynamoDB tables and assign SLA Domains to protect those tables...","saas/aws_dynamodb_deleting_tag_rules.html@@@Deleting tag rules for Amazon DyanmoDB tables@@@Delete a tag rule assigned to the Amazon DynamoDB tables associated with your AWS account...","saas/aws_dynamodb_details.html@@@Amazon DynamoDB details@@@Viewing and analyzing detailed information about Amazon DynamoDB tables helps in making informed decisions. Key aspects include protection status, detailed attributes, snapshots calendar, and events log for audit and compliance...","saas/aws_dynamodb_granular_recovery_permissions.html@@@Required RSC permissions for DynamoDB granular recovery@@@Information about the RSC role permissions that you need to search Amazon DynamoDB snapshot records and restore records in place...","saas/aws_dynamodb_granular_recv_limitations.html@@@Limitations for Amazon DynamoDB granular search and recovery@@@Information about limitations that apply when you search Amazon DynamoDB snapshot records and restore records in place...","saas/aws_dynamodb_inplace_records_recovery.html@@@Restoring Amazon DynamoDB records in place@@@Restore specific records from an Amazon DynamoDB snapshot directly to the source table without creating a new table...","saas/aws_dynamodb_performing_pitr.html@@@Performing point-in-time recovery for Amazon DynamoDB@@@Perform a point-in-time recovery for an Amazon DynamoDB table to restore data to a specific point in time using continuous backups, with the ability to create the new table in a different AWS region...","saas/aws_dynamodb_performing_snapshot_recv.html@@@Performing snapshot recovery for Amazon DynamoDB@@@Perform a snapshot recovery for an Amazon DynamoDB table to recover data using either an on-demand snapshot or a scheduled snapshot taken according to the assigned SLA Domain...","saas/aws_dynamodb_recovery.html@@@Amazon DynamoDB recovery@@@You can recover Amazon DynamoDB tables using the various recovery options provided by RSC...","saas/aws_dynamodb_recovery_options.html@@@Recovery options for Amazon DynamoDB@@@RSC provides three recovery options for Amazon DynamoDB tables: point-in-time recovery for precise data restoration, snapshot recovery for flexible data management, and granular search and in-place recovery for restoring individual records...","saas/aws_dynamodb_recv_network_reqs.html@@@Networking requirements for Amazon DynamoDB recovery@@@You can ensure successful Amazon DynamoDB recovery by considering key networking requirements such as provisioned Write Capacity Units, VPC configuration, security group settings, and NACLs...","saas/aws_dynamodb_regn_s3_backup_repo.html@@@Regional S3 backup repository for DynamoDB@@@Rubrik provisions a dedicated Amazon S3 bucket in the same AWS region as the source Amazon DynamoDB table for the backup process...","saas/aws_dynamodb_regn_specific_backups.html@@@Region-specific backups for DynamoDB@@@RSC automatically selects a region to take a backup of Amazon DynamoDB global tables and stores the snapshot in that selected region...","saas/aws_dynamodb_req_permissions.html@@@Required permissions for Amazon DynamoDB@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires at Read and Write access levels to protect Amazon DynamoDB objects in terms of various use cases...","saas/aws_dynamodb_searching_snapshot_records.html@@@Searching Amazon DynamoDB snapshot records@@@Search for specific records in Amazon DynamoDB snapshots using partition key and optional attribute filters, then preview or export the matched results...","saas/aws_dynamodb_snapshot_info_list.html@@@Amazon DynamoDB snapshot information list@@@The Snapshots tab displays information about the snapshots for a selected Amazon DynamoDB table...","saas/aws_dynamodb_snapshot_records_recovery.html@@@Recovering specific Amazon DynamoDB records from a snapshot@@@Search for and restore specific records from a selected Amazon DynamoDB snapshot directly to the source table, without performing a full-table recovery...","saas/aws_dynamodb_tag_rule_edits.html@@@Tag rule edits for Amazon DynamoDB tables@@@After creating a tag rule, if you want to update the protection details related to an Amazon DynamoDB table, you can edit the name of the tag rule, associated AWS account, and the SLA Domain...","saas/aws_dynamodb_taking_ods.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshot of an Amazon DynamoDB table@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, take an on-demand snapshot of Amazon DynamoDB to protect the information that resides in the DynamoDB tables...","saas/aws_dynamodb_viewing_accounts_page.html@@@Viewing DynamoDB accounts page@@@Access the AWS accounts page for Amazon DynamoDB to view information about the cloud accounts created on RSC...","saas/aws_dynamodb_viewing_inv_page.html@@@Viewing the Amazon DynamoDB inventory page@@@Access the AWS accounts page for DynamoDB to view information about the cloud accounts created on RSC...","saas/aws_ebs_snapshot_lock.html@@@EBS snapshot lock in AWS@@@The AWS EBS snapshot lock is a native AWS security feature that provides immutability for EC2 instance and EBS volume snapshots, preventing their deletion or modification...","saas/aws_ec2_ebs_creating_tag_rules.html@@@Creating tag rules for Amazon EC2 instances or EBS volumes@@@Create and assign a tag rule to protect the Amazon EC2 instances or EBS volumes associated with your AWS account...","saas/aws_ec2_ebs_deleting_tag_rules.html@@@Deleting tag rules for Amazon EC2 instances or EBS volumes@@@Delete a tag rule assigned to the Amazon EC2 instances or EBS volumes associated with your AWS account...","saas/aws_ec2_ebs_details.html@@@Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes details@@@Viewing and analyzing detailed information about Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes helps in making informed decisions. Important aspects include protection status, detailed attributes, snapshots calendar, and events log for audit and compliance...","saas/aws_ec2_ebs_editing_tag_rules.html@@@Editing a tag rule for Amazon EC2 instances or EBS volumes@@@Change the tag rule name, SLA Domain, and the AWS accounts associated with a tag rule for Amazon EC2 instances or EBS volumes. The tag key and tag value are not editable...","saas/aws_ec2_ebs_recovery_options.html@@@Recovery options for Amazon EC2 instances@@@A comparative overview of the various recovery options for Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes...","saas/aws_ec2_ebs_snapshot_management.html@@@EC2 instance and EBS volume snapshots management@@@You can manage snapshots of Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes. This includes taking on-demand snapshots, changing retention policies, and deleting snapshots...","saas/aws_ec2_ebs_tag_based_protection.html@@@Tag-based protection for AWS workloads@@@You can protect AWS workloads by grouping them using tags and assigning SLA Domains using the tag...","saas/aws_ec2_ebs_volume.html@@@Manage Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes@@@After you set up protection for Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes, RSC takes automated snapshots of those instances and volumes based on the configured policies in SLA Domains. You can also take on-demand snapshots, refresh AWS accounts, and add AWS custom tags for better resource management...","saas/aws_ec2_marketplace_support.html@@@AWS EC2 marketplace support@@@RSC supports indexing, archiving, restoring, and exporting snapshots of EC2 instances deployed from the AWS EC2 marketplace and recovering files or folders from those instances using the direct read APIs...","saas/aws_ec2_recovery.html@@@Amazon EC2 instance recovery@@@You can recover Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes using the various recovery options that RSC provides...","saas/aws_eks_container_repos.html@@@Docker container repositories for EKS cluster@@@Information about the repositories for the Docker container from where the EKS cluster retrieves images...","saas/aws_eks_restrict_rsc_access.html@@@Access restriction of EKS cluster to RSC IP addresses@@@You can perform configurations so that only RSC IP addresses can access the AWS EKS cluster created by Rubrik for security enhancement...","saas/aws_enabling_file_indexing.html@@@Enabling file indexing for a specific EC2 snapshot@@@Enable file indexing of a snapshot of an Amazon EC2 instance or EBS volume for enabling file recovery...","saas/aws_encryption_key_req_exocompute.html@@@Encryption key requirements for AWS centralized Exocompute@@@RSC shares the snapshots of AWS workloads in the application account with the centralized Exocompute host account for indexing, archiving, and security operations such as Lambda jobs. Before mapping an application account to a centralized Exocompute host account, you must complete the required key-sharing actions based on how your source workloads are encrypted...","saas/aws_ephemeral_vm_exclusion_from_discovery.html@@@AWS ephemeral VMs exclusion from discovery@@@RSC automatically excludes ephemeral Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes created by supported third-party services, such as Databricks, from discovery...","saas/aws_evaluate_options_cloud_acc_setup.html@@@Evaluate AWS cloud account setup options@@@When adding an AWS cloud account to RSC, it is important to evaluate the available options for adding the account, including data scanning and role chaining capabilities, including the mandatory cloud discovery baseline and optional protection and security features...","saas/aws_evaluate_sla_option.html@@@Evaluate AWS SLA Domain options@@@Understanding the various protection options is important when creating an SLA Domain for your AWS workloads. This ensures alignment with organizational needs. Thoroughly evaluating these options enables informed decisions and provides effective protection for the workloads...","saas/aws_exo_configuring_s3_gw_vpc_endpoint.html@@@Configuring an S3 Gateway VPC endpoint for Exocompute on AWS@@@Configure an Amazon S3 Gateway VPC endpoint in the VPC used by your Exocompute cluster to route S3 traffic over the AWS private network and avoid NAT gateway data processing charges...","saas/aws_exo_cost_best_practices.html@@@Best practices for reducing Exocompute on AWS costs@@@You can configure your AWS network and storage settings to avoid unexpected costs when using Exocompute on AWS for archiving and data protection operations...","saas/aws_exocompute_common_terms.html@@@Common terms for Exocompute on AWS@@@Understanding certain common terms associated with the Rubrik Exocompute on AWS feature is important when configuring Exocompute on AWS...","saas/aws_exocompute_evaluate_options.html@@@Evaluate Exocompute on AWS options@@@When setting up Exocompute on AWS for the accounts onboarded using the self-managed deployment model, it is important to evaluate the options for deployment and networking. Thorough evaluation of these choices helps to align them with the needs of your organization prior to Exocompute configuration...","saas/aws_exocompute_health_check.html@@@Exocompute health check for AWS@@@The Exocompute health check for AWS is a feature in RSC that runs a health check for an Elastic Kubernetes Service cluster immediately after its configuration and displays the relevant status...","saas/aws_exocompute_health_check_status.html@@@Health check statuses for AWS Exocompute@@@Information about the various health check statuses for AWS Exocompute...","saas/aws_exocompute_local_central.html@@@Localized versus centralized Exocompute on AWS@@@Overview of deployment models for Exocompute on AWS...","saas/aws_exocompute_network_choices.html@@@Network choices for Exocompute on AWS@@@Information about network choices for Exocompute on AWS for self-managed accounts, required for seamless integration and optimal operation...","saas/aws_exocompute_quota_management.html@@@Quota management for Exocompute on AWS@@@Exocompute on AWS relies on sufficient EC2 quotas for its EKS-managed containerized operations, such as backup, indexing, and archiving. Without adequate quotas, Exocompute might face operational disruptions, highlighting the need for effective quota management...","saas/aws_exocompute_workflow_example.html@@@Exocompute on AWS workflow example@@@A workflow example to demonstrate the Exocompute lifecycle on AWS when indexing a snapshot of an Amazon EC2 instance...","saas/aws_gateway_kms_key_centralized_exo.html@@@Gateway KMS key for AWS centralized Exocompute@@@You can optionally configure a centralized gateway KMS key in RSC to use a single customer-managed key across multiple AWS accounts and regions instead of the default alias-based method...","saas/aws_hierarchy_sla_assignment.html@@@SLA Domain assignment hierarchy for AWS@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based, automatic protection for AWS workloads, simplifying the assignment of protection across various levels, such as AWS accounts and individual workloads...","saas/aws_hosted_license_usage.html@@@Licenses and usage for AWS cloud accounts@@@The license you hold determines which AWS deployment model is available when you add an AWS cloud account, and the Licenses and Usage page shows how much capacity your RSC-managed accounts consume...","saas/aws_hosted_limitations.html@@@RSC-managed AWS protection limitations@@@Review the constraints of the RSC-managed model before you choose it for an AWS account...","saas/aws_hosted_planning.html@@@Plan your RSC-managed AWS protection@@@Before you add an AWS account, confirm your license, supported workloads and regions, permissions, and storage and encryption choices...","saas/aws_hosted_required_permissions.html@@@Required permissions for RSC-managed AWS protection@@@RSC-managed accounts need an IAM cross-account role and no Exocompute permissions in your AWS account. VPC and networking permissions are needed only for Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) workloads...","saas/aws_hosted_sla_domains.html@@@SLA Domains for RSC-managed AWS accounts@@@SLA Domains for RSC-managed accounts archive to Rubrik Cloud Vault by default and do not support replication...","saas/aws_hosted_supported_workloads_regions.html@@@Supported workloads and regions for RSC-managed AWS protection@@@The RSC-managed model supports specific workload types in commercial AWS regions, with some regions excluded...","saas/aws_hosted_vault_encryption.html@@@Vault encryption options for RSC-managed AWS protection@@@By default, RSC manages the encryption keys for data in Rubrik Cloud Vault, and you can specify your own key during onboarding...","saas/aws_instant_tiering.html@@@AWS Instant Tiering@@@In RSC, you can instantly tier the Amazon EC2 instance, EBS volume, or DynamoDB table snapshots to the specified archival location, enhancing cost efficiency...","saas/aws_ip_planning_eks_cluster.html@@@IP address planning for Exocompute on AWS EC2@@@For the Exocompute on AWS feature that uses Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service clusters as the underlying compute resources, IP address planning is critical. The number of IP addresses required and the corresponding subnet size are calculated based on your specific environment and workload...","saas/aws_key_features_protection.html@@@Key features for protecting AWS workloads@@@RSC provides unified data management, automated global data protection, various recovery options for AWS workloads, and advanced security features to protect your workloads...","saas/aws_kms_key_sharing_automation.html@@@AWS KMS key sharing automation@@@For AWS application accounts mapped to a centralized Exocompute host account, RSC automates Key Management Service key sharing, removing the need to manually update key policies or create gateway Key Management Service keys before mapping...","saas/aws_maintenance_exocompute.html@@@Maintain Exocompute on AWS@@@Maintaining Exocompute on AWS involves regularly reviewing and updating settings and removing obsolete configurations to ensure optimal performance and resource management...","saas/aws_manage_cld_acc.html@@@Manage AWS cloud accounts@@@You can manage the AWS cloud accounts available in RSC...","saas/aws_manage_role_chaining_acc.html@@@Manage an AWS role chaining account@@@You can manage an existing AWS role chaining account in RSC by downloading its CloudFormation template, revoking or restoring access, or removing the account...","saas/aws_managing_file_indexing.html@@@Managing file indexing for all EC2 snapshots@@@Manage file indexing for Amazon EC2 instances or EBS volumes by turning on or turning off file indexing. Turning on file indexing facilitates quick file recovery by allowing you to search across indexed snapshots and initiate recovery. When it is no longer needed, you can turn off file indexing...","saas/aws_managing_granular_perms_cloud_acc.html@@@Managing granular permissions for an AWS cloud account@@@You can manage the permission categories for an AWS cloud account that you have already added to RSC by including or excluding permission categories, as required...","saas/aws_managing_granular_perms_cloud_acc_2.html@@@Managing granular permissions for an AWS cloud account@@@You can manage the permission categories for an AWS cloud account that you have already added to RSC by including or excluding permission categories, as required...","saas/aws_manual_vs_cft_config_cld_acc.html@@@Manual versus CFT configuration for AWS cloud accounts@@@A comparative overview of the manual and CloudFormation Template methods for adding an AWS cloud account to RSC...","saas/aws_migrating_existing_acc_org.html@@@Migrating existing AWS accounts to AWS Organization@@@Migrate existing AWS accounts to an AWS Organization. When you choose to migrate an AWS account to an AWS Organization, RSC selects all the AWS accounts eligible for migration instead of providing an option to select which accounts to migrate...","saas/aws_multi_role_architecture.html@@@AWS multiple-role IAM architecture@@@With the multiple-role IAM architecture, RSC provisions a dedicated IAM role for each feature you enable instead of a single shared cross-account IAM role...","saas/aws_multiple_arch_loc.html@@@Multiple archival locations for AWS workloads@@@RSC supports SLA Domains with multiple archival locations for Amazon EC2 instances, EBS volumes, Amazon RDS PostgreSQL database, Aurora PostgreSQL database, RDS MySQL database, Aurora MySQL database, and RDS SQL Server databases, enabling granular control over data archiving with up to two distinct archiving policies...","saas/aws_multiple_vpc_with_tgw_checklist.html@@@AWS multiple VPC with transit gateway checklist@@@Information about the network configurations to check and validate when you are using multiple AWS VPCs with a transit gateway...","saas/aws_multiple_vs_indv_acc_addition.html@@@Multiple versus individual AWS cloud account addition@@@A comparative overview of multiple and individual addition of AWS cloud accounts...","saas/aws_network_setup_exocompute.html@@@Network setup for Exocompute on AWS@@@To ensure the proper functioning of Exocompute on AWS for the accounts that are onboarded using the self-managed deployment model, meet specific network prerequisites for seamless communication among RSC, the EKS cluster, and AWS services. You provision and manage compute resources such as Exocompute in your own AWS account for the accounts onboarded using the self-managed deployment model...","saas/aws_nw_rules_eks_node_vpc_fw.html@@@Network rules for EKS node at VPC or firewall@@@Information about the network rules for an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service node at the VPC or firewall level...","saas/aws_orgs_req_permissions.html@@@Required permissions for AWS Organization@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to retrieve the AWS Organization hierarchy...","saas/aws_perm_model_privilege_elevation.html@@@Permission model and privilege elevation for AWS@@@RSC provides a least permission model for AWS cloud accounts, granting minimal necessary permissions, starting with read-only access. You can add the Basic permission category initially and elevate permissions for recovery operations when required...","saas/aws_permission_categories.html@@@Permissions categories for AWS workloads@@@RSC groups the permissions required from AWS into different categories, enabling you to manage permissions at a granular level and maintain a least-privilege posture...","saas/aws_permission_validation.html@@@AWS permission validation@@@RSC provides the permission validation feature to run on-demand checks for the AWS accounts added to RSC, proactively identifying missing permissions essential for protecting the AWS workloads...","saas/aws_plan_exocompute.html@@@Exocompute planning for self-managed AWS accounts@@@Exocompute for self-managed AWS accounts runs in your own AWS account, so the deployment, network, and encryption decisions are best made before you configure Exocompute...","saas/aws_planning_protection.html@@@Plan your AWS protection@@@Before setting up an AWS cloud account in RSC, it is necessary to plan the user and access management for designated RSC users. This planning also involves reviewing the permissions that RSC requires in your AWS environment to protect your AWS workloads...","saas/aws_prereq_cld_acc_setup.html@@@Prerequisites for AWS cloud account setup@@@Information about prerequisites that you must complete before adding AWS cloud accounts to RSC...","saas/aws_prereq_exocompute.html@@@Prerequisites for Exocompute on AWS@@@Before configuring Exocompute in AWS regions for an AWS account onboarded using the self-managed deployment model, where you provision and manage compute resources such as Exocompute in your own AWS account, ensure you have established a robust network setup and addressed encryption key requirements to enable secure communication and data protection...","saas/aws_primary_snapshot_retention.html@@@Primary snapshot retention for AWS workloads@@@Primary snapshot retention for AWS workloads ensures data protection and recoverability by allowing you to set various retention policies. These policies include retaining hourly, daily, monthly, and yearly snapshots to meet compliance, business continuity, and disaster recovery requirements...","saas/aws_protect_implementation.html@@@AWS protection implementation workflow@@@The AWS protection implementation workflow involves a structured approach to secure data management, starting with planning and preparation, followed by cloud account setup, infrastructure configuration, setup verification, workload protection, continuous management and optimization, and workload recovery...","saas/aws_protect_large_s3_buckets.html@@@Large Amazon S3 buckets protection@@@With RSC, you can protect Amazon S3 buckets with up to one billion objects...","saas/aws_protection_config.html@@@Configure AWS protection@@@After you have decided on the protection policies you want to configure, you can begin configuration by creating an SLA Domain and assigning protection to AWS workloads and AWS accounts...","saas/aws_protection_high_level_arch.html@@@High-level architecture for AWS protection@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects AWS workloads and the RSC AssumeRole workflow...","saas/aws_protection_limitations.html@@@AWS protection limitations@@@Information about RSC limitations for AWS protection and recovery...","saas/aws_protection_overview.html@@@AWS protection overview@@@RSC protects the following types of Amazon Web Services workloads: EC2 instances, EBS volumes, Amazon S3, Amazon RDS and Aurora databases, Amazon DynamoDB, AWS Glue Iceberg Tables, and AWS S3 Tables...","saas/aws_quick_links.html@@@Quick links for AWS workloads@@@Immediate access to important tasks and information, enabling quick setup, daily operations, and critical recovery...","saas/aws_rbac_cnp.html@@@RBAC for AWS cloud-native protection@@@Role-based Access Control for AWS cloud-native protection allows for precise access permissions on AWS workloads, thereby enhancing security...","saas/aws_rds.html@@@Manage Amazon RDS and Aurora databases@@@RSC protects the data and resources of Amazon RDS and Amazon Aurora databases...","saas/aws_rds_archival_verification.html@@@AWS RDS archival snapshot verification@@@As part of each AWS RDS database archiving, RSC automatically performs snapshot verification to confirm that the archived snapshot is recoverable...","saas/aws_rds_assigning_protection.html@@@Assigning protection to Amazon RDS@@@Assign a data protection policy to Amazon RDS and Aurora databases...","saas/aws_rds_changing_ondemand_snapshot_retention.html@@@Changing retention policy for on-demand snapshots@@@Change the retention policy for on-demand snapshots for a specific snapshot...","saas/aws_rds_changing_policy_based_snapshots.html@@@Changing retention policy for Amazon RDS policy-based snapshots@@@Change the retention policy of policy-based snapshots of the AWS-RDS objects with no SLA Domain...","saas/aws_rds_changing_retention_policy_relic_snapshots.html@@@Changing retention policy for Amazon RDS relic snapshots@@@Change the retention policy of the snapshots of Amazon RDS relic objects...","saas/aws_rds_continuous_backups.html@@@Continuous backups for Amazon RDS@@@To capture all changes in data and transaction logs for Amazon RDS and Aurora databases, you can enable continuous backups for point-in-time recovery using RSC or the AWS management Console...","saas/aws_rds_creating_tag_rules.html@@@Creating tag rules for Amazon RDS databases@@@Create and assign a tag rule to protect the Amazon RDS databases associated with an AWS account...","saas/aws_rds_cross_account_replication.html@@@Cross-account snapshot replication and export for Amazon RDS@@@RSC supports replication and export of Amazon RDS snapshots to another AWS account to ensure that all snapshots are available during disaster recovery or when the original snapshot is deleted or corrupted...","saas/aws_rds_database_details.html@@@Amazon RDS database details@@@The Amazon RDS database details page displays the protection status of the objects, snapshots details, object details, and events of Amazon RDS databases...","saas/aws_rds_deleting_cloud_account.html@@@Deleting permissions for an Amazon RDS cloud account@@@Delete permissions for an Amazon RDS account project and delete the RSC cloud account...","saas/aws_rds_deleting_ondemand_snapshot.html@@@Deleting Amazon RDS snapshots@@@Delete snapshots that have a Forever retention policy...","saas/aws_rds_deleting_tag_rules.html@@@Deleting tag rules for Amazon RDS databases@@@Delete a tag rule assigned to Amazon RDS databases associated with your AWS account...","saas/aws_rds_encryption_scenarios.html@@@Encryption scenarios for RDS snapshot replication or export@@@Information about encryption configurations required for same-region or cross-region replication and export of Amazon RDS snapshots...","saas/aws_rds_engine_version_selection.html@@@Amazon RDS and Aurora PostgreSQL export and recovery engine options@@@Engine version availability varies by engine type and snapshot type when you export or recover a snapshot. Selecting an unsupported version fails the export operation. Use this reference to identify the supported target versions and to understand the error messages that appear when an invalid version is chosen...","saas/aws_rds_eol_engine_versions.html@@@Support for end-of-life engine versions@@@When an AWS RDS engine version reaches end of standard support, AWS restricts the snapshot restore operations that RSC relies on for archiving and export. Learn how RSC continues to protect RDS PostgreSQL and Aurora PostgreSQL snapshots on deprecated versions, and what actions you can take when a version nears or reaches end of life...","saas/aws_rds_export_snapshots.html@@@Export RDS snapshots@@@You can retain or modify the target RDS instance settings when you export RDS on-demand, scheduled, or continuous snapshots, and archived snapshots for Amazon RDS PostgreSQL, Aurora PostgreSQL, Aurora MySQL, RDS MySQL, and RDS SQL Server database...","saas/aws_rds_exporting_snapshots.html@@@Exporting Amazon RDS snapshots@@@To create a point-in-time copy of an Amazon RDS database, export an Amazon RDS on-demand, scheduled, or continuous snapshot. For RDS PostgreSQL, Aurora PostgreSQL, RDS MySQL, Aurora MySQL, and RDS SQL Server databases, RSC supports exporting snapshots from primary and archived snapshots...","saas/aws_rds_import_s3_postgresql.html@@@Importing the recovered files into a PostgreSQL database@@@RSC writes the dump files to your S3 bucket and you run the import into a PostgreSQL server of your choice...","saas/aws_rds_ip_plan_exocompute.html@@@IP address planning for Exocompute on RDS@@@For the Exocompute on AWS feature that uses Elastic Kubernetes Service clusters as the underlying compute resources, depending on your Amazon RDS databases, you need to plan the number of IP addresses required for your cluster nodes and use a subnet size accordingly...","saas/aws_rds_quota_prereq_archiving.html@@@Quotas prerequisites for Amazon RDS archiving@@@Information about the Amazon RDS instance quotas prerequisites for archiving Amazon RDS PostgreSQL, Aurora PostgreSQL, RDS MySQL, Aurora MySQL, and RDS SQL Server databases...","saas/aws_rds_recover_to_s3.html@@@Archived snapshot to Amazon S3 recovery use cases@@@Understand when to use Export to S3, the output file layout written to your Amazon S3 bucket, and the bucket and encryption behavior to consider before you start...","saas/aws_rds_recovery.html@@@Amazon RDS recovery@@@You can recover Amazon RDS, Aurora, Aurora PostgreSQL, Aurora MySQL, RDS MySQL, and RDS SQL Server databases using the various recovery options that RSC provides...","saas/aws_rds_recovery_considerations.html@@@Amazon RDS recovery considerations@@@Review the recovery behavior before recovering Amazon RDS and Aurora databases...","saas/aws_rds_recovery_options.html@@@Recovery options for Amazon RDS@@@RSC provides two recovery options for Amazon RDS and Aurora databases. Point-in-time export ensures recovery within the same region based on continuous backups, while snapshot export supports recovery within the same region or across regions using on-demand or scheduled snapshots...","saas/aws_rds_required_permissions.html@@@Required permissions for Amazon RDS databases@@@RSC requires certain permissions to protect Amazon RDS databases...","saas/aws_rds_snapshot_types.html@@@Snapshot types@@@To protect and manage your data in RSC, based on your requirements, you can take an on-demand snapshot, configure an SLA Domain to take scheduled snapshots and continuous snapshots for point-in-time recovery (PITR), or both, and archived snapshots...","saas/aws_rds_taking_ods.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshot of an Amazon RDS database@@@In addition to policy based snapshots, manually initiate an on-demand snapshot of the Amazon RDS database...","saas/aws_rds_upgrade_eol_snapshot.html@@@Upgrading AWS RDS snapshots for end-of-life engine version@@@Upgrade an AWS RDS snapshot that is on an end-of-life engine version to a supported minor version or a newer major version, instead of using the version that RSC selects automatically...","saas/aws_rds_view_database_details.html@@@Viewing the Amazon RDS database details page@@@To view information about an Amazon RDS database, access the database details page...","saas/aws_recommendations_add_cloud_acc.html@@@Recommendations for adding AWS cloud account@@@Rubrik recommends specific actions when adding AWS cloud accounts to RSC...","saas/aws_recover_ec2_ebs.html@@@Recover Amazon EC2 instances@@@You can recover your Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes using options such as recovering files or folders, exporting, and restoring...","saas/aws_recovery_assigning_perm_cat.html@@@Assigning a permission category for AWS recovery@@@When you are performing recovery operations such as exporting, restoring, or recovering files and the target AWS account does not have the required permission category, you must assign the permission category to ensure recovery...","saas/aws_recovery_privilege_elevation.html@@@Privilege elevation for AWS recovery@@@RSC provides you with an option to secure AWS cloud accounts by using a least permission model, granting minimal necessary permissions starting with the Basic permission category. For recovery operations, you can elevate permissions by including permission categories and updating the IAM role in your AWS environment...","saas/aws_refreshing_account.html@@@Refreshing an AWS account@@@Besides the periodic background job that RSC runs every three hours, you can refresh the metadata for your AWS account on demand if required...","saas/aws_region_level_sla_domain_assignment.html@@@Region level SLA Domain assignment for AWS@@@You can apply a unified policy to an entire AWS region with a region-level SLA Domain assignment, ensuring any new resource in that region is automatically protected...","saas/aws_removing_role_chaining_account.html@@@Removing an AWS role chaining account@@@Permanently remove an AWS role chaining account from RSC when it is no longer needed...","saas/aws_req_perms_cc_es.html@@@Required permissions for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services@@@Information about specific permissions AWS automatically applies to the Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage instance when you add the AWS cloud account to RSC. These permissions correspond to the roles and resources that RSC creates for cluster operation when you add the cloud account...","saas/aws_req_rbk_perms_cloud_acc.html@@@Required RSC permissions for AWS cloud accounts@@@RSC requires specific permissions in your AWS environment to protect the AWS workloads...","saas/aws_required_permissions_native_protection.html@@@Required permissions for native AWS protection@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to protect AWS workloads...","saas/aws_required_permissions_storage_tiering.html@@@Required permissions for AWS storage tiering@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to perform storage tiering...","saas/aws_required_perms_exocompute.html@@@Required permissions for AWS Exocompute@@@Information about permissions that RSC requires to configure an AWS Exocompute instance for self-managed accounts, EKS worker nodes, and KMS permissions...","saas/aws_required_perms_exocompute_2.html@@@Required permissions for AWS Exocompute@@@Information about permissions that RSC requires to configure an AWS Exocompute instance for self-managed accounts, EKS worker nodes, and KMS permissions...","saas/aws_restoring_access_role_chaining.html@@@Restoring access to a revoked role chaining account@@@After revoking access, you can restore RSC access to your AWS accounts by reverting the IAM trust policy modification on the AWS role chaining account...","saas/aws_retention_lock.html@@@Retention lock for AWS workloads@@@A retention lock on an SLA Domain is a security feature that prevents premature deletion of AWS snapshots...","saas/aws_revoking_access_role_chaining_acc.html@@@Revoking access to an AWS role chaining account@@@Temporarily revoke RSC access to your AWS environment by modifying its IAM trust policy of your AWS role chaining account...","saas/aws_role_chaining.html@@@AWS role chaining@@@With the AWS role chaining feature, RSC introduces a dedicated AWS account that serves as a centralized gateway to securely manage multiple AWS accounts from a single administrative point...","saas/aws_role_customization_fields.html@@@AWS role customization fields@@@Information about the role names and paths you must specify to use the AWS role customization option...","saas/aws_rsc_managed_creating_sla.html@@@Creating an RSC-managed SLA Domain for AWS@@@Create a custom SLA Domain for AWS accounts that use the RSC-managed deployment model, so that RSC archives your backups to Rubrik Cloud Vault or to storage that you own...","saas/aws_rsc_managed_terraform.html@@@Adding an RSC-managed AWS account using Terraform@@@Add an AWS account that uses the RSC-managed deployment model by using the RSC provider for Terraform...","saas/aws_rubrik_hosted_ecr_pcr.html@@@Rubrik-hosted ECR versus PCR@@@Overview of the Rubrik-hosted Elastic Container Registry and a Private Container Registry for AWS...","saas/aws_s3_storage_classes.html@@@Amazon S3 storage classes@@@RSC supports six Amazon S3 storage classes to meet different storage requirements...","saas/aws_s3_storage_classes_2.html@@@Amazon S3 storage classes@@@RSC supports six Amazon S3 storage classes to meet different storage requirements...","saas/aws_scp_restrictions.html@@@AWS SCP restrictions@@@Service control policies can restrict actions in AWS environments, potentially obstructing RSC operations such as S3 bucket creation. Understanding and adjusting these policies ensures RSC functionality while maintaining security and compliance...","saas/aws_sec_grp_network_rules.html@@@Network rules for AWS security groups@@@Information about the networking rules that RSC configures for Polaris-Exocompute-eks-worker-node and Polaris-Exocompute-eks-control-plane security groups...","saas/aws_secondary_subnets_eks_pods.html@@@Secondary subnets for EKS cluster pods@@@When setting up Exocompute for Rubrik-managed clusters, it is recommended to add secondary subnets for EKS cluster pods. This helps prevent IP address exhaustion by keeping pod IP addresses separate from other resources, simplifying network management, and ensuring job stability...","saas/aws_sharing_cust_kms_exo_host_acc.html@@@Sharing AWS custom KMS keys with Exocompute host account@@@If your source snapshot is encrypted using an AWS custom KMS key in the application account, you need to share this key with the centralized Exocompute host account...","saas/aws_sharing_keys_cross_acc_replication.html@@@Sharing KMS keys for cross-account operations@@@When replicating or exporting AWS EC2 instance and EBS volume snapshots to a different account, you must share the customer-managed KMS keys with the target AWS account to enable RSC to read the encrypted snapshot in the target account...","saas/aws_single_vpc_checklist.html@@@AWS single VPC checklist@@@Information about the network configurations to validate when you are using a single AWS VPC...","saas/aws_snapshot_storage_pmk_encrypted_wkl.html@@@Snapshot storage for PMK-encrypted AWS workloads@@@For AWS workloads, such as EC2 instances and EBS volumes encrypted with a platform-managed key, RSC re-encrypts snapshots using the gateway KMS key when Exocompute tasks such as archiving, indexing, or cross-account replication are configured, and stores the re-encrypted copy as the primary snapshot...","saas/aws_stackset_prereq.html@@@AWS StackSets prerequisites@@@Bulk addition of AWS cloud accounts option uses AWS StackSets to create or update stacks across multiple cloud accounts in an AWS Organization. You must meet certain AWS prerequisites for a successful deployment and management of AWS StackSets...","saas/aws_storage_tiering_evaluate_options.html@@@Evaluate AWS storage tiering options@@@Before setting up AWS storage tiering, it is important to evaluate the tiering options to align with archiving needs, balancing cost, performance, and data retrieval. Key considerations include Amazon S3 storage classes, instant tiering, and encryption standards...","saas/aws_storage_tiering_setup.html@@@Set up AWS storage tiering@@@You can use AWS storage tiering to archive Amazon EC2 instance, EBS volume, or DynamoDB table snapshots that exceed a specified threshold to Amazon S3 storage classes. By archiving snapshots to these storage classes, you can optimize costs...","saas/aws_supported_regions_onboarding_cft.html@@@Supported AWS regions for CFT-based onboarding@@@RSC supports a specific set of AWS regions for deploying CloudFormation templates during the cloud account onboarding process...","saas/aws_tags.html@@@AWS tags@@@RSC attaches specific tags to the AWS resources you create using RSC...","saas/aws_updating_indv_acc_perms_template.html@@@Updating an individual AWS account permissions by template@@@Update permissions for an individual AWS cloud account to ensure that the required permissions for the new features are included in RSC. You can use the AWS CloudFormation template to update the permissions. You can also remove permissions that are no longer needed...","saas/aws_updating_perms_org_acc.html@@@Updating permissions for AWS Organization accounts@@@Update permissions for all the AWS cloud accounts that are added using an AWS Organization to ensure that the required permissions for the new features are included in RSC. You can use the AWS CloudFormation template to update the permissions. You can also remove the permissions that are no longer needed...","saas/aws_validating_permissions.html@@@Validating permissions for AWS accounts@@@Run the on-demand validation permission for AWS accounts to identify any missing permissions necessary for cloud-native protection of AWS workloads...","saas/aws_verify_account_setup.html@@@Verifying your AWS account setup@@@Confirm that the AWS account is connected, that RSC discovers your workloads, and that the permissions are in place before you assign protection...","saas/aws_verifying_vpc_config.html@@@Verifying your Amazon VPC configuration@@@Verify your Amazon VPC configuration to ensure DNS settings, subnet distribution, and endpoint associations are correctly set up...","saas/aws_viewing_exocompute_details_page.html@@@Viewing details of Exocompute on AWS@@@To add or delete regions, review the details of an AWS Exocompute configuration...","saas/aws_vpc_interface_endpoints.html@@@AWS VPC interface endpoints@@@An AWS VPC interface endpoint enables private access to AWS services within a VPC, enhancing security, reducing latency, and simplifying network architecture by utilizing AWS PrivateLink and Elastic Network Interfaces. Rubrik Exocompute leverages these endpoints for secure, efficient data management operations...","saas/aws_workload_recovery.html@@@Recover AWS workloads@@@After RSC takes snapshots of your AWS workloads, you can recover the required workloads...","saas/aws_workloads.html@@@Amazon Web Services workloads@@@RSC protects the following types of Amazon Web Services workloads: EC2 instances, EBS volumes, Amazon S3, Amazon RDS and Aurora databases, Amazon DynamoDB, AWS Glue Iceberg Tables, and AWS S3 Tables...","saas/aws_workloads_protection_setup.html@@@Set up AWS workloads protection@@@You can set up SLA Domains to apply data protection policies, ensuring automatic and hierarchical protection of AWS accounts and individual AWS workloads, with granular control overriding higher-level assignments...","saas/azr_activating_exocompute_cluster.html@@@Activating an Exocompute cluster on Azure@@@Activate an Exocompute cluster in a specific region to bring up the Azure Kubernetes Service cluster when it is not yet deployed or has been deactivated...","saas/azr_adding_api_perms_ms_entra_app.html@@@Adding API permissions to Microsoft Entra application@@@After you have created a Microsoft Entra application for Rubrik, you must add API permissions to that application...","saas/azr_adding_client_secret.html@@@Adding a client secret@@@After you have added the required API permissions to the Microsoft Entra application for Rubrik, you must add a client secret to that application...","saas/azr_adding_cloud_account_akv_manager.html@@@Adding a cloud account\u2014based Azure Key Vault key manager@@@Add a cloud account\u2014based Azure Key Vault key manager to give RSC access to your Azure Key Vault key for client-side encrypted cloud-native archival locations...","saas/azr_adding_subs_mgmt_grp_oauth.html@@@Adding Azure subscriptions using management group with OAuth@@@Add multiple Azure subscriptions using an Azure management group with the Configure with OAuth method. This method uses OAuth for authentication and automatically configures the required roles and permissions...","saas/azr_adding_subs_mgmt_grp_without_oauth.html@@@Adding Azure subscriptions using management group without OAuth@@@Add multiple Azure subscriptions using an Azure management group with the Configure without OAuth method. This method requires you to grant elevated permissions in the Azure portal before proceeding with the onboarding...","saas/azr_adv_exo_settings_aks_clusters.html@@@Advanced settings for Exocompute on Azure@@@For better performance, scalability, and advanced security features such as encryption at the host where Azure encrypts data before it is written to storage disks, you can optionally configure advanced Exocompute settings using RSC...","saas/azr_aks_container_repos.html@@@Container repositories for Exocompute on Azure@@@Exocompute on Azure uses Azure Kubernetes Service clusters to perform operations, managing them using Docker containers from Azure Container Registries hosted by Rubrik and Microsoft for efficient deployment and management...","saas/azr_archiving_workloads.html@@@Archiving of Azure workloads@@@Archiving in RSC tiers Azure virtual machine or managed disk snapshots to lower-cost storage, ensuring cost savings, compliance, and security...","saas/azr_assigning_kv_perms_mi.html@@@Assigning key vault permissions to a managed identity@@@To ensure your managed identity has the correct data-plane permissions to access encryption keys across resource groups, you must create a dedicated access policy on the Azure key vault...","saas/azr_assigning_protection_sub_rg.html@@@Assigning protection to Azure subscriptions or resource groups@@@Assign a data protection policy at the Azure subscription or resource group level...","saas/azr_assigning_protection_vm_md.html@@@Assigning protection to Azure virtual machines or managed disks@@@Assign a data protection policy to specific Azure virtual machines or managed disks...","saas/azr_auto_vs_manual_network_setup.html@@@Automated versus manual networking setup@@@Overview of networking setup options for Exocompute on Azure...","saas/azr_best_practices_sla_assignment.html@@@Best practices for Azure SLA Domain assignment@@@Information about the best practices for assigning SLA Domains to Azure workloads, ensuring effective data protection and compliance...","saas/azr_bulk_vs_indv_cloud_acc_addition.html@@@Bulk versus individual Azure cloud account addition@@@A comparative overview of bulk and individual addition of Azure cloud accounts, including management group onboarding...","saas/azr_changing_retention_policy_relic_snapshots.html@@@Changing retention policy for Azure relic snapshots@@@Change the retention policy of snapshots of Azure relic objects...","saas/azr_cld_acc_add_mgmt_grp_oauth.html@@@Azure cloud account addition using management group with OAuth@@@You can add multiple Azure subscriptions using an Azure management group with the Configure with OAuth method. This method uses OAuth for authentication and automatically configures the required roles and permissions...","saas/azr_cld_acc_add_mgmt_grp_without_oauth.html@@@Azure cloud account addition with management group without OAuth@@@You can add multiple Azure subscriptions using an Azure management group with the Configure without OAuth method. This method requires you to manually configure the service principal permissions in the Azure portal before onboarding...","saas/azr_cloud_acc_addition_terraform.html@@@Azure cloud account addition using Terraform@@@You can add multiple Azure cloud accounts to RSC at once using the RSC provider for Terraform...","saas/azr_cloud_acc_addition_without_oauth.html@@@Azure cloud account addition without OAuth@@@You can set up an Azure cloud account on RSC using the Configure without OAuth method and start protecting your Azure workloads...","saas/azr_cloud_acc_setup.html@@@Set up Azure cloud accounts@@@You can set up an Azure cloud account in RSC to start protecting Azure workloads...","saas/azr_cloud_accounts_page_details.html@@@Azure cloud account page details@@@The tabs, filters, and use case statuses on the Azure subscriptions page in RSC show which Azure subscriptions are onboarded and which need a permission update...","saas/azr_cloud_discovery.html@@@Azure cloud discovery@@@The cloud discovery feature provides a read-only view of Azure resources in RSC. This feature separates workload discovery from workload protection, so you can view all the resources that exist before choosing what to protect...","saas/azr_cnp_arch.html@@@Cloud-native protection for Azure@@@A high-level architectural overview about how RSC protects the Azure workloads within your Azure subscription...","saas/azr_cnp_archival_encryption_options.html@@@Encryption options for Azure cloud-native archival@@@RSC supports server-side encryption using a cloud provider\u2014managed key or a customer-managed key. It also supports client-side encryption using your own Azure Key Vault key for Azure cloud-native archival locations...","saas/azr_cnp_client_side_encryption.html@@@Client-side encryption for Azure Blob Storage@@@Client-side encryption protects archived Azure Blob Storage data using your own Azure Key Vault key before the data leaves the Exocompute environment in your Azure subscription and reaches cloud storage...","saas/azr_cnp_client_side_encryption_vm.html@@@Client-side encryption for Azure virtual machines@@@Client-side encryption protects archived Azure virtual machine data using your Azure Key Vault key before the data leaves the Exocompute environment in your Azure subscription and reaches cloud storage...","saas/azr_comm_rbk_azr_subscription.html@@@Communication between RSC and Azure subscription@@@A high-level architecture overview of how RSC communicates with your Azure subscription when using the Configure with OAuth method for Azure cloud account setup. It details the use of Service Principals, custom roles, and the trust relationship established between Microsoft Entra ID and RSC for secure operations...","saas/azr_common_protection_terms.html@@@Common Azure protection terms@@@It is important to understand some common terms when protecting Azure workloads with RSC...","saas/azr_config_method_cloud_acct.html@@@Configuration methods for Azure cloud account@@@A comparative overview of the Configure without OAuth and Configure with OAuth methods for adding an Azure cloud account to RSC...","saas/azr_config_storage_tiering.html@@@Configure Azure storage tiering@@@To configure Azure storage tiering, you must create an archival location or a Rubrik Cloud Vault location for archiving snapshots and storing backups. Additionally, you can configure a private or service endpoint to tier snapshots to an Azure storage account...","saas/azr_configuration_cloud_acc.html@@@Configure Azure cloud accounts@@@Start the configuration of your Azure cloud accounts by adding them to RSC and performing other maintenance operations, such as editing and upgrading accounts...","saas/azr_configuration_exocompute.html@@@Configure Exocompute on Azure@@@The configuration workflow sequence for localized and centralized Exocompute, Rubrik-hosted ACR, and Rubrik-managed AKS cluster. This workflow is applicable only if you have chosen the manual networking setup...","saas/azr_configuring_exo_host_acct_rmc.html@@@Configuring Exocompute for Rubrik-managed clusters@@@After creating an Exocompute host account for a Rubrik-managed cluster, configure an Exocompute instance in the host account by adding a region...","saas/azr_configuring_private_endpoint.html@@@Configuring an Azure private endpoint for storage tiering@@@Configure an Azure private endpoint to tier snapshots to an archival location with a region-specific setting...","saas/azr_configuring_specific_settings_sp.html@@@Configuring specific settings for the service principal@@@After you have added a client secret to the Microsoft Entra application for Rubrik, you need to configure specific settings for the service principal associated with that application...","saas/azr_configuring_udr_fw.html@@@Configuring User Defined Routing with Azure firewall@@@Configure User Defined Routing for Azure Kubernetes Service clusters to manage outbound traffic through an Azure firewall. This setup ensures compliance with Azure policies by routing traffic through defined routes, eliminating the need for public IP addresses for AKS nodes...","saas/azr_creating_arch_loc_storage_acc.html@@@Creating a customer-controlled archival location for Azure storage accounts@@@Create an archival location for the Azure storage account created for archiving the Azure virtual machine or managed disk snapshots and for storing Azure SQL backups...","saas/azr_creating_blob_arch_loc_storage_acc.html@@@Creating an archival location for Azure Blob Storage@@@Create a cloud-native archival location for the Azure storage account to store your Azure Blob Storage backups...","saas/azr_creating_cld_acc_data_scanning.html@@@Creating an Azure cloud account for Data scanning@@@Create an Azure cloud account in RSC for protection, and then enable Data scanning. Data scanning helps you manage cloud posture risks...","saas/azr_creating_cloud_account_oauth.html@@@Creating Azure cloud accounts with OAuth@@@Create an Azure cloud account with OAuth configuration in RSC to protect Azure resources using a Microsoft Entra ID application...","saas/azr_creating_cloud_account_without_oauth.html@@@Creating Azure cloud accounts without OAuth@@@To protect your Azure resources by using a Microsoft Entra ID application, create an Azure cloud account without OAuth configuration in RSC...","saas/azr_creating_custom_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for Azure@@@Create a custom role with Role-based Access Control privileges for managing your Azure workloads. These privileges provide finer granularity for determining which permissions an RSC user has for performing specific actions on specific objects...","saas/azr_creating_key_vault_target_region.html@@@Creating Azure key vaults in the target region@@@Create an Azure key vault in the target Azure region to securely store encryption keys...","saas/azr_creating_ms_entra_app_rbk.html@@@Creating a Microsoft Entra application for Rubrik@@@Create a Microsoft Entra application for Rubrik if you have opted for the Configure without OAuth or the manual method of adding an Azure cloud account...","saas/azr_creating_ms_entra_grp_wo_oauth.html@@@Creating a Microsoft Entra group for Exocompute without OAuth@@@When you use Microsoft Entra ID to authenticate Exocompute on Azure instances without OAuth, create a Microsoft Entra group containing the service principal for the enterprise application you created for the Rubrik cluster. Microsoft Entra ID uses the object ID of this group to authenticate the Exocompute on Azure subscription...","saas/azr_creating_tag_rules.html@@@Creating a tag rule for Azure virtual machines or managed disks@@@Create a tag rule to protect the Azure virtual machines or managed disks by specifying combinations of tag keys and values, and assign a protection setting to that tag rule...","saas/azr_creating_user_assigned_mi_storage.html@@@Creating a user-assigned managed identity for storage@@@Create a user-assigned managed identity if you are adding an Azure cloud account for the storage use case...","saas/azr_creating_vnet.html@@@Creating a VNet@@@Create a VNet on the Azure portal to configure localized or centralized Exocompute with Rubrik-hosted ACR and Rubrik-managed AKS clusters...","saas/azr_cross_region_export_ade_vm.html@@@Cross-region export of ADE virtual machines@@@Cross-region export of Azure Disk Encryption-enabled virtual machines involves securely migrating encryption keys and secrets to a new key vault in the target Azure region...","saas/azr_custom_tag.html@@@Azure custom tags@@@You can specify Azure custom tags in RSC to implement specific policies for cost allocation, financial management, and resource creation...","saas/azr_customer_arch_loc_versus_rcv.html@@@Customer-controlled archival location versus RCV@@@A comparative overview of the customer-controlled archival location and Rubrik Cloud Vault...","saas/azr_deleting_account.html@@@Removing an Azure cloud account@@@Remove an Azure cloud account by removing all active use cases for that subscription...","saas/azr_deleting_cloud_discovery.html@@@Deleting cloud discovery for Azure@@@Delete cloud discovery when you want to remove an Azure account integration with RSC or stop metadata collection...","saas/azr_deleting_exocompute_subscription.html@@@Deleting the Exocompute on Azure host subscription@@@After you have unmapped an Exocompute on Azure host subscription from its associated application subscriptions, delete the Exocompute host subscription from the Azure page...","saas/azr_deleting_ondemand_snapshot.html@@@Deleting an on-demand snapshot@@@Delete snapshots from an Azure VM or managed disk when they are no longer required...","saas/azr_deleting_relic_snapshot.html@@@Deleting snapshots of relic Azure virtual machines@@@Delete a snapshot of a relic Azure virtual machine...","saas/azr_deleting_tag_rules.html@@@Deleting a tag rule for Azure virtual machines@@@Delete a tag rule assigned to the Azure virtual machines or managed disks...","saas/azr_downloading_backup_source_kv.html@@@Downloading backup of the source Azure key vault@@@Download backup files for both keys and secrets from the source Azure key vault to export them to the target Azure key vault...","saas/azr_editing_cloud_account.html@@@Editing an Azure cloud account@@@Edit the details of an Azure cloud account configured with or without OAuth...","saas/azr_editing_cnp_archival_location.html@@@Editing a customer-controlled Azure cloud-native archival location@@@Edit the name, storage tier, network access, and storage tags of a customer-controlled Azure cloud-native archival location and view its encryption settings...","saas/azr_editing_exo_host_acct_rmc.html@@@Editing Exocompute for Rubrik-managed clusters@@@For an Azure Exocompute host account created for a Rubrik-managed cluster where the Exocompute instance is already configured, edit the configuration to specify different regions...","saas/azr_editing_policy_exemption.html@@@Editing an existing Azure policy for exemption@@@Edit an existing Azure policy to allow the creation of public IP addresses in the Azure Kubernetes Service node resource group...","saas/azr_editing_rcv_cnp_archival_location.html@@@Editing an Azure Rubrik Cloud Vault cloud-native archival location@@@Edit the name and redundancy of an Azure Rubrik Cloud Vault cloud-native archival location, and view its encryption settings...","saas/azr_encryp_mgmt_cloud_locations_tab.html@@@Azure cloud archival location encryption details@@@Reference information for the Cloud locations view in Encryption Management, including column definitions for encryption type, rekey status, and per-region encryption detail for Azure archival locations...","saas/azr_entra_domain_mapping_moving_subs.html@@@Microsoft Entra Domain mapping after moving subscriptions@@@After moving Azure subscriptions to a different Microsoft Entra Domain on the Azure portal, you must update the domain mapping, upgrade permissions for the moved subscriptions in RSC, and recreate the Entra ID group within the new Microsoft Entra ID domain to avoid data protection failures...","saas/azr_ephemeral_vm_exclusion_from_discovery.html@@@Azure ephemeral VMs exclusion from discovery@@@RSC excludes ephemeral Azure virtual machines and managed disks created by supported third-party services from discovery, based on vendor-specific resource tags that the third-party services automatically apply. This keeps protection focused on your own long-lived workloads, prevents wasted protection effort on short-lived resources that will soon be deleted, and reduces unnecessary discovery load on RSC...","saas/azr_evaluate_options_cloud_acc_setup.html@@@Evaluate Azure cloud account setup options@@@When adding an Azure cloud account to RSC, it is important to evaluate the available options for adding the account, including data scanning capabilities...","saas/azr_evaluate_options_workload_protect.html@@@Evaluate Azure workload protection options@@@Understanding the various Azure workload protection options when creating an SLA Domain enables you to make informed decisions and ensure effective data protection...","saas/azr_excluding_managed_disks_from_vm.html@@@Excluding protection for specific managed disks@@@Exclude specific managed disks while protecting other managed disks attached to an Azure virtual machine instance...","saas/azr_excom_firewall_config.html@@@Firewall configuration for Exocompute on Azure@@@Information about the endpoints you can add to the firewall allowlist so that Exocompute on Azure can perform archiving and indexing operations...","saas/azr_exo_cost_best_practices.html@@@Best practices for reducing Exocompute on Azure costs@@@Configuring your Azure network, storage, and cluster settings correctly can significantly reduce ongoing costs when using Exocompute on Azure for archiving and data protection operations...","saas/azr_exocompute.html@@@Set up Exocompute on Azure@@@With the Exocompute on Azure feature, RSC launches an Azure Kubernetes Service cluster to perform various operations to protect Azure workloads. RSC uses the Azure Kubernetes Service cluster to serve as a compute resource in your Azure subscription...","saas/azr_exocompute_common_terms.html@@@Common terms for Exocompute on Azure@@@Understanding certain common terms associated with the Rubrik Exocompute on Azure feature is important when configuring Exocompute on Azure...","saas/azr_exocompute_details.html@@@Exocompute on Azure details@@@The Exocompute on Azure details page displays the list of Exocompute host subscriptions and application subscriptions and their details...","saas/azr_exocompute_editing_oauth.html@@@Editing an Exocompute subscription on Azure with OAuth@@@When using Microsoft Entra ID authentication, you can update an Exocompute on Azure instance configured with OAuth...","saas/azr_exocompute_editing_wo_oauth.html@@@Editing Exocompute on Azure without OAuth@@@When you use Microsoft Entra ID authentication, edit the subscription name or group object ID for Exocompute on an Azure instance configured without OAuth...","saas/azr_exocompute_evaluate_choices.html@@@Evaluate Exocompute on Azure options@@@When setting up Exocompute on Azure, it is important to evaluate the options for deployment and networking. Thorough evaluation of these choices helps to align them with the needs of your organization prior to Exocompute configuration...","saas/azr_exocompute_health_check.html@@@Exocompute health check for Azure@@@The Exocompute health check for Azure feature in RSC runs a health check for an Azure Kubernetes Service cluster immediately after its configuration and displays the current status of the cluster. With the health check feature, you can determine if the Azure Kubernetes Service cluster is functioning correctly...","saas/azr_exocompute_health_check_status.html@@@Health check statuses for Exocompute on Azure@@@Information about the various health check statuses for Exocompute on Azure...","saas/azr_exocompute_local_central.html@@@Localized versus centralized Exocompute on Azure@@@Overview of deployment models for Exocompute on Azure...","saas/azr_exocompute_network_choices.html@@@Network choices for Exocompute on Azure@@@Information about network settings for Excompute on Azure required for seamless integration and optimal operation...","saas/azr_exocompute_network_setup.html@@@Set up network for Exocompute on Azure@@@When you choose the manual networking setup, you must manually configure all Virtual Networks, subnets, and security rules to align with requirements of Rubrik. This setup is essential for the Exocompute on Azure feature to ensure seamless communication between RSC, the AKS cluster, and Azure services...","saas/azr_exocompute_quota_reqs.html@@@Exocompute on Azure vCPU quota requirements@@@Azure vCPU quotas limit virtual CPU allocations for a subscription to manage resources and prevent monopolization. Adequate quotas for Exocompute ensure uninterrupted operations...","saas/azr_exporting_relic_snapshots.html@@@Exporting relic snapshots@@@Export a snapshot of a relic Azure virtual machine...","saas/azr_exporting_vm_snapshot.html@@@Exporting Azure virtual machine snapshots@@@Export a snapshot of an Azure virtual machine to create a virtual machine from a point-in-time copy of the source virtual machine...","saas/azr_file_indexing.html@@@File indexing for Azure virtual machines@@@RSC uses Exocompute instances to extract file system index metadata from the managed disk snapshots created while protecting Azure virtual machines or managed disks...","saas/azr_granting_perms_servc_prin_mgmt_grp.html@@@Granting permissions to service principal for management group onboarding@@@Before you onboard Azure subscriptions using a management group with the Configure without OAuth method, grant the required elevated permissions to the service principal in the Azure portal...","saas/azr_granting_perms_users_mgmt_grp.html@@@Granting permissions to user for management group onboarding@@@Before you onboard Azure subscriptions using a management group with the Configure with OAuth method, grant the required permissions to the user performing the onboarding in the Azure portal...","saas/azr_hierarchy_sla_assignment.html@@@SLA Domain assignment hierarchy for Azure@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based, automatic protection for Azure workloads, simplifying the assignment of protection across various levels such as subscriptions, resource groups, and individual workloads...","saas/azr_ifr_prereq.html@@@Prerequisites for Azure In-place File Recovery@@@Information about prerequisites that you must fulfill before performing an Azure in-place file recovery...","saas/azr_in_place_file_recovery.html@@@Azure In-place File Recovery@@@With the In-place File Recovery feature, you can recover Azure files from an indexed snapshot either to a source virtual machine or a different virtual machine or export the files to a different virtual machine...","saas/azr_instant_tiering.html@@@Azure instant tiering@@@RSC provides the capability to instantly tier the Azure virtual machine or managed disk snapshots to the specified archival location...","saas/azr_ip_planning_aks_cluster.html@@@IP address planning for Exocompute on Azure@@@For the Exocompute on Azure feature that uses Azure Kubernetes Service clusters as the underlying compute resources, depending on your workloads, you need to plan the number of IP addresses required for your cluster nodes and use a subnet size accordingly...","saas/azr_key_features_protection.html@@@Key features for protecting Azure workloads@@@RSC provides unified data management, automated global data protection, various recovery options for Azure workloads, and additional security features to protect your workloads...","saas/azr_kv_perms_cross_rg_deployment.html@@@Azure key vault permissions for cross-resource group deployments@@@Deploying Azure resources with key vaults in separate resource groups enhances security by enforcing least privilege. You must ensure managed identity access by assigning a dedicated access policy on the key vault...","saas/azr_limitations.html@@@File recovery limitations@@@File indexing and recovery have certain limitations...","saas/azr_maintenance_and_cleanup.html@@@Maintain Exocompute on Azure@@@Maintaining Exocompute on Azure involves regularly reviewing and updating settings and removing obsolete configurations to ensure optimal performance and resource management...","saas/azr_manage_vm_md.html@@@Manage Azure virtual machines@@@After completing the protection setup for Azure virtual machines and managed disks, RSC takes automated snapshots of those virtual machines and disks based on the configured policies in SLA Domains. You can also take on-demand snapshots, refresh Azure subscriptions, and add Azure custom tags for better resource management...","saas/azr_managing_exocompute_mapping.html@@@Mapping Azure accounts to centralized Exocompute@@@After you have configured an Exocompute instance in the Exocompute host subscription by adding regions and confirmed that the Azure Kubernetes Service cluster is healthy, map an application subscription to an Exocompute host subscription from the Azure page. Update or remove an existing mapping as required...","saas/azr_managing_file_indexing.html@@@Managing file indexing for all available snapshots@@@Manage file indexing for Azure virtual machines or managed disks by turning on or turning off file indexing. Turning on file indexing facilitates quick file recovery by allowing you to search across indexed snapshots and initiate recovery without waiting for file indexing to complete. When it is no longer needed, you can turn off file indexing...","saas/azr_managing_global_tags.html@@@Managing global tags for Azure subscriptions@@@Manage global tags by assigning custom tags or configuring tag exclusion rules that apply across all Azure subscriptions added to RSC...","saas/azr_mgmt_group_onboarding.html@@@Management group onboarding for Azure subscriptions@@@An overview of how RSC uses Azure management groups to onboard multiple Azure subscriptions in bulk, including how onboarding works, available methods, and ongoing permission management...","saas/azr_mgmt_group_req_permissions.html@@@Required permissions for onboarding Azure management group@@@Information about the Azure permissions that RSC requires to retrieve the management group hierarchy and onboard subscriptions through a management group...","saas/azr_mgmt_group_req_perms_custom_role_def.html@@@Required permissions for creating custom role definitions@@@To onboard Azure subscriptions through a management group, RSC creates custom Azure role definitions at the management group scope. This requires you to temporarily grant administrative permissions to the onboarding identity in the Azure portal...","saas/azr_migrating_existing_accounts_cloud_discovery_model.html@@@Migrating existing Azure subscriptions to cloud discovery model@@@Migrate existing Azure subscriptions to the cloud discovery model by updating the required permissions...","saas/azr_migrating_existing_subs_mgmt_grp.html@@@Migrating existing Azure subscriptions to management group@@@Migrate existing individually onboarded Azure subscriptions to an Azure management group to consolidate management and enable unified permission updates. The subscriptions must already belong to the target management group in the Azure portal...","saas/azr_modifying_access_control_target_kv.html@@@Modifying access control of the target Azure key vault@@@Modify the access control permissions in the target Azure key vault to enable backup and restore operations...","saas/azr_modifying_tag_secret_target_kv.html@@@Modifying the tag of restored secret in target Azure key vault@@@Modify the tag for the restored secret to reflect the key identifier of the target key vault to maintain encryption integrity...","saas/azr_multiple_arch_loc.html@@@Multiple archival locations for Azure@@@RSC supports multiple archival locations for Azure virtual machines and managed disks, allowing granular control over data archiving with up to two distinct archiving policies...","saas/azr_nw_config_cni_overlay.html@@@Network configuration for Azure CNI overlay@@@Information on configuring network settings, required ports, network rules, and dynamic ports for Azure CNI overlay to ensure proper functionality of Exocompute on Azure...","saas/azr_outbound_rules_nsg.html@@@Outbound rules for Azure network security group@@@Information about the minimal set of outbound rules for Azure virtual machines and Azure SQL workloads that require configuration on the network security group associated with the subnet used for the Exocompute on Azure feature...","saas/azr_performing_file_indexing.html@@@Performing file indexing for a specific snapshot@@@Perform file indexing for a snapshot of an Azure virtual machine or managed disk for enabling file recovery...","saas/azr_performing_in_place_file_recovery.html@@@Performing an Azure In-place File Recovery@@@To recover the files of an Azure virtual machine from an indexed snapshot to the source virtual machine or export the files to a different virtual machine, perform an In-place File Recovery...","saas/azr_perm_model_privilege_elevation.html@@@Permission model and privilege elevation for Azure@@@RSC provides a least permission model for Azure cloud accounts, granting minimal necessary permissions, starting with read-only access. You can add the Basic permission category initially and elevate permissions for recovery operations when required...","saas/azr_perm_validation.html@@@Azure permission validation@@@RSC provides the permission validation feature to run on-demand checks for all the Azure subscriptions added to RSC, proactively identifying missing permissions essential for protecting Azure workloads...","saas/azr_permission_categories.html@@@Permission categories for Azure workloads@@@For tasks that operate on Azure workloads, such as indexing, recovery, and storage tiering, RSC requires specific permissions. RSC groups these permissions into categories for granular management so that you can include or exclude these categories as required...","saas/azr_pol_review_exempt.html@@@Azure policies review and exemptions@@@You can review Azure policy assignments to identify rules blocking public IP address creation and provide exemptions for the Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) node resource group to ensure successful AKS cluster deployment...","saas/azr_primary_snapshot_retention.html@@@Primary snapshot retention for Azure workloads@@@Primary snapshot retention for Azure workloads ensures data protection and recoverability by allowing you to set various retention policies, such as retaining hourly, daily, monthly, and yearly snapshots, to meet compliance, business continuity, and disaster recovery requirements...","saas/azr_private_container_registry.html@@@Private Container Registry for Azure@@@For security purposes, when you do not want to retrieve Docker images from a registry hosted by Rubrik or when you want to scan the Docker images for CVEs, you can configure a Private Container Registry to retrieve these Docker images from a registry you host...","saas/azr_private_service_endpoints_usage_archival.html@@@Private and service endpoints usage for Azure storage tiering@@@You can reduce data transfer costs by tiering snapshots to an Azure storage account by using Azure private or service endpoints...","saas/azr_protect_implementation.html@@@Azure protection implementation workflow@@@A six-phase workflow for implementing Azure workload protection in RSC, from initial planning through workload recovery. The diagram provides a high-level overview of the complete workflow. You can select any phase to navigate directly to the corresponding documentation...","saas/azr_protecting_first_subscription.html@@@Protecting your first Azure subscription@@@Complete the minimum configuration steps to protect Azure virtual machines in RSC using Configure with OAuth and automated Exocompute networking...","saas/azr_protection_config.html@@@Configure Azure protection@@@After you have decided on the protection policies you want to configure, you can begin the protection setup by creating an SLA Domain and assigning protection to workloads, resource groups, and subscriptions...","saas/azr_protection_get_started.html@@@Get started with Azure workloads protection@@@RSC protects Azure workloads through a set of configuration steps that must be completed in a specific order. Cloud account setup, Exocompute configuration, network requirements, and SLA Domain assignment each depend on the previous step...","saas/azr_protection_high_level_arch.html@@@High-level architecture for Azure protection@@@A high-level architectural overview of how RSC protects Azure workloads and the RSC application registration workflow...","saas/azr_protection_planning.html@@@Plan your Azure protection@@@Before setting up an Azure cloud account in RSC, you are required to plan the user and access management for designated RSC users. This planning also involves reviewing the permissions that RSC requires in your Azure environment to protect your Azure workloads...","saas/azr_protection_rsc_user_management.html@@@RSC user management for Azure protection@@@Designating specific users with appropriate privileges and roles in RSC enhances security for managing Azure cloud accounts...","saas/azr_psql_adding_subscription.html@@@Adding an Azure subscription for Azure PostgreSQL@@@Add an Azure subscription to RSC to discover and protect Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Servers. Use this procedure whether you are setting up Azure PostgreSQL for the first time or adding another Azure subscription to an existing configuration...","saas/azr_psql_assigning_protection.html@@@Assigning protection to Azure PostgreSQL servers@@@Assign a data protection policy to individual or multiple Azure PostgreSQL servers...","saas/azr_psql_backup_capabilities.html@@@Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Server backup capabilities@@@RSC provides enterprise-grade data protection, backup, recovery, and compliance capabilities for Azure PostgreSQL servers...","saas/azr_psql_creating_sla.html@@@Creating an SLA Domain for Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Server@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to define the backup frequency, retention period, backup location, and log backup retention for Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Server protection...","saas/azr_psql_full_snapshot_recovery.html@@@Recovering an Azure PostgreSQL server from a snapshot@@@Restore a PostgreSQL Flexible Server to a specific snapshot state by recovering data into an existing target server...","saas/azr_psql_limitations.html@@@Azure PostgreSQL backup and recovery limitations@@@Before protecting Azure Database for PostgreSQL Flexible Servers, review the known limitations that apply to backup and recovery of databases that use PostgreSQL extensions...","saas/azr_psql_manage.html@@@Manage Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Servers@@@RSC enhances Azure native backup capabilities for Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Servers by providing advanced, Rubrik-managed protection with customizable SLA Domain policies, immutable backups, point-in-time recovery, and flexible cross-subscription recovery...","saas/azr_psql_nw_configs.html@@@Network configurations for Azure PostgreSQL server@@@Review the network configurations that RSC supports for backing up Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Servers. Public access and Private Access network configurations are supported. Servers accessible only through Azure Private Endpoints, with no public access and no VNet integration, are not supported...","saas/azr_psql_performing_pitr_recovery.html@@@Performing a point-in-time recovery of an Azure PostgreSQL server@@@Recover an Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Server to any point in time within the log backup retention window by provisioning a new server...","saas/azr_psql_server_details.html@@@Azure PostgreSQL Server details@@@The server details page provides protection status, object properties, and snapshot information for an Azure PostgreSQL Server...","saas/azr_psql_server_protection_mechanism.html@@@Azure PostgreSQL Server protection mechanism@@@A high-level overview of how RSC backs up and recovers Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Servers using Exocompute and a temporary export server...","saas/azr_psql_supported_extensions.html@@@Azure PostgreSQL extension support@@@Information about the PostgreSQL extensions that are validated for backup and recovery of Azure Database for PostgreSQL Flexible Servers, and the extensions that are not supported...","saas/azr_psql_taking_ods.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of an Azure PostgreSQL server@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of an Azure PostgreSQL server...","saas/azr_psql_workload_recovery.html@@@Recover Azure PostgreSQL servers@@@RSC provides backup and recovery for Azure PostgreSQL flexible servers, enabling you to restore data quickly and meet compliance requirements...","saas/azr_pvt_aks_clusters.html@@@Private AKS clusters@@@Private AKS clusters enable secure in-VNet communication between the control plane and node pools, restricting API server access to the VNet. They manage a private DNS zone by default but can be configured with a custom DNS zone for specific network needs...","saas/azr_quick_links.html@@@Quick links for Azure workloads@@@Immediate access to important tasks and information, enabling quick setup, daily operations, and critical recovery...","saas/azr_rcv_configuring_private_endpoint.html@@@Configuring a private endpoint for RCV archiving of Azure workloads@@@Configure a private endpoint between the Exocompute virtual network and the Rubrik Cloud Vault storage account to restrict archival traffic to private connectivity...","saas/azr_rcv_configuring_service_endpoint.html@@@Configuring a service endpoint for RCV archiving of Azure workloads@@@Configure a service endpoint on the Exocompute subnet to keep RCV archival traffic on the Azure backbone and restrict the RCV storage account to the specified virtual network...","saas/azr_rcv_private_service_endpoints.html@@@Private and service endpoints for RCV archiving of Azure workloads@@@When archiving Azure workloads to Rubrik Cloud Vault using customer-hosted Exocompute, archival traffic travels over the public internet by default. Configuring a private or service endpoint restricts this traffic to use private connectivity instead...","saas/azr_rcv_removing_endpoint.html@@@Removing a private or service endpoint from an RCV archival location@@@Removing a private or service endpoint from an RCV archival location requires coordination with Rubrik through a support case. Self-service removal from RSC is not available for RCV archiving of cloud-native workloads...","saas/azr_recommendations_add_cloud_acc.html@@@Recommendations for adding Azure cloud accounts@@@Rubrik recommends specific actions and best practices for adding Azure cloud accounts to RSC...","saas/azr_recover_vm_md.html@@@Recover Azure virtual machines@@@You can recover your Azure virtual machines and managed disks using options such as recovering files or folders, exporting, restoring, mounting, and Azure in-place file recovery...","saas/azr_recovery_privilege_elevation.html@@@Privilege elevation for Azure recovery@@@RSC provides you an option to secure Azure cloud accounts by using a least permission model, granting only necessary read permissions at the subscription level. For recovery operations, you can temporarily elevate permissions either by authorizing a service principal role or by using a security token...","saas/azr_refresh_azure_subscription.html@@@Refreshing an Azure subscription@@@RSC refreshes Azure subscription data as an on-demand task or as a periodic background job that runs every three hours...","saas/azr_refresh_subscription_info.html@@@Refresh Azure subscription information@@@Information about Azure subscription account details are refreshed either automatically or on demand to maintain accurate resource metadata...","saas/azr_region_level_sla_assignment.html@@@Region-level SLA Domain assignment for Azure@@@You can apply a unified policy to an entire Azure region with a region-level SLA Domain assignment, ensuring any new resource in that region is automatically protected...","saas/azr_removal_prerequisites.html@@@Removal Prerequisites for Azure Subscriptions@@@Before removing certain Azure subscription use cases, complete the required prerequisites for each use case that shows Attention required in the Remove Use Cases wizard...","saas/azr_remove_use_case.html@@@Removing a use case from an Azure subscription@@@Remove one or more use cases from an Azure subscription while keeping other active use cases and the subscription itself in RSC...","saas/azr_removing_archival_locations.html@@@Removing archival locations from an Azure subscription@@@Remove all data center and cloud native archival locations associated with an Azure subscription before removing the Archive and Storage use case...","saas/azr_removing_pcr_configuration.html@@@Removing Azure Private Container Registry configurations@@@When you no longer want to use your Private Container Registry and you want Exocompute to pull images using a registry Rubrik hosts, remove the Private Container Registry configuration...","saas/azr_replication_snapshots.html@@@Replication of Azure snapshots@@@Replication allows snapshots of Azure virtual machines and managed disks to be copied to another region based on SLA Domain, using APIs to minimize costs. This process ensures multi-region availability and data protection for virtual machines and managed disks...","saas/azr_req_fw_network_rules_udr.html@@@Required firewall network rules for UDR@@@Setting up User Defined Routing in the Azure firewall requires adding service tag rules and FQDN network rules...","saas/azr_req_perms_auto_network_setup.html@@@Required permissions for automated networking setup@@@RSC requires a specific set of permissions to enable automated network configuration for Exocompute and to manage the lifecycle of networking infrastructure within your Azure environment. These permissions enables RSC to orchestrate a seamless setup without manual intervention...","saas/azr_req_perms_auto_network_setup_2.html@@@Required permissions for automated networking setup@@@RSC requires a specific set of permissions to enable automated network configuration for Exocompute and to manage the lifecycle of networking infrastructure within your Azure environment. These permissions enables RSC to orchestrate a seamless setup without manual intervention...","saas/azr_req_perms_data_classification.html@@@Required permissions for Data scanning in Azure@@@Information about permissions RSC requires to scan and classify sensitive data in Azure subscriptions...","saas/azr_req_perms_discover_cloud_obj.html@@@Required permissions for discovering Azure cloud objects@@@Information about the basic permissions that RSC requires to discover Azure cloud objects...","saas/azr_req_perms_exocompute_oauth.html@@@Required permissions for Exocompute on Azure with OAuth@@@When using Microsoft Entra ID for authentication, RSC requires certain permissions when adding an Exocompute on Azure instance with OAuth. You must apply these permissions to the Azure cloud account for the Exocompute instance...","saas/azr_req_perms_key_management.html@@@Required permissions for Azure key management@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to discover Azure Key Vaults and the permissions that you grant on your Azure Key Vault for client-side encryption of archival locations...","saas/azr_req_perms_outpost_account.html@@@Required permissions for Azure outpost account@@@Information about the permissions that the outpost account requires to access the Azure account...","saas/azr_req_perms_postgresql_protect.html@@@Required permissions for managing Azure PostgreSQL backups@@@RSC requires specific permissions on the protected Azure subscription to manage backup and recovery of Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Servers...","saas/azr_req_rbk_perms_cloud_acc.html@@@Required RSC permissions for Azure cloud accounts@@@RSC requires specific permissions in your Azure environment to protect the Azure workloads...","saas/azr_requirements_for_protecting_workloads.html@@@Requirements for protecting Azure workloads@@@An Azure user must meet specific requirements to configure Azure protection by RSC...","saas/azr_resolving_common_exocompute_issues.html@@@Resolving common Azure Exocompute issues@@@You can troubleshoot and resolve common Azure Exocompute issues that occurs while setting up an Azure Kubernetes Service cluster. The AKS cluster not starting properly is a common issue reported to Rubrik Support. Some reasons for this are described below...","saas/azr_resource_manager_templates.html@@@Azure resource manager templates@@@Downloading and reviewing the Azure Resource Manager templates is allowed when adding an Azure account in RSC using the configure without OAuth method...","saas/azr_restore_snapshot.html@@@Restoring Azure virtual machine using a snapshot@@@Use an Azure virtual machine snapshot to replace the original virtual machine with a fully functional point-in-time copy...","saas/azr_restoring_key_secret_target_kv.html@@@Restoring downloaded key and secret in the target Azure key vault@@@Perform the restore operation to import the previously downloaded keys and secrets into the target Azure key vault to enable encryption services...","saas/azr_retention_lock.html@@@Retention lock for Azure workloads@@@A retention lock on an RSC SLA Domain is a security feature that prevents premature deletion of Azure snapshots...","saas/azr_running_exocompute_health_check.html@@@Running an Exocompute health check on Azure@@@Run an on-demand health check on an Azure Kubernetes Service cluster to verify that the Exocompute instance is functioning correctly...","saas/azr_snapshots.html@@@Azure virtual machine snapshots@@@To manage and protect your data in RSC, you can take an on-demand snapshot or configure an SLA Domain to take scheduled snapshots based on your requirements...","saas/azr_sql_assigning_protection.html@@@Assigning protection to Azure SQL workloads@@@Assign a data protection policy to individual or multiple Azure SQL workloads...","saas/azr_sql_creating_custom_sla.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain for Azure SQL@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to protect Azure SQL workloads through either RSC backups or native Azure backup policies...","saas/azr_sql_creating_custom_sla_2.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain for Azure SQL@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to protect Azure SQL workloads through either RSC backups or native Azure backup policies...","saas/azr_sql_database_overview_tab.html@@@Azure SQL database overview@@@Available database information of Azure SQL workloads on RSC...","saas/azr_sql_databases_tab.html@@@Databases tab@@@Information available on the Databases tab for the Azure SQL Databases inventory...","saas/azr_sql_db_backup_verification.html@@@Azure SQL DB backup verification@@@As part of each Azure SQL Database Rubrik backup, RSC automatically performs backup verification to confirm that the backup is recoverable...","saas/azr_sql_db_config_rbk_backup.html@@@Azure SQL DB Rubrik backup configuration@@@Setting up Rubrik backups for Azure SQL Databases involves configuring cloud accounts, an archival location, and an SLA Domain...","saas/azr_sql_db_configuring_pvt_endpoint.html@@@Configuring a private endpoint for Azure SQL DB@@@RSC uses your Exocompute instance to connect to the Rubrik-managed Azure SQL server, take Rubrik backups, and upload those backups to Azure storage. For enhanced security and improved performance, configure a private endpoint for this connection...","saas/azr_sql_db_configuring_srvc_endpoint.html@@@Configuring a service endpoint for Azure SQL DB@@@RSC uses your Exocompute instance to connect to the Rubrik-managed Azure SQL server, take Rubrik backups, and upload those backups to Azure storage. For a simple, cost-effective, and broadly accessible method of enabling this, configure a service endpoint for this connection...","saas/azr_sql_db_failover_groups.html@@@Azure SQL Database Failover Groups@@@When Azure SQL Databases are configured in a Failover Group, RSC has specific behavior for discovery, backup, and recovery that you must understand before assigning protection...","saas/azr_sql_db_manage.html@@@Manage Azure SQL Database@@@RSC enhances Azure native backup capabilities for SQL Databases by offering advanced, Rubrik-managed protection. This solution overcomes native limitations with customizable SLA Domain policies, on-demand snapshots, and flexible cross-subscription recovery, ensuring a consistent and automated approach to data security...","saas/azr_sql_db_mapping_acc_exo_subs.html@@@Mapping Azure SQL DB account to Exocompute subscription@@@Map your Azure cloud account for protecting Azure SQL Databases to an Exocompute host subscription. This task links your database environment to the data processing resources needed for backups, preparing the environment for creating an archival location and securing your data with Rubrik backups...","saas/azr_sql_db_nw_configs.html@@@Network configurations for Azure SQL DB@@@To securely back up an Azure SQL Database, you need to configure either a service endpoint or a private endpoint for the temporary Rubrik-managed SQL server that RSC creates, and a private endpoint for the cloud-native location storage account that stores the backup data...","saas/azr_sql_db_prereq_rbk_backups.html@@@Prerequisites for Azure SQL DB Rubrik backup@@@Rubrik backups of Azure SQL databases require specific configuration on both RSC and Azure...","saas/azr_sql_db_pvt_endpoint_config_cli.html@@@Private endpoint configuration for Azure SQL DB using Azure CLI@@@You can also use the Azure CLI commands for configuring a private endpoint for the Rubrik-managed SQL server. This method is an alternative to using the Azure portal UI...","saas/azr_sql_db_rbk_backup_components.html@@@Rubrik backup components for Azure SQL DB@@@RSC protects Azure SQL Databases by taking Rubrik backups that use several key components: Rubrik Exocompute for data processing, the Cloud Storage Layer for efficient storage, and snapshot immutability for cyber resilience. These backups offer significant advantages, including a logical air gap and flexible recovery options...","saas/azr_sql_db_rbk_backup_limitations.html@@@Azure SQL DB Rubrik backup limitations@@@Rubrik backup and recovery of Azure SQL Databases has certain limitations...","saas/azr_sql_db_recovery_settings.html@@@Azure SQL Database recovery settings@@@Recovering Azure SQL Server databases by exporting snapshots requires specific configuration...","saas/azr_sql_db_supp_datatypes_rbk_backup.html@@@Supported datatypes for Azure SQL DB Rubrik backups@@@Information about the datatypes that RSC supports for the Azure SQL Database Rubrik backups...","saas/azr_sql_db_upgrading_tde_cmk.html@@@Upgrading TDE with CMK for Azure SQL DB@@@Existing cloud accounts need a one-time upgrade to enable Transparent Data Encryption (TDE) with Customer-Managed Key (CMK) support and update subscription settings with a User-assigned Managed Identity (UMI)...","saas/azr_sql_db_viewing_details.html@@@Viewing Azure SQL Databases details@@@Access the Azure SQL Databases inventory page to view the details of your databases...","saas/azr_sql_deleting_backup_credentials.html@@@Deleting backup credentials@@@Delete the database credentials for a specific Azure SQL Managed Instance from RSC...","saas/azr_sql_exporting_ltr_backup.html@@@Exporting a long-term retention backup@@@Recover Azure SQL workloads by exporting a long-term retention backup. The long-term retention backup can be immutable or non-immutable...","saas/azr_sql_independent_sla_support.html@@@Independent SLA support for Rubrik and Azure backups@@@RSC provides independent SLA Domain support for Rubrik backups and Azure-native backups, enabling both to coexist within the same environment...","saas/azr_sql_independent_sla_support_2.html@@@Independent SLA support for Rubrik and Azure backups@@@RSC provides independent SLA Domain support for Rubrik backups and Azure-native backups, enabling both to coexist within the same environment...","saas/azr_sql_managed_instances_tab.html@@@Managed Instances tab@@@Information available on the Managed Instances tab for the Azure SQL Managed Instances inventory...","saas/azr_sql_managing_backup_creds_using_admin_creds.html@@@Managing backup credentials using administrator credentials@@@Authorize RSC to create login credentials and enable Change Data Capture by connecting to the Azure SQL Managed Instance using the credentials of the database administrator...","saas/azr_sql_managing_backup_creds_using_oauth.html@@@Managing backup credentials using OAuth@@@Authorize RSC to create login credentials and enable Change Data Capture by using OAuth to sign in to a specific Azure Active Directory domain...","saas/azr_sql_mi_bak_backups.html@@@BAK-based backups for Azure SQL Managed Instance@@@RSC uses BAK-based backups to protect Azure SQL Managed Instance databases using the native SQL Server backup format. This method provides universal schema compatibility, enterprise scalability, and integrated encryption without requiring database-level configuration...","saas/azr_sql_mi_config_rbk_backup.html@@@Configure Azure SQL MI Rubrik backups@@@Information about the configuration tasks to set up Rubrik backups for Azure SQL Managed Instances...","saas/azr_sql_mi_configuring_pvt_endpoint.html@@@Configuring a private endpoint for Azure SQL MI@@@RSC uses your Exocompute instance to connect to the source Azure SQL MI that you are protecting with RSC, take Rubrik backups, and upload those backups to Azure storage. For enhanced security and improved performance, configure a private endpoint for this connection...","saas/azr_sql_mi_configuring_srvc_endpoint.html@@@Configuring VNet peering for Azure SQL MI@@@RSC uses the Exocompute instance to connect to the source Azure SQL MI, take Rubrik backups, and upload those backups to Azure storage. For a cost-effective method of enabling this connection, configure VNet peering by peering the Exocompute VNet with the SQL MI VNet and adding the required network security group rules...","saas/azr_sql_mi_cred_mgmt_rbk_backup.html@@@Credential management for Azure SQL MI Rubrik backups@@@Credential management for taking Rubrik backups of Azure SQL Managed Instance involves creating database login credentials with the permissions required for the backup workflow...","saas/azr_sql_mi_manage.html@@@Manage Azure SQL Managed Instance@@@RSC enhances Azure native backup capabilities for SQL Managed Instances by offering advanced, Rubrik-managed protection. This solution overcomes native limitations with customizable SLA Domain policies, on-demand snapshots, and flexible cross-subscription recovery, ensuring a consistent and automated approach to data security...","saas/azr_sql_mi_managing_backup_creds_script.html@@@Managing Azure SQL MI backup credentials using a script@@@Download and use a script to create login credentials, enable Change Data Capture, and configure database credentials for taking Rubrik backups of Azure SQL Managed Instance databases...","saas/azr_sql_mi_mapping_strg_rbk_backup.html@@@Mapping storage for Azure SQL MI Rubrik backup@@@Map the source subscription to the Azure SQL Managed Instance Rubrik-backup archival location in the storage subscription...","saas/azr_sql_mi_nw_configs.html@@@Network configurations for Azure SQL MI@@@To back up an Azure SQL Managed Instance, you must configure a network connection between the Rubrik Exocompute instance and the source managed instance. You can configure this connection using a private endpoint or VNet peering...","saas/azr_sql_mi_prereq_rbk_backup.html@@@Prerequisites for Azure SQL MI Rubrik backup@@@Enabling Rubrik backups of Azure SQL Managed Instances requires specific configuration on both RSC and Azure...","saas/azr_sql_mi_rbk_backup_components.html@@@Rubrik backup components for Azure SQL MI@@@RSC provides cyber-resilient protection for Azure SQL Managed Instances by leveraging Rubrik Exocompute to orchestrate secure, BAK-based backups that are logically air-gapped from the source. These backups are stored separately from your source data and locked with snapshot immutability...","saas/azr_sql_mi_rbk_backup_limitations.html@@@Azure SQL MI Rubrik backup limitations@@@Taking immutable BAK-based backups of Azure SQL Managed Instance databases has certain limitations...","saas/azr_sql_mi_rbk_backup_sql_permissions.html@@@SQL Server permissions for Azure SQL MI Rubrik backups@@@Information about the minimal set of permissions that RSC uses during backup, combined with the SQL Server objects it creates on the source Azure SQL Managed Instance during setup, ensuring secure and isolated operations...","saas/azr_sql_mi_recovery_settings.html@@@Azure SQL Managed Instance recovery settings@@@Recovering Azure SQL Managed Instance databases by exporting Rubrik backups supports two authentication methods, each requiring specific settings...","saas/azr_sql_mi_setting_rbk_backups.html@@@Setting up Azure SQL MI Rubrik backups@@@Set up Rubrik backups for Azure SQL Managed Instance databases...","saas/azr_sql_mi_unmapping_strg_rbk_backup.html@@@Unmapping storage for Azure SQL MI Rubrik backup@@@Using the unmap storage for the Azure SQL Managed Instance Rubrik backup feature in RSC, unmap the source subscription to the backup storage location in the target subscription...","saas/azr_sql_mi_viewing_details.html@@@Viewing Azure SQL Managed Instances details@@@Access the Azure SQL Managed Instances inventory page to view the details of your databases...","saas/azr_sql_native_backup_capability.html@@@Azure SQL native backup capabilities@@@Azure provides native backup solutions for Azure SQL workloads, including Point-in-Time Retention and Long-Term Retention. While these offer foundational protection, they have certain limitations...","saas/azr_sql_native_backup_capability_2.html@@@Azure SQL native backup capabilities@@@Azure provides native backup solutions for Azure SQL workloads, including Point-in-Time Retention and Long-Term Retention. While these offer foundational protection, they have certain limitations...","saas/azr_sql_native_vs_rbk_backups.html@@@Azure SQL native versus Rubrik backups@@@A comparative overview of Azure-native backup policies and Rubrik backups for Azure SQL workloads...","saas/azr_sql_native_vs_rbk_backups_2.html@@@Azure SQL native versus Rubrik backups@@@A comparative overview of Azure-native backup policies and Rubrik backups for Azure SQL workloads...","saas/azr_sql_private_service_endpoints_usage.html@@@Azure SQL private and service endpoints usage@@@For balancing security and compliance needs against setup complexity and costs, you can choose between the private and service endpoints to configure access between the Exocompute instance and the Azure SQL server. RSC uses the Exocompute instance to take backups of your Azure SQL workloads and upload those backups to Azure storage...","saas/azr_sql_recovery_rbk_backups.html@@@Azure SQL recovery from Rubrik backups@@@Information about the options for recovering Azure SQL workloads from Rubrik backups...","saas/azr_sql_req_permissions_hosting_aks_cluster.html@@@Required permissions for hosting an AKS cluster@@@RSC requires specific permissions on the Azure subscriptions where the AKS cluster will be hosted...","saas/azr_sql_req_permissions_manage_db_backups.html@@@Required permissions for managing Azure SQL Database backups@@@RSC requires specific permissions for the protected Azure subscriptions to manage backup and recovery of Azure SQL Databases...","saas/azr_sql_req_permissions_manage_mi_backups.html@@@Required permissions for managing Azure SQL Managed Instance backups@@@RSC requires specific permissions on the protected Azure subscriptions to manage backup and recovery of Azure SQL Managed Instance databases...","saas/azr_sql_req_permissions_storing_immutable_backups.html@@@Required permissions for storing immutable backups@@@RSC requires specific subscription permissions to allow it to store immutable backups...","saas/azr_sql_resource_groups_tab.html@@@Resource Groups tab@@@Information available on the Resource Groups tab for Azure SQL Databases and Managed Instances...","saas/azr_sql_resource_groups_tab_2.html@@@Resource Groups tab@@@Information available on the Resource Groups tab for Azure SQL Databases and Managed Instances...","saas/azr_sql_restoring_to_point_in_time.html@@@Restoring Azure SQL workloads to a point in time@@@Restore an Azure SQL workload to a point in time using the short-term retention backups...","saas/azr_sql_servers_tab.html@@@Servers tab@@@Information available on the Servers tab for Azure SQL Databases...","saas/azr_sql_subscriptions_tab.html@@@Subscriptions tab@@@Information available on the Subscriptions tab for Azure SQL Databases and Managed Instances...","saas/azr_sql_subscriptions_tab_2.html@@@Subscriptions tab@@@Information available on the Subscriptions tab for Azure SQL Databases and Managed Instances...","saas/azr_sql_supp_backup_recv_types.html@@@Supported Azure SQL backup and recovery types@@@RSC protects Azure SQL Databases and Managed Instances by supporting different types of backup and recovery options...","saas/azr_sql_supp_backup_recv_types_2.html@@@Supported Azure SQL backup and recovery types@@@RSC protects Azure SQL Databases and Managed Instances by supporting different types of backup and recovery options...","saas/azr_sql_tag_rules_tab.html@@@Tag rules tab@@@Information available on the Servers tab for Azure SQL Databases and Managed Instances...","saas/azr_sql_tag_rules_tab_2.html@@@Tag rules tab@@@Information available on the Servers tab for Azure SQL Databases and Managed Instances...","saas/azr_sql_taking_ods.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Azure SQL workloads@@@Manually initiate an on-demand snapshot of an Azure SQL database object...","saas/azr_sql_workload_information_filters.html@@@Azure SQL workload information filters@@@Filters are available on the various tabs for Azure SQL Databases and Managed Instances to find specific information...","saas/azr_sql_workload_information_filters_2.html@@@Azure SQL workload information filters@@@Filters are available on the various tabs for Azure SQL Databases and Managed Instances to find specific information...","saas/azr_sql_workload_recovery.html@@@Azure SQL workload recovery@@@RSC supports recovering Azure SQL workloads at the individual database level...","saas/azr_stnd_load_balancer_settings.html@@@Azure standard load balancer settings@@@Exocompute on Azure uses a standard load balancer with a public IP address to manage network traffic for Azure Kubernetes Service clusters. However, Azure policies that prevent the creation of public IPs can cause these deployments to fail. To prevent this, you can provide policy exemptions or configure User Defined Routing...","saas/azr_storage_tiering_evaluate_options.html@@@Evaluate Azure storage tiering options@@@Before setting up Azure storage tiering, it is important to evaluate the tiering options to align with archiving needs, balancing cost, performance, and data retrieval. Key considerations include archival location, access tiers, instant tiering, endpoint usage, and encryption standards...","saas/azr_storage_tiering_setup.html@@@Set up Azure storage tiering@@@You can use Azure storage tiering to archive Azure virtual machine or managed disk snapshots, which are older than a specified threshold, to Azure storage access tiers. By archiving snapshots to these access tiers, you can optimize cost...","saas/azr_supp_encryption_storage_tiering.html@@@Supported encryption types for Azure storage tiering@@@RSC supports three encryption types for data stored in Azure archival locations: server-side encryption with platform-managed keys, server-side encryption with customer-managed keys, and client-side encryption...","saas/azr_tag_based_protection.html@@@Tag-based protection for Azure workloads@@@You can protect Azure workloads by grouping them using tags and assigning SLA Domains based on those tags...","saas/azr_tags.html@@@Azure tags@@@RSC attaches specific tags to the Azure resources you create using RSC...","saas/azr_taking_ondemand_snapshot.html@@@Taking on-demand Azure VMs or managed disks snapshots@@@Manually initiate an on-demand snapshot of the Azure VMs and managed disks with or without assigning an SLA Domain...","saas/azr_udr_config.html@@@Azure User Defined Routing configuration@@@To manage outbound traffic for an Azure Kubernetes Service cluster without using public IP addresses, you can configure User Defined Routes in your Azure VNet used for Exocompute...","saas/azr_updating_entra_dom_map_without_oauth.html@@@Updating Microsoft Entra Domain mapping without OAuth@@@Update the Microsoft Entra Domain mapping for the Azure subscription you initially added to RSC using the configure without OAuth method. Do this when you move the subscription to a different Microsoft Entra Domain in the Azure portal...","saas/azr_updating_entra_domain_mapping_oath.html@@@Updating Microsoft Entra Domain mapping with OAuth@@@Update the Microsoft Entra Domain mapping for the Azure subscription you initially added to RSC using the configure with OAuth method. Do this when you move the subscription to a different Microsoft Entra Domain in the Azure portal...","saas/azr_updating_perms_mgmt_grp_subs.html@@@Updating permissions for management group subscriptions@@@Update permissions for all the Azure subscriptions that are onboarded using a management group. For example, when a new release requires additional Azure permissions...","saas/azr_upgrading_account.html@@@Upgrading an Azure cloud account@@@Upgrade an Azure cloud account that is in the Update permissions state...","saas/azr_user_perms_config_storage_tiering.html@@@User permissions for configuring Azure storage tiering@@@To set up Azure storage tiering, the RSC user must be assigned a role with specific permissions...","saas/azr_validating_perms_subs.html@@@Validating permissions for Azure subscriptions@@@Run the on-demand permission validation for Azure subscriptions to identify any missing permissions necessary for cloud-native protection of Azure workloads...","saas/azr_view_azure_subscription.html@@@Viewing the Azure subscription page@@@View the Azure subscription page from RSC...","saas/azr_view_relic_virtual_machine.html@@@Viewing relic Azure virtual machine information@@@View relic Azure virtual machine details from the Inventory tab...","saas/azr_view_resource_grp.html@@@Viewing the Azure resource group page@@@The Azure resource group list displays protection status, region, and subscription ID of the resource groups...","saas/azr_viewing_exocompute_details_page.html@@@Viewing the Exocompute on Azure details page@@@View the details of an Exocompute host subscription, including mapped accounts, network configuration, and region-level health status. From the details panel, you can also edit the Exocompute configuration...","saas/azr_vm_details.html@@@Azure VMs and managed disk details@@@The Azure VM and Azure Managed Disk details page displays protection status, a calendar view of the snapshots, and events of Azure VMs and managed disks...","saas/azr_vm_md_details.html@@@Azure virtual machines and managed disks details@@@Viewing and analyzing detailed information about Azure virtual machines and managed disks helps in making informed decisions. Key aspects include protection status, detailed attributes, snapshots calendar, and events log for audit and compliance...","saas/azr_vm_md_recovery_options.html@@@Recovery options for Azure virtual machines@@@A comparative overview of the various recovery options for Azure virtual machines and managed disks...","saas/azr_vm_recovery.html@@@Azure virtual machine recovery@@@You can recover Azure virtual machines and managed disks using the various recovery options that RSC provides...","saas/azr_vm_snapshot_management.html@@@Management of Azure virtual machine snapshots@@@You can perform management tasks for the snapshots of Azure virtual machines and managed disks. This includes taking on-demand snapshots, changing the retention policies, and deleting the snapshots...","saas/azr_workflow_example_exocompute.html@@@Exocompute on Azure workflow example@@@A workflow example to demonstrate the Exocompute lifecycle on Azure when indexing a snapshot of an Azure virtual machine...","saas/azr_workload_recovery.html@@@Recover Azure workloads@@@After RSC takes snapshots of your Azure workloads, you can recover the required workloads...","saas/azr_workloads.html@@@Microsoft Azure workloads@@@RSC protects the data and resources of Azure virtual machines, Azure managed disks, Azure Blob Storage, Azure SQL workloads, and Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Servers in Azure subscriptions...","saas/azr_workloads_protection_setup.html@@@Set up Azure workloads protection@@@You can set up SLA Domains to apply data protection policies, ensuring automatic and hierarchical protection of Azure subscriptions, resource groups, and individual Azure workloads, with granular control overriding higher-level assignments...","saas/azure_cc_es_rsc.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@You can use Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure to protect applications and data within a Microsoft Azure virtual network...","saas/azure_changing_retention_policy_for_on_demand_snapshot.html@@@Changing retention policy for an on-demand snapshot@@@Change the retention policy of on-demand snapshots of Azure protected objects...","saas/azure_data_classification.html@@@Data scanning in Azure@@@When you enable data scanning in an Azure account, RSC scans and classifies your Azure data based on its sensitivity and also generates intelligent insights into the data. Data scanning helps you manage cloud posture risks...","saas/azure_disabling_data_scanning.html@@@Disabling data scanning for Azure cloud accounts@@@Disable data scanning for an Azure account to stop the collection of data sensitivity insights...","saas/azure_ds_cleanup_script_params.html@@@Azure data scanning resource cleanup script parameters@@@The rubrik_resource_cleanup.ps1 script accepts specific parameters to control the cleanup process...","saas/azure_enabling_data_scanning.html@@@Enabling Data scanning for Azure cloud accounts@@@Enable the Data scanning feature for an existing Azure cloud account in RSC. Data scanning helps you manage cloud posture risks...","saas/azure_policy_restrictions.html@@@Azure policy restrictions@@@Azure policies can obstruct RSC operations such as storage account creation. Knowing how to adjust these policies is crucial for maintaining both security and compliance...","saas/azure_removing_data_scanning_resources.html@@@Removing data scanning resources from Azure cloud account@@@After disabling data scanning, remove the Rubrik-created Azure resources by running a PowerShell cleanup script for an Azure subscription. The script preserves all resource groups and custom resources...","saas/azure_sql_backup_version_compliance.html@@@Azure SQL backup versioning and compliance@@@RSC uses different backup versions based on the backup service selected in an SLA Domain to manage snapshot retention and ensure data integrity...","saas/azure_sql_tde_support.html@@@Support for Azure SQL TDE with customer-managed keys@@@RSC supports the backup and recovery of Azure SQL Databases encrypted using Transparent Data Encryption with Customer-Managed Keys...","saas/azure_vm_changing_snapshot_retention.html@@@Changing retention policy for an Azure virtual machine or managed disk@@@Change the retention policy of existing policy-based snapshots of the Azure object with no SLA Domain...","saas/backup_throttle_host_filesets.html@@@Backup throttle for host filesets@@@RSC provides backup throttle modes for host fileset protection to optimize resource use and match storage array capabilities...","saas/behavioral_diff_gov_and_comp_rl_sla_domain.html@@@Behavioral differences between governance and compliance retention-locked SLA Domains@@@Governance and compliance retention-locked SLA Domains have specific differences based on the SLA Domain modifications. Administrators make these modifications to adjust backup frequency, retention duration, archival locations, and so on. These changes ensure that data protection strategies comply with regulatory requirements and organizational policies, optimizing storage costs and data accessibility...","saas/breached_password_detection.html@@@Breached password detection@@@RSC administrators can proactively identify and address potential security vulnerabilities within their RSC domain by using the breached password detection feature. This feature validates whether the login credentials of local users have been compromised in any public data breaches...","saas/bulk_recover_current_resource_live_mount.html@@@Bulk recovery to current compute resources using Live Mounts@@@You can perform bulk recovery of multiple vSphere virtual machines from selected snapshots to their current compute resources or to new ones using Live Mounts...","saas/bulk_recovery_vSphere_vms.html@@@Bulk recovery of vSphere virtual machines@@@To recover multiple vSphere virtual machines at the same time, you can use the vSphere VMs page to perform a bulk recovery operation...","saas/bulk_recovery_virtual_machines_Exports.html@@@Bulk recovery of virtual machines using Export@@@Using the Export option for bulk recovery of vSphere virtual machines lets you restore multiple virtual machines from selected snapshots to their current compute resources or to new ones...","saas/canceling_a_m365_restore_job.html@@@Canceling a Microsoft 365 Restore Job@@@Cancel Microsoft 365 restore jobs from the Events tab...","saas/cascading_archival.html@@@Cascading archival@@@Using cascading archival, you can increase replicated data redundancy and decrease data storage costs by archiving replicated snapshots from a replication target Rubrik cluster to a remote archival location...","saas/cascading_archival_config_examples.html@@@Cascading archival configuration examples@@@Examples explaining how to configure data retention settings to achieve the required retention period when cascading archival is enabled...","saas/cces_adding_gcp_project_for_cces.html@@@Adding a GCP project@@@Add a GCP project as a cloud account for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage...","saas/cces_aws_required_permissions_iaas.html@@@Required permissions for protecting IaaS workloads@@@The CloudFormation stack grants the Rubrik cross-account role the permissions needed to protect RSC-managed Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) workloads...","saas/cces_deployment_models.html@@@CCES deployment models@@@When you use RSC to protect data on the AWS platform, you can choose from a variety of deployment models to find one that fits your business needs, available compute infrastructure, and budget...","saas/cces_disabling_dynamic_scaling.html@@@Disabling dynamic scaling@@@Turn off dynamic scaling on an existing Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage deployment so that the cluster uses a fixed number of nodes...","saas/cces_dynamic_scaling.html@@@Dynamic scaling in Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage@@@Dynamic scaling for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on RSC optimizes compute costs by automatically adjusting the number of active nodes based on workload demand...","saas/cces_iaas_workloads_prerequisites.html@@@RSC-managed IaaS workload prerequisites@@@Your AWS environment must meet the following prerequisites for protecting Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) workloads in an RSC-managed deployment...","saas/cces_managed_identities.html@@@Microsoft Azure managed identities for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage@@@For more secure authentication to your storage container, you can use Microsoft Azure managed identities instead of connection strings...","saas/cces_pausing_resuming_dynamic_scaling.html@@@Pausing and resuming dynamic scaling@@@Temporarily pause and resume dynamic scaling to prevent worker nodes in a Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage deployment from scaling down or turning off...","saas/cces_recoverability.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage recoverability@@@Rebuild your Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage instance to recover cluster data when all other methods for recovering the cluster nodes fail...","saas/cces_rsc_managed_iaas_workloads.html@@@RSC-managed IaaS workloads@@@RSC provisions and manages the AWS resources required to back up Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) workload hosts on your behalf, and uses AWS Systems Manager to install the Rubrik Backup Service on the hosts, when you use an RSC-managed deployment...","saas/cces_subscribing_aws_marketplace.html@@@Subscribing to Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage in the AWS Marketplace@@@Subscribing to Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage in the AWS Marketplace allows RSC to provision Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage instances...","saas/cces_transitioning_managed_identities.html@@@Transitioning to using Azure managed identities@@@For enhanced security, transition your cluster from using connection strings to using managed identities as the authentication type to your storage container...","saas/cces_troubleshooting_iaas_workload.html@@@Troubleshooting IaaS workload protection@@@Common issues that occur when onboarding Infrastructure as a Service workloads into an RSC-managed AWS deployment, and how to resolve them...","saas/cdm_relic_data_sources.html@@@Relic data sources@@@A data source is designated as a relic if it is managed by, but is no longer accessible to the Rubrik cluster...","saas/changes_sla_domains_after_switching.html@@@Changes in SLA Domains after switching@@@Information about the functionality changes in SLA Domains after switching to align with the new architecture, enhancing centralized management...","saas/changes_sla_domains_created_on_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Changes in SLA Domains created on a Rubrik cluster@@@Information about the functionality changes in the SLA Domains created on a Rubrik cluster. These changes align with the new architecture, enhancing centralized management...","saas/changing_account_ownership.html@@@Changing account ownership@@@Assign the owner role to another local user account. Only an account with the owner role can assign the owner role to another user account...","saas/changing_comp_disable_rl.html@@@Changing to compliance mode or disabling the retention-locked SLA Domain@@@To comply with regulatory requirements or remove specific data security measures, change the mode of a retention-locked SLA Domain from governance to compliance mode or disable the retention lock...","saas/changing_primary_cluster_host.html@@@Changing the primary Rubrik cluster of a host@@@When RBS installed on a host is registered with multiple Rubrik clusters, you can use RSC to change the primary Rubrik cluster of a host...","saas/changing_retention_multiple_objects.html@@@Changing the retention period of multiple objects@@@Change the retention period of all the snapshots of an object or multiple objects associated with data center or cloud native workloads...","saas/changing_retention_period_m365_snpshts.html@@@Changing the retention period of Microsoft 365 snapshots@@@Increase or decrease the retention period of a Microsoft 365 snapshot depending on how long you want to retain it...","saas/changing_retention_period_snapshot.html@@@Changing the retention period of a snapshot@@@Change the retention period of a snapshot of data center, cloud native, or NAS CD workload objects...","saas/changing_retention_sap_hana_snapshots.html@@@Changing retention of SAP HANA snapshots@@@Based on your specific data governance and compliance needs, change the retention period of SAP HANA snapshots. You can change the retention period by assigning a different SLA Domain or by choosing to retain them forever...","saas/changing_sla_domain_rl.html@@@Changing an SLA Domain to a retention-locked SLA Domain@@@To ensure enhanced control and authorization for retention policies, change an SLA Domain to a retention-locked SLA Domain...","saas/changing_snapshot_retention_inv_page.html@@@Changing retention of snapshots from the Inventory page@@@Change the retention period of individual snapshots from the Snapshots card on the Inventory page to implement the required modifications...","saas/changing_the_password.html@@@Changing the password@@@Change the password from the RSC login page...","saas/classification_hits.html@@@Classification hits@@@Data Security Posture analyzes sensitive data and identifies them as hits when a data types detects a specific piece of content in a location that is not allowed by a specified policy...","saas/classification_job_results.html@@@Classification job results@@@Data Security Posture provides results from classification jobs, such as the classification job time, the number of hits in files, and the location of the data being searched...","saas/classifying_dynamodb_tables.html@@@Classifying Amazon DynamoDB tables@@@Identify sensitive data in Amazon DynamoDB tables by enabling sampling-based classification...","saas/cleaning_cluster_storage.html@@@Cleaning up cluster storage@@@Remove relic, downloaded, protected, or unprotected snapshots from a CDM cluster to reclaim storage space...","saas/cleaning_source_database_details.html@@@Cleaning up source database details@@@Run a script on the SAP HANA host to clean up the details of the source database using the CLI...","saas/cleaning_source_database_details_ui.html@@@Cleaning up source database details using RSC@@@Unconfigure the system copy to clean up the details of the source database using RSC...","saas/clear_network_misconfiguration.html@@@Clearing a network misconfiguration alert@@@Clear a network misconfiguration alert for a Rubrik cluster...","saas/cloning_custom_sla_domain.html@@@Cloning a custom SLA Domain@@@Create a clone of an existing SLA Domain...","saas/cloud_license_usage_details.html@@@Cloud license and usage details@@@The Cloud Licenses and Usage page provides detailed information about the purchased licenses and consumption details across different cloud providers, such as Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud Platform...","saas/cloud_understand_data_arch_snap_ret.html@@@Understand data archival and snapshot retention dynamics@@@Information about how Rubrik manages data archival and snapshot retention for Amazon EC2 instances and Azure virtual machines. Understanding these dynamics is crucial for managing storage costs and ensuring data compliance. The approach of Rubrik to archival varies based on the archival type defined in the SLA Domain...","saas/cloud_understand_data_arch_snap_ret_2.html@@@Understand data archival and snapshot retention dynamics@@@Information about how Rubrik manages data archival and snapshot retention for Amazon EC2 instances and Azure virtual machines. Understanding these dynamics is crucial for managing storage costs and ensuring data compliance. The approach of Rubrik to archival varies based on the archival type defined in the SLA Domain...","saas/cloud_workload_dashboard_aws.html@@@Cloud workload dashboard for AWS@@@The cloud workload dashboard for AWS provides a high-level view of the objects within your AWS accounts, classified by sensitivity, region, and object type...","saas/cloud_workload_dashboard_azure.html@@@Cloud workload dashboard for Azure@@@The cloud workload dashboard for Azure provides a high-level view of the objects within your Microsoft Azure accounts, classified by sensitivity, region, and object type...","saas/cluster_configuration_parameters.html@@@Cluster configuration parameters@@@Reference for Rubrik cluster configuration parameters in RSC, including parameter states, scope, and access requirements...","saas/cluster_resources_archival_policies.html@@@Cluster resource considerations for archival policies@@@An SLA Domain with more than two archival policies relies on a Rubrik cluster with sufficient resources to upload snapshots to all configured archival locations...","saas/cluster_resources_archival_policies_2.html@@@Cluster resource considerations for archival policies@@@An SLA Domain with more than two archival policies relies on a Rubrik cluster with sufficient resources to upload snapshots to all configured archival locations...","saas/cluster_storage_reclamation.html@@@Cluster storage reclamation@@@RSC displays notifications when CDM clusters are running low on storage and provides a workflow to reclaim space by removing relic, downloaded, protected, or unprotected snapshots...","saas/clusters_page.html@@@Clusters page@@@The Clusters page provides a list of Rubrik clusters connected to RSC...","saas/common/accessing_nas_cd_ui_from_rsc.html@@@Accessing the NAS CD UI from RSC@@@Access the NAS CD UI directly from RSC to manage and configure the selected NAS CD cluster...","saas/common/accessing_notifications.html@@@Accessing notifications@@@Access the Notifications tab from the menu bar to read the notifications and take appropriate actions...","saas/common/accessing_release_notes.html@@@Accessing release notes@@@Access the Release Notes tab from the menu bar to read the RSC release notes...","saas/common/account_locking.html@@@Account locking@@@Locking a user account prevents login access, even with the correct credentials. Accounts are automatically locked due to brute force attacks or user account inactivity, based on RSC configurations. Administrators can also manually lock accounts to prevent unauthorized access...","saas/common/account_unlocking.html@@@Account unlocking@@@When the user account lockout feature has locked a user account to stop a brute force attack or because of user inactivity, or if an administrator initiated the lockout, an administrator can unlock it. After unlocking the account, the user can log in using the correct credentials...","saas/common/add_floating_ip_address_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Adding floating IP addresses to a Rubrik cluster@@@Add floating IPv4 and IPv6 addresses to a Rubrik cluster for high availability and load balancing...","saas/common/adding_floating_ip_cdm.html@@@Adding floating IP addresses in CDM@@@Add floating IPv4 and IPv6 addresses to a Rubrik cluster running CDM version 9.2.0 or earlier to ensure high availability and load balancing...","saas/common/adding_ip_addresses_allowlist.html@@@Adding IP addresses to the IP allowlist@@@Add IP addresses or ranges to the RSC IP allowlist to restrict unauthorized login attempts...","saas/common/adding_local_user.html@@@Adding a local user@@@Add a local user account in RSC...","saas/common/adding_nodes_physical_clusters.html@@@Adding nodes to physical clusters@@@Add a node to physical clusters such as Rubrik appliances and supported third-party hardware appliances...","saas/common/adding_ntp_server_cdm.html@@@Adding NTP servers in CDM@@@Add an NTP server to the Rubrik cluster running CDM version 9.2.0 or earlier for a network time synchronization...","saas/common/adding_ntp_server_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Adding NTP servers to a Rubrik cluster@@@Add an NTP server to the Rubrik cluster for network time synchronization...","saas/common/adding_proxy_settings_cdm.html@@@Adding proxy settings in CDM@@@Add settings for a proxy server connected to a Rubrik cluster running CDM version 9.2.0 or earlier to filter and monitor web traffic from the Rubrik cluster, to save bandwidth by caching files or compressing incoming traffic, and to improve security...","saas/common/adding_proxy_settings_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Adding proxy settings to a Rubrik cluster@@@Add settings for a proxy server connected to a Rubrik cluster to filter and monitor web traffic from the Rubrik cluster, to save bandwidth by caching files or compressing incoming traffic, and to improve security...","saas/common/adding_routing_table_cluster.html@@@Adding a static route to a Rubrik cluster@@@Add a static route for a Rubrik cluster to a specified network destination with other network details such as netmask, gateway and interface for efficient network routing and better performance...","saas/common/adding_vlan_cdm.html@@@Adding VLANs in CDM@@@Add a VLAN to a Rubrik cluster running CDM version 9.2.0 or earlier for a logical segmentation of networks...","saas/common/adding_vlan_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Adding VLANs to a Rubrik cluster@@@Add a VLAN to a Rubrik cluster to enable a logical segmentation of networks, enhancing network and security management...","saas/common/adding_webhooks.html@@@Adding webhooks@@@Add a webhook in RSC to send event and audit details to a URL endpoint on an external system...","saas/common/advanced_custom_auth_snow_oauth.html@@@Advanced or custom authentication using ServiceNow OAuth 2.0@@@To use the Advanced or Custom Authentication method for a webhook in RSC, you are required to provide the access token for your ServiceNow instance. Before that, you are required to set up an OAuth 2.0 application in ServiceNow and generate an access token...","saas/common/anomalies_report.html@@@Anomalies report@@@The Anomalies report in RSC displays data for systems impacted by attacks such as ransomware encryption and mass deletion...","saas/common/apply_groupings_report_charts.html@@@Apply groupings to report charts@@@Groupings in report charts combine data into aggregated values, so you can compare results across clusters, object types, locations, and more...","saas/common/apply_report_filters.html@@@Apply report filters@@@You can use report filters to select the relevant data for each RSC report. Report filters apply to the entire report, including all tables and charts...","saas/common/assigning_rbac_custom_reports.html@@@Assigning role-based access control on custom reports@@@Administrators and owners can assign role-based access control on custom reports, allowing more granular control over reports...","saas/common/assigning_tasks_nascd_vms.html@@@Assigning tasks to NAS CD virtual machines@@@Name a NAS CD virtual machine and choose the types of tasks that it runs...","saas/common/audit_log_details.html@@@Audit log details@@@The Audit Log tab provides several filters with detailed information about the audit logs...","saas/common/audit_log_details_2.html@@@Audit log details@@@The Audit Log tab provides several filters with detailed information about the audit logs...","saas/common/audit_report.html@@@Audit report@@@For daily operations and auditing purposes, you can view the Audit report in RSC, which displays a comprehensive log of system activities, user actions, and internal jobs...","saas/common/authorization.html@@@Authorization@@@RSC provides role-based access control, and several methods for authenticating a user account...","saas/common/backup_strikes_reports.html@@@Backup strikes reports@@@A backup strike is an indication that an object could not successfully complete all backups scheduled on a single day...","saas/common/brute_force_lock.html@@@Brute force lock@@@A brute force lock is a type of user account locking that prevents brute force attacks. A user account is automatically locked after a configurable number of consecutive unsuccessful login attempts...","saas/common/cdm_users_report.html@@@CDM users report@@@For security monitoring and migration auditing, you can view the CDM Users Report in RSC, which displays all user accounts configured on connected CDM clusters...","saas/common/cloning_roles.html@@@Cloning a role@@@Clone an existing role to copy its permissions and settings as a new role...","saas/common/closing_a_support_tunnel.html@@@Closing a support tunnel@@@Close the support tunnel on one or more Rubrik clusters after the Rubrik Support engineer resolves the hardware or software issues...","saas/common/cloud_data_prot_usage_chargeback.html@@@Cloud data protection usage and chargeback@@@You can optimize your cloud data protection usage by confirming your total data consumption against your Rubrik license. You can use the Cloud Object Capacity report to validate the cloud usage consumption numbers and perform internal chargeback reporting to the appropriate cloud accounts...","saas/common/cloud_obj_capacity_report.html@@@Cloud Object Capacity report@@@The Cloud Object Capacity report provides a unified view of your cloud object capacity usage across your cloud workloads, such as Microsoft Azure, AWS, and Google Cloud Platform (GCP)...","saas/common/cluster_details_page.html@@@Cluster details page@@@Information about the cluster, configurations, and encryption status for a selected Rubrik cluster...","saas/common/clusters_overview_page.html@@@Clusters overview page@@@The Clusters overview page displays performance, hardware health, capacity, compliance, and protection details for a selected Rubrik cluster...","saas/common/compliance_report.html@@@Compliance report@@@For daily operations and auditing purposes, you can view the Compliance report in RSC, which displays information about the adherence of protected objects to established policies and regulatory requirements...","saas/common/configuring_account_lockout_settings.html@@@Configuring account lockout settings@@@As an RSC user with global administrator privileges, you can set up account lockout settings. This can include limits for failed login attempts, auto-unlock to protect against brute force attacks, and locking out inactive users to secure accounts after a period of inactivity...","saas/common/configuring_auto_unlock_brute_force_lock.html@@@Configuring auto unlock for brute force lock@@@As an administrator, you can configure the automatic unlocking of user accounts that have been locked due to brute force attempts...","saas/common/configuring_mfa_login_settings.html@@@Configuring MFA and login settings@@@Configure how local users log in to RSC using passkeys and TOTP through an authenticator app...","saas/common/configuring_microsoft_sentinel_integration.html@@@Configuring the Microsoft Sentinel integration@@@Integrate RSC with Microsoft Sentinel to forward anomaly detection and threat events as alerts and incidents, and optionally to initiate threat-hunting and recovery actions from Microsoft Sentinel...","saas/common/configuring_report_date_time_settings.html@@@Configuring report date and time settings@@@Configure the time zone, date format, and time format for reports to standardize how timestamps appear across the UI, PDF and CSV exports, and API responses...","saas/common/configuring_servicenow_create_incident.html@@@Configuring ServiceNow to create an incident automatically@@@To automatically create a ServiceNow incident by using the data received from an RSC webhook, configure a scripted REST API resource, add a webhook, and define the processing script...","saas/common/configuring_session_management.html@@@Configuring session management@@@With an RSC user account with administrator privileges, enhance system security by configuring the values for session timeout, maximum session timeout, and maximum concurrent sessions...","saas/common/configuring_vlan_ports_new_nodes_cli.html@@@Configuring VLAN ports for new nodes@@@Configure the VLAN ports for nodes that you are adding to an existing cluster by using the Rubrik CLI...","saas/common/create_rubrik_nas_cloud_direct_reports.html@@@Rubrik NAS Cloud Direct report templates@@@Rubrik NAS Cloud Direct report templates in RSC provide insights into resource usage and related operations...","saas/common/creating_a_report.html@@@Creating reports from templates@@@Use RSC to create a custom report by selecting a template and configuring columns, filters, and charts in the Report Creation Wizard...","saas/common/creating_a_report_schedule.html@@@Creating report schedules@@@Create and store the schedule information for a report on the Reports page. You can use this stored schedule information when you want to send the report to the selected email addresses at specific intervals...","saas/common/creating_rbac_role_dba.html@@@Creating an RBAC role for the database administrator@@@Create a new database administrator role with role-based access control privileges. These privileges provide finer granularity for determining what permissions database administrators have for performing which actions and on which objects...","saas/common/creating_role.html@@@Creating a role@@@Create a role by defining a custom set of user permissions or start by using a role template with a set of preselected permissions that you can edit for your use case...","saas/common/creating_role_2.html@@@Creating a role@@@Create a role by defining a custom set of user permissions or start by using a role template with a set of preselected permissions that you can edit for your use case...","saas/common/data_management_permission_types.html@@@Data management permission types@@@Information on data management permissions for a role based on object types, Rubrik clusters, or data sources...","saas/common/data_security.html@@@Data security@@@RSC does not access the data on Rubrik clusters or on objects protected by Rubrik clusters...","saas/common/database_log_backup_events.html@@@Database log backup events@@@RSC tracks, monitors, and displays events related to log backups and delays for your database workloads...","saas/common/deleting_a_report.html@@@Deleting reports@@@Delete a report using RSC...","saas/common/deleting_a_role.html@@@Deleting a role@@@Delete a role to remove a defined set of user permissions...","saas/common/deleting_ntp_server_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Deleting NTP servers for a Rubrik cluster@@@Delete an NTP server from a Rubrik cluster if you do not need the NTP server for network time synchronization...","saas/common/deleting_static_route_cluster.html@@@Deleting a static route from a Rubrik cluster@@@Delete an unneeded static route from the routing table of a Rubrik cluster...","saas/common/deleting_users.html@@@Deleting users@@@Remove local or SSO users from RSC...","saas/common/deleting_vlans_cdm.html@@@Deleting VLANs in CDM@@@Remove the VLANs you no longer need for the Rubrik cluster network running CDM version 9.2.0 or earlier...","saas/common/deleting_vlans_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Deleting VLANs from a Rubrik cluster@@@Delete VLANs from a Rubrik cluster to remove unnecessary network segmentation and free up resources...","saas/common/disabling_ip_allowlist.html@@@Disabling the IP allowlist@@@As an RSC administrator, disable the existing IPv4 allowlist to remove login restrictions...","saas/common/downloading_a_report.html@@@Downloading reports@@@Download reports from RSC for monitoring or auditing...","saas/common/downloading_nas_cd_virtual_machine_image.html@@@Downloading NAS CD virtual machine image@@@Use the Download VM Images option to download a NAS CD virtual machine image for hypervisor platforms, or to retrieve user data containing an order key to provision a new virtual machine on AWS EC2 or Azure virtual machine...","saas/common/edit_dns_search_domains_cdm.html@@@Editing DNS and search domains in CDM@@@Edit the DNS and search domains for a Rubrik cluster running CDM version 9.2.0 or earlier to maintain network efficiency, security, and reliability...","saas/common/edit_dns_search_domains_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Editing DNS and search domains for a Rubrik cluster@@@Edit the DNS and search domains for a Rubrik cluster to improve the network efficiency, security, and accessibility...","saas/common/editing_a_report_in_wizard.html@@@Editing reports using the wizard@@@Use the Report Creation Wizard to edit a saved report&apos;s column, filter, and chart settings...","saas/common/editing_a_report_schedule.html@@@Editing report schedules@@@Edit an existing report schedule to change and store the name of the report schedule, subscription frequency and time, and the email recipient...","saas/common/editing_a_role.html@@@Editing a role@@@Add additional permissions to a role or remove particular permissions from a role...","saas/common/editing_ntp_server_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Editing NTP servers for a Rubrik cluster@@@Edit an NTP server for a Rubrik cluster to update NTP server address, key ID, key, and key type associated with the NTP server...","saas/common/editing_role_asmt_multiple_obj.html@@@Editing role assignments for multiple users, SSO groups, or service accounts@@@Change the roles that are assigned to multiple users, SSO groups, or service accounts to modify the privileges associated with the objects...","saas/common/editing_role_asmt_single_obj.html@@@Editing role assignments for a single user, SSO group, or service account@@@Edit the roles that are assigned to a single user, SSO group, or service account to modify the privileges associated with the object...","saas/common/editing_support_access.html@@@Editing support access duration@@@A user with the Grant Own Support Access or Grant All Support Access permission can increase the support access duration for an existing support access grant...","saas/common/editing_vlans_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Editing VLANs of a Rubrik cluster@@@Edit a VLAN to update the network details associated with the VLAN...","saas/common/editing_webhook.html@@@Editing a webhook@@@Update the settings of a webhook added to RSC...","saas/common/email_notifications.html@@@Email notifications@@@Information about configuring RSC to send email notifications to users...","saas/common/enabling_ip_allowlist.html@@@Enabling the IP allowlist@@@As an RSC administrator, enable the existing IP allowlist to restrict unauthorized login attempts...","saas/common/enabling_support_access.html@@@Enabling support access@@@You can enable support access for an RSC user account...","saas/common/encryption.html@@@Encryption@@@Encryption restricts the ability of an unauthorized party to read data...","saas/common/event_types.html@@@Event types@@@Information, such as actions, changes, and operations, for the various event types in RSC. Event type information is accessed through the Events tab. You can use this information to track, monitor, and troubleshoot RSC activities...","saas/common/events.html@@@Events@@@RSC identifies, isolates, and prioritizes events and provides a unified view of all Rubrik events...","saas/common/events_page.html@@@Events page@@@The Events page displays the events of all connected Rubrik clusters in the local time zone...","saas/common/gcp_creating_custom_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for GCP@@@You can create a custom role to grant permissions to GCP resources for accessing and managing GCP resources...","saas/common/getting_started_with_rsc.html@@@Getting started with RSC@@@To start using Rubrik Security Cloud, add authorized user accounts before adding Rubrik clusters...","saas/common/inactive_account_lock.html@@@Inactive account lock@@@An inactive lock automatically protects local user accounts by locking them after a configured duration of inactivity. This feature stops unauthorized access to dormant or forgotten accounts...","saas/common/infrastructure_report.html@@@Infrastructure report@@@For daily operations and auditing purposes, you can view the Infrastructure report in RSC, which displays information about the status, health, and utilization of the data protection infrastructure components...","saas/common/ip_allowlist.html@@@IP allowlist@@@RSC administrators can specify IPv4 addresses, or IPv6 addresses if the account supports them, for the IP allowlist. RSC blocks unauthorized login attempts and unauthenticated API calls that originate from addresses that are not on the allowlist...","saas/common/locking_user_accounts_administratively.html@@@Locking user accounts administratively@@@As a user with global administrator or RSC account owner privileges, lock a local user account or an SSO user account to temporarily block user access...","saas/common/managing_high_impact_changes.html@@@Managing high impact changes@@@Administrators can review, deploy, and revert high impact changes on their own schedule during the 30-day self-service window before RSC rolls them out automatically...","saas/common/managing_webhook.html@@@Managing a webhook@@@Enable, disable, or delete a webhook added to RSC...","saas/common/maximum_concurrent_sessions.html@@@Maximum concurrent sessions@@@To enhance system security, as part of session management, RSC limits the number of concurrent sessions allowed for each user account...","saas/common/maximum_session_timeout.html@@@Maximum session timeout@@@To enhance system security, as part of session management, RSC automatically logs out user accounts and ends active user sessions after a specific duration...","saas/common/mfa_disabling_passwordless_login.html@@@Disabling passwordless login@@@Disable passwordless login to require all users to authenticate with a username and password instead of a passkey...","saas/common/mfa_enabling_passwordless_login.html@@@Enabling passwordless login@@@Enable passwordless login to enable users to authenticate with a passkey instead of a username and password...","saas/common/mfa_logging_in_with_passkey.html@@@Logging in with a passkey@@@Log in to RSC using a passkey for a faster and more secure sign-in experience...","saas/common/mfa_methods.html@@@Multifactor authentication methods@@@Multifactor authentication is a multi-step login process that enhances security by requiring multiple verification methods, reducing the risk of account compromise from stolen credentials...","saas/common/mfa_passwordless_login.html@@@Passwordless login@@@Passwordless login enables users with configured and compatible passkeys to use them as their primary login credential...","saas/common/nas_cd_cluster_details_page.html@@@NAS CD Cluster details@@@View information about virtual machines connected to a NAS CD cluster from the NAS CD Cluster Details page in RSC...","saas/common/nas_cd_ire_recovery_workflow.html@@@Recovering NAS CD data to an isolated recovery environment@@@Use task assignment and paused virtual machines to run recoveries to an isolated recovery environment, and then return to normal operation...","saas/common/nas_cd_vm_task_assignment.html@@@Task assignment for NAS CD virtual machines@@@You can control which types of tasks each NAS CD virtual machine runs and dedicate virtual machines to backups or to recoveries based on your requirements...","saas/common/navigation_history.html@@@RSC navigation history@@@You can view the navigation history for the recently visited pages in RSC...","saas/common/node_details_disk_rbk_or_supp_tp_cluster.html@@@Node disk details for Rubrik or third-party clusters@@@The node details page displays disk information for each node in a Rubrik or supported third-party cluster, including disk status, RAID configuration status, and hardware identifiers...","saas/common/node_fw_update.html@@@Node firmware update@@@Rubrik Security Cloud provides a centralized method to manage and update hardware firmware for Rubrik appliances. This includes firmware for BIOS, BMC, and HDDs. This process is independent of Rubrik CDM software upgrades...","saas/common/node_replacement_rsc.html@@@Node replacement in RSC@@@You can use RSC to replace a node in a Rubrik cluster or a supported third-party hardware cluster. You can replace faulty node hardware while keeping the same set of disks intact...","saas/common/notifications_release_notes.html@@@Notifications and release notes@@@You can access notifications and see information related to pending tasks on the Notifications tab. You can view RSC release information on the Release Notes tab...","saas/common/object_audit_report.html@@@Object Audit report@@@For daily operations and auditing purposes, you can view the Object Audit report in RSC which displays a historical record of actions and changes performed on protected objects and the users who initiated those actions...","saas/common/object_backup_task_summary_report.html@@@Object Backup Task Summary report@@@The Object Backup Task Summary report provides information about scheduled backup tasks that are triggered by the protection policy of the assigned SLA Domain...","saas/common/object_capacity_over_time_report.html@@@Object Capacity Over Time report@@@For daily operations and planning purposes, you can view the Object Capacity Over Time report in RSC...","saas/common/object_capacity_report.html@@@Object Capacity report@@@For daily operations and auditing purposes, you can view the Object capacity report in RSC, which displays the current storage consumption and size attributes of protected objects...","saas/common/opening_a_support_tunnel.html@@@Opening a support tunnel@@@Open a support tunnel on one or more Rubrik clusters to allow a Rubrik Support engineer to access the clusters and resolve hardware or software issues...","saas/common/optional_fields_for_adding_an_ntp_server.html@@@Optional fields for adding an NTP server@@@Information about the optional fields available when adding an NTP server to a Rubrik cluster...","saas/common/optional_settings_for_adding_a_webhook.html@@@Optional settings for adding a webhook@@@Information about optional settings that you can configure while adding a webhook...","saas/common/outbound_connection_through_ports.html@@@Outbound connection through ports@@@RSC requires you to open an outbound connection through port 443 for a Rubrik cluster to access specific sites...","saas/common/password_constraints.html@@@RSC password constraints@@@RSC passwords must comply with the password constraints...","saas/common/pausing_nas_cd_vm_tasks.html@@@Pausing tasks on NAS CD virtual machines@@@Pause a NAS CD virtual machine to stop it from running new tasks without removing it from the cluster...","saas/common/prerequisites_adding_nodes.html@@@Prerequisites for adding nodes@@@Review additional steps that may be required before adding or replacing nodes on a Rubrik cluster that has special network settings, such as VLAN or LACP, configured...","saas/common/prerequisites_node_replacement.html@@@Prerequisites for node replacement@@@Information about the prerequisites that you must perform before replacing a node...","saas/common/protection_pause_report.html@@@Paused Protection report@@@The Paused Protection report lists the objects, clusters, and SLA Domains with directly paused protection. You can use this report to audit paused entities and schedule recurring reminders to resume their protection...","saas/common/protection_pause_report_fields.html@@@Paused Protection report fields@@@Information about the Paused Protection report fields...","saas/common/protection_report.html@@@Protection report@@@For daily operations and auditing purposes, you can view the Protection report in RSC, which displays the current protection status and key attributes of protected objects...","saas/common/protection_task_detail_report.html@@@Protection Tasks Details report@@@For daily operations and auditing purposes, you can view the Protection Tasks Details report in RSC, which displays detailed information about the tasks related to data protection activities...","saas/common/qauth_roles_report.html@@@Quorum Authorization Roles report@@@The Quorum Authorization Roles report displays a list of users who can approve specific policies associated with a Quorum Authorization request. Using this report, you can easily find the users with the QAuth reviewer role and the policies they can approve...","saas/common/rbac_practical_scenarios_role_config.html@@@Practical scenarios for role configuration@@@Information about the scenarios that map common administrative tasks to their minimum required privileges, offering a blueprint to help create custom roles based on the Principle of Least Privilege (PoLP)...","saas/common/rbac_roles_dba.html@@@Role-based access control roles for database administrators@@@Role-based access control roles for database administrators allow you to specify with granularity which objects database administrators have access to and what permissions they have to perform actions on these objects...","saas/common/recovery_tasks_details_report.html@@@Recovery Tasks Details report@@@For monitoring service level agreements and evaluating the efficiency of your disaster recovery plan, you can view the Recovery Tasks Details report in RSC...","saas/common/remove_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Remove a Rubrik cluster@@@You can remove a Rubrik cluster from RSC when it is no longer needed...","saas/common/removing_connected_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Removing a connected Rubrik cluster@@@Remove a connected Rubrik cluster from RSC if it is no longer required...","saas/common/removing_disconnected_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Removing a disconnected Rubrik cluster@@@Remove a disconnected Rubrik cluster from RSC because it is no longer required...","saas/common/removing_disk_rbk_or_supp_tp_cluster.html@@@Removing a disk from Rubrik or third-party clusters@@@Remove a disk from a Rubrik or supported third-party cluster to replace a failed or missing disk...","saas/common/removing_ip_addresses_ip_allowlist.html@@@Removing IP addresses from the IP allowlist@@@Remove IP addresses or ranges from the RSC IP allowlist, either individually or in bulk...","saas/common/remvg_node_rubrik_third_party_hw_cluster.html@@@Removing a node from a Rubrik or supported third-party hardware cluster@@@Permanently remove a node from your Rubrik or supported third-party hardware cluster to repurpose the node or to update a cluster configuration during a hardware refresh...","saas/common/replacing_node_rbk_third_party_hw_cluster.html@@@Replacing a node in a Rubrik or supported third-party hardware cluster@@@In RSC, replace a faulty node in a Rubrik or supported third-party hardware cluster when there is no disk failure...","saas/common/report_date_time_settings.html@@@Report date and time settings@@@You can configure the time zone, date format, and time format to control how timestamps appear in reports...","saas/common/report_schedules.html@@@Report schedules@@@Report schedules automatically deliver RSC reporting data, reducing the amount of time spent on generating accurate and timely reports...","saas/common/reporting.html@@@Reports@@@You can use the Reports feature to perform audits and data management planning by creating customizable reports for application data protection and for the underlying infrastructure of Rubrik Security Cloud...","saas/common/reports_page_nav.html@@@Find reports using the navigation panel@@@You can use the navigation panel on the Reports page to find reports by category, search, or pinned status...","saas/common/resuming_nas_cd_vm_tasks.html@@@Resuming tasks on NAS CD virtual machines@@@Resume paused tasks on a NAS CD virtual machine to continue the assigned task again...","saas/common/revoking_support_access.html@@@Revoking support access@@@A user with the Grant Own Support Access or Grant All Support Access permission can revoke an existing support access grant...","saas/common/roles_and_permissions.html@@@User roles and permissions@@@Roles are sets of permissions that are assigned to a user account. You can assign multiple roles to a user account...","saas/common/roles_report.html@@@Roles report@@@For daily operations and auditing purposes, you can view the Roles report in RSC, which displays the roles created by the administrator and their descriptions...","saas/common/rsc_rmfa_totp.html@@@Rubrik MFA with TOTP@@@The Rubrik two-step verification feature uses time-based one-time passwords in addition to the user login credentials to enforce multi-factor authentication on user accounts...","saas/common/rsc_rmfa_totp_2.html@@@Rubrik MFA with TOTP@@@The Rubrik two-step verification feature uses time-based one-time passwords in addition to the user login credentials to enforce multi-factor authentication on user accounts...","saas/common/rsc_roles.html@@@Roles@@@Roles define privileges for user accounts in a Rubrik cluster. With the administrator account, you can assign roles that grant different access permissions to user accounts for specific purposes...","saas/common/rsc_ui_table_data_export.html@@@RSC web UI table data export@@@You can export the data available in tables in the RSC web UI as CSV files for further analysis or reporting...","saas/common/rubrik_clusters.html@@@Rubrik clusters@@@A Rubrik cluster is an instance of Rubrik CDM running on any virtual or physical platform. You can add the Rubrik cluster to RSC to enable extended features for the cluster...","saas/common/rubrik_clusters_2.html@@@Rubrik clusters@@@A Rubrik cluster is an instance of Rubrik CDM running on any virtual or physical platform. You can add the Rubrik cluster to RSC to enable extended features for the cluster...","saas/common/rubrik_custom_webhook_template.html@@@Rubrik custom webhook template@@@You can create custom webhook templates in RSC by defining JSON payloads with variables supported by Rubrik...","saas/common/rubrik_nas_cd_clusters.html@@@Rubrik NAS CD clusters@@@Rubrik NAS Cloud Direct clusters are Rubrik clusters that protect large-scale NAS data...","saas/common/rubrik_secure_vault.html@@@Rubrik Secure Vault@@@Rubrik Secure Vault is the backup storage platform that forms the data plane of the Rubrik architecture. RSC manages Rubrik Secure Vault...","saas/common/saas_authentication.html@@@Authentication@@@Rubrik Security Cloud authentication restricts access to a specified set of users through strong passwords and mandatory MFA...","saas/common/searching_an_event.html@@@Searching for an event@@@RSC searches a specific event by object name...","saas/common/sec_editing_device_name.html@@@Editing a device name@@@You can edit the name of a device that you used to log in to RSC from the User Preferences page. Providing a unique name to a device improves device identification and helps you distinguish between different devices accessing your RSC account...","saas/common/sec_new_device_login_notification.html@@@New device login notification@@@RSC notifies you when a new device is used to log in to your RSC account, providing details such as device name, IP address, and location...","saas/common/sec_removing_device.html@@@Removing a device@@@You can remove a device from the My Devices page in RSC to get notified whenever RSC detects a login from that device...","saas/common/security.html@@@Security@@@Rubrik Security Cloud provides end-to-end security for data management information...","saas/common/service_account_report.html@@@Service Account report@@@For daily operations and auditing purposes, you can view the Service Account report in RSC, which displays service accounts and their roles...","saas/common/session_inactivity_timeout.html@@@Session inactivity timeout@@@To enhance system security, as part of session management, RSC automatically logs out user accounts and ends user sessions after a specific duration of inactivity...","saas/common/session_management.html@@@Session management@@@The session management feature enhances system security by ending inactive user sessions, ending active user sessions after a specific duration, and limiting the number of concurrent sessions allowed for each user...","saas/common/session_timeout_notifications.html@@@Session timeout notifications@@@To help you anticipate and respond to session expiry, RSC displays advance warnings before your session ends and, after logout, shows the reason that the session ended...","saas/common/setting_data_management_privileges.html@@@Setting data management privileges by Rubrik cluster@@@Set privileges for a role to permit user accounts with the role to manage backup and recovery operations on a Rubrik cluster...","saas/common/setting_disk_rbk_or_supp_tp_cluster.html@@@Setting up disks on Rubrik or supported third-party clusters@@@Set up a disk on a Rubrik or supported third-party cluster...","saas/common/setting_dm_privileges_by_object_type.html@@@Setting data management privileges by object type@@@Set data protection and recovery permissions for protected data objects...","saas/common/setting_system_configuration_privileges.html@@@Setting system configuration privileges@@@System configuration privileges enable users to manage aspects of RSC and the associated Rubrik clusters...","saas/common/sso_group_report.html@@@SSO Groups report@@@For daily operations and auditing purposes, you can view the SSO Groups report in RSC, which displays SSO groups and their roles...","saas/common/support_access.html@@@Support access@@@The support access feature provides Rubrik Support with secure, read-only access to your Rubrik Security Cloud domain on behalf of an existing user account...","saas/common/support_tunnel_page_available_info.html@@@Information available on the Support Tunnel page@@@Information about the details provided by the Support Tunnel page, including cluster name, UUID, tunnel status, open nodes, open port, time opened, and time left...","saas/common/support_tunnel_timeout_setting.html@@@Timeout setting for support tunnels@@@You can specify the duration for which a Rubrik support tunnel remains open by setting either an inactivity timeout or an absolute timeout. Inactivity timeout resets with any activity, and absolute timeout is fixed regardless of activity...","saas/common/support_tunnels.html@@@Support tunnel for RSC@@@Support tunnel is a functionality that allows authorized Rubrik Support engineers gain secure, logged access to Rubrik clusters for diagnosis and resolution of hardware and software issues...","saas/common/table_describing_aws_dba_permissions.html@@@Table describing AWS database administrator permissions@@@Information about role-based access control permissions required for database administrators to perform actions on AWS...","saas/common/table_describing_aws_dba_permissions_2.html@@@Table describing AWS database administrator permissions@@@Information about role-based access control permissions required for database administrators to perform actions on AWS...","saas/common/table_describing_db2_dba_permissions.html@@@Table describing Db2 database administrator permissions@@@Information about role-based access control permissions required for database administrators to perform actions on Db2...","saas/common/table_describing_mongodb_dba_permissions.html@@@Table describing MongoDB database administrator permissions@@@Information about role-based access control permissions required for database administrators to perform actions on MongoDB...","saas/common/table_describing_mv_dba_permissions.html@@@Table describing Managed Volume database administrator permissions@@@Information about role-based access control permissions required for database administrators to perform actions on Managed Volumes...","saas/common/table_describing_oracle_dba_permissions.html@@@Table describing Oracle database administrator permissions@@@Information about role-based access control permissions required for database administrators to perform actions on Oracle...","saas/common/table_describing_sap_hana_dba_permissions.html@@@Table describing SAP HANA database administrator permissions@@@Information about role-based access control permissions required for database administrators to perform actions on SAP HANA...","saas/common/table_describing_sql_server_dba_permissions.html@@@Table describing SQL Server database administrator permissions@@@Information about role-based access control permissions required for database administrators to perform actions on SQL Server...","saas/common/testing_webhook.html@@@Testing a webhook@@@Determine if the webhook settings are working correctly...","saas/common/threat_monitoring_report.html@@@Threat Monitoring report@@@For proactive security monitoring and auditing purposes, you can view the Threat Monitoring report in RSC, which displays details about identified security threats and their status...","saas/common/unlocking_inactive_accounts.html@@@Unlocking inactive accounts@@@Unlock user accounts locked due to inactivity using a self-service password reset feature...","saas/common/unlocking_user_accounts_administratively.html@@@Unlocking user accounts administratively@@@As a user with administrator or RSC account owner privileges, unlock a local user account or an SSO user account locked due to administrative actions, brute force, or user inactivity...","saas/common/updating_node_firmware_in_rsc.html@@@Updating node firmware in RSC@@@Update the firmware for hardware components on Rubrik cluster nodes directly from Rubrik Security Cloud. You can update specific nodes or the entire cluster using a rolling upgrade process...","saas/common/user_account_lockout.html@@@User account lockout@@@The user account lockout feature enhances system security by providing global administrators the ability to lock and unlock user accounts. This feature also prevents unauthorized access from brute force attacks and safeguards local user accounts by automatically locking them after a configurable period of inactivity...","saas/common/users_reports.html@@@Users report@@@For daily operations and auditing purposes, you can view the Users report in RSC, which displays users and their roles...","saas/common/viewing_audit_log_information.html@@@Viewing audit log information@@@RSC displays the Audit log page and lists user-initiated events by user names...","saas/common/viewing_clusters_page.html@@@Viewing the Clusters page@@@RSC displays an aggregate view of all connected Rubrik clusters on the Clusters page...","saas/common/viewing_events_page_clusters_tab.html@@@Viewing the Events page from the Clusters tab@@@View the Events page from the Clusters tab to get a global view of all events of the selected Rubrik cluster connected to RSC...","saas/common/viewing_nas_cd_virtual_machine_details.html@@@Viewing NAS CD virtual machine details@@@View the details of a NAS CD virtual machine...","saas/common/viewing_network_details_cdm_921_later.html@@@Viewing network details in CDM v9.2.1 or later@@@View network details of a Rubrik cluster to manage the network settings of the Rubrik cluster...","saas/common/viewing_network_details_rubrik_clusters.html@@@Viewing network details for Rubrik clusters@@@From the Network Details page, review and manage networks associated with a Rubrik cluster. This includes viewing network configurations such as node names, networks, IP addresses, floating IPs, and subnet masks...","saas/common/viewing_session_timeout_info.html@@@Viewing session timeout information@@@View your remaining session time and the per-organization session timeout policies that apply to your RSC account...","saas/common/viewing_support_access_audit_logs.html@@@Viewing support access audit logs@@@A user with the View All Support Access permission can view and download the audit log information of a support access instance...","saas/common/viewing_the_events_page_from_the_dashboard.html@@@Viewing the Events page from the Dashboard@@@View the Events page from the Dashboard for a global view of RSC events...","saas/common/visiting_a_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Visiting a Rubrik cluster@@@RSC allows easy and direct access to connected Rubrik clusters from the Clusters page...","saas/common/webhook_microsoft_sentinel_config_requirements.html@@@Microsoft Sentinel webhook configuration requirements@@@Webhooks in RSC for Microsoft Sentinel integration require specific Azure prerequisites and endpoint information...","saas/common/webhook_payload.html@@@Webhook payload@@@Event and audit payload formats that RSC sends to a webhook endpoint share a common format...","saas/common/webhook_payload_identity_activity.html@@@Webhook payload for identity activity log events@@@Information about the payload format that RSC sends to a webhook endpoint for identity activity log events...","saas/common/webhook_payload_threat_hunt.html@@@Webhook payload for threat hunting events@@@RSC sends webhook events at each stage of a threat hunt, each with a different eventInfo payload...","saas/common/webhook_payload_threat_hunt_lifecycle.html@@@Threat hunt lifecycle events@@@RSC sends ThreatHuntStarted, ThreatHuntInProgress, and ThreatHuntFailed webhook events with a null eventInfo field during the lifecycle of a threat hunt...","saas/common/webhook_payload_threat_hunt_match.html@@@Threat hunt file match events@@@RSC sends one ThreatHuntMatchDetails webhook event per file match detected during a threat hunt...","saas/common/webhook_payload_threat_hunt_success.html@@@Threat hunt success events@@@RSC sends ThreatHuntSucceeded or ThreatHuntPartiallySucceeded webhook events when a threat hunt finishes, each carrying the same eventInfo fields...","saas/common/webhook_payload_threat_monitoring.html@@@Webhook payload for Threat Monitoring events@@@RSC sends one webhook event per file match detected during a Threat Monitoring scan...","saas/common/webhook_splunk_config_requirements.html@@@Splunk requirements@@@RSC webhooks require specific Splunk settings...","saas/common/webhooks.html@@@Webhooks@@@Webhook integration sends event details related to a service account from RSC to external systems. This makes it easier to monitor and analyze logs for security incidents while keeping control over data transmission...","saas/common/webhooks_identity_activity.html@@@Identity activity log webhooks@@@Identity activity log webhooks stream identity change events from your identity providers to an external Security Information and Event Management or alerting platform...","saas/common/webhooks_threat_detection.html@@@Threat detection webhooks@@@Threat detection webhooks send event payloads from Threat Monitoring, threat hunting, and threat intel to an external Security Information and Event Management or alerting platform...","saas/common/workload_level_data_mgmt_perms.html@@@Workload-level data management permissions@@@Some data management permissions can be assigned at several different hierarchy levels, including the entire workload level...","saas/common_fileset_use_cases.html@@@Common Fileset Use Cases@@@Provides examples of how Rubrik Security Cloud interprets inclusion and exclusion rules for filesets...","saas/common_perms_errors_solution.html@@@Common permission errors and solutions@@@Information about common permission-related errors, their causes, and recommended solutions...","saas/compliance_rl_cnp_workloads.html@@@Compliance retention lock for cloud native workloads@@@Compliance retention lock for cloud native workloads provides a higher level of security than Governance mode by enforcing strict immutability for your cloud data...","saas/config_anomaly_detection_sensitivity.html@@@Configuring Anomaly Detection sensitivity@@@Configure how aggressively Anomaly Detection flags potential threats by selecting a sensitivity level...","saas/configure_sap_hana_storage_snapshots.html@@@Configure SAP HANA storage snapshots@@@Using RSC, you can take storage snapshots of SAP HANA systems running on an Azure virtual machine and use those snapshots to recover your SAP HANA databases. Storage snapshots are fast, encrypted, have negligible network load, and capture the entire data area at a particular point in time...","saas/configure_sap_hana_system_replication.html@@@Configure SAP HANA system replication@@@SAP HANA system replication ensures high availability and disaster recovery for your SAP HANA system by setting up a backup system in the same or a different data center. RSC protects these configurations through SLA Domain policies...","saas/configuring_app_consistency_batch.html@@@Configuring batch application consistency@@@Configure application consistency across virtual machines, hosts, clusters, data centers, and other objects in vSphere environments...","saas/configuring_app_consistency_single_vm.html@@@Configuring application consistency for a single VM@@@Configure application consistency for a single vSphere virtual machine in RSC...","saas/configuring_archival_policy.html@@@Configuring an archival policy@@@When you create or edit a custom SLA Domain, configure the archival policy for the SLA Domain to define which snapshots to archive, the archive schedule, and the archival location...","saas/configuring_archival_policy_2.html@@@Configuring an archival policy@@@When you create or edit a custom SLA Domain, configure the archival policy for the SLA Domain to define which snapshots to archive, the archive schedule, and the archival location...","saas/configuring_aws_exo_host_acct_rmc.html@@@Configuring an AWS Exocompute host account for a Rubrik-managed cluster@@@After creating an Exocompute host account for a Rubrik-managed cluster, configure an Exocompute instance in the Exocompute host account by adding a region...","saas/configuring_backup_throttle_fileset.html@@@Configuring backup throttle for a fileset@@@Configure or edit the backup throttle mode for a fileset to optimize the backup performance...","saas/configuring_cascading_archival.html@@@Configuring cascading archival@@@When you create or edit an SLA Domain, configure cascading archival settings for a replication target Rubrik cluster...","saas/configuring_cdm_admin_mfa_device.html@@@Configuring the CDM admin user MFA device@@@Configure or change the time-based one-time password (TOTP) device used for multi-factor authentication on the admin account of a Rubrik cluster from RSC...","saas/configuring_certificates_sso_idp.html@@@Configuring certificates for SSO IdP@@@You can use the default TLS certificates or select any TLS certificate that you have added to RSC to authenticate the SAML Service Provider for your IdP...","saas/configuring_email_notifications.html@@@Configuring email notifications@@@In RSC, configure email notification preferences for users...","saas/configuring_kmip_credentials.html@@@Configuring KMIP credentials@@@Before adding a KMIP server to a Rubrik cluster, to establish a connection between the Rubrik cluster and KMIP server, you must configure RSC with the address and credentials of the KMIP server...","saas/configuring_mfa_account.html@@@Configuring MFA for your account@@@Increase the security of your account by enabling multifactor authentication...","saas/configuring_object_level_snapshot_window.html@@@Configuring an object-level snapshot window@@@Configure a snapshot window on one or more CDM objects to override the snapshot window defined in the SLA Domain...","saas/configuring_okta_itp_integration.html@@@Configuring Okta ITP integration@@@To secure sensitive data in your production environment by combining Rubrik User intelligence and Okta Identity Threat Protection, configure Okta integration in RSC using the Integrations page...","saas/configuring_password_policy_local_users.html@@@Configuring password policy for local users@@@An administrator for RSC configures the password policy for local user accounts to enforce security requirements...","saas/configuring_post_failover_backup.html@@@Configuring post-failover backup behavior@@@Define how RSC handles the first backup after an SAP HANA failover occurs at the system level...","saas/configuring_pre_post_snapshot_scripts.html@@@Configuring pre-snapshot and post-snapshot scripts@@@Before enabling the application-consistent snapshot feature for a virtual machine, to notify the associated application before and after taking the snapshot of the virtual machine, configure pre-snapshot and post-snapshot scripts in RSC...","saas/configuring_private_container_registry.html@@@Configuring Private Container Registry@@@Configure a Private Container Registry to retrieve the Docker images from a registry you host...","saas/configuring_replication_policy.html@@@Configuring replication policy@@@Configure the replication policy for an SLA Domain when creating a custom SLA Domain or when editing any SLA Domain...","saas/configuring_service_principal_rmc.html@@@Configuring a service principal for Rubrik-managed credentials@@@Configure a service principal in your Azure Key Vault tenant and grant it the required permissions so that Rubrik can access your keys using secretless provisioning...","saas/configuring_snmpv2c_support.html@@@Configuring SNMPv2c and SNMP v3 support@@@To allow an SNMP manager to poll the Rubrik cluster, configure SNMPv2c and SNMP v3 on the Rubrik cluster...","saas/configuring_sso_rsc_adfs.html@@@Configuring single sign-on in RSC@@@Configure SSO in RSC by uploading the metadata file of the identity provider and downloading the RSC metadata file...","saas/configuring_sso_rsc_adfs_2.html@@@Configuring single sign-on in RSC@@@Configure SSO in RSC by uploading the metadata file of the identity provider and downloading the RSC metadata file...","saas/connecting_a_cdm_cluster.html@@@Connecting a Rubrik cluster@@@To enhance data protection capabilities, connect a Rubrik cluster to a Rubrik Security Cloud account...","saas/connecting_crowdstrike_threat_intel.html@@@Connecting CrowdStrike Threat Intel to RSC@@@Connect a CrowdStrike Threat Intel instance to RSC so that Threat Monitoring can scan your data using indicators of compromise (IOCs) from your CrowdStrike feed...","saas/connecting_servicenow_instance.html@@@Connecting a ServiceNow instance@@@Connect a ServiceNow instance to RSC to enable ServiceNow ticket creation for Data Security Posture...","saas/connecting_taxii_threat_intel.html@@@Connecting a TAXII threat intel source to RSC@@@Connect a TAXII 2.1 server to RSC so that Threat Monitoring can scan your data using indicators of compromise from a TAXII feed...","saas/connecting_to_microsoft_purview.html@@@Connecting to Microsoft Purview@@@You can connect to Microsoft Purview to detect and assign Microsoft Information Protection labels that do not match data sensitivity findings in RSC. When configured, Rubrik will have visibility into the labels applied to your documents, and you can define your own policies to identify mislabeled and unlabeled sensitive data...","saas/continuous_data_protection_dashboard.html@@@Continuous Data Protection dashboard@@@The Continuous Data Protection dashboard provides information on the CDP status of virtual machines...","saas/create_user_acct_bucket_access.html@@@Creating a user account with access to the bucket@@@Create an IAM user account with policy-based access to the Amazon S3 bucket...","saas/creating_a_live_mount_of_a_virtual_disk_snapshot_for_recovery.html@@@Creating a Live Mount of a virtual disk snapshot for recovery@@@Create new virtual disks from a snapshot using the Rubrik cluster as the datastore...","saas/creating_a_sdd_report.html@@@Creating a Data Security Posture report@@@Use RSC to create reports using the available templates...","saas/creating_advanced_tags.html@@@Creating advanced tags@@@Create advanced tags by combining multiple tags with conditional logic...","saas/creating_aws_cloud_account.html@@@Creating an AWS cloud account@@@Create a cloud account for the Protection use case to protect AWS resources within the account. When archiving is required, add the target account as a cloud account for the Storage use case...","saas/creating_aws_iam_policy_for_cloudout.html@@@Creating an AWS IAM policy for Amazon S3 archival locations@@@Create an AWS Identity and Access Management policy for Amazon S3 archival locations...","saas/creating_classification_jobs_predefined_policies.html@@@Creating classification jobs with predefined data categories@@@You can use predefined data categories to create classification jobs...","saas/creating_cloud_archival_location_aws_storage_account.html@@@Creating archival locations for AWS storage accounts@@@Create a customer-controlled AWS archival location and select the encryption type for EC2 instance, EBS volume, S3 buckets, or DynamoDB table snapshots...","saas/creating_custom_role_anomaly_detection.html@@@Creating a custom role for Anomaly Detection@@@To grant specific privileges for Anomaly Detection and other security features, you can create a custom role and manually assign permissions...","saas/creating_cyber_rp_ad_forest.html@@@Creating a cyber Recovery Plan for an Active Directory forest@@@Create a cyber Recovery Plan to recover an Active Directory forest into an isolated VMware environment...","saas/creating_cyber_rp_ahv.html@@@Creating a cyber Recovery Plan for AHV virtual machines@@@Create a cyber Recovery Plan to protect a set of AHV virtual machines...","saas/creating_cyber_rp_aws.html@@@Creating a cyber Recovery Plan for AWS EC2 instances@@@Create a cyber Recovery Plan to protect a set of AWS EC2 instances...","saas/creating_cyber_rp_azure.html@@@Creating a cyber Recovery Plan for Azure virtual machines@@@Create a cyber Recovery Plan to protect a set of Azure virtual machines...","saas/creating_cyber_rp_vsphere.html@@@Creating a cyber Recovery Plan for vSphere virtual machines@@@Create a cyber Recovery Plan to protect a set of virtual machines...","saas/creating_disaster_rp_ahv.html@@@Creating a disaster Recovery Plan for AHV virtual machines@@@Create a disaster Recovery Plan to enable failover testing and production failover orchestration for a set of AHV virtual machines...","saas/creating_disaster_rp_vsphere.html@@@Creating a disaster Recovery Plan for vSphere virtual machines@@@Create a disaster Recovery Plan to enable failover testing and production failover orchestration for a set of virtual machines...","saas/creating_in_place_rp.html@@@Creating an in-place Recovery Plan@@@Create an in-place Recovery Plan to protect a set of virtual machines and enable recovery on the same Rubrik cluster where the source virtual machines are protected...","saas/creating_live_mount_of_a_virtual_machine_for_recovery.html@@@Creating a Live Mount of a virtual machine for recovery@@@Create a virtual machine from the snapshot...","saas/creating_ncd_compliance_report.html@@@Creating a NAS CD compliance report@@@In RSC, create a report using the Compliance report template to summarize the details about the compliance status of NAS CD objects...","saas/creating_ncd_object_capacity_report.html@@@Creating a NAS CD Object Capacity report@@@In RSC, create a report using the Object Capacity report template to summarize the storage consumption details of the protected NAS CD objects...","saas/creating_ncd_protection_report.html@@@Creating a NAS CD protection report@@@In RSC, create a report using the Protection report template to summarize the details about the protection status of NAS CD objects...","saas/creating_passkeys.html@@@Creating passkeys@@@Create a platform or roaming security passkey to enable web authentication for your RSC user account...","saas/creating_personal_access_token.html@@@Creating a personal access token@@@Create a personal access token to authenticate to the RSC API under your own user identity...","saas/creating_qauth_policy_for_rcv_actions.html@@@Creating a quorum authorization policy for RCV actions@@@To prevent a single user from performing data-modifying management actions on your Rubrik Cloud Vault locations, create a policy for quorum authorization of such actions...","saas/creating_rcv_loc_cn_workloads_aws.html@@@Creating RCV locations for cloud native workloads on AWS@@@Create a Rubrik Cloud Vault location to archive the backups of cloud-native workloads...","saas/creating_rcv_loc_cn_workloads_aws_2.html@@@Creating RCV locations for cloud native workloads on AWS@@@Create a Rubrik Cloud Vault location to archive the backups of cloud-native workloads...","saas/creating_rcv_loc_cn_workloads_gcp.html@@@Creating RCV locations for cloud-native workloads on GCP@@@Create a Rubrik Cloud Vault location on GCP to archive GCP workload snapshots...","saas/creating_rcv_loc_dc_workloads_aws.html@@@Creating RCV locations for AWS data center workloads@@@Create a Rubrik Cloud Vault location, assign it to a Rubrik cluster, and configure encryption with an AWS KMS or RSA key for archiving backups of data center workloads...","saas/creating_rcv_loc_dc_workloads_gcp.html@@@Creating RCV locations for GCP data center workloads@@@Create a Rubrik Cloud Vault location on GCP, assign it to a Rubrik cluster, and configure encryption with an RSA key to archive backup data for data center workloads...","saas/creating_rcv_loc_nas_cd_aws.html@@@Creating RCV locations for NAS CD objects on AWS@@@Create a Rubrik Cloud Vault location for assigning to NAS CD objects...","saas/creating_sla_domains_without_snapshot_schedules.html@@@Creating SLA Domains without snapshot schedules@@@Create an SLA Domain without snapshot schedules for Continuous Data Protection-only SLA Domains...","saas/creating_sla_domains_without_snapshot_schedules_2.html@@@Creating SLA Domains without snapshot schedules@@@Create an SLA Domain without snapshot schedules for Continuous Data Protection-only SLA Domains...","saas/creating_support_case.html@@@Creating a support case from the Support Cases page@@@Submit a new Rubrik support case directly from the Support Cases page in RSC...","saas/crowdstrike_threat_intel_filters.html@@@IOC filters for CrowdStrike Threat Intel@@@Filters that Threat Monitoring applies to IOCs from a CrowdStrike Threat Intel instance...","saas/crowdstrike_threat_intel_integration.html@@@CrowdStrike Threat Intel integration@@@You can connect CrowdStrike Threat Intel to RSC and have Threat Monitoring scan your data for indicators of compromise (IOCs) from your own CrowdStrike feed...","saas/custom_intel_feed.html@@@Custom intel feed@@@To monitor data for specific threats, you can create a custom feed of indicators of compromise...","saas/customer_support.html@@@Customer Support for RSC@@@You can grant support access and open and close a support tunnel in the Customer Support menu. The support access feature enables Rubrik Support to access your RSC domain securely in read-only mode. Rubrik Support uses the support tunnel to examine the health of the Rubrik cluster and to troubleshoot and resolve issues. You can also run network diagnostics from the Customer Support menu...","saas/customizing_dashboard_widgets.html@@@Customizable dashboard widgets@@@Customize dashboard widgets by adding, removing, resizing, or rearranging the widgets on the dashboard page...","saas/customizing_date_and_time_settings.html@@@Customizing date and time settings@@@Customize date and time settings based on your preferences, location, and specific requirements...","saas/customizing_the_data_protection_dashboard.html@@@Customizing the Data Protection dashboard@@@Customize the Data Protection dashboard by adding, removing, resizing, and rearranging the widgets...","saas/cyber_event_lockdown.html@@@Cyber Event Lockdown@@@When a suspected cyber attack, ransomware attack, or other event affecting data integrity impacts your environment, you can use Cyber Event Lockdown to protect the data on your Rubrik clusters...","saas/cyber_recovery_ad_forest_prereq.html@@@Cyber Recovery for Active Directory forest prerequisites@@@Infrastructure and data protection requirements that must be in place before you create a cyber recovery plan to recover an Active Directory forest into an isolated environment...","saas/data_centers_license_usage_details.html@@@Data Centers license and usage details@@@The Data Centers Licenses and Usage page provides detailed information about purchased licenses and consumption details across data centers...","saas/data_discovery_and_classification.html@@@Data Discovery and Classification@@@The Data Discovery and Classification feature in Data Security Posture discovers sensitive information in structured and unstructured data that is subject to regulation...","saas/data_discovery_class_dynamodb.html@@@Data Discovery and Classification for Amazon DynamoDB@@@Data Discovery and Classification for Amazon DynamoDB uses sampling to identify sensitive information while minimizing data reads and operational costs...","saas/data_discovery_class_microsoft_365.html@@@Data Discovery and Classification for Microsoft 365@@@The classification performed by Data Discovery and Classification for Microsoft 365 identifies sensitive data that matches a specified policy within backups...","saas/data_discovery_class_oracle_db_req.html@@@Oracle database requirements@@@Data Discovery and Classification for Oracle databases has specific requirements depending on the authentication method...","saas/data_discovery_class_oracle_dbs.html@@@Data Discovery and Classification for Oracle databases@@@The classification mechanism for Oracle databases has specific processes and requirements compared to file system classification for other supported workloads...","saas/data_discovery_class_sql_server_db_req.html@@@Microsoft SQL Server requirements@@@Data Discovery and Classification for SQL Server databases requires specific configuration based on the authentication method...","saas/data_discovery_class_sql_server_dbs.html@@@Data Discovery and Classification for MS SQL Server databases@@@The classification performed by Data Discovery and Classification for Microsoft SQL Server databases differs from the file system classification for other supported workloads...","saas/data_impact_individual_object_view.html@@@Individual object view@@@The individual object view shows file change activity for a single protected object across backup snapshots. The Snapshot and File Activity tabs support investigation and recovery initiation at the snapshot level and file level...","saas/data_impact_investigation.html@@@Data impact investigation@@@Data impact investigation enables IT and backup administrators to identify the scope of objects and files affected by events such as ransomware, mass deletion, or accidental data loss, and to recover to a healthy snapshot without switching between tools...","saas/data_impact_investigation_dashboard.html@@@Investigation dashboard@@@The Investigation dashboard lists all objects with Anomaly Detection enabled and their most recent file change activity, so administrators can quickly identify objects impacted by a deletion or encryption event...","saas/data_impact_prereq_object_types.html@@@Prerequisites and supported object types@@@Requirements for accessing data impact investigation and the workload types that support the feature...","saas/data_management_permissions.html@@@Data management permissions@@@Details of data management permissions that are available for assignment to different roles in RSC...","saas/data_observability_enablement.html@@@Data Observability enablement@@@You can enable Anomaly Detectionand Data Security Posture for providing Data Observability. Enabling Anomaly Detection and Data Security Posture for Azure virtual machines and managed disks has specific requirements...","saas/data_observability_for_azure_vms.html@@@Data Observability for Azure virtual machines and managed disks@@@To provide Data Observability, you can enable Anomaly Detection to detect ransomware attacks, and enable Data Security Posture to identify sensitive data in backups for Azure virtual machines and managed disks...","saas/data_observability_req_ncd_data_sets.html@@@NAS CD Data Observability requirements and limitations@@@NAS CD data sets have specific requirements for enabling backups and configuring Data Observability...","saas/data_observability_sharepoint_onedrive.html@@@Data Observability for Microsoft SharePoint and OneDrive@@@To provide Data Observability, you can enable Anomaly Detection and Threat Monitoring to detect ransomware attacks and configure Data Security Posture to identify sensitive data in backups of Microsoft OneDrive and SharePoint objects...","saas/data_observability_sharepoint_onedrive_2.html@@@Data Observability for Microsoft SharePoint and OneDrive@@@To provide Data Observability, you can enable Anomaly Detection and Threat Monitoring to detect ransomware attacks and configure Data Security Posture to identify sensitive data in backups of Microsoft OneDrive and SharePoint objects...","saas/data_protection_dashboard.html@@@Data Protection dashboard@@@The Data Protection dashboard provides information about the current state of the Rubrik clusters connected to RSC...","saas/data_protection_dashboard_details.html@@@Data Protection dashboard details@@@The Data Protection dashboard provides information about events, tasks, and compliance status of the Rubrik clusters connected to RSC...","saas/data_protection_insights_aws.html@@@Data scanning in AWS@@@When you enable data scanning in an AWS account, RSC scans and classifies your AWS data based on their sensitivity and generate intelligent insights. Data scanning helps you manage cloud posture risks...","saas/data_protection_pane_features.html@@@Data Protection pane@@@The Data Protection pane of the Global dashboard provides several interactive elements...","saas/data_security_posture_aws.html@@@Data Security Posture for AWS@@@Using Data Security Posture, you can scan your AWS environment to classify sensitive data, monitor for threats, and manage your data security risks...","saas/data_security_posture_for_azure.html@@@Data Security Posture for Azure@@@Using Data Security Posture, you can scan your Azure environment to classify sensitive data, monitor for threats, and manage your data risks...","saas/data_sources.html@@@Data Sources@@@You can add hosts, instances, and servers for various data-center workloads in the Data Sources menu. Additionally, you can configure access credentials by setting up Guest OS settings and SMB security...","saas/date_and_time_customization.html@@@Date and time customization@@@Date and time is a setting under User Preferences that allows you to customize the date and time settings based on your preferences...","saas/date_and_time_settings.html@@@Date and time settings@@@You can use the date, time, and time zone settings to select options for time zone, date format, and time format...","saas/deactivating_personal_access_token.html@@@Deactivating personal access tokens@@@Deactivate the personal access tokens of one or more users to prevent further API access with those credentials...","saas/dedicated_tenants.html@@@Licenses and usage for Dedicated Tenants@@@RSC tracks and reports license usage for MSP customers using the PayGo license and the Dedicated Tenants feature to manage tenant accounts from a primary account...","saas/default_sla_domains.html@@@Default SLA Domains@@@RSC provides preconfigured SLA Domains...","saas/deleting_a_sdd_report.html@@@Deleting a Data Security Posture report@@@Delete a Data Security Posturereport using RSC...","saas/deleting_a_service_account.html@@@Deleting a service account@@@Delete a service account if it is not required to represent any client application that needs to access the RSC APIs...","saas/deleting_a_tls_certificate.html@@@Deleting a TLS certificate@@@Delete a certificate that has expired or does not match requirements...","saas/deleting_advanced_tags.html@@@Deleting advanced tags@@@Delete an advanced tag from the Rubrik cluster when it is no longer required...","saas/deleting_an_sla_domain.html@@@Deleting an SLA Domain@@@Delete an SLA Domain to remove it from RSC...","saas/deleting_aws_cloud_account.html@@@Deleting an AWS cloud account@@@Delete a cloud account if it is no longer protecting any EC2 instances, EBS volumes, Amazon S3 buckets, or Amazon DynamoDB tables...","saas/deleting_aws_exocompute.html@@@Deleting AWS Exocompute from regions@@@You can remove the AWS Exocompute configuration from selected regions after you have launched the AWS Exocompute configuration in multiple regions...","saas/deleting_guest_os_credentials.html@@@Deleting guest OS credentials@@@Delete guest OS credentials from the list of credentials that RSC uses to access virtual machines...","saas/deleting_kms.html@@@Deleting KMS@@@Delete an AWS KMS key manager, Azure Key Vault, Google Cloud KMS key manager, or KMIP server when it is no longer needed and no particular KMS is currently encrypting any data locations...","saas/deleting_object_level_snapshot_window.html@@@Deleting an object-level snapshot window@@@Delete the object-level snapshot window from one or more CDM objects to restore the snapshot window of the SLA Domain for those objects...","saas/deleting_personal_access_token.html@@@Deleting a personal access token@@@Delete your personal access token to permanently revoke API access using those credentials...","saas/deleting_rp.html@@@Deleting a Recovery Plan@@@You can delete a Recovery Plan of any workload type from the Recovery Plan details page...","saas/deleting_smb_domain.html@@@Deleting an SMB domain@@@If the authentication status of an SMB domain is in a failed state for some reason, such as someone deleting the computer account associated with the SMB domain, first delete the SMB domain before creating another one...","saas/deleting_snapshot.html@@@Deleting a snapshot@@@Delete a specific snapshot or multiple snapshots of a workload object or multiple objects when you want to identify unmanaged snapshots and perform cleanup activity to reduce cloud costs, respectively...","saas/deleting_sso_user_account_rsc.html@@@Deleting an SSO user account from RSC@@@Delete SSO user accounts from RSC to remove them from the Users tab...","saas/deleting_zscaler_integration.html@@@Deleting a Zscaler integration@@@Delete the Zscaler integration from RSC if it is no longer required...","saas/determining_rubrik_cluster_uuid.html@@@Determining the UUID of a Rubrik cluster@@@From RSC, determine the UUID of a Rubrik cluster to use as input for GraphQL API queries and mutations...","saas/disabling_domain_email_allowlist.html@@@Disabling domain and email allowlist@@@Disable Domain and Email Allowlisting to stop restricting local user creation to permitted email domains and addresses...","saas/disabling_force_reauth_sso.html@@@Disabling force re-authentication for SAML SSO@@@Disable force re-authentication for an identity provider to let users reuse an active identity provider session without re-entering credentials at each RSC login...","saas/disconnecting_okta_tenant.html@@@Disconnecting a Okta tenant@@@After configuring Okta integration with RSC, you can disconnect a Okta tenant if it is no longer required...","saas/displaying_sso_users.html@@@Displaying a hidden SSO user@@@As an RSC user with the required permission, display an SSO user who is hidden but has access to RSC...","saas/domain_email_allowlisting.html@@@Domain and email allowlisting@@@You can restrict local user creation in RSC to pre-approved email domains or addresses using Domain and Email Allowlisting. It reduces the risk of unauthorized access from mistyped email addresses...","saas/download_rbk_cdm_soft_upgrade_package.html@@@Rubrik CDM software upgrade package download@@@With RSC, you can download the Rubrik CDM software upgrade package to the Rubrik cluster before starting the upgrade...","saas/downloading_a_sdd_report.html@@@Downloading a Data Security Posture report@@@Download a Data Security Posture report in one of the available formats...","saas/downloading_adfs_metadata_file.html@@@Downloading the ADFS metadata file@@@Download the ADFS federation metadata file associated with the ADFS server...","saas/downloading_backup_report_host_fileset.html@@@Downloading backup report for host fileset@@@Download the backup report from RSC to assess the success or failure of the files in a fileset backup operation. RSC supports downloading backup report from Rubrik CDM version 9.2.3 or later...","saas/downloading_quarantined_files_analysis.html@@@Downloading quarantined files for forensic analysis@@@Download quarantined files to examine and analyze them for malicious content...","saas/downloading_rsc_metadata_file.html@@@Downloading the RSC metadata file@@@Download the RSC metadata to configure single sign-on (SSO) with Active Directory Federation Services (ADFS)...","saas/downloading_rubrik_mib_file.html@@@Downloading the Rubrik MIB file@@@To work with the SNMP feature, download the Rubrik MIB file...","saas/downloading_snapshot_and_assigning_sla.html@@@Downloading a snapshot and assigning an SLA Domain@@@Download a snapshot from an archival or replication location and assign an SLA Domain to manage the retention of the snapshot after download on the Rubrik cluster...","saas/downloading_task_monitoring_data.html@@@Downloading task monitoring data@@@Download a CSV file that contains the data from the task monitoring screen...","saas/downloading_the_rubrik_cluster_upgrade_report.html@@@Downloading the Rubrik cluster upgrade report@@@Download and view the Rubrik cluster upgrade report for monitoring or auditing...","saas/downloading_upgrade_package.html@@@Downloading an upgrade package@@@Download a Rubrik CDM software upgrade package to a Rubrik cluster using RSC before upgrading the Rubrik CDM software...","saas/dsp_conf_workloads.html@@@Data Security Posture configuration for workloads@@@Enabling Data Security Posture has specific requirements according to the workload...","saas/dsp_identity_inventory.html@@@Identity Inventory information@@@The Identity Inventory provides the ability to review user access, track user activity on sensitive data, and evaluate user risk. This comprehensive visibility helps security teams in detecting excessive privileges and unauthorized access, while also accelerating incident response through detailed user and access context...","saas/dsp_windows_audit_log_configuration.html@@@Windows audit log configuration for AD identities@@@Enabling the Identity Inventory successfully requires specific audit log configuration in the Windows security auditing feature to monitor relevant events...","saas/dta_dashboard.html@@@Data Threat Analytics dashboard@@@The Data Threat Analytics dashboard provides a comprehensive analysis of data threats including a summary of anomalies, threat monitoring matches, matched threat hunts for protected objects, and object timeline analysis...","saas/ec2_changing_retention_policy_for_on_demand_snapshot.html@@@Changing the retention policy for an EC2 or EBS on-demand snapshot@@@Change the retention policy of on-demand snapshots of the chosen AWS object...","saas/ec2_changing_retention_policy_for_policy_based_snapshot.html@@@Changing the retention policy for an EC2 or EBS snapshot@@@Change the retention policy of existing policy-based snapshots of the AWS object with no SLA Domain...","saas/ec2_changing_retention_policy_relic_snapshots.html@@@Changing the retention policy for relic snapshots of an Amazon EC2 instance@@@Change the retention policy of the snapshots of AWS relic objects...","saas/ec2_deleting_relic_snapshot.html@@@Deleting snapshots of relic Amazon EC2 instances or EBS volumes@@@Delete a snapshot of AWS relic objects...","saas/ec2_deleting_snapshots_ec2instance_ebsvolume.html@@@Deleting snapshots of an EC2 instance or EBS volume@@@Delete snapshots that have a Forever retention policy...","saas/ec2_ebs_file_search_and_recovery.html@@@File indexing for Amazon EC2 instances@@@RSC uses Exocompute on AWS to extract file system index metadata from the EBS volume snapshots created when protecting Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes...","saas/ec2_instance_details.html@@@EC2 instance details@@@The EC2 instance details page displays protection status, calendar view of the snapshots, object details, and events...","saas/ec2_snapshot_information_list.html@@@EC2 snapshots information list@@@The Snapshots tab displays information about the snapshots for a selected EC2 instance or EBS volume...","saas/ec2_taking_on_demand_snapshot.html@@@Taking on-demand EC2 instances or EBS volumes snapshots@@@Manually initiate an on-demand snapshot of the EC2 instances and EBS volumes with or without assigning an SLA Domain...","saas/edit_aws_account.html@@@Edit an AWS account@@@You can edit an existing AWS account in RSC to change the data protection preferences for your AWS account...","saas/edit_sla_domain.html@@@Edit an SLA Domain@@@Make changes to an existing custom SLA Domain...","saas/editing_a_sdd_report.html@@@Editing a Data Security Posture report@@@Use the available options to edit or customize a Data Security Posture report...","saas/editing_a_sdd_report_schedule.html@@@Editing a Data Security Posture report schedule@@@Edit the Data Security Posture report schedule to change the name, time, or emails it is sent to...","saas/editing_a_tls_certificate.html@@@Editing a TLS certificate@@@Edit a TLS certificate based on your requirements...","saas/editing_advanced_tags.html@@@Editing advanced tags@@@Edit the advanced tag to modify the backup setup assigned to the appropriate SLA Domain...","saas/editing_allowlisted_domain_email.html@@@Editing an allowlisted domain or email address@@@Update a domain or email address in the RSC Domain and Email Allowlist page...","saas/editing_aws_exo_host_acct_rmc.html@@@Editing an AWS Exocompute host account for a Rubrik-managed cluster@@@For the AWS Exocompute host account created for a Rubrik-managed cluster where the Exocompute instance is already configured, edit the existing configuration to specify regions different from those specified previously...","saas/editing_custom_intel_feed.html@@@Editing a custom intel feed@@@To change the source name or description of the custom intel field, edit the intel feed source details...","saas/editing_cyber_rp.html@@@Editing a cyber Recovery Plan@@@Edit a cyber recovery Recovery Plan when deployment requirements change...","saas/editing_disaster_rp.html@@@Editing a disaster Recovery Plan@@@Edit a disaster Recovery Plan when deployment requirements change...","saas/editing_downloaded_snapshot_retention.html@@@Editing the retention of a downloaded snapshot@@@Change the retention of a downloaded snapshot by editing or reassigning the SLA Domain associated with the object...","saas/editing_email_notification_setting.html@@@Editing an email notification setting@@@Edit an email notification setting in RSC to change the notification preferences, such as recipients, event types, and event severity...","saas/editing_guest_os_credentials.html@@@Editing a guest OS credential@@@Edit a guest OS credential to update the Rubrik cluster with changes to the authentication server, username, or password...","saas/editing_in_place_rp.html@@@Editing an in-place Recovery Plan@@@Edit an in-place Recovery Plan when deployment requirements change...","saas/editing_kms.html@@@Editing KMS@@@Edit the KMS credentials to update configuration details for an existing KMS instance as per the KMS type...","saas/editing_okta_tenant.html@@@Editing Okta tenants@@@After configuring Okta integration with RSC, edit the settings of an Okta tenant and validate using the Integrations page...","saas/editing_pam_configuration.html@@@Editing the PAM configuration@@@Edit the Privileged Access Management configuration to update its display name and allowed IP addresses...","saas/editing_passkey_names.html@@@Editing passkey names@@@Edit a passkey name to match your requirements and make it easily identifiable...","saas/editing_role_authorized_sso_user.html@@@Editing the directly assigned roles for an authorized SSO user@@@Edit the role assignment for an authorized SSO user in RSC to directly assign additional roles...","saas/editing_rsc_sso_configuration.html@@@Editing an existing RSC SSO configuration@@@Edit the SSO configuration in RSC when any updates are required...","saas/editing_rsc_sso_configuration_2.html@@@Editing an existing RSC SSO configuration@@@Edit the SSO configuration in RSC when any updates are required...","saas/editing_rubrik_cluster_direct_access.html@@@Editing a Rubrik cluster for direct access@@@Edit a Rubrik cluster to specify an IP address or a fully qualified domain name to be used for direct cluster access...","saas/editing_sla_domains_without_snapshot_schedules.html@@@Editing SLA Domains without snapshot schedules@@@Edit an existing SLA Domain without snapshot schedules for Continuous Data Protection-only SLA Domains...","saas/editing_taxii_threat_intel.html@@@Editing a TAXII threat intel source@@@Change the name or description of a TAXII threat intel source in RSC...","saas/editing_zscaler_integration.html@@@Editing a Zscaler integration@@@To update the service account, drop target, drop target path, and assigned policies as required, edit an existing Zscaler integration...","saas/emails.html@@@Emails@@@Email notifications in RSC notify users about events, such as backup, recovery, anomaly detection, and so on...","saas/enable_data_scanning_aws_acc.html@@@Enabling data scanning for an AWS account@@@Enable the data scanning feature for an AWS account you have already added to RSC. Data scanning helps you manage cloud posture risks...","saas/enable_dsp_sharepoint_and_onedrive.html@@@Enable Data Security Posture for Microsoft SharePoint and OneDrive@@@To find data matching a specified data policy within snapshots, enable Data Security Posture for Microsoft SharePoint and OneDrive...","saas/enabling_anomaly_det_sharepoint_onedrive.html@@@Enabling Anomaly Detection for SharePoint and OneDrive@@@Enable Anomaly Detection for Microsoft SharePoint and OneDrive objects. Anomaly Detection performs behavioral and content analysis on the file system and provides details about potentially anomalous incidents...","saas/enabling_anomaly_detection.html@@@Enabling Anomaly Detection@@@Enable Anomaly Detection to perform behavioral and content analysis on the file system and show details about potentially anomalous incidents...","saas/enabling_anomaly_detection_amzn_ec2_instnc_ebs_vol.html@@@Enabling Anomaly Detection for Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes@@@Enable Anomaly Detection to your AWS account to perform behavioral and content analysis on your Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes. Enabling Anomaly Detection for your AWS account helps safeguard the data in your Amazon EC2 instances and EBS volumes from ransomware attacks...","saas/enabling_app_consistency_azure.html@@@Enabling application-consistent backups in Azure@@@To preserve the working state of applications running on a protected Azure virtual machine, enable the app-consistent backups in RSC...","saas/enabling_app_consistent_snapshots_ec2_instances.html@@@Enabling application-consistent snapshots for an AWS EC2 instance@@@After you have installed the Rubrik Backup Service on an AWS EC2 instance, registered that AWS EC2 instance with RSC, and configured the pre-snapshot and post-snapshot scripts, to take application-consistent snapshots, enable the application consistency feature for the corresponding AWS EC2 instance...","saas/enabling_auto_quarantine.html@@@Enabling automatic quarantine for a threat intelligence feed@@@Enable automatic quarantine for a threat intelligence feed to isolate matching files when Threat Monitoring detects them...","saas/enabling_cyber_event_lockdown_rsc.html@@@Enabling Cyber Event Lockdown@@@Enable Cyber Event Lockdown to protect all data stored on a Rubrik cluster from an event that could affect data integrity, such as a security breach or accidental deletion...","saas/enabling_data_discovery_Azure_vms.html@@@Enable Data Security Posture for Azure virtual machines and managed disks@@@To find data matching a specified data policy within snapshots, enable Data Security Posture for Azure virtual machines and managed disks that have a Rubrik Cloud Vault archival location configured...","saas/enabling_domain_email_allowlist.html@@@Enabling domain and email allowlist@@@Enable Domain and Email Allowlist to restrict local user creation in RSC to permitted email domains and addresses...","saas/enabling_dsp_azure_cloud_account.html@@@Enabling Data Security Posture for Azure cloud accounts@@@Enable Data Security Posture for an existing Azure cloud account in RSC...","saas/enabling_dsp_existing_aws_account.html@@@Enabling Data Security Posture for existing AWS accounts@@@Enable Data Security Posture for an existing AWS cloud account in RSC...","saas/enabling_federated_access.html@@@Enabling federated access@@@Enable federated access to enable user accounts to access connected Rubrik clusters without entering login credentials, access cluster interfaces and NAS CD interfaces, and download cluster snapshots directly from RSC...","saas/enabling_force_reauth_sso.html@@@Enabling force re-authentication for SAML SSO@@@Enable force re-authentication for an identity provider to ensure that users to authenticate with the identity provider on every RSC login...","saas/enabling_stringent_policies_organizations.html@@@Enabling stringent policies for organizations@@@An user with administrator privileges for a global organization can enable global enforcement settings to enforce stricter policies for tenant organizations...","saas/encryp_mgmt_archives_tab.html@@@Archives tab@@@Information about data locations of encrypted archives for data center and cloud-native archiving, including encryption details, and options for managing and monitoring the encryption process...","saas/encryp_mgmt_cloud_locations_tab.html@@@Cloud archival location encryption details@@@Reference information for the Cloud locations view in Encryption Management, including column definitions for encryption type, rekey status, and per-region encryption detail...","saas/encryp_mgmt_clusters_tab.html@@@Clusters tab@@@Information about the encryption status of data stored on connected clusters, including filtering options by encryption type, key type, and status, and options for rotating encryption keys...","saas/encryp_mgmt_kms_settings_tab.html@@@Key Managers tab@@@Information about configuring and managing key managers includes adding new key manager instances, viewing key vault identifiers, and tracking associated storage locations with filtering options for KMS type and provisioning method...","saas/encryp_mgmt_m365_tab.html@@@Microsoft 365 tab@@@Information about Microsoft 365 organizations...","saas/encryption_mgmt_details.html@@@Encryption management details@@@The Encryption Management page provides centralized access to encryption settings, Key Management Systems, and encryption status, enabling effective management and monitoring of encryption...","saas/enforcing_r2sv_for_specific_users.html@@@Enforcing Rubrik Two-step verification for specific users@@@A user with the required privileges can enforce multifactor authentication for selected local user accounts...","saas/enforcing_smb_security.html@@@Enforcing SMB security@@@For additional security, enforce the SMB client to use the SMB security from the Rubrik cluster side, regardless of the SMB client configuration...","saas/event_details.html@@@Event details@@@Select an event on the Events page to see detailed information for the event...","saas/event_logs_details.html@@@Event Logs details@@@The Events page displays the events occurring in all connected Rubrik clusters, shown in the local time zone...","saas/event_logs_details_2.html@@@Event Logs details@@@The Events page displays the events occurring in all connected Rubrik clusters, shown in the local time zone...","saas/event_logs_details_3.html@@@Event Logs details@@@The Events page displays the events occurring in all connected Rubrik clusters, shown in the local time zone...","saas/events_information.html@@@Events information@@@RSC displays the Events page from the Dashboard page, the Events tab, and the Clusters page...","saas/everpure_adding_flasharray.html@@@Adding an Everpure FlashArray@@@Add an Everpure FlashArray to RSC to discover its Protection Groups and volumes for protection...","saas/everpure_assigning_sla_domains.html@@@Assigning SLA Domains to Everpure FlashArray Protection Groups and volumes@@@Assign an SLA Domain to an Everpure FlashArray Protection Group or standalone volume. You can also exclude individual volumes from a Protection Group&apos;s snapshots...","saas/everpure_configuring_app_consistent_backups.html@@@Configuring Everpure FlashArray application-consistent backups@@@Configure pre-backup, post-snapshot, and post-backup scripts on a script host to produce application-consistent FlashArray snapshots for an Everpure FlashArray Protection Group...","saas/everpure_excluding_volumes.html@@@Excluding volumes from an Everpure FlashArray Protection Group@@@Exclude specific volumes from snapshots of a Protection Group. Excluded volumes remain members of the Protection Group but are not included in backups or recovery operations...","saas/everpure_flasharray.html@@@Everpure FlashArray@@@You can protect Everpure FlashArray Protection Groups and volumes through RSC using FlashArray-native snapshots and changed-block tracking...","saas/everpure_flasharray_connection_management.html@@@Everpure FlashArray connection management@@@After you add an Everpure FlashArray to RSC, three operations are available for managing the FlashArray connection over its lifecycle: refresh, edit, and delete...","saas/everpure_flasharray_management.html@@@Manage Everpure FlashArray@@@Configure application-consistent backups and monitor protection activity for Everpure FlashArray Protection Groups...","saas/everpure_flasharray_requirements.html@@@Everpure FlashArray requirements@@@Everpure FlashArray volume protection has specific requirements for Purity//FA version, authentication, and network connectivity...","saas/everpure_flasharray_setup.html@@@Set up Everpure FlashArray@@@Add an Everpure FlashArray to RSC, configure the connection, and assign protection policies to its Protection Groups and volumes...","saas/everpure_protection_group_monitoring.html@@@Everpure FlashArray Protection Group monitoring@@@View the protection status, snapshot history, and events for an Everpure FlashArray Protection Group...","saas/everpure_volume_protection_arch_data_flow.html@@@Everpure FlashArray volume protection architecture and data flow@@@Everpure FlashArray volume protection in RSC uses a two-tier architecture with FlashArray-native snapshots and incremental changed-block tracking...","saas/everpure_volume_recovery.html@@@Recover Everpure FlashArray volumes@@@You can recover an Everpure FlashArray volume by exporting a snapshot to a target FlashArray. Every recovery creates a new volume on the target FlashArray...","saas/excluding_ebs_volumes_from_an_ec2_instance.html@@@Excluding EBS volumes from an EC2 instance@@@RSC can exclude specific EBS volumes in an EC2 instance while protecting the other EBS volumes in that EC2 instance...","saas/exocompute_for_aws.html@@@Set up Exocompute on AWS@@@With the Exocompute on AWS feature, RSC launches an Elastic Kubernetes Service cluster to perform various operations to protect AWS workloads. RSC uses the Elastic Kubernetes Service cluster as a compute resource in your AWS account...","saas/export_azure_md_snapshot.html@@@Exporting an Azure managed disk snapshot@@@Export a snapshot of an Azure managed disk to create a new disk from a point-in-time copy of the source managed disk...","saas/export_of_ec2_instance_and_ebs_volume_snapshot.html@@@Export of EC2 Instance and EBS volume snapshots@@@When a snapshot of an EC2 instance or an EBS volume is exported, RSC manages encryption, key sharing, and tags for the new instance or volume...","saas/exporting_an_ebs_volume.html@@@Exporting an EBS volume snapshot@@@Export an EBS volume snapshot to create a volume. The new volume can be exported to the original region or to a new region...","saas/exporting_an_ec2_instance_snapshot.html@@@Exporting an EC2 instance snapshot@@@Export an EC2 instance snapshot to create an instance. You can export the new instance to the original region or to a new region...","saas/exporting_impacted_snapshots.html@@@Exporting objects from impacted snapshots@@@Recover a virtual machine affected by a deletion or encryption event by exporting it from a clean snapshot to another virtual machine on a target cluster...","saas/extending_sla_domain_switching_period.html@@@Extending the SLA Domain switching period@@@To have more time to plan switching your SLA Domain management from a Rubrik cluster to RSC, you can request a one-time extension of the switching period...","saas/extra_dense_migration_cces_clusters.html@@@Extra-dense node migration for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage@@@Extra-dense nodes offer greater storage and performance, without a loss of storage capacity. Using extra-dense nodes, organizations can reduce node counts by half during migration. Customization options are available through the GraphQL API...","saas/failback_operations.html@@@Failback operations@@@A failback operation restores production data back to the original site after initial failover to a secondary location...","saas/failback_rcv.html@@@Failback for Rubrik Cloud Vault@@@The failback process for Rubrik Cloud Vault involves switching to the new secondary region after geo-redundant storage has been re-established. This resumes the backup operations in the designated region...","saas/failed_or_canceled_backups.html@@@Failed or canceled backups@@@RSC provides the ability to retry the most recent failed or canceled backups. Backups can be retried up to seven days after the failed or canceled backup...","saas/failover_operations.html@@@Failover operations@@@A failover operation recovers a workload to a secondary recovery site...","saas/false_positive_mgmt_dta.html@@@False positives management in Threat Monitoring@@@You can often resolve false positives that occur in Threat Monitoring...","saas/fast_upgrade_rbk_cdm_software.html@@@Fast upgrade of Rubrik CDM software@@@With the fast upgrade of Rubrik CDM software running on your Rubrik cluster, you can simultaneously upgrade all Rubrik cluster nodes. This option saves time but requires some system downtime...","saas/federated_access.html@@@Federated access@@@Federated access enables RSC user and service accounts to access connected Rubrik clusters, including Rubrik NAS Cloud Direct clusters. This access is provided through the RSC user interface using Single Sign-On, eliminating the need for separate login credentials...","saas/fetb_license_usage_calculation.html@@@FETB usage calculation for PayGo licenses@@@RSC calculates PayGo usage for license products measured in Front-End Terabytes, split across Foundation Edition, Business Edition, and Enterprise Edition...","saas/file_preparation_center.html@@@File preparation center@@@The File Preparation Center tab on the Events page provides information about reports downloaded or sent to email recipients...","saas/file_preparation_center_2.html@@@File preparation center@@@The File Preparation Center tab on the Events page provides information about reports downloaded or sent to email recipients...","saas/file_preparation_center_details.html@@@File preparation center details@@@The File Preparation Center tab contains details about the reports downloaded or sent to email recipients...","saas/file_preparation_center_details_2.html@@@File preparation center details@@@The File Preparation Center tab contains details about the reports downloaded or sent to email recipients...","saas/filesystems_indexing_limitations.html@@@Indexing limitations@@@Information about the file systems supported for indexing in RSC...","saas/filesystems_indexing_limitations_2.html@@@Indexing limitations@@@Information about the file systems supported for indexing in RSC...","saas/filesystems_indexing_limitations_3.html@@@Indexing limitations@@@Information about the file systems supported for indexing in RSC...","saas/finding_ip_address.html@@@Finding the RSC outbound IP addresses@@@Locate the complete list of outbound IP addresses that RSC uses to connect to your SaaS application, and add them to your network allowlist...","saas/finding_legal_hold_cloud_snapshots.html@@@Finding cloud-native snapshots on legal hold@@@Use the Legal Hold page in RSC to find cloud-native snapshots that are currently on legal hold across your environment...","saas/finding_rsc_region.html@@@Finding the RSC domain region@@@Find the region in which your RSC domain is running...","saas/force_reauth_saml_sso.html@@@Force re-authentication for SAML single sign-on@@@The force re-authentication setting requires users to authenticate with the identity provider every time they access RSC, even when they have an active identity provider session...","saas/fs_adding_fileset_host.html@@@Adding a fileset host@@@To begin managing and protecting filesets on a host, add the host to a Rubrik cluster...","saas/fs_changing_the_retention_policy_for_fileset_snapshot.html@@@Changing the retention policy for a fileset snapshot@@@Change the retention policy for existing snapshots of a host or service fileset...","saas/fs_creating_a_failover_cluster.html@@@Creating a failover cluster@@@Create a failover cluster by grouping Windows hosts or Linux and Unix hosts...","saas/fs_creating_failover_cluster_service.html@@@Creating a failover cluster service@@@Create a failover cluster service to assign filesets and SLA Domains required to automate data protection across the failover cluster...","saas/fs_creating_fileset.html@@@Creating a fileset@@@Create a fileset to define a set of data in a file system. You can assign a fileset to a host to protect the data set specified by the fileset on that host...","saas/fs_data_recovery_from_a_host_fileset.html@@@Data recovery from a host fileset@@@RSC allows recovering data from a host fileset...","saas/fs_deleting_a_fileset_from_a_host.html@@@Deleting a fileset from a host@@@Delete the association between a fileset and a host to stop SLA Domain protection of the selected host fileset...","saas/fs_deleting_a_fileset_from_the_cluster.html@@@Deleting a fileset from the Rubrik cluster@@@Delete a fileset from the Rubrik cluster to remove all existing associations of that fileset with the hosts that use the fileset to protect files and folders on the hosts...","saas/fs_deleting_fileset_snapshots.html@@@Deleting host fileset snapshots@@@Delete snapshots that have the Forever retention policy...","saas/fs_downloading_data_fileset_snapshot.html@@@Downloading data from fileset snapshots@@@You can use RSC to recover files or folders by downloading the backed-up data...","saas/fs_export_path.html@@@Export path for fileset snapshot data@@@The path to export the fileset snapshot data must comply with the rules that RSC enforces...","saas/fs_exporting_fileset_snapshot_data.html@@@Exporting fileset snapshot data@@@Export files or folders from the fileset snapshot to a host that is different from the source host...","saas/fs_failover_cluster_management_actions.html@@@Failover cluster management actions@@@RSC provides the ability to edit and delete failover clusters...","saas/fs_failover_cluster_service_management_actions.html@@@Failover cluster service management actions@@@RSC provides the ability to edit and delete all failover cluster services...","saas/fs_fileset_details.html@@@Fileset details@@@For every fileset, RSC displays details including the fileset rules and the number of hosts being protected through the fileset...","saas/fs_fileset_host_details.html@@@Fileset host details@@@For every fileset host, RSC displays important details including the list of filesets on the host and the SLA Domains protecting the filesets...","saas/fs_fileset_host_management_actions.html@@@Fileset host management actions@@@For every fileset host, RSC provides the ability to check the connection status, update the certificate, and edit the identity of the host...","saas/fs_fileset_management_actions.html@@@Fileset management actions@@@For every fileset, RSC provides the ability to edit, clone, and delete the fileset...","saas/fs_fileset_protection_failover_clusters.html@@@Fileset protection for failover clusters@@@RSC supports backup of hosts grouped into failover clusters through filesets...","saas/fs_fileset_protection_hosts.html@@@Fileset protection for hosts@@@The combination of a fileset with a host creates a protectable object referred to as a host fileset...","saas/fs_filesets.html@@@Filesets@@@RSC manages the protection of folders and files on host computers through filesets...","saas/fs_filesystems.html@@@File systems@@@RSC provides management and protection of file system data on supported Linux, Unix, and Windows hosts through filesets...","saas/fs_host_management_for_filesets.html@@@Host management for filesets@@@RSC supports protection of file system data on Windows, Linux, and Unix hosts...","saas/fs_local_pages_for_fileset_objects.html@@@Local pages for fileset objects@@@The local pages of a fileset host and a failover cluster service provide detailed information about tasks related to protecting filesets and managing available snapshots...","saas/fs_locating_a_fileset_snapshot_for_recovery.html@@@Locating a fileset snapshot for recovery@@@Locate a fileset snapshot to recover data from the entire snapshot or from a selection of files and folders within the snapshot...","saas/fs_managing_protection_for_failover_cluster_services.html@@@Managing protection for failover cluster services@@@Manage protection for failover cluster services by assigning or removing an SLA Domain...","saas/fs_managing_protection_for_failover_clusters.html@@@Managing protection for failover clusters@@@Manage protection for the nodes of a failover cluster by assigning or removing an SLA Domain...","saas/fs_managing_protection_for_filesets.html@@@Managing protection for filesets@@@Manage protection for filesets on the failover cluster services by assigning or removing an SLA Domain...","saas/fs_overview_tab_actions_list.html@@@Overview tab actions list@@@The Overview tab on the local page of a fileset host and failover cluster service provides access to actions related to fileset management and protection...","saas/fs_overview_tab_details.html@@@Overview tab details@@@The Overview tab on the local page of a fileset host and a failover cluster service provides information about the filesets associated with the host or the service, the Rubrik cluster to which the host or service is connected, and the snapshots of the associated filesets in a calendar view...","saas/fs_protecting_a_host_fileset.html@@@Protecting a host fileset@@@Create a host fileset by pairing a fileset with a host. Assign an SLA Domain to the host fileset to protect the data in the host fileset...","saas/fs_protection_hierarchy_for_failover_clusters.html@@@Protection hierarchy for failover clusters@@@RSC enables hierarchy-based, automatic protection of failover clusters...","saas/fs_removing_a_fileset_host.html@@@Removing a fileset host@@@You can delete the host from the Rubrik cluster to stop protecting the fileset data on a host...","saas/fs_removing_protection_for_host_fileset.html@@@Removing protection for a host fileset@@@Remove SLA Domain protection from a host fileset...","saas/fs_restoring_fileset_snaps_data_new_loc.html@@@Restoring fileset snapshot data to a new location@@@Restore files or folders from the fileset snapshot to a location that is different from the original location of the data on the source host...","saas/fs_restoring_fileset_snapshot_data_src.html@@@Restoring fileset snapshot data to the source location@@@Restoring files or folders from the fileset snapshot to the original location of the source data overwrites the original data...","saas/fs_searching_for_a_file_or_folder_for_recovery.html@@@Searching for a file or folder for recovery@@@Use the search capability to find a specific file or folder from a fileset snapshot for recovery...","saas/fs_snapshots_card_calendar_view.html@@@The Snapshots card calendar view for filesets@@@The calendar view of the Snapshots card displays information at different levels of granularity...","saas/fs_snapshots_card_for_filesets.html@@@Snapshots card for filesets@@@The Snapshots card in the Overview tab provides a list of snapshots stored on the local Rubrik cluster and on the replication location for a selected date...","saas/fs_snapshots_tab_for_filesets.html@@@Snapshots tab for filesets@@@The Snapshots tab on the local page of a fileset host or service displays information about all the associated snapshots...","saas/fs_taking_on_demand_snapshot_of_a_host_fileset.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshot of a host fileset@@@Create a backup by taking an on-demand snapshot of a host fileset...","saas/fs_viewing_the_failover_cluster_service_local_page.html@@@Viewing the failover cluster service local page@@@Access the local page of a failover cluster service to view details and perform tasks related to fileset protection...","saas/fs_viewing_the_fileset_host_local_page.html@@@Viewing the fileset host local page@@@Access the local page of a fileset host to view details and perform tasks related to fileset protection...","saas/full_snapshot_recovery_of_a_virtual_machine.html@@@Full snapshot recovery of a virtual machine@@@A full snapshot of a virtual machine can be recovered from the Anomaly Detection page...","saas/gcp_cloud_cluster_es_rsc.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on GCP@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Google Cloud Platform protects applications and data by running Rubrik CDM software on Google Cloud Platform instances within a virtual private cloud...","saas/gcp_creating_role_service_acct.html@@@Creating roles and service accounts@@@Create a custom role with specific permissions required for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Google Cloud Platform, then assign it to a service account...","saas/gcp_kms_supported_keys_permissions.html@@@Supported keys and permissions in Google Cloud KMS@@@Requirements for supported key types in Google Cloud KMS include enabled symmetric encryption keys and a service account with the required permissions...","saas/generating_a_csr.html@@@Generating a CSR@@@Generate a CSR to authenticate and import a TLS certificate...","saas/generating_certificate.html@@@Generating certificates@@@Generate a certificate using the RSA private key to establish secure communication between RSC and Microsoft...","saas/generating_rsa_private_keys.html@@@Generating RSA private keys@@@Generate an RSA private key using OpenSSL and use the key to generate a certificate...","saas/global_dashboard_required_permissions.html@@@Global Dashboard required permissions@@@User accounts must have specific permissions to view the RSC dashboard...","saas/granular_snapshot_deletion.html@@@Granular snapshot deletion@@@You can delete snapshot copies from individual locations without changing the SLA Domain or retention of the snapshot...","saas/group_claim_rules.html@@@Group claim rules@@@Before writing custom group claim rules, review the example group claim rules in this topic. The example group claim rules in this topic can be adapted to work with various group naming conventions...","saas/guidelines_for_adding_service_accounts.html@@@Guidelines for adding service accounts@@@Guidelines to optimize the security of the client application represented by a service account...","saas/healthcare_dashboard.html@@@Healthcare dashboard@@@The Healthcare dashboard provides a unified view of data protection, compliance, and recoverability for the entire Epic ecosystem...","saas/healthcare_dashboard_widgets.html@@@Healthcare dashboard widgets@@@The Healthcare dashboard provides information about data backup duration, capacity trends over time, daily compliance patterns, and the recent data recoveries for the selected objects...","saas/hiding_sso_users.html@@@Hiding an SSO user@@@As an RSC user with the required permission, hide an SSO user so the account no longer appears on the Users tab...","saas/hsr_config_scenarios.html@@@HSR configuration scenarios@@@Information about the various scenarios related to SAP HANA system replication configuration for high availability and disaster recovery and the corresponding results or operations you can perform...","saas/hyper_v/assigned_sla_domain_changes.html@@@Assigned SLA Domain changes@@@A protected virtual machine may be assigned to another SLA Domain in order to satisfy specific business requirements (for example, data governance policy changes or space management requirements)...","saas/hyper_v/azure_local_cluster_role_warning.html@@@Azure Local cluster role warning@@@When you export or live mount a virtual machine to an Azure Local cluster, the Rubrik Backup Service generates a cluster role warning if you have not configured it to log on as a domain user account with cluster administrative privileges...","saas/hyper_v/azure_stack_hci_limitations.html@@@Azure Local limitations@@@Recovering virtual machines to an Azure Local (Azure Stack HCI) has certain limitations, but these limitations have workarounds...","saas/hyper_v/azure_stack_hci_management.html@@@Azure Local management@@@Azure Local (Azure Stack HCI) is a hyperconverged clustering solution that uses validated hardware to run virtualized workloads on-premises. Adding Azure Local to RSC recognizes it as a Hyper-V cluster and discovers these virtualized workloads as Hyper-V virtual machines. You can utilize Rubrik Hyper-V management capabilities to manage Azure Local workloads...","saas/hyper_v/azure_stack_hci_overview.html@@@Azure Local overview@@@With RSC, you can protect on-premises Microsoft workloads and Azure Local (Azure Stack HCI) resources in a unified control plane and provide insight into critical data...","saas/hyper_v/calendar_view_fields.html@@@Hyper-V Calendar view fields@@@The calendar view of the Snapshot card displays information based on the selected calendar period...","saas/hyper_v/configure_rbs_logon_account_azure_local.html@@@Configuring the RBS logon account on Azure Local@@@Configure the Rubrik Backup Service to log on as a domain user account with cluster administrative privileges to prevent the cluster role warning during virtual machine exports and live mounts...","saas/hyper_v/edit_scvmm_servers.html@@@Edit SCVMM servers@@@You can edit information about SCVMM servers, such as the server IP address or hostname...","saas/hyper_v/excluding_hyperv_vhd_files.html@@@Excluding Hyper-V virtual machine VHD files@@@Among the VHD files on a virtual machine, some VHD files might not require a backup. Exclude these VHD files from the backup, thereby reducing the size of the snapshots...","saas/hyper_v/hyper_v_performance_and_scalability.html@@@Performance and scalability@@@The Rubrik cluster provides a high performance, highly scalable, integration with the Hyper-V Windows Management Instrumentation and Microsoft Volume Shadow Copy Service to back up virtual machines hosted on Hyper-V hypervisors...","saas/hyper_v/hyper_v_searching_snapshots.html@@@Searching for files and folders@@@Use RSC to browse for a file or folder in a snapshot, replica, or archival snapshot...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_accessing_local_vm_page.dita.html@@@Accessing the local page of a Hyper-V virtual machine@@@Access the local page of a Hyper-Vvirtual machine to view information about a virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_adding_hosts.html@@@Adding Hyper-V hosts@@@To begin protecting and managing filesets on a host, add the host to a Rubrik cluster...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_adding_scvmm_servers.html@@@Adding SCVMM Servers@@@Add Microsoft SCVMM servers, which administer virtual machines across multiple hosts. RBS should be installed on all hosts running SCVMM...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_assigning_system_tags_scvmm.html@@@Assigning a System Tag to SCVMM native tags from the Hyper-V inventory@@@Assign an RSC System Tag to System Center Virtual Machine Manager native tags from the Hyper-V inventory to group Hyper-V VMs for automated SLA Domain assignment...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_automatic_protection.html@@@Protection hierarchy for Hyper-V virtual machines@@@A Rubrik cluster provides automatic protection of virtual machines through inheritance of the SLA Domain assigned to a parent object...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_batch_recovery.html@@@Hyper-V batch recovery@@@To recover multiple Hyper-V virtual machines at the same time, you can perform a batch recovery operation...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_creating_live_mount.html@@@Creating Live Mounts for Hyper-V virtual machines@@@Create a Live Mount that creates a new virtual machine from a point-in-time copy of the source virtual machine. The live-mounted virtual machine uses the Rubrik cluster as its datastore...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_deleting_on_demand_snapshot.html@@@Deleting on-demand snapshots for Hyper-V VMs@@@Delete an on-demand snapshot for a Hyper-V virtual machine to remove it from RSC...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_downloading_rbs_scvmm.html@@@Downloading Rubrik Backup Service on an SCVMM host@@@Download Rubrik Backup Service software for System Center Virtual Machine Manager hosts...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_export.html@@@Hyper-V export@@@An export creates a new virtual machine from a point-in-time copy of the source virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_export_batch_recovery.html@@@Recovering a batch of Hyper-V virtual machines using exports in Data Protection@@@When you want to recover multiple Hyper-V virtual machines at one time, you can perform an export of multiple Hyper-V virtual machines to create new Hyper-V virtual machines from a snapshot...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_find_protected_objects.html@@@Find protected objects@@@You can use several methods for finding protected objects...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_host_config.html@@@Hyper-V host configuration@@@To protect Hyper-V with a Rubrik cluster, the Failover Clustering feature must be enabled on the Hyper-V host even if the Hyper-V host is not part of a Failover cluster...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_host_management.html@@@Hyper-V host management@@@After installing the Rubrik Backup Service software on a Hyper-V host, adding a host to the Rubrik cluster establishes a secure connection between the Rubrik cluster and the Rubrik Backup Service that is running on the host...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_inplace_recovery.html@@@Hyper-V in-place recovery@@@Hyper-V in-place recovery offers a faster and more efficient option for virtual machine recovery compared to other Hyper-V recovery methods. In-place recovery transfers only the changed blocks in a Virtual Hard Disk (VHDX) file, significantly reducing the number of blocks transferred and the latency in recovering virtual machines...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_installing_rbs_scvmm.html@@@Installing RBS on an SCVMM host@@@Install RBS on an SCVMM host...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_instant_batch_recovery.html@@@Recovering a batch of Hyper-V virtual machines using instant recovery in Data Protection@@@When you want to restore multiple Hyper-V virtual machines at one time, you can perform an instant recovery to create new Hyper-V virtual machines from a selected snapshot that replace the source virtual machines...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_mount_batch_recovery.html@@@Recovering a batch of Hyper-V virtual machines using live mounts in Data Protection@@@When you want to recover multiple Hyper-V virtual machines, you can create a Live Mount for a batch of Hyper-V virtual machines, to create virtual machines from a point-in-time copy of the source virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_new_vm_protection.html@@@Protection for new Hyper-V virtual machines@@@A new virtual machine is one for which there are no policy-driven snapshots. After a new virtual machine is assigned to an SLA Domain, all of its snapshots, replicas and archival snapshots are created and managed based on the SLA rules of the SLA Domain...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_on_demand_snapshots.html@@@Hyper-V on-demand snapshots@@@In addition to policy based snapshots, you can create virtual machine snapshots by using the on demand snapshot process...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_overview_tab.html@@@Hyper-V Overview tab@@@Description of the fields in the Hyper-V overview tab. In the overview tab, you can view information such as the name of the SLA Domain used for protection. By using the Calendar view, you can access the snapshots, which you can use to restore the virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_performing_export.html@@@Performing a Hyper-V virtual machine snapshot export@@@Perform an export to create a virtual machine from a point-in-time copy of the source virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_protection_consequences.html@@@Protection consequences@@@The SLA rules defined by an SLA Domain impact the protection of virtual machines in several ways. SLA rules specify when snapshots are created, when snapshots expire, and where snapshot data is stored...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_recovering_downloading_vm_files.html@@@Recovering Hyper-V virtual machines by downloading virtual machine files@@@Recover a Hyper-V virtual machine by downloading specific virtual disks and virtual machine files without downloading the entire virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_recovering_files_folders.html@@@Recovering a file or folder@@@The Rubrik cluster provides file-level restore of files and folders from any local snapshot, replica, or archival snapshot that was successfully indexed...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_recovering_mounting_disks.html@@@Recovering Hyper-V virtual machines by mounting virtual disks@@@Recover a Hyper-V virtual machine by mounting virtual disks from a snapshot onto a target virtual machine. The target virtual machine is on the same Rubrik cluster as the source virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_recovery_download_vm_files.html@@@Hyper-V virtual machine recovery by downloading virtual machine files@@@You can recover a Hyper-V virtual machine by downloading virtual disks and virtual machine files without downloading the entire virtual machine. You can fully restore the original virtual machine by downloading all files and disks, or you can download specific disks and configuration files to restore a virtual machine with only the data from the disks...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_recovery_vms_mount_virtual_disk.html@@@Hyper-V virtual machine recovery by mounting virtual disks@@@You can recover a Hyper-V virtual machine by mounting virtual disks from a snapshot on the source Rubrik cluster onto a target virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_removing_hosts.html@@@Removing Hyper-V hosts@@@To stop managing the data on a host, delete the host from the Rubrik cluster...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_retention.html@@@Hyper-V archival snapshot retention@@@The retention period assigned to the archival snapshot by the associated SLA Domain determines the expiration of an archival snapshot...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_ri_creating_live_mounts.html@@@Recovering a batch of Hyper-V virtual machines using Live Mounts in Data Threat Analytics@@@When you want to recover multiple Hyper-V virtual machines, you can create a Live Mount for a batch of Hyper-V virtual machines, to create virtual machines from a point-in-time copy of the source virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_ri_exports_batch_recovery.html@@@Recovering a batch of Hyper-V virtual machines using exports in Data Threat Analytics@@@When you want to recover multiple Hyper-V virtual machines at one time, you can perform an export of multiple Hyper-V to create new Hyper-V virtual machines from a snapshot...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_ri_instant_recovery.html@@@Recovering a batch of Hyper-V virtual machines using instant recovery in Data Threat Analytics@@@When you want to restore multiple Hyper-V virtual machines at one time, you can perform an instant recovery to create new Hyper-V virtual machines from a selected snapshot that replaces the source virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_scvmm_tags_tab.html@@@SCVMM Tags tab on the Hyper-V inventory Page@@@The SCVMM Tags tab on the Hyper-V VMs inventory page lists all System Center Virtual Machine Manager native tags discovered from your System Center Virtual Machine Manager environment and shows the System Tag assigned to each native tag...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_sla_domain_assignment.html@@@Hyper-V SLA Domain assignment@@@Provide protection for a virtual machine through an SLA Domain...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_snapshots_tab.html@@@Hyper-V Snapshots card@@@For the selected local virtual machine, the Snapshots card provides the ability to browse the snapshots that reside on the local Rubrik cluster and on the archival location...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_taking_ods.html@@@Taking on demand snapshots for Hyper-V virtual machines@@@In addition to policy based snapshots, create virtual machine snapshots by using the on demand snapshot process...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_virtual_machines.html@@@Hyper-V virtual machines@@@A Rubrik cluster provides data management and protection for virtual machines that are deployed in a Microsoft Hyper-V environment. The Rubrik cluster can manage and protect virtual machines in an environment with multiple Hyper-V servers and virtual machines...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_vm_live_mount_ops.html@@@Hyper-V virtual machine Live Mount operations@@@The operations available for a Live Mounted Hyper-V virtual machine on the Live Mounts page vary depending on the type of Live Mount...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_vm_protection.html@@@Hyper-V virtual machine protection@@@Rubrik clusters can protect virtual machines based on a direct SLA Domain assignment or based on inheritance of the SLA Domain assigned to the parent object...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_vm_recovery_actions.html@@@Hyper-V virtual machine recovery actions@@@You can recover a source virtual machine for a Rubrik cluster by mounting a point-in-time copy of the source virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_vm_recovery_live_mount.html@@@Hyper-V virtual machine recovery using Live Mount@@@You can recover a Hyper-V virtual machine using the Live Mount recovery option and choose to migrate the data from the Rubrik cluster to a Hyper-V host...","saas/hyper_v/hyperv_wo_scvmm_rbs.html@@@Hyper-V without SCVMM@@@For Hyper-V without SCVMM, the Rubrik cluster uses the same Rubrik Backup Service software that is used for Windows file system protection...","saas/hyper_v/info_avail_day_view_loc_vm.html@@@Information available on the day view for a local Hyper-V virtual machine@@@The day view provides information about snapshots for a local virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/installing_rbs_wdac_azr_local.html@@@Installing RBS on Azure Local with WDAC enabled@@@The Rubrik Backup Service package includes a supplemental policy for installing RBS on Azure Local where Windows Defender Application Control is enabled. Install Rubrik Backup Service on an Azure Local system by deploying and activating the supplemental policy and then installing the Rubrik Backup Service MSI package...","saas/hyper_v/live_mount_advanced_options.html@@@Hyper-V Live Mount advanced options@@@When you create a Live Mount for Hyper-V virtual machines, you can configure the following advanced settings...","saas/hyper_v/local_host_page_hyperv.html@@@Local Hyper-V host page@@@The local host page provides detailed information about the protection of a virtual machine, and tasks related to the virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/managing_protection_hyperv.html@@@Managing protection for Hyper-V virtual machines@@@Assign an SLA Domain to protect a Hyper-V virtual machine...","saas/hyper_v/managing_protection_hyperv_clusters.html@@@Managing protection for Hyper-V clusters and hosts@@@Choose a data protection policy for a Hyper-V cluster or host...","saas/hyper_v/manually_register_vm_cluster_role_azure_local.html@@@Manually registering a VM as a cluster role on Azure Local@@@Manually register an exported or live mounted virtual machine as a Failover Cluster role on Azure Local...","saas/hyper_v/migrating_existing_hyperv_live_mounts.html@@@Migrating existing Hyper-V Live Mounts@@@Migrate data from an existing Hyper-V Live Mount in a Rubrik cluster to a storage location on a Hyper-V host to access the data from the Hyper-V host directly...","saas/hyper_v/performing_inplace_recovery_hyperv.html@@@Performing an in-place recovery of Hyper-V virtual machines@@@Perform an in-place recovery using RSC for faster recovery of data in Hyper-V virtual machines...","saas/hyper_v/performing_instant_recovery_hyperv.html@@@Performing an instant recovery of Hyper-V virtual machines@@@Use RSC to perform an instant recovery...","saas/hyper_v/powering_off_after_instant_recovery_hyperv.html@@@Powering off after Instant Recovery or Live Mount@@@Power off a recovered virtual machine from the Live Mounts page...","saas/hyper_v/rbs_azure_local_wdac_enabled.html@@@RBS on Azure Local with WDAC enabled@@@Azure Local systems with Windows Defender Application Control enabled can run any application enabled by the active policies. To install Rubrik Backup Service, you must first deploy and activate the Windows Defender Application Control supplemental policy for Rubrik, and then install the MSI package...","saas/hyper_v/recovery_and_restore_vm_data.html@@@Hyper-V virtual machine recovery@@@You can recover virtual machines and restore data by using any Rubrik data protection object and using an available recovery action...","saas/hyper_v/refreshing_scvmm_servers.html@@@Refreshing SCVMM servers@@@Refresh an SCVMM server so that the Rubrik cluster can discover new SCVMM servers or mark removed SCVMM servers as archived...","saas/hyper_v/removing_rbs_host.html@@@Removing RBS from a host@@@Remove RBS from a Windows host...","saas/hyper_v/removing_scvmms.html@@@Deleting SCVMM servers@@@Delete an SCVMM server to remove it from RSC...","saas/hyper_v/reprotection_vm.html@@@Reprotection of a virtual machine@@@At times, a virtual machine that is protected by one SLA Domain might be temporarily set to Don&apos;t protect and then reassigned to another SLA Domain for protection...","saas/hyper_v/rubrik_backup_service_scvmm.html@@@Rubrik Backup Service for Hyper-V@@@The Rubrik Backup Service provides enhanced integration with protected resources and host systems...","saas/hyper_v/scvmm_prerequisites.html@@@Prerequisites for System Center Virtual Machine Manager@@@Microsoft provides SCVMM hosts to manage virtual machines across multiple hosts. The Rubrik Backup Service should be installed on all hosts running SCVMM...","saas/hyper_v/troubleshooting_hyperv.html@@@Troubleshooting Hyper-V@@@You can diagnose and resolve common issues that affect Hyper-V virtual machine protection and recovery in RSC...","saas/hyper_v/unmanaged_data.html@@@Unmanaged data@@@RSC supports managing file system and application data that is not subject to a retention policy...","saas/hyper_v/unmounting_recovery_live_mount.html@@@Umounting after Instant Recovery or Live Mount@@@Unmount a recovered virtual machine from the Live Mounts page of RSC...","saas/identity_inventory_prereqs_limitations.html@@@Identity Inventory prerequisites and limitations@@@Enabling the Identity Inventory to view user activity and sensitive file activity has specific requirements and limitations...","saas/idp_info_sso_config.html@@@IdP information for SSO configuration@@@You can provide identity provider information to RSC to configure SSO successfully...","saas/idp_testing_sso_login_config.html@@@Testing the SSO login configuration@@@After configuring the SAML attributes in a SAML response, test the SSO login configuration to verify that the SSO connection has been established. You can also check whether the SAML attributes have been correctly received from the IdP...","saas/idp_testing_sso_login_config_2.html@@@Testing the SSO login configuration@@@After configuring the SAML attributes in a SAML response, test the SSO login configuration to verify that the SSO connection has been established. You can also check whether the SAML attributes have been correctly received from the IdP...","saas/immutable_rcv_locations.html@@@Immutable Rubrik Cloud Vault locations@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault locations provide immutability for cloud-native, NAS CD, and data center workloads, depending on the Rubrik CDM version and the cloud provider. Immutability ensures retention policies are enforced and prevents alteration or deletion of snapshots for the specified period, safeguarding data integrity...","saas/import_users_roles_rsc.html@@@Import users and roles to RSC@@@You can import users and roles created on the Rubrik cluster to manage them on RSC. After import, you can view the CDM RBAC migration summary report for confirmation or for further changes to users and roles...","saas/importing_tls_certificate.html@@@Importing a TLS certificate to support authentication@@@Import a TLS certificate or certificate chain into RSC to support authentication requirements...","saas/importing_users_roles_rsc.html@@@Importing users and roles to RSC@@@To manage users, roles, and SSO configurations created on the Rubrik cluster easily in the RSC, import them to RSC...","saas/initiating_advanced_threat_hunt.html@@@Initiating an advanced threat hunt@@@Initiate an advanced threat hunt to scan Rubrik backups for indicators of compromise and identify files at risk. An advanced threat hunt supports all three IOC types: YARA rule, file hash, and file pattern...","saas/initiating_turbo_threat_hunt.html@@@Initiating a turbo threat hunt@@@A turbo-charged threat hunt scans for hashes of file types most often used by threat agents. You can initiate this scan on both Rubrik clusters and cloud accounts...","saas/installing_cdp_filter.html@@@Installing the CDP filter@@@Install the CDP filter on the vCenter Server to protect virtual machine workloads with continuous data protection...","saas/instant_recovery_vSphere_VMs.html@@@Instant Recovery of vSphere virtual machines@@@You can use Instant Recovery to restore vSphere virtual machines with snapshots to their current compute resources or to a new compute resource...","saas/integration_third_party_apps_in_rsc.html@@@Integration of third-party applications in RSC@@@You can access the Integrations page to configure and manage your third-party SaaS integrations in RSC...","saas/investigating_and_recovering_anomalous_files.html@@@Investigating and recovering anomalous files for filesets@@@View and recover suspicious, deleted, or modified files at the protected object level or at the level of individual files or filesets...","saas/investigating_and_recovering_anomalous_files_for_virtual_machines.html@@@Investigating and recovering anomalous files for virtual machines@@@View and recover suspicious, deleted, or modified files at the protected object level or at the level of individual files for virtual machines...","saas/investigating_ri_anomalies.html@@@Investigating an anomaly@@@Investigate anomalous incidents and recover selected files from the Data Threat Analytics Anomaly Detection page...","saas/key_management_service.html@@@Key Management Services@@@Rubrik supports Key Management Services integration so that you can use your own encryption keys for data at rest. This Bring Your Own Key approach ensures Rubrik never accesses your master keys...","saas/key_mgmt_dare.html@@@Key management for data-at-rest encryption@@@With advanced key management, including key rotation, rekeying, and KMS integration, Rubrik enhances data-at-rest encryption by providing secure and flexible management of encryption keys to ensure ongoing protection of stored data...","saas/legal_hold_limitations.html@@@Legal hold limitations@@@Legal hold in RSC, does not support certain workloads, and legal hold status does not carry over between source and target Rubrik clusters...","saas/legal_hold_snapshot_rtn.html@@@Legal hold for snapshot retention@@@Legal hold ensures that snapshots are retained indefinitely until the hold is removed, overriding the scheduled expiry of an SLA Domain policy. This ensures that snapshots are available as long as necessary to meet legal obligations...","saas/legal_hold_snapshot_rtn_2.html@@@Legal hold for snapshot retention@@@Legal hold ensures that snapshots are retained indefinitely until the hold is removed, overriding the scheduled expiry of an SLA Domain policy. This ensures that snapshots are available as long as necessary to meet legal obligations...","saas/legal_hold_workloads.html@@@Legal hold for RSC workloads@@@Legal hold preserves cloud-native and SaaS snapshots indefinitely, overriding SLA Domain expiration to meet legal and compliance requirements...","saas/licenses_usage_details.html@@@Licenses and usage details@@@The Licenses and Usage page in RSC tracks license consumption and usage details across workloads to help you plan renewals and respond to expiration and overage alerts...","saas/licenses_usage_details_primary_tenant_accounts.html@@@License usage for primary and tenant accounts@@@For primary accounts using the Dedicated Tenants feature under the MSP PayGo license, the Licenses and Usage page shows license usage across associated tenant accounts...","saas/limitations_akv_secureauth.html@@@Limitations for Azure Key Vault with secretless provisioning@@@Review the known limitations when using secretless provisioning for Azure Key Vault integration...","saas/limitations_replication_config.html@@@Limitations in replication configuration@@@Configuring replication as part of the SLA Domain creation process has specific limitations that require consideration...","saas/limitations_upgrading_disks_azure_cces.html@@@Limitations on upgrading disks for Azure CCES@@@Azure CCES PremiumV2_LRS functions as a staging disk. A staging disk has certain restrictions involving OS disk use, region support, supported software versions and zones, and node limits...","saas/limits_configuring_cascading_archival.html@@@Limitations for configuring cascading archival@@@Information about actions and limitations for configuring cascading archival, including restrictions on shared target clusters, isolated clusters, and on-demand snapshots...","saas/live_mounting_impacted_snapshots.html@@@Mounting live objects from impacted snapshots@@@Recover a virtual machine affected by a deletion or encryption event using a live mount to restore access while the data remains on the Rubrik cluster...","saas/local_retention_frequency_requirements.html@@@Local retention requirements for snapshot frequencies@@@For each snapshot frequency that is not part of the archival policy, the local retention of an SLA Domain must be greater than the sum of the snapshot frequency and snapshot retention. Otherwise, RSC displays a validation error when you save the SLA Domain...","saas/local_user_account_lockout.html@@@Local user account lockout@@@Local user accounts are automatically locked after a configured number of failed login attempts or due to inactivity, enhancing security against unauthorized access...","saas/local_users.html@@@Local users@@@You can manage local user accounts on RSC...","saas/lock_cyber_recoveries.html@@@Locked cyber recoveries@@@Locking a cyber recovery prevents accidental cleanup and changes to the recovery in future Orchestrated Recovery operations...","saas/m365.html@@@Microsoft 365@@@Using the data management and protection services offered by Rubrik Security Cloud, you can protect Microsoft 365 data operations...","saas/m365_adding_app.html@@@Adding M365 apps@@@To improve backup and recovery speeds, add a Microsoft 365 app to RSC. RSC uses one app for each application, such as one app for Exchange, one app for SharePoint, and one app for OneDrive, for all backup, refresh, and restore operations...","saas/m365_adding_entra_id_group.html@@@Adding Entra ID groups@@@Add a wildcard group in Entra ID to assign specialized data protection policies...","saas/m365_adding_sharepoint_group.html@@@Adding SharePoint groups@@@Create a wildcard group in SharePoint to assign specialized data protection policies...","saas/m365_adding_teams_group.html@@@Adding Teams groups@@@Add a wildcard group in Teams to assign specialized data protection policies...","saas/m365_advanced_flow_setup.html@@@Microsoft 365 advanced setup@@@You can create a custom Azure Active Directory app to provide Rubrik Security Cloud authentication in your tenant. The app allows you to add Microsoft 365 subscriptions without requiring someone with the Azure Active Directory Global Administrator role...","saas/m365_api_prioritized_recovery_params.html@@@Microsoft 365 API prioritized data recovery parameters@@@Starting, canceling, and viewing the status of prioritized data recovery requires certain parameters, such as providing the mass recovery ID or the recovery point from which to restore the workload...","saas/m365_app_perms_mgmt_enterprise.html@@@Permissions settings for the Management Enterprise App@@@The Management Enterprise App requires specific permissions to authorize RSC access to Microsoft Entra ID...","saas/m365_application_permissions_exchange.html@@@Exchange enterprise application permissions@@@Permissions settings for RSC operations using the Microsoft 365 API and Microsoft Exchange...","saas/m365_application_permissions_onedrive.html@@@OneDrive enterprise application permissions@@@Permissions settings for RSC operations using the Microsoft 365 API and OneDrive...","saas/m365_application_permissions_sharepoint.html@@@SharePoint enterprise application permissions@@@Permissions settings for RSC operations using the Microsoft 365 API and SharePoint...","saas/m365_autonomous_business_recovery.html@@@Autonomous business recovery for Microsoft 365@@@Using autonomous business recovery for Microsoft 365, you can recover your critical Microsoft Exchange, OneDrive, and SharePoint data to all the users in a defined group...","saas/m365_azure_ent_app_mgmt.html@@@Azure Enterprise applications management@@@Rubrik Security Cloud supports Azure Enterprise applications deployed on Microsoft 365...","saas/m365_backup_details.html@@@Backup status details in the Microsoft 365 dashboard@@@The Microsoft 365 dashboard displays information and a graph related to the backup status of Microsoft 365 object types. You can monitor details, such as status of full backups, incremental backups, number of backed up protected object types, and compliance information...","saas/m365_backup_recovery_snapshots.html@@@Backup and recovery with Microsoft 365 snapshots@@@RSC protects and manages Microsoft 365 data using snapshots of source Microsoft 365 objects. You can take snapshots of backup data for Microsoft Exchange, OneDrive, SharePoint, and Teams to recover lost or compromised information...","saas/m365_backup_skipped_items.html@@@Skipped items during Microsoft 365 backup@@@Occasionally, RSC skips backing up some Microsoft 365 items due to Microsoft API errors or, in rare cases, internal errors. RSC events provide detailed information about items that were not backed up...","saas/m365_backup_sp_columns.html@@@Backup of Microsoft SharePoint columns@@@As part of Microsoft SharePoint backup and recovery, RSC backs up columns for SharePoint sites, document libraries, and lists, which you can restore during recovery...","saas/m365_byok.html@@@Bring Your Own Key encryption for Microsoft 365@@@By using Bring Your Own Key encryption for Microsoft 365 accounts on Rubrik Security Cloud, you can control the keys that Rubrik uses to encrypt your data...","saas/m365_canceling_mass_recovery_api.html@@@Canceling a Microsoft 365 mass recovery and prioritized data recovery with the API@@@Cancel the recovery task when you want to stop recovering Microsoft 365 objects during a full mass recovery and to stop prioritized data recovery...","saas/m365_changing_app_access_mode.html@@@Changing the access option for a Microsoft 365 app@@@Change a Microsoft 365 app between full access and just-in-time access to control the permissions that RSC holds between recoveries...","saas/m365_configuring_azure_app_secret.html@@@Setting a client secret in the Azure AD app for RSC@@@Set a client secret in the Azure AD app for RSC. You must set a client secret when deploying a Microsoft 365 workload using the Advanced setup method...","saas/m365_conflict_res_examples_entraid.html@@@Conflict resolution examples for Entra ID groups for SLA Domains@@@Information about the resolution of SLA Domain assignments and retention-locked SLA Domain assignments when Microsoft 365 user objects are members of multiple Entra ID groups...","saas/m365_conflict_resolution_groups.html@@@Conflict resolution for Microsoft 365 groups@@@When Microsoft 365 objects are members of multiple Entra ID, SharePoint, or Teams groups, rules are applied to resolve conflicts in SLA Domain assignments.You can assign an SLA Domain, compliance retention-locked SLA Domain, or a governance retention-locked SLA Domain to these objects. RSC uses different rules for each SLA Domain to resolve conflicts...","saas/m365_create_enterprise_aad.html@@@Creating the enterprise AAD app@@@Create the enterprise Azure Active Directory app used by RSC Microsoft 365 workloads when you are using advanced setup...","saas/m365_create_groups_autonomous_bus_rec.html@@@Creating critical operations groups for autonomous business recovery@@@Create a critical operations group that defines the critical resources for recovery. During recovery, these resources are prioritized over all other resources...","saas/m365_creating_azure_ad_app.html@@@Creating an Azure AD app for RSC@@@Create an Azure AD app for RSC on your tenant to use with the advanced setup process...","saas/m365_creating_role_groups.html@@@Creating roles for Microsoft 365 groups@@@Create a role and configure role permissions required to access a Microsoft 365 group...","saas/m365_cust_hosted_deployment_reqs.html@@@Customer-hosted deployment mode requirements@@@System requirements for the customer-hosted deployment mode for Microsoft 365 protection...","saas/m365_dashboard.html@@@Microsoft 365 dashboard@@@The Microsoft 365 dashboard provides important insights into your protected Microsoft 365 environment. By using the dashboard, you can view and monitor information such as deployment locations and settings, backup and recovery status, events, and compliance information...","saas/m365_dashboard_details.html@@@M365 Dashboard details@@@The Microsoft 365 Dashboard displays summary information for each subscription and the applications provisioned within the subscription in a dedicated pane. For example, you can view details about subscriptions, backups, and errors and warnings...","saas/m365_deleting_groups_autonomous_bus_rec.html@@@Deleting critical operations groups for autonomous business recovery@@@Delete a critical operations group that defines the critical resources for recovery when you no longer need it...","saas/m365_deleting_subscription.html@@@Deleting a Microsoft 365 subscription@@@Delete a Microsoft 365 subscription...","saas/m365_deployment_mode.html@@@Deployment modes@@@RSC supports deployment modes for the data plane responsible for the Microsoft 365 data source computing activities...","saas/m365_downloading_files_folders.html@@@Downloading files or folders for Microsoft 365@@@After exporting recovery data, to obtain the data, download a ZIP archive of the data from an indexed snapshot of a OneDrive account, SharePoint document library, or email messages from an Exchange mailbox...","saas/m365_downloading_mass_recovery_reports.html@@@Downloading Microsoft 365 mass recovery reports@@@You can download a report in CSV format that includes details about the objects RSC recovered or could not recover during a successful or partially successful mass recovery...","saas/m365_downloading_skipped_items_backup.html@@@Downloading a list of Microsoft 365 items skipped during backup@@@When RSC cannot back up some Microsoft 365 data, you can download a list containing information about the skipped OneDrive, Exchange, SharePoint, or Teams items...","saas/m365_duplicates_recovery.html@@@Duplicate objects for Microsoft in-place recovery@@@When you are performing an in-place recovery, you can create a duplicate of an object and also retain the original object, or you can overwrite the old, duplicate objects with the objects to recover...","saas/m365_editing_groups_autonomous_bus_rec.html@@@Editing critical operations groups for autonomous business recovery@@@Edit a critical operations group that defines the critical resources for recovery. During recovery, these resources are prioritized over all other resources...","saas/m365_enterprise_aad_app_permissions_settings.html@@@Enterprise AAD app API permissions settings@@@Required Microsoft 365 API permission settings for the enterprise Azure Active Directory app...","saas/m365_exchange_acct_prioritized_recovery.html@@@Performing a prioritized data recovery for an Exchange account@@@When recovering multiple Microsoft Exchange accounts, you can recover your most critical data first before recovering all your data...","saas/m365_exchange_prioritized_multiple.html@@@Performing prioritized data recovery for multiple Exchange accounts@@@When recovering multiple Microsoft Exchange accounts, you can recover your most critical data first before recovering all your data...","saas/m365_exchange_prioritized_recover.html@@@Performing a prioritized data recovery for Exchange@@@Perform a prioritized data recovery for Microsoft Exchange to restore a specified subset of data. You can perform a prioritized data recovery before performing a recovery of all objects...","saas/m365_exchange_recovery.html@@@Backup and recovery of Exchange data@@@RSC protects and manages Microsoft 365 Exchange data using snapshots of source Microsoft 365 Exchange objects to recover lost or compromised information...","saas/m365_exchange_supported_data.html@@@Supported and unsupported data types for Microsoft 365 Exchange@@@RSC backs up specific Microsoft 365 Exchange data types. You can review the supported and unsupported data types to understand what data RSC includes in Exchange backups...","saas/m365_exporting_sharepoint_objs.html@@@Exporting SharePoint document libraries and files@@@Export SharePoint document libraries and their files to a .zip file that you can download and then use for recovery...","saas/m365_exporting_skipped_items.html@@@Exporting Microsoft 365 items skipped during recovery@@@If RSC fails to recover certain Microsoft 365 data, you can either export a ZIP archive of the skipped items or download a detailed list of them...","saas/m365_firewall_rules.html@@@Firewall rules@@@Lists the firewall rules needed for communication between the RSC, Microsoft 365, and Microsoft Azure when using customer-hosted deployment...","saas/m365_groups.html@@@Groups in M365@@@RSC uses groups to assign data protection and management policies uniformly to Microsoft 365 objects...","saas/m365_groups_assignments_sla_domain.html@@@SLA Domain assignments in M365 groups@@@In RSC, you can assign SLA Domains, compliance retention-locked SLA Domains, and governance retention-locked SLA Domains to Entra ID groups, SharePoint groups, and Teams groups in Microsoft 365...","saas/m365_immutability.html@@@Microsoft 365 immutability@@@RSC uses immutable storage for Azure Blob Storage to provide immutability protection for Microsoft 365 when creating an Azure storage account for Microsoft 365 deployments. Immutability protection ensures that your data remains unaltered, which is critical for disaster recovery, protection from ransomware attacks, and data compliance...","saas/m365_implicit_permissions_rbac.html@@@Implicit permissions and Microsoft 365 objects@@@Rubrik Security Cloud uses implicit permissions to help provide access to specific objects in the Microsoft 365 hierarchy...","saas/m365_jit_access.html@@@Microsoft 365 just-in-time access@@@Just-in-time access reduces the permissions that the Azure Enterprise applications for RSC hold between recoveries. RSC assigns write permissions only for the duration of a recovery and then revokes them...","saas/m365_key_rotation.html@@@Key rotation and protection for Microsoft 365@@@To better protect your Microsoft 365 data, you can use the Rubrik Security Cloud automatic key rotation and rekeying policies...","saas/m365_legal_hold_snapshots.html@@@Legal hold for Microsoft 365 snapshots@@@Legal hold preserves Microsoft 365 snapshots indefinitely, overriding SLA Domain expiration to meet legal and compliance requirements...","saas/m365_license_usage_details.html@@@Microsoft 365 license and usage details@@@The Microsoft 365 Licenses and Usage page provides detailed information about the purchased licenses and consumption across Microsoft 365 services...","saas/m365_mass_recovery.html@@@Microsoft 365 mass recovery and prioritized data recovery@@@You can recover data from multiple Entra ID, SharePoint, and Teams groups to recover multiple Microsoft 365 objects. You can start, cancel, and track the progress of mass recovery in a single place. You can also perform a prioritized data recovery for Exchange, SharePoint, and OneDrive to restore your most important data first before recovering the rest of the data...","saas/m365_mass_recovery_getting_status_api.html@@@Getting the status of a Microsoft 365 mass recovery or prioritized data recovery with the API@@@Get the status of a full Microsoft 365 mass recovery, or the status of a prioritized data recovery for Microsoft Exchange, to view the following details: number of objects that could be recovered, number of objects that could not be recovered, number of objects without snapshots, and so on...","saas/m365_mass_recovery_parameters.html@@@Microsoft 365 API mass recovery parameters@@@Starting, canceling, and viewing the status of a full mass recovery requires certain parameters. These parameters include the mass recovery ID or snapshots from which to restore the workload...","saas/m365_mass_recovery_status_output.html@@@Get mass recovery and prioritized data recovery status output fields@@@The output from getting the status of the mass recovery or prioritized data recovery provides important details and status information, such as recovery ID and number of objects recovered...","saas/m365_multigeo.html@@@Microsoft 365 Multi-Geo@@@Rubrik Security Cloud supports Microsoft 365 Multi-Geo for Microsoft 365 subscriptions...","saas/m365_onedrive_prioritized_recover.html@@@Performing a prioritized data recovery for OneDrive@@@Perform a prioritized data recovery for Microsoft 365 OneDrive to recover a subset of data. You can perform a prioritized data recovery before performing a remaining data recovery of all objects...","saas/m365_onedrive_recover_download.html@@@Recovering OneDrive files or folders by downloading files@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to search for and recover specific files from Microsoft OneDrive by downloading the files...","saas/m365_onedrive_recover_sso.html@@@Recovering OneDrive data for SSO users@@@SSO users can recover OneDrive files or folders in RSC...","saas/m365_onedrive_recover_sub.html@@@Recovering OneDrive files or folders to different subscriptions@@@Recover a Microsoft 365 OneDrive file or folder to different Microsoft 365 subscription associated with the same RSC account...","saas/m365_outlook_recover_sso.html@@@Recovering Outlook data for SSO users@@@SSO users can recover Microsoft Outlook email messages, calendar events, or contact information in RSC...","saas/m365_performing_mass_recvry_entraid_grps.html@@@Performing a mass recovery for Entra ID groups@@@Perform a mass recovery to restore multiple snapshots for Microsoft 365 Entra ID Exchange and OneDrive groups when data is lost or compromised...","saas/m365_performing_mass_recvry_sharepoint_grps.html@@@Performing a mass recovery for SharePoint groups@@@Perform a mass recovery to restore multiple Microsoft 365 SharePoint snapshots when data is lost or compromised...","saas/m365_performing_mass_recvry_teams_grps.html@@@Performing a mass recovery for Teams groups@@@Perform a mass recovery to recover multiple Microsoft 365 Teams snapshots when data is lost or compromised...","saas/m365_performing_rekey.html@@@Performing a rekey for Microsoft 365@@@Perform a rekey of the master key or intermediate key to update your encryption key to an alternative encryption key. This ensures that your data location uses up-to-date encryption...","saas/m365_performing_remaining_recovery.html@@@Performing a remaining data recovery with the API@@@After you have performed a prioritized data recovery, perform a data recovery to restore all objects...","saas/m365_protecting_applications.html@@@Protecting Microsoft 365 applications@@@Choose a data protection policy for the applications in a Microsoft 365 subscription...","saas/m365_protecting_sharepoint_objects.html@@@Protecting SharePoint objects@@@Configure a data protection policy for SharePoint objects...","saas/m365_protecting_teams_data.html@@@Protecting Microsoft Teams data@@@Specify a data protection policy for RSC to use when protecting Microsoft Teams data...","saas/m365_protecting_useraccount_objects.html@@@Protecting Microsoft 365 user account objects@@@Choose a data protection policy for objects in a Microsoft 365 subscription...","saas/m365_protecting_using_groups.html@@@Protecting Microsoft 365 workloads using groups@@@Manage the protection of Microsoft 365 workloads by assigning a data protection policy to an Entra ID, SharePoint, or Teams group...","saas/m365_protection.html@@@Microsoft 365 protection@@@Use SLA Domains to apply the data protection policies and management policies to Microsoft 365 resources...","saas/m365_protection_hierarchy.html@@@Protection hierarchy for Microsoft 365 resources@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based, automatic protection of Microsoft 365 resources...","saas/m365_protection_reqs_rubrik_hosted.html@@@Rubrik-hosted deployment mode requirements@@@System requirements for the Rubrik-hosted deployment mode for Microsoft 365 protection...","saas/m365_reauthenticating_teams_app.html@@@Re-authenticating a Teams App@@@Re-authenticate a Teams App through RSC when you update or add permissions to an existing Teams application...","saas/m365_recover_calendars_org_loc.html@@@Recovering calendars to the original location@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to search for and recover specific calendar events, meetings, and appointments to the original location...","saas/m365_recover_contacts_org_loc.html@@@Recovering contacts to the original location@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to search for and recover specific Exchange contacts to the original location...","saas/m365_recover_email_original_loc.html@@@Recovering email messages to the original location@@@Search for and recover specific email messages to the original user account by using indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots...","saas/m365_recover_exchange_another_sub.html@@@Recovering Exchange objects to another subscription@@@Recover Microsoft Exchange objects, such as mailboxes, calendars, and contacts, to another Microsoft 365 subscription in the same RSC account...","saas/m365_recover_groups_autonomous_bus_rec.html@@@Recovering Microsoft 365 data using autonomous business recovery@@@Use autonomous business recovery to recover Microsoft 365 Exchange, OneDrive, or SharePoint objects for all the members in a Microsoft Entra ID group...","saas/m365_recover_onedrive_another_loc.html@@@Recovering OneDrive files or folders to another location@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to search for and recover files to another location...","saas/m365_recover_original_loc.html@@@Recovering OneDrive files or folders to the original location@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to search for specific files or folders from Microsoft 365 OneDrive to recover these files or folders to the original location. RSC also recovers certain permissions for the files or folders...","saas/m365_recover_relic_user_acct_snapshots.html@@@Recovering relic Microsoft 365 user account snapshots@@@Recover relic Microsoft 365 object snapshots from the Inventory page...","saas/m365_recover_sharepoint_coll_org.html@@@Recovering SharePoint site collection to the original collections@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover an active or relic SharePoint site collection to the original collection. A relic collection is a deleted collection that is not active...","saas/m365_recover_sharepoint_coll_sub.html@@@Recovering a SharePoint site collection to another subscription@@@Recover an active SharePoint site collection to another subscription by using indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots...","saas/m365_recover_sharepoint_new_coll.html@@@Recovering SharePoint site collections to new collections@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover all the SharePoint objects such as document libraries and lists, along with permissions in an active SharePoint collection to a new collection in the same subscription...","saas/m365_recover_sharepoint_objects_sub.html@@@Recovering SharePoint objects to another subscription@@@Recover active SharePoint document libraries, lists, files, list items, and apps to another Microsoft 365 subscription by using indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots...","saas/m365_recover_sharepoint_objs_loc.html@@@Recovering SharePoint objects to another location@@@Recover active SharePoint objects, which are document libraries, lists, files, list items, and app catalogs, to another location by using indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots...","saas/m365_recover_sharepoint_objs_org.html@@@Recovering SharePoint objects to the original location@@@Recover active and relic SharePoint objects, including document libraries, lists, files, list items, and apps, to a new site by using indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots. Relic objects are deleted objects that are not active. An in-place recovery also recovers certain site permissions...","saas/m365_recover_teams_shrd_chnl_convs_sub.html@@@Recovering Teams shared channel conversations to another subscription@@@Recover conversations associated with Microsoft Teams shared channel to another Microsoft 365 subscription in the same RSC account...","saas/m365_recover_teams_shrd_chnl_org_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams shared channels to the original channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover all content from the shared channel associated with Microsoft Teams shared to the original channel...","saas/m365_recover_teams_shrd_conv_new_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams shared channel conversations to a new channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover conversations posted in a shared Microsoft Teams channel to a new channel...","saas/m365_recover_teams_shrd_convs_org_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams shared channel conversations to the original channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover conversations posted in a shared Microsoft Teams channel...","saas/m365_recover_teams_shrd_files_download.html@@@Downloading from Teams shared channel files@@@Search for and recover Microsoft Teams files or folders by downloading a ZIP file that contains the specified files or folders...","saas/m365_recover_teams_shrd_files_new_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams shared channel files to a new channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover files uploaded to a shared Microsoft Teams channel to a channel that you create...","saas/m365_recover_teams_shrd_files_org_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams shared channel files to the original channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover files uploaded to a shared channel associated with Microsoft Teams to the original channel...","saas/m365_recovering_calendars_another_location.html@@@Recovering calendars to another location@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to search for and recover specific calendar events, meetings, and appointments to another user...","saas/m365_recovering_contacts_another_location.html@@@Recovering contacts to another location@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to search for and recover specific Exchange contacts to another location...","saas/m365_recovering_emails_another_location.html@@@Recovering email messages to another location@@@Search for and recover specific email messages to another user by using indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots...","saas/m365_recovering_emails_by_downloading.html@@@Recovering email messages by downloading messages@@@Search for and recover specific email messages by using indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to download a ZIP archive containing one or more PST files that you can import into Microsoft Outlook.Search for and recover specific email messages by using indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to download a PST file containing that you can import into Microsoft Outlook...","saas/m365_recovering_remaining_data.html@@@Recovering remaining data for Microsoft 365@@@Recover your remaining data if you did not automatically recover this data after performing a prioritized data recovery or autonomous business recovery...","saas/m365_recovering_teams_shrd_chnl_new_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams shared channels to a new channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover all content from a Microsoft Teams shared channel to a new channel...","saas/m365_recovering_teams_shrd_chnl_sub.html@@@Recovering Teams shared channels to another subscription@@@Recover a shared channel associated with Microsoft Teams to another Microsoft 365 subscription in the same RSC account...","saas/m365_recovery_perms.html@@@Permissions required for Microsoft 365 backup and recovery@@@You require the appropriate permissions to back up and recover Microsoft 365 data...","saas/m365_registering_apps.html@@@Registering a Microsoft 365 app@@@Register a Microsoft 365 app in the Azure portal and create an app secret for authentication...","saas/m365_relic_management.html@@@Relic Microsoft 365 management@@@Microsoft 365 does not support user accounts once the user license is revoked. RSC archives inactive user accounts without snapshots and manages the ones with snapshots as relics...","saas/m365_removing_apps.html@@@Removing M365 apps@@@Remove a Microsoft 365 app when you no longer need it...","saas/m365_resources_deployed_in_azure_account.html@@@Resources deployed in the Azure account@@@The Azure resources deployed in the user account build the infrastructure to protect data in a Microsoft 365 subscription...","saas/m365_setting_up_advanced_flow.html@@@Setting up a Microsoft 365 subscription using advanced setup@@@Set up a Microsoft 365 subscription with a direct connection to Azure Active Directory...","saas/m365_setting_up_api_mass_recovery.html@@@Setting up the API for Microsoft 365 for mass recovery and prioritized data recovery@@@Set up the API to recover multiple Microsoft Exchange, SharePoint, or OneDrive objects for a Microsoft 365 group in a single action. Additionally, you can set up the API to perform a prioritized data recovery for Exchange, SharePoint, and OneDrive. You can recover selected, important data first from these workloads before restoring all objects...","saas/m365_setting_up_subscription.html@@@Setting up a Microsoft 365 subscription for customer hosting@@@Set up the integration between a Microsoft 365 subscription and RSC for the customer-hosted deployment mode...","saas/m365_setting_up_subscription_rubrik_hosted.html@@@Adding a Microsoft 365 subscription for Rubrik hosting@@@Add a Microsoft 365 subscription in RSC for Rubrik hosting...","saas/m365_sharepoint_backup_recovery.html@@@Backup and recovery of SharePoint sites and site collections@@@Rubrik Security Cloud provides backup protection for SharePoint site collections and the site data stored in each collection...","saas/m365_sharepoint_prioritized_recover.html@@@Performing a prioritized data recovery for SharePoint@@@Perform a prioritized data recovery for Microsoft SharePoint to recover only a subset of data. You can perform a prioritized data recovery before performing a recovery of all remaining objects...","saas/m365_sharepoint_recovery_modes.html@@@SharePoint recovery modes@@@If you have protected SharePoint objects in the Legacy mode, a version filter displays several modes when recovering SharePoint objects...","saas/m365_sharepoint_site_perms.html@@@Supported SharePoint site permissions@@@As part of Microsoft 365 SharePoint backup and recovery, RSC backs up certain site permissions that you can recover in certain scenarios...","saas/m365_single_use_permissions.html@@@Single-use permissions@@@For the customer-hosted deployment, RSC obtains a set of single-use permissions for the Azure cloud account...","saas/m365_skipped_items.html@@@Skipped items during Microsoft 365 recovery@@@RSC might skip recovering some Microsoft 365 items during the recovery process. To provide greater insight into the recovery process, RSC events provide detailed information about the items that RSC could not recover...","saas/m365_starting_mass_recovery_exchange_api.html@@@Starting a mass recovery for Microsoft Exchange with the API@@@Start a full mass recovery to restore email messages, calendar events, meetings, appointments, and contacts for an Exchange group from an indexed Microsoft 365 snapshot...","saas/m365_starting_mass_recovery_onedrive_api.html@@@Starting a mass recovery for Microsoft OneDrive with the API@@@Start a full mass recovery to recover multiple OneDrive files from a Microsoft 365 group from an indexed Microsoft 365 snapshot...","saas/m365_starting_mass_recovery_sharepoint_api.html@@@Starting a mass recovery for Microsoft SharePoint with the API@@@Start full mass recovery to restore complete SharePoint collections (sites, document libraries, lists, files, and list items) from a SharePoint group from an indexed Microsoft 365 snapshot...","saas/m365_starting_prioritized_recovery_exchange_api.html@@@Using the API to start a prioritized data recovery for Exchange@@@Start a prioritized data recovery using the API to restore selected data for an Exchange group from an indexed Microsoft 365 snapshot...","saas/m365_starting_prioritized_recovery_onedrive_api.html@@@Using the API to start a prioritized data recovery for OneDrive@@@Start a prioritized data recovery using the API to restore selected data for a OneDrive group from an indexed Microsoft 365 snapshot...","saas/m365_starting_prioritized_recovery_sharepoint_api.html@@@Using the API to start a prioritized data recovery for SharePoint@@@Start a prioritized data recovery using the API to restore selected data for an SharePoint group from an indexed Microsoft 365 snapshot...","saas/m365_subscription_management.html@@@M365 subscription management@@@RSC provides management and protection of Microsoft 365 subscriptions...","saas/m365_supported_sharepoint_objects.html@@@Supported SharePoint objects@@@The SharePoint objects supported for backup and recovery by RSC...","saas/m365_taking_ods_exchange_onedrive.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Microsoft Exchange and OneDrive objects@@@Take on-demand snapshots of Microsoft 365 Exchange and OneDrive objects, in addition to policy-based snapshots, to protect the data in the Exchange and OneDrive objects...","saas/m365_taking_ods_sharepoint.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Microsoft SharePoint objects@@@Take on-demand snapshots of Microsoft 365 SharePoint objects, in addition to policy-based snapshots, to protect your data in the SharePoint objects...","saas/m365_taking_ods_teams.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Microsoft Teams objects@@@Take on-demand snapshots of Microsoft 365 Teams objects, in addition to policy based snapshots, to protect your data in the Teams objects...","saas/m365_teams_data_recovery.html@@@Teams data recovery@@@You can use RSC to recover various types of Teams data...","saas/m365_teams_prioritized_recovery.html@@@Performing a prioritized data recovery for Teams@@@Perform a prioritized data recovery for Microsoft Teams to recover only a subset of data. You can perform a prioritized data recovery before performing a recovery of all remaining objects...","saas/m365_teams_protect_channel.html@@@Microsoft Teams channel protection@@@You can use Rubrik Security Cloud to back up and recover standard and private Microsoft Teams channels...","saas/m365_teams_recover_prvt_chnl_anr_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams private channels to another channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover all content from a Microsoft Teams private channel to another private channel...","saas/m365_teams_recover_prvt_chnl_convs_sub.html@@@Recovering Teams private channel conversations to another subscription@@@Recover Microsoft Teams private channel conversations to another Microsoft 365 subscription in the same RSC account...","saas/m365_teams_recover_prvt_chnl_files_sub.html@@@Recovering Teams private channel files to another subscription@@@Recover files from a Microsoft Teams private channel to another Microsoft 365 subscription in the same RSC account...","saas/m365_teams_recover_prvt_chnl_org_chnl.html@@@Recovering all Teams private channel content to the original channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover all content from a Microsoft Teams private channel to the original private channel...","saas/m365_teams_recover_prvt_chnl_sub.html@@@Recovering Teams private channels to another subscription@@@Recover a Microsoft Teams private channel to another Microsoft 365 subscription in the same RSC account...","saas/m365_teams_recover_prvt_cons_anr_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams private channel conversations to another channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover conversations posted in a Microsoft Teams private channel...","saas/m365_teams_recover_prvt_conv_org_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams private channel conversations to the original channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover conversations posted in a Microsoft Teams private channel...","saas/m365_teams_recover_prvt_files_anr_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams private channel files to another channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover files uploaded to a Microsoft Teams private channel...","saas/m365_teams_recover_prvt_files_org_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams private channel files to the original channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover files uploaded to a Microsoft Teams private channel to the original channel...","saas/m365_teams_recover_shrd_chnl_files_sub.html@@@Recovering files from a Teams shared channel to another subscription@@@Recover files in a Microsoft Teams shared channel to another Microsoft 365 subscription in the same RSC account...","saas/m365_teams_recover_std_chnl_anr_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams standard channels to another channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover all content from a Microsoft Teams standard channel to another channel...","saas/m365_teams_recover_std_chnl_org_chnl.html@@@Recovering all Teams standard channel content to the original channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover all content from a Microsoft Teams standard channel to the original channel...","saas/m365_teams_recover_std_chnl_sub.html@@@Recovering Teams standard channels to another subscription@@@Recover a Microsoft Teams standard channel to another Microsoft 365 subscription in the same RSC account...","saas/m365_teams_recover_std_conv_org_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams standard channel conversations to the original channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover conversations posted in a standard Microsoft Teams channel...","saas/m365_teams_recover_std_convs_anr_chnl.html@@@Recovering conversations from a Teams standard channel to another location@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover conversations posted in a standard Microsoft Teams channel...","saas/m365_teams_recover_std_files_anr_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams standard channel files to another channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover files uploaded to a standard Microsoft Teams channel to another channel...","saas/m365_teams_recover_std_files_org_chnl.html@@@Recovering Teams standard channel files to the original channel@@@Use indexed Microsoft 365 snapshots to recover files uploaded to a standard Microsoft Teams channel to the original channel...","saas/m365_teams_recover_std_files_sub.html@@@Recovering Teams standard channel files to another subscription@@@Recover files in a Microsoft Teams standard channel to another Microsoft 365 subscription in the same RSC account...","saas/m365_teams_recover_stnd_chnl_convs_sub.html@@@Recovering Teams standard channel conversations to another subscription@@@Recover Microsoft Teams standard conversations to another Microsoft 365 subscription in the same RSC account...","saas/m365_updating_app_secrets_and_cert.html@@@Updating expired app secrets and certificates@@@You can update expired app secrets and certificates in RSC...","saas/m365_user_license_usage_calculation.html@@@Microsoft 365 user license usage calculation@@@Describes how RSC calculates Microsoft 365 (M365) user license usage for Foundation Edition (FE), Professional Edition (PE), and Enterprise Edition (EE)...","saas/m365_viewing_relic_user_account_details.html@@@Viewing relic Microsoft 365 user account details@@@View relic Microsoft 365 object details from the Inventory page...","saas/manage_cdm_admin_access.html@@@Manage CDM administrator access@@@From RSC, you can view and manage the credentials for the default admin user account on connected Rubrik CDM clusters, including the email address, password, MFA device, and SSH keys...","saas/manage_retention_sap_hana_snapshots.html@@@Manage retention of SAP HANA snapshots@@@To meet data governance and regulatory compliance, you can increase the retention period of individual SAP HANA snapshots, as required...","saas/managing_aws_exocompute_mapping.html@@@Mapping AWS accounts to centralized Exocompute@@@After you have configured an Exocompute instance in the Exocompute host account by adding regions and confirmed that the cluster is healthy, map an application account to an Exocompute host account. You can update or remove an existing mapping as required...","saas/managing_disabled_iocs.html@@@Managing disabled IOCs in Threat Monitoring@@@View all disabled indicators of compromise and restore detection coverage for previously suppressed detections...","saas/managing_granular_perm_azr_cloud_acnt.html@@@Managing granular permissions for an Azure cloud account@@@Manage the permission categories for an Azure cloud account that you have already added to RSC by including or excluding permission categories, as required...","saas/managing_llm_analysis_anomaly_detection.html@@@Managing LLM analysis for Anomaly Detection@@@Manage the use of LLM analysis for Anomaly Detection in RSC by disabling it when it is not required. To enhance the accuracy of Anomaly Detection, enable LLM analysis for Anomaly Detection...","saas/managing_pat_policy.html@@@Managing the personal access token policy@@@Configure organization-wide policy settings for personal access tokens, including concurrent session limits, inactivity timeout, and session timeout...","saas/managing_protection_for_snapmirror_cloud.html@@@Managing protection with SnapMirror Cloud@@@Assign an SLA Domain configured with a SnapMirror Cloud archival location to a NetApp NAS host...","saas/managing_protection_object.html@@@Managing protection for an object@@@Manage protection for an object by assigning an SLA Domain to optimize data management and enhance data protection...","saas/mandatory_mfa.html@@@Mandatory multi-factor authentication@@@Multi-factor authentication enforcement is mandatory for all user accounts in your RSC environment...","saas/mfa_changing_dev.html@@@Changing the TOTP device@@@Rubrik Two-Step Verification uses time-based one-time passwords generated by a user device as an additional authentication factor. A user can change which device is used to generate this authentication factor from RSC...","saas/microsoft_purview_integration.html@@@Microsoft Purview integration@@@You can classify and protect your organization&apos;s data by applying Microsoft Information Protection labels to documents in Microsoft Azure, Microsoft 365 environments, and data sources connected to the Microsoft Purview platform...","saas/migration_arch_loc_rcv.html@@@Migration of archival locations to RCV@@@You can migrate existing archival location data from Amazon S3, S3-compatible, or Azure Blob storage to Rubrik Cloud Vault by using a supported migration tool with assistance from Rubrik Professional Services...","saas/migration_arch_loc_rcv_2.html@@@Migration of archival locations to RCV@@@You can migrate existing archival location data from Amazon S3, S3-compatible, or Azure Blob storage to Rubrik Cloud Vault by using a supported migration tool with assistance from Rubrik Professional Services...","saas/migration_organizations_from_rubrik_cdm.html@@@Migration of organizations from Rubrik CDM@@@To successfully migrate organizations from Rubrik CDM to RSC, you must complete certain tasks...","saas/modes_of_rl_sla_domains.html@@@Modes of retention-locked SLA Domains@@@Retention-locked SLA Domains support two modes, governance mode and compliance mode, each offering distinct methods for managing data security and compliance requirements within SLA Domains...","saas/monitor_orchestrated_recovery.html@@@Monitor recoveries@@@You can monitor Orchestrated Recovery recoveries by reviewing events, plan and recovery details, and recovery reports, and by troubleshooting failed recoveries...","saas/mounting_azr_virtual_disks_for_data_recovery.html@@@Mounting Azure virtual disks for data recovery@@@To recover critical data in a disaster or outage that can pose a significant business problem, mount the Azure virtual disks to the source virtual machine or a different virtual machine running in another region or subscription...","saas/ms_entra_id.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID@@@RSC supports backup and recovery of Microsoft Entra ID...","saas/ms_entra_id_adding_ehub_existing.html@@@Adding Event Hub ingestion to existing directories@@@Add Event Hub log ingestion for a Microsoft Entra ID directory already configured in RSC...","saas/ms_entra_id_adding_ehub_no_oauth.html@@@Adding Event Hub ingestion without OAuth@@@Add Event Hub log ingestion when adding a new Microsoft Entra ID directory to RSC without OAuth authentication...","saas/ms_entra_id_adding_ehub_oauth.html@@@Adding Event Hub ingestion with OAuth@@@Add Event Hub log ingestion when adding a new Microsoft Entra ID directory to RSC with OAuth authentication...","saas/ms_entra_id_admin_units_recov.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID administrative units recovery@@@RSC supports recovery of Microsoft Entra ID administrative units. Backing up and recovering administrative units requires granting specific permissions on the Microsoft Entra ID directory...","saas/ms_entra_id_apps_recovery.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID enterprise app and app registrations recovery@@@RSC backs up and recovers Microsoft Entra ID enterprise apps and app registrations, including SSO configuration...","saas/ms_entra_id_backup.html@@@Back up Microsoft Entra ID@@@Protect your Microsoft Entra ID environment by assigning SLA Domains and taking snapshots of your directories...","saas/ms_entra_id_ca_obj_perms.html@@@Permissions for Conditional Access recovery@@@Configuring RSC without OAuth requires the Microsoft Graph permissions that correspond to each Conditional Access object type...","saas/ms_entra_id_ca_prereqs.html@@@Conditional Access recovery prerequisites@@@Recovering Microsoft Entra ID Conditional Access objects with RSC requires meeting several prerequisites...","saas/ms_entra_id_conditional_access_recovery.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID Conditional Access recovery@@@For Microsoft Entra ID directories that support Conditional Access, RSC can protect Microsoft Entra ID Conditional Access objects and relationships...","saas/ms_entra_id_configure.html@@@Configure Microsoft Entra ID protection@@@Configure Microsoft Entra ID protection by adding the directory to RSC and configuring access controls...","saas/ms_entra_id_ctr.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID cross-tenant recovery@@@Microsoft Entra ID cross-tenant recovery restores directory data from a source tenant to a separate, distinct target tenant to ensure business continuity during catastrophic events...","saas/ms_entra_id_ctr_config.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID cross-tenant recovery configuration@@@Configuration requirements for Microsoft Entra ID cross-tenant recovery include Microsoft licensing tiers, RBAC privileges, target directory environment settings, and domain mapping configurations...","saas/ms_entra_id_ctr_hybrid_iden_envs.html@@@Cross-tenant recovery for hybrid identity environments@@@When you perform a cross-tenant recovery in a hybrid identity environment, you must manually re-anchor on premises Active Directory users to the target Microsoft Entra ID tenant before RSC can restore supported relationships for those hybrid identities...","saas/ms_entra_id_ctr_limitations.html@@@Cross-tenant recovery limitations@@@Microsoft Entra ID on RSC has known limitations for cross-tenant recovery, including supported object types, unique identifier collisions, and hybrid environment configurations...","saas/ms_entra_id_deleting_domain.html@@@Deleting a Microsoft Entra ID directory@@@Delete a Microsoft Entra ID directory from RSC when it no longer requires protection...","saas/ms_entra_id_deleting_snapshot.html@@@Deleting a Microsoft Entra ID snapshot@@@Delete a Microsoft Entra ID snapshot that has the Forever retention policy assigned...","saas/ms_entra_id_devices_protection.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID device protection@@@RSC protects Microsoft Entra ID device data by securing critical recovery data against ransomware and accidental data loss...","saas/ms_entra_id_dir_auth_options.html@@@Authentication paths for Microsoft Entra ID directories@@@The authentication paths for adding a Microsoft Entra ID directory to RSC differ in how you set up the required Azure application and permissions...","saas/ms_entra_id_editing_domain.html@@@Editing a Microsoft Entra ID domain@@@Edit the configuration for a Microsoft Entra ID domain added to RSC...","saas/ms_entra_id_event_hub.html@@@Event Hub log ingestion for Microsoft Entra ID@@@RSC collects Microsoft Entra ID audit and sign-in logs through Microsoft Graph API polling by default with an optional Event Hub configuration that reduces delivery latency to near-real time streaming...","saas/ms_entra_id_event_hub_prereqs.html@@@Azure prerequisites for Event Hub log ingestion@@@Event Hub log ingestion in RSC without OAuth requires specific Azure resources to be in place in the Entra ID tenant, including an Event Hubs namespace, event hub, diagnostic setting, and role assignment...","saas/ms_entra_id_full_domain_recov.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID full tenant recovery@@@Using Microsoft Entra ID full tenant recovery, administrators can restore all objects and relationships in a tenant from a previous state. You can specify objects to exclude from recovery...","saas/ms_entra_id_idgov_config_reqs.html@@@Identity Governance configuration requirements@@@Microsoft Entra ID Identity Governance protection requires a Rubrik Identity Recovery or Identity Resilience license, a supporting Microsoft license, and additional Microsoft Graph API permissions...","saas/ms_entra_id_idgov_limits.html@@@Identity Governance limitations@@@Microsoft Entra ID on RSC has known limitations for protecting and recovering Identity Governance objects...","saas/ms_entra_id_intune_protected_obj.html@@@Protected Microsoft Intune object types@@@RSC protects Microsoft Intune policy objects that control device configuration, compliance, security, and administration...","saas/ms_entra_id_intune_protection_config.html@@@Microsoft Intune protection configuration@@@Microsoft Intune protection requires specific RSC configuration settings, Microsoft Graph API permissions, and licensing requirements...","saas/ms_entra_id_jit_access.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID just-in-time access@@@Just-in-time access for Microsoft Entra ID separates read and write access to align with the principle of least privilege, ensuring that critical write permissions are active only during necessary recovery operations. Just-in-time access is available for Microsoft Entra ID domains using OAuth authentication...","saas/ms_entra_id_known_limits_apps.html@@@Application limitations@@@Microsoft Entra ID on RSC has known limitations for backing up and recovering app registrations and enterprise apps...","saas/ms_entra_id_known_limits_identity.html@@@Identity limitations@@@Microsoft Entra ID on RSC has known limitations for backing up and recovering user and group identities...","saas/ms_entra_id_known_limits_rsc.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID on RSC limitations@@@Microsoft Entra ID on RSC has known limitations across object types, properties, and recovery scenarios...","saas/ms_entra_id_manage.html@@@Manage your Entra ID environment@@@You can view directory details, review snapshot protection status, and manage snapshots for your Microsoft Entra ID environment...","saas/ms_entra_id_no_oauth_perms.html@@@Permissions for Microsoft Entra ID@@@RSC requires specific Microsoft Graph API permissions to protect a Microsoft Entra ID directory, whether you onboard the directory with or without OAuth...","saas/ms_entra_id_non_recov_soft_del_obj_rsc.html@@@Non-recovery of higher-privileged soft-deleted objects@@@RSC does not recover higher-privileged, soft-deleted Microsoft Entra ID user or group objects unless the Rubrik service principal is granted the required Microsoft Entra role...","saas/ms_entra_id_obj_recov_across_snapshots.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID object recovery across snapshots@@@With RSC, you can search Microsoft Entra ID user, groups, and roles objects for recovery across different snapshots. This functionality enables recovery of objects and relationships from a specific date and time...","saas/ms_entra_id_obj_relationship_recovery.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID object and relationship recovery@@@RSC recovers Microsoft Entra ID objects and object relationships, including users, groups, roles, enterprise apps, and app registrations...","saas/ms_entra_id_performing_full_ctr.html@@@Performing a full-tenant cross-tenant recovery@@@Recover all protected objects and relationships in a Microsoft Entra ID directory to a new tenant...","saas/ms_entra_id_performing_granular_ctr.html@@@Performing a granular cross-tenant recovery@@@Recover selected Microsoft Entra ID objects and relationships to a new tenant...","saas/ms_entra_id_plan.html@@@Plan your Microsoft Entra ID protection@@@Microsoft Entra ID protection requires planning for supported object types, known limitations, and environment-specific requirements...","saas/ms_entra_id_postrec_tasks.html@@@Post-recovery tasks for Microsoft Entra ID@@@Recovered Microsoft Entra ID enterprise apps and app registrations can require that you perform manual post-recovery tasks to restore authentication credentials and configurations...","saas/ms_entra_id_product_license_recov.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID product license recovery@@@RSC recovers Microsoft product license entitlements as part of user and group recovery, restoring Microsoft licenses...","saas/ms_entra_id_protect_idgov.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID Identity Governance protection@@@Rubrik Security Cloud protects Microsoft Entra ID Identity Governance objects so you can recover privileged access policies, entitlement configurations, and access review definitions alongside identity and endpoint data...","saas/ms_entra_id_protect_microsoft_intune.html@@@Microsoft Intune device protection@@@RSC protects Microsoft Intune policies, helping you maintain a resilient identity and endpoint posture...","saas/ms_entra_id_protected_device_data.html@@@Protected device data types@@@RSC protects the following Microsoft Entra ID device data types...","saas/ms_entra_id_protecting.html@@@Protecting Microsoft Entra ID@@@Assign an SLA Domain to a Microsoft Entra ID directory to protect it...","saas/ms_entra_id_rec_ca_ctx_tou.html@@@Recovering authentication contexts and terms of use@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID Conditional Access authentication contexts and terms of use and their linked policies from a specific point in time with RSC...","saas/ms_entra_id_rec_ca_named_auth_str.html@@@Recovering named locations and authentication strengths@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID Conditional Access named locations and authentication strengths and their linked policies from a specific point in time with RSC...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_bitlocker_key_data.html@@@Recovering Microsoft Entra ID BitLocker key data@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID BitLocker key data by using a snapshot from a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_cond_access_pol_rel.html@@@Recovering Conditional Access policies and relationships@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID Conditional Access policy objects and relationships from a specific point in time with RSC...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_device_data.html@@@Recovering Microsoft Entra ID device data@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID device data by using a snapshot from a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_full_domain.html@@@Recovering a Microsoft Entra ID full tenant@@@Recover all protected objects and relationships in a Microsoft Entra tenant to their original locations...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_grp_role_acr_snp.html@@@Recovering groups and roles across snapshots@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID group and role objects and relationships across snapshots, and specify the exact objects and relationships for recovery...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_grp_role_obj_rel.html@@@Recovering groups and roles@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID group and role objects and relationships by using a snapshot from a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_local_admin_pwd.html@@@Recovering Microsoft Entra ID local administrator passwords@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID local administrator passwords by using a snapshot from a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_user_attr_date.html@@@Recovering user attributes from date ranges@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID user attributes and relationships from a snapshot within a selected date range...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_user_attr_pit.html@@@Recovering user attributes from a point in time@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID user attributes and relationships by selecting a snapshot from a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_user_obj_relationships.html@@@Recovering user objects and relationships@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID user objects and relationships using a snapshot from a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_user_pw_manual.html@@@Recovering user objects and relationships manually@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID user objects and their relationships from a specific point-in-time snapshot by manually creating temporary login passwords for each recovered object. This operation requires 50 or fewer objects...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_users_across_snapshots.html@@@Recovering users across snapshots@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID user objects and relationships across snapshots, and specify the exact objects and relationships for recovery...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_users_hybrid_env.html@@@Recovering users from a hybrid environment@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID user objects and relationships, as well as synced Active Directory user object relationships, by using a snapshot from a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recov_users_hybrid_env_man.html@@@Recovering users from a hybrid environment manually@@@Recover up to 50 Microsoft Entra ID user objects and relationships with manual passwords, as well as synced Active Directory user relationships, by using a snapshot from a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recover.html@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID@@@RSC provides multiple recovery methods for Microsoft Entra ID, including granular object recovery, cross-snapshot recovery, attribute recovery, full domain recovery, and clean recovery...","saas/ms_entra_id_recovering_admin_units.html@@@Recovering Microsoft Entra ID administrative units@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID administrative units, including their user, group, and device membership, from a snapshot taken at a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recovering_app_reg.html@@@Recovering app registrations and relationships@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID app registrations and relationships by using a snapshot from a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recovering_ent_apps.html@@@Recovering enterprise apps and relationships@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID enterprise apps and relationships by using a snapshot from a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recovering_groups_hybrid_env.html@@@Recovering group objects from a hybrid environment@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID group object properties and relationships, as well as synced Active Directory group object relationships, by using a snapshot from a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recovering_idgov.html@@@Recovering Identity Governance objects@@@Recover selected Microsoft Entra ID Identity Governance objects from a directory snapshot...","saas/ms_entra_id_recovering_intune.html@@@Recovering Microsoft Intune objects@@@Recover selected Microsoft Intune objects from a Microsoft Entra ID directory snapshot...","saas/ms_entra_id_recovering_sso_policies.html@@@Recovering SSO policies@@@Recover Microsoft Entra ID SSO policies using a snapshot from a specific point in time...","saas/ms_entra_id_recovery_hybrid_env.html@@@Hybrid identity environment recovery@@@In a hybrid Microsoft Entra ID and Active Directory environment on RSC, you can view Active Directory group and user assignments synced from the Active Directory domain. You can additionally recover relationships for synced Active Directory user and group objects and protect the Active Directory domain...","saas/ms_entra_id_recovery_strategies.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID recovery strategies@@@When recovering Microsoft Entra ID objects that already exist in the target tenant, RSC provides three recovery strategies to control how it reconciles attribute drift and relationship conflicts...","saas/ms_entra_id_relationship_recovery_modes.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID relationship recovery modes@@@Describes the modes RSC uses to recover relationships between Microsoft Entra ID objects...","saas/ms_entra_id_retention_lock.html@@@Retention lock for Microsoft Entra ID@@@A retention lock on an SLA Domain prevents premature deletion of Microsoft Entra ID snapshots and directories...","saas/ms_entra_id_rev_intune_protection_limits.html@@@Microsoft Intune protection limitations@@@Microsoft Entra ID on RSC has known limitations for protecting and recovering Microsoft Intune policies...","saas/ms_entra_id_snapshot_protection_details.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID snapshot protection details@@@The Overview tab on the object details page of a Microsoft Entra ID directory displays protection and snapshot details...","saas/ms_entra_id_sso_policies.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID SSO policy recovery@@@RSC backs up and recovers SSO policies that control authentication behavior for enterprise apps and app registrations in Microsoft Entra ID...","saas/ms_entra_id_taking_ods.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of Microsoft Entra ID@@@Take on-demand snapshots of Microsoft Entra ID protectable objects in addition to the policy-based snapshots provided by the SLA Domain...","saas/ms_entra_id_user_obj_attr_recov.html@@@Microsoft Entra ID user object attribute recovery@@@Attribute recovery for a Microsoft Entra ID user object selectively restores specific attributes that were maliciously or accidentally altered without performing a full object restore. You can compare user object attributes from a snapshot against live data and recover only the changed attributes...","saas/ms_entra_id_viewing_directories.html@@@Viewing Microsoft Entra ID directories@@@View details for the Microsoft Entra ID directories...","saas/ms_exchange_adding_host.html@@@Adding a Microsoft Exchange host@@@Add a host to a Microsoft Exchange deployment...","saas/ms_exchange_assigning_sla_domain.html@@@Assigning an SLA Domain to a Microsoft Exchange database availability group@@@Assign an SLA Domain to a Microsoft Exchange database availability group to provide Microsoft database availability group snapshot management based on SLA Domain policies...","saas/ms_exchange_availability_groups.html@@@Microsoft Exchange availability groups@@@The Availability groups tab provides information on Microsoft Exchange hosts connected to RSC...","saas/ms_exchange_changing_retention_snapshot.html@@@Changing Microsoft Exchange snapshot retention@@@Change the retention period for specified snapshots of a Microsoft Exchange workload object...","saas/ms_exchange_databases.html@@@Microsoft Exchange databases@@@The Databases tab provides information on Microsoft Exchange databases connected to RSC...","saas/ms_exchange_deleting_snapshot.html@@@Deleting a Microsoft Exchange database snapshot@@@You can delete a Microsoft Exchange database snapshot from RSC...","saas/ms_exchange_hosts.html@@@Microsoft Exchange hosts@@@The Hosts tab provides information on Microsoft Exchange hosts connected to RSC...","saas/ms_exchange_management.html@@@Microsoft Exchange management@@@Rubrik Security Cloud provides backup and recovery for Microsoft Exchange deployments...","saas/ms_exchange_protection.html@@@Microsoft Exchange protection@@@You can use Rubrik Security Cloud data protection features to secure Microsoft Exchange deployments...","saas/ms_exchange_protection_hierarchy.html@@@Protection hierarchy for Microsoft Exchange@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based, automatic protection for Microsoft Exchange resources...","saas/ms_exchange_protection_prerequisites.html@@@Prerequisites for Microsoft Exchange protection@@@To protect Microsoft Exchange workloads, all components must meet specific prerequisites...","saas/ms_exchange_recovering_snapshot.html@@@Recovering a Microsoft Exchange database snapshot@@@You can recover on-demand and scheduled snapshots for Microsoft Exchange databases...","saas/ms_exchange_server.html@@@Microsoft Exchange Server@@@Rubrik Security Cloud provides protection for Microsoft Exchange Servers...","saas/ms_exchange_setting_backup_preference.html@@@Setting a backup preference for a Microsoft Exchange database availability group@@@Choose a backup preference for a Microsoft Exchange database availability group...","saas/ms_exchange_snapshots.html@@@Microsoft Exchange snapshots@@@Rubrik Security Cloud protects and manages data by taking snapshots of the source object...","saas/ms_exchange_taking_ods.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of a Microsoft Exchange database@@@You can take on-demand snapshots of Microsoft Exchange databases...","saas/ms_exchange_workflow.html@@@Microsoft Exchange workflow@@@The Microsoft Exchange workflow provides a summary of the actions involved in protecting Microsoft Exchange data on Rubrik Security Cloud...","saas/mssql_actions_available_database_details.html@@@Microsoft SQL Server database details actions@@@Multiple actions are available for a selected database on the database details page...","saas/mssql_adding_sql_server_db_host.html@@@Adding a Microsoft SQL Server database host@@@Add a Windows Server host with Microsoft SQL Server databases to the Rubrik cluster to begin managing and protecting Microsoft SQL Server databases...","saas/mssql_adding_windows_server_failover_clusters.html@@@Adding Windows Server failover clusters@@@Add Windows Server failover clusters to begin managing and protecting the failover cluster instance databases on those clusters...","saas/mssql_advanced_export_of_sql_server_database.html@@@Performing an advanced export of a Microsoft SQL Server database backup@@@Use the advanced method to export the files from a Microsoft SQL Server database backup to specified locations...","saas/mssql_backup_immutability.html@@@Microsoft SQL Server backup immutability@@@When you archive Microsoft SQL Server backup data to an archival location with an immutability policy, RSC automatically protects SQL Server database snapshot and log backup files with object-level locks that prevent deletion for the duration of the retention period...","saas/mssql_configuring_default_cbt_settings.html@@@Configuring default Change Block Tracking settings@@@Enable or disable Change Block Tracking for all hosts...","saas/mssql_configuring_sens_data_auth.html@@@Configuring Sensitive Data Authentication for SQL Server@@@Configure a Windows Server host to authenticate to an SQL Server database with an authenticated RBS user to perform Data Discovery and Classification...","saas/mssql_creating_a_t_log_backup.html@@@Creating an on-demand T-log backup@@@Create an on-demand T-log backup to protect records that were written to the transaction log after the most recent transaction log backup...","saas/mssql_creating_bidi_repl_sla_domain.html@@@Creating a bidirectional replication SLA Domain@@@Create a bidirectional replication SLA Domain to protect the primary and secondary database replicas of multi-data center availability groups that span two Rubrik clusters...","saas/mssql_database_details.html@@@Microsoft SQL Server database details@@@The Microsoft SQL Server database details page provides detailed information about the database, its protection status, Live Mounts, available snapshots, database events and snapshots...","saas/mssql_database_export.html@@@Microsoft SQL Server database export recovery@@@You can export a selected recovery point of a database to a Microsoft SQL Server instance on the same Windows Server host or on another available Windows Server host...","saas/mssql_deleting_log_shipping_configuration.html@@@Deleting the log shipping configuration@@@Delete a log shipping configuration from the Rubrik cluster...","saas/mssql_download_snapshot_transaction_logs.html@@@Downloading MS SQL Server snapshots and transaction logs@@@Download a Microsoft SQL Server database snapshot and transaction logs bundled together in a single zip file...","saas/mssql_downloading_snapshot_log_backups_archive.html@@@Downloading an archived database snapshot and log backups@@@Download a selected snapshot and transaction logs from the archival location. Stage them locally to decrease the time taken by restore operations...","saas/mssql_editing_cbt_windows_host.html@@@Editing Change Block Tracking on a Windows host@@@Edit Change Block Tracking for selected Windows hosts...","saas/mssql_exporting_sql_server_dbs.html@@@Exporting Microsoft SQL Server databases@@@Export some or all of the databases from a Microsoft SQL Server instance to capture the state of the databases at a specific point in time...","saas/mssql_ha_mssql_workloads.html@@@High Availability for Microsoft SQL Server workloads@@@RSC provides High Availability Policies that you can assign to Microsoft SQL Server workloads to maintain uninterrupted backup and recovery operations against hardware failures, software errors, natural disasters, power outages, and network issues...","saas/mssql_linking_multi_dc_ag_dbs.html@@@Linking multi-data center availability group databases@@@Link individual databases from two multi-data center availability groups to a bidirectional SLA Domain that spans two Rubrik clusters. This configuration enables the SLA Domain to manage protection for primary and secondary database replicas located in different data centers...","saas/mssql_linking_multi_dc_ags.html@@@Linking multi-data center availability groups@@@Link two multi-data center availability groups to a bidirectional SLA Domain that spans two Rubrik clusters. This configuration enables the SLA Domain to manage protection for primary and secondary database replicas located in different data centers...","saas/mssql_live_mounting_sql_server_database.html@@@Live Mounting a Microsoft SQL Server database@@@Use Live Mount to create a Microsoft SQL Server database from a point-in-time copy of a source database...","saas/mssql_log_backup_retention.html@@@Log backup retention@@@An SLA Domain controls whether to archive and replicate Microsoft SQL Server log backups and enables different retention periods per target...","saas/mssql_manage_mssql_database_hosts.html@@@Manage Microsoft SQL Server database hosts@@@After adding a Microsoft SQL Server host, you can manage the host by refreshing metadata, updating certificates, editing host settings, modifying Change Block Tracking, or deleting the host...","saas/mssql_managing_and_protecting_fci_databases_through_a_parent_object.html@@@Managing and protecting FCI databases through a parent object@@@Protect databases in a failover cluster instance by assigning an SLA Domain to the parent failover cluster, or to the parent Microsoft SQL Server database...","saas/mssql_managing_protecting_individual_fci_databases.html@@@Managing and protecting individual FCI databases@@@To provide data management and protection for an individual failover cluster instance database, assign an SLA Domain to that database...","saas/mssql_multi_data_center_avail_grp.html@@@Multi-data center availability group support@@@Multi-data center availability groups improve the backup behavior for availability groups with a bidirectional replication SLA Domain...","saas/mssql_overview_tab.html@@@Overview details for Microsoft SQL Server databases@@@The Overview tab on the database details page provides general status and snapshot information...","saas/mssql_pausing_resuming_protection.html@@@Pausing and resuming protection for Microsoft SQL Server databases@@@Pause scheduled backup, archival, and replication actions for a specific database workload without affecting the protection of other objects managed by the SLA Domain...","saas/mssql_prereqs_multi_data_center_ag.html@@@Prerequisites for multi-data center availability groups@@@Microsoft SQL Server hosts and Rubrik clusters must meet the following requirements before they can support multi-data center availability groups...","saas/mssql_protecting_dbs_through_parent_obj.html@@@Protecting databases through a parent object@@@Assign an SLA Domain to a Windows Server host, Microsoft SQL Server instance, or individual databases to protect Microsoft SQL Server databases. Derived assignments from a host or instance allow uniform management and protection of database groups...","saas/mssql_protecting_individual_dbs.html@@@Protecting individual Microsoft SQL Server databases@@@To provide data management and protection for an individual Microsoft SQL Server database, assign that database to an SLA Domain...","saas/mssql_recover_export_fci_database_recovery_points.html@@@Recovery options for FCI database recovery points@@@You can recover a Microsoft SQL Server failover cluster instance database from a selected recovery point by replacing the source database, exporting a copy, creating a Live Mount, or downloading the snapshot and transaction logs...","saas/mssql_recover_mssql_databases.html@@@Recover Microsoft SQL Server databases@@@You can use a Rubrik cluster to recover Microsoft SQL Server databases from snapshots and, after transaction log backups are available, to any point in time...","saas/mssql_recovering_availability_grp_db.html@@@Recovering an availability group database@@@Recover an availability group database by exporting a selected recovery point...","saas/mssql_recovering_multi_dc_avail_grp.html@@@Recovering multi-data center availability groups@@@Recover a multi-data center availability group database by exporting a Microsoft SQL Server instance, including its underlying databases, to a specific point in time...","saas/mssql_removing_sla_domain_assignment.html@@@Removing Microsoft SQL Server database protection@@@Remove an SLA Domain assignment from a Microsoft SQL Server database to prevent policy-driven snapshots and log backups for the database. Both derived and individual SLA Domain assignments can be removed...","saas/mssql_removing_windows_server_host.html@@@Removing a Microsoft SQL Server database host@@@Remove a Windows Server host from the Rubrik cluster to stop managing the data for the Microsoft SQL Server databases on that host...","saas/mssql_reseed_a_sql_server_database.html@@@Reseed a Microsoft SQL Server database@@@Reseed a Microsoft SQL Server database by resetting the secondary database...","saas/mssql_reseeding_a_sql_server_database.html@@@Reseeding a Microsoft SQL Server database@@@When a log shipping configuration fails, create the secondary database by reseeding the database...","saas/mssql_restoring_a_database.html@@@Recovering a Microsoft SQL Server database@@@Restore and recover a database from a selected recovery point in the database backup...","saas/mssql_restoring_sql_server_dbs.html@@@Restoring Microsoft SQL Server databases@@@Restore some or all of the databases from a Microsoft SQL Server instance to the state they were in at a specific point in time...","saas/mssql_rubrik_backup_service.html@@@RBS for SQL Server databases@@@RBS backs up and restores SQL Server databases and provides enhanced integration with SQL Server protected resources and host systems...","saas/mssql_setting_advanced_export_log_shipping_target.html@@@Setting Up an advanced export to a log shipping target@@@Set up an advanced export to a log shipping target to receive logs of the transactions that are run on the primary database...","saas/mssql_setting_default_log_backup_frequency.html@@@Changing the default log backup path@@@Edit the default log backup properties to change the log backup location for a protected Microsoft SQL Server database...","saas/mssql_setting_up_simple_export_log_shipping_target.html@@@Setting up a simple export to a log shipping target@@@Set up a simple export to a log shipping target to receive logs of the transactions that are executed on the primary database...","saas/mssql_setup_mssql.html@@@Set up Microsoft SQL Server@@@You can set up Microsoft SQL Server in RSC to start protecting Microsoft SQL Server workloads...","saas/mssql_simple_export_a_database.html@@@Creating a simple export of a Microsoft SQL Server database@@@Create a simple export of a selected recovery point of a database to a Microsoft SQL Server instance on the same Windows Server host or on another available Windows Server host...","saas/mssql_sla_domain_assignments.html@@@SLA Domain assignments for SQL Server objects@@@Assigning an SLA Domain activates automated protection for your Microsoft SQL Server databases. Direct or inherited SLA Domain assignment supports policy-driven management of database and log backups...","saas/mssql_support_large_databases.html@@@Support for large SQL Server databases@@@RSC provides support for backup and recovery of large SQL Server databases with a high file count...","saas/mssql_taking_group_on_demand_snapshot_task.html@@@Taking a group on-demand snapshot task@@@Take a single on-demand snapshot of a group of Microsoft SQL Server databases to use fewer resources than are required to take an on-demand snapshot of each individual database in the group...","saas/mssql_taking_on_demand_snapshot.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot@@@Create an on-demand snapshot of the databases on a Microsoft SQL Server instance or of individual Microsoft SQL Server database...","saas/mssql_unlinking_multi_dc_avail_grp.html@@@Unlinking multi-data center availability groups@@@Unlink multi-data center availability groups from a bidirectional SLA Domain when protection for primary and secondary database replicas for both Rubrik clusters is no longer needed...","saas/mssql_viewing_database_details_page.html@@@Viewing the Microsoft SQL Server database details@@@View detailed information about the database, its protection status, Live Mounts, available snapshots, and tasks related to the database and snapshots...","saas/mssql_viewing_failover_clusters.html@@@Viewing failover clusters and databases@@@View the available failover clusters, the Microsoft SQL Server databases on each failover cluster, and the restore points for each database...","saas/mssql_windows_server_failover_clustering.html@@@Windows Server Failover Clustering@@@The Rubrik cluster provides protection for Windows Server Failover Clustering at the failover cluster instance level...","saas/mt_Editing_an_org.html@@@Editing an organization@@@Edit a tenant organization in RSC...","saas/mt_MFA_for_tenant_org.html@@@Multifactor authentication for a tenant organization@@@Enabling multifactor authentication adds one or more factors to the basic authentication process and is recommended to protect against ransomware and other vulnerabilities...","saas/mt_SSO_options_for_tenant_organizations.html@@@SSO options for tenant organizations@@@The global organization administrator can configure SSO options for user access in the tenant organizations...","saas/mt_archival_locations_for_tenant_orgs.html@@@Archival locations for tenant organizations@@@The global administrator can assign archival location options or archival view and manage privileges to the tenant organization during organization creation or editing...","saas/mt_assigning_tenant_org_storage_quota.html@@@Assigning the tenant organization storage quota@@@Assign storage-based quota to a tenant organization to restrict resource utilization and protect resource availability...","saas/mt_cert_csr_mgmt_orgs.html@@@Certificate and Certificate Signing Request management for organizations@@@Tenant organizations with the required permissions can view and manage certificates and Certificate Signing Requests for their organizations...","saas/mt_creating_tenant_org.html@@@Creating a tenant organization@@@Create a tenant organization by adding a name, adding user accounts, and assigning clusters and objects to protect...","saas/mt_ded_tenant.html@@@Dedicated tenants@@@Dedicated Rubrik Security Cloud tenants provide Managed Service Providers with physically isolated Rubrik Security Cloud instances for their clients, ensuring complete data separation and feature parity across security applications...","saas/mt_deleting_an_org.html@@@Deleting an organization@@@Delete a tenant organization from RSC...","saas/mt_dt_access_control.html@@@Granular access control for dedicated tenant management@@@Granular access control enables an administrator to delegate dedicated tenant management to non-administrator users in the primary RSC account by assigning view or create-and-edit permissions to custom roles...","saas/mt_dt_assign_perms.html@@@Assigning permissions to a custom role@@@Update an existing custom role in the primary RSC account to grant users access to the Dedicated Tenants management page...","saas/mt_dt_create_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for dedicated tenant management@@@Create a custom role in the primary RSC account and assign a dedicated tenant management permission so that non-administrator users can view, create, or edit dedicated tenant accounts...","saas/mt_dt_creating_dedicated_tenants.html@@@Creating dedicated tenants@@@Create a dedicated RSC tenant to provide users with a physically isolated RSC instance that supports full feature parity and independent management...","saas/mt_dt_creation_limits.html@@@Dedicated tenant creation limitations@@@Dedicated RSC tenant management involves specific restrictions regarding administrative ownership, account nesting, regional availability, and license dependencies...","saas/mt_dt_creation_prereqs.html@@@Dedicated tenant creation prerequisites@@@Before creating and managing dedicated Rubrik Security Cloud tenants, the primary account must meet specific account type, licensing, and administrative role requirements for isolation and resource allocation across tenant accounts...","saas/mt_dt_manage_dedicated_tenants.html@@@Manage dedicated tenants@@@After provisioning dedicated tenants, administrators in the primary Rubrik Security Cloud account can control access, allocate licenses, monitor account metrics, and suspend or resume tenant accounts...","saas/mt_dt_metrics.html@@@Dedicated tenant metrics@@@The Dedicated Tenants dashboard provides a centralized view of account status, products provisioned, and regional distribution for all tenant accounts...","saas/mt_dt_mng_licenses.html@@@Managing licenses for dedicated tenants@@@Manage licenses for dedicated tenants by allocating licenses from a shared pool to enable data protection and security services...","saas/mt_dt_msp_capabilities.html@@@Service provider capabilities@@@Rubrik Security Cloud multi-account management provides service providers with tools to provision isolated dedicated tenants, manage shared licenses, and access advanced security features across all client environments...","saas/mt_dt_nc_about.html@@@Network Connectors@@@Network Connectors enable Rubrik to back up and recover workloads in environments where network segmentation, NAT, or overlapping IP address ranges prevent the Rubrik cluster from directly reaching tenant workloads...","saas/mt_dt_nc_deploying.html@@@Deploying Network Connectors in a tenant network@@@Deploy the Network Connector virtual appliance in the tenant environment and configure its initial network settings before registering it with a Rubrik cluster...","saas/mt_dt_nc_deregistering.html@@@Removing a Network Connector from a tenant account@@@Remove a Network Connector appliance from a Rubrik cluster in the RSC tenant account...","saas/mt_dt_nc_live_mount_ips.html@@@Configuring Live Mount IP addresses in tenant accounts@@@Configure Live Mount IP addresses for Network Connectors on a cluster in the RSC tenant account...","saas/mt_dt_nc_overview.html@@@Network Connectors for RSC tenant accounts@@@Network Connectors enable secure backup and recovery of tenant workloads in RSC tenant account environments where network segmentation, NAT, or overlapping IP addresses prevent the Rubrik cluster from directly reaching tenant workloads. Network Connectors support both dedicated and shared Rubrik clusters assigned to the RSC tenant account...","saas/mt_dt_nc_registering.html@@@Registering Network Connectors in a tenant account@@@Register a deployed Network Connector appliance with a Rubrik cluster from the RSC tenant account...","saas/mt_dt_nc_scale.html@@@Network Connectors scale and performance limits@@@Network Connectors in RSC tenant account environments support defined scale, throughput, and availability targets...","saas/mt_dt_nc_topologies.html@@@Supported network topologies for Network Connectors@@@Network Connectors support a range of Layer 2, Layer 3, and Layer 7 network segmentation topologies for RSC tenant accounts...","saas/mt_dt_nc_viewing_status.html@@@Viewing and monitoring Network Connectors@@@View the connection status and configuration of registered Network Connectors, and review events and audit log entries, from the RSC tenant account...","saas/mt_dt_nc_workloads.html@@@Supported workloads and operations for Network Connectors@@@Network Connectors support specific workloads, protocols, and operations for RSC tenant accounts...","saas/mt_dt_perms_overview.html@@@Dedicated tenant management permissions@@@Permissions that control access to the Dedicated Tenants management page in the primary RSC account...","saas/mt_dt_provision_dedicated_tenants.html@@@Provision dedicated tenants@@@Provisioning a dedicated Rubrik Security Cloud tenant involves meeting account and licensing prerequisites, understanding operational limitations, selecting a supported region, and creating the tenant through the account creation wizard...","saas/mt_dt_retry_prov_failed_accounts.html@@@Retrying provisioning for failed accounts@@@Retry the provisioning process for a dedicated tenant account that failed during the initial setup...","saas/mt_dt_retry_prov_product.html@@@Retrying product provisioning for dedicated tenants@@@Retry product provisioning for dedicated tenants by identifying failed products and monitoring Product Status to ensure successful deployment...","saas/mt_dt_sup_regions.html@@@Supported regions for dedicated tenants@@@Rubrik Security Cloud supports specific geographic regions for provisioning dedicated tenant accounts to ensure compliance with data residency requirements and infrastructure availability...","saas/mt_dt_suspend_tenant.html@@@Suspending a dedicated tenant@@@Suspend a dedicated Rubrik Security Cloud tenant to temporarily block tenant users and administrators from the UI and API while configured snapshots, replication, and archiving continue...","saas/mt_dt_suspending_unsuspending.html@@@Dedicated tenant suspension and resumption@@@Primary account users with the Suspend and Resume Dedicated Tenant Accounts permission can temporarily block a dedicated Rubrik Security Cloud tenant&apos;s users and admins from the UI and API while data protection operations continue, and these users can restore access at any time...","saas/mt_dt_unsuspend_tenant.html@@@Resuming a dedicated tenant@@@Resume a dedicated Rubrik Security Cloud tenant to restore full UI and API access for tenant users and admins...","saas/mt_editing_tenant_org_storage_quota.html@@@Editing the tenant organization storage quota@@@Edit the tenant organization storage quota to increase or decrease the storage limits for an organization...","saas/mt_events_reports_tenants.html@@@Events and reports for tenant organizations@@@Events and reports for tenant organizations are limited to the objects and privileges assigned to them...","saas/mt_global_organization_administrator_privileges.html@@@Global organization administrator privileges@@@The global organization administrator or global organization owner role has privileges in the global organization as well as the tenant organization...","saas/mt_impact_deleting_tenant.html@@@Impact of deleting a tenant organization@@@Deleting a tenant organization impacts the information that the RSC account stores for that organization...","saas/mt_multitenancy.html@@@Multitenancy with RSC@@@Rubrik Security Cloud multitenancy uses a multi-account management framework that enables a single primary Rubrik Security Cloud account to provision, manage, and monitor multiple Rubrik Security Cloud environments. The architecture is designed to support both shared infrastructure and strict physical isolation...","saas/mt_organizations.html@@@Organizations@@@Multitenancy in Rubrik Security Cloud provides logical isolation of shared compute, storage, and network resources in such a way that each organization can only access its own data, especially for shared infrastructure platforms...","saas/mt_replication_tenant_org.html@@@Replication for tenant organizations@@@The global organization administrator sets up replication targets, options, and permissions for the tenant organization when creating or editing the organization...","saas/mt_sc_assigning_shared_clusters.html@@@Assigning shared clusters to tenant accounts@@@Assign a Rubrik cluster to multiple tenant accounts to extend infrastructure resources to more than one tenant while maintaining tenant data isolation...","saas/mt_sc_configuring_replication_network.html@@@Configuring replication network settings for a tenant@@@Managed Service Provider (MSP) administrators configure the replication network paths that a tenant can use when creating replication pairings on a shared cluster...","saas/mt_sc_creating_sc_replication_pairing.html@@@Creating a shared cluster replication pairing@@@Tenant users with replication configuration permissions can create a replication pairing between a shared cluster and another cluster, using the network paths that the Managed Service Provider (MSP) configured...","saas/mt_sc_encryption_shared_clusters.html@@@Encryption on shared clusters@@@The MSP encrypts all tenant data on shared clusters at rest using a single cluster-wide key. Tenants can independently configure encryption keys for their own archival locations...","saas/mt_sc_mt_requirements_limitations.html@@@Shared cluster multitenancy requirements and limitations@@@Shared cluster multitenancy has specific requirements and does not support certain configurations...","saas/mt_sc_preparing_offline_data_recovery.html@@@Preparing for offline data recovery@@@Create local user accounts for tenant administrators on shared clusters that you can use for data recovery if RSC becomes unavailable...","saas/mt_sc_primary_tenant_tasks.html@@@Who can perform shared cluster tasks@@@Primary and tenant account users can perform different tasks on dedicated tenants that share clusters...","saas/mt_sc_recovering_sc_offline.html@@@Recovering data when RSC is unavailable@@@When RSC is unavailable, authorized Managed Service Provider (MSP) administrators can log in directly to the Rubrik cluster UI to perform tenant-scoped recovery operations on behalf of tenants...","saas/mt_sc_recovery_target_isolation.html@@@Recovery target isolation on shared clusters@@@On shared clusters, Rubrik enforces tenant isolation for Live Mount recovery target selection and Managed Volume exports. MSPs must also configure network controls at the access layer to prevent cross-tenant access...","saas/mt_sc_scale_performance_limits.html@@@Shared cluster scale and performance limits@@@Shared cluster multitenancy enforces quantitative limits for capacity planning and sizing...","saas/mt_sc_shared_cluster_multitenancy.html@@@Shared cluster multitenancy@@@Shared cluster multitenancy lets a Managed Service Provider serve multiple clients from a single Rubrik cluster while still giving each client a fully dedicated RSC tenant experience...","saas/mt_sc_shared_cluster_replication.html@@@Replication for shared clusters@@@Tenant account administrators can configure replication pairings when one or both clusters in the pairing are shared clusters...","saas/mt_sc_shared_clusters.html@@@Shared clusters@@@Shared clusters provide software-enforced isolation between dedicated tenants provisioned on a single RSC cluster, ensuring data separation and feature parity while maximizing hardware ROI...","saas/mt_sc_smb_workloads_shared_clusters.html@@@SMB workloads on shared clusters@@@On shared clusters, all SMB workload operations require Active Directory authentication. Tenants must register their Active Directory domain before performing any SMB operation, and certain configurations can prevent SMB operations from completing successfully...","saas/mt_sc_tenant_workloads_sc.html@@@Tenant workloads on shared clusters@@@Connecting tenant workloads to a multitenant shared cluster requires planning for network topology, firewall rules, and port access...","saas/mt_sla_domain_management_multitenancy.html@@@SLA Domain management@@@In a multitenant environment, SLA Domains can be assigned to tenant organizations by the global organization administrator during the tenant organization creation or editing process. Tenant organizations can also be provided the ability to create and manage their own SLA Domains...","saas/mt_tenant_comparison.html@@@Tenant comparison@@@Rubrik Security Cloud offers various multitenancy models to support different requirements for resource isolation, administrative autonomy, and access to advanced security applications...","saas/mt_tenant_org_administrator_privileges.html@@@Tenant organization administrator privileges@@@The tenant organization administrator role is assigned specific permissions by the global organization administrator...","saas/mt_tenant_org_details.html@@@Tenant organization details@@@You can view detailed information about the organization such as the storage consumption, tasks, and the usage information, in the organization details page...","saas/mt_tenant_org_in_rsc.html@@@Tenant Organizations in RSC@@@RSC supports tenant organizations with some similarities to and some differences from the tenant organizations support provided on Rubrik clusters...","saas/mt_tenant_org_user_privileges.html@@@Tenant organization user privileges@@@The tenant organization user roles are assigned specific permissions by the tenant organization administrator...","saas/mt_tenant_organizations.html@@@Tenant organizations@@@Tenant organizations in Rubrik Security Cloud are a defined subset of the global organization with specified resources, workloads, SLA Domains, and permissions...","saas/mt_viewing_tenant_org_storage_quota.html@@@Viewing the tenant organization storage quota@@@View the storage consumption of the provisioned Rubrik clusters for the organization...","saas/multi_cluster_rbs.html@@@RBS registration to multiple Rubrik clusters@@@A single RBS host can connect to multiple Rubrik clusters...","saas/multi_region_redundancy_status.html@@@Multi-region redundancy statuses@@@Information about the various redundancy statuses and scenarios in Rubrik Cloud Vault, detailing the transition process during failover and failback to former primary region and re-establishing redundancy to Multi-region...","saas/multiple_archival_policies.html@@@Multiple archival policies@@@RSC enables you to configure an SLA Domain with up to three archival policies for data center workloads and up to two archival policies for cloud-native workloads...","saas/multiple_az_support_cces.html@@@Multiple Availability Zones for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage@@@Multiple Availability Zone support distributes cluster nodes across multiple availability zones within a cloud region to improve infrastructure resiliency...","saas/multiple_key_value_tag_pair.html@@@Multiple key-value tag pair@@@Tag-based assignment automates cloud workload protection by replacing manual selection with dynamic, multi-layered logic. By using multiple key-value pairs, organizations can apply either the AND or the OR condition to precisely target high-risk data while reducing rule complexity...","saas/multiple_key_value_tag_pair_2.html@@@Multiple key-value tag pair@@@Tag-based assignment automates cloud workload protection by replacing manual selection with dynamic, multi-layered logic. By using multiple key-value pairs, organizations can apply either the AND or the OR condition to precisely target high-risk data while reducing rule complexity...","saas/multiple_role_assignment_scenarios.html@@@Multiple role assignment scenarios@@@Information about the permissions when multiple roles are assigned to a user or a group...","saas/nas_cd_license_usage_details.html@@@NAS CD license and usage details@@@Information about the purchased licenses and consumption details of theRubrik NAS Cloud Direct services...","saas/nas_cd_usage_report_transition.html@@@NAS CD Usage report transition@@@Rubrik recommends that you transition from the NAS CD Usage report to the RSC Object Capacity or Object Capacity Over Time reports because Rubrik is deprecating the NAS CD Usage report...","saas/nascd_compliance_report.html@@@NAS CD Compliance report@@@The Rubrik NAS Cloud Direct Compliance report provides information about the compliance status of NAS CD objects. By using this report, you can determine whether the snapshots taken for an object are in compliance with the policy schedule associated with the object...","saas/nascd_creating_object_capacity_over_time_report.html@@@Creating a NAS CD Object Capacity Over Time report@@@Create a report using the NAS CD Object Capacity Over Time report template to retrieve details about the size of a NAS Share and the storage space used to back up the NAS Share over a period of time...","saas/nascd_object_capacity_over_time_report.html@@@NAS CD Object Capacity Over Time report@@@The Rubrik NAS Cloud Direct Object Capacity Over Time report provides details about the size of a NAS Share and the storage space used to back up the NAS Share over a period of time. You can use the Rubrik NAS Cloud Direct Object Capacity Over Time report for insights on your storage consumption for effective resource management and future planning...","saas/nascd_object_capacity_report.html@@@NAS CD Object Capacity report@@@The Rubrik NAS Cloud Direct Object Capacity report provides details about the size of a NAS Share and the storage space used to back up the NAS Share. You can use the Rubrik NAS Cloud Direct Object Capacity report for insights on your storage consumption for effective resource management and future planning...","saas/nascd_protection_report.html@@@NAS CD Protection report@@@The Rubrik NAS Cloud Direct Protection Report shows the protection status of NAS CD on the Reports page. You can use this report to check the health of a backup for data integrity and safety...","saas/nascd_report_details.html@@@NAS CD report details@@@Information about the details you can view in the Rubrik NAS Cloud Direct Protection, Object Capacity, Object Capacity Over Time, and Compliance reports...","saas/ncd_adding_custom_intel_feeds.html@@@Adding custom intel feeds for NAS CD@@@Create a custom intel feed to monitor your NAS CD data sets for specific Indicators of Compromise (IOCs) tailored to the security needs of your organization. While Rubrik provides built-in, vetted threat intelligence, custom feeds enable you to target unique or emerging threats immediately...","saas/ncd_assigning_a_NAS_CD_policy_for_data_obs.html@@@Assigning a NAS CD policy for Data Observability@@@Assign a NAS CD protection policy to a NAS data set for enabling Data Observability...","saas/ncd_creating_a_policy_for_data_obs.html@@@Creating a NAS CD policy for Data Observability@@@Create a NAS CD policy to send backups to a storage target, and use this policy to enable Data Observability features, Data Threat Analytics, and Data Security Posture...","saas/ncd_data_discovery.html@@@Data Security Posture for NAS CD data sets@@@For NAS CD data sets that have a Rubrik Cloud Vault location configured, you can enable Data Security Posture to find data sets matching a specified data policy within snapshots...","saas/ncd_data_observability.html@@@Data Observability for NAS CD data sets@@@To provide Data Observability, you can enable Data Threat Analytics and configure Data Security Posture for NAS CD data sets. Data Threat Analytics detects ransomware attacks and Data Security Posture identifies sensitive data in your NAS CD data sets...","saas/ncd_data_sets.html@@@NAS CD data sets@@@Rubrik NAS Cloud Direct offers secure data protection with high-performance, scalable enterprise backup, and archive services for unstructured file data...","saas/ncd_enabling_ad_rcv_arch_loc.html@@@Enabling Anomaly Detection for RCV archival locations@@@Enable Anomaly Detection for NAS CD data protected by a NAS CD policy or an SLA Domain using a Rubrik Cloud Vault storage target...","saas/ncd_enabling_anomaly_detection_cluster.html@@@Enabling Anomaly Detection for NAS CD clusters@@@Enable Anomaly Detection for NAS CD data protected by a NAS CD policy or an SLA Domain using a Rubrik Cloud Vault storage target or a custom storage provider target...","saas/ncd_enabling_threat_monitoring.html@@@Enabling Threat Monitoring for NAS CD clusters@@@Enable Threat Monitoring for a NAS CD cluster to monitor threats and identify malware infections on your NAS CD backups...","saas/ncd_initiating_threat_hunt_cluster.html@@@Initiating a Threat Hunt for NAS CD clusters@@@Initiate a Turbo Threat Hunt to perform an on-demand scan to identify impacted files when a ransomware attack happens. A turbo-charged Threat Hunt scans for hashes of file types most often used by threat agents...","saas/ncd_unstructured_data_dashboard.html@@@Unstructured Data dashboard@@@The Unstructured Data dashboard in RSC provides a comprehensive data protection summary for all connected clusters, displaying statistics on data collection, archive usage, storage, and the status of protected files and shares...","saas/ncd_unstructured_data_dashboard_2.html@@@Unstructured Data dashboard@@@The Unstructured Data dashboard in RSC provides a comprehensive data protection summary for all connected clusters, displaying statistics on data collection, archive usage, storage, and the status of protected files and shares...","saas/ncd_unstructured_data_dashboard_pane.html@@@Unstructured Data dashboard pane@@@The Unstructured Data dashboard aggregates the backup and restore task information of all NAS CD clusters connected to RSC...","saas/ncd_unstructured_data_dashboard_pane_2.html@@@Unstructured Data dashboard pane@@@The Unstructured Data dashboard aggregates the backup and restore task information of all NAS CD clusters connected to RSC...","saas/ncd_viewing_unstructured_data_dashboard.html@@@Viewing the Unstructured Data dashboard@@@Use the Unstructured Data dashboard to view the backup and restore summary information of the NAS CD clusters connected to RSC...","saas/ncd_viewing_unstructured_data_dashboard_2.html@@@Viewing the Unstructured Data dashboard@@@Use the Unstructured Data dashboard to view the backup and restore summary information of the NAS CD clusters connected to RSC...","saas/netapp_volume_export.html@@@NetApp volume export@@@To allow backups of read-only NetApp volumes, you must first export the volumes through NFS...","saas/network_diagnostics.html@@@Network Diagnostics@@@Through Network Diagnostics, you can check your network status and troubleshoot issues in RSC...","saas/network_prerequisite_govcloud_dca_lck.html@@@Network prerequisites@@@Certain network settings must be completed to onboard AWS GovCloud, DCA, and LCK cloud accounts...","saas/node_removal_cces.html@@@Node removal from Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage@@@You can remove a node from a Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage deployment when you want to scale down the cluster...","saas/node_removal_rsc.html@@@Node removal from RSC@@@You can remove a node from a Rubrik cluster or a supported third-party hardware cluster when you want to repurpose the node or update a cluster configuration during a hardware refresh...","saas/notifications.html@@@Notifications@@@In the Notifications menu, you can configure event email preferences, add webhooks, set up SNMP for network management and monitoring, and create a syslog export rule to enable the Rubrik cluster to send server messages to an external Syslog server...","saas/oar.html@@@RSC Orchestrated Application Recovery@@@The Orchestrated Application Recovery feature automates recovery, including disaster recovery and application migration to a secondary recovery site...","saas/oar_audit_log_filters.html@@@Orchestrated Recovery Audit Log filters@@@The Audit Logs page provides a chronological record of user-initiated actions that occur during Orchestrated Recovery operations, with filtering options to refine the displayed results...","saas/oar_cleaning_up_after_recovery.html@@@Cleaning up after a recovery@@@Clean up a recovery to delete the virtual machines that Orchestrated Recovery provisioned in the target environment during a test failover or cyber recovery...","saas/oar_creating_disaster_rp_ahv.html@@@Creating a disaster Recovery Plan for AHV virtual machines@@@Create a disaster Recovery Plan to orchestrate test and production failovers for a set of AHV virtual machines...","saas/oar_creating_disaster_rp_vsphere.html@@@Creating a disaster Recovery Plan for vSphere virtual machines@@@Create a disaster Recovery Plan to orchestrate test and production failovers for a set of virtual machines...","saas/oar_creating_in_place_rp.html@@@Creating an in-place Recovery Plan@@@Create an in-place Recovery Plan to recover a set of virtual machines on the same Rubrik cluster where the source virtual machines are protected...","saas/oar_evaluate_recovery_options.html@@@Evaluate your recovery options@@@Understanding the available recovery types and approaches for Orchestrated Recovery helps determine the right fit for a given environment and recovery objectives...","saas/oar_event_log_filters.html@@@Orchestrated Recovery Event Log filters@@@The Event Logs page provides a chronological record of operational details that occur during Orchestrated Recovery operations, with filtering options to refine the displayed results...","saas/oar_events.html@@@Orchestrated Recovery events@@@Event logs and audit logs provide a chronological record of automated operational tasks and user actions performed during Orchestrated Recovery, allowing activity monitoring and tracking, and maintaining accountability...","saas/oar_pane.html@@@Orchestrated Recovery pane@@@The Orchestrated Recovery pane of the Global Dashboard provides several interactive elements...","saas/oar_performing_failover.html@@@Performing a failover operation@@@Perform a failover for the virtual machines in the selected Recovery Plan using the specified recovery points...","saas/oar_planning_checklist.html@@@Planning checklist for Orchestrated Recovery@@@You can use this checklist to confirm the prerequisites and configuration decisions for a Recovery Plan before you create one...","saas/oar_preseeding_disks.html@@@Pre-seeding disks for disaster recovery@@@Pre-seeding disks reduces failover time for VMware disaster Recovery Plans by maintaining a warm-standby copy of each protected virtual machine in the target datastore before a disaster occurs...","saas/oar_reports.html@@@Orchestrated Recovery reports@@@RSC generates a PDF report for each completed Orchestrated Recovery recovery. The report summarizes the recovery outcome, timing, and per-object results. You can download reports for 7 days after generation...","saas/oar_rp.html@@@Recovery Plans@@@RSC uses Recovery Plans as templates to store the virtual machine configurations and resource mappings used during recovery...","saas/oar_sizing_rto_rpo.html@@@Sizing, RTO, and RPO@@@Recovery time objective (RTO) and recovery point objective (RPO) for Orchestrated Recovery recoveries depend on your SLA Domain configuration and the RTO optimization method you select when creating a VMware disaster Recovery Plan...","saas/oar_testing_failover.html@@@Testing a failover@@@Test a failover for a selected Recovery Plan using a point in time that you choose...","saas/oar_troubleshooting.html@@@Troubleshooting failed recoveries@@@This reference describes common Orchestrated Recovery recovery failures and the appropriate remediation actions...","saas/oar_vmware_post_script_requirements.html@@@Post-script requirements for VMware virtual machines@@@Supported input formats for the Post Scripts field when creating a Recovery Plan for VMware virtual machines...","saas/object_filters_snapshot_retention.html@@@Object filters for snapshot retention@@@Information about the filters that you can apply to the objects on the Snapshot Retention page. These filters are available on the Data Center and Cloud tabs of the Snapshot Retention page...","saas/object_level_protection_pause_resume.html@@@Object-level protection pause and resume@@@The object-level protection pause and resume feature provides granular control over data protection activities with RSC...","saas/object_level_snapshot_window.html@@@Object-level snapshot windows@@@Object-level snapshot windows let you control when backups run for individual CDM objects, independently of the snapshot window configured in the SLA Domain...","saas/oci_cloud_cluster_rsc.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure protects applications and data by running Rubrik CDM software on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure instances within a virtual private cloud...","saas/oci_downloading_access_token_rsc.html@@@Downloading an access token@@@Generate a secret key and access token to authenticate Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure for a deployment on RSC...","saas/okta_integration.html@@@Okta Identity Threat Protection integration@@@Integration of Okta Identity Threat Protection with Rubrik Security Cloud supports accurate identification of malicious and compromised user accounts within your environment...","saas/okta_integration_workflow.html@@@Okta integration workflow@@@The integration workflow provides a high-level view of the requirements for configuration of SSO with Okta...","saas/on-demand_classification.html@@@On-demand classification@@@On-demand classification jobs run against the most recent snapshot of the specified resources to generate classification results and reports...","saas/on_demand_snapshot_retention_options.html@@@On-demand snapshot retention options@@@When you take an on-demand snapshot, you can choose the retention period by selecting an SLA Domain, by retaining the snapshot according to the SLA Domain currently assigned to the object, or by retaining the snapshot forever...","saas/onelogin_adding_claim_rules.html@@@Adding claim rules for OneLogin@@@Add claim rules to tell OneLogin how to format the claims sent to RSC...","saas/onelogin_configuring_application_details.html@@@Configuring application details@@@Configure the Rubrik Security Cloud application to work with OneLogin...","saas/onelogin_download_onelogin_metadata.html@@@Downloading the OneLogin metadata file@@@Create a custom application connector for RSC in OneLogin, then download the OneLogin metadata file...","saas/onelogin_granting_access_to_rsc.html@@@Granting access to RSC for OneLogin users@@@In the OneLogin UI, grant user access to RSC for OneLogin users...","saas/onelogin_integration_workflow.html@@@OneLogin integration workflow@@@The OneLogin integration workflow provides a high-level view of the tasks involved in configuring single sign-on with OneLogin...","saas/onpr/user_guide/creating_retention_locked_sla_domain.html@@@Creating a retention-locked SLA Domain@@@Create a retention-locked SLA Domain to prevent the retention period and frequency assigned to snapshots protected by the SLA Domain from being reduced...","saas/onpr/user_guide/endpoints_requiring_firewall_access.html@@@Endpoints requiring firewall access@@@To enable the outbound connection to specific endpoints from a Rubrik cluster to RSC, you must open the port 443 on the Rubrik cluster and allow access to the endpoints in the firewall and proxy settings...","saas/onpr/user_guide/inbound_port_requirements.html@@@Inbound port requirements@@@Information about ports required to enable inbound access to RSC...","saas/onpr/user_guide/onpr_adding_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Adding a Rubrik cluster@@@Add a Rubrik cluster to an RSC instance to manage the cluster through the instance...","saas/onpr/user_guide/onpr_configuring_network_settings.html@@@Configuring network settings@@@Rubrik Security Cloud requires network settings you must configure to allow for Internet routing, time information, and secure connections...","saas/onpr/user_guide/onpr_initial_setup.html@@@Initial setup@@@To start using RSC, an administrator adds authorized user accounts before adding Rubrik clusters...","saas/onpr/user_guide/onpr_logging_in_first_time.html@@@Logging in for the first time@@@After the initial login, the administrator account can configure additional users for the RSC instance...","saas/onpr/user_guide/onpr_password_constraints.html@@@Password constraints@@@Password requirements are enforced by the software...","saas/onpr/user_guide/outbound_port_requirements.html@@@Outbound port requirements@@@Information about ports required to enable outbound access from RSC during initial setup...","saas/onpr/user_guide/user_management.html@@@User Management@@@RSC provides role-based access control and various user account authentication methods...","saas/orchestrated_recovery_operating_systems.html@@@Supported operating systems for IP reconfiguration@@@Orchestrated Application Recovery supports static IP reconfiguration for specific operating systems during VMware virtual machine recovery. This topic covers static IP reconfiguration only; Orchestrated Application Recovery supports recovery orchestration for all operating systems supported by the underlying hypervisor...","saas/organization_branding.html@@@Organization branding@@@Organization branding personalizes RSC by displaying a selected custom brand logo for all users in the global organization and associated tenant organizations...","saas/passkeys_mfa.html@@@Passkeys for MFA@@@Passkeys provide an alternative MFA method in RSC using biometrics or hardware security keys to verify identity and enable passwordless login...","saas/password_policy.html@@@Password policy@@@RSC administrators can enhance the security of their RSC domain by using the password policy feature to configure password complexity rules for local users...","saas/pattern_based_recovery.html@@@Prioritized recovery for Amazon S3@@@You can prioritize the recovery of specific Amazon S3 objects using glob patterns to recover your most critical data first. You can also use glob patterns to selectively recover specific objects from your Amazon S3...","saas/pause_resume_cluster_notifications.html@@@Pause and resume Rubrik cluster notifications@@@To improve operational management while performing maintenance work for a Rubrik cluster, you can temporarily pause webhook, email, and event digest notifications...","saas/pause_resume_protection_activity.html@@@Pause and resume protection activity@@@When you are performing maintenance activities on a Rubrik cluster, you can temporarily pause the protection activity and then resume it by using the pause and resume protection activity feature...","saas/pausing_cluster_protection.html@@@Pausing protection activity@@@Pause the protection activity on a Rubrik cluster when performing maintenance activities on the associated applications...","saas/pausing_object_protection.html@@@Pausing object protection@@@Pause protection for specific data-center objects by applying pause directly at the object level or on a parent object...","saas/pausing_resuming_cn.html@@@Pausing and resuming Rubrik cluster notifications@@@Temporarily pause the notification activity on a Rubrik cluster when performing maintenance activities on the associated applications, and then resume it. Pausing notifications prevents you from receiving continuous notifications for expected behavior during maintenance...","saas/pausing_sla_domain_protection.html@@@Pausing SLA Domain protection@@@To temporarily stop protection for specific objects in a Rubrik cluster, pause the protection activity of the SLA Domain that protects those objects. This action only pauses the protection activity for the objects under that SLA Domain, while other objects in the cluster protected by different SLA Domains remain unaffected...","saas/paygo_key_terms.html@@@MSP PayGo licensing terms@@@MSP PayGo licensing uses distinct terms for the PayGo billing program, usage measurement units, and supported Rubrik products...","saas/performing_an_export_from_a_snapshot.html@@@Performing an Export from a snapshot@@@Create a virtual machine from a snapshot for recovery...","saas/performing_bulk_recovery_for_recoveryplans.html@@@Performing bulk recovery for Recovery Plans@@@Recover virtual machines in multiple Recovery Plans...","saas/performing_cyber_recovery_ad_forest.html@@@Performing a cyber recovery for an Active Directory forest using a Recovery Plan@@@Use a cyber recovery plan to recover an Active Directory forest into an isolated VMware environment...","saas/performing_cyber_recovery_ahv_vms.html@@@Performing a cyber recovery for AHV virtual machines using a Recovery Plan@@@Perform a cyber recovery using a Recovery Plan to recover AHV virtual machines into an isolated recovery environment. Recovery can also be conducted to shared infrastructure with IP networks not connected to production environments...","saas/performing_cyber_recovery_aws_vms.html@@@Performing a cyber recovery for AWS EC2 instances using a Recovery Plan@@@Perform a cyber recovery using a Recovery Plan to recover AWS EC2 instances to a target recovery environment...","saas/performing_cyber_recovery_azure_vms.html@@@Performing a cyber recovery for Azure virtual machines using a Recovery Plan@@@Perform a cyber recovery using a Recovery Plan to recover Azure virtual machines to a target recovery environment...","saas/performing_cyber_recovery_export_ahv.html@@@Performing a cyber recovery using Export on AHV virtual machines@@@Perform an export to recover selected AHV virtual machines to a local or remote, isolated recovery environment. You can also recover to shared infrastructure with IP networks that are not connected to production environments...","saas/performing_cyber_recovery_export_aws.html@@@Performing a cyber recovery using Export on AWS EC2 instances@@@Perform a cyber recovery to recover AWS EC2 instances to a target recovery environment without using a pre-existing Recovery Plan. You can save your recovery specifications as a Recovery Plan for future use...","saas/performing_cyber_recovery_export_azure.html@@@Performing a cyber recovery using Export on Azure virtual machines@@@Perform a cyber recovery to recover Azure virtual machines to a target recovery environment without using a pre-existing Recovery Plan. You can save your recovery specifications as a Recovery Plan for future use...","saas/performing_cyber_recovery_export_vsphere.html@@@Performing a cyber recovery using Export on vSphere virtual machines@@@Perform an export to recover selected vSphere virtual machines to a local or remote, isolated recovery environment. You can also recover to shared infrastructure with IP networks that are not connected to production environments...","saas/performing_cyber_recovery_live_mount.html@@@Performing a cyber recovery using Live Mount on vSphere and AHV virtual machines@@@Perform a cyber recovery using Live Mount to restore selected virtual machines to a local or remote recovery environment. You can also recover to shared infrastructure with IP networks that are not connected to production environments...","saas/performing_cyber_recovery_vsphere.html@@@Performing a cyber recovery for vSphere virtual machines using a Recovery Plan@@@Perform a cyber recovery using a Recovery Plan to recover vSphere virtual machines into an isolated recovery environment. Recovery can also be conducted to shared infrastructure with IP networks not connected to production environments...","saas/performing_disaster_recovery.html@@@Performing a disaster recovery@@@Use a Recovery Plan to recover virtual machines to a recovery site during disaster recovery or application migration...","saas/performing_failback_rcv_arch_loc.html@@@Performing a failback for RCV archival location@@@To restore your Rubrik Cloud Vault to its original configuration, perform a failback from the secondary region to the primary region for archival locations with Multi-region redundancy. This step re-establishes the primary region as the active one, ensuring that normal data operations resume after a failover...","saas/performing_failover_operation.html@@@Performing a failover operation@@@Perform a failover for the virtual machines in the selected Recovery Plan using the specified recovery points...","saas/performing_in_place_recovery.html@@@Performing an in-place recovery@@@Perform an in-place recovery to replace the virtual machines specified by a Recovery Plan with point-in-time copies...","saas/performing_prerestore_system_copy.html@@@Performing pre-restore steps for system copy restore@@@Run the pre-restore script for the SAP HANA host using the CLI...","saas/performing_prerestore_system_copy_ui.html@@@Performing pre-restore steps for system copy restore using RSC@@@Configure the system copy to get the SAP HANA system ready for system copy restore using RSC...","saas/performing_vm_instant_recovery.html@@@Performing an Instant Recovery of a vSphere virtual machine@@@Replace the source virtual machine with a new virtual machine created from the selected snapshot...","saas/permissions_reqs_ms_teams.html@@@Teams enterprise application permissions@@@Permission requirements for RSC operations using the Microsoft 365 API and Teams...","saas/permissions_reqs_ms_teams_2.html@@@Teams enterprise application permissions@@@Permission requirements for RSC operations using the Microsoft 365 API and Teams...","saas/personal_access_tokens.html@@@Personal access tokens@@@Personal access tokens enable RSC users to authenticate to the RSC API under their own identity, outside of the RSC web UI...","saas/placing_legal_hold_cloud_snapshot.html@@@Placing a legal hold on a cloud-native snapshot@@@Place a legal hold on a cloud-native snapshot to prevent it from expiring while it is subject to a legal or compliance requirement...","saas/placing_legal_hold_m365_snapshot.html@@@Placing a legal hold on a Microsoft 365 snapshot@@@Place a legal hold on a Microsoft 365 snapshot to prevent it from expiring while it is subject to a legal or compliance requirement...","saas/placing_legal_hold_sap_hana.html@@@Placing SAP HANA snapshots on legal hold@@@To prevent the Rubrik cluster from expiring and removing the snapshots of SAP HANA databases, place a legal hold on the snapshots listed on the SAP HANA inventory page...","saas/placing_legal_hold_snapshot.html@@@Placing a legal hold on a snapshot@@@Placing a legal hold on a snapshot indefinitely retains that snapshot...","saas/plan_orchestrated_recovery.html@@@Plan a recovery@@@Before you create a Recovery Plan, you can review the recovery options, prerequisites, permissions, and sizing guidance for Orchestrated Recovery...","saas/prereq_adding_teams_rsc.html@@@Prerequisites for Teams accounts in RSC@@@Information about the prerequisites for adding Microsoft Teams accounts in RSC...","saas/prereqs_crowdstrike_threat_intel.html@@@Prerequisites for CrowdStrike Threat Intel integration@@@Licensing, API access, and regional requirements for connecting CrowdStrike Threat Intel to RSC...","saas/prereqs_taxii_threat_intel.html@@@Prerequisites for TAXII threat intel integration@@@TAXII server, authentication, and role requirements for connecting a TAXII threat intel source to RSC...","saas/prerequisites_for_sap_hana_protection.html@@@Prerequisites for SAP HANA protection@@@There are a number of prerequisites that you must complete to protect SAP HANA systems...","saas/prerequisites_servicenow.html@@@Prerequisites for Data Security Posture ServiceNow integration@@@The Data Security Posture ServiceNow integration from RSC has specific prerequisites...","saas/private_access_azr_snapshot.html@@@Private access to an Azure snapshot@@@When the public access network policy for an Azure disk is not enabled and you want RSC to access a snapshot using the private access network policy, you must include specific permission categories for the associated Azure subscription and Exocompute so that RSC can access the snapshot...","saas/private_container_registry.html@@@Private Container Registry for AWS@@@For security purposes, when you do not want to retrieve Docker images from a registry hosted by Rubrik, you can configure a Private Container Registry to retrieve these Docker images from a registry hosted by you...","saas/privileged_access_management.html@@@Privileged access management@@@You can create and manage API credentials to use with the Privileged Access Management solution...","saas/protection_hierarchy_for_sap_hana.html@@@Protection hierarchy for SAP HANA objects@@@RSC provides hierarchy-based, automatic protection of SAP HANA objects...","saas/provisioning_aws_cces.html@@@Provisioning Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on AWS@@@Provision and deploy Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services from RSC to protect applications and data on Amazon EC2 instances within a virtual private cloud...","saas/provisioning_azure_cc_es.html@@@Provisioning Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Azure@@@Provision and deploy Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure from RSC to protect applications and data within a Microsoft Azure virtual network...","saas/provisioning_gcp_cces_rsc.html@@@Provisioning Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on GCP@@@Provision Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Google Cloud Platform from RSC to protect applications and data within your Google Cloud project...","saas/provisioning_oci_cces_rsc.html@@@Provisioning Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI@@@Provision Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure from RSC to protect applications and data by running Rubrik CDM software on OCI instances within a virtual cloud network (VCN)...","saas/qauth_for_rcv.html@@@Quorum authorization for Rubrik Cloud Vault management actions@@@You can protect the management actions on your Rubrik Cloud Vault locations using quorum authorization. When enabled, quorum authorization requires the requesters of the protected actions to obtain additional approvals to perform the requested actions...","saas/quarantine.html@@@Quarantine overview@@@The Quarantine feature in Data Threat Analytics isolates potentially malicious files or objects to support data recovery and avoid reinfection...","saas/quarantining_matched_objects_or_files.html@@@Quarantining matched files or objects@@@Quarantine a matched file or object indicated in a threat hunt to separate potentially malicious objects or files before proceeding with recovery...","saas/rbac_anomaly_detection.html@@@RBAC for Anomaly Detection@@@Information about the privileges available to manage role-based access control for Anomaly Detection...","saas/rbac_data_impact_investigation.html@@@RBAC for data impact investigation@@@Information about the privileges required to access and use the data impact investigation feature in Anomaly Detection...","saas/rbac_orchestrated_recovery.html@@@RBAC for Orchestrated Application Recovery@@@Viewing and managing Recovery Plans and recoveries in Orchestrated Recovery require RBAC privileges...","saas/rbac_permissions_for_quarantine.html@@@RBAC privileges for quarantine@@@RBAC privileges are required to remove files or objects from quarantine, bypass quarantine, and download files for forensic analysis...","saas/rbac_privileges_threat_hunt.html@@@RBAC privileges for threat hunt@@@RBAC privileges are required to create a threat hunt and view threat hunt results...","saas/rbac_troubleshooting_permissions.html@@@Troubleshooting permissions@@@Information about how you can troubleshoot permission issues when a user or service account cannot perform an intended task...","saas/rbk_cdm_soft_upgrade_rsc.html@@@Rubrik CDM software upgrade using RSC@@@To take advantage of the latest features and improvements that Rubrik offers, you can upgrade the Rubrik CDM version running on any connected Rubrik cluster to the latest version using RSC...","saas/rbk_cdm_software_upgrade.html@@@Rubrik CDM software upgrade@@@Upgrading Rubrik CDM software provides the latest features, security updates, and performance improvements for Rubrik clusters...","saas/rbk_refreshing_reader_location_objects.html@@@Refreshing reader location objects@@@Use RSC to update a reader cluster with the latest snapshot metadata...","saas/rbs_host_registration_multiple_clusters.html@@@Host registration with RBS on multiple clusters@@@A Rubrik Backup Service host can be registered to multiple Rubrik clusters by adding the host to both source and target clusters...","saas/rcca_signed_rba_certificates.html@@@Rubrik CA-signed RBA certificates@@@You can use the Rubrik Cluster Certificate Authority to sign Rubrik Backup Agent certificates to establish a centralized root of trust for secure communication with Rubrik CDM clusters. This transition streamlines trust management, ensures centralized lifecycle control, and enables automated certificate renewals...","saas/rcv_aws_config.html@@@RCV configuration on AWS@@@Information about configuring Rubrik Cloud Vault locations on AWS...","saas/rcv_aws_reader_network_settings.html@@@Configuring network settings for AWS RCV reader locations@@@When connecting a reader cluster to an AWS RCV location that has private connectivity or an IP allow list configured, configure matching network settings during the Connect As Reader wizard...","saas/rcv_azure_config.html@@@RCV configuration on Azure@@@Information about configuring Rubrik Cloud Vault locations on Azure...","saas/rcv_azure_converting_immutable_loc.html@@@Converting Azure RCV locations to immutable@@@Convert non-immutable Rubrik Cloud Vault locations on Azure to immutable locations...","saas/rcv_best_practices.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault best practices@@@Information about the Rubrik Cloud Vault best practices, which aim to optimize data protection and compliance...","saas/rcv_blob_immutability_azure.html@@@Blob-level immutability for RCV locations on Azure@@@RSC applies blob-level immutability, by default, to the Rubrik Cloud Vault locations created for data center workloads on Rubrik clusters running CDM version 9.1 and later...","saas/rcv_cloud_native_workloads.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault specifications for cloud-native workloads@@@Before creating a Rubrik Cloud Vault (RCV) location, Rubrik recommends that you review the RCV specifications related to the cloud-native workloads to prevent potential issues...","saas/rcv_config_rubrik_hosted_migration.html@@@Configuring Rubrik-hosted migration@@@Configure your environment to permit the Rubrik-hosted DataSync service to read data from AWS S3 or on-premises S3-compatible stores...","saas/rcv_configuring_aws_private_connectivity.html@@@Enabling AWS private connectivity for an existing RCV location@@@Enable AWS VPC interface endpoints on an existing Rubrik Cloud Vault location for data center workloads to route archival traffic over private network paths. You must disable the location before making changes to its network settings...","saas/rcv_configuring_azure_private_endpoint.html@@@Enabling Azure private endpoints for an existing RCV location@@@Create an Azure private endpoint for an existing Rubrik Cloud Vault location for data center workloads to route archival traffic over the Azure backbone network instead of the public internet. You must disable the location before you create a private endpoint...","saas/rcv_configuring_cust_hosted_migration.html@@@Configuring customer-hosted migration@@@Configure the security permissions required for AWS DataSync to move data, including fetching bucket names, creating IAM roles, and registering destination roles with RSC...","saas/rcv_connecting_reader_location.html@@@Connecting a reader location@@@Connect a secondary Rubrik cluster to an existing RCV location as a reader to provide read-only access to archived data...","saas/rcv_converting_backup_to_archive_tier.html@@@Converting an RCV location to the Archive tier@@@Convert an existing cloud-native Rubrik Cloud Vault location from the Backup tier to the Archive tier to support long-term data retention and compliance requirements...","saas/rcv_converting_location_tier.html@@@Converting an RCV location to the Recovery tier@@@Convert an existing cloud-native Rubrik Cloud Vault location from the Backup tier to the Recovery tier to support advanced security operations...","saas/rcv_converting_redundancy.html@@@Converting RCV redundancy@@@Convert the storage redundancy of an existing RCV on Azure Backup tier location to meet security or compliance requirements...","saas/rcv_creating_loc_for_ncd_azure.html@@@Creating RCV locations for NAS CD objects on Azure@@@Create a Rubrik Cloud Vault location on Azure for assigning to NAS CD objects...","saas/rcv_creating_rcv_cn_workloads_azure.html@@@Creating RCV locations for cloud-native workloads on Azure@@@Create a Rubrik Cloud Vault location on Azure to archive the backups of cloud-native workloads...","saas/rcv_creating_rcv_cn_workloads_azure_2.html@@@Creating RCV locations for cloud-native workloads on Azure@@@Create a Rubrik Cloud Vault location on Azure to archive the backups of cloud-native workloads...","saas/rcv_creating_rcv_dc_workloads_azure.html@@@Creating RCV locations for data center workloads on Azure@@@Create a Rubrik Cloud Vault location on Azure, assign it to a Rubrik cluster, and configure encryption with an Azure Key Vault or RSA Key for archiving backups of data center workloads...","saas/rcv_cust_managed_migration_process.html@@@Customer-hosted migration process@@@You can migrate an archival location to RCV by running the migration tool in your own AWS environment...","saas/rcv_dashboard.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault dashboard@@@The Rubrik Cloud Vault dashboard in RSC displays the data protection and usage summary of all the Rubrik Cloud Vault locations connected to RSC...","saas/rcv_dashboard_info.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault dashboard information@@@The Rubrik Cloud Vault dashboard aggregates the backup, storage, and license information for all the Rubrik Cloud Vault locations connected to RSC...","saas/rcv_data_protection_sla_domain.html@@@RCV data protection using SLA Domain@@@You can configure a Rubrik Cloud Vault location as the archival or backup destination of an SLA Domain...","saas/rcv_deleting_locations.html@@@Deleting RCV locations@@@Delete a Rubrik Cloud Vault location when you do not need the archived data...","saas/rcv_details.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault details@@@The Rubrik Cloud Vaults page displays detailed information for each Rubrik Cloud Vault location and provides filters to find locations based on various criteria...","saas/rcv_disabling_locations.html@@@Disabling RCV locations@@@You can stop a Rubrik Cloud Vault location from archiving and any other background operations that can change data on the archival location...","saas/rcv_editing_locations.html@@@Editing RCV locations@@@Edit a Rubrik Cloud Vault location to modify settings such as the location name, proxy configuration, private endpoints or VPC interface endpoints, or IP allow list. Editable settings vary by cloud provider, such as Azure, AWS, or GCP, and location type, such as data center, cloud-native, or NAS Cloud Direct...","saas/rcv_enabling_rbk_clus_resolve_str_url.html@@@Enabling the Rubrik cluster to resolve the storage URL@@@Enable the Rubrik cluster to resolve the storage URL to the private IP address of the endpoint. This is required to use Rubrik Cloud Vault with a private endpoint...","saas/rcv_encryption_options.html@@@RCV encryption options@@@RSC supports client-side encryption for data center RCV locations and server-side encryption for cloud-native protection and NAS Cloud Direct RCV locations...","saas/rcv_evaluate_options_loc_creation.html@@@Evaluation of options for RCV location creation@@@When creating a Rubrik Cloud Vault location, it is important to evaluate the available options for adding the location. By evaluating these options, you can ensure that your data protection strategy is cost-effective, resilient, and aligned with your recovery objectives...","saas/rcv_failover_azure.html@@@Failover for RCV on Azure@@@The failover process for Rubrik Cloud Vault ensures continuous data availability during regional outages and disasters by switching between primary and secondary regions configured with Multi-region redundancy...","saas/rcv_finalizing_customer_hosted_migration.html@@@Finalizing customer-hosted migration@@@After the data transfer is complete, perform the final configuration and validation steps to finalize the migration to the RCV location...","saas/rcv_finalizing_rbk_hosted_migration.html@@@Finalizing Rubrik-hosted migration@@@Finalize the migration by coordinating with the Rubrik Professional Services team to convert metadata, run conversion commands, and re-enable the archival location...","saas/rcv_finding_azure_allowlist.html@@@Finding RCV location endpoints for allowlisting@@@Find the list of endpoints that you need to allowlist to streamline restricting network traffic to trusted Rubrik Cloud Vault location endpoints...","saas/rcv_gcp_config.html@@@Configuration of RCV on GCP@@@Information about configuring Rubrik Cloud Vault locations on GCP...","saas/rcv_immutability_conv_azure_loc.html@@@Immutability conversion for Azure RCV locations@@@Using RSC, you can convert non-immutable data center RCV locations on Azure to immutable locations...","saas/rcv_license_management.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault license management@@@Monitor your RCV storage consumption, view the storage runway and forecast, receive notifications at consumption thresholds, and replace licenses when required...","saas/rcv_license_replacement.html@@@RCV license replacement@@@You can replace an existing Rubrik Cloud Vault license with a new license mid-term, ensuring backup and archiving continuity during the transition...","saas/rcv_license_usage_details.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault license and usage details@@@The Rubrik Cloud Vault Licenses and Usage page tracks purchased license capacity and consumption across storage tiers and redundancy options...","saas/rcv_loc_data_recovery.html@@@Data recovery from RCV locations@@@You can recover your data from the Rubrik Cloud Vault locations in the event of a cyber incident or a disaster recovery scenario...","saas/rcv_location_management.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault location management@@@RSC provides different options to manage your Rubrik Cloud Vault locations...","saas/rcv_managing_private_endpoints.html@@@Managing private endpoints@@@Manage your private endpoints by adding, modifying, or deleting them...","saas/rcv_migration_workflow.html@@@RCV migration workflow@@@Migration of archival locations to Rubrik Cloud Vault involves specific responsibilities for both the customer and Rubrik Professional Services, depending on whether the workflow is customer-hosted or Rubrik-hosted...","saas/rcv_networking.html@@@RCV network connectivity@@@All Rubrik Cloud Vault (RCV) locations require allowlisted network endpoints, and additional options such as private connectivity depend on whether the location serves data center, Cloud Native Protection, or NAS Cloud Direct workloads...","saas/rcv_networking_all_locations.html@@@Networking for all RCV locations@@@You must allowlist specific endpoints in your network for all RCV locations. Depending on your location type, additional networking configuration may also be required...","saas/rcv_networking_cnp.html@@@Networking for Cloud Native Protection workloads@@@Cloud Native Protection (CNP) RCV locations support Azure private endpoints to secure archival traffic within your Azure virtual network...","saas/rcv_networking_dc.html@@@Networking for data center workloads@@@This topic describes how to secure archival traffic between your Rubrik clusters and RCV locations for data center workloads by using Azure private endpoints or AWS private connectivity, and how to configure proxy, IP allow list, and reader cluster network settings...","saas/rcv_networking_ncd.html@@@Networking for NAS Cloud Direct workloads@@@NAS Cloud Direct (NCD) RCV locations on Azure support Azure private endpoints. No additional networking configuration is available in RSC for NCD locations...","saas/rcv_notifications.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault notifications@@@Rubrik sends notifications about storage capacity usage and subscription status for Rubrik Cloud Vault locations. These notifications ensure that you can take timely actions to maintain service availability and data protection...","saas/rcv_object_immutability_aws.html@@@Object-level immutability for RCV locations on AWS@@@RSC applies object-level immutability, by default, to the Rubrik Cloud Vault locations created for data center workloads on Rubrik clusters running CDM version 9.3.1 or later...","saas/rcv_object_immutability_gcp.html@@@Object-level immutability for RCV locations on GCP@@@RSC applies object-level immutability by default to all Rubrik Cloud Vault locations on GCP. No configuration is required...","saas/rcv_options_resolve_storage_url.html@@@Options to resolve the storage URL@@@To use Rubrik Cloud Vault with a private endpoint, the Rubrik cluster must be able to resolve the storage URL to the private IP address of the endpoint created...","saas/rcv_page.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vaults page@@@The Rubrik Cloud Vaults page provides a list of all available archival locations and the actions that RSC supports for each location...","saas/rcv_pausing_locations.html@@@Pausing RCV locations@@@You can pause a Rubrik Cloud Vault location to temporarily stop the archiving jobs on the Rubrik Cloud Vault locations...","saas/rcv_performing_failover_cn_arch_loc.html@@@Performing a failover for cloud native archival location@@@To ensure data availability during a disaster, perform a failover from the primary region to the secondary region for cloud native archival locations with Multi-region redundancy. The failover process shifts data operations to the secondary region, protecting against regional outages and minimizing downtime...","saas/rcv_performing_failover_dc_arch_loc.html@@@Performing a failover for data center archival locations@@@To ensure data availability during a disaster, perform a failover from the primary region to the secondary region for data center archival locations with Multi-region redundancy. The failover process shifts data operations to the secondary region, protecting against regional outages and minimizing downtime...","saas/rcv_prep_location_creation.html@@@Preparation for RCV location creation@@@Before using Rubrik Cloud Vault, you must understand the options available for creating an RCV location to ensure optimal data protection and recovery...","saas/rcv_prep_rubrik_hosted_migration.html@@@Prepare for Rubrik-hosted migration@@@Prepare for a Rubrik-hosted migration by validating source location eligibility, disabling the source archival location, and configuring encryption settings...","saas/rcv_preparing_customer_hosted_migration.html@@@Preparing for customer-hosted migration@@@Prepare the source location for migration by validating source location eligibility, disabling the archival location, and updating the encryption key...","saas/rcv_prereq_arch_loc_migration.html@@@Prerequisites for migrating archival locations to RCV@@@Before migrating your data center archival location to Rubrik Cloud Vault, ensure your source location, Rubrik cluster, and SLA Domain configurations meet all requirements...","saas/rcv_rbk_managed_migration_process.html@@@Rubrik-hosted migration process@@@You can migrate an archival location to RCV by authorizing Rubrik to run the migration tool within the Rubrik AWS environment...","saas/rcv_redundancy_conversion.html@@@RCV redundancy conversion@@@You can convert the storage redundancy of an existing RCV Backup tier location on Azure to a different type...","saas/rcv_reqs_using_private_endpoint.html@@@Requirements for using a private endpoint with Rubrik Cloud Vault@@@Connecting a private endpoint to send data to Rubrik Cloud Vault over a private connection has specific requirements...","saas/rcv_rubrik_cloud_vault.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault is a Rubrik-managed cloud service that provides isolated and immutable copies of protected data, enhancing cyber resiliency...","saas/rcv_running_cust_hosted_migration.html@@@Running the customer-hosted migration task@@@Create and start the AWS DataSync transfer task to migrate data from the source location to the destination RCV bucket...","saas/rcv_running_rbk_hosted_migration.html@@@Running Rubrik-hosted migration task@@@After the Rubrik Professional Services team finalizes the configuration, they run the migration task while you monitor its progress to completion...","saas/rcv_runway_forecast_details.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault storage forecast and runway@@@The Rubrik Cloud Vault storage forecast and runway help you monitor storage consumption trends and plan capacity upgrades before your RCV license reaches its limit...","saas/rcv_secure_connectivity_azr_pe.html@@@Secure connectivity with Azure private endpoints@@@For data center workloads, an Azure private endpoint in your own Azure tenant sends data from your Rubrik clusters to RCV over a private connection, such as ExpressRoute, instead of the public internet...","saas/rcv_security.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault security@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault adheres to security standards for the protection of archived backups...","saas/rcv_security_dc_workloads.html@@@RCV security for data center workloads@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault adheres to security standards for the protection of archived backups from data center workloads...","saas/rcv_storage_redundancy.html@@@RCV storage redundancy@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault offers various storage redundancy options across different cloud platforms to meet your data availability and durability targets. These options provide protection against hardware failures, network outages, and natural disasters...","saas/rcv_storage_tiers.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault storage tiers@@@Information about Rubrik Cloud Vault storage tiers, which include backup, archive, and recovery tiers, each with corresponding retention periods, access times, and immutability features to meet various data storage requirements...","saas/rcv_supported_workloads_recovery_tier.html@@@Supported workloads for RCV Recovery tier@@@The Recovery tier in Rubrik Cloud Vault is restricted to supported cloud-native workloads to facilitate orchestrated recovery. This allows for periodic recovery testing to support compliance and cyber preparedness...","saas/rcv_usage_calculation.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Vault usage calculation@@@RSC calculates PayGo usage for Rubrik Cloud Vault (RCV) in Back-End Terabytes...","saas/rcv_viewing_dashboard.html@@@Viewing the RCV dashboard@@@View the Rubrik Cloud Vault dashboard for backup and archive summary information related to all the Rubrik Cloud Vault locations connected to RSC...","saas/rcv_viewing_rcv_page.html@@@Viewing the Rubrik Cloud Vaults page@@@View the Rubrik Cloud Vaults page to access Rubrik Cloud Vault locations...","saas/rcv_viewing_runway_forecast.html@@@Viewing the Rubrik Cloud Vault runway and forecast@@@View the Rubrik Cloud Vault storage runway and the 3-month consumption forecast from the RCV dashboard to plan additional purchases or reduce usage before backups are affected...","saas/rcv_workloads_protection.html@@@Protection of workloads in RCV@@@You can protect your workloads in the Rubrik Cloud Vault locations by assigning SLA Domains to your workloads...","saas/reconnecting_disconnected_cluster.html@@@Reconnecting to a Rubrik cluster@@@Reestablish a secure connection with a Rubrik cluster...","saas/recover_orchestrated_recovery.html@@@Recover@@@You can recover virtual machines with Orchestrated Recovery by using a Recovery Plan, by running a cyber recovery without a plan, or by performing failover operations...","saas/recovering_files_folders_aws.html@@@Recovering files or folders from an EC2 snapshot@@@Recover files or folders from EC2 instances or EBS volumes to an S3 bucket if the files that you want to access are deleted, corrupted, or encrypted...","saas/recovering_files_folders_to_azr_storage_account.html@@@Recovering files or folders to an Azure storage account@@@Recover files or folders from Azure virtual machines or managed disks to an Azure storage account if the files that you want to access are deleted, corrupted, or encrypted...","saas/recovering_files_from_a_snapmirror_cloud_snapshot.html@@@Recovering files from a SnapMirror Cloud snapshot@@@Recover a selected set of files on a SnapMirror Cloud archival location to a specified destination...","saas/recovering_files_relic_ec2_instance_or_ebs_volume_snapshots.html@@@Recovering files from relic EC2 instance or EBS volume snapshots@@@Recover relic EC2 instances or EBS volumes from the selected snapshots...","saas/recovering_from_smc_to_existing_volume.html@@@Recovering a volume from a SnapMirror Cloud snapshot to an existing volume@@@Recover a volume from a snapshot to an existing empty volume...","saas/recovering_from_smc_to_new_volume.html@@@Recovering a volume from a SnapMirror Cloud snapshot to a new volume@@@Recover a volume from a snapshot to a newly created volume on a NetApp host...","saas/recovering_impacted_files.html@@@Recovering impacted files and folders@@@Recover a specific set of files or folders impacted by a deletion or encryption event, without recovering the entire object...","saas/recovering_mulitple_VMs_using_Live_Mounts.html@@@Recovering bulk vSphere VMs to current compute resources@@@Use Instant Recovery to recover multiple vSphere virtual machines with Exports to current compute resources. Instant Recovery is a workflow option that you can use to quickly replace a source virtual machine with a new virtual machine using a snapshot...","saas/recovering_rubrik_cc_es_aws.html@@@Recovering Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services@@@Recover Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services. You can do this only when you cannot recover the cluster nodes by other means and the cluster has immutability enabled...","saas/recovering_rubrik_cc_es_azure.html@@@Recovering Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Recover Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure to restore data even when you cannot retrieve the nodes...","saas/recovering_rubrik_cc_es_gcp.html@@@Recovering Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on GCP@@@Recover Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Google Cloud Platform to restore data even when you cannot retrieve the nodes...","saas/recovering_sap_hana_storage_snapshot.html@@@Recovering an SAP HANA storage snapshot@@@Recover an SAP HANA storage snapshot using RSC to create storage and make that storage available on the SAP HANA system primary host at a non-disruptive temporary path. Then, an SAP HANA database administrator can mount the recovered storage to the data volume path and recover the databases using SAP HANA cockpit and storage system tools...","saas/recovering_vm_file_guest_os_creds.html@@@Recovering a virtual machine file using guest OS credentials@@@Recover a virtual machine file through VMware Tools using guest OS credentials. You can use guest OS credentials to recover files to guest operating systems that do not have the RBS installed...","saas/recovering_vm_when_CDP_Filter_installed.html@@@Recovering a virtual machine with a CDP-enabled SLA Domain@@@Recover a virtual machine from the latest point in time or a specific point in time when an SLA Domain with CDP has been assigned...","saas/recovery_information.html@@@Recovery information@@@The Recoveries page provides information about the outcomes of Recovery Plan recoveries...","saas/recovery_plan_details.html@@@Recovery Plan details@@@The Recovery Plan details page provides information about the configured Recovery Plan...","saas/recovery_plan_page_actions.html@@@Actions available for Recovery Plans@@@The Recovery Plans page provides a detailed overview of the Recovery Plans as well as options to search, create, and recover...","saas/recovery_plan_states.html@@@Recovery plan states@@@Recovery plan statuses indicate the current state of a plan and determine which actions are available on the Recovery Plans page...","saas/recovery_secondary_mssql_host.html@@@Recovery to a secondary Microsoft SQL Server host@@@You can add a secondary Microsoft SQL Server host to a Rubrik cluster to provide more target options for snapshot recovery...","saas/recovery_using_rp.html@@@Recovery using a Recovery Plan@@@Recovery Plans define how RSC recovers virtual machines, including boot order, network configuration, and the recovery point to use...","saas/recovery_without_rp.html@@@Recovery without using a Recovery Plan@@@Using the Cyber Recovery wizard, you can select and recover objects on demand even without a Recovery Plan...","saas/reference_orchestrated_recovery.html@@@Reference@@@You can look up Recovery Plans and Recoveries page descriptions, Recovery Plan states, and post-script requirements for Orchestrated Recovery...","saas/refreshing_standalone_esxi_host.html@@@Refreshing a standalone ESXi host@@@Refresh the status of a connected standalone ESXi host to update its configuration and data for accurate management and protection...","saas/reg_supporting_multi_zone_rcv_gcp.html@@@GCP regions supporting multi-zone redundancy@@@Information about GCP regions that support multi-zone redundancy for Rubrik Cloud Vault...","saas/reg_supporting_single_multi_zone_rcv_aws.html@@@AWS regions supporting single and multi-zone redundancy@@@Information about the supported tiers and redundancy options for Rubrik Cloud Vault on AWS...","saas/regions_supporting_multi_region_rcv.html@@@Azure regions supporting multi-region redundancy for RCV@@@Information about Azure regional pairs across North America, South America, Europe, and APAC that support multi-region storage for Rubrik Cloud Vault...","saas/regions_supporting_multi_zone_rcv.html@@@Azure regions supporting multi-zone redundancy for RCV@@@Information about Azure regions across North America, South America, APAC, and EMEA that support multi-zone storage for Rubrik Cloud Vault, including specific regional support information...","saas/regions_supporting_single_zone_rcv.html@@@Azure regions supporting single zone redundancy for RCV@@@Information about Azure regions across North America, South America, EMEA, and APAC that support single zone redundancy for Rubrik Cloud Vault, providing the details about the availability of backup and archive tiers and their respective license bundles...","saas/registering_rbs_host.html@@@Registering a virtual machine running RBS@@@After installing RBS on a virtual machine, register the virtual machine with RSC. Registering the virtual machine enables RSC to coordinate backup operations with RBS...","saas/registering_rbs_host_2.html@@@Registering a virtual machine running RBS@@@After installing RBS on a virtual machine, register the virtual machine with RSC. Registering the virtual machine enables RSC to coordinate backup operations with RBS...","saas/registering_rbs_host_3.html@@@Registering a virtual machine running RBS@@@After installing RBS on a virtual machine, register the virtual machine with RSC. Registering the virtual machine enables RSC to coordinate backup operations with RBS...","saas/rekey_m365_keys.html@@@Rekey for Microsoft 365 keys@@@You can perform a rekey of the master key or intermediate key for Microsoft 365 to update your encryption key to an alternative encryption key. This ensures that your data location uses up-to-date encryption...","saas/rekeying_a_data_center_archival_location.html@@@Rekeying a data center archival location@@@Perform a rekey of the master key and/or root key to update your encryption key to an alternative encryption key. This ensures that your data location uses up-to-date encryption...","saas/rekeying_cnp_archival_location.html@@@Rekeying a cloud archival location@@@Rekey a client-side encrypted cloud archival location to replace the KMS key that protects it, without re-encrypting the archived data...","saas/relic_ec2_instance_or_ebs_volume.html@@@Relic EC2 instance or EBS volume@@@When an EC2 instance or EBS volume is deleted from AWS and is still available on RSC, that instance or volume is no longer managed or protected by any SLA Domain...","saas/relic_virtual_machine.html@@@Relic Azure virtual machine@@@RSC archives inactive Azure virtual machines...","saas/removed_on_demand_instance_or_volume_snapshot.html@@@Removed on-demand snapshots of EC2 instances or EBS volumes@@@Removed on-demand EC2 instance or EBS volume snapshots are snapshots that are deleted from an AWS account...","saas/removing_allowlisted_domain_email.html@@@Removing an allowlisted domain or email address@@@Remove a domain or email address from the RSC Domain and Email Allowlist page...","saas/removing_cdm_admin_ssh_keys.html@@@Removing SSH keys for the CDM admin user@@@Remove one or more SSH public keys from the admin account on a Rubrik cluster from RSC...","saas/removing_crowdstrike_threat_intel.html@@@Removing a CrowdStrike Threat Intel source@@@Remove a CrowdStrike Threat Intel source from RSC when you no longer want Threat Monitoring to use indicators of compromise from your CrowdStrike feed...","saas/removing_custom_intel_feed.html@@@Removing a custom intel feed@@@Remove a custom intel feed when it no longer meets your requirements...","saas/removing_deleted_on_demand_instance_or_volume_snapshots.html@@@Removing deleted on-demand snapshots of EC2 instance or EBS volume@@@Remove deleted on-demand snapshots of EC2 instances or EBS volumes from RSC after they are deleted from an AWS account...","saas/removing_ioc_from_custom_intel_feed.html@@@Removing an IOC from a custom intel feed@@@When you do not agree with the indicators of compromise results or the indicator of compromise is too noisy, remove it from custom intel feed...","saas/removing_legal_hold_cloud_snapshot.html@@@Removing legal hold from a cloud-native snapshot@@@Remove legal hold from a cloud-native snapshot to return it to normal SLA Domain retention management...","saas/removing_legal_hold_m365_snapshot.html@@@Removing legal hold from a Microsoft 365 snapshot@@@Remove legal hold from a Microsoft 365 snapshot to return it to normal SLA Domain retention management...","saas/removing_legal_hold_sap_hana.html@@@Removing legal hold from SAP HANA snapshots@@@To remove a legal hold from the snapshots of SAP HANA databases for returning to a regular retention management, log in using an RSC administrator account and open the SAP HANA inventory page...","saas/removing_m365_groups.html@@@Removing groups from Microsoft 365 protection@@@Remove SharePoint or Teams groups, or Entra ID groups from the RSC Microsoft 365 protection hierarchy...","saas/removing_nodes_cld_cluster.html@@@Removing selected nodes from a Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage deployment@@@Remove nodes that you select individually from your Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage deployment to scale down the cluster...","saas/removing_nodes_count_cces.html@@@Removing nodes from Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage by count@@@Remove nodes from a Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage deployment by specifying the number of nodes to remove and letting RSC choose the nodes...","saas/removing_pam_configuration.html@@@Removing the PAM configuration@@@Remove the Privileged Access Management configuration when you prefer not to manage its credentials in RSC...","saas/removing_passkeys.html@@@Removing passkeys@@@Remove a passkey when it no longer meets your requirements or you are no longer using it...","saas/removing_private_container_registry_configuration.html@@@Removing the Private Container Registry configuration@@@When you no longer want to use your Private Container Registry and want to use Exocompute to pull images using a registry hosted by Rubrik, remove the Private Container Registry configuration...","saas/removing_quarantine_mgmt_center.html@@@Removing items from the Quarantine Management Center@@@Remove objects or files from quarantine using the Quarantine Management Center to restore full recovery options for the affected snapshots...","saas/removing_quarantined_file_or_object.html@@@Removing a quarantined file or object@@@Remove a quarantined file or object to make it available for recovery...","saas/removing_snapshot_legal_hold.html@@@Removing a legal hold from a snapshot@@@Remove a legal hold from a snapshot to return to normal retention management for that snapshot...","saas/removing_sso_group.html@@@Removing an SSO group@@@Remove an SSO group from RSC to revoke the assigned roles from all users in the group...","saas/removing_standalone_esxi_host.html@@@Removing a standalone ESXi host@@@Remove a connected standalone ESXi host to stop managing its virtual machines and backups, ensuring that the host is no longer part of the data protection operations...","saas/removing_taxii_threat_intel.html@@@Removing a TAXII threat intel source@@@Remove a TAXII threat intel source from RSC when you no longer want Threat Monitoring to use indicators of compromise from the TAXII feed...","saas/renewing_rba_self_rcca_certificates.html@@@Renewing RBA self-signed to RCCA-signed certificates@@@Replace self-signed RBA certificates with RCCA-signed certificates to improve security and simplify certificate lifecycle management...","saas/replication_and_cascading_arch_settings.html@@@Replication and cascading archival settings@@@When you enable cascading archival, you can determine the snapshot retention period by managing specific settings...","saas/replication_config_types_sla_domain.html@@@Replication configuration types in SLA Domain@@@You can configure replication types, such as many-to-one and one-to-one, and configure replication between multiple source and target clusters using a single SLA Domain to maintain consistent backup and disaster recovery...","saas/replication_settings_for_specific_workloads.html@@@Replication settings for specific workloads@@@When creating or editing an SLA Domain, enabling replication for certain workloads requires additional settings...","saas/replication_settings_for_specific_workloads_2.html@@@Replication settings for specific workloads@@@When creating or editing an SLA Domain, enabling replication for certain workloads requires additional settings...","saas/report_templates.html@@@Report templates@@@Report templates in RSC are organized by category to help you find the right report for your goal...","saas/reporting_false_positive_anomaly.html@@@Reporting a false positive anomaly@@@You can report an anomaly as a false positive when it is not an indicator of any malicious activity and is triggered by an internal system process...","saas/req_perms_data_scanning.html@@@Required permissions for data scanning in AWS@@@Information about the permissions that RSC requires to scan data and generate insights for AWS objects...","saas/req_perms_discover_cloud_objects.html@@@Required permissions for discovering AWS cloud objects@@@Information about the basic permissions that RSC requires to discover AWS cloud objects...","saas/req_perms_outpost_account.html@@@Required permissions for AWS outpost account@@@Information about the permissions that the outpost account requires to access the AWS account...","saas/req_perms_protecting_azr_resources.html@@@Required permissions for protecting Azure resources@@@RSC requires certain permissions to protect Azure resources, configure an Exocompute instance, store tiered data, and manage encryption of the tiered data...","saas/req_perms_protecting_azr_resources_2.html@@@Required permissions for protecting Azure resources@@@RSC requires certain permissions to protect Azure resources, configure an Exocompute instance, store tiered data, and manage encryption of the tiered data...","saas/requesting_escalation_support_case.html@@@Requesting escalation for a support case@@@Request escalation for an urgent or critical support case from the Case Detail view...","saas/required_permissions_for_role_chaining.html@@@Required permissions for role chaining@@@Information about the permission a role chaining account requires to manage the associated AWS accounts...","saas/required_permissions_storage_tiering.html@@@Required permissions for AWS storage tiering@@@To set up AWS storage tiering, it is required to assign specific permissions to the RSC user...","saas/requirements_for_setting_up_amazon_ec2_instance_and_ebs_volume_backup.html@@@Amazon EC2 instance and EBS volume protection requirements@@@Setting up protection for EC2 instances and EBS volumes requires the addition of AWS cloud accounts in RSC and the provision of cross-account access to RSC using the AWS CloudFormation service...","saas/requirements_for_sla_domain_names.html@@@Requirements for SLA Domain names@@@An SLA Domain must meet specific name requirements...","saas/requirements_guidelines_archiving.html@@@Requirements and guidelines for archiving@@@An SLA Domain archival policy for data center workloads must meet specific requirements...","saas/resetting_passkeys_user.html@@@Resetting passkeys for a user@@@When a user is locked out and is unable to authenticate access using any of the preconfigured passkeys or TOTP, the administrator can reset passkeys to enable user authentication...","saas/resetting_password.html@@@Resetting the password@@@If you suspect your RSC domain has been compromised or have other security concerns, reset your password from the User Preferences page...","saas/resetting_r2sv.html@@@Resetting Rubrik Two-step verification@@@Reset the multifactor authentication configuration for a user to reconfigure Rubrik Two-step verification from the beginning...","saas/resolution_of_failed_canceled_backups.html@@@Resolution of failed or canceled backups@@@RSC provides the ability to retry failed or canceled backups...","saas/resolving_aks_cluster_health_check_failure.html@@@Resolving AKS cluster health-check failure@@@You can often troubleshoot and resolve Exocompute health-check failure issues while setting up an Azure Kubernetes Service cluster...","saas/resolving_anomaly.html@@@Resolving an anomaly@@@You can resolve anomalies that are not indicative of abnormal behavior after you complete your investigation...","saas/resolving_archival_lag.html@@@Resolving archival lag@@@RSC alerts you when archival lag builds up on a data center archival location and recommends prioritized actions. Use the Resolving Archival Lag dialog box to review and apply the recommendations that reduce lag before it affects backups and recovery...","saas/resolving_azr_quota_error_dspm_onboarding.html@@@Resolving Azure quota errors while onboarding Data Security Posture@@@Request an Azure App Service quota increase through the Azure self-service portal when the Azure Function App deployment fails during Data Security Posture onboarding...","saas/restoring_an_ec2_instance_snapshot.html@@@Restoring an EC2 instance snapshot@@@Restore an EC2 instance snapshot to replace the original instance with a fully functional point-in-time copy...","saas/restoring_hana_database_catalog_deleted.html@@@Restoring a SAP HANA database without the backup catalog@@@Restore a SAP HANA database to the same or a different system using SAP HANA Studio when the backup is deleted from the catalog...","saas/restoring_hana_database_studio.html@@@Restoring SAP HANA database using SAP HANA Studio@@@Restore an SAP HANA database to the same system by using SAP HANA Studio...","saas/restoring_sap_database_using_replicated_database.html@@@Restoring SAP HANA database using replicated database@@@Restore an SAP HANA database from a replicated database using SAP HANA Studio...","saas/restoring_system_copy_using_studio.html@@@Restoring SAP HANA database system copy using SAP HANA Studio@@@Restore the system copy of an SAP HANA database to RSC-initiated backup on a different target system...","saas/resuming_cluster_protection.html@@@Resuming protection activity@@@Resume protection activity to remove restrictions of the pause feature...","saas/resuming_object_protection.html@@@Resuming object protection@@@Resume protection for data-center objects that have been paused. RSC provides a centralized management page to manage pause and resume at object, cluster, and SLA Domain levels...","saas/resuming_sla_domain_protection.html@@@Resuming SLA Domain protection@@@Resume protection activity for a paused SLA Domain for all the objects on the Rubrik cluster which are protected by the SLA Domain...","saas/retention_locked_sla_domain.html@@@Retention-locked SLA Domains@@@The retention lock feature on RSC SLA Domains ensures the security and integrity of your data for a specified duration by preventing the premature deletion of snapshots for various workloads...","saas/retention_management.html@@@Retention management@@@You can assign retention policies to existing scheduled snapshots, on-demand snapshots, and snapshots available in an archival location...","saas/retention_mgmt_existing_snapshots.html@@@Retention management for existing snapshots@@@You can manage the retention period of existing snapshots to prevent accidental data loss, ensuring the preservation of individual snapshot retention even when modifying SLA Domains...","saas/retention_policy_modificn_exist_snpsht.html@@@Retention policy modification for existing snapshots@@@After configuring the SLA Domain settings, you can modify the retention policy for existing snapshots...","saas/retrieving_snapshot_data_for_restore.html@@@Retrieving snapshot backup ID and prefix@@@Retrieve the snapshot backup ID and prefix that are required for restoring a SAP HANA database using the SAP HANA Studio...","saas/retrying_failed_or_canceled_backups.html@@@Retrying failed or canceled backups@@@Manually initiate policy-based snapshots to replace failed or canceled backups...","saas/ri_anomaly_event_messages.html@@@Anomaly event messages@@@RSC Data Threat Analytics provides messages for each event in the anomaly event series...","saas/ri_batch_recovery_of_vm.html@@@Recovery of a batch of virtual machines@@@When you want to recover multiple vSphere, AHV, and Hyper-V virtual machines from a snapshot in a single operation for Rubrik clusters, you can perform a batch recovery of the virtual machines...","saas/ri_best_practices_threat_hunts.html@@@Threat hunt best practices@@@Following these best practices when configuring threat hunts produces optimal performance and results...","saas/ri_events.html@@@Data Threat Analytics events@@@Data Threat Analytics provides filters and real-time search capabilities you can use to find specific events...","saas/ri_events_for_protected_objects.html@@@Anomaly Detection events for protected objects@@@Anomaly Detection events are enabled by default for supported and scanned objects...","saas/ri_features.html@@@Anomaly Detection features@@@Anomaly Detection protects data by performing file system behavioral and content analysis...","saas/ri_pane.html@@@Data Threat Analytics pane@@@The Data Threat Analytics pane of the Global Dashboard provides several interactive elements...","saas/ri_ransomware_monitoring.html@@@RSC Data Threat Analytics@@@RSC Data Threat Analytics provides Anomaly Detection and data recovery services on protected resources...","saas/ri_recovering_batch_ahv_vm_using_export.html@@@Recovering a batch of AHV virtual machines using exports@@@Perform exports for recovering a batch of AHV virtual machines in a single operation using Anomaly Detection...","saas/ri_recovering_batch_ahv_vm_using_live_mount.html@@@Recovering a batch of AHV virtual machines using Live Mounts@@@Create live mounts for recovering a batch of AHV virtual machines in a single operation using Anomaly Detection...","saas/ri_recovering_batch_vsphere_vm_using_export.html@@@Recovering a batch of vSphere virtual machines using exports@@@Perform exports for recovering a batch of vSphere virtual machines in a single operation using Anomaly Detection...","saas/ri_recovering_batch_vsphere_vm_using_live_mounts.html@@@Recovering a batch of vSphere virtual machines using Live Mounts@@@Create live mounts for recovering a batch of vSphere virtual machines in a single operation using Anomaly Detection...","saas/ri_reports.html@@@Anomaly Detection reports@@@Anomaly Detection reports provide information about the changes in snapshots for anomaly events. You can also download, save, or delete the reports...","saas/ri_threat_hunts.html@@@Threat hunts@@@On-demand threat hunts scan Rubrik backups for user-defined indicators of compromise and identify the systems potentially affected by an attack...","saas/rl_sla_cnp.html@@@Retention-locked SLA Domain for cloud workloads@@@A retention lock on an RSC SLA Domain is a security feature that prevents premature deletion of snapshots...","saas/rl_sla_domain_modes_auth.html@@@Retention-locked SLA Domain modes and authorization@@@Retention-locked SLA Domains offer modes for regulating data management and ensuring compliance. Each mode has a different set of configurations and authorization requirements...","saas/rm_performing_cyber_recovery_vm_export.html@@@Performing cyber recovery of virtual machines using Export@@@Select and recover virtual machines using export, based on threat hunting results, to a local, isolated recovery environment...","saas/rm_performing_cyber_recovery_vm_live_mount.html@@@Performing cyber recovery of virtual machines using Live Mount@@@Select and recover virtual machines using Live Mount, based on threat hunting results, to a local, isolated recovery environment...","saas/rncd_access_mgmt_tenant_org_users.html@@@Access management for tenant organization users@@@You can add a tenant organization to manage user access to the NAS CD data sets. Following the recommended sequence to add users, user permissions, and NAS CD systems is necessary for successful system access management...","saas/rncd_accessing_nascd_inventory_page.html@@@Accessing NAS Cloud Direct Inventory page@@@Access the NAS CD Inventory page to view the NAS CD data sets from RSC and recover the backups from associated snapshots...","saas/rncd_accessing_nascd_inventory_page_2.html@@@Accessing NAS Cloud Direct Inventory page@@@Access the NAS CD Inventory page to view the NAS CD data sets from RSC and recover the backups from associated snapshots...","saas/rncd_add_nas_cd_targets.html@@@Add NAS CD targets from NAS CD@@@You can add and manage NAS CD supported targets using NAS CD...","saas/rncd_add_shares_rsc.html@@@Add shares from RSC@@@You can use RSC to add a system and discover the shares associated with the source system...","saas/rncd_adding_amzn_fsxnetapp_ontap_sysem.html@@@Adding Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP systems@@@Add a Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its shares, exports, and namespaces in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_azr_netapp_files_systems.html@@@Adding Azure NetApp Files systems@@@Add an Azure NetApp Files system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect the data in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_azure_files_systems.html@@@Adding Azure Files systems@@@Add an Azure Files system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its shares and exports in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_dell_powerscale_systems.html@@@Adding Dell PowerScale systems@@@Add a Dell PowerScale system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its exports and shares in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_generic_nfs_systems.html@@@Adding Generic NFS systems@@@Add a Generic NFS system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect the data in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_generic_nfsv4_systems.html@@@Adding Generic NFSv4 systems@@@Add a Generic NFSv4 system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect the data in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_generic_s3_systems.html@@@Adding Generic S3 systems@@@Add a Generic S3 system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its S3 buckets in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_generic_smb.html@@@Adding Generic SMB systems@@@Add a Generic SMB system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its shares in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_ibm_storage_scale_systems.html@@@Adding IBM Storage Scale systems@@@Add an IBM Storage Scale or IBM Spectrum Scale system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its exports and shares in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_netapp7mode_systems.html@@@Adding NetApp ONTAP 7 Mode systems@@@Add a NetApp ONTAP 7 Mode system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its exports and shares in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_netapp_cluster_mode_systems.html@@@Adding NetApp ONTAP Cluster Mode systems@@@Add a NetApp ONTAP Cluster Mode system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its exports and shares in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_nutanix_files_systems.html@@@Adding Nutanix Files systems@@@Add a Nutanix Files system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its exports and shares in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_pure_flasharray_systems.html@@@Adding Pure FlashArray systems@@@Add a Pure FlashArray system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its exports and shares in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_pure_flashblade_systems.html@@@Adding Pure FlashBlade systems@@@Add a Pure FlashBlade system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its exports and shares in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_qumulo_qf2_systems.html@@@Adding Qumulo File Fabric systems@@@Add a Qumulo File Fabric system as a data source using RSC. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its exports and shares in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_shares.html@@@Adding shares to a NAS system@@@If the shares are not discovered automatically, you can manually add them to a source system...","saas/rncd_adding_systems.html@@@Adding systems@@@Add a system using RSC to configure the system as a data source. After adding the system, you can discover and protect its shares, exports, and namespaces in RSC...","saas/rncd_adding_vast_data_systems.html@@@Adding VAST Data systems@@@Add a VAST Data system as a data source using RSC to back up and archive your data...","saas/rncd_amazon_s3_target_creation.html@@@Create Amazon S3 target@@@You can create an Amazon S3 target for the secure storage of backup snapshots and archived data. Additionally, you can customize proxy settings and choose an S3 endpoint for managing data transfers to the target...","saas/rncd_amzn_s3_detail_ncd_target.html@@@Amazon S3 details for NAS CD targets@@@Information about Amazon S3 location details that you need to provide while creating an Amazon S3 target for your NAS CD data sets...","saas/rncd_assigning_sla_domains_ncd_datasets.html@@@Assigning SLA Domains to NAS CD data sets@@@Assign an SLA Domain to a NAS CD data set to protect it with the backup-related policies in an SLA Domain...","saas/rncd_backup_policy_limitations.html@@@Limitations for multi-frequency backup policies@@@Information about the limitations that apply when configuring multiple backup policies for NAS CD SLA Domains...","saas/rncd_changing_retention_nascd_snapshots.html@@@Changing the retention policy of NAS CD snapshots@@@Change the retention period of individual NAS CD snapshots to manage storage and ensure data accessibility for NAS shares and S3 buckets...","saas/rncd_cloning_sla_domains.html@@@Cloning SLA Domains for NAS CD@@@Clone an existing NAS CD SLA Domain to save time by avoiding creation and configuration of a new SLA Domain from scratch. You can make any necessary adjustments to the cloned SLA Domain...","saas/rncd_cloud_storage_cost_considerations.html@@@Cloud storage cost considerations for NAS CD data sets@@@When protecting cloud-hosted data with NAS CD, you must consider how the storage tier selection and data retrieval pricing of your cloud provider affect your backup and scanning costs...","saas/rncd_cloud_storage_cost_considerations_2.html@@@Cloud storage cost considerations for NAS CD data sets@@@When protecting cloud-hosted data with NAS CD, you must consider how the storage tier selection and data retrieval pricing of your cloud provider affect your backup and scanning costs...","saas/rncd_cluster_settings.html@@@Rubrik cluster settings for NAS CD@@@You can configure network authentication, WAN, Kerberos, and SMB users settings for a NAS CD cluster that contains one or more NAS CD systems...","saas/rncd_configuring_bckup_setting_ntfs_file.html@@@Configuring backup settings for NTFS files@@@Configure the NTFS system and offline file settings to specify if you want to include these files in the backup...","saas/rncd_configuring_kerberos.html@@@Configuring Kerberos settings@@@Configure Kerberos settings for a Rubrik cluster to manage credentials and enforcement modes of Kerberos security for NFSv4 backups...","saas/rncd_configuring_latency_threshold.html@@@Configuring latency threshold@@@Configure the latency threshold for a system to control the maximum read latency permitted for an operation...","saas/rncd_configuring_smb_users.html@@@Configuring SMB users@@@Configure SMB user to back up and restore your data in SMB protocol...","saas/rncd_configuring_wan_settings.html@@@Configuring WAN settings@@@Configure WAN settings for a system to control the maximum amount of data that NAS CD transfers per second to the cloud storage for a given task...","saas/rncd_creating_amazons3_targets.html@@@Creating Amazon S3 targets from RSC@@@Create an Amazon S3 target to back up and archive your NAS data from a source system using RSC...","saas/rncd_creating_cstm_rol_ncd_ds_al_obj_typ.html@@@Creating roles by all-object types for NAS CD-based protection@@@Create a custom role in RSC with Role-based Access Control privileges for NAS CD-based protection of NAS CD objects with permissions configured by all object types. These privileges provide granularity for determining the permissions to perform actions, and on which objects...","saas/rncd_creating_custm_role_ncd_ds_cluster.html@@@Creating roles by cluster for NAS CD-based protection@@@Create a custom role in RSC with Role-Based Access Control privileges for NAS CD-based protection of RSC objects with permissions configured by clusters. These privileges provide granularity for determining the permissions to perform actions, and on which objects...","saas/rncd_creating_custm_role_ncd_ds_obj_type.html@@@Creating roles by object type for NAS CD-based protection@@@Create a custom role in RSC with Role-Based Access Control privileges for NAS CD-based protection of NAS CD objects with permissions configured by object type. These privileges provide granularity for determining the permissions to perform actions, and on which objects...","saas/rncd_creating_directory_rules.html@@@Creating Directory Rules for NAS CD data sets@@@Create a directory rule to automatically assign an SLA Domain to a subset of NAS data in a NAS share or bucket...","saas/rncd_creating_gcp_targets.html@@@Creating Google Cloud Platform targets from RSC@@@Create a Google Cloud Platform target to back up and archive your NAS data from a source system using RSC...","saas/rncd_creating_microsoft_azure_targets.html@@@Creating Microsoft Azure targets from RSC@@@Create a Microsoft Azure target to back up and archive your NAS data from a source system using RSC...","saas/rncd_creating_nfs_targets.html@@@Creating Network File System targets from RSC@@@Create a Network File System target to back up and archive your NAS data from a source system using RSC...","saas/rncd_creating_role_al_obj_typ_rsc_protct.html@@@Creating roles by all-object types for RSC-based protection@@@Create a custom role in RSC with Role-Based Access Control privileges for RSC-based protection of NAS CD objects with permissions configured by all object types. These privileges provide granularity for determining the permissions to perform actions, and on which objects...","saas/rncd_creating_role_cluster_rsc_protect.html@@@Creating roles by cluster for RSC-based protection@@@Create a custom role in RSC with Role-Based Access Control privileges for RSC-based protection of NAS CD objects with permissions configured by clusters. These privileges provide granularity for determining the permissions to perform actions, and on which objects...","saas/rncd_creating_role_obj_type_rsc_protect.html@@@Creating roles by object type for RSC-based protection@@@Create a custom role in RSC with Role-Based Access Control privileges for RSC-based protection of the NAS CD objects with permissions configured by object type. These privileges provide granularity for determining the permissions to perform actions, and on which objects...","saas/rncd_creating_s3_compatible_targets.html@@@Creating S3-compatible targets from RSC@@@Create an S3-compatible target to back up and archive your NAS data from a source system using RSC...","saas/rncd_creating_sla_domains_nascd.html@@@Creating an SLA Domain for NAS CD@@@Create an SLA Domain in RSC for a NAS CD data set to protect the NAS data in a source system...","saas/rncd_deleting_nascd_snapshots.html@@@Deleting NAS CD snapshots@@@Delete snapshots of NAS CD shares or buckets to free up storage space and manage your data retention...","saas/rncd_deleting_sla_domains.html@@@Deleting SLA Domains for NAS CD@@@Delete an SLA Domain if you no longer need the SLA Domain...","saas/rncd_deleting_systems.html@@@Deleting Systems@@@Delete a system if you no longer want to backup data in the system...","saas/rncd_deleting_targets.html@@@Deleting targets from RSC@@@Delete a target location that you no longer require for backing up, archiving, or accessing data...","saas/rncd_disabling_targets.html@@@Disabling targets from RSC@@@Disable a target to stop backup and other background operations that change data on the target location...","saas/rncd_editing_sla_domains.html@@@Editing SLA Domains for NAS CD@@@Edit an existing NAS CD SLA Domain to update its details...","saas/rncd_editing_targets.html@@@Editing targets from RSC@@@Edit a target to change its details in RSC...","saas/rncd_events.html@@@Events in NAS CD@@@You can see all the events associated with all the connected Rubrik clusters for NAS CD under the Events tab...","saas/rncd_events_2.html@@@Events in NAS CD@@@You can see all the events associated with all the connected Rubrik clusters for NAS CD under the Events tab...","saas/rncd_finding_legal_hold_snapshots.html@@@Finding NAS CD snapshots on legal hold@@@Use RSC Legal Hold page to find NAS CD snapshots that are currently on legal hold...","saas/rncd_gcp_detail_ncd_target.html@@@Google Cloud Platform details for NAS CD targets@@@Information about Google Cloud Platform (GCP) details that you need to provide while creating a GCP target for your NAS CD data sets...","saas/rncd_legal_hold_snapshots.html@@@Legal hold for NAS CD snapshots@@@Legal hold ensures that NAS CD snapshots required for litigation are protected for the duration of the legal hold, providing a compliant and efficient way to manage data subject to legal obligations...","saas/rncd_managing_network_settings.html@@@Managing Networks on a NAS System@@@Configure and manage the network settings for a system within the RSC user interface. You can define the networks for different protocols that RSC uses to transfer data...","saas/rncd_mircrosoft_azure_detail_ncd_target.html@@@Microsoft Azure details for NAS CD targets@@@Information about Microsoft Azure target details that you need to provide while creating a Microsoft Azure target for your NAS CD data sets...","saas/rncd_modifying_directory_rules.html@@@Modifying Directory Rules for NAS CD data sets@@@Modify an existing Directory Rule to change the SLA Domain, protection type, and exclude a directory path or a file pattern...","saas/rncd_nascd_inventory_management.html@@@NAS CD Inventory Management@@@Inventory management provides options to view NAS CD data sets and perform recoveries of their backups...","saas/rncd_nascd_inventory_management_2.html@@@NAS CD Inventory Management@@@Inventory management provides options to view NAS CD data sets and perform recoveries of their backups...","saas/rncd_ncd_exclusion_pattern_syntax.html@@@Backup Exclusion pattern syntax for NAS CD@@@NAS CD uses a glob-style pattern syntax for excluding files from backups...","saas/rncd_nfs_detail_ncd_target.html@@@Network File System details for NAS CD targets@@@Information about NFS details that you need to provide while creating a NFS target for your NAS CD data sets...","saas/rncd_object_tagging_generic_s3.html@@@Object tag protection for Generic S3 systems@@@After you enable object tagging on a Generic S3 source system, NAS CD captures S3 object tags during backup operations and applies them during restore operations...","saas/rncd_placing_legal_hold_snapshot.html@@@Placing a NAS CD snapshot on legal hold@@@Placing a legal hold on a NAS CD snapshot indefinitely retains that snapshot regardless of the assigned SLA Domain retention policy...","saas/rncd_prequistites_target_immutability.html@@@Prerequisites for target immutability@@@You can use immutability that prevents alteration or deletion of snapshots for a specified period, safeguarding data integrity. You must fulfill certain prerequisites to successfully use immutability for your data...","saas/rncd_rbac_nascd.html@@@RBAC for NAS CD-based protection@@@You can use role-based access control to assign a role containing a set of permissions to a RSC user. You can also assign multiple roles to a user...","saas/rncd_rbac_rsc_based_protection.html@@@RBAC for RSC-based protection@@@You can use role-based access control to assign a role containing a set of permissions to a RSC user. You can also assign multiple roles to a user...","saas/rncd_recovering_nascd_data_sets.html@@@Recovering NAS CD data sets@@@Recover a NAS CD share from snapshots, using RSC...","saas/rncd_recovering_nascd_data_sets_2.html@@@Recovering NAS CD data sets@@@Recover a NAS CD share from snapshots, using RSC...","saas/rncd_refreshing_systems.html@@@Refreshing systems@@@Refresh a system to rescan and rediscover a source system to detect any changes that may have occurred in the source system storage...","saas/rncd_removing_legal_hold_snapshot.html@@@Removing legal hold from a NAS CD snapshot@@@Remove legal hold from a NAS CD snapshot to return the snapshot to normal retention management...","saas/rncd_s3_compatible_details_ncd_targets.html@@@S3-compatible details for NAS CD targets@@@Information about S3-compatible storage details that you need to provide while creating an S3-compatible target for your NAS CD data sets...","saas/rncd_search_limitations.html@@@NAS CD search limitations@@@Information on the limitations of searching NAS CD files and folders...","saas/rncd_searching_file_folder_global.html@@@Searching for NAS CD files and folders using global search@@@Use the global search in RSC to search for files and directories on NAS CD clusters...","saas/rncd_searching_file_folder_snapshot.html@@@Searching and recovering NAS CD files within a share@@@Search for files across all snapshots of a specific NAS CD share and recover them from RSC...","saas/rncd_snapshot_backup_generic_systems.html@@@Snapshot-based backups for generic NAS systems@@@You can configure RSC to use existing snapshots on generic NFS, NFSv4, and SMB systems for consistent backups, instead of backing up from the live system...","saas/rncd_system_settings.html@@@System settings@@@You can configure settings related to network for a system in RSC. Configuring these settings provides you with better control on your data protection options...","saas/rncd_taking_ods_ncd_datasets.html@@@Taking on-demand snapshots of NAS CD data sets@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, back up your NAS data at any time by taking an on-demand snapshot...","saas/rncd_vast_data_views_rsc.html@@@VAST Data views in RSC@@@Information about the VAST Data views that RSC imports from the VAST Data storage based on the configured security flavor and access flavor for a protocol...","saas/rncd_viewing_targets.html@@@Viewing targets from RSC@@@View the targets to manage them from the NAS Cloud Direct Locations page in RSC...","saas/rolling_upgrade_advantages.html@@@Advantages of using a rolling upgrade@@@With a rolling upgrade, you can upgrade a Rubrik cluster or third-party hardware without downtime. Rolling upgrades provide a set of advantages, such as simplified upgrade workflow, support for third-party hardware upgrades, and varied levels of job resumability...","saas/rolling_upgrade_eligibility.html@@@Rolling upgrade eligibility and qualification criteria@@@Rubrik Security Cloud performs automated checks to verify that a Rubrik cluster meets the specific technical requirements and workload configurations necessary to support a zero-downtime rolling upgrade...","saas/rolling_upgrade_enable.html@@@Enabling rolling upgrades for a Rubrik cluster@@@Enable the rolling upgrade capability for specific Rubrik clusters to make it available during the software update process...","saas/rolling_upgrade_limitations.html@@@Rolling upgrade limitations and requirements@@@Rolling upgrades have specific technical constraints and environment requirements that affect cluster scale, workload support, and network configuration...","saas/rolling_upgrade_rbk_cdm_software.html@@@Rolling upgrade of Rubrik CDM software@@@Rolling upgrades provide a zero-downtime method for updating Rubrik CDM software by processing nodes sequentially. Administrators can enable and manage this feature for eligible clusters using Rubrik Security Cloud to ensure continuous data availability...","saas/rolling_upgrade_statuses.html@@@Rolling upgrade statuses for workloads@@@Information about the statuses for workloads, such as resumable, restartable, and unsupported, during a rolling upgrade...","saas/rotating_encryption_keys.html@@@Rotating encryption keys@@@To provide enhanced encryption key security, you must rotate the encryption key or switch to another root of trust for your encryption key. This functionality does not apply to encryption keys for data center archival locations...","saas/rotating_personal_access_token_secret.html@@@Rotating the personal access token secret@@@Generate a new secret for your personal access token if the current secret is lost or compromised. Rotating the secret invalidates the existing secret...","saas/rotating_the_client_secret.html@@@Rotating the client secret@@@Generate a client secret for a service account and invalidate the old secret...","saas/rp_management.html@@@Recovery Plan requirements and settings@@@Recovery Plans manage recovery specifications for the different types of recovery...","saas/rsc_api_proxy_nascd_rest_api.html@@@RSC API proxy for NAS CD REST API@@@Using the RSC API proxy, you can send NAS CD REST API requests directly to an RSC instance instead of a NAS CD instance. This simplifies data management across NAS CD clusters and streamlines API interactions, reduces complexity, and enables efficient management of NAS CD data from a single, secure location...","saas/rsc_certificate_management.html@@@Certificate management@@@RSC Certificate Management provides a centralized dashboard to manage certificates across all connected Rubrik clusters and for RSC workflows...","saas/rsc_creating_custom_sla_domain.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to define and customize workload protection and management policies...","saas/rsc_creating_custom_sla_domain_2.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to define and customize workload protection and management policies...","saas/rsc_creating_custom_sla_domain_3.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to define and customize workload protection and management policies...","saas/rsc_creating_custom_sla_domain_4.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to define and customize workload protection and management policies...","saas/rsc_creating_custom_sla_domain_5.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to define and customize workload protection and management policies...","saas/rsc_creating_sla_domains_manytoone_rep.html@@@Creating SLA Domains for many-to-one replication@@@Create an SLA Domain for many-to-one replication, the traditional replication mode supported by RSC SLA Domains. This method consolidates data protection from multiple source clusters onto a single target cluster, ensuring centralized recovery and protection...","saas/rsc_creating_sla_domains_manytoone_rep_2.html@@@Creating SLA Domains for many-to-one replication@@@Create an SLA Domain for many-to-one replication, the traditional replication mode supported by RSC SLA Domains. This method consolidates data protection from multiple source clusters onto a single target cluster, ensuring centralized recovery and protection...","saas/rsc_creating_sla_domains_onetoone_rep.html@@@Creating SLA Domains for one-to-one replication@@@Create an SLA Domain for one-to-one replication when there are more than two replication targets and the source and replication clusters are in a dedicated replication configuration. With one-to-one replication, you can configure multiple replication pairs, but a source cluster can replicate to a maximum of two target clusters...","saas/rsc_creating_sla_domains_onetoone_rep_2.html@@@Creating SLA Domains for one-to-one replication@@@Create an SLA Domain for one-to-one replication when there are more than two replication targets and the source and replication clusters are in a dedicated replication configuration. With one-to-one replication, you can configure multiple replication pairs, but a source cluster can replicate to a maximum of two target clusters...","saas/rsc_dashboards.html@@@Dashboards@@@RSC dashboards provide information about the connected Rubrik clusters and the installed RSC apps...","saas/rsc_data_at_rest_encryption.html@@@Data-at-rest encryption@@@Depending on the specific model of the Rubrik Brik, Rubrik clusters encrypt data at rest using software or hardware encryption...","saas/rsc_domain_url_change.html@@@RSC domain URL change@@@RSC enables you to change your RSC domain URL without losing any existing metadata or account configurations. This feature ensures continuous workflow continuity, as only the domain URL itself changes, while your data and settings remain unchanged...","saas/rsc_encryption_management.html@@@Encryption management@@@With the encryption management feature in RSC, you can view information about data-at-rest encryption for the Rubrik clusters and archives, access to your Key Management Services, and enhance data security through automated key rotation every 30 days...","saas/rsc_global_dashboard.html@@@Global Dashboard@@@The Global dashboard displays summary information for each installed RSC app...","saas/rsc_hc.html@@@RSC Help Center@@@You can use the Help Center in RSC to search product documentation, access the Rubrik knowledge base, and create support cases...","saas/rsc_hc_creating_support_case.html@@@Creating a support case through the RSC Help Center@@@If you need to engage Rubrik Support, you can create a support case through the RSC Help Center...","saas/rsc_hosting_platforms.html@@@RSC hosting platforms@@@Rubrik Security Cloud is hosted on Amazon Web Services (AWS) or Google Cloud Platform (GCP). Rubrik hosts accounts for European customers in the AWS European Sovereign Cloud...","saas/rsc_info_sso_config.html@@@RSC information for SSO configuration@@@The RSC metadata file includes information that an IdP can extract to configure SSO successfully...","saas/rsc_insights.html@@@RSC Insights@@@RSC Insights identifies problems in your Rubrik environment, proposes solutions, and provides actionable information to minimize the need for help from Rubrik Support...","saas/rsc_manage_protection_options.html@@@Manage protection options@@@Options available on the Manage protection dialog box...","saas/rsc_manage_protection_options_2.html@@@Manage protection options@@@Options available on the Manage protection dialog box...","saas/rsc_private_access_azr_snapshot.html@@@RSC using private access to access an Azure snapshot@@@Information about how RSC accesses an Azure snapshot using the private access network policy to perform various operations, such as indexing and archiving...","saas/rsc_security.html@@@Security settings@@@Rubrik Security Cloud provides enhanced security authentication services and features...","saas/rsc_settings_menu.html@@@Settings menu@@@You can use the RSC Settings menu to access and configure the global settings for all your Rubrik applications...","saas/rsc_slowness_reporting.html@@@Slowness Reporting@@@Slowness Reporting provides a way to record your browser activity during a slow RSC UI session and submit a diagnostic report to Rubrik Support...","saas/rsc_smb_security.html@@@SMB security@@@With the SMB security feature in RSC, a Rubrik cluster provides security for SMB shares by requiring Active Directory authentication and enforcing SMB security...","saas/rsc_sso_workflow.html@@@RSC SSO workflow@@@RSC supports configuring single sign-on with an identity provider for secure authentication...","saas/rubrik_ai_data_security_posture.html@@@Rubrik AI for Data Security Posture@@@Use Rubrik AI to speed up investigations in Data Security Posture...","saas/rubrik_application_privileges.html@@@Rubrik application privileges@@@Details of application-specific privileges that are available for assignment to different roles in RSC...","saas/rubrik_cc_es_on_saas.html@@@Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage@@@You can use Rubrik Security Cloud to provision a Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage deployment...","saas/rubrik_cdm_release_information.html@@@Rubrik CDM release information@@@The Rubrik CDM release information includes details such as release date, end of support date, and current adoption rate. You can use this information to compare the available versions for making a decision about upgrading...","saas/rubrik_cdm_release_table.html@@@Rubrik CDM release table@@@Release information for the CDM versions, such as release date, end of support date, and current adoption rate...","saas/rubrik_cdm_upgrades_page.html@@@Rubrik CDM upgrades page@@@The Rubrik CDM upgrades page provides information about the installed Rubrik CDM versions, cluster software support status, upgrade status, and notifications for available upgrades...","saas/rubrik_cluster_direct_access_config.html@@@Rubrik cluster direct access configuration@@@You can configure the IP address or the fully qualified domain name of a managing load balancer to enable direct access to a Rubrik cluster...","saas/rubrik_cluster_upgrade_reports.html@@@Rubrik cluster upgrade reports@@@The Rubrik cluster upgrade report is downloaded as a CSV file and provides a variety of information about the cluster upgrades...","saas/rubrik_cluster_upgrade_states.html@@@Rubrik cluster upgrade states@@@Information about how a Rubrik cluster transitions through specific states when the installed Rubrik CDM software version is upgraded...","saas/rubrik_hosted_acr_pcr.html@@@Rubrik-hosted ACR versus PCR@@@Overview of the Rubrik-hosted Azure Container Registry and a Private Container Registry for Azure...","saas/rules_add_update_vm_scripts.html@@@Rules to add or update virtual machine scripts@@@Information about supported virtual machine scripts for AHV and vSphere virtual machines and required rules to ensure that the scripts run successfully...","saas/rules_add_update_vm_scripts_2.html@@@Rules to add or update virtual machine scripts@@@Information about supported virtual machine scripts for AHV and vSphere virtual machines and required rules to ensure that the scripts run successfully...","saas/rules_archiving_replication_policies.html@@@Rules for archiving and replication policies@@@When configuring an SLA Domain, Rubrik clusters that are selected for archiving in the archival policy do not appear as replication target options in the replication policy...","saas/running_network_diagnostics_rsc.html@@@Running Network Diagnostics for RSC@@@Run diagnostics to check your network status and troubleshoot issues in RSC...","saas/running_rsc_slowness_reporting.html@@@Recording and Submitting a Slowness Report@@@Record your browser activity while experiencing a performance issue in RSC UI and submit a diagnostic report to Rubrik Support...","saas/s3_configuring_multiple_backup_locations.html@@@Configuring multiple backup locations for S3@@@Configure up to two backup locations for your Amazon S3 bucket by creating an SLA Domain with multiple backup policies...","saas/s3_multiple_backup_locations.html@@@Multiple backup locations for Amazon S3@@@You can configure multiple backup locations within a single SLA Domain to meet enhanced data resilience and compliance requirements for your Amazon S3 buckets...","saas/saas_workloads.html@@@SaaS workloads@@@RSC protection for SaaS workloads simplifies protecting and managing backups for SaaS application instances...","saas/sai_diagnostics_resolution.html@@@RSC Insights diagnostics and resolution@@@RSC Insights helps diagnose and resolve issues found in your Rubrik clusters...","saas/sai_issue_types_severities.html@@@Issue types and severities@@@Information about the insight types and severities used to describe each insight...","saas/sai_viewing_insights.html@@@Viewing insights@@@View anomalies or other issues along with actionable insights for your Rubrik clusters...","saas/saml_attr_sso_config.html@@@SAML attributes for SSO configuration@@@RSC uses certain SAML attributes in the SAML response from an IdP to configure SSO successfully...","saas/sample_error_codes.html@@@Sample error codes@@@RSC displays error codes and other error details for the failed or canceled backups that can be retried...","saas/sap_download_archived_snapshot_earlier_v812.html@@@Downloading an archived SAP HANA snapshot with earlier versions of CDM@@@When you want to download an archived snapshot of an SAP HANA database to a Rubrik cluster that is running a CDM version earlier than 8.1.2, you must follow a specific process...","saas/sap_hana_architecture.html@@@SAP HANA protection architecture@@@RSC integrates with SAP HANA through its native Backint client, which is deployed automatically on the SAP HANA host when the RBS or an external tool is deployed...","saas/sap_hana_archival.html@@@SAP HANA archival@@@RSC allows you to include an archival policy in an SLA Domain for archiving SAP HANA snapshots to an archival location...","saas/sap_hana_auto_full_backup_after_failover.html@@@SAP HANA automatic full backup after a failover@@@RSC provides an option for backups after a failover to either run according to the SLA Domain or to force a full backup during the next scheduled backup for systems running on Rubrik cluster version 9.5 or later...","saas/sap_hana_backup_compression.html@@@Managing native backup compression for SAP HANA databases@@@Enable SAP HANA native backup compression at the database level to reduce backup size and improve backup performance...","saas/sap_hana_database_details.html@@@SAP HANA database details@@@The details page for an SAP HANA database displays the protection status, snapshot calendar, and protection events list...","saas/sap_hana_database_restoration_from_replicated_database.html@@@SAP HANA databases restoration from a replicated database@@@SAP HANA databases can be restored from a replicated database using the SAP HANA Studio...","saas/sap_hana_download_archived_snapshot.html@@@Downloading an archived SAP HANA snapshot@@@When you want to download an archived snapshot of an SAP HANA database to a Rubrik cluster that is running CDM version 8.1.2 or later, use the download option available on the SAP HANA database details page...","saas/sap_hana_download_replicated_snapshot.html@@@Downloading a replicated SAP HANA snapshot@@@You can prepare to use a replicated snapshot to recover an SAP HANA database by downloading the full replicated snapshot to local storage on the source Rubrik cluster...","saas/sap_hana_external_backup_trigger.html@@@SAP HANA external backup trigger@@@RSC enables you to initiate SAP HANA database backups using external tools such as SAP HANA Studio, Cockpit, API calls, cron jobs, or direct command-line execution. This method provides greater control and flexibility over backup scheduling, as it does not rely on Rubrik-managed SLA Domain policies to trigger backups...","saas/sap_hana_multi_cluster_rbs.html@@@Multi-cluster RBS for SAP HANA@@@You can connect an SAP HANA host to multiple Rubrik clusters to enable cross-cluster database restore without reinstalling the Rubrik Backup Service...","saas/sap_hana_protection.html@@@SAP HANA databases@@@RSC enables administrators to implement backup policies on SAP HANA databases running on public clouds and on-premises...","saas/sap_hana_recovering_db_original.html@@@Recovering an SAP HANA database to the original database@@@Recover an SAP HANA database to its original location by restoring a snapshot...","saas/sap_hana_recovering_db_target.html@@@Recovering an SAP HANA snapshot to a target database@@@Recover an SAP HANA database to a target database using either point-in-time or full snapshot recovery...","saas/sap_hana_recovery.html@@@SAP HANA recovery@@@RSC provides point-in-time, full snapshot, and system copy recovery methods for SAP HANA databases. You can recover SAP HANA databases by using RSC or SAP HANA Studio...","saas/sap_hana_recovery_rubrik_vs_studio.html@@@SAP HANA recovery using RSC versus SAP HANA Studio@@@Information about the key differences between recovering an SAP HANA database using RSC and using SAP HANA Studio...","saas/sap_hana_recovery_studio.html@@@SAP HANA recovery using SAP HANA Studio@@@SAP HANA Studio provides a user interface for performing database recovery operations. This method primarily involves direct interaction with database backups and logs, either through a backup catalog or by directly specifying file system locations...","saas/sap_hana_recovery_using_rsc.html@@@SAP HANA recovery using RSC@@@RSC provides various SAP HANA recovery options, including point-in-time, full snapshot, and system copy restores. These options makes sure data integrity and quick recovery to original or target databases, considering impacts on SYSTEMDB and ongoing backups...","saas/sap_hana_replication.html@@@SAP HANA replication@@@In RSC, you can use the SLA Domain replication policy to replicate SAP HANA snapshots from one Rubrik cluster to another...","saas/sap_hana_secure_user_store.html@@@SAP HANA Secure User Store@@@You can use the SAP HANA Secure User Store tool to create a secure user key that RSC can use to authenticate to an SAP HANA system instead of using login credentials...","saas/sap_hana_selecting_recovery_method.html@@@Selecting an SAP HANA recovery method@@@Select a method to recover your SAP HANA database using RSC. These methods include restoring SAP HANA databases either to their original state or to a target database...","saas/sap_hana_storage_snapshot_recovery.html@@@SAP HANA recovery using storage snapshots@@@You can use the SAP HANA storage snapshot to recover your SAP HANA databases. Storage snapshots are fast, encrypted, have negligible network load, and capture the entire data area at a particular point in time. Use RSC to recover SAP HANA databases from storage snapshots on Azure...","saas/sap_hana_taking_ods.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of SAP HANA workloads@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, use the on-demand snapshot process to take backint snapshots of a SAP HANA database for full, incremental, and differential backups. You can also take storage snapshots of an SAP HANA system for full backups...","saas/saphana.html@@@SAP HANA@@@RSC protects SAP HANA databases on on-premises infrastructure and on public cloud environments, including AWS, Azure, and GCP, using policy-driven SLA Domains and native Backint integration...","saas/saphana_adding_host_scale_out.html@@@Adding hosts for a scale-out SAP HANA system@@@In a scale-out or multi-host deployment, add all hosts in the scale-out cluster to RSC...","saas/saphana_adding_host_scale_up.html@@@Adding a host for a scale-up SAP HANA system@@@In a scale-up or single-host deployment, add the single SAP HANA host to RSC for managing and protecting the databases on that host...","saas/saphana_adding_system_scale_out.html@@@Adding a scale-out SAP HANA system@@@Add a scale-out or multi-host SAP HANA system to the RSC domain to start protecting SAP HANA workloads...","saas/saphana_adding_system_scale_up.html@@@Adding a scale-up SAP HANA system@@@Add a scale-up or single-host SAP HANA system to the RSC domain to start protecting SAP HANA workloads...","saas/saphana_assigning_protection.html@@@Assigning protection to SAP HANA@@@Assign an SLA Domain to SAP HANA systems or individual databases to apply data protection and management policies to your SAP HANA workloads...","saas/saphana_best_practices_sla.html@@@Best practices for SAP HANA SLA Domain assignment@@@Information about the best practices for assigning SLA Domains to SAP HANA workloads, ensuring effective data protection and compliance...","saas/saphana_common_protection_terms.html@@@Common SAP HANA protection terms@@@Information about common terms used when protecting SAP HANA databases with RSC...","saas/saphana_configure_protection.html@@@Configure SAP HANA protection@@@You can configure protection for your SAP HANA workloads by creating a custom SLA Domain, assigning it to SAP HANA systems or databases, and taking on-demand snapshots as needed...","saas/saphana_creating_custom_role.html@@@Creating a custom role for SAP HANA@@@Create a custom role with Role-based Access Control privileges for managing your SAP HANA workloads. These privileges provide finer granularity for determining which permissions an RSC user has for performing specific actions on SAP HANA databases...","saas/saphana_creating_custom_sla.html@@@Creating a custom SLA Domain for SAP HANA@@@Create a custom SLA Domain to streamline and customize protection and management policies for your SAP HANA workloads...","saas/saphana_evaluate_deployment_options.html@@@SAP HANA deployment options@@@SAP HANA supports two deployment options: scale-up and scale-out. The differences between these options affect how you configure data protection with RSC...","saas/saphana_evaluate_protection_options.html@@@Evaluate SAP HANA protection options@@@Understanding the various SAP HANA protection options when creating an SLA Domain enables you to make informed decisions and ensure effective data protection...","saas/saphana_implementation_workflow.html@@@SAP HANA protection implementation workflow@@@Protecting SAP HANA databases involves a structured workflow that starts with planning and preparation, followed by system setup, protection configuration, ongoing management, and recovery...","saas/saphana_key_features_protection.html@@@Key features for SAP HANA protection@@@RSC provides automated backup management, flexible recovery options, and advanced data protection features for SAP HANA databases running on on-premises infrastructure and public cloud environments...","saas/saphana_manage_data.html@@@Manage SAP HANA data@@@You can manage your SAP HANA data by configuring legal holds, adjusting snapshot retention, and viewing database details...","saas/saphana_plan_protection.html@@@Plan your SAP HANA protection@@@Before setting up SAP HANA protection, it is important that you review the prerequisites, configure user access, and verify the required permissions in RSC...","saas/saphana_protect_databases.html@@@Protect SAP HANA databases@@@You can protect your SAP HANA databases by understanding the protection hierarchy, reviewing best practices, evaluating protection options, and configuring SLA Domains...","saas/saphana_protection_hsr_config_dr.html@@@Configure HSR for disaster recovery@@@With RSC, you can protect the SAP HANA system replication configuration for disaster recovery by performing specific actions...","saas/saphana_protection_hsr_config_high_avail.html@@@Configure HSR for high availability@@@With RSC, you can protect the SAP HANA system replication configuration for high availability by performing specific actions...","saas/saphana_quick_links.html@@@Quick links for SAP HANA protection@@@Immediate access to important tasks and information for SAP HANA setup, daily operations, and recovery...","saas/saphana_recover_data.html@@@Recover SAP HANA data@@@RSC provides various recovery options for SAP HANA databases, including recovery through RSC, SAP HANA Studio, storage snapshots, and from archived or replicated snapshots...","saas/saphana_recovery_options.html@@@Recovery options for SAP HANA@@@A comparative overview of the various recovery options for SAP HANA databases...","saas/saphana_restoring_db_mv_snapshot.html@@@Restoring a database from a Managed Volume snapshot@@@Restore a database from an exported Managed Volume snapshot using RSC...","saas/saphana_setup_scale_out.html@@@Set up a scale-out SAP HANA system@@@A scale-out SAP HANA deployment distributes the database system across multiple hosts. You must review the configuration required for setting up a scale-out system with RSC...","saas/saphana_setup_scale_up.html@@@Set up a scale-up SAP HANA system@@@A scale-up SAP HANA deployment runs the entire database system on a single host. You must review the configuration required for setting up a scale-up system with RSC...","saas/saphana_setup_system.html@@@Set up your SAP HANA system@@@You can set up your SAP HANA system for protection by evaluating your deployment options, installing Rubrik Backup Service, and adding the SAP HANA host and system to RSC...","saas/saphana_user_management.html@@@RSC user management for SAP HANA protection@@@Designating specific users with appropriate privileges and roles in RSC enhances security for managing SAP HANA backup and recovery operations...","saas/schedule_recoveries_rp.html@@@Scheduled recoveries for Recovery Plans@@@The scheduled recovery feature automates periodic testing of disaster Recovery Plans and cyber recovery plans in Orchestrated Recovery...","saas/scheduling_a_sdd_report.html@@@Scheduling a Data Security Posture report@@@Create the schedule for a Data Security Posture report...","saas/scheduling_test_recovery.html@@@Scheduling a test recovery@@@Configure a schedule for automating test recoveries using a selected Recovery Plan. Recovery testing strengthens preparedness and helps identify potential recovery issues before an event occurs...","saas/sdd_adding_mssql_db_host.html@@@Adding Microsoft SQL Server hosts for Sensitive Data Discovery@@@Add a Microsoft SQL Server database host for Sensitive Data Discovery...","saas/sdd_downloading_classification_results.html@@@Downloading classification results@@@Download a CSV file containing the results of a classification job. The CSV file lists the files with hits and the number of hits in each file...","saas/sdd_events.html@@@Data Security Posture events@@@The Data Security Posture Event Logs pageprovides information about the status of classification jobs...","saas/sdd_events_filters.html@@@Data Security Posture events filters@@@The Data Security Posture Event Logs page displays the events of all connected Rubrik clusters in the local time zone...","saas/sdd_pane.html@@@Data Security Posture pane@@@The Data Security Posture pane of the Global Dashboard provides an interactive element...","saas/sdd_reports.html@@@Data Security Posture reports@@@Customizable reports are available for Rubrik clusters with access to Data Security Posture...","saas/searching_object_on_snapshot_retention_page.html@@@Searching for an object on the Snapshot Retention page@@@Search for a specific object by object name on the Snapshot Retention page...","saas/secure_smb_domain_information.html@@@Secure SMB domain information@@@Information about the fields in an SMB domain that are required to enable security for a SMB share...","saas/select_a_new_VM_compute_resource.html@@@Selecting a new compute resource for vSphere VMs@@@Use Instant Recovery to perform an instant recovery of multiple vSphere virtual machines by selecting a new target compute resource for all selected virtual machines...","saas/selecting_a_compute_resource_live_mounts.html@@@Selecting a new compute resource using Live Mounts@@@Perform a live mount of multiple vSphere virtual machines by selecting a target compute resource for all selected virtual machines...","saas/selecting_a_new_compute_resource_vms.html@@@Selecting a new compute resource for virtual machines@@@Recover vSphere virtual machines in a batch using the Export option on the vSphere VM page...","saas/service_account.html@@@Service accounts@@@RSC uses service accounts to represent services and client applications that need to invoke RSC APIs...","saas/service_account_modification.html@@@Service account modification@@@Only the description of a service account can be modified...","saas/service_account_role_scenarios.html@@@Service account role scenarios@@@Information about the scenarios that demonstrate the application of the Principle of Least Privilege (PoLP) when configuring roles for service accounts in automated workflows...","saas/service_accounts_automation.html@@@RSC service accounts for automation@@@Information about using RSC service accounts to securely automate API access with CDM 9.4 and later...","saas/servicenow_integration_rsc.html@@@ServiceNow integration@@@The RSC integration with ServiceNow provides data management and protection capabilities...","saas/servicenow_ticket_creation_dsp.html@@@ServiceNow ticket creation for Data Security Posture@@@You can create ServiceNow tickets directly from RSC to address data access issues in Data Security Posture. You can also provide additional contextual information through a protected link and view the status of tickets through this integration...","saas/setting_default_dashboard.html@@@Setting the default dashboard@@@Choose the dashboard you want to set as the default landing page for quicker access to the information you care about...","saas/single_sign_on.html@@@Single sign-on@@@Rubrik Security Cloud supports SSO using the SAML 2.0 standard. With SSO, you can log in to RSC using credentials associated with an identity provider...","saas/sla_domain_administration.html@@@SLA Domain administration@@@RSC provides centralized administration of SLA Domains...","saas/sla_domain_attributes.html@@@SLA Domain attributes@@@Information about the details for managing SLA Domains and the available actions and attributes on the SLA Domains dashboard...","saas/sla_domain_deployment_model.html@@@SLA Domain deployment models@@@The deployment model for an SLA Domain determines who manages the archival storage and compute resources for cloud workload protection...","saas/sla_domain_details.html@@@SLA Domain details@@@Information about SLA Domain details page that provides a list of tabs, actionable options, and key details summarized through information cards...","saas/sla_domain_pause_resume.html@@@SLA Domain protection pause and resume@@@SLA Domain protection pause and resume feature enables you to temporarily pause and resume the protection activity within an SLA Domain...","saas/sla_domain_states.html@@@SLA Domain states@@@RSC protects objects through an SLA Domain. The SLA Domain state determines an object protection...","saas/sla_domain_switching_elements.html@@@SLA Domain switching elements@@@Information about SLA Domain switching elements in RSC...","saas/sla_domain_switching_notifications.html@@@SLA Domain switching notifications@@@Information about notifications during SLA Domain switching in RSC...","saas/sla_domain_sync_rubrik_cluster.html@@@SLA Domain synchronization with a Rubrik cluster@@@By synchronizing the SLA Domains from Rubrik Security Cloud with a Rubrik cluster, you can take on-demand snapshots from the CDM web UI and the CDM REST APIs without assigning the SLA Domains to any object...","saas/sla_domains.html@@@SLA Domains@@@SLA Domains in RSC unify data protection policies, providing a unified approach to manage data protection across various workloads and environments...","saas/sla_domains_assignment.html@@@SLA Domains assignment@@@You can protect and manage your data by assigning SLA Domains across various workloads in RSC...","saas/sla_domains_features.html@@@SLA Domains features@@@Information about the features available when creating an SLA Domain...","saas/sla_domains_switching.html@@@SLA Domains switching@@@By switching Rubrik cluster SLA Domains toRubrik Security Cloud, you can centrally manage and protect multiple objects across Rubrik clusters...","saas/sla_domains_without_snapshot_schedules.html@@@Continuous Data Protection-only SLA Domains for Amazon RDS@@@RSC workloads, such as Amazon RDS, support both continuous data backup and scheduled backups. You can enable them as needed. With Continuous Data Protection-only SLA Domains, you can exclude snapshot schedules for supported workloads by turning off the frequency and retention when creating or editing the Continuous Data Protection-only SLA Domains...","saas/sla_domains_without_snapshot_schedules_2.html@@@Continuous Data Protection-only SLA Domains for Amazon RDS@@@RSC workloads, such as Amazon RDS, support both continuous data backup and scheduled backups. You can enable them as needed. With Continuous Data Protection-only SLA Domains, you can exclude snapshot schedules for supported workloads by turning off the frequency and retention when creating or editing the Continuous Data Protection-only SLA Domains...","saas/sla_retention_lock_m365.html@@@Retention-locked SLA Domain for Microsoft 365@@@A retention lock on an RSC SLA Domain prevents premature deletion of snapshots belonging to Microsoft 365 workloads...","saas/sla_snapshot_download_overview.html@@@SLA Domain assignment during snapshot download@@@When downloading snapshots from archival or replication locations, you can assign an SLA Domain to control the retention period of the downloaded snapshot on the Rubrik cluster...","saas/smb_domain_authentication_status.html@@@Authentication status of SMB domain@@@Information about the authentication status of an SMB domain in RSC...","saas/snapmirror_cloud.html@@@SnapMirror Cloud@@@RSC protects user data replicated by the NetApp SnapMirror Cloud service...","saas/snapmirrorcloud_delete_snapshots.html@@@Snapshots deletion@@@The latest snapshot that has not been synchronized to the cloud cannot be deleted without removing protection from the volume...","saas/snapshot_expiry.html@@@Snapshot expiration behavior@@@Rubrik expires a snapshot when its retention period ends. The retention period depends on the snapshot type and on the SLA Domain...","saas/snapshot_frequency_mapping.html@@@Snapshot frequency mapping@@@Rubrik maps each policy-based snapshot to a frequency in the SLA Domain when it takes the snapshot. The frequency determines the retention period of the snapshot and does not change afterward...","saas/snapshot_management.html@@@Snapshots@@@Snapshots and backup information for relic objects and protected objects appear on the Snapshots page...","saas/snapshot_replication_aws.html@@@Cross-account snapshot replication for Amazon EC2 instances@@@RSC supports cross-account and cross-region replication of Amazon EC2 instance or EBS volume snapshots to ensure that all snapshots are available during disaster recovery or when the original snapshot is deleted or corrupted...","saas/snapshot_retention_management.html@@@Snapshot retention management@@@Rubrik implements a concept of buckets to manage snapshot expiration based on an SLA Domain...","saas/snapshots_types.html@@@Snapshot types@@@Information about types of the snapshots. Each snapshot is a fully functional, current copy of the source object...","saas/snmp_integration.html@@@SNMP integration@@@RSC uses Simple Network Management Protocol integration for central monitoring of managed devices on IP networks. Simple Network Management Protocol is a protocol for collecting and organizing information about managed devices on IP networks...","saas/sqlserver_db_instance_export_opts.html@@@Export options for Microsoft SQL Server databases@@@The export wizard offers these options when you export databases from a Microsoft SQL Server instance...","saas/sso_azure.html@@@Azure SSO@@@Configuring single sign-on with Azure involves several individual tasks, which must be performed in the correct order...","saas/sso_azure_assigning_app_roles_to_users.html@@@Assigning app roles to users and groups@@@In the Azure portal, assign the custom app role to the user accounts who need single sign-on access to RSC...","saas/sso_azure_authorizing_sso_groups.html@@@Authorizing RSC SSO groups for Azure SSO@@@After creating Azure custom app roles and assigning the roles to user accounts in Azure SSO groups, create RSC SSO group roles or use existing roles and authorize RSC SSO groups by mapping Azure custom app roles to RSC SSO group roles...","saas/sso_azure_config_claims.html@@@Configuring user attributes and claims@@@In the Azure portal, configure the claims for RSC by assigning values to the email address and group attributes...","saas/sso_azure_configuring_sso_in_rsc.html@@@Configuring Azure SSO@@@Configure SSO in RSC by uploading the Azure metadata file and downloading the Rubrik metadata file...","saas/sso_azure_creating_custom_app_roles.html@@@Creating custom app roles@@@In the Azure portal, create custom app roles to determine the permissions for user accounts that log in to RSC using Azure SSO...","saas/sso_azure_creating_non_gallery_enterprise_app.html@@@Creating a non-gallery enterprise application@@@Create a non-gallery enterprise application for RSC in the Azure portal...","saas/sso_azure_retrieving_saml_config_from_rubrik.html@@@Retrieving service provider SAML configuration@@@Retrieve the entity ID and callback URL values from RSC for preparing the federation metadata file in Azure...","saas/sso_azure_unauthorized_access_condition.html@@@Unauthorized access condition@@@Investigating the Azure SSO configuration can help find the cause of an unauthorized access error...","saas/sso_azure_updating_signing_certificate.html@@@Updating an expiring Azure SSO signing certificate@@@When the Azure SSO signing certificate is near expiration, create a new certificate in the Azure portal and update the SSO configuration in RSC to restore uninterrupted SSO access...","saas/sso_azure_uploading_rsc_metadata_file.html@@@Uploading the Rubrik metadata file@@@Upload the Rubrik metadata file to the enterprise application in Azure...","saas/sso_azure_user_attributes_and_claims.html@@@User attributes and claims in Azure@@@For SSO authentication, RSC requires that Azure issue specific claims and attributes...","saas/sso_saml_metadata_files.html@@@SAML 2.0 metadata files@@@SAML 2.0 uses information from metadata files to exchange information between an identity provider and a service provider, such as RSC, to establish a trust relationship...","saas/sso_testing_sso_configuration.html@@@Testing the SSO configuration@@@Test the SSO configuration to verify that authentication requests are handled by the identity provider...","saas/sso_testing_sso_configuration_2.html@@@Testing the SSO configuration@@@Test the SSO configuration to verify that authentication requests are handled by the identity provider...","saas/sso_testing_sso_configuration_3.html@@@Testing the SSO configuration@@@Test the SSO configuration to verify that authentication requests are handled by the identity provider...","saas/sso_users_groups.html@@@SSO users and groups@@@You can manage SSO users and groups together from a single page in RSC. SSO groups map identity provider groups to roles, and you can assign roles directly to individual users as needed...","saas/standalone_esxi_host_protection.html@@@Standalone ESXi host protection@@@Rubrik supports protecting and restoring virtual machines on standalone ESXi hosts, providing continuous data security in environments that do not include a vCenter server...","saas/subscription_management.html@@@Azure subscription and resource group management@@@Using RSC, you can monitor and manage the details of your Azure subscriptions and resource groups. You can also refresh an Azure subscription on-demand to obtain the most up-to-date metadata based on your specific requirements...","saas/support_cases_management.html@@@Support Cases management in RSC@@@The Support Cases page provides an integrated workspace in RSC for viewing, creating, and managing Rubrik support cases without leaving the platform...","saas/supported_features_for_workloads.html@@@Supported features for RSC workloads@@@Supported features for specific RSC workloads when creating or modifying an SLA Domain...","saas/supported_keys_perms_akv.html@@@Supported keys and permissions in Azure Key Vault@@@Requirements for supported key types in Azure Key Vault include enabled and unexpired RSA keys with required permissions...","saas/supported_keys_perms_aws_kms.html@@@Supported keys and permissions in AWS KMS@@@Permission requirements to add AWS KMS keys for data encryption on locations created using a Rubrik cluster running CDM version 9.4.2 or later...","saas/supported_rep_targets_for_failover.html@@@Supported replication targets for failover operations@@@RSC supports specific types of replication targets for failover operations...","saas/supported_rubrik_cdm_instance_types.html@@@Supported Rubrik CDM instance types@@@RSC supports several Rubrik CDM instance types...","saas/supported_rubrik_cdm_instance_types_2.html@@@Supported Rubrik CDM instance types@@@RSC supports several Rubrik CDM instance types...","saas/supported_workloads_rolling_upgrade.html@@@Supported workloads for rolling upgrade@@@Information about the supported workloads during a rolling upgrade...","saas/surgical_recovery_ec2.html@@@Recovering a quarantined EC2 instance snapshot@@@Use surgical recovery to restore or export a quarantined AWS EC2 instance snapshot without the quarantined files...","saas/surgical_recovery_file_level.html@@@Recovering folders and files from a quarantined snapshot@@@Use surgical recovery to recover folders and files from a quarantined VMware vSphere virtual machine or fileset snapshot while automatically excluding the quarantined files...","saas/surgical_recovery_image_level.html@@@Recovering a quarantined vSphere VM snapshot@@@Use surgical recovery to live mount or export a quarantined VMware vSphere virtual machine snapshot while automatically excluding the quarantined files...","saas/surgical_recovery_overview.html@@@Surgical recovery overview@@@Surgical recovery is an option in the recovery workflow that excludes quarantined files and restores clean data from a quarantined snapshot...","saas/surgical_recovery_prerequisites.html@@@Prerequisites and supported workloads@@@Surgical recovery requires specific licensing, software, and workload configurations...","saas/switching_all_sla_domains.html@@@Switching all SLA Domains@@@As a user with administrator privileges, switch all Rubrik cluster SLA Domain to Rubrik Security Cloud to manage all SLA Domains through a single platform...","saas/switching_sla_domains.html@@@Switching SLA Domains@@@To manage and protect multiple workloads across Rubrik clusters, switch SLA Domains from a Rubrik cluster to RSC SLA Domains...","saas/switching_sla_domains_manually.html@@@Switching SLA Domains manually@@@As a user with administrator privileges, manually switch Rubrik cluster SLA Domains to Rubrik Security Cloud to manage all SLA Domains through a single platform...","saas/switching_ui_language_japanese.html@@@Switching RSC user interface language to Japanese@@@To view the user interface of RSC in Japanese language, open the User Preferences page and switch the language to Japanese...","saas/sync_sla_domain_rubrik_cluster.html@@@Synchronizing an SLA Domain with a Rubrik cluster@@@In scenarios such as ransomware recovery, to take on-demand snapshots and to maintain data protection, synchronize an SLA Domain with a Rubrik cluster using RSC...","saas/system_config_privileges.html@@@System configuration privileges@@@Details of system configuration privileges that are available for assignment to different roles in RSC...","saas/taking_an_on_demand_snapshot_of_snapmirror_cloud.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of a NetApp volume@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, you can take snapshots of NetApp volumes by using the ondemand snapshot process...","saas/task_monitoring.html@@@Task monitoring@@@The task monitoring screen provides statistics for in-progress tasks, failed tasks, completed tasks, scheduled tasks, and canceled tasks...","saas/task_monitoring_details.html@@@Task monitoring details@@@The task monitoring dashboard displays information about in-progress tasks, failed tasks, completed tasks, scheduled tasks, and canceled tasks...","saas/taxii_threat_intel_filters.html@@@IOC filters for TAXII threat intel sources@@@Filters that Threat Monitoring applies to indicators of compromise ingested from a TAXII threat intel source...","saas/taxii_threat_intel_integration.html@@@TAXII threat intel integration@@@You can extend Threat Monitoring with your own threat intelligence by connecting a TAXII 2.1 server to RSC...","saas/tenant_org_pwd_policy_inherit_scenarios.html@@@Tenant organization password policy inheritance scenarios@@@Information about the different scenarios when the tenant organization inherits the password policies from a global organization...","saas/test_and_production_failover.html@@@Test and production failover@@@Test failover operations have several differences from production failover operations...","saas/testing_failover.html@@@Testing a failover@@@Test a failover for a selected Recovery Plan using the most recent snapshots...","saas/tests_for_disaster_recovery_failover.html@@@Tests for disaster recovery failover@@@You can test failover configurations by initiating a test failover from the primary site to the secondary site...","saas/threat_hunt_details.html@@@Threat hunt details@@@The Threat Hunts page provides comprehensive information about threat hunts and the matches identified over time...","saas/threat_hunt_object_details.html@@@Threat hunt object details@@@Provides information about the threat hunt object details page. When you open a threat hunt object, you can see all the details of the files that matched the hunt...","saas/threat_monitoring.html@@@Threat Monitoring@@@Threat Monitoring automatically and continuously scans snapshots for indicators of compromise to identify potential threats...","saas/threat_monitoring_and_hunt_event_details.html@@@Threat Monitoring and threat hunt event details@@@The Events page provides detailed information about a Threat Monitoring or threat hunt event, including the fields unique to each event type...","saas/threat_monitoring_details.html@@@Threat Monitoring details@@@The Threat Monitoring page displays information about scanned objects and threats identified during a selected time range...","saas/threat_monitoring_object_details.html@@@Threat Monitoring object details@@@The threat details page provides information about threats detected for a specific object and actions you can take to protect the object...","saas/tm_enabling.html@@@Enabling Threat Monitoring@@@Enable Threat Monitoring to scan snapshots for threats based on indicators of compromise...","saas/tm_ioc_support.html@@@YARA rule and file hash IOC support@@@Threat Monitoring supports both YARA rules and file hashes as indicators of compromise for cloud virtual machines and their associated storage. The indicator type and scan frequency affect Exocompute usage and archive retrieval costs...","saas/tm_prereqs_and_supported_workloads.html@@@Prerequisites and supported workloads@@@Threat Monitoring has specific prerequisites for enablement within RSC, as well as separate prerequisites for various workloads...","saas/transforming_email_address_name_id.html@@@Transforming email addresses to name IDs@@@Transform an email address to a name ID in ADFS by adding a rule...","saas/troubleshooting_akv_secureauth.html@@@Troubleshooting Azure Key Vault with secretless provisioning@@@Review common error scenarios and remedies when configuring Azure Key Vault integration using secretless provisioning...","saas/troubleshooting_cdp_filter_installation.html@@@Troubleshooting CDP filter installation@@@Troubleshooting information to resolve the IO filter installation error that can occur when you install the CDP filter on VMware Cloud Foundation 9.0...","saas/turbo_adv_threat_hunts.html@@@Turbo threat hunts and advanced threat hunts@@@RSC provides two distinct types of threat hunts, turbo threat hunts and advanced threat hunts to enhance security measures against potential threats...","saas/turning_off_ioc.html@@@Disabling an IOC in Threat Monitoring@@@Disable an indicator of compromise at a specific scope to suppress detections without disabling it for the entire account...","saas/turning_off_passkeys.html@@@Turning off passkeys@@@Turning off one or both types of passkeys when you no longer want to use them for web authentication...","saas/types_of_orchestrated_recovery.html@@@Types of Orchestrated Recovery@@@You can use the recovery type that is best suited for your virtual machine, environment, and recovery requirements in Orchestrated Recovery...","saas/uninstalling_cdp_filter.html@@@Uninstalling the CDP filter@@@Uninstall the CDP filter to stop continuous data protection...","saas/unmounting_azr_virtual_disk_from_azr_vm.html@@@Unmounting an Azure virtual disk from Azure virtual machine@@@When you no longer need an Azure virtual disk attached to an Azure virtual machine, from the Live Mounts page, unmount the corresponding virtual disk to free up storage space...","saas/updating_adv_exo_settings_rmc_clusters.html@@@Updating advanced Exocompute settings for Rubrik clusters@@@Update additional advanced Exocompute settings for Rubrik-managed clusters for better performance, scalability, and security...","saas/updating_aws_acnt_perms_manual.html@@@Updating AWS account permissions manually@@@Update permissions for an AWS cloud account to ensure that the required permissions for the new features are included in RSC. You can update the permissions manually. You can also remove unneeded permissions...","saas/updating_aws_outpost_account_perms.html@@@Updating the AWS outpost account permissions@@@You can update the AWS outpost account permissions settings in RSC...","saas/updating_azr_outpost_account_perms.html@@@Updating the Azure outpost account permissions@@@You can update the Azure outpost account permissions settings in RSC...","saas/updating_cdm_admin_email.html@@@Updating the CDM admin user email address@@@Update the email address associated with the admin account on a Rubrik cluster from RSC...","saas/updating_cdm_admin_password.html@@@Updating the CDM admin user password@@@Set a new password for the admin account on a Rubrik cluster from RSC...","saas/updating_master_key.html@@@Updating the master key for a reader location@@@Update the master key to ensure data center reader locations can continue accessing archived data after a rekey operation on the owner location...","saas/updating_rbs_when_upgrading_from_rubrik_cdm_version_5_3_to_version_6_0_1.html@@@Updating RBS when upgrading from Rubrik CDM version 5.3 to version 6.0.1@@@Update the Rubrik Backup Service when upgrading from Rubrik CDM version 5.3 to version 6.0.1...","saas/upgrade_prechecks.html@@@Upgrade prechecks@@@Information about prechecks performed for the fast and rolling upgrade types, including error messages and resolutions in case of failure...","saas/upgrade_preparation_and_prechecks.html@@@Upgrade preparation and prechecks@@@Rubrik clusters use automated prechecks to prepare for the upgrade process and identify potential obstacles...","saas/upgrade_rbk_cdm_soft_rsc.html@@@Rubrik CDM software upgrade using RSC@@@After you have downloaded the Rubrik CDM software upgrade package, you can upgrade the Rubrik CDM version running on any connected Rubrik cluster to the latest version using RSC...","saas/upgrading_an_aws_account.html@@@Upgrading an AWS cloud account@@@Upgrade an AWS cloud account in the &quot;Update permissions&quot; state to retrieve the current set of permissions...","saas/upgrading_aws_cces_gp3_disks.html@@@Upgrading Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services to use GP3 disks@@@To use GP3 disk features in an existing Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services deployment with GP2 disks, upgrade GP2 disks to GP3 using the upgrading disks workflow...","saas/upgrading_cdm_saas.html@@@Upgrading Rubrik CDM from RSC@@@After downloading the Rubrik CDM software upgrade package and ensuring that no precheck errors exist, upgrade the Rubrik CDM version of a Rubrik cluster from RSC...","saas/upgrading_cdp_filter.html@@@Upgrading the CDP filter@@@Upgrade the Continuous Data Protection filter with the latest available updates to ensure continuous data protection...","saas/upgrading_disks_azure_cces.html@@@Upgrading Azure CCES clusters to use PremiumV2_LRS disks@@@Upgrade existing Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage clusters for Azure from PremiumV1_LRS disks to PremiumV2_LRS disks using the upgrading disks workflow...","saas/usage_allocation_msp_billing.html@@@License usage for MSP primary accounts@@@MSP primary accounts can view aggregated license usage and per-tenant breakdowns across all tenant accounts...","saas/usage_tracking_paygo_licenses.html@@@Usage tracking for PayGo licenses@@@RSC tracks PayGo (pay-as-you-go) licenses across tenant accounts in the Dedicated Tenants model...","saas/user_auth.html@@@User authorization@@@Information about explicit authorization of the user to perform actions on resources specified in the assigned roles...","saas/user_group_assignment_okta_integration.html@@@User and group assignment in Okta integration@@@Okta requires you to assign the application integration to users and groups after updating the identity provider information in RSC...","saas/users_access.html@@@Users and Access@@@RSC provides role-based access control and several methods for authenticating a user account...","saas/users_roles_import_status_lmts.html@@@Users and roles import status and limitations@@@You can view the import status of the users and roles imported from CDM in the RSC import wizard. Importing users and roles from Rubrik CDM also has specific limitations...","saas/using_client_creds_to_obtain_at.html@@@Obtaining an access token@@@Obtain an access token by sending a request to the authorization server with service account client credentials or personal access token credentials. This access token is required to invoke the RSC APIs...","saas/using_different_TLS_certificates.html@@@Using a different TLS Certificate@@@Choose a different TLS certificate for the Rubrik cluster...","saas/using_rsc_api_proxy_nascd_rest_api.html@@@Using RSC API proxy for NAS CD REST API@@@Use the RSC API proxy to send NAS CD REST API for managing your NAS CD cluster from an RSC instance...","saas/using_service_sid_rbs_sql_server.html@@@Using a Service SID for RBS on SQL Server@@@Use a Service SID to grant permissions to RBS on Microsoft SQL Server...","saas/verify_adfs_service_provider_settings.html@@@Verifying ADFS Service Provider settings@@@After downloading the Rubrik metadata file and setting up custom claim rules, verify that all ADFS Service Provider settings are correct...","saas/verifying_connectivity.html@@@Verifying Nutanix VLAN connectivity@@@Verify that the segmented Nutanix network is routing traffic correctly and that Rubrik can reach all required endpoints...","saas/viewing_Azure_protected_objects.html@@@Viewing Azure protected objects@@@The details page for virtual machines and managed disks displays the protection status, calendar view of the snapshots, and events...","saas/viewing_a_sdd_report.html@@@Viewing a Data Security Posture report@@@View object classification details in a previously configured Data Security Posture report...","saas/viewing_activity_details.html@@@Viewing activity details@@@You can view activities about a specific task running on RSC...","saas/viewing_anomaly_compliance_report.html@@@Viewing the Anomaly Detection Compliance Report@@@Open the Anomaly Detection Compliance Report to review Anomaly Detection coverage and identify objects that need attention...","saas/viewing_anomaly_events_events_page.html@@@Viewing anomaly events from the Events page@@@RSC provides information about detected anomaly events for a Rubrik cluster in the Events page. You can also investigate the specific snapshot for further details...","saas/viewing_anomaly_events_from_the_critical_alert_email.html@@@Viewing anomaly events from the Critical Alert email@@@View details of an anomaly event from the link provided in the Critical Alert email...","saas/viewing_anomaly_events_from_the_dashboard.html@@@Viewing anomaly events from the Dashboard@@@RSC provides detailed information about detected anomaly events in the Data Threat Analytics dashboard...","saas/viewing_anomaly_reports.html@@@Viewing anomaly reports@@@Anomaly reports contain information about anomaly snapshots and object anomalies captured by Data Threat Analytics...","saas/viewing_classification_job_results.html@@@Viewing classification job results on demand@@@View classification job results on demand...","saas/viewing_dashboard_information.html@@@Viewing the Data Protection dashboard@@@The Data Protection dashboard provides a comprehensive summary of all events and SLA protection compliance of all the Rubrik clusters connected to RSC...","saas/viewing_exo_health_check_events.html@@@Viewing Exocompute events@@@View the Events page from the Dashboard to see the Exocompute events...","saas/viewing_exo_health_check_events_2.html@@@Viewing Exocompute events@@@View the Events page from the Dashboard to see the Exocompute events...","saas/viewing_exo_health_check_events_3.html@@@Viewing Exocompute events@@@View the Events page from the Dashboard to see the Exocompute events...","saas/viewing_live_mounts_page_for_azr_vm.html@@@Viewing Live Mounts page for Azure virtual machines@@@To review detailed information about the target virtual machines in Azure, such as the number of mounted virtual disks, the time when the disks were mounted, and the status of the mount task, open the Live Mounts page for Azure virtual machines. Additionally, you can unmount a disk from the target virtual machine...","saas/viewing_m365_dashboard_information.html@@@Viewing the Microsoft 365 dashboard@@@View the Microsoft 365 dashboard for information about all the backup events and compliances across the data sources within a Microsoft 365 subscription connected to RSC...","saas/viewing_oar_audit_logs.html@@@Viewing Orchestrated Recovery audit logs@@@The Orchestrated Recovery Audit Logs page provides a chronological record of user-initiated actions during recovery operations...","saas/viewing_oar_event_logs.html@@@Viewing Orchestrated Recovery event logs@@@The Orchestrated Recovery Event Logs page provides a chronological record of operational details during recovery events...","saas/viewing_precheck_logs_rerun_prechecks.html@@@Viewing precheck logs and rerunning precheck@@@If precheck errors occur while downloading a Rubrik CDM software upgrade package or upgrading the Rubrik CDM software of a Rubrik cluster, view the precheck errors, resolve those errors, and manually rerun the precheck to ensure that the Rubrik cluster is ready for an upgrade...","saas/viewing_quarantined_files.html@@@Viewing quarantined files or objects in threat hunts@@@You can view threat hunts that have quarantined files or objects as well as the number of impacted snapshots...","saas/viewing_relic_ec2_instance_or_ebs_volume_information.html@@@Viewing relic EC2 instance or EBS volume information@@@View relic EC2 instance or EBS volume details from the Inventory page...","saas/viewing_ri_investigations.html@@@Viewing Anomaly Detection@@@View information about anomalous incidents detected by Data Threat Analytics...","saas/viewing_rp_details.html@@@Viewing Recovery Plans and recoveries@@@The Recovery Plans page displays all configured Recovery Plans and their details...","saas/viewing_rubrik_cdm_release_information.html@@@Viewing Rubrik CDM release information@@@View the Rubrik CDM release details, which provide information about major release status, release adoption, release dates, end of support date, latest minor release, and the number of days that have elapsed after the last minor release or last patch release...","saas/viewing_sdd_audit_log_information.html@@@Viewing Data Security Posture audit log information@@@View the Audit Log tab for information about user-initiated events...","saas/viewing_sdd_events.html@@@Viewing Data Security Posture events@@@The Data Security Posture Events page provides a global view of all Data Security Posture events on the connected Rubrik clusters...","saas/viewing_sensitive_data_anomaly_details.html@@@Viewing sensitive data for an anomaly@@@View the sensitive data classification results for files impacted by an anomaly...","saas/viewing_sla_domain_details.html@@@Viewing SLA Domain details@@@RSC provides a specific page for each SLA Domain...","saas/viewing_smb_security_tab.html@@@Viewing the SMB Security tab@@@To add a Rubrik cluster to an SMB domain, enforce SMB security for a Rubrik cluster, or delete an SMB domain, view the SMB Security tab to review the details of the SMB domains...","saas/viewing_the_aws_accounts_page.html@@@Viewing the AWS accounts page@@@Access the AWS accounts page to view information about the cloud accounts created on RSC...","saas/viewing_the_aws_ec2_applications_page.html@@@Viewing the AWS - EC2 & Applications inventory page@@@View the AWS - EC2 & Applications inventory page from RSC...","saas/viewing_the_continuous_data_protection_dashboard.html@@@Viewing the Continuous Data Protection dashboard@@@View information about objects that are protected by an SLA Domain with Continuous Data Protection enabled...","saas/viewing_the_events_page.html@@@Viewing the Events page@@@The Events page provides a global view of RSC events...","saas/viewing_the_global_dashboard.html@@@Viewing the Global dashboard@@@Change views to the Global Dashboard to view summary information for RSC apps...","saas/viewing_the_upgrade_logs.html@@@Viewing upgrade logs@@@After you have started the operation to download a Rubrik CDM software upgrade package or started upgrading the Rubrik CDM software version, you can view the upgrade logs to know the current status of the operation. If the upgrade fails, you can create a Rubrik Support ticket or rollback to the previous Rubrik CDM software if you are using the fast upgrade...","saas/viewing_threat_hunts.html@@@Viewing threat hunts@@@View the completed and in-progress threat hunts with details on matches found, impacted objects, and impacted snapshots...","saas/viewing_threat_monitoring_info.html@@@Viewing Threat Monitoring information@@@To better understand the indicators of compromise and the affected snapshots, check the Threat Monitoring results for scanned objects...","saas/vm_encryption_detection.html@@@VM Encryption Detection@@@VM Encryption Detection identifies encryption on the host, allowing you to receive anomaly alerts for encryption activity on virtual machines. You can use this information to quickly assess the blast radius and recover from such attacks...","saas/vm_pre_post_backup_script_config.html@@@Configuring virtual machine backup scripts@@@Configure pre- and post-backup scripts to ensure application-consistent snapshots...","saas/vm_pre_post_backup_script_config_2.html@@@Configuring virtual machine backup scripts@@@Configure pre- and post-backup scripts to ensure application-consistent snapshots...","saas/vmc_adding_a_vmc_vcenter_server.html@@@Adding a VMware Cloud vCenter Server@@@Protect the virtual machines of a vCenter Server hosted in VMware Cloud by adding the vCenter Server to a Rubrik Cloud Cluster...","saas/vmc_adding_a_vmc_vcenter_server_2.html@@@Adding a VMware Cloud vCenter Server@@@Protect the virtual machines of a vCenter Server hosted in VMware Cloud by adding the vCenter Server to a Rubrik Cloud Cluster...","saas/vmc_adding_a_vmc_vcenter_server_3.html@@@Adding a VMware Cloud vCenter Server@@@Protect the virtual machines of a vCenter Server hosted in VMware Cloud by adding the vCenter Server to a Rubrik Cloud Cluster...","saas/vmc_adding_a_vmc_vcenter_server_4.html@@@Adding a VMware Cloud vCenter Server@@@Protect the virtual machines of a vCenter Server hosted in VMware Cloud by adding the vCenter Server to a Rubrik Cloud Cluster...","saas/vmc_editing_proxy_vm_for_vmc_vcenter_server.html@@@Editing proxy virtual machine details@@@Update the network settings for the proxy virtual machine configured for a vCenter Server hosted in VMware Cloud...","saas/vmc_editing_proxy_vm_for_vmc_vcenter_server_2.html@@@Editing proxy virtual machine details@@@Update the network settings for the proxy virtual machine configured for a vCenter Server hosted in VMware Cloud...","saas/vmc_editing_proxy_vm_for_vmc_vcenter_server_3.html@@@Editing proxy virtual machine details@@@Update the network settings for the proxy virtual machine configured for a vCenter Server hosted in VMware Cloud...","saas/vmc_editing_proxy_vm_for_vmc_vcenter_server_4.html@@@Editing proxy virtual machine details@@@Update the network settings for the proxy virtual machine configured for a vCenter Server hosted in VMware Cloud...","saas/vmware_vcenter_aws_evs.html@@@VMware vCenter on AWS EVS@@@RSC provides data protection for VMware vCenter virtual machines running on AWS Elastic VMware Service...","saas/vs_action_bar.html@@@Actions available on the Overview tab@@@Actions available for a selected virtual machine...","saas/vs_adding_vcenter_server_connection_info.html@@@Adding vCenter Server connection information@@@Add information for connecting a vCenter Server to a Rubrik cluster allowing the Rubrik cluster to protect the virtual machines running in the vCenter Server environment...","saas/vs_app_consistency_indiv_batch.html@@@Application consistency@@@You can set application consistency for vSphere virtual machines individually or in batch at different levels in the vSphere hierarchy...","saas/vs_application_consistency.html@@@Application consistency@@@The Rubrik cluster supports application-consistent snapshots for many guest OS types and application types...","saas/vs_automatic_protection.html@@@Automatic protection@@@To provide consistency when applying automatic protection, the Rubrik cluster adheres to a specific set of rules...","saas/vs_changing_snapshot_retention_policy.html@@@Changing the retention policy for a vSphere virtual machine snapshot@@@Assign a retention policy to existing snapshots of a vSphere virtual machine...","saas/vs_creating_live_mount.html@@@Creating a Live Mount of a vSphere virtual machine@@@When you are unable to access a vSphere virtual machine or when a virtual machine is deleted, create a virtual machine from a point-in-time copy of the source virtual machine...","saas/vs_creating_live_mount_vdisk_snapshot.html@@@Creating a Live Mount of a virtual disk snapshot of a vSphere virtual machine@@@A Live Mount creates a virtual disk or disks from point-in-time copies of the disks on a source vSphere virtual machine. The recovered virtual disks use the Rubrik cluster as the datastore...","saas/vs_creating_live_mounts_in_batch.html@@@Creating live mounts in a batch@@@When you are unable to access several vSphere virtual machines, or when multiple virtual machines are deleted and are required to be live-mounted together, create live mounts in a batch...","saas/vs_deleting_snapshots_virtual_machine.html@@@Deleting a snapshot from a vSphere virtual machine@@@Delete a snapshot that has a retention policy of Forever...","saas/vs_deleting_vcenter_server_connection_info.html@@@Deleting vCenter Server connection information@@@Delete the vCenter Server connection information that is stored by a Rubrik cluster to remove protection of the virtual machines of that vCenter Server...","saas/vs_deploying_rbs_windows_guest.html@@@Deploying RBS on Windows guests@@@You can set up a Rubrik cluster to automatically install and register RBS on a supported Windows guest at the next scheduled or on-demand backup...","saas/vs_downloading_file_folder_vsphere_vm.html@@@Downloading a file or folder@@@Download files or folders from a vSphere virtual machine snapshot to your local machine...","saas/vs_downloading_virtual_machine_files.html@@@Downloading virtual machine files@@@Download virtual machine files from Rubrik clusters to perform data analysis...","saas/vs_edit_vcenter_server_connection_info.html@@@vCenter Server connection information edits@@@Some properties of the vCenter Server connection information are editable from RSC...","saas/vs_excluding_vmdk_files_vm.html@@@Excluding VMDK files from a vSphere virtual machine@@@When backups are not required for some of the VMDK files of a virtual machine, exclude those VMDK files from backups...","saas/vs_exporting_vm.html@@@Exporting a vSphere virtual machine@@@Export a vSphere virtual machine snapshot or a VM template managed through a vCenter folder or content library to create a point-in-time copy for backup or migration...","saas/vs_exporting_vm_8_0_earlier.html@@@Exporting a vSphere virtual machine on CDM clusters 8.0 and earlier@@@To create a new vSphere virtual machine from a point-in-time copy of the source virtual machine, export a vSphere virtual machine on Rubrik CDM version 8.0 or earlier...","saas/vs_exporting_vm_file_folder.html@@@Exporting a virtual machine file or folder@@@Export files or folders from a vSphere virtual machine snapshot to a different recovery target...","saas/vs_exporting_vmt_as_vmt.html@@@Exporting a vSphere VM template as a VM template@@@You can export a vSphere VM template that is managed either through a vCenter folder or a content library to a new VM template. Exporting a VM template allows you to create a copy of a virtual machine that you can use to create and provision new virtual machines...","saas/vs_find_protected_objects.html@@@Find protected vSphere objects@@@RSC provides several methods for finding protected objects in the vSphere Inventory list page...","saas/vs_hitachi_storage_array_mangmnt_req.html@@@Hitachi storage array management requirements@@@For Hitachi storage array management, Rubrik recommends a Hitachi user account with an assigned storage administrator role...","saas/vs_migrating_to_a_vcenter_datastore.html@@@Migrating to a vCenter datastore@@@Migrate the VMDKs for a live mounted virtual machine to a vCenter Server datastore. Migration moves the data and control of the VMDKs to the vCenter Server. Migration also frees up the Rubrik cluster storage that was used for the datastore...","saas/vs_ods.html@@@On-demand snapshots of vSphere virtual machines@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, create virtual machine snapshots by using the on-demand snapshot process...","saas/vs_overview_card.html@@@Overview tab@@@Information available on the Overview card...","saas/vs_overwriting_vm_file_folder.html@@@Overwriting a virtual machine file or folder@@@Recover files or folders from a vSphere virtual machine snapshot to the original path, overwriting the existing files or folders...","saas/vs_performing_an_instant_recovery.html@@@Performing instant recovery for vSphere virtual machines@@@Perform an instant recovery to replace the source vSphere virtual machine with a fully functional point-in-time copy...","saas/vs_performing_inplace_recovery.html@@@Performing an in-place recovery@@@Perform an in-place recovery of a vSphere virtual machine to restore it to its original state while preserving its identity and location within the vSphere environment...","saas/vs_power_off_mounted_vm.html@@@Powering off after Instant Recovery or Live Mount@@@Power off a mounted virtual machine from the Live Mounts page of the RSC web UI...","saas/vs_protecting_vsphere_virtual_machine.html@@@Protecting a vSphere virtual machine@@@Protect a virtual machine by assigning an SLA Domain...","saas/vs_protecting_vsphere_vms_by_object.html@@@Protecting vSphere virtual machines by object@@@RSC classifies vSphere virtual machines according to virtual machines, folders, clusters, hosts, content libraries, and tags. You can assign an SLA Domain to a virtual machine, folder, cluster, host, content library, or tag category to protect all virtual machines in that group...","saas/vs_recovering_file_folder_another_folder.html@@@Recovering a file or folder to another folder@@@Recover files or folders from a vSphere virtual machine snapshot to a different location on the same virtual machine...","saas/vs_recovery_rbac_permissions.html@@@Required RBAC permissions for vSphere VM Recovery@@@Each vSphere virtual machine recovery operation in RSC requires a set of RBAC permissions to be applied to specific objects. You can grant minimum permissions when creating a custom role for users who perform vSphere virtual machine recoveries...","saas/vs_recovery_vm.html@@@Recovery of vSphere virtual machines@@@To recover a vSphere virtual machine, a Rubrik cluster mounts a point-in-time copy of that virtual machine...","saas/vs_recovery_vm_file_folder.html@@@Recovery of virtual machine files or folders@@@You can recover individual files or folders from a vSphere virtual machine when data is deleted, corrupted, or encrypted...","saas/vs_refresh_vcenter_metadata.html@@@Refreshing the metadata provided by a vCenter Server@@@Manually refresh the metadata provided by a vCenter Server...","saas/vs_removing_vm_entry_after_migration.html@@@Removing a virtual machine entry after live migration@@@After live migration of a recovered virtual machine, for example through the VMware Storage vMotion process, the Rubrik cluster maintains an entry for the migrated virtual machine on the Live Mounts page...","saas/vs_resource_visibility.html@@@vSphere resource visibility@@@In RSC, you can allocate vSphere resources to multiple Rubrik clusters for protection, customizing your RSC deployment for data management that fits your requirements...","saas/vs_scheduling_automatic_unmounting.html@@@Scheduling automatic unmounting for a vSphere virtual machine@@@Schedule automatic unmounting of a live-mounted vSphere virtual machine from the Rubrik cluster...","saas/vs_setting_resource_visibility.html@@@Setting vSphere resource visibility@@@Configure the vCenter compute clusters and host groups of virtual machines for protection by the Rubrik cluster...","saas/vs_sla_domain_assignment_options_for_vms.html@@@SLA Domain assignment options for virtual machines@@@Protect a set of virtual machines by assigning the selected set to an SLA Domain. Assigning virtual machines to an SLA Domain protects the virtual machines by applying the data protection policies of the SLA Domain...","saas/vs_snapshot_card.html@@@Snapshots card for vSphere virtual machines@@@For a selected local virtual machine, the Snapshots card in the Overview tab provides the ability to browse snapshots that reside on the local Rubrik cluster and on the replication location...","saas/vs_snapshots_tab.html@@@Snapshots tab for vSphere virtual machines@@@The Snapshots tab contains information for all snapshots for the chosen virtual machine...","saas/vs_specifying_crash_consistent_backups.html@@@Specifying crash consistent backups@@@By default, RSC initiates application-consistent backups for a virtual machine when the environment permits...","saas/vs_storage_array_adding_sa_rsc.html@@@Adding a storage array for vSphere support in RSC@@@Add a storage array to RSC to support vSphere. Storage arrays reduce the time a vSphere virtual machine is quiescent during snapshot operations, resulting in improved performance of virtual machine systems and applications...","saas/vs_storage_array_admin_requirements.html@@@NetApp storage array management requirements@@@For NetApp ONTAP operations, Rubrik recommends an ONTAP user account with an assigned custom ONTAP administrative role...","saas/vs_storage_array_deleting_sa_rsc.html@@@Deleting storage array support for vSphere in RSC@@@Delete a storage array that supports vSphere. Storage arrays reduce the time a vSphere virtual machine is quiescent during snapshot operations, resulting in improved performance of virtual machine systems and applications...","saas/vs_storage_array_editing_sa_rsc.html@@@Editing a storage array for vSphere support in RSC@@@Modify a storage array that supports vSphere in RSC. Storage arrays reduce the time a vSphere virtual machine is quiescent during snapshot operations, resulting in improved performance of virtual machine systems and applications...","saas/vs_storage_array_integration.html@@@Storage array integration@@@Rubrik Security Cloud provides a user interface for integrating Rubrik clusters with storage arrays, reducing the time a virtual machine is quiescent during snapshot operations...","saas/vs_storage_array_managing_int_rsc.html@@@Managing vSphere storage array integration in RSC@@@Enable or disable storage array-integrated backup support for vSphere virtual machines in a Rubrik cluster. Storage arrays reduce the time a vSphere virtual machine is quiescent during snapshot operations, resulting in improved performance of virtual machine systems and applications...","saas/vs_taking_on_demand_snapshot.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of a vSphere virtual machine@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of a single virtual machine, a VM template managed through a VMware server, or a VM template managed through a content library for backups and instant recovery...","saas/vs_unmounting_after_instant_recovery_or_live_mount.html@@@Unmounting after Instant Recovery or Live Mount@@@After performing instant recovery or creating a live mount of a virtual machine, remove the virtual machine from the Live Mounts page...","saas/vs_view_vm_details_page.html@@@Viewing the vSphere virtual machine details page@@@Access the virtual machine details page to view information about a specific vSphere virtual machine...","saas/vs_virtual_machine_protection.html@@@vSphere virtual machine protection@@@RSC provides protection for virtual machines through individual assignment of the virtual machine to an SLA Domain or through automatic protection...","saas/vs_virtual_machine_scripts.html@@@vSphere virtual machine scripts@@@RSC allows you to configure the Rubrik cluster to run scripts on a guest OS before a snapshot, after a snapshot, and after the Rubrik cluster completes the backup process...","saas/vs_virtual_machines.html@@@vSphere virtual machines@@@Rubrik Security Cloud provides data management and SLA Domain protection for vSphere virtual machines, including vSphere VM templates that are managed either through a VMware vSphere environment or a content library...","saas/vs_vm_details_page.html@@@vSphere virtual machine details page@@@The vSphere virtual machine details page provides detailed information about the virtual machine, protection of the virtual machine, available snapshots, and tasks related to the virtual machine and snapshots...","saas/vs_vm_protection_states.html@@@vSphere virtual machine protection states@@@Depending on the state of a virtual machine, there are several states of virtual machine protection...","saas/vs_vm_template_export.html@@@vSphere VM template export@@@You can export a vSphere VM template snapshot as a virtual machine or as a VM template...","saas/vs_vm_templates.html@@@vSphere VM templates@@@Rubrik Security Cloud support selected backup and recovery operations for vSphere VM templates and content library items. These operations include file recovery, export, live mount, mounting virtual disks, and recovering virtual machine images as a template...","saas/vs_vmdk_files.html@@@VMDK files@@@Virtual machines can include VMDK files that do not need to be protected...","saas/vs_vsphere_management.html@@@vSphere management@@@The Rubrik cluster accesses virtual machine data through a connection with the VMware vCenter Server or ESXi host that manages the hypervisor running the virtual machine...","saas/web_browser_support_rsc.html@@@Web browser support@@@When using the RSCweb UI, the latest version of Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge provides the best viewing experience...","saas/windows_volume_groups.html@@@Windows volume groups@@@A volume group is a Rubrik workload comprised of at least one data storage volume on a Windows host...","saas/workflow_aws_cloud_cluster.html@@@AWS Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage provisioning tasks@@@Provisioning a Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Amazon Web Services from RSC consists of several tasks...","saas/workflow_azure_cloud_cluster_es.html@@@Workflow for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure@@@Review the tasks required for provisioning Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Microsoft Azure from RSC...","saas/workflow_oci_cloud_cluster_es.html@@@Workflow for Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on OCI@@@Provisioning Rubrik Cloud Cluster Elastic Storage on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure from RSC consists of several tasks...","saas/workflow_sap_hana_storage_snapshots.html@@@Workflow for SAP HANA storage snapshots@@@Recovering an SAP HANA database using a storage snapshot requires you to meet specific prerequisites and perform several tasks...","saas/workload_specific_settings_sla_domains.html@@@Workload-specific settings for SLA Domains@@@Information about workload-specific settings configured when creating or editing SLA Domains for continuous data protection and backups for supported workloads...","saas/wvg_adding_a_windows_host.html@@@Adding a Windows host@@@Add a new Windows host to the Rubrik cluster to begin managing and protecting it...","saas/wvg_bare_metal_recovery.html@@@Bare metal recovery for Windows Volumes groups@@@The Rubrik Bare Metal Recovery solution for physical servers leverages native tools and volume-based backup software to enable flexible, cost-effective restoration without relying on third-party software...","saas/wvg_bmr_restore.html@@@Restoring a volume group using BMR@@@You can restore a Windows Volume group by using a bootable ISO file created through the Bare Metal Recovery process. You can create a recovery boot ISO file from any Windows OS, such as a laptop or a desktop server...","saas/wvg_configuring_the_volume_filter_driver_on_a_windows_host.html@@@Configuring the Volume Filter Driver on a Windows host@@@The Rubrik Volume Filter Driver improves the performance of incremental backups of protected volumes...","saas/wvg_creating_lm_win_with_rbs.html@@@Creating a Live Mount on Windows with RBS@@@Create a Live Mount of a volume group to a Windows host with RBS installed for direct access to the volumes in the group...","saas/wvg_creating_lm_win_without_rbs.html@@@Creating a Live Mount on Windows without RBS@@@Create a Live Mount of a volume group to a Windows host without RBS installed through the OS functionality...","saas/wvg_protecting_a_windows_volume_group.html@@@Protecting a Windows Volume group@@@Protecting Windows volumes uses the Rubrik Backup Service on a Windows host to read data from the protected volumes, and in some cases to create a Virtual Hard Drive file...","saas/wvg_recover_files_folders_win_with_rbs.html@@@Recovering files to Windows with RBS@@@Recover files at the volumes level or at the level of individual files for a volume group on a Windows host with RBS...","saas/wvg_taking_an_on_demand_snapshot_of_a_windows_volumes_group.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of a Windows Volumes group@@@In addition to policy-based snapshots, use the on-demand process to take snapshots of a Windows Volume group...","saas/wvg_verifying_connectivity.html@@@Verifying connectivity@@@Confirm host connectivity details from the Windows Volume group details page...","saas/wvg_viewing_windows_volumes_group_details.html@@@Viewing Windows Volumes group details@@@The Windows Volumes group details page provides information about the Windows Volumes group...","saas/wvg_volume_group_recovery.html@@@Windows volume group recovery@@@Multiple recovery options are available for Windows Volumes groups protected by a Rubrik cluster...","saas/wvg_windows_volumes_group_details.html@@@Windows Volumes group details@@@The Windows Volumes group details page displays the details of the object in the Overview, Events, and Snapshots tab...","saas/zscaler_integration.html@@@Zscaler integration for data loss prevention@@@You can protect your sensitive data by integrating Zscaler with RSC. You can identify sensitive data objects and prevent any unauthorized transfer of your most critical data by leveraging the Rubrik Data Security Posture and Zscaler Data Loss Prevention services...","salesforce/analyzing_salesforce_data.html@@@Analyzing Salesforce data and metadata changes@@@Analyze changes in Salesforce data and metadata over a period of time and make informed decision about restoring the data and metadata...","salesforce/changing_api_limits_sf_org.html@@@Changing API limits for Salesforce organizations@@@Change the API limits of a Salesforce organization that RSC can use for backup, restore, or any other operations...","salesforce/cloning_data_masking_template.html@@@Cloning a data masking template@@@Cloning an existing data masking template creates a duplicate with similar configuration settings...","salesforce/creating_data_masking_template.html@@@Creating a data masking template@@@Create a data masking template by specifying the object and fields to mask and the corresponding masking rules...","salesforce/data_masking_methods.html@@@Data masking methods@@@RSC provides a number of data masking methods for Salesforce data...","salesforce/data_masking_template_details.html@@@Data masking template details@@@Data masking templates contain configurations for objects, fields, and methods used to anonymize Salesforce data...","salesforce/data_types_substitution_masking.html@@@Supported data types for substitution masking@@@Salesforce data types supported for substitution masking include financial, personal, and geographic identifiers...","salesforce/deleting_data_masking_template.html@@@Deleting a data masking template@@@Deleting a data masking template permanently removes the configuration and masking rules for Salesforce data protection from RSC...","salesforce/editing_data_masking_template.html@@@Editing a data masking template@@@Edit an existing data masking template to update the data fields and methods used to mask sensitive information...","salesforce/managing_salesforce_data_protection.html@@@Managing Salesforce protection@@@Protect data in a Salesforce organization by assigning an SLA Domain with defined data protection policies...","salesforce/monitoring_salesforce_organizations.html@@@Monitoring Salesforce organizations@@@View details about a Salesforce instance to monitor the data changes, backup jobs, status, backup summary, and license usage...","salesforce/performing_in_place_data_masking.html@@@Performing in-place masking of sandbox data@@@In-place data masking uses a masking template to anonymize sensitive information that exists in a sandbox...","salesforce/salesforce_adding_alerts.html@@@Adding smart alerts for Salesforce@@@Add a smart alert to receive notifications about Salesforce data or metadata changes detected since your last backup...","salesforce/salesforce_adding_organization.html@@@Adding a Salesforce organization@@@Add a Salesforce organization to back up the data in your organization...","salesforce/salesforce_adding_records_rtbf_classic.html@@@Adding records to the RTBF list using the RSC wizard@@@Use the RSC wizard to add Salesforce records to the Right to Be Forgotten list without using Rubrik AI...","salesforce/salesforce_adding_records_rtbf_rubrik_ai.html@@@Adding records to the RTBF list using Rubrik AI@@@Add Salesforce records to the Right to Be Forgotten list to anonymize personally identifiable information during restore and sandbox seeding operations by using Rubrik AI...","salesforce/salesforce_api_usage_details.html@@@View API usage details for Salesforce@@@The API Usage page displays information about the API calls made in your Salesforce organization...","salesforce/salesforce_apis.html@@@Salesforce APIs@@@Rubrik accesses a Salesforce organization using APIs. Before a scheduled backup or restore job starts, RSC checks API availability. RSC also monitors API usage throughout each job and throttles operations to remain within the assigned API limits...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving.html@@@Salesforce archiving@@@Salesforce archiving enables you to move inactive or aged records out of your Salesforce production organization into lower-cost durable storage while preserving record content, relationships, and accessibility...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_cloning_policy.html@@@Cloning a Salesforce archival policy@@@Clone an existing archival policy to use it as a starting point for a new policy...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_creating_policy.html@@@Creating a Salesforce archival policy@@@Create an archival policy to define which Salesforce records are moved to lower-cost storage, how related records are handled, when the policy runs, and how long archived data is retained...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_deleting_policy.html@@@Deleting a Salesforce archival policy@@@Permanently delete an archival policy when it is no longer needed...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_disabling_policy.html@@@Disabling a Salesforce archival policy schedule@@@Disable the schedule for an active archival policy to suspend all scheduled runs without deleting the policy...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_editing_policy.html@@@Editing a Salesforce archival policy@@@Edit an existing archival policy to update its configuration before a policy run starts...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_enabling_policy.html@@@Enabling a Salesforce archival policy schedule@@@Enable the schedule for an inactive archival policy to reactivate scheduled runs according to the configured frequency...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_installing_lwc.html@@@Installing the Rubrik Archiving Lightning Web Component@@@Install and configure the Rubrik Archiving Lightning Web Component to view, search, and restore archived records directly from Salesforce record pages...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_monitoring_audit.html@@@Monitoring Salesforce archival jobs@@@Monitor archival job activity, review storage reclaimed, and track policy run history from the archive dashboard and the policy detail page in RSC...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_policy_management.html@@@Salesforce archival policy management@@@After creating archival policies, you can clone, run, edit, enable or disable schedules, or delete them from the Archive Policies page...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_prerequisites.html@@@Salesforce Archiving prerequisites@@@Salesforce Archiving requires a specific Salesforce add-on, API connectivity, and user permissions before you can configure archival policies...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_restoring_records.html@@@Unarchiving Salesforce records@@@Unarchive one or more archived Salesforce records to recover them to their original Salesforce organization...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_running_policy.html@@@Running a Salesforce archival policy on demand@@@Run an archival policy on demand to start a one-time run...","salesforce/salesforce_archiving_workflow.html@@@Salesforce archival workflow@@@A typical Salesforce archival workflow takes you from connecting your Salesforce organization through creating and activating an archival policy to monitoring jobs and restoring records when needed...","salesforce/salesforce_backup_recovery.html@@@Salesforce backup and recovery@@@RSC securely backs up your Salesforce organization with snapshots and recovers your data from those snapshots...","salesforce/salesforce_cascading_behavior.html@@@Cascading behavior for Salesforce recovery@@@When recovering Salesforce data, RSC recovers the parent object and cascades recovery to child objects and dependencies...","salesforce/salesforce_cloning_seed_template.html@@@Cloning seeding templates@@@Clone an existing template and optionally modify its settings to create a seeding template...","salesforce/salesforce_configure_alerts.html@@@Smart alerts for Salesforce@@@You can create and customize smart alerts based on data changes in your Salesforce organization so that RSC can inform you of any unexpected changes in your data...","salesforce/salesforce_configuring_permissions.html@@@Configuring permissions for Salesforce before connecting with Rubrik@@@To enable Salesforce to authenticate with RSC, configure the required Salesforce permissions and connected app policies in Salesforce...","salesforce/salesforce_create_gen_meta_temp.html@@@Creating general metadata seeding templates@@@Create a general metadata seeding template to specify the general metadata, such as configurations and business processes, to send to the sandbox...","salesforce/salesforce_create_obj_meta_temp.html@@@Creating object metadata seeding templates@@@Create an object metadata seeding template to seed custom and object metadata, such as structures, relationships, and UI, to the sandbox...","salesforce/salesforce_creating_data_seed_templates.html@@@Creating data seeding templates@@@Create a reusable data seeding template to specify the root object records and child objects that you want to send to a sandbox environment...","salesforce/salesforce_dashboard_details.html@@@Salesforce dashboard details@@@RSC monitors Salesforce data and displays details such as API and license usage, and the number of failed or successful backups...","salesforce/salesforce_dashboard_details_2.html@@@Salesforce dashboard details@@@RSC monitors Salesforce data and displays details such as API and license usage, and the number of failed or successful backups...","salesforce/salesforce_data_analysis.html@@@Salesforce data analysis@@@RSC generates insights about the changes in Salesforce data and metadata, facilitating detailed monitoring and secure restore operations...","salesforce/salesforce_data_masking_templates.html@@@Data masking templates@@@A data masking template defines data fields and the methods to prevent the exposure of sensitive data when recovering a production snapshot to a non-production environment...","salesforce/salesforce_data_protection.html@@@Salesforce Data Protection@@@Salesforce Data Protection is a Rubrik-hosted SaaS service that extends RSC by securely backing up your critical Salesforce data and metadata for standard and custom objects...","salesforce/salesforce_delete_handling.html@@@Soft and hard delete handling for Salesforce records@@@When you recover a deleted Salesforce record, RSC recovers it directly from the Salesforce Recycle Bin when possible to preserve the original record ID, or creates a new record when the original has been permanently purged...","salesforce/salesforce_deleting_alerts.html@@@Deleting smart alerts for Salesforce@@@Delete a smart alert when you no longer need it...","salesforce/salesforce_deleting_seed_template.html@@@Deleting seeding templates@@@Delete a seeding template that you no longer need...","salesforce/salesforce_disabling_alerts.html@@@Disabling smart alerts for Salesforce@@@Disable alerts for a Salesforce organization to stop receiving notifications about data changes...","salesforce/salesforce_editing_alerts.html@@@Editing smart alerts for Salesforce@@@Edit the criteria and settings of an existing alert to adjust monitoring thresholds or notification preferences...","salesforce/salesforce_editing_seed_template.html@@@Editing seeding templates@@@Modify an existing seeding template when you want to update its settings...","salesforce/salesforce_enabling_alerts.html@@@Enabling smart alerts for Salesforce@@@Enable disabled alerts to receive notifications about data changes...","salesforce/salesforce_gen_metadata_types.html@@@Salesforce general metadata types and components@@@Metadata types in Salesforce classify metadata into logical categories. For example, ContentAsset represents the metadata for creating an asset file. Metadata types have metadata components that you can recover...","salesforce/salesforce_managing_excluded_perms.html@@@Managing excluded permissions@@@Manage the permissions that you excluded for a Salesforce organization...","salesforce/salesforce_managing_missing_perms.html@@@Managing missing permissions@@@Manage the missing permissions for a Salesforce organization from the Missing Permissions tab on the Missing Permissions page...","salesforce/salesforce_managing_rtbf_list.html@@@Managing the RTBF list for a Salesforce organization with Rubrik AI enabled@@@View the Right to Be Forgotten list, edit the fields selected for anonymization by using Rubrik AI, and remove records from the list...","salesforce/salesforce_managing_rtbf_list_classic.html@@@Managing the RTBF list using the RSC UI@@@View and search the Right to Be Forgotten list for a Salesforce organization, and remove records from the list, without using Rubrik AI...","salesforce/salesforce_monitoring_api.html@@@Monitoring API usage for Salesforce@@@View and monitor the Bulk 2.0 and REST API usage details over a period of time from the API Usage page...","salesforce/salesforce_object_coverage.html@@@Salesforce object coverage@@@RSC protects a wide range of Salesforce objects, with specific limits for unsupported objects, metadata types, recovery behavior, and schema changes...","salesforce/salesforce_permissions.html@@@Salesforce permissions for backup and recovery@@@Backing up and restoring data requires that you assign certain Salesforce permissions for user account authentication in Salesforce...","salesforce/salesforce_rbac.html@@@Table of RBAC privileges for Salesforce Data Protection@@@Accessing Salesforce protection features within RSC requires the appropriate RBAC permissions. You can use the default Salesforce Admin role or a custom role...","salesforce/salesforce_reauthenticating_account.html@@@Reauthenticating your Salesforce account@@@Reauthenticate your Salesforce account when Salesforce revokes authentication after a while or when the account used to authenticate is no longer active in the Salesforce site...","salesforce/salesforce_recovering_data_metadata.html@@@Recovering Salesforce data and metadata@@@Recover Salesforce data or metadata from a snapshot to a Salesforce production or sandbox environment...","salesforce/salesforce_recovering_fields.html@@@Recovering Salesforce fields@@@Recover specific fields in Salesforce records from a snapshot to a Salesforce production environment...","salesforce/salesforce_recovering_general_metadata.html@@@Recovering Salesforce general metadata@@@Recover Salesforce general metadata components, such as user permissions and reports, from a snapshot to a Salesforce production or sandbox environment. General metadata includes user permissions and reports...","salesforce/salesforce_recovering_object_metadata.html@@@Recovering Salesforce object metadata@@@Recover Salesforce custom object metadata associated with individual Salesforce objects from a snapshot to a Salesforce production or sandbox environment. You can recover all metadata related to individual objects, or you can recover specific metadata. Object metadata that you can restore includes fields, validation rules, record types, and page layouts...","salesforce/salesforce_recovering_objects.html@@@Recovering Salesforce objects@@@Recover Salesforce objects from a snapshot to a Salesforce production or sandbox environment. Recovering an object also recovers all its files and records...","salesforce/salesforce_recovering_profiles.html@@@Recovering Salesforce profiles@@@Recover Salesforce profiles, along with their associated permissions, from a snapshot to a Salesforce production or sandbox environment...","salesforce/salesforce_recovering_records.html@@@Recovering Salesforce records@@@Recover Salesforce records from a snapshot to a Salesforce production or sandbox environment...","salesforce/salesforce_recovering_special_objects.html@@@Recovering specialized Salesforce objects@@@Recover specialized Salesforce objects by identifying and recovering the corresponding underlying technical objects...","salesforce/salesforce_regions.html@@@Supported regions for Salesforce@@@RSC provides support for Salesforce protection in several regions. You select the region when you set up the Salesforce instance in RSC...","salesforce/salesforce_removing_org.html@@@Removing Salesforce organizations@@@Remove a Salesforce organization to remove all snapshots and configurations from RSC...","salesforce/salesforce_required_permissions.html@@@Required Salesforce permissions@@@To back up and restore Salesforce data, you require specific Salesforce permissions...","salesforce/salesforce_right_to_be_forgotten.html@@@Salesforce Right to Be Forgotten@@@RSC anonymizes personally identifiable information in Salesforce backup data during restore and seeding operations to support privacy compliance. This is known as the Right to Be Forgotten feature...","salesforce/salesforce_rtbf_classic.html@@@RTBF with the RSC UI@@@You can add Salesforce records to the Right to Be Forgotten list and manage the list by using the RSC wizard and list page, without Rubrik AI...","salesforce/salesforce_rtbf_requirements.html@@@Salesforce RTBF requirements@@@RSC has specific requirements for using the Salesforce Right to Be Forgotten feature...","salesforce/salesforce_rtbf_restore_seeding_behavior.html@@@RTBF anonymization during restore and seeding operations@@@When a restore or sandbox seeding operation includes records on the Right to Be Forgotten list, RSC automatically anonymizes the personally identifiable information (PII) fields before writing the data to the target Salesforce organization...","salesforce/salesforce_rtbf_rubrik_ai.html@@@RTBF with Rubrik AI@@@You can add Salesforce records to the Right to Be Forgotten list and manage the list by entering requests in Rubrik AI...","salesforce/salesforce_running_perms_check.html@@@Running permissions checks for Salesforce@@@RSC automatically runs a permissions check every 24 hours to determine whether the authenticated user has any missing permissions...","salesforce/salesforce_seed_data.html@@@Seeding sandboxes with data@@@Seed a sandbox with a subset of data from a snapshot for testing and development in an isolated environment before pushing changes to production...","salesforce/salesforce_seed_metadata.html@@@Seeding sandboxes with metadata@@@Seed a sandbox with metadata from a snapshot for testing and development in an isolated environment before pushing changes to production...","salesforce/salesforce_seeding.html@@@Salesforce sandbox seeding@@@You can send a subset of data from a snapshot created in a Salesforce production environment to a sandbox environment. This allows you to use meaningful data for testing your changes in an isolated environment before pushing the changes to production...","salesforce/salesforce_supported_data_types.html@@@Supported Salesforce organizations, editions, products, and APIs@@@Information about supported Salesforce organizations, editions, products, and APIs for data protection and archiving...","salesforce/salesforce_taking_on_demand_snapshot.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot of a Salesforce instance@@@Take an on-demand snapshot to back up Salesforce data or metadata at any time...","salesforce/salesforce_viewing_outbound_ips.html@@@Viewing RSC outbound IP addresses for Salesforce@@@View the complete list of IP addresses that RSC uses to connect to your Salesforce organization, and add them to your network allowlist...","salesforce/sf_backup_indexing_strategy.html@@@Salesforce backup indexing strategy@@@RSC uses an optimized indexing strategy during Salesforce full backups to reduce backup time and make backed-up data available for search and filter operations...","salesforce/sf_recovering_missing_salesforce_record.html@@@Recovering a missing Salesforce record@@@Recover a related record to Salesforce when no corresponding record exists in the destination Salesforce organization...","salesforce/sf_recovering_record_already_exists.html@@@Recovering a record that already exists in Salesforce@@@Recover records to Salesforce without overwriting records that already exist in the destination organization...","salesforce/sf_recovering_required_parent.html@@@Recovering records that have a required parent relationship@@@Recover Salesforce records, where RSC automatically includes the parent record in the recovery operation when it is a mandatory relationship...","salesforce/sf_recovery_cascading_behavior.html@@@Salesforce recovery cascading behavior@@@When recovering Salesforce records, RSC automatically restores related records based on their relationship type and your selections during the hierarchy restore process...","salesforce/sf_recovery_related_records_salesforce.html@@@Recovery of related records in Salesforce@@@RSC validates and repairs incomplete or missing relationships before recovering related Salesforce records, ensuring data integrity across parent and child objects...","security/remote_syslog_server.html@@@Syslog workflow@@@Syslog workflow on Rubrik clusters support multiple remote syslog servers and message filtering based on event reporting facility and event severity...","security/syslog_supported_levels.html@@@Supported facility and severity syslog levels@@@Syslog messages are classified according to facility and severity levels...","system_tags/assigning_sla_system_tags.html@@@Assigning SLA Domains to System Tags@@@Assign an SLA Domain to a System Tag to protect all objects associated with the tag...","system_tags/assigning_system_tags_objects.html@@@Assigning System Tags to objects@@@Assign System Tags to an object to efficiently manage the assets in RSC...","system_tags/creating_system_tags.html@@@Creating System Tags@@@Create System Tags and associate them with objects or System Center Virtual Machine Manager native tags to organize and manage your data assets efficiently...","system_tags/deleting_system_tags.html@@@Deleting System Tags@@@Delete a System Tag to permanently remove it from RSC...","system_tags/editing_system_tags.html@@@Editing System Tags@@@Edit the name and description of an existing System Tag...","system_tags/key_features_system_tags.html@@@Key features of System Tags@@@System Tags in RSC provide flexible and efficient methods for managing data protection through enhanced object visibility and reporting...","system_tags/manage_report_based_system_tags.html@@@Manage reports based on System Tags@@@You can use the System Tags filter in RSC to generate reports and view metrics based on the created tags...","system_tags/managing_system_tags.html@@@Managing System Tags@@@Managing System Tags involves several key actions performed in the RSC UI to manage your data assets efficiently...","system_tags/native_tags_scvmm.html@@@System Tag assignment for SCVMM native tags@@@You can assign RSC System Tags to System Center Virtual Machine Manager native tags from your System Center Virtual Machine Manager environment to automate SLA Domain assignment for Hyper-V virtual machines...","system_tags/removing_native_tags_system_tags.html@@@Removing an SCVMM native tag from a System Tag@@@Remove a System Center Virtual Machine Manager native tag from a System Tag to unlink the native tag and its associated Hyper-V virtual machines from the System Tag group...","system_tags/removing_objects_system_tags.html@@@Removing objects from System Tags@@@Remove objects from a System Tag to unassign the objects associated with the System Tag...","system_tags/system_tag_keys_and_values.html@@@System Tag keys and values@@@System Tags support an optional key paired with a required value, enabling you to more precisely categorize and filter data assets in RSC...","system_tags/system_tags.html@@@System Tags@@@You can use Rubrik System Tags in RSC to manage your data assets efficiently by categorizing them based on tags relevant to a business context...","vcd/adding_vcd_instance.html@@@Adding a VMware Cloud Director instance@@@Add a VMware Cloud Director instance to protect VCD workloads...","vcd/deleting_vcd_instances.html@@@Deleting VMware Cloud Director instances@@@Remove vApp protection by deleting a VMware Cloud Director instance...","vcd/editing_vcd_instance.html@@@Editing a VMware Cloud Director instance@@@Edit a VMware Cloud Director instance to make changes to its account information...","vcd/excluding_vm_vapp.html@@@Excluding virtual machines@@@Exclude a virtual machine from the snapshots of the vApp...","vcd/field_descriptions_for_recovering_folders.html@@@Field descriptions for recovering folders@@@Recovering folders require input for a number of fields...","vcd/including_excluded_vms_vapp.html@@@Including excluded virtual machines@@@Include a previously excluded virtual machine in the snapshots of the vApp...","vcd/interaction_with_vsphere_protection_hierarchy.html@@@Interaction with vSphere protection hierarchy@@@An SLA Domain assignment made through the VMware Cloud Director hierarchy prevents an SLA Domain assignment through the vSphere hierarchy and overrides an existing assignment in the vSphere hierarchy...","vcd/managing_protection_vapps.html@@@Managing vApp protection@@@Assign an SLA Domain directly to a vApp to manage vApp protection...","vcd/managing_protection_vcd_orgs.html@@@Managing VMware Cloud Director organization protection@@@Manage the protection for VMware Cloud Director organization...","vcd/managing_synchronization_vcd.html@@@Managing synchronization for vCloud Director@@@Synchronization enables the Rubrik cluster to simultaneously initiate snapshots for all virtual machines within a vApp...","vcd/managing_vapp_template_protection.html@@@Managing vApp template protection@@@Assign an SLA Domain to all the vApps in a vApp template to manage vApp template protection...","vcd/metadata_protection.html@@@Metadata protection@@@Protection of vApps by Rubrik includes the metadata of the vApp...","vcd/migration_from_vm_level_protection.html@@@Migration from virtual-machine-level protection@@@Virtual machines that are protected through an individual SLA Domain assignment can be moved to protection through a containing vApp...","vcd/protection_and_management_features.html@@@Protection and management features@@@In addition to full SLA-Domain-based protection of vApps, other features available for vSphere virtual machines are also provided for vApps...","vcd/recovery_restore_vapp_data.html@@@Recovery and restore of vApp data@@@You can use Instant Recovery, Export, or file-level recovery to recover data from a vApp snapshot...","vcd/recoverying_vapp_templates.html@@@Recovering vApp templates@@@Recover your vApp templates using Export...","vcd/refreshing_vcd_instances.html@@@Refreshing VMware Cloud Director instances@@@Refresh one or more VMware Cloud Director instances to view the most recent vApp information...","vcd/rsc_vapp_recovery_workflow.html@@@Recovery workflow@@@Recovery provides a way to replace a virtual machine in a vApp with a snapshot of the virtual machine...","vcd/taking_ondemand_snapshot_vcd.html@@@Taking an on-demand snapshot@@@Take an on-demand snapshot of a vApp to capture the vApp at specific point in time and manage the selected snapshot using the SLA Domain policies, which may be different from the one assigned to the vApp...","vcd/vapp_export_options.html@@@vApp export options@@@The Configure Recovery Options section of a vApp export operation includes a number of optional parameters...","vcd/vapp_management.html@@@vApp management@@@After a VMware Cloud Director instance is added, the Rubrik cluster provides methods for finding, viewing, and protecting the vApps...","vcd/vapps_limitations.html@@@vApps limitations@@@Information about the specific limitations for vApps support provided by Rubrik...","vcd/vcd_changing_snapshot_retention.html@@@Changing the retention policy for a VCD vApp workload@@@Change the retention policy for on-demand snapshots of a VCD vApp workload...","vcd/vcd_exporting_full_vapp.html@@@Exporting a full vApp@@@Use Export to create a vApp using a vApp snapshot...","vcd/vcd_exporting_partial_vapp.html@@@Exporting a partial vApp@@@Export virtual machines from a vApp snapshot to create a vApp or to add to an existing vApp...","vcd/vcd_performing_instant_recovery.html@@@Performing an Instant Recovery of a vApp@@@Use Instant Recovery to recover an entire vApp from a snapshot...","vcd/vcd_recovering_files_folders.html@@@Recovering folders and files on vCloud Director@@@Recover folders and files from one of the virtual machine snapshots in a vApp snapshot...","vcd/viewing_vapp_details.html@@@Viewing VMware Cloud Director vApp details@@@The local page of a vApp provides information about the SLA Domain assignment, virtual machines, activities, and snapshots for a vApp...","vcd/vmw_cd_protection_hierarchy.html@@@Protection hierarchy for VMware Cloud Director@@@You can protect virtual machines through several levels of the VMware Cloud Director management hierarchy...","vcd/vmware_cloud_director_instances.html@@@VMware Cloud Director instances@@@A Rubrik cluster works with vApps through VMware Cloud Director instances...","vcd/vmware_cloud_director_vapps.html@@@VMware Cloud Director vApps@@@The Rubrik cluster provides SLA Domain protection and data management for VMware Cloud Director vApps...","vmware_cloud/vmware_cloud.html@@@VMware Cloud@@@A Rubrik Cloud Cluster effectively protects virtual machines deployed on VMware Cloud on AWS, Microsoft Azure VMware Solution, and Google Cloud VMware Engine..."];
